(249, '2026', '129396', 'Some learners have not yet reached the required proficiency levels in reading comprehension and numeracy skills; presence of struggling and non-readers; limited time for remediation and intervention; insufficient differentiated instructional materials; varying learner readiness and support at home', 'Learners’ performance in the NAT is below the expected proficiency level in several learning areas; gaps in higher-order thinking and 21st century skills; insufficient mastery of competencies; limited use of varied and innovative teaching strategies; inadequate review and preparation for standardized assessments; lack of localized and contextualized learning resources', 'absence or limited implementation of School-Based ALS program; lack of monitoring and tracking system for ALS learners; insufficient coordination with ALS implementers; limited awareness and participation of potential ALS learners in the community', '', '', '', 'Lack of knowledge and skills of teachers in conducting test item analysis; absence of a standardized process or tool for item analysis; limited time due to teaching workload; insufficient training on data analysis and interpretation; lack of coordination and monitoring in implementing assessment analysis practices', 'No available data on partnerships with local industries; absence or limited engagement with industry partners; lack of established linkages for work immersion and skills training; insufficient coordination and communication with potential industry stakeholders; limited opportunities for learners to experience real-world applications of TLE-TVL competencies', 'Presence of reported bullying incidents among learners; limited awareness or inconsistent understanding of anti-bullying policies; reluctance of learners to report incidents; need to strengthen monitoring and reporting mechanisms; insufficient involvement of parents and stakeholders in addressing bullying cases', 'No available data on child abuse cases; absence or limited documentation and reporting system for child protection concerns; possible underreporting of incidents due to lack of awareness or fear of disclosure; limited orientation on child protection policies among learners, teachers, and parents; need to strengthen coordination with child protection committees and external agencies', 'Persistent cases of learners at risk of dropping out; absenteeism and low learner engagement; economic difficulties of families affecting school attendance; limited monitoring and follow-up of at-risk learners; insufficient intervention programs to address the root causes of drop-out', 'Culture-sensitive activities are implemented but not consistently across all grade levels; limited integration of local culture and traditions in some learning areas; insufficient resources and materials to support culturally responsive activities; need for stronger stakeholder and community involvement', 'No available data on programs and services for disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adult learners; absence or limited implementation of inclusive learning opportunities; lack of coordination with ALS and community partners; insufficient identification and profiling of target learners; limited awareness and outreach within the community', 'No available data on the implementation of a school-based ALS program; absence or limited establishment of ALS classes in the school; lack of trained ALS implementers or facilitators; insufficient coordination with ALS coordinators; limited awareness and support from stakeholders regarding ALS programs', 'Child Protection Committee is not fully functional or consistently active; unclear roles and responsibilities of committee members; limited training and capacity on child protection policies and procedures; irregular meetings and monitoring of child protection concerns; insufficient documentation and reporting of cases and actions taken', 'DRRM plan is in place but not consistently updated and fully implemented; limited participation of stakeholders in DRRM planning and activities; insufficient resources and materials for disaster preparedness; need to strengthen regular drills and capacity-building activities; gaps in monitoring and evaluation of DRRM implementation', 'No available data on mental wellness support mechanisms; absence or limited structured mental health programs and services; lack of trained personnel to provide mental health support; limited awareness of mental health concerns among learners, teachers, and parents; insufficient coordination with external mental health service providers', 'PWD-friendly facilities are available but not fully adequate or accessible in all areas; need for improvement and expansion of SPED-related resources and infrastructure; limited specialized equipment and learning materials for learners with special needs; insufficient maintenance and upgrading of existing facilities; need for stronger support services for inclusive education', '', 'School-community planning team is organized but not consistently active; limited participation of some stakeholders in planning activities; irregular meetings and coordination; need to strengthen communication and collaboration between school and community members; limited documentation of planning activities and outputs', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'N/A', 'Teachers consistently implement remediation programs and intervention strategies; availability of intervention materials and structured remediation plans; regular assessment and monitoring of learners’ progress; strong support from school leadership; active collaboration among teachers through LAC sessions; engagement of parents in supporting learners’ improvement', 'Teachers consistently integrate values formation and peace education across learning areas; strong alignment with DepEd core values (Maka-Diyos, Maka-tao, Makakalikasan, Makabansa); availability of learning materials and guides that support values integration; positive school culture that promotes respect, inclusivity, and discipline; active participation of learners in values-driven activities and programs', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'N/A', '', 'Active participation and leadership of student officers; strong support and guidance from teacher-advisers and school head; regular implementation of student-led programs and activities; clear organizational structure and defined roles; engagement of learners in school governance and decision-making processes', 'Adoption of innovative practices and digital tools in delivering services; strong leadership support in improving frontline services; responsive and client-oriented school personnel; availability of feedback mechanisms from stakeholders; continuous improvement culture within the school', 'Clear alignment between strategic goals and implementation plans; strong leadership and management support; defined roles and responsibilities of personnel; availability of resources to support plan execution; regular monitoring and evaluation of implementation progress', 'Active participation and collaboration of SGC members; strong leadership and support from the school head; regular conduct of meetings and planning activities; clear roles and responsibilities of council members; effective stakeholder engagement in school governance and decision-making', 'Active participation and cooperation of parents and teachers; strong leadership of PTA officers; regular meetings and communication with stakeholders; support of PTA in school programs and activities; collaborative relationship between school and community', 'Strong collaboration and communication with stakeholders and partner schools; active participation in joint programs and activities; support from school leadership in partnership initiatives; established linkages and networks; shared resources and best practices among partners', 'Established monito