ection Policy\r\nCoordination with LGU and child protection agencies\r\nTeacher vigilance and awareness', '', '', '', '', 'Existing Child Protection Committee\r\nSupport from school head and stakeholders\r\nClear DepEd policies on child protection', 'Existing DRRM plan and structure\r\nSupport from LGU and DRRM offices\r\nActive participation of school personnel', '', '', '', '', 'Active student leaders and organizations\r\nSupport from teacher-advisers\r\nExisting student governance structure', '', 'Existing School Improvement Plan (SIP)\r\nStrong leadership of school head\r\nActive participation of teachers and stakeholders', '', 'Active PTA officers\r\nStrong support from parents and community\r\nExisting PTA programs and initiatives', '', '', '', 'Existing IPCRF system\r\nSupport from school head and raters\r\nClear DepEd performance standards', 'Existing OPCRF system\r\nSupport from school leadership\r\nDefined office performance indicators', 'Active LAC sessions\r\nSupport from Master Teachers and School Head\r\nAvailability of training resources\r\n\r\nCategory:', '', '', 'Established payroll system\r\nCoordination with DepEd and finance offices\r\nSupport from administrative staff', 'Clear guidelines on workload distribution\r\nSupport from school head\r\nCooperation among teachers', '', '', '', 'Existing utility connections\r\nSupport from service providers\r\nSchool maintenance system', '', 'Established financial management system\r\nSupport from school head and finance personnel\r\nClear DepEd guidelines', 'Trained administrative personnel\r\nEstablished financial procedures\r\nSupport from DepEd and accounting offices', 2, 1, 2, 1, 1, 6, 1, 2, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 2, 2, 5, 6, 5, 2, 2, 6, 1, 2, 2, 6, 2, 1, 6, 1, 1, 1, 3, 2, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Not Applicable ', 'Conduct intensive NAT review sessions and drills\r\nDevelop intervention programs targeting least mastered competencies\r\nMonitor learner progress through periodic assessments\r\nStrengthen teacher capacity through training and LAC sessions', 'Not Applicable ', 'Conduct LAC sessions on contextualization and localization of materials\r\nDevelop and share contextualized lesson exemplars\r\nEncourage collaborative material development among teachers\r\nMonitor and evaluate usage of contextualized materials', 'Develop structured remediation and intervention plans\r\nConduct regular pull-out or after-class remediation sessions\r\nMonitor learner progress through assessment tracking\r\nProvide teacher training on differentiated instruction', 'Strengthen documentation of values integration in DLL/DLP\r\nConduct training on integrating peace education and core values\r\nIncorporate values-based assessment in lessons\r\nShare best practices during LAC sessions', 'Conduct training on test item analysis and data interpretation\r\nInstitutionalize regular item analysis after major exams\r\nUse results to identify least mastered competencies\r\nIntegrate findings into lesson planning and remediation', 'Establish formal partnerships with local industries (MOA/MOU)\r\nStrengthen work immersion programs\r\nConduct regular coordination meetings with partners\r\nAlign TLE-TVL curriculum with industry needs', 'Strengthen reporting and documentation system\r\nConduct regular anti-bullying campaigns and orientations\r\nEnsure immediate response and intervention for reported cases\r\nMonitor and evaluate implementation of anti-bullying policies', 'Strengthen coordination with external agencies (DSWD, LGU)\r\nConduct awareness programs on child protection\r\nEnsure proper documentation and reporting procedures\r\nMaintain a safe and protective school environment', 'Strengthen learner monitoring system (attendance tracking)\r\nConduct home visitation and parent conferences\r\nProvide intervention programs (feeding, financial assistance linkage)\r\nImplement retention programs and incentives', 'Integrate culture-sensitive activities in school programs\r\nCollaborate with community cultural leaders\r\nDocument and evaluate cultural activities\r\nPromote inclusivity and respect for diversity', 'Strengthen ALS and alternative learning programs\r\nConduct community mapping and outreach activities\r\nProvide flexible learning schedules and modalities\r\nPartner with LGU and NGOs for support programs', 'Establish and operationalize school-based ALS program\r\nAssign ALS focal person and coordinators', 'Conduct regular meetings and document proceedings\r\nProvide training and capacity building for committee members\r\nStrengthen implementation of child protection policies\r\nMonitor and evaluate child protection programs', 'Conduct regular DRRM drills (earthquake, fire, etc.)\r\nUpdate DRRM plan annually\r\nStrengthen coordination with local DRRM offices\r\nEnsure availability of emergency kits and resources', 'Strengthen school-based mental health programs and services\r\nConduct regular mental health awareness activities and seminars\r\nProvide training for teachers on psychological first aid\r\nEstablish referral system with health professionals and agencies', 'Improve school facilities to be PWD-friendly (ramps, CR, signage)\r\nAllocate budget for inclusive and accessible infrastructure\r\nProvide training for teachers on inclusive education\r\nStrengthen coordination with SPED specialists and programs', 'Strengthen stakeholder participation in planning process\r\nRegularly review and update the School Improvement Plan (SIP)\r\nAlign school programs and activities with SIP targets\r\nMonitor and evaluate implementation of strategic plans', 'Conduct regular planning meetings with stakeholders\r\nStrengthen collaboration with LGU, PTA, and community leaders\r\nDocument all planning activities and outputs\r\nEncourage active participation in decision-making', 'Conduct leadership training and capacity building for officers\r\nStrengthen student participation in school programs\r\nEnsure proper documentation of activities\r\nEncourage student-led initiatives and projects', 'Introduce digital systems for school transactions (e.g., online forms, tracking)\r\nImprove communication channels with stakeholders\r\nEstablish feedback and evaluation mechanisms\r\nContinuously innovate and improve service delivery', 'Strengthen implementation planning aligned with SIP\r\nEnsure all activities are documented and monitored\r\nConduct regular review of implementation progress\r\nAlign all programs with strategic priorities', 'Conduct regular SGC meetings\r\nStrengthen stakeholder engagement and participation\r\nDocument all resolutions and decisions\r\nMonitor implementation of SGC plans', 'Strengthen communication with parents\r\nConduct regular PTA meetings and activities\r\nEncourage active participation of all parents\r\nImplement programs beneficial to learners', 'Establish formal partnerships (MOA/MOU)\r\nConduct regular coordination meetings\r\nDocument all partnership activities\r\nStrengthen stakeholder engagement programs', 'Strengthen monitoring and evaluation system\r\nConduct regular program evaluation\r\nUtilize results for continuous improvement\r\nEnsure proper documentation of reports', 'Strengthen monitoring and documentation of IPCRF\r\nConduct regular performance review and feedback sessions\r\nProvide coaching and mentoring for personnel\r\nAlign performance targets with school goals', 'Strengthen monitoring of OPCRF targets\r\nImprove documentation and reporting system\r\nConduct regular evaluation of office performance\r\nAlign office targets with school objectives', 'Conduct needs assessment for LAC topics\r\nStrengthen documentation of LAC sessions\r\nAlign LAC with PPST indicators\r\nMonitor impact of training on teaching practices', 'Allocate budget for training and development\r\nEncourage participation in online and external trainings\r\nEnsure equal access to professional development opportunities\r\nTrack and monitor training participation', 'Establish formal recognition and incentive system\r\nConduct regular awarding ceremonies\r\nDocument achievements and recognitions\r\nPromote a culture of appreciation and motivation', 'Strengthen coordination with finance and payroll offices\r\nMonitor timely release of salaries and benefits\r\nAddress compensation issues promptly\r\nMaintain accurate records of compensation', 'Ensure equitable distribution of workload\r\nMonitor teacher assignments regularly\r\nProvide support for teachers with heavy workload\r\nAlign workload with teacher specialization', 'Conduct regular and scheduled infrastructure inspections\r\nStrengthen documentation and reporting system\r\nUtilize inspection results for timely action\r\nAssign responsible personnel for monitoring', 'Prioritize infrastructure needs based on urgency\r\nStrengthen partnerships for funding support\r\nAllocate budget efficiently for improvements\r\nMonitor implementation of projects', 'Update and acquire new library resources\r\nImprove library facilities and environment\r\nEncourage learners to utilize library services\r\nConduct reading programs and activities', 'Strengthen coordination with service providers\r\nEstablish backup systems where possible\r\nRegular monitoring of utility services\r\nEnsure continuous availability of services', 'Repair and maintain existing computers\r\nRequest additional ICT resources\r\nConduct ICT integration training for teachers\r\nMaximize utilization of computer lab', 'Strengthen financial planning and budgeting\r\nMonitor utilization of MOOE regularly\r\nEnsure transparency and accountability\r\nAlign expenses with school priorities', 'Ensure timely submission of liquidation reports\r\nStrengthen documentation and record-keeping\r\nMonitor compliance with financial policies\r\nProvide training on financial procedures', 'Conduct regular stakeholder satisfaction surveys\r\nEstablish feedback and complaint mechanisms\r\nAnalyze feedback for improvement\r\nEnhance communication and service delivery', 1, 126, 12, 103);
