(282, '2026', '205506', 'Home and Environmental Factors: Gadget distractions, family issues, low parental support, overcrowded classrooms, and lack of home reading practice.', 'A significant number of learners fall below the proficiency level in core subjects (e.g., Math, Science, English).', 'No learners enrolled in ALS', '', '', '', '', 'Resource Limitations and no TLE-TVL course offering in school ', '', '', '', '', 'School has no OSYs, and adult learners', 'no base ALS program in School', '', '', 'Lack of a structured, consistent, and accessible mental wellness support system within the school.', '', '', '', '', 'Delayed responses to inquiries, complaints, and requests from parents, learners, and partners.', '', 'Lacks consistent stakeholder engagement, proper documentation, and effective monitoring.', '', 'Limited and irregular participation of stakeholders and partner schools in school programs and activities, resulting in weak collaboration and minimal shared responsibility in school improvement initiatives.', '', 'Stakeholder satisfaction ratings fluctuate or fall below the “satisfactory” level in some areas (e.g., services, communication, facilities).', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'The library has limited, outdated, or non-aligned books and reference materials.', 'Internet access is weak, intermittent, or unavailable in some areas of the school.', 'Poor internet access limits research and ICT-based activities.', '', '', '', '', '', 'visible in the classroom, comtextualized IMs and lesson plans', 'Regular and dedicated time for reading remediation, math and science remediation activities', 'Teachers embed peace topics like conflict resolution and core values (Maka-Diyos, Maka-tao, Makakalikasan, Makabansa and subject integration', 'Item analysis is conducted and monitored after every periodical examination.\r\nThis ensures timely insights for refining teaching and learning processes.', '', 'Strong anti-bullying policies and comprehensive teachers and staff training', 'Prioritize child safety through training, policies, and community engagement', 'Regular monitoring of attendance, grades, and  students showing warning signs of potential dropout risk  for timely interventions', 'Schools conducting culture-sensitive activities create inclusive environments by honoring students\' diverse backgrounds', '', '', 'Schools maintain consistently functional child protection committees through structured support and accountability.', 'Trained School DRRM Coordinator and team with clear roles conduct regular drills, hazard assessments, and plan updates', '', 'Schools maintain PWD-friendly and special education facilities, such as ramps in SNED program building', 'Committed School Head and management team such as  they set timelines, chair planning sessions, and assign clear roles', 'The school has a functional school‑community planning team because of clear policies, committed leadership, active stakeholder participation, adequate training, and an inclusive, supportive community environment', 'Active and meaningful student participation, where officers and members are trained, take initiative, and allowing student leaders to plan and lead projects under supervision ', '', 'The school has Committed School Head and management team religiously set their timelines, chair planning sessions, and assign clear roles', '', 'School has strong leadership that regularly convenes the PTA, active and trusting parent participation, capable and trained PTA officers, transparent use of resources, and strong linkages between the PTA and school programs.', '', 'The school monitors and evaluates its programs, projects, and activities because of clear DepEd guidelines, committed leadership, organized data‑gathering and reporting systems, standardized tools, and a culture of using results to continuously improve school performance', '', 'School personnel achieve an average rating of very satisfactory in the individual performance commitment and review because of clear performance standards, regular coaching and mentoring, consistent monitoring of targets, timely feedback, and a supportive school culture that encourages professional growth and accountability.', 'The school achieves an average rating of “Very Satisfactory” in the Office Performance Commitment and Review because of clear standards, strong leadership oversight, regular feedback, reliable documentation, and a culture of accountability and improvement \r\n\r\n', 'Strong administrative leadership from school heads, protected time slots prioritized over routine meetings, collaborative teacher groups with clear roles and norms, needs assessments aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Philippine Professional Standards for Teachers (PPST), adequate resource allocation from MOOE funds', 'Strong administrative support,access to diverse CPD activities like INSETs, LACs, mentoring, coaching, online learning, and action research; teacher motivation tied to career advancement', 'Administrative commitment to motivation through adequate allocation from MOOE or special funds for awards and certificates, transparent criteria aligned with IPCRF and PPST milestones, established ceremonies or public acknowledgments to foster a culture of appreciation. ', 'School ensuring timely receipt of correct salaries, allowances, and compensation ', 'School heads ensure a transparent allocation policies prioritizing teacher specialization and class sizes, workload audits balancing teaching with preparation/remediation tasks.', 'Walk-throughs by school heads with maintenance staff , parent-teacher committees joining to spot classroom wear-and-tear from a parent\'s perspective, and quick repairs using school funds before small issues become safety hazards or big expenses', 'Proactive school leadership prioritizing safety through School Improvement Plans (SIPs), strategic MOOE fund allocation for minor repairs via the School-Based Repair and Maintenance', '', '', '', 'Strategic alignment of expenditures with Annual Improvement Plan (AIP) priorities, proactive planning by school heads with detailed liquidation timelines, transparent documentation and regular financial reporting to division office and strong community partnerships like PTA contributions to supplement funds for projects ', 'School strict adherence to DepEd Order 008 s. 2019 checklists requiring complete documentation and timely submission of liquidation reports', 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 2, 2, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 2, 2, 'Daily reading routines using take-home storybooks, gadget-free classroom zones with engaging hands-on activities during peak distraction hours, and flexible grouping in overcrowded rooms to ensure every child gets small-group teacher attention for phonics and basic math practice', 'Implement targeted intervention programs (remedial classes, tutoring sessions, pull-out programs).', 'Information drives', 'Teachers and school head commit to prominently displaying contextualized instructional materials and lesson plans in every classroom', 'Sustaining the remediation program and strengthening the support in reading, math and science by regularly conducting targeted intervention and tracking learners\' improvement', 'School consistently promote a culture peace, and teachers continuously integrate topics promoting peace and DepEd core values', 'Item analysis will be performed consistently after every periodical examination', 'Train elementary TLE educators on local industry basics .', 'Commit to maintaining zero child bullying incidence by fostering a safe, inclusive, and respectful learning environment for all students.', ' Commit to achieving and maintaining zero child abuse incidence by prioritizing the safety, welfare, and protection of every child in our care.', 'Continuously Implement behavior flags tracking attendance, grades, and engagement to identify and intervene with at-risk students promptly.', ' conduct regular culture-sensitive activities that celebrate diversity, foster inclusion.', 'Mapping and targeted outreach', 'Launch info drives that offer blended delivery (modular/online)', 'Maintaining a consistently functional Child Protection Committee (CPC) that safeguards every learner from abuse, violence, and exploitation.', 'Maintaining a fully functional Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (DRRM) Plan that ensures the safety of students, staff, and facilities year-round', 'Capacity Building for Teachers on Mental Health Awareness and create a school mental health and wellness program with clear goals and policies.', 'Commit to maintaining fully accessible special education and PWD-friendly facilities that ensure equitable participation for all learners with disabilities.', 'Commitment to clear leadership and facilitation, transparency and validation.', 'Ensuring clear policies are followed, school leadership actively guides the team, stakeholders are regularly involved in decision‑making, and the school continuously fosters an inclusive and supportive community environment', 'Fostering active and meaningful participation in the Supreme Elementary Learner Government(SELG) and ensuring that all student leaders are supervised and mentored', 'Establish a standard response time policy (e.g., 24–48 hours).\r\nDesignate a frontline service team or help desk.\r\nUse tracking systems for monitoring requests and responses.', 'Commitment to clear leadership and facilitation,  transparency and validation', 'Strengthen participation, regularize meetings, build capacity, and institutionalize monitoring and governance practices.', 'Sustaining a strong and functional Parent‑Teacher Association by regularly convening meetings, promoting active and trusting parent participation, ensuring capable and trained PTA officers, practicing transparent use of resources, and maintaining strong linkages between the PTA and school programs and improvement plans.', ' Actively collaborate with stakeholders and other schools by fostering supportive leadership, establishing clear shared goals, encouraging meaningful stakeholder participation', 'Regularly monitoring and evaluating its programs, projects, and activities through committed leadership, organized data‑gathering and reporting systems, standardized tools, and a culture that consistently uses results to identify gaps, make adjustments, and improve school performance.', 'The school commits to supporting school personnel in achieving an average rating of “VS” in the IPCRF by ensuring clear performance standards, providing regular coaching and mentoring, consistently monitoring targets, giving timely feedback, and fostering a supportive school culture that promotes professional growth, accountability, and continuous improvement.', 'Improving its performance and achieving an average rating of “Very Satisfactory” in the Office Performance Commitment and Review by ensuring clear performance standards, providing strong leadership oversight, giving regular feedback and coaching, keeping reliable documentation of office outputs, and fostering a culture of accountability, teamwork.', 'School heads\' sustained leadership in organizing and monitoring sessions, teachers\' active participation through collaborative problem-solving and reflection on PPST-aligned needs assessments, collective dedication to SIP goals via protected time and MOOE-funded resources', 'The commitment to strong administrative support and access to diverse CPD activities like INSETs, LACs, mentoring, coaching, online learning, and action research, alongside teacher motivation tied to career advancement, involves school heads actively prioritizing resources, time, and opportunities', 'The commitment to administrative allocation from MOOE or special funds for awards, transparent IPCRF/PPST-aligned criteria, and established ceremonies fostering appreciation involves school heads actively budgeting and prioritizing recognition ', 'Ensuring teachers maintaining updated service records and accurate DTRs for STEP increments and allowances', ' Ensuring transparent allocation policies prioritizing teacher specialization and class sizes, along with workload audits balancing teaching with preparation/remediation tasks', 'Actively involving parents and staff in hands-on inspections while documenting issues immediately via photos or simple forms, and promptly allocating MOOE funds for fixes before small problems escalate into safety risks or major expenses', 'school heads consistently integrating infrastructure upgrades into annual SIP targets with clear timelines and budgets, actively monitoring progress through monthly walk-throughs.', 'Conduct a library needs assessment and inventory.\r\nAcquire updated, relevant, and curriculum-aligned books.\r\nSeek support from stakeholders for book donations and resource augmentation.', 'Upgrade to a higher bandwidth internet plan.\r\nInstall Wi-Fi access points across the campus.\r\nPartner with service providers or stakeholders for improved connectivity.', 'Improve internet bandwidth and connectivity.\r\nInstall reliable routers and network systems.\r\nProvide offline resources when internet is unavailable.', 'School strategic MOOE alignment with AIP priorities, proactive planning by school heads, transparent documentation and reporting, and PTA partnerships through  actively engaging parents through regular PTA meetings ', 'The entire school finance team prioritizing liquidation over other tasks to ensure prompt replenishment and avoid delays in next month\'s MOOE release.', 'Conduct regular satisfaction surveys (quarterly/annual).\r\nAnalyze results to identify weak areas and implement targeted improvement plans.\r\nSet clear performance benchmarks for satisfaction ratings.', 1, 15, 12, 61),
