(399, '2026', '3042229', '', '', 'Strong support from ALS implementers, effective learning delivery modalities, and continuous monitoring enable learners to successfully attain certification.', 'Limited time, resources, and capacity of teachers hinder the consistent development of high-quality contextualized learning materials.', '', '', '', '', 'Underreporting of bullying incidents due to fear, lack of awareness, or ineffective reporting mechanisms may affect the accurate monitoring of school safety.', 'Possible underreporting and limited detection of child abuse cases due to learners’ fear, stigma, and lack of awareness of reporting procedures may hinder accurate monitoring.', 'Persistent factors such as poverty, family responsibilities, and limited learner engagement still pose risks of dropout despite improved retention efforts.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Learners demonstrate low mastery of higher-order thinking skills (HOTS), particularly in analysis, critical thinking, and problem-solving, which significantly affects their performance in the National Achievement Test (NAT).', '', '', 'Teachers’ strong commitment, use of varied remediation strategies, and regular monitoring of learner progress effectively support the conduct of remediation activities.', 'Teachers’ strong value orientation, consistent modeling of behavior, and integration of peace education in daily lessons effectively promote DepEd core values among learners.', 'The regular practice of test item analysis is supported by teachers’ familiarity with assessment tools, established school data systems, and strong instructional leadership that promotes data-driven decision-making.', 'Strong partnerships with local industries, active stakeholder engagement, and responsive school-industry collaboration enable the continuous ', '', '', '', 'Strong respect for diversity, active stakeholder participation, and integration of cultural awareness in school programs support the consistent conduct of culture-sensitive activities.', 'Strong inclusive education policies, committed ALS implementers, and active community support enable continuous access to learning opportunities for disadvantaged, out-of-school youth, and adult learners.', 'Limited resources, irregular attendance of learners, and constrained availability of trained ALS implementers may affect the full optimization of the school-based ALS program.', 'Strong school leadership support, clear child protection policies, and active collaboration among committee members ensure the effective functioning of the Child Protection Committee.', 'Strong coordination among stakeholders, regular DRRM training and drills, and clear implementation of safety protocols support the effective functioning of the school DRRM plan.', 'Strong collaboration among guidance personnel, trained teachers, and stakeholders, along with increasing awareness on mental health, supports the effective implementation of mental wellness programs.', 'Strong adherence to inclusive education policies, stakeholder support, and existing accessible facility provisions enable the continuous implementation of SPED- and PWD-friendly facilities.', 'Strong leadership, collaborative stakeholder participation, and data-informed decision-making support the effective development of the school strategic plan.', 'Strong collaboration between school leaders, teachers, and community stakeholders ensures active participation and effective functioning of the school-community planning team.', 'Strong student leadership, active faculty advisers, and supportive school administration enable the effective functioning of the Supreme Student Government/Supreme Pupil Government.', 'Limited resources, varying staff ICT skills, and inconsistent standardization of processes may hinder the full optimization of innovative frontline service delivery.', 'Strong instructional leadership, clear alignment of goals, and active participation of stakeholders support the effective operationalization of the school’s strategic plan through an implementation plan.', 'Strong collaboration among school leaders, teachers, parents, and community stakeholders ensures the active and effective functioning of the School Governance Council (SGC).', 'Strong parent engagement, active school leadership support, and shared commitment to learner development ensure the effective functioning of the Parent-Teacher Association (PTA).', 'Strong stakeholder engagement, shared goals, and established networks with partner schools and organizations support effective collaboration in strengthening partnerships.', 'Strong leadership support, established M&E systems, and active participation of stakeholders enable the effective monitoring and evaluation of school programs, projects, and activities.', 'Consistent service delivery, responsive school leadership, and active stakeholder engagement contribute to maintaining a satisfactory rating from internal and external stakeholders.', 'Strong performance management systems, clear targets in the IPCRF, and continuous coaching and feedback from supervisors enable school personnel to achieve very satisfactory ratings.', 'teamwork, effective planning and implementation of office targets, and consistent performance monitoring contribute to achieving a very satisfactory rating in the Office Performance Commitment and Review (OPCRF).', 'Supportive school leadership; availability of LAC framework from Department of Education (Philippines)', 'Strong instructional leadership, identified teacher development needs, and collaborative professional learning culture support the effective conduct of needs-based LAC sessions and L&D activities.', 'Strong school leadership support, established recognition systems, and a culture of appreciation motivate the consistent recognition and rewarding of personnel milestone achievements.', 'Efficient administrative processes, strong coordination with the finance office, and reliable payroll systems ensure the timely and accurate release of salaries, allowances, and other compensation.', 'Transparent workload planning, collaborative scheduling, and adherence to DepEd guidelines on teaching assignments support the fair and equitable distribution of teacher workload.', 'Regular maintenance schedules, strong leadership oversight, and coordination with relevant stakeholders support the consistent inspection of school infrastructure and facilities.', 'Strong leadership initiative, stakeholder support, and availability of improvement plans and funding proposals enable the continuous enhancement of school infrastructure and facilities.', 'Strong support from school leadership, availability of learning resources, and active utilization by learners and teachers ensure the effective functioning of the school library.', 'Strong coordination with service providers, regular maintenance, and allocated resources ensure the continuous functionality of water, electricity, and internet facilities in the school.', 'Availability of ICT resources, regular maintenance, and integration of technology in teaching and learning support the effective functionality of the computer laboratory/classroom.', 'Efficient budget planning, timely procurement processes, and strong financial monitoring systems ensure the optimal utilization of the school’s MOOE.', 'Strict compliance with accounting and auditing rules, timely submission of supporting documents, and effective coordination between school and finance personnel ensure 100% liquidation of MOOE.', 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 6, 6, 2, 2, 2, 6, 5, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, '', 'The school commits to strengthening targeted interventions, data-driven instruction, and continuous teacher capacity-building to ensure all learners achieve the desired proficiency level in the NAT.', 'The school commits to sustaining quality ALS implementation through strengthened instruction, learner support, and regular assessment to ensure continued certification success.', 'The school commits to providing continuous capacity-building, sufficient resources, and collaborative planning time to support teachers in developing effective contextualized learning materials.', 'The school commits to sustaining and enhancing remediation programs through continuous teacher training, provision of appropriate materials, and data-driven interventions to address learning gaps.', 'To continuously strengthen values integration through sustained teacher development, enriched learning materials, and consistent reinforcement of peace and core values in all learning areas.', 'Strengthen teachers’ capacity through training on test item analysis and provide dedicated time for collaborative data review to ensure results are effectively used to enhance teaching and learning.', 'The school commits to sustaining and expanding industry linkages through continuous partnership building, alignment of TLE-TVL competencies with labor market needs, and regular stakeholder collaboration.', 'The school commits to strengthening child protection mechanisms, improving reporting systems, and promoting a safe and supportive school environment to ensure all bullying incidents are properly addressed.', 'To strengthening child protection policies, intensifying awareness campaigns, and ensuring safe, confidential reporting mechanisms to protect learners from all forms of abuse.', 'The school commits to sustaining and strengthening retention programs, targeted learner support, and community partnerships to further reduce dropout incidence.', 'The school commits to continuously promote inclusivity by strengthening culture-sensitive programs, engaging diverse communities, and integrating cultural respect in all learning activities.', 'The school commits to sustaining inclusive and flexible learning opportunities by strengthening outreach programs, stakeholder partnerships, and learner-centered delivery modalities for all marginalized groups.', 'The school commits to strengthening the school-based ALS program through sustained resource support, capacity-building of implementers, and enhanced learner tracking and engagement strategies.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen the Child Protection Committee through regular monitoring, capacity-building, and proactive implementation of child protection policies to ensure learner safety and well-being.', 'To continuously strengthen its DRRM plan through regular updating, capacity-building, and strict implementation of safety measures to ensure preparedness and resilience.', 'To strengthening mental wellness support mechanisms through continuous capacity-building, accessible psychosocial services, and sustained awareness programs for learners and staff.', 'Improvie accessibility and inclusivity by continuously upgrading facilities, ensuring compliance with universal design standards, and strengthening support services for learners with special needs.', 'continuously strengthen strategic planning through inclusive stakeholder engagement, evidence-based planning, and regular monitoring and evaluation for sustained school improvement.', 'Sustain and strnthen  the school-community planning team through continuous stakeholder engagement, participatory planning processes, and collaborative implementation of school programs and projects.', 'continuously develop student leadership by strengthening the SSG/SPG through capacity-building, active participation in school governance, and meaningful involvement in school programs and decision-making.', 'strengthen innovative frontline services through continuous staff development, improved systems and resources, and standardization of processes to ensure efficient and responsive service delivery.', 'continuously strengthen the implementation of its strategic plan through regular monitoring, data-driven adjustments, and sustained stakeholder collaboration to ensure achievement of school goals.', 'Continuously strengthen the School Governance Council through inclusive participation, regular consultations, and collaborative decision-making to support effective school governance and improvement.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen the PTA through sustained collaboration, transparent communication, and active involvement in school programs and learner support initiatives.', 'expand and sustain partnerships through active collaboration, regular coordination, and mutually beneficial programs with stakeholders and other schools.', 'continuously strengthen its monitoring and evaluation system through data-driven assessment, regular feedback mechanisms, and evidence-based decision-making for school improvement.', 'Sustain high performance by strengthening performance monitoring, providing continuous professional development, and fostering a culture of accountability and excellence among personnel.', 'The school commits to continuously improve office performance through collaborative goal setting, data-driven management, and sustained quality service delivery aligned with OPCRF targets.', 'Conduct regular training needs analysis (TNA); prepare structured LAC plans; ensure protected time for LAC sessions; monitor attendance and outputs', 'The school commits to continuously enhance teacher competencies through sustained, data-driven LAC sessions and targeted professional development activities aligned with learner needs and school priorities.', 'To continuously uphold a culture of recognition by systematically acknowledging personnel achievements and providing meaningful incentives to sustain', 'strengthen payroll monitoring and coordination with relevant offices to ensure the timely, accurate, and transparent release of personnel compensation.', 'The school commits to continuously ensure fair and equitable workload distribution through data-driven planning, regular review of assignments, and participatory decision-making among school leaders and teachers.', 'to continuously conduct regular inspection and maintenance of infrastructure and facilities to ensure safety, functionality, and a conducive learning environment.', 'The school commits to continuously upgrade and improve infrastructure and facilities through strategic planning, resource mobilization, and strong stakeholder collaboration to ensure a safe and conducive learning environment.', 'The school commits to continuously enhance and sustain a functional library through resource upgrading, improved management systems, and promotion of reading culture among learners and staff.', 'The school commits to continuously maintain and improve its water, electric, and internet facilities through regular monitoring, timely repairs, and strengthened partnerships with utility providers to support uninterrupted learning.', 'to continuously enhance the computer laboratory through upgrading ICT equipment, improving access and utilization, and strengthening digital literacy programs for learners and teachers.', 'The school commits to continuously ensure efficient, transparent, and timely utilization of MOOE funds through strict budget monitoring, compliance with procurement guidelines, and needs-based financial planning.', 'The school commits to continuously uphold full compliance in financial reporting by ensuring timely, accurate, and complete liquidation of all MOOE expenditures in accordance with COA regulations.', 'The school commits to continuously improve performance and stakeholder satisfaction through quality assurance measures, regular feedback utilization, and sustained service enhancement initiatives.', 1, 44, 12, 58),
(400, '2026', '128597', '', 'Low NAT performance in key learning areas (English, Mathematics, Science, and other core subjects)\r\nLearners’ difficulty in applying 21st century skills such as critical thinking, collaboration, and problem-solving\r\nUneven academic performance across different grade levels and sections', 'The school has no School-based ALS learners enrolment', '', '', '', '', 'Lack of formalized Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) with industry partners', '', '', '', '', 'Limited identification and profiling of Out-of-School Youths (OSYs) and adult learners in the community\r\nInadequate awareness of ALS programs and enrollment opportunities among target learners\r\nLack of structured and updated database of disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adults\r\nLimited learning materials and modules tailored for diverse learner backgrounds and levels', 'TThe school has no established or functional school-based ALS program', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'The school shall continuously conduct needs-based Learning Action Cells (LACs) aligned with identified teacher development needs and learner performance gaps.\r\nLAC sessions shall be planned, structured, and based on data such as assessment results, classroom observations, and NAT performance.\r\nThe school shall ensure active participation of all teachers in LAC and Learning & Development (L&D) activities.', 'Limited availability of training opportunities due to budget constraints\r\nScheduling conflicts affecting attendance in professional development activities\r\nInadequate number of slots for seminars, trainings, and scholarships\r\nLack of awareness or information dissemination on available training programs', '', '', '', 'Limited budget for regular repair, maintenance, and upgrading of school facilities\r\nIncomplete or outdated documentation of infrastructure inspection reports\r\nInsufficient tools and technical expertise for thorough facility inspection\r\nDelay in repair and maintenance due to procurement and approval processes', 'Limited budget allocation for major infrastructure improvement projects\r\nDelays in approval and implementation of infrastructure-related proposals\r\nAging and deteriorating school buildings requiring extensive repair and upgrading\r\nLack of technical designs, plans, or feasibility studies for improvement projects', 'Limited updated and relevant reading materials, references, and learning resources\r\nInsufficient budget for acquisition of books, journals, and library materials\r\nInadequate library space and seating capacity for learners', '', 'Outdated hardware and software affecting performance and usability', '', '', 'Low reading comprehension and numeracy performance among some learners\r\nLimited parental support in reinforcing skills at home', '', '', 'Strong teacher understanding of learners’ needs, interests, and learning levels\r\nAvailability of DepEd curriculum guides and MELCs as basis for contextualization\r\nSupportive school leadership encouraging innovation in instructional materials\r\nRegular LAC sessions focused on material development and sharing of best practices', 'Strong use of assessment results (formative, summative, and diagnostic) to identify learning gaps\r\nRegular monitoring of learners’ performance by teachers and school heads\r\nAvailability of intervention and remediation materials aligned with MELCs\r\nDedicated time allocation for remediation activities within school schedules', 'Strong understanding and consistent application of DepEd Core Values (Maka-Diyos, Makatao, Makakalikasan, Makabansa)\r\nIntegration of peace education and values formation in daily lesson plans and learning activities\r\nSupportive school leadership promoting character formation and positive discipline\r\nRegular LAC sessions focusing on values integration and classroom application strategies', 'Regular administration of formative, summative, and quarterly assessments aligned with MELCs\r\nStrong teacher competence in test construction and assessment literacy\r\nAvailability of standardized templates and tools for item analysis\r\nUse of data-driven instruction to guide teaching strategies and interventions', '', 'Strong implementation of Child Protection Policy (DepEd Order No. 40, s. 2012)\r\nActive school Child Protection Committee (CPC) monitoring learner behavior and cases\r\nRegular conduct of values formation and peace education activities\r\nEffective classroom management and positive discipline practices by teachers', 'Strict implementation of the Child Protection Policy (DepEd Order No. 40, s. 2012)\r\nActive Child Protection Committee (CPC) with clear roles and monitoring system\r\nStrong coordination between school, parents, LGU, and barangay officials for child protection\r\nRegular orientation and awareness campaigns on child abuse prevention and reporting mechanisms', 'Strong implementation of learner tracking and monitoring system (attendance and performance records)\r\nEarly identification of at-risk learners through class advisers and guidance personnel', 'Strong awareness and respect for cultural diversity among teachers and learners\r\nIntegration of culture-based education in lesson planning and classroom activities', '', '', 'Strict implementation of DepEd Child Protection Policy (DepEd Order No. 40, s. 2012)\r\nClear composition, roles, and responsibilities of the Child Protection Committee (CPC) members\r\nStrong commitment and active participation of school heads, teachers, and guidance personnel\r\nRegular monitoring and reporting of child protection concerns and cases', 'Strong compliance with DepEd DRRM policies and guidelines\r\nActive School DRRM Committee with defined roles and responsibilities\r\nRegular updating and review of the school DRRM plan\r\nConduct of periodic drills (fire, earthquake, evacuation, etc.)', 'Availability of trained guidance counselor or designated guidance focal person\r\nStrong implementation of