ponsibilities\r\nRegular and well-organized SGC meetings with active attendance and participation\r\nStrong school leadership promoting shared governance and stakeholder engagement', 'Strong participation and commitment of parents and guardians in school activities\r\nRegular conduct of PTA meetings and assemblies with active attendance\r\nClear understanding of PTA roles, functions, and responsibilities\r\nStrong collaboration between teachers, school leaders, and parents', 'Strong support from school leadership in establishing and sustaining partnerships\r\nActive engagement of stakeholders (LGU, PTA, SGC, community organizations, private partners)\r\nEstablished culture of collaboration and shared responsibility among schools and partners\r\nRegular coordination meetings, consultations, and joint planning activities', 'Strong implementation of monitoring and evaluation (M&E) system in the school\r\nClear assignment of roles and responsibilities for program implementers and monitors\r\nRegular conduct of program reviews, progress monitoring, and evaluation activities\r\nAvailability of updated data and reports for evidence-based decision-making', 'Strong commitment of school leadership to quality service and stakeholder satisfaction\r\nEffective implementation of frontline services following DepEd Citizen’s Charter\r\nRegular feedback mechanisms (surveys, consultations, suggestion forms)\r\nPositive relationship and strong communication between school and stakeholders', 'Clear performance targets aligned with DepEd Key Result Areas (KRAs) and individual duties\r\nStrong understanding of IPCRF guidelines and performance standards among personnel\r\nRegular coaching, mentoring, and performance monitoring by school heads\r\nContinuous professional development and training opportunities for teachers and staff', 'Clear alignment of school goals and office targets with DepEd Key Result Areas (KRAs)\r\nStrong leadership and effective school management practices\r\nRegular monitoring, evaluation, and coaching of school performance outputs\r\nCollaborative planning among school heads, teachers, and administrative personnel', '', '', 'Strong support from school leadership in promoting a culture of recognition and appreciation\r\nEstablished recognition system for outstanding performance, milestones, and achievements\r\nRegular conduct of awarding ceremonies during school programs and meetings\r\nClear criteria and guidelines for recognizing personnel accomplishments', 'Strong coordination between school, division office, and payroll/unit for timely processing of salaries and benefits\r\nAccurate and updated personnel records and payroll information\r\nCompliance with government accounting and auditing rules and regulations\r\nEfficient submission of required documents and reports by school personnel', 'Strong and supportive school leadership ensuring fair assignment of duties and responsibilities\r\nClear workload distribution guidelines aligned with DepEd policies and standards\r\nCollaborative planning among school heads and teachers in assigning teaching loads and ancillary tasks\r\nRegular review and adjustment of workloads based on teacher capacity and school needs\r\nTransparent assignment of committee roles and school responsibilities', '', '', '', 'Reliable support from LGU and utility providers ensuring continuous basic services\r\nStrong school maintenance system for water, electrical, and internet facilities\r\nRegular monitoring and inspection of utility systems to ensure functionality', '', 'Strong financial management and planning by school leadership\r\nClear understanding and compliance with DepEd budgeting and procurement guidelines\r\nTimely submission of liquidation reports and financial documents\r\nRegular monitoring of budget utilization and fund allocation', 'Strong adherence to DepEd financial policies, accounting, and auditing rules and regulations\r\nEfficient and organized financial documentation system for all transactions\r\nTimely submission of liquidation reports and supporting documents\r\nCompetent and trained personnel handling school financial management and liquidation processes', 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 2, 3, 3, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 'Implementation of structured remediation programs (e.g., reading recovery, numeracy drills, pull-out sessions) for struggling learners.', 'Strengthen data-driven instruction by regularly analyzing NAT, formative, and summative assessment results to guide teaching strategies and interventions.\r\nIntensify NAT review and remediation programs at the school level, focusing on least mastered competencies and high-impact learning areas.\r\nIntegrate 21st century skills (critical thinking, communication, collaboration, creativity, and ICT literacy) in daily lesson plans and classroom activities.\r\nConduct regular teacher training and upskilling on assessment literacy, test-taking strategies, and effective review techniques.', 'Strengthen intensified ALS review and certification preparation programs for elementary level', 'The school shall ensure that teachers continuously develop and use contextualized learning materials aligned with learners’ needs and the MELCs.\r\nTeachers shall integrate local culture, community experiences, and real-life situations in the development of instructional materials.\r\nRegular LAC sessions shall be conducted to support collaboration and sharing of best practices in material development.', 'The school shall institutionalize regular remediation programs to address identified learning gaps in reading, comprehension, Science and Technology, and Mathematics.\r\nTeachers shall utilize assessment results as basis for planning targeted remediation and intervention activities.', 'The school shall ensure the continuous integration of peace education and DepEd Core Values (Maka-Diyos, Makatao, Makakalikasan, Makabansa) in all learning areas.\r\nTeachers shall consistently incorporate values formation and peace-promoting topics in daily lesson plans and classroom activities.', 'The school shall ensure the regular conduct of test item analysis after formative, summative, and quarterly assessments.\r\nTeachers shall utilize item analysis results as basis for instructional planning, remediation, and enrichment activities.\r\nThe school shall strengthen data-driven instruction by integrating assessment results in teaching strategies.', 'The school shall initiate and formalize Memoranda of Agreement (MOA) with identified industry partners to sustain collaboration.', 'The school shall strictly implement the Child Protection Policy (DepEd Order No. 40, s. 2012) to ensure a safe and child-friendly learning environment.\r\nThe Child Protection Committee (CPC) shall continuously monitor and address any potential bullying-related concerns.\r\nThe school shall strengthen awareness campaigns on anti-bullying, child rights, and positive behavior among learners, parents, and staff.', 'The school shall strictly enforce the Child Protection Policy (DepEd Order No. 40, s. 2012) to ensure the safety and well-being of all learners.\r\nThe Child Protection Committee (CPC) shall be strengthened to continuously monitor, report, and address child protection concerns.', 'The school shall strengthen its learner tracking and monitoring system to regularly identify and support at-risk learners.\r\nClass advisers and guidance personnel shall conduct early intervention strategies for learners showing signs of absenteeism or disengagement.', 'The school shall consistently integrate culture-sensitive and inclusive activities in school programs, lessons, and events.\r\nTeachers shall incorporate local culture, traditions, and Indigenous Peoples (IP) practices in instructional activities when applicable.', 'The school shall strengthen the identification and profiling of Out-of-School Youths (OSYs), disadvantaged, and adult learners in coordination with barangay and LGU officials.\r\nThe school shall intensify advocacy and information dissemination on ALS programs and alternative learning opportunities.\r\nA comprehensive and updated database of OSYs and adult learners shall be developed and regularly maintained.', 'The school’s school-based ALS program is not functional.”', 'The school shall continuously strengthen the Child Protection Committee (CPC) to ensure effective implementation of child protection policies and programs.\r\nThe CPC shall regularly conduct meetings, monitoring, and evaluation of child protection concerns and interventions.', 'The school shall continuously implement, update, and strengthen its Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (DRRM) Plan in accordance with DepEd guidelines.\r\nThe School DRRM Committee shall conduct regular monitoring, evaluation, and updating of the DRRM plan to ensure relevance and effectiveness.\r\nRegular conduct of emergency drills (fire, earthquake, evacuation, and other hazards) shall be strictly implemented and documented.', 'The school shall strengthen its guidance and counseling program to ensure continuous support for learners’ mental health and well-being.\r\nMental health awareness activities, orientations, and campaigns shall be regularly conducted for learners, parents, and school personnel.', 'The school shall continuously maintain and improve SPED and PWD-friendly facilities to ensure accessibility and inclusivity for all learners.\r\nThe school shall strictly comply with DepEd inclusive education policies and standards for learners with special needs.', 'The school shall continuously develop, implement, and update its Strategic Improvement Plan (SIP) aligned with DepEd goals and learner needs.\r\nSchool stakeholders (teachers, PTA, SGC, and LGU) shall be actively engaged in the planning, review, and validation of the strategic plan.', 'The school shall continuously strengthen the School-Community Planning Team to ensure active and meaningful participation of stakeholders in school planning processes.\r\nRegular planning meetings, consultations, and validation sessions shall be conducted with PTA, SGC, LGU, and other community partners.', 'The school shall continuously strengthen the Supreme Student Government (SSG) / Supreme Pupil Government (SPG) to ensure active and meaningful student participation in school governance.\r\nRegular elections, assemblies, and organizational meetings shall be conducted in accordance with DepEd policies and guidelines.', 'The school shall continuously improve and innovate its frontline services to ensure efficiency, accessibility, and stakeholder satisfaction.', 'The school shall ensure that the Strategic Improvement Plan (SIP) is effectively translated into a clear and actionable Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).\r\nAll programs, projects, and activities (PPAs) shall be implemented in accordance with the approved implementation plan and school priorities.', 'The school shall continuously strengthen the functionality of the School Governance Council (SGC) through active participation of all stakeholders.\r\nRegular and well-organized meetings shall be conducted to ensure effective planning, monitoring, and evaluation of school programs.', 'The school shall continuously strengthen the functionality of the Parent-Teacher Association (PTA) through regular meetings and active participation of parents and guardians.\r\nPTA officers and members shall actively participate in school planning, implementation, and evaluation of programs, projects, and activities.', 'The school shall continuously strengthen collaboration with stakeholders and partner schools to support quality education and school improvement.\r\nRegular coordination meetings, consultations, and joint planning activities shall be conducted with stakeholders and partner institutions.\r\nThe school shall actively engage LGU, PTA, SGC, and community partners in implementing school programs, projects, and activities.', 'The school shall continuously strengthen its Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) system to ensure effective implementation of all programs, projects, and activities.\r\nRegular monitoring activities shall be conducted to track progress and ensure alignment with SIP and AIP targets.', 'The school shall ensure that all personnel set clear, measurable, and aligned performance targets based on DepEd KRAs and organizational priorities.\r\nRegular coaching, mentoring, and performance monitoring shall be conducted by school heads to support continuous improvement.', 'Strong culture of collaboration, sharing of best practices, and peer learning\r\nSupport from DepEd supervisors in providing technical assistance and guidance', 'School leadership shall provide full support in scheduling, facilitating, and monitoring LAC implementation.\r\nTeachers shall apply LAC learnings in classroom instruction to improve teaching strategies and learner outcomes.', 'The school shall strengthen the implementation of a continuous professional development (CPD) plan for all personnel aligned with DepEd priorities and individual needs.\r\nThe school shall ensure equal access to training opportunities, seminars, and capacity-building activities for all personnel.', 'Personnel achievements and milestones shall be properly documented and validated as basis for recognition.\r\nThe school shall allocate appropriate resources to support awards, tokens, and recognition incentives.', 'The school shall ensure the timely and accurate submission of payroll-related documents and requirements to the concerned offices.\r\nRegular coordination shall be maintained with the Division Office and finance units to ensure correct and prompt release of salaries and benefits.The school shall maintain accurate and updated personnel records to avoid delays and discrepancies in payroll processing.', 'The school shall ensure fair and equitable distribution of teaching loads and ancillary duties in accordance with DepEd policies and guidelines.\r\nWorkload assignments shall be based on data such as class size, subject specialization, and teacher capacity.', 'The school shall conduct regular and systematic inspection of all school infrastructure and facilities to ensure safety and functionality.\r\nA designated inspection team or committee shall be strengthened to regularly assess the condition of school facilities.', 'The school shall develop and implement a long-term infrastructure improvement plan aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP).\r\nPriority infrastructure needs shall be identified, documented, and regularly updated based on safety and learning requirements', 'The school shall strengthen and maintain a functional library that supports teaching and learning needs.\r\nThe school shall allocate resources for the continuous acquisition of updated books, references, and learning materials.\r\nLibrary facilities shall be improved to ensure adequate space, seating, ventilation, and conducive learning environment.', 'The school shall ensure the continuous functionality and maintenance of water, electrical, and internet facilities to support effective teaching and learning.\r\nRegular monitoring and inspection of utility systems shall be conducted to prevent interruptions and ensure reliability.', 'The school shall allocate resources for the repair, upgrading, and maintenance of computer units and related equipment.', 'Regular monitoring and tracking of MOOE utilization shall be conducted to ensure optimal and appropriate use of funds.', 'The school shall ensure the timely and complete liquidation of all MOOE funds in accordance with DepEd financial policies and COA rules and regulations.\r\nProper documentation and record-keeping of all financial transactions shall be strictly observed to support accurate liquidation.', 'Strong collaboration with PTA, SGC, LGU, and community stakeholders shall be maintained to address concerns and expectations.', 1, 35, 12, 58),
