(418, '2026', '128626', 'arying learning abilities of learners, lack of parental support and involvement', 'low mastery of fundamental competencies, absenteeism.', 'irregular attendance of ALS learners, diverse learning levels and backgrounds of ALS learners.', '', '', '', '', 'limited partnership with local industries and establishments', 'continuous monitoring of learner behavior, possible underreporting of bullying incidents, limited awareness among learners and parents about anti-bullying policies and reporting mechanisms', 'zero recorded child abuse incidence, the lack of full disclosure or reporting, as some cases of abuse may remain hidden due to fear, stigma, or lack of awareness among learners', 'economic difficulty of learners and families, low learner motivation and engagement,irregular attendance caused by distance, transportation issues, or health-related concerns.', '', '', '', '', '', 'limited number of trained personnel in mental health support, low level of awareness and openness among learners to seek help.', 'limited availability of complete PWD-friendly infrastructure, gap in specialized learning resources and assistive devices, the limited number of trained SPED teachers and personnel,', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'strong instructional leadership of school heads, continuous professional development of teachers through trainings, workshops, and Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions.', 'instructional leadership and monitoring, collaborative school culture,', 'instructional leadership and clear policy direction, Teachers’ commitment and understanding of DepEd core values , professional development activities such as LAC sessions, trainings, and seminars', 'The availability of standardized assessment tools and recording templates, strong instructional leadership and clear assessment policies,  collaborative culture among teachers.', '', '', '', '', 'Teachers awareness and appreciation of cultural diversity among learners, strong instructional leadership', 'strong inclusive school leadership, Teachers’ commitment to inclusive education and learner diversity, strong collaboration with community stakeholders, LGUs.', 'trong leadership and commitment of the school administration, trained and dedicated ALS teachers', 'strong school leadership and commitment to child safeguarding policies, clearly defined Child Protection Policy and school-based guidelines.', 'strong school leadership and commitment to safety and preparedness, Regular DRRM trainings, drills, and simulations.', '', '', 'strong school leadership and governance, Active stakeholder participation, collaborative planning activities and consultations among school personnel', 'strong school leadership and governance, ', 'strong school leadership and guidance, Active teacher-adviser support and mentoring, active participation and commitment of student officers and members.', 'strong school leadership and commitment to quality public service, adoption of technology-based systems and digital tools, collaboration and support from stakeholders', 'strong instructional leadership and governance, use of data-driven planning and decision-making, Active collaboration among school personnel and stakeholders', 'strong school leadership and governance, active engagement of stakeholders, Clear roles, responsibilities, and functions of SGC members.', 'strong school leadership and active partnership with parents, active participation and commitment of parents and guardians, strong collaboration and shared commitment of stakeholders', 'Strong school leadership and governance, Active engagement of stakeholders such as LGUs, parents, commitment and active participation of all partners', 'strong instructional leadership and governance, use of data-driven monitoring tools and evaluation instruments, Active participation of teachers and school personnel.', 'strong school leadership and responsive governance, implementation of effective communication and feedback mechanisms, Regular monitoring and improvement of school programs and services, Strong collaboration with parents, community members, and partner organizations.', 'strong school leadership and performance management systems,  implementation of results-based performance management, Regular coaching, mentoring, and performance feedback from school heads', 'strong school leadership and effective governance, Regular monitoring, coaching, and feedback from supervisors and school heads, the commitment, efficiency, and professionalism of school staff.', 'strong instructional leadership, use of data-driven assessment results and classroom observations, Active teacher participation and collaboration, Regular planning and coordination among school leaders and teachers', 'strong school leadership and effective human resource management, Regular capacity-building activities such as trainings, seminars, workshops, and Learning Action Cells, trong support and encouragement from school leaders', 'strong school leadership and governance,  clear recognition policies and DepEd guidelines on awards and incentives, positive and supportive school culture.', 'strong school leadership and efficient administrative management, use of standardized DepEd financial procedures and guidelines, Regular coordination with the Schools Division Office (SDO) and relevant government agencies.', 'strong school leadership and instructional supervision, Regular consultation and collaboration among school heads and teachers,  transparent planning and scheduling process.', 'strong school leadership and governance, Regular scheduled inspection activities and maintenance checks,  Strong coordination with LGUs, engineers, and other technical experts', 'strong school leadership and proactive governance, regular needs assessment and facility inspection results, school improvement planning and budgeting, Strong stakeholder participation and commu nity support', 'strong school leadership and commitment to literacy development, designated and competent library-in-charge or focal person, Strong integration of library use in classroom instruction.', 'strong school leadership and effective facilities management, proper utilization of school maintenance funds, Regular coordination with utility service providers.', 'strong school leadership and ICT-focused governance, designated ICT coordinator or laboratory-in-charge, integration of ICT in teaching and learning processes', 'strong school leadership and effective financial management, implementation of a well-prepared Annual Procurement Plan, Regular monitoring, tracking, and reporting of fund utilization, commitment to transparency and accountability in financial management.', 'strong school leadership and sound financial governance, Regular monitoring and internal checking of financial records, commitment of school leadership to transparency, accountability, and fiscal responsibility.', 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 'The school commits to ensuring that all Grade 3 learners achieve the required proficiency level in early language, literacy, and numeracy skills through the implementation of responsive and learner-centered strategies. Teachers will consistently apply differentiated instruction and provide targeted interventions such as remedial classes, small-group tutoring, and enrichment activities to address the diverse needs of learners.', 'The school will strengthen curriculum implementation by ensuring alignment of teaching strategies, learning competencies, and assessment practices with the standards and cognitive demands of the NAT. Teachers will integrate 21st century skills—critical thinking, communication, collaboration, and creativity—into daily lessons through interactive and meaningful learning activities.\r\n\r\nTeachers will also enhance assessment practices by conducting regular formative and summative assessments patterned after the NAT, including the use of higher-order thinking skills (HOTS) questions. Results of these assessments will be systematically analyzed to identify learning gaps and design targeted interventions such as remediation classes, tutorials, and enrichment programs.', 'The school will enhance flexible and learner-centered delivery of instruction by adapting teaching strategies that suit the diverse needs, schedules, and learning levels of ALS learners. Remedial sessions and differentiated activities will be provided to address gaps in foundational skills such as reading, writing, and numeracy. To address attendance issues, the school commits to implement flexible scheduling and continuous learner engagement strategies, including modular learning, catch-up sessions, and regular follow-ups to ensure consistent participation.', 'The school commits to sustaining the consistent development of contextualized learning materials by strengthening teacher collaboration, continuous professional development, and stakeholder support to ensure responsive, inclusive, and learner-centered instruction.', 'The school commits to sustaining effective remediation programs by strengthening data-driven instruction, enhancing teacher capacity, and ensuring continuous support from stakeholders to address learners’ gaps in reading, comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics.', 'The school commits to sustaining the integration of peace education and DepEd core values in all learning areas through continuous teacher development, strong instructional leadership, and collaborative efforts that promote a values-driven learning environment.', 'The school commits to sustaining the regular conduct and utilization of test item analysis to guide data-driven instruction, improve teaching strategies, and enhance learner performance through targeted interventions.', 'The school commits to strengthening partnerships with local industries through formalized agreements, improved coordination, and sustained collaboration to enhance TLE-TVL course offerings and provide learners with meaningful work-based learning opportunities and practical skills development.', 'The school commits to sustaining a safe and child-friendly environment by strengthening awareness on anti-bullying policies, improving monitoring and reporting mechanisms, and continuously promoting positive behavior among learners to maintain zero bullying incidence.', 'The school commits to sustaining a zero child abuse incidence by strengthening child protection policies, enhancing awareness among stakeholders, improving reporting and monitoring mechanisms, and continuously building the capacity of school personnel to ensure a safe, secure, and child-protected learning environment.', 'The school commits to further reducing drop-out incidence by strengthening early identification and monitoring of at-risk learners, intensifying intervention programs, and enhancing collaboration with parents and stakeholders to ensure learner retention and completion.', 'The school commits to sustaining culture-sensitive activities by promoting inclusivity, strengthening teacher capacity, and fostering active stakeholder engagement to ensure respect for cultural diversity in all school programs and learning experiences.', 'The school commits to sustaining inclusive access to learning by strengthening ALS implementation, enhancing stakeholder partnerships, and providing flexible, contextualized learning opportunities for disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adult learners.', 'The school commits to sustaining a functional School-Based ALS program through strong leadership, continuous capacity building of implementers, stakeholder collaboration, and provision of flexible and contextualized learning opportunities for ALS learners.', 'The school commits to sustaining a functional Child Protection Committee by strengthening policy implementation, enhancing stakeholder collaboration, and ensuring continuous monitoring and capacity building to guarantee a safe and child-protected learning environment.', 'The school commits to sustaining a functional DRRM Plan by strengthening preparedness measures, enhancing coordination with partner agencies, conducting regular drills, and continuously improving safety and risk reduction practices to ensure a safe learning environment.', 'The school commits to strengthening its mental wellness support mechanism by enhancing the capacity of personnel, improving access to counseling and psychosocial services, increasing learner awareness, and strengthening partnerships with external mental health professionals to ensure continuous and responsive support for learners’ well-being.', 'The school commits to strengthening special education and PWD-friendly facilities by improving accessibility infrastructure, providing assistive learning resources, enhancing teacher capacity, and securing stakeholder support to ensure an inclusive and equitable learning environment for all learners.', 'The school commits to sustaining the development of a strategic plan through data-driven planning, stakeholder engagement, and strong leadership to ensure continuous school improvement and achievement of educational goals.', 'he school commits to sustaining a functional School-Community Planning Team through strong collaboration, data-driven decision-making, and active stakeholder engagement to ensure responsive and effective school planning and development.', 'The school commits to sustaining a functional Supreme Student/Pupil Government by strengthening leadership development, providing continuous mentoring, and promoting active student participation in school governance and activities.', 'The school commits to sustaining innovation in frontline services by strengthening digital systems, improving service processes, and promoting a responsive and customer-friendly environment for all stakeholders.', 'The school commits to sustaining the effective operationalization of its strategic plan through a well-structured implementation plan, data-driven monitoring, and strong stakeholder collaboration to ensure continuous school improvement.', 'The school commits to sustaining a functional School Governance Council through active stakeholder engagement, collaborative decision-making, and data-driven governance to support continuous school improvement and learner success.', 'The school commits to sustaining a functional Parent-Teacher Association through active collaboration, open communication, and shared responsibility in supporting school programs and promoting learner success.', 'The school commits to sustaining strong collaboration with stakeholders and partner schools by strengthening linkages, promoting shared initiatives, and ensuring continuous support for improved teaching, learning, and school development.', 'The school commits to sustaining effective monitoring and evaluation of all programs, projects, and activities through data-driven processes, stakeholder engagement, and continuous improvement strategies to ensure achievement of school goals.', 'The school commits to sustaining a very satisfactory performance rating among personnel by strengthening performance management systems, providing continuous professional development, and promoting a culture of excellence and accountability.', 'The school commits to sustaining a very satisfactory OPCRF rating by strengthening performance management, enhancing teamwork, and ensuring efficient, transparent, and results-driven office operations.', 'The school commits to sustaining needs-based LAC and Learning and Development activities by strengthening data-driven planning, promoting teacher collaboration, and ensuring continuous professional growth aligned with instructional needs and school improvement goals.', 'The school commits to sustaining the promotion and continuous professional development of its personnel by strengthening leadership support, enhancing capacity-building programs, and promoting a culture of lifelong learning and professional growth.', 'The school commits to sustaining the recognition and rewarding of personnel achievements by promoting a culture of appreciation, ensuring fair and transparent processes, and continuously motivating staff toward excellence and professional growth.', 'The school commits to sustaining the timely and accurate release of salaries, allowances, and other compensation by ensuring efficient financial management, adherence to DepEd guidelines, and strong coordination with relevant offices.', 'The school commits to sustaining fair and equitable distribution of teacher workload by adhering to DepEd guidelines, promoting transparent consultation, and ensuring balanced assignment of tasks to support teacher well-being and instructional effectiveness.', 'The school commits to sustaining regular inspection of infrastructure and facilities by ensuring systematic monitoring, stakeholder collaboration, and continuous maintenance to provide a safe and conducive learning environment.', 'The school commits to sustaining infrastructure and facility improvements through data-driven planning, strong stakeholder collaboration, and continuous allocation of resources to ensure a safe and conducive learning environment.', 'The school commits to sustaining a functional library by improving access to learning resources, strengthening literacy programs, and ensuring continuous enhancement of library services for learners and teachers.', 'The school commits to sustaining functional water, electric, and internet facilities through regular maintenance, efficient resource management, and strong coordination with service providers to support effective teaching and learning.', 'The school commits to sustaining a functional computer laboratory/classroom through proper maintenance, ICT integration in instruction, and continuous improvement of digital learning resources to enhance teaching and learning outcomes.', 'The school commits to sustaining efficient utilization of MOOE funds by strengthening financial planning, ensuring compliance with procurement guidelines, and promoting transparent and needs-based resource allocation.', 'The school commits to sustaining 100% liquidation of MOOE by ensuring strict compliance with financial guidelines, maintaining complete documentation, and strengthening transparent and accountable financial management practices.', 'The school commits to sustaining a satisfactory rating from stakeholders by continuously improving service delivery, strengthening feedback mechanisms, and promoting responsive and transparent school governance.', 0, 43, 12, 58),
