(463, '2026', '128958', 'Limited conduciveness of the learning environment for effective language, literacy, and numeracy development', 'Limited mastery of competencies, insufficient remediation programs, and inconsistent learner attendance', 'N/A', 'Limited availability of instructional resources and insufficient time for teachers to develop contextualized and localized learning materials.', 'Some learners continue to exhibit learning gaps despite remediation efforts due to irregular attendance and limited remediation time.', 'Integration of peace education and core values is not consistently emphasized across all learning areas.', '', 'N/A', '', '', '', 'Limited implementation of culture‑based and indigenous learning activities due to lack of training and instructional materials.', 'The school has no established program or mechanism to reach and support OSYs, adult learners, and other disadvantaged groups.', 'N/A', '', '', 'Limited mental health programs and absence of trained personnel to address learners’ and teachers’ mental wellness concerns.', 'Lack of PWD‑friendly infrastructure and insufficient resources to support learners with special education needs.School personnel are aware of inclusive education principles and are willing to support initiatives for learners ', 'Strategic planning is not consistently conducted due to limited stakeholder participation and lack of technical guidance in plan formulation.', 'Inconsistent attendance and participation of some community representatives during planning activities.', '', 'Limited use of innovative and technology‑based approaches in delivering frontline services due to lack of training and resources.', 'Some activities in the implementation plan are not fully aligned with timelines and available resources.', 'The School Governance Council is not yet fully organized and operational due to limited stakeholder awareness and involvement.', '', '', 'Inconsistent documentation and monitoring schedules for some programs and projects.', 'Feedback mechanisms are not consistently utilized to gather stakeholder satisfaction data.', '', '', 'Limited time and resources restrict the regular conduct and follow‑through of some needs‑based LAC and L&D activities.', '', '', '', '', 'Inspection schedules are not always consistently documented and some minor issues are not immediately addressed due to limited resources.', 'Limited funding and prioritization constraints affect the timely implementation of infrastructure improvement projects.', 'The school lacks a fully equipped library with adequate learning resources and designated personnel.', '', 'The school lacks a fully equipped computer laboratory due to insufficient ICT equipment, limited space, and inadequate internet connectivity.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Presence of assessment tools, regular conduct of item analysis meetings, and teachers’ competence in assessment and data‑driven instruction.', '', 'Strong implementation of Child Protection Policy, active guidance services, vigilant teachers, and positive learner behavior.', 'Functional Child Protection Committee, clear reporting procedures, and coordinated support from stakeholders.', 'Implementation of learner tracking, intervention programs, home visitation, and strong school‑community partnership.', '', '', '', 'Organized Child Protection Committee, clear policies and procedures, and strong stakeholder awareness.', 'Established DRRM committee, available DRRM plan, and cooperation from school personnel and stakeholders.', '', '', '', '', 'Active student leaders, supportive teachers, and school administration that recognizes student participation in governance.', '', '', '', 'Strong parent support, active PTA officers, and positive collaboration between parents and school personnel.', 'Strong leadership support, active stakeholder participation, and existing linkages with partner institutions and nearby schools.', '', '', 'Competent and dedicated school personnel, regular performance monitoring, supportive leadership, and clear performance standards.', 'Clear office performance targets, teamwork among staff, and consistent supervision and support from school leadership.', '', 'Supportive school leadership, availability of professional development programs, and motivated school personnel.', 'Established recognition mechanisms, strong morale among staff, and supportive school administration.', 'Competent administrative staff, clear compensation procedures, and coordination with the division office.', 'Transparent workload assignment, participative decision‑making, and supportive school leadership.', '', '', '', 'Reliable basic utility connections, coordination with service providers, and proper maintenance practices.', '', 'Effective financial planning, proper budgeting, and transparent financial management practices.', 'Competent financial staff, established liquidation procedures, and support from school leadership.', 5, 1, 0, 1, 1, 6, 1, 0, 6, 6, 6, 6, 2, 0, 6, 5, 6, 5, 2, 2, 6, 1, 2, 2, 6, 2, 1, 6, 1, 1, 1, 2, 6, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Tap stakeholders’ commitment to improve learning facilities and support instructional needs', 'Strengthen remediation and intervention programs; conduct regular monitoring of learner performance; engage parents and stakeholders in academic support', 'N/A', 'Conduct capacity‑building activities on the development of contextualized instructional materials and provide school‑based support and resources to assist teachers in producing localized learning materials.', 'Strengthen remediation programs through structured interventions, increased monitoring of learner progress, and stronger parental involvement.', 'Provide orientation and instructional support on values integration and encourage consistent incorporation of peace education and DepEd core values across all subjects.', 'Sustain the regular conduct of test item analysis and provide continuous capacity‑building on data interpretation to further improve teaching strategies.', 'N/A', 'Sustain the strict implementation of anti‑bullying programs, strengthen guidance services, and continue awareness activities to maintain a safe learning environment.', 'Continue enforcing child protection policies, conduct regular orientations, and strengthen coordination with parents and community stakeholders.11. The school has reduced its drop‑out incidenceAlways ManifestedIsolated risk of absenteeism among learners due to socio‑economic factors.Implementation of learner tracking, intervention programs, home visitation, and strong school‑community partnership. Social Sustain learner retention', 'Sustain learner retention programs, strengthen early intervention strategies, and enhance parental involvement to prevent potential drop‑out cases.', 'Conduct capacity‑building on culture‑responsive teaching and integrate local culture and traditions into school activities and classroom instruction.', 'Coordinate with the ALS unit of the division, conduct community mapping to identify potential learners, and initiate planning for inclusive learning programs.', '', 'Sustain the functionality of the Child Protection Committee through regular meetings, continuous orientation, and monitoring of child‑related concerns.', 'Regularly review and update the DRRM plan, conduct drills and capacity‑building activities, and strengthen coordination with local DRRM offices.', 'Strengthen mental wellness support by coordinating with guidance counselors and health offices, and by conducting mental health awareness and psychosocial support trainings.', 'Advocate for the development of PWD‑friendly facilities, integrate inclusive design in school plans, and coordinate with stakeholders for funding and technical assistance.', 'Conduct training on strategic planning, strengthen stakeholder participation, and institutionalize regular review and updating of the school strategic plan.', 'Strengthen engagement of community stakeholders through regular consultations, clearer roles, and sustained collaboration in school planning activities.', 'Sustain the functionality of the SSG/SPG by providing leadership training, continuous mentoring, and opportunities for meaningful student participation in school governance.', 'Enhance frontline service delivery by introducing technology‑supported systems, conducting capacity‑building on customer service innovation, and strengthening stakeholder feedback mechanisms.', 'Review and align the implementation plan with available resources and timelines, and regularly monitor and evaluate progress to ensure full operationalization.', 'Organize and activate the School Governance Council, orient stakeholders on their roles and responsibilities, and establish regular meetings and decision‑making processes.', 'Sustain PTA operations through regular meetings, strengthen parent engagement activities, and encourage broader parental involvement in school programs and projects.', 'Sustain and strengthen school partnerships through regular coordination meetings, documentation of agreements, and continuous engagement with stakeholders and partner schools.', 'Strengthen monitoring and evaluation systems by standardizing documentation, conducting regular reviews, and using results to improve program implementation.', 'Sustain high individual performance by continuing performance monitoring, providing professional development opportunities, and recognizing exemplary performance.', 'Maintain high office performance through continuous monitoring, improvement of documentation processes, and regular review of performance targets and accomplishments.', 'Strengthen needs assessment for LAC sessions, allocate time for regular L&D activities, and ensure proper monitoring of LAC outputs and learning outcomes.', 'Sustain continuous professional development by supporting personnel promotion, providing access to training programs, and encouraging lifelong learning initiatives.', 'Continue institutionalizing recognition and reward systems to motivate personnel and acknowledge outstanding performance and milestone achievements.', 'Sustain timely facilitation of compensation by ensuring accurate and complete documentation and continuous coordination with concerned offices.', 'Maintain fair workload distribution by regularly reviewing teaching assignments and ensuring transparency and consultation in task allocation.', 'Strengthen regular inspection schedules, improve documentation, and promptly address identified infrastructure concerns through proper planning and coordination.', 'Prioritize critical infrastructure needs, strengthen stakeholder partnerships, and actively seek support for funding and facility enhancement projects.', 'Advocate for the establishment of a functional library by allocating space, sourcing learning materials, and coordinating with stakeholders for support.', 'Sustain functionality of utilities through regular maintenance, timely reporting of issues, and continuous coordination with service providers.', 'Advocate for the provision of ICT equipment, improve internet connectivity, and coordinate with stakeholders for support in establishing a functional computer laboratory.', 'Sustain efficient MOOE utilization through regular financial monitoring, alignment of expenditures with AIP priorities, and adherence to financial guidelines.', 'Maintain full MOOE liquidation by ensuring timely preparation of documents, continuous capacity‑building on financial reporting, and close coordination with concerned offices.', 'Enhance stakeholder feedback mechanisms, regularly analyze satisfaction results, and use feedback to improve school services and programs.', 1, 145, 12, 59),
