ivities\r\nSome activities need further localization and contextualization', 'Weak coordination with ALS implementers and community partners', 'Limited coordination with ALS implementers and district ALS coordinators\r\nALS program is not fully integrated into the school’s monitoring and planning systems', 'CPC is organized but not consistently active\r\nLimited capacity‑building activities for CPC members\r\nInadequate documentation of meetings, actions, and case management', 'DRRM plan exists but requires regular updating\r\nLimited simulation drills and refresher orientations\r\nSome stakeholders need increased awareness of DRRM roles and procedures', 'Limited school‑based mental health programs and activities\r\nLack of trained personnel to address mental wellness concerns\r\nMinimal referral system for learners and staff needing psychosocial support', 'Limited PWD‑friendly infrastructure such as ramps, handrails, and accessible toilets\r\nInsufficient learning resources for learners with special needs\r\nLimited funds for facility improvement and assistive devices', '', 'Inconsistent participation of some community stakeholders\r\nLimited documentation of planning team meetings and outputs\r\nNeed to strengthen shared ownership of school plans', 'Limited leadership training and capacity‑building activities for student officers\r\nStudent participation in school decision‑making can be further strengthened\r\nSome activities are not well documented', 'Innovations are implemented but not consistently documented\r\nLimited use of digital platforms for frontline services\r\nNeed to further improve efficiency and responsiveness of services', 'Need for closer alignment of implementation timelines with available resources\r\nLimited monitoring of implementation progress', 'Limited participation of some stakeholders in decision‑making\r\nInconsistent documentation of SGC meetings and resolutions', 'Varying levels of parent participation in PTA activities\r\nLimited capa