ith ALS facilitators, district ALS coordinators, and partners', '• Conduct LAC sessions on contextualization and localization of learning materials\r\n• Develop a school learning resource bank (print and digital)\r\n• Allocate MOOE / solicit stakeholder support for reproduction of materials\r\n• Encourage peer sharing and recognition of teacher-developed materials\r\n• Monitor utilization of contextualized materials in classrooms', 'Strengthen the use of diagnostic assessment results as basis for remediation\r\nSchedule structured and regular remediation sessions (small-group or focused instruction)\r\nMonitor learner progress quarterly using progress tracking tools\r\nEngage parents to support learner attendance and reinforcement at home', 'Conduct LAC sessions on explicit integration of peace education and DepEd core values\r\nProvide lesson exemplars highlighting contextualized values integration\r\nRequire reflection of values integration in DLLs and classroom activities\r\nReinforce core values through school programs and learner discipline initiatives', 'Institutionalize regular test item analysis after major assessments\r\nDiscuss results during LAC sessions and use them for instructional planning\r\nUtilize analysis results as basis for remediation and enrichment activities\r\nConduct capacity-building activities on data analysis and utilization', 'Not applicable', 'Strengthen implementation of the Child Protection Policy (CPP)\r\nConduct regular awareness campaigns for learners, parents, and teachers\r\nEncourage reporting through child‑friendly and confidential mechanisms\r\nEnsure proper documentation and timely response to reported cases', 'Sustain capacity‑building activities on child protection for teachers and staff\r\nStrengthen coordination with LGUs and child protection agencies\r\nMaintain functional Child Protection Committee (CPC)\r\nPromote a safe, respectful, and child‑friendly school environment', 'Sustain and strengthen existing dropout prevention strategies\r\nContinue learner monitoring and early intervention mechanisms\r\nStrengthen parental involvement and home–school coordination\r\nProvide targeted support for at‑risk learners', 'Integrate culture‑sensitive activities in school programs and lesson plans\r\nEncourage teacher initiatives that reflect local culture and traditions\r\nDocument and assess implementation of culture‑sensitive activities\r\nEngage community members and elders as resource persons', 'Strengthen coordination with ALS coordinators, LGUs, and partner stakeholders\r\nConduct mapping and profiling of disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adult learners\r\nAdvocate for community‑based learning opportunities and support programs\r\nIntegrate access‑focused initiatives in the SIP and AIP', 'Coordinate with the district/division ALS office to validate ALS program status\r\nEstablish a school‑based ALS data monitoring and documentation system\r\nIntegrate ALS concerns and plans into the SIP and AIP\r\nStrengthen advocacy and community awareness on ALS opportunities', 'Reorganize and reactivate the Child Protection Committee\r\nConduct orientation and capacity‑building activities for CPC members\r\nSchedule regular CPC meetings and ensure proper documentation\r\nStrengthen implementation and monitoring of the Child Protection Policy', 'Review and update the DRRM plan annually\r\nConduct regular drills (earthquake, fire, flood, etc.)\r\nOrient learners, teachers, and parents on DRRM procedures\r\nStrengthen coordination with LGUs and disaster response agencies', 'Integrate mental health and psychosocial support activities in school programs\r\nConduct capacity‑building for teachers on basic mental health awareness\r\nStrengthen referral mechanisms with guidance offices, health units, and partners\r\nPromote a supportive and caring school environment', 'Conduct an assessment of school facilities to identify PWD‑related needs\r\nPrioritize inclusion of SPED‑ and PWD‑friendly facilities in the AIP and SIP\r\nSeek support from LGUs, stakeholders, and partners for infrastructure improvement\r\nAdvocate for inclusive education and accessibility within the school community', 'Sustain participatory and data‑driven strategic planning processes\r\nRegularly review and update the strategic plan based on monitoring and evaluation results\r\nEnsure alignment of the strategic plan with SIP, AIP, and DepEd thrusts\r\nStrengthen stakeholder participation in planning and implementation', 'Strengthen organization and roles of the school‑community planning team\r\nConduct regular meetings with proper documentation\r\nEncourage active participation of parents, LGUs, and community partners\r\nPromote shared accountability in planning, implementation, and monitoring', 'Provide leadership and values formation activities for SSG/SPG officers\r\nEncourage meaningful student participation in school programs and initiatives\r\nStrengthen documentation and monitoring of SSG/SPG activities\r\nSupport student‑led projects aligned with school goals', 'Document and institutionalize innovative frontline service practices\r\nUtilize available digital tools and platforms to improve service delivery\r\nGather feedback from stakeholders to enhance frontline services\r\nContinuously improve systems to ensure timely, efficient, and client‑friendly services', 'Monitor implementation progress regularly and address delays promptly\r\nUse monitoring results to refine and adjust implementation strategies', 'Reorganize and orient SGC members on their roles and responsibilities\r\nConduct regular SGC meetings with proper documentation\r\nStrengthen stakeholder participation in school governance and decision‑making\r\nPromote transparency and shared accountability', 'Encourage active participation of parents in school programs and activities\r\nConduct capacity‑building and orientation activities for PTA officers\r\nStrengthen collaboration between the PTA and school management\r\nAlign PTA initiatives with school priorities and learner needs', 'Strengthen and expand partnerships with stakeholders and nearby schools\r\nFormalize partnerships through MOAs and written agreements\r\nDocument and monitor partnership activities and results\r\nEngage partners in planning, implementation, and evaluation of school programs', 'Institutionalize a clear monitoring and evaluation framework\r\nUse M&E results to improve planning and implementation of PPAs\r\nStrengthen documentation and reporting of monitoring activities\r\nBuild teachers’ capacity in basic monitoring and evaluation', 'Sustain performance monitoring and coaching mechanisms\r\nProvide regular feedback to personnel to maintain performance standards\r\nSupport personnel through capacity‑building and mentoring programs', 'Sustain collaborative implementation of office targets\r\nRegularly review OPCR accomplishments and adjust strategies as needed\r\nStrengthen teamwork and accountability mechanisms', 'Continue needs‑based planning of LAC and L&D activities\r\nIntegrate best practices and action research outputs in LAC sessions\r\nSustain documentation and monitoring of LAC implementation', 'Continue encouraging participation in trainings, seminars, and graduate studies\r\nSupport personnel in promotion and career advancement requirements\r\nProvide mentoring and coaching for professional growth', 'Develop a simple and sustainable school‑based recognition program\r\nRecognize achievements through non‑monetary incentives and acknowledgments\r\nInstitutionalize recognition during assemblies, meetings, or school events\r\nEngage stakeholders to support recognition initiatives', 'Sustain timely submission and verification of required documents\r\nStrengthen coordination with concerned offices\r\nEnsure transparency and timely communication with personnel', 'Regularly review and adjust workload assignments\r\nEnsure transparency and fairness in task distribution\r\nPromote teamwork and mutual support among teachers', 'Conduct regular and scheduled inspection of school facilities\r\nImprove documentation of inspection results and identified issues\r\nCoordinate with LGUs and concerned offices for technical support\r\nPrioritize immediate repair of identified safety concerns', 'Include priority infrastructure needs in the SIP and AIP\r\nMaximize use of available MOOE and seek stakeholder support\r\nCoordinate with LGUs and partners for infrastructure assistance\r\nMonitor progress of infrastructure improvement projects', 'Establish or improve a designated library or reading area\r\nGradually acquire age‑appropriate and updated learning resources\r\nSeek support from stakeholders, LGUs, and partners for library development\r\nAssign a teacher‑in‑charge to manage library resources', 'Coordinate with LGUs and service providers to improve basic utilities\r\nAllocate available funds for minor facility improvements\r\nExplore alternative connectivity options where feasible\r\nPrioritize access to basic utilities in school planning', 'Include establishment of a computer laboratory in the SIP and AIP\r\nSeek donations and partnerships for ICT equipment\r\nUtilize available devices through shared or mobile ICT arrangements\r\nProvide basic ICT skills training for teachers', 'Sustain effective budgeting and utilization of MOOE\r\nPrioritize expenditures aligned with school goals and learner needs\r\nStrengthen financial monitoring and transparency', 'Sustain timely and accurate liquidation of MOOE\r\nEnsure complete and proper documentation of expenses\r\nStrengthen coordination with concerned offices\r\nMaintain transparency and accountability in financial management', 'Strengthen feedback and satisfaction survey mechanisms\r\nAnalyze stakeholder feedback to improve school services\r\nAddress concerns promptly and transparently\r\nSustain quality service delivery and stakeholder engagement', 1, 139, 12, 59),
