(489, '2026', '128857', 'Attendance issues of some learners that affects the proficiency level of the Grade 3 learners', 'Poor learning Conditions, Teacher Training Limitations , Socio-Economic of Learners,Inappropriate Technology, low parental involvement', 'Not implemented in school', 'Limited localized content, Lack of Teacher Training, Insufficient research-based models,digital resource inequality.Limited  funding and support', 'Lack of Specialized Training , Diverse learners\' needs, Limited Resources and Materials ', 'Resource and budgetary  Gaps , Teacher- Related Challenges , student and Environmental Barriers, Assessment and Monitoring Issues', 'Teacher workload and overload,Inadequate Training , Lack of standardization', 'N/A', 'Learners\' Discipline', 'Non- Functional child-protection ,untrained guidance counselor , Delayed  case resolution', '', 'Limited Cultural Representation,Lack of Teacher Preparation,Insufficient Community Involvement', 'Limited Identification and Tracking,Low Enrollment and Participation,Insufficient Learning Resources,Weak Community and Stakeholder Support', 'N/a', '', '', 'Limited Mental Health Personnel,Weak Implementation of Programs,Insufficient Training for Teachers,Limited Counseling Services', 'Inadequate Physical Infrastructure,Limited SPED Facilities and Resources,Insufficient Trained Personnel', '', 'Inconsistent Functionality of the Team,Limited Stakeholder Participation,Insufficient Capacity in Planning', 'SSG/SPG exists but activities are not consistently implemented\r\nSome planned projects and programs are not fully carried out,Limited Leadership Capacity', 'Frontline services are still mostly manual or paper-based\r\nLack of online systems for inquiries, requests, and transactions,taff lack training in customer service, innovation, and ICT-based systems\r\nLimited awareness of efficient frontline service practices', 'Weak Alignment Between Plans and Implementation,Incomplete or Unclear Implementation Plan,Budget Constraints and Misalignment', 'Inconsistent Participation of Members,Weak Understanding of Roles and Functions,Irregular Meetings and Coordination,Limited Stakeholder Representation', '', '', 'Inconsistent Monitoring Practices,Weak Evaluation System,Incomplete Documentation and Reporting,Limited Use of Data for Decision-Making', 'Inconsistent Stakeholder Satisfaction,Communication Gaps,Weak Feedback Mechanism,Service Delivery Concerns', '', '', 'Overlapping of Activities,LAC and L&D topics are not always based on actual teacher needs or classroom data\r\nWeak use of assessment results to identify priority training areas,Irregular Conduct of LAC Sessions', '', '', '', '', '', 'Insufficient funds for major repairs, renovation, and new construction\r\nDependence on external funding or donations,Delayed Implementation of Improvement Projects,Inadequate Facilities and Learning Spaces', 'Insufficient and outdated books, references, and learning materials\r\nLack of updated reading materials aligned with curriculum needs', '', 'Insufficient working units for the number of learners\r\nSome computers are outdated, slow, or frequently malfunctioning', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'innovations for the  LARDOs ', '', '', '', 'Established structured Child  Protection Policy Protection in school ', 'Functionalized DRRM Plan', '', '', 'The school has strengthened strategic plan ', '', '', '', '', '', 'Active SPTA implementation in school ', 'Strengthened Partnership among internal and external stakeholders', '', '', 'School personnel manifested outstanding IPCR', 'School Head\'s IPCR  manifested VS rating ', '', 'The school facilitates promotions of teachers', 'The school  has rewards and recognition achievements of its personnel', 'Updated teachers salaries,allowances and other compensation', 'The school ensures a fair and equitable distribution of teacher workload through a transparent and consultative assignment process anchored on competence, subject specialization, and workload balance. Assignments are carefully planned at the beginning of the school year through collaborative discussions among school leaders and faculty to promote efficiency, fairness, and teacher well-being.', 'Constant inspection of infrastructure and facilities', '', '', 'updated school water, electric and internet facilities', '', '100% utilization of School MOOE', '100% MOOE liquidation ', 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 6, 1, 0, 6, 1, 6, 3, 6, 0, 2, 2, 6, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Home Visitation and remedial class given ', 'Upskilling and Reskilling of Teachers, Teacher training in HOTS Curriculum Realignment', 'N/A', 'Strengthen Teacher capacity, promote research and evidence- based practices , Improve access to digital tools ', 'Institutionalization of remediation, provision of capacity building , allocation of resources', 'Zero - Tolerance Policies ,Establishment of peace hubs , Contextualization of materials ', 'Quality Assured Test Bank , Teacher Commitment,', 'N/A', 'Establishment of a specialized team, Mandatory Reporting and confidentiality, Teacher commitment', 'Mandatory CPC Functionality ,Report to Disciplining Authority', 'Home Visitation , Remedial Instruction', 'integrate diverse cultural perspectives in daily instruction, and provide adequate resources and support for sustainable implementation.Promote inclusive and equitable representation of all cultures present in the school\r\nProvide continuous professional development for teachers on cultural sensitivity and diversity\r\nEncourage active involvement of parents, community members, and cultural groups in school activities.', 'Conduct comprehensive mapping and profiling of disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adult learners in coordination with the barangay and community stakeholders\r\nIncrease awareness and advocacy efforts to encourage enrollment and participation in ALS and other learning programs\r\nProvide flexible and inclusive learning delivery options (e.g., modular, blended, weekend, or evening classes)', 'N/A', 'The school recognizes the importance of a fully functional Child Protection Committee (CPC) in ensuring the safety, welfare, and well-being of all learners. However, gaps such as inconsistent meetings, limited awareness of policies, inadequate training of members, and weak monitoring mechanisms may affect its effectiveness. In response, the school resolves to strengthen the structure and operations of the CPC by ensuring active participation, regular capacity building, strict adherence to child protection policies, and systematic monitoring of cases and interventions', 'Ensure the development, updating, and full implementation of a comprehensive and functional DRRM Plan\r\nStrengthen the School DRRM Committee with clearly defined roles and active participation\r\nConduct regular disaster preparedness drills (e.g., earthquake, fire, flood, and other hazards)\r\nProvide continuous training and orientation for teachers, staff, and learners on DRRM protocols\r\nEstablish and maintain early warning systems and emergency communication mechanisms\r\nEnsure safe school facilities and hazard-free learning environments through regular risk assessment', 'Strengthen the role of the Guidance Designate/Committee in planning and implementing mental health programs\r\nProvide regular psychosocial support activities such as counseling, peer support, and stress management sessions\r\nConduct continuous awareness campaigns to reduce stigma and promote mental health literacy among learners, parents, and staff\r\nTrain teachers and personnel on basic counseling skills, psychological first aid, and learner well-being identification\r\nDevelop and implement a clear referral system in coordination with LGUs, health units, and mental health professionals\r\nCreate a safe, confidential, and child-friendly counseling environment within the school', 'Develop and maintain PWD-friendly and accessible school facilities such as ramps, handrails, and accessible comfort rooms\r\nStrengthen and expand SPED services and programs to address diverse learner needs\r\nProvide and utilize appropriate assistive learning materials and technologies for learners with disabilities\r\nEnhance the capacity of teachers through continuous training on inclusive education and SPED strategies\r\nEnsure the implementation of Individualized Education Plans (IEPs) for learners with special needs', 'Develop a comprehensive, data-driven, and participatory strategic plan aligned with DepEd priorities and school goals\r\n\r\n\r\nEnsure active involvement of internal and external stakeholders in the planning process\r\n\r\n\r\nUtilize updated and accurate data as basis for planning and decision-making\r\n\r\n\r\nAlign the strategic plan with School Improvement Plan (SIP), Annual Implementation Plan (AIP), and other school programs\r\n\r\n\r\nClearly define goals, objectives, strategies, and performance indicators in the plan\r\n\r\n\r\nStrengthen collaboration among school leaders, teachers, parents, and community partners\r\n\r\n\r\nPromote transparency and shared ownership of the strategic planning process\r\n\r\n\r\nConduct regular review and updating of the strategic plan based on emerging needs and evaluation results\r\n\r\n\r\nEnsure proper documentation and dissemination of the strategic plan to all stakeholders\r\n\r\n\r\nCommit to continuous improvement and effective implementation of the strategic directions of the school\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you want, I can also compile all your resolutions into a complete SMEA or School Performance Portfolio, or format them into a table with indicators, issues, actions, and success measures.', 'Ensure the active and sustained functionality of the school-community planning team throughout the school year\r\nStrengthen stakeholder participation including parents, LGUs, and community representatives in planning activities\r\nConduct regular and well-documented planning sessions with clear outputs and agreements\r\nEnhance the capacity of planning team members on strategic planning, SIP/AIP preparation, and results-based management\r\nPromote data-driven planning using updated and accurate school performance data\r\nStrengthen coordination and collaboration among school leaders, teachers, and community stakeholders\r\nEnsure proper documentation, consolidation, and dissemination of planning outputs\r\nIntegrate planning outputs into the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)\r\nStrengthen monitoring and follow-through of agreed plans and commitments\r\nFoster a culture of shared ownership and accountability in school planning and development', 'Ensure the active and functional operation of the SSG/SPG throughout the school year\r\nStrengthen leadership training and capacity-building programs for student leaders\r\nPromote active participation of the student body in SSG/SPG programs and activities\r\nProvide consistent guidance and support from faculty advisers and school administration\r\nImprove planning, implementation, documentation, and evaluation of student government projects', 'Strengthen and institutionalize innovative and efficient frontline service delivery systems\r\nPromote the use of ICT and digital platforms to improve accessibility and speed of services\r\nDevelop and implement a clear and updated Citizen’s Charter or service standards\r\nEnsure consistent and timely delivery of services following established procedures and timelines\r\nConduct capacity building for personnel on customer service, ICT tools, and innovation practices', 'Ensure that the implementation plan is fully aligned with the School Strategic Plan, SIP, and AIP priorities\r\nDevelop clear and detailed action plans with defined objectives, timelines, persons responsible, and success indicators\r\nStrengthen results-based monitoring and evaluation systems to track progress and outcomes of implemented activities\r\nEnsure proper and timely budget allocation and utilization aligned with priority programs', 'Ensure the full functionality and active participation of the School Governance Council (SGC) in all governance-related activities\r\nStrengthen the orientation and capacity building of SGC members on their roles, responsibilities, and DepEd governance policies\r\nConduct regular and well-documented SGC meetings with clear agenda, minutes, and follow-through actions\r\nEnhance stakeholder representation and engagement to ensure inclusive and participatory decision-making\r\nStrengthen the involvement of SGC in SIP/AIP planning, implementation, and review processes', 'Ensure the active and functional operation of the Parent-Teacher Association (PTA) at all levels\r\nStrengthen parent engagement and participation in school programs, projects, and activities\r\nConduct regular PTA meetings with clear agenda, proper documentation, and follow-up actions\r\nEnhance communication and collaboration between parents, teachers, and school leaders\r\nInvolve PTA in the planning, implementation, and evaluation of school programs and projects\r\nPromote transparency and accountability in PTA funds and activities\r\nProvide orientation and capacity-building activities for PTA officers and members', 'Establish and sustain strong partnerships with stakeholders, other schools, and community organizations\r\nStrengthen collaborative programs and shared initiatives that support teaching, learning, and school development\r\nConduct regular coordination meetings, dialogues, and consultations with partners\r\nEngage stakeholders in SIP/AIP planning, implementation, and evaluation processes\r\nMobilize resources, technical assistance, and support services from partners to enhance school programs\r\nPromote inter-school collaboration and sharing of best practices\r\nStrengthen linkages with LGUs, NGOs, private sectors, and alumni associations', 'Establish and sustain a systematic and regular monitoring and evaluation system for all PPAs\r\nDevelop and use standardized M&E tools, indicators, and reporting templates\r\nEnsure clear assignment of roles and responsibilities in monitoring and evaluation activities\r\nStrengthen the capacity of teachers and staff on M&E processes and results-based management\r\nPromote the use of data and evaluation results in planning and decision-making\r\nEnsure complete, accurate, and timely documentation and reporting of all programs and activities\r\nStrengthen stakeholder involvement in providing feedback on school programs and services', 'Sustainability of Teachers\' performance', 'Sustainability of School Head\'s OPCR rating', ' Conduct regular and well-planned LAC sessions and L&D activities based on identified teacher and learner needs\r\nStrengthen needs assessment processes to ensure relevant and targeted professional development topics\r\nEnsure strict adherence to scheduled LAC implementation as part of the school’s annual plan\r\nImprove documentation, reporting, and utilization of LAC outputs in classroom practice\r\nAlign LAC and L&D activities with DepEd priorities, school goals, and teaching-learning improvement needs\r\nStrengthen the capacity of facilitators and teachers in conducting effective professional learning sessions\r\nPromote active participation and engagement of all teachers in LAC and L&D activities\r\nProvide post-training coaching, mentoring, and monitoring to ensure application of learning\r\nEnhance resource support and use of ICT tools to make sessions more interactive and effective', 'Ensure the implementation of a structured and needs-based professional development program for all personnel\r\nStrengthen the development and monitoring of Individual Development Plans (IDPs/IPDPs) aligned with career goals\r\nProvide equal access to training, seminars, and learning opportunities for all school personnel\r\nSupport personnel in understanding and completing promotion requirements and processes\r\nEstablish a transparent system for tracking training, upskilling, and professional growth', 'Establish and sustain a fair and transparent recognition and rewards system for personnel achievements\r\nRegularly recognize milestone accomplishments, exemplary performance, and service contributions of school personnel\r\nInstitutionalize awarding ceremonies and recognition programs at school-level activities and events\r\nEnsure clear criteria and guidelines for selection of awardees based on merit and performance\r\nPromote timely and meaningful acknowledgment of achievements and professional milestones', 'Sustainability of the facilities implementation', 'Ensure a transparent, consultative, and equitable distribution of teacher workload at the beginning of the school year and as needed\r\nBase workload assignments on teacher qualifications, specialization, and competency areas\r\nRegularly review and adjust workload to ensure balance and prevent overloading of personnel\r\nPromote fairness in the assignment of teaching loads, ancillary tasks, and committee responsibilities', 'Conduct regular and systematic inspection of school infrastructure and facilities\r\nEnsure safety, accessibility, and functionality checks of classrooms, offices, and learning areas\r\nEstablish a clear schedule and checklist for facility inspection and monitoring\r\nPromptly address identified defects, hazards, and maintenance needs\r\nStrengthen coordination with LGUs, engineers, and maintenance personnel for facility improvements\r\nMaintain proper documentation and reporting of inspection results and actions taken', 'Develop and implement a systematic and prioritized infrastructure improvement plan aligned with school needs\r\nStrengthen coordination with LGUs, PTA, stakeholders, and partner agencies for resource mobilization and support\r\nEnsure regular maintenance and timely repair of school facilities and equipment\r\nPrioritize the development of safe, accessible, and learner-friendly facilities', 'Ensure the establishment and maintenance of a functional and learner-friendly library\r\nImprove and update library resources, books, and reference materials aligned with curriculum needs\r\nStrengthen library management and organization systems for easy access and utilization\r\nPromote regular reading programs and literacy activities to encourage learner engagement\r\nIntegrate library use into classroom instruction and learning activities\r\nAssign and support a trained library-in-charge or focal person for effective management', 'Ensure the continuous functionality and reliability of water, electricity, and internet services in the school\r\nStrengthen coordination with service providers and local government units for consistent utility support\r\nAllocate and prioritize resources for the maintenance and improvement of utility systems\r\nPromote efficient and responsible use of water, electricity, and internet facilities among learners and personnel', 'Ensure the proper functionality, maintenance, and continuous improvement of the computer laboratory\r\nUpgrade and maximize the use of ICT equipment and digital learning resources for instruction\r\nStrengthen internet connectivity and technical support systems for efficient ICT use\r\nImplement a regular maintenance and repair program for all computer units and equipment\r\nProvide training and upskilling for teachers on ICT integration and digital pedagogy\r\nEstablish a clear scheduling and utilization system to ensure equitable access for learners', 'Sustainability of the implementation ', 'Sustainability of 100% utilized MOOE', 'Establish and sustain a functional stakeholder feedback and satisfaction monitoring system\r\nRegularly conduct surveys, consultations, and feedback mechanisms to gather stakeholder inputs\r\nStrengthen transparent and timely communication with parents, learners, partners, and community members\r\nImprove quality of school services, programs, and learner support systems\r\nEnhance stakeholder engagement and participation in school planning and implementation\r\nEnsure prompt action and response to stakeholder concerns and recommendations\r\nStrengthen recognition and appreciation programs for stakeholders’ contributions and support\r\nUse data-driven results from satisfaction surveys to inform planning and decision-making\r\nPromote a positive, inclusive, and responsive school environment that fosters trust and collaboration\r\nSustain continuous improvement initiatives to consistently raise stakeholder satisfaction levels', 1, 139, 12, 59),
