(540, '2026', '128940', 'Misalignment of assessment data (Grade 4 used instead of Grade 3); absence of valid Grade 3 baseline data.', 'Absence of NAT data for Grade 6 due to non-administration of the exam; incomplete performance dataset for basic education levels.', 'Absence of Alternative Learning System (ALS) program implementation in the school; no enrolled ALS learners.', '', '', '', '', 'limited coordination capacity for partnership building.', '', '', '', '', '', 'Absence of a school-based Alternative Learning System (ALS) program implementation.', '', '', 'Presence of basic guidance-related activities and teacher concern for learner well-being\r\nExisting Teen Center/learner support initiatives that can be expanded for mental health services\r\nTeachers’ awareness of learners’ emotional and behavioral needs in the classroom\r\nSupportive school environment promoting care, respect, and positive relationships\r\nInitial coordination with stakeholders that may support psychosocial programs', 'School commitment to inclusive education and learner diversity\r\nExisting awareness among teachers on inclusive and differentiated instruction\r\nSupportive school leadership open to accessibility and equity improvements\r\nBasic infrastructure that may be improved for future accessibility upgrades\r\nCoordination potential with LGUs and stakeholders for facility development support', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Basic monitoring activities conducted during implementation\r\nPresence of school reports and accomplishment submissions\r\nAwareness among staff on importance of M&E', 'Existing feedback mechanisms from stakeholders\r\nBasic stakeholder engagement activities conducted\r\nSchool openness to feedback and improvement', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Presence of basic reading materials and classroom-based reading corners\r\nTeachers’ initiative in promoting reading activities\r\nInitial efforts in organizing learning resources', '', 'The school has no existing computer equipment for learners', '', '', '', '', '', 'Teachers demonstrate strong commitment to differentiated and learner-centered instruction.', 'Teachers regularly conduct diagnostic and formative assessments to identify learning gaps\r\nImplementation of school-based remediation programs (e.g., reading and numeracy sessions)\r\nAvailability of instructional materials and intervention modules for remedial instruction', 'Teachers consistently integrate DepEd Core Values (Maka-Diyos, Maka-tao, Makakalikasan, Makabansa) in daily lessons', 'Teachers’ competence in conducting basic item analysis and interpreting assessment data', '', 'trong implementation of the Child Protection Policy (CPP) and related DepEd guidelines\r\nActive presence of Guidance Designate/Teacher and reporting mechanisms for learner concerns', 'Sustaining the operations of the Teen Center', 'Active classroom monitoring and early identification of at-risk learners', 'Celebration of national and local cultural events (e.g., Buwan ng Wika, Indigenous Peoples’ activities when applicable)', 'Presence of learner support systems such as guidance service', '', 'Active implementation of the DepEd Child Protection Policy (CPP)\r\nClearly designated and organized Child Protection Committee members with defined roles', 'Established and updated School DRRM Plan aligned with DepEd guidelines\r\nActive School DRRM Committee with clearly defined roles and responsibilities\r\nRegular conduct of drills (earthquake, fire, and other hazards) to ensure preparedness\r\nAvailability of emergency supplies and basic response equipment', '', '', 'Strong school leadership commitment in planning and decision-making\r\nActive participation of teachers and stakeholders in collaborative planning processes\r\nAvailability of DepEd guidelines (SIP/AIP framework) as basis for strategic planning\r\nUse of data (assessment results, SBM indicators, school performance data) in planning\r\nConduct of regular planning workshops and consultations with stakeholders\r\nAlignment of school goals with DepEd priorities and learner needs', 'Active collaboration between school leadership, teachers, and stakeholders in planning activities\r\nEstablished School Planning Team (SPT) with clearly defined roles and responsibilities\r\nRegular conduct of planning workshops and consultation meetings', 'Active implementation of learner leadership programs and DepEd student governance guidelines\r\nStrong support from school administration in recognizing and mentoring student leaders\r\nRegular conduct of elections, meetings, and organizational activities', 'Strong commitment of school personnel to efficient and responsive service delivery', 'Clear alignment of SIP/AIP with DepEd priorities and school goals\r\nActive involvement of teachers and stakeholders in implementation planning', 'Active participation of stakeholders, LGU, PTA, and community leaders\r\nRegular SGC meetings and consultations\r\nStrong school leadership promoting shared governance', 'Active PTA officers and strong parent participation\r\nRegular PTA meetings and school involvement\r\nStrong communication between teachers and parents', 'Strong linkages with LGUs, NGOs, and partner institutions\r\nParticipation in cluster/district activities and collaborations\r\nOpen communication and partnership-building initiatives', '', '', 'Strong performance monitoring and coaching by school leadership\r\nClear performance targets aligned with RPMS indicators\r\nRegular feedback and mentoring among teachers\r\nCommitment of personnel to quality teaching performance', 'Effective leadership and management practices\r\nStrong collaboration among school personnel\r\nAlignment of school programs with performance targets', 'Regular conduct of LAC sessions based on identified needs\r\nCollaboration among teachers in sharing best practices\r\nSupport from school leadership in professional development', 'Active support for CPD programs, trainings, and graduate studies\r\nGuidance on promotion requirements and career progression\r\nStrong encouragement from school leadership', 'Regular recognition during school programs and activities\r\nAppreciation of service milestones and achievements\r\nSupportive school leadership culture', 'Efficient coordination with payroll and finance offices\r\nProper submission of requirements and documents\r\nStrong administrative support system', 'Transparent assignment of teaching loads\r\nConsideration of teacher strengths and specialization\r\nCollaborative planning in workload distribution', 'Regular conduct of school facility inspection and monitoring\r\nActive involvement of school head and maintenance committee\r\nCoordination with stakeholders for safety and readiness checks', 'Strong leadership initiative in facility improvement projects\r\nSupport from LGU and stakeholders for infrastructure development\r\nProper prioritization of school needs in SIP/AIP', '', 'Stable access to basic utilities in school', '', 'Proper financial planning and budgeting system\r\nActive monitoring of fund utilization\r\nCompliance with DepEd financial guidelines', 'Proper documentation and accounting procedures\r\nTimely submission of liquidation reports\r\nStrong coordination with accounting and finance offices', 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 'Conduct immediate baseline/diagnostic assessment for all Grade 3 learners to generate accurate data', 'Implement school-based summative assessments and quarterly standardized tests aligned with MELCs and NAT competencies.\r\nUtilize diagnostic and formative assessment results to approximate learner proficiency levels.', 'Coordinate with the Division ALS focal person for possible establishment or linkage of ALS learners to the nearest ALS Community Learning Center.\r\nConduct advocacy and information dissemination to identify potential ALS learners in the community.', 'Sustain and enhance the development of contextualized and differentiated learning materials across learning areas\r\nStrengthen collaborative planning and LAC sessions for continuous improvement of instructional materials', 'Sustain and strengthen regular remediation programs across all learning areas\r\nImprove tracking and monitoring system for learners with identified learning gaps\r\nDevelop more targeted intervention materials for reading, science, and mathematics', 'Sustain consistent integration of peace education and DepEd core values in all learning areas', 'Standardize the use of item analysis templates across all grade levels\r\nEnsure consistent use of results to design remediation and enrichment activities\r\nImprove documentation and monitoring of learners’ least mastered competencies\r\nStrengthen collaboration among teachers for shared analysis and instructional planning', 'Develop a school partnership plan aligned with TLE–TVL competencies and local industry needs.', 'Sustain strict implementation of the Child Protection Policy  in our Teen Center and anti-bullying measures\r\nStrengthen awareness campaigns on anti-bullying and positive discipline among learners', 'The school commits to sustain the operations of the Teen Center by ensuring its continuous use as a safe space for learners’ guidance, counseling, and psychosocial support activities.', 'Strengthen parental involvement and communication strategies to address absenteeism', 'Ensure continuous documentation and monitoring of culture-based activities', 'Ensure regular monitoring and documentation of learner participation and progress', 'Coordinate with the Division ALS focal person for possible establishment of a school-based ALS program or linkage to nearby ALS center.', 'Sustain the full functionality of the Child Protection Committee through regular meetings and monitoring\r\nStrengthen documentation, reporting, and case management systems', 'Sustain the implementation and regular updating of the School DRRM Plan\r\nConduct periodic simulation drills and orientation for learners and personnel\r\nStrengthen monitoring and evaluation of DRRM preparedness activities\r\nEnhance capacity building for teachers and staff on disaster response and risk reduction\r\nEnsure continuous availability and replenishment of emergency supplies and kits', 'Establish a formal school-based mental wellness support mechanism (e.g., counseling system, referral pathway, and intervention program)\r\nDesignate or strengthen a trained focal person or guidance designate for mental health concerns\r\nConduct mental health awareness activities, orientations, and psychoeducation sessions for learners and staff\r\nDevelop a clear referral system for learners needing specialized psychosocial support\r\nStrengthen coordination with LGUs, health offices, and partner agencies for mental health services\r\nIntegrate wellness activities (stress management, peer support, resilience building) into school programs', 'Advocate for the establishment of PWD-friendly and inclusive school facilities (e.g., ramps, handrails, accessible comfort rooms)\r\nCoordinate with LGU, DepEd engineering office, and stakeholders for infrastructure support and funding\r\nConduct needs assessment to identify learners requiring SPED and accessibility support\r\nStrengthen inclusive education practices while facilities are being developed\r\nIntegrate accessibility improvements into the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and AIP\r\nEstablish linkage with SPED resource support or nearby SPED centers for technical assistance\r\nCommit to creating a safe, inclusive, and barrier-free learning environment for all learners', 'Sustain and strengthen the evidence-based strategic planning process of the school\r\nEnsure continuous stakeholder engagement and consultation in updating the strategic plan\r\nRegularly update the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) based on emerging needs\r\nStrengthen data utilization and monitoring systems to guide planning and decision-making\r\nConduct periodic review and evaluation of strategic plan implementation\r\nPromote shared accountability among school personnel and stakeholders in achieving targets', 'Sustain the functionality of the School-Community Planning Team through regular meetings and consultations\r\nStrengthen stakeholder engagement and participation in school planning and implementation', 'Sustain the functionality of the SELG through regular elections and capacity-building activities\r\nStrengthen leadership training programs for student officers\r\nEncourage active participation of student leaders in school planning, programs, and decision-making', 'Sustain and further enhance innovative frontline services for stakeholders', 'Sustain effective implementation of SIP through AIP execution\r\nStrengthen monitoring and evaluation of implemented activities\r\nEnsure continuous stakeholder involvement in implementation\r\nRegularly update plans based on performance results and emerging needs', 'Sustain regular SGC meetings and participation\r\nStrengthen stakeholder engagement in school decision-making\r\nEnhance documentation and tracking of SGC actions and resolutions', 'Sustain active PTA engagement in school programs and projects\r\nStrengthen parent participation in learner support activities\r\nImprove coordination and communication mechanismsSustain active PTA engagement in school programs and projects\r\nStrengthen parent participation in learner support activities\r\nImprove coordination and communication mechanisms.', 'Sustain and expand partnerships with stakeholders and schools\r\nStrengthen formal MOAs/MOUs where applicable\r\nEnhance documentation of partnership activities and outcomes', 'Establish a structured monitoring and evaluation (M&E) system\r\nStrengthen use of tools for tracking PPAs implementation\r\nConduct regular post-implementation review and feedback sessions\r\nAssign focal persons for systematic monitoring of programs', 'Sustain high performance through continuous coaching and feedback\r\nStrengthen individual professional development plans\r\nMaintain results-based performance monitoring', 'Sustain high organizational performance standards\r\nStrengthen results-based planning, implementation, and evaluation\r\nContinuously improve school systems and processes', 'Sustain needs-based LAC implementation\r\nStrengthen alignment of LAC topics with learner and teacher needs\r\nEnhance documentation and evaluation of L&D activities', 'Sustain support for professional growth and promotion opportunities\r\nEncourage continuous skills upgrading and CPD participation\r\nProvide guidance on career development pathways', 'Sustain a culture of recognition and appreciation\r\nInstitutionalize regular awards and recognition programs\r\nStrengthen motivation through positive reinforcement', 'Sustain timely processing of salaries and benefits\r\nStrengthen coordination with division and finance offices\r\nEnsure accurate and updated personnel records', 'Sustain fair and balanced workload distribution\r\nRegularly review and adjust teaching assignments\r\nEnsure equity and transparency in workload allocation', 'Sustain regular inspection and monitoring of facilities\r\nStrengthen documentation of inspection results and findings\r\nEnsure timely reporting of maintenance needs', 'Sustain continuous improvement of school facilities\r\nStrengthen coordination with LGU and DepEd engineering office\r\nPrioritize urgent infrastructure needs in planning', 'Develop and strengthen a functional school library system\r\nAllocate space, materials, and reading resources\r\nAssign library focal person and improve management system\r\nSeek stakeholder support for library improvement and resources', 'Sustain functionality of water, electricity, and internet services\r\nRegular monitoring and preventive maintenance\r\nStrengthen coordination with service providers', 'dvocate for the provision of computer sets/laptops and ICT equipment for instructional use\r\nCoordinate with LGU, stakeholders, and DepEd offices for resource support and funding', 'Sustain efficient and transparent MOOE utilization\r\nStrengthen financial monitoring and reporting\r\nEnsure alignment of expenses with SIP/AIP priorities', 'Sustain 100% timely liquidation of MOOE funds\r\nEnsure complete and accurate documentation of expenses\r\nMaintain compliance with COA and DepEd financial policies', 'Strengthen stakeholder feedback collection and analysis system\r\nImprove service delivery and responsiveness to client needs\r\nConduct regular satisfaction surveys and action planning\r\nEnhance transparency and communication with stakeholders\r\nImplement continuous quality improvement initiatives', 0, 144, 12, 59);
