(541, '2026', '129051', 'Some Leaner\'s difficulty in reading comprehension and basic numerscy skills\r\n-Irregular attendance of pupils affecting mastery of skills', 'Learners lack higher-order thinking and problem solving\r\n-insufficient review and preparation of NAT', '', 'Time constraint for developing localized material.', 'Inssuficient time and varied learner need.', 'Limited integration in daily lesson plans.', 'lack of teacher skills in item analysis', '', 'Cases of bullying still occur, especially in lower grades.', '', 'Some learners leave due to financial hardship or family responsibilities.', 'Limited participation from minority groups.', 'Lack of monitoring system for disadvantaged learners.', 'No designated ALS coordinator or structured program.', 'Irregular meeting', 'lack of updated equipment', 'Limited professional counselors.', 'Lack of ramps, accessible toilets, and SPED teachers.', 'Strategic plan not regularly updated; limited stakeholder input.', 'Low participation from community members; meetings are irregular.', '', 'Services are mostly traditional; limited use of technology and feedback systems.', 'Limited staff involvement in planning and execution ', 'Inactive or irregular SGC meetings; Low stakeholder participation ', '', 'Inconsistent coordination with external stakeholders', 'Inconsistent documentation and reporting ', 'Limited feedback mechanisms from stakeholders ', '', '', 'Limited time; overlapping schedules', '', 'Limited incentives; irregular recognition programs', '', '', '', '', 'Lack of library space; insufficient books and learning materials; no assigned librarian', '', 'outdated equipment; limited ICT resources', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong child protection policy and vigilant staff.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Active student participation and supportive advisers.', '', '', '', 'Active PTA officers and regular meetings;Strong support from parents and teachers ', '', '', '', 'Clear RPMS guidelines; committed personnel', 'Collaborative planning; clear office targets; effective monitoring system', '', 'Access to division trainings; motivated personnel; leadership support', '', 'Efficient administrative staff; coordination with payroll offices', 'Clear workload policies; transparent task distribution', 'Active school inspection team; regular monitoring schedule; supportive stakeholders', 'stakeholder participation; available MOOE and partnerships', '', 'Existing service providers', '', 'Efficient financial management; trained personnel; proper planning', 'clear guidelines; organized record-keeping', 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 6, 1, 0, 6, 2, 3, 6, 2, 2, 2, 5, 6, 5, 2, 6, 6, 2, 1, 2, 6, 2, 1, 6, 1, 1, 1, 2, 6, 3, 2, 1, 3, 5, 1, 5, 3, 3, 'Strengthen reading and numeracy intervention program eg. remedial classess, peer tutoring\r\n-conduct regular monitoring', 'Provide capacity-building for teachers \r\n-Intergrate 21st century skills in daily lessons\r\n-Conduct regular NAT review classes', '', 'LAC sessions for material develpment and sharing best prctices', 'Strengthen remediation program and the one is to one ration in conducting the remediation to cater individuals need.', 'Strengthen values education in all subject areas and conduct awareness activities.', 'Conduct training on test item analysis and data utilization.', '', ', conduct anti-bullying campaigns, and enforce stricter monitoring', 'Continue awareness sessions and maintain reporting mechanisms.', 'Expand livelihood support for families, strengthen home-school partnerships, and enhance flexible learning options.', ': Involve community elders, integrate local culture into curriculum, and provide inclusive materials.', 'Establish baseline data, coordinate with DepEd ALS, and create outreach programs.', 'Assign ALS focal person, allocate resources, and collaborate with barangay learning centers.', 'Schedule quarterly meetings, conduct refresher training, and strengthen reporting protocols.', 'Conduct regular drills, update DRRM plan annually, and request additional resources.', 'Partner with local health units, train teachers in basic counseling, and organize wellness activities.', 'Request funding for facility upgrades, train teachers in inclusive education, and establish SPED classes.', 'Conduct annual review workshops, involve teachers, parents, and students in planning, and align with DepEd priorities.', 'Formalize the team with clear roles, schedule quarterly meetings, and strengthen collaboration with barangay and LGU officials.', 'Provide leadership training, integrate SELG projects into school improvement plan, and encourage peer-led initiatives.', 'Introduce digital platforms for announcements and feedback, streamline enrollment processes, and pilot innovative service delivery models.', 'Develop a detailed implementation plan with timelines and assigned responsibilities ', 'Reactivate SGC through regular scheduled meetings; Clarify roles and responsibilities of members', 'Increase parent engagement through flexible meeting schedules;Strengthen transparency in fund utilization', 'Conduct regular stakeholder meetings and joint activities', 'Conduct training on data collection and reporting ; Schedule regular program reviews and feedback sessions ', 'Strengthen coaching and mentoring; ensure timely submission of MOVs; conduct regular performance review sessions', 'Enhance alignment of OPCRF and IPCRF; conduct periodic monitoring; set internal deadlines', 'Develop structured LAC plan; schedule regular sessions', 'Encourage participation trainings; ensure equitable access to opportunities', 'Institutionalize recognition program; allocate minimal budget; include awards during school events', 'Ensure timely submission of documents; strengthen coordination with division office; maintain updated records', 'Regular review of workload distribution; adjust assignments as needed; ensure transparency and consultation', 'Strengthen routine inspection checklist; assign focal persons per area; allocate quick-response repair fund', 'Prioritize projects in SIP/AIP; seek LGU and partner support; implement phased improvements', 'Establish mini-library/reading corner; request book donations; assign library coordinator; include in SIP', 'Coordinate with providers for stable connection; budget allocation for utilities; explore backup internet options', 'Request ICT equipment from DepEd/LGU; repair existing units; seek donations; integrate ICT in SIP', 'Improve procurement planning; monitor fund utilization regularly; ensure transparency', 'Maintain updated financial records; conduct regular monitoring; provide training on liquidation procedures', 'Conduct regular stakeholder satisfaction surveys; Establish feedback and grievance mechanisms', 1, 148, 12, 59),
(542, '2026', '129046', 'Some Grade 3 learners still demonstrate difficulty in reading comprehension, basic numeracy operations, and writing skills due to learning gaps from previous grade levels.\r\nInconsistent parental support in home-based reading and numeracy activities.', 'Inconsistent performance in core subjects and 21st‑century skills.\r\nLimited mastery of higher‑order thinking skills.', '', 'Limited skills and time in developing contextualized materials\r\nLack of localized reference materials', 'Some learners still show learning gaps despite remediation\r\nLimited time for extended remediation sessions', 'Limited integration of peace education and core values in lessons\r\nLack of teaching materials focused on values integration', 'Limited teacher skills in conducting item analysis\r\nInconsistent use of test results for instructional planning', '', 'Lack of systematic anti-bullying awareness sessions for learners\r\nIncidents are sometimes unreported due to fear or stigma\r\nInconsistent monitoring during recess and non-classroom activities\r\nLimited documentation of minor bullying cases', '', '', 'Limited integration of local culture, traditions, and languages in school activities\r\nTeachers have minimal training on culture-responsive teaching\r\nFew school events highlight indigenous or community practices', '', '', 'CPC meetings are not always conducted regularly due to competing school priorities\r\nSome CPC members require further training on updated Child Protection protocols\r\nLimited documentation of minor concerns and preventive interventions', 'DRRM plan implementation is sometimes limited to drills only\r\nInsufficient orientation of learners and parents on DRRM protocols\r\nLimited disaster preparedness resources and equipment', 'Limited trained personnel in mental health and psychosocial support\r\nCounseling services are not always accessible to all learners\r\nLack of dedicated space for guidance and mental wellness activities', 'Classrooms are not fully designed to accommodate learners with special needs\r\nLimited budget allocation for inclusive infrastructure improvements', 'The school does not have an updated and clearly documented strategic plan. Stakeholders’ participation in planning is limited, and the plan is not regularly reviewed or communicated to personnel.', 'The planning team is organized, but meetings are irregular, and attendance of some community stakeholders is inconsistent.', '', 'Frontline services largely rely on traditional processes. Limited use of technology and feedback mechanisms affects service efficiency and accessibility.', 'The school strategic plan is not fully translated into a detailed and time-bound implementation plan. Roles, timelines, and monitoring mechanisms are unclear, resulting in limited execution of planned programs and projects.', 'The School Governance Council is not yet organized. There is limited awareness among stakeholders regarding the roles and importance of the SGC in school governance and decision-making.', '', 'Collaboration with stakeholders and partner schools exists but is not sustained throughout the year. Some partnerships lack formal agreements, and follow-through on joint activities is sometimes limited.', 'Monitoring and evaluation activities are conducted, but documentation and data analysis are sometimes limited, affecting evidence-based decision-making.', 'Feedback mechanisms are present but not consistently administered, and some stakeholder concerns are not immediately addressed.', '', '', 'LAC and learning activities are conducted but not always based on a comprehensive needs assessment. Documentation and follow-through of agreed action plans are sometimes limited.', '', 'Recognition activities are conducted but are not always systematic or timely. Some achievements are acknowledged informally rather than through structured programs.', '', '', '', '', 'Lack of designated library space; insufficient reading materials, furniture, and librarian-in-charge.', '', 'The school has limited number of computers; no designated computer laboratory/classroom; insufficient ICT equipment and unstable internet connectivity.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Functional and active Child Protection Committee (CPC) with clearly defined roles and responsibilities\r\nStrong and consistent implementation of the DepEd Child Protection Policy (DO No. 40, s. 2012)\r\nRegular orientation and awareness programs for learners, parents, and school personnel\r\nTeachers and staff trained on child-friendly, learner-centered, and rights-based approaches\r\nEstablished reporting and referral mechanisms with confidentiality ensured\r\nStrong collaboration with parents, barangay officials, and other child-protection partners\r\nSchool culture that promotes respect, safety, and learner welfare', 'Effective implementation of the Early Warning System (EWS) for learners at risk of dropping out\r\nRegular learner monitoring, profiling, and home visitation conducted by advisers and school heads\r\nStrong school–parent partnership that supports learner attendance and performance\r\nAvailability and sustainability of intervention programs (feeding program, remedial classes, guidance support)\r\nActive involvement of stakeholders and external partners (LGU, NGOs, alumni) in learner support', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'The Supreme Student/Pupil Government officers are formally elected, actively involved in school activities, and supported by designated teacher-advisers.', '', '', '', 'The PTA is duly organized with elected officers, conducts regular meetings, and actively supports school programs, projects, and activities.', '', '', '', 'School personnel consistently meet or exceed performance expectations, supported by clear targets, regular coaching, and monitoring by school heads.', 'The school office demonstrates effective teamwork, clear delegation of functions, and strong leadership, resulting in the consistent achievement of office performance targets.', '', 'The school consistently supports seminars, trainings, Learning Action Cells (LACs), coaching, and mentoring programs that promote continuous professional growth of personnel.', '', 'Efficient coordination between school administration and the Schools Division Office; timely submission of payroll and financial documents; clear communication with concerned personnel.', 'Transparent assignment of teaching loads; collaborative planning among teachers; observance of policies on workload distribution; supportive school leadership.', 'Regular monitoring by the school head and designated committee; availability of inspection checklists and scheduled quarterly inspections.', 'Active school leadership; strong support from stakeholders, PTA, and local government; inclusion of infrastructure improvement in the AIP and SIP.', '', 'Existing water supply, electricity, and internet connections; regular payment and maintenance; support from  MOOE', '', 'Proper financial planning; timely preparation of AIP and procurement plan; regular monitoring of expenditures; active School Head and finance committee.', 'Presence of trained school personnel; proper documentation and record-keeping; guidance from school head and division finance office.\r\n', 6, 6, 0, 1, 6, 2, 1, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 0, 2, 1, 6, 3, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 3, 5, 3, 3, 'Strengthen reading and numeracy intervention programs such as remedial classes and peer tutoring.\r\nEngage parents through orientation and literacy support activities to reinforce learning at home.', 'Conduct NAT review and remediation.\r\nEnhance teaching strategies through trainings.\r\nStrengthen learner monitoring and support.', '', 'Conduct training on contextualization of lessons\r\nProvide technical assistance and sample localized materials', 'Strengthen remedial and intervention programs\r\nMonitor learner progress regularly\r\nEngage parents in supporting remediation activities', 'Integrate peace education and core values across subjects\r\nProvide orientations and teaching guides on values integration', 'Conduct training on test construction and item analysis\r\nUse item analysis results to improve teaching strategies', '', 'Strengthen implementation of the Anti-Bullying Policy through quarterly orientations for learners, teachers, and parents\r\nEstablish a confidential reporting mechanism (suggestion box, guidance referral)\r\nIntegrate Values Education and ESP lessons promoting respect, empathy, and inclusion\r\nAssign teachers on duty rotation to monitor high-risk areas (corridors, playgrounds)', 'Continuously upholding and strictly implementing the Child Protection Policy in all school activities and engagements\r\nMaintaining an active and functional Child Protection Committee (CPC) that regularly monitors, documents, and reports concerns\r\nConducting regular orientations and capacity-building activities for learners, parents, teachers, and non-teaching personnel', 'Continuously implementing the Early Warning System (EWS) to identify and support learners at risk\r\nStrengthening learner monitoring, home visitation, and guidance interventions\r\nSustaining learner support programs such as feeding programs, remedial classes, and psychosocial support\r\nEnhancing school–parent–community collaboration to address attendance, economic, and social concerns\r\nMobilizing stakeholders and partners to provide resources and assistance that promote learner retention and completion', 'Integrate local culture and context in lessons, activities, and celebrations\r\nConduct INSET sessions on culture-sensitive and inclusive education\r\nInvolve community elders, parents, and cultural bearers in school programs\r\nCelebrate local history, language, and traditions during school events (Buwan ng Wika, Community Day)', '', '', 'Institutionalize regular CPC meetings with documented minutes and action plans\r\nConduct capacity-building activities on Child Protection for CPC members\r\nStrengthen documentation, monitoring, and reporting systems\r\nEnsure continuity of CPC operations through clear role designation and succession planning', 'Regularly review, update, and disseminate the DRRM Plan\r\nIntegrate DRRM concepts in classroom instruction and school activities\r\nStrengthen coordination with LGU and local DRRM councils\r\nMobilize stakeholders to support procurement of basic disaster preparedness materials', 'Conduct trainings and seminars on mental health awareness for teachers\r\nStrengthen the Guidance and Counseling Program\r\nEstablish referral mechanisms with health offices and professionals\r\nPromote mental wellness through school-wide campaigns and learner-support activities', 'Prioritize PWD‑friendly facilities in the School Improvement Plan (SIP)\r\nCoordinate with LGU, NGOs, and stakeholders for infrastructure support', 'Conduct a school-wide strategic planning workshop with active involvement of teachers, parents, and community partners. Formulate, document, and regularly monitor the implementation of the school strategic plan.', 'Strengthen stakeholder engagement through regular meetings, clear role assignments, and capacity-building activities to ensure consistent participation and shared decision-making.', 'Sustain and enhance leadership opportunities by providing continuous leadership training and involving student leaders in school governance initiatives.', 'Introduce simple digital tools (online feedback forms, messaging platforms) and improve service delivery procedures to ensure timely, efficient, and stakeholder-friendly frontline services.', 'Develop a comprehensive implementation plan that clearly defines activities, responsibilities, timelines, and success indicators. Conduct regular monitoring and evaluation to ensure alignment between the strategic plan and actual school operations.', 'Organize the School Governance Council in accordance with DepEd policies. Conduct orientation and capacity-building activities to ensure active stakeholder participation in school governance and continuous school improvement.', 'Sustain and strengthen the functionality of the PTA by increasing parent engagement through regular communication, recognition of support, and collaborative planning of school activities.', 'Strengthen partnerships by formalizing agreements (MOAs), planning regular collaborative activities, and establishing a monitoring system to ensure continuity and mutual benefits.', 'Monitoring and evaluation activities are conducted, but documentation and data analysis are sometimes limited, affecting evidence-based decision-making.', 'Sustain high individual performance through continuous coaching, performance feedback, recognition programs, and targeted professional development activities.', 'Maintain effective office systems, improve resource utilization, and strengthen teamwork to continuously achieve and sustain very satisfactory office performance.', 'Strengthen needs assessment processes, ensure proper documentation of LAC sessions, and regularly monitor the implementation of learning and development action plans.', 'The school consistently supports seminars, trainings, Learning Action Cells (LACs), coaching, and mentoring programs that promote continuous professional growth of personnel.', 'Institutionalize a structured recognition and rewards system to ensure timely, fair, and consistent acknowledgment of personnel achievements.', 'Sustain timely preparation and submission of required documents; conduct regular orientation for staff on compensation-related requirements; strengthen coordination with finance offices to avoid possible delays.', 'Continue equitable workload distribution; regularly review teaching assignments; maintain open communication and collaborative decision-making among staff to address workload concerns promptly.\r\n\r\n\r\n', 'Continue regular inspection and documentation; prioritize repair needs and strengthen coordination with the LGU and stakeholders for funding support.\r\n\r\n\r\n', 'Sustain stakeholder partnerships; continuously update the infrastructure development plan; seek additional funding from external partners.', 'Allocate a room for library use; request library resources through DepEd programs and stakeholders; gradually organize a functional library with proper management.', 'Strengthen coordination with service providers; explore alternative internet solutions; include upgrades in the school improvement plan.', 'Include establishment of a computer laboratory in the SIP and AIP; seek support from LGU, DepEd programs, and stakeholders for computers, internet connection, and laboratory setup.', 'Sustain efficient financial management practices; strengthen procurement planning to ensure timely and effective utilization of MOOE.', 'Continue strengthening financial documentation practices; ensure timely submission of liquidation reports; provide refresher orientation on financial guidelines.', 'Enhance stakeholder feedback systems, promptly address concerns raised, and continuously improve service delivery to increase satisfaction levels.', 1, 148, 12, 59),
