laborative planning', '', 'Encouragement from leadership;', '', 'established coordination with higher offices', 'Transparent workload system; open communication', 'availability of inspection tools/checklists', 'support from stakeholders and LGU; prioritization of needs', '', 'regular maintenance', '', 'Efficient financial planning; knowledgeable staff; clear guidelines', 'Efficient financial planning; knowledgeable staff; clear guidelines', 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 2, 6, 5, 1, 6, 6, 1, 1, 4, 6, 4, 1, 6, 1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 5, 5, 5, 1, 1, 3, 3, 'Intensify reading and numeracy intervention programs', 'Strengthen review sessions and NAT simulations', 'promote ALS enrollment in the community', 'Allocate time and provide resources for material development', 'Engage parents to ensure learner participation', 'Monitor and support consistent implementation', 'Provide training on test item analysis', 'not applied for elementary level\r\n\r\n', 'Conduct regular awareness campaigns', 'Strengthen referral system with agencies', 'Provide interventions (feeding, support programs)', 'Integrate culture in curriculum and activities', 'Partner with stakeholders for support', 'Community demand for alternative learning', 'Conduct regular meetings and planning', 'Allocate resources for preparedness', 'Provide mental health training for teachers', 'Allocate budget for SPED resources', 'Sustain collaborative planning; improve scheduling', 'Strengthen communication strategies;  maintain strong partnerships', 'Provide continuous leadership training; strengthen mentoring and monitoring of activities', 'Introduce digital systems (e.g., online feedback, appointment systems); conduct capacity-building', 'Strengthen monitoring and feedback mechanisms; align timelines with realistic targets; utilize simple tracking tools (e.g., Gantt charts, progress monitoring forms)', 'Reactivate and reorganize the SGC; conduct orientation on roles and responsibilities; schedule regular meetings; strengthen stakeholder engagement and partnership building', 'Sustain engagement through flexible meeting schedules; strengthen communication channels; recognize active participation of parents', 'Maintain and expand partnerships; formalize agreements (MOA/MOU); improve coordination and planning mechanisms', 'Strengthen documentation and reporting systems; provide training on monitoring and evaluation; allocate time for regular review', 'Sustain coaching and mentoring; ensure timely submission and review', 'Strengthen alignment of IPCR and OPCR; improve planning and consolidation processes', 'schedule protected time for LAC sessions', 'Expand access to capacity-building programs; maximize free online training opportunities', 'Institutionalize recognition programs; allocate budget for incentives; adopt non-monetary recognition schemes', 'Ensure accurate and timely submission of documents; availability of AO in school would be of  grate help; strengthen coordination with division office', 'Maintain transparency in workload distribution; regularly review assignments; consider teacher strengths and welfare', 'Sustain regular inspections; strengthen coordination with technical experts; improve documentation', 'Prioritize critical projects;  improve procurement planning', 'Establish or rehabilitate library; allocate funds for resources; assign/designate library personnel; seek donations and partnerships', 'Ensure regular maintenance; establish contingency measures; coordinate with service providers', 'improve facilities', 'Sustain efficient and needs-based use of MOOE through proper planning and monitoring.', 'Maintain 100% timely and accurate liquidation through proper documentation and compliance with guidelines.', 'Improve feedback systems (e.g., surveys, suggestion boxes); increase stakeholder participation; use results for continuous improvement', 1, 43, 12, 58),
(586, '2026', '500847', 'Language transition difficulty (Mother Tongue to Filipino/English) causing confusion in comprehension.', 'Grade 6, 10, and 12 learners demonstrate low proficiency in higher-order thinking skills (HOTS), particularly in critical thinking and problem-solving components of the National Achievement Test (NAT), resulting in difficulty analyzing texts, interpreting data, and applying concepts across learning areas', 'N/A', '', '', '', 'Inconsistent use and limited capacity in interpreting test item analysis results, leading to gaps in effectively identifying least mastered skills and translating data into targeted instructional interventions.', 'N/A', '', '', 'Some learners still experience irregular attendance due to long distance from school, household responsibilities, and occasional lack of transportation support, which may still lead to potential drop-out cases if not closely monitored.', '', '', 'N/A', '', '', '', '', 'The school’s strategic planning process is in place but stakeholder participation and data-driven analysis are not consistently maximized, resulting in plans that may not fully capture emerging needs and priorities.', '', '', 'While the school has introduced innovations in frontline services, there are occasional challenges in sustaining digital systems and ensuring that all stakeholders are fully aware and able to access these improved services, especially in areas with limited connectivity.', 'There are instances where the implementation plan is not fully aligned with the timelines and resource availability in the strategic plan, resulting in delays and partial execution of some priority programs and activities.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Although the school has a functional library, there are gaps in the availability of updated reading materials and limited learner utilization due to scheduling conflicts and insufficient reading engagement activities.', '', 'The school currently does not have a functional computer laboratory/classroom due to insufficient ICT equipment, limited budget allocation for computer units and maintenance, and lack of stable internet infrastructure, which affects the delivery of ICT-integrated instruction.', '', '', '', '', '', 'strong collaboration among teachers in developing and sharing localized and culturally relevant instructional materials, enabling lessons to be more meaningful and responsive to learners’ contexts.', 'established implementation of structured and regular remediation sessions supported by available assessment data, allowing teachers to promptly identify and address learners’ difficulties in reading, comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics.', 'Consistent integration of DepEd core values and peace education concepts in daily lesson planning and classroom activities, which helps reinforce positive behavior, respect, and social responsibility among learners.', '', '', 'Strong implementation of child protection policies supported by active classroom supervision and consistent reinforcement of positive discipline practices, which helps maintain a safe and respectful learning environment and contributes to zero child bullying incidence.', 'Strong child protection mechanisms are in place, including an active Child Protection Committee (CPC), regular orientation of teachers and learners on child safeguarding policies, and strict implementation of reporting protocols for any suspected abuse cases. This promotes a safe, monitored, and responsive school environment.', '', 'The school actively integrates Indigenous Peoples (IP) education and culture-sensitive practices through the observance of local traditions, use of culturally responsive learning materials, and participation of community elders in school activities, ensuring respect and appreciation of learners’ cultural background.', 'The school implements inclusive education programs such as Alternative Learning System (ALS) coordination, flexible learning modalities, and community-based outreach activities, allowing out-of-school youth (OSYs), adult learners, and disadvantaged learners to access basic education services.', '', 'The school has an active and well-trained Child Protection Committee (CPC) that regularly conducts monitoring, learner awareness activities, and immediate response to child protection concerns, ensuring a safe and supportive learning environment for all learners.', 'The school has an updated and functional Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (DRRM) plan that is regularly reviewed, includes hazard mapping, and is supported by organized school DRRM committees and conducted simulation drills to ensure preparedness of learners and personnel.', 'The school has an established mental health and psychosocial support system, including trained guidance focal persons, regular wellness activities, peer support initiatives, and referral mechanisms for learners and personnel needing further psychological assistance.', 'The school provides accessible and inclusive facilities such as ramps, handrails, designated learning spaces, and appropriate classroom accommodations that support learners with disabilities (PWDs) and those with special education needs, ensuring their full participation in school activities.', '', 'The school has an active School-Community Planning Team composed of school personnel, parents, barangay officials, and other stakeholders who regularly collaborate in planning, implementing, and monitoring school programs and projects.', 'The school has an active and functional Supreme Pupil Government (SPG) that regularly participates in school planning, implements learner-led initiatives, and serves as a partner in promoting discipline, school programs, and student welfare.', '', '', 'The school has a functional School Governance Council (SGC) composed of committed stakeholders from the community, parents, and school leadership who actively participate in decision-making, policy formulation, and monitoring of school programs and projects.', 'The school has an active and functional Parent-Teacher Association (PTA) that regularly supports school programs through active participation in meetings, provision of resources, and collaboration in implementing school activities and learner welfare initiatives.', 'The school maintains strong and active partnerships with stakeholders such as LGU, PTA, NGOs, and nearby schools through regular collaboration in school programs, resource-sharing activities, and joint implementation of educational initiatives.', 'The school has a functional monitoring and evaluation system that regularly tracks the implementation of programs, projects, and activities through scheduled reviews, feedback mechanisms, and documentation of results to ensure continuous improvement.', 'The school consistently receives satisfactory ratings from both internal and external stakeholders due to its transparent communication, responsive leadership, and effective delivery of programs and services aligned with stakeholder needs and expectations.', 'The school implements effective performance management practices such as regular coaching, mentoring, and classroom observation, which support school personnel in consistently achieving a Very Satisfactory rating in their Individual Performance Commitment and Review Form (IPCRF).', 'The school has an effective planning, monitoring, and performance alignment system that ensures all office targets and deliverables are consistently met through coordinated teamwork, efficient resource management, and regular performance tracking, resulting in an Outstanding rating in the Office Performance Commitment and Review (OPCR).', 'The school regularly conducts needs-based Learning Action Cells (LACs) and Learning & Development (L&D) activities anchored on classroom observation results, learner performance data, and teachers’ identified professional development needs, ensuring continuous instructional improvement.', 'The school actively supports the promotion and continuous professional development of its personnel through regular dissemination of scholarship opportunities, in-service trainings, mentoring programs, and assistance in meeting promotion requirements.', 'The school regularly implements a recognition and rewards system that acknowledges the milestone achievements of personnel such as years of service, exemplary performance, and contributions to school improvement through simple but meaningful ceremonies and incentives.', 'The school has an efficient payroll monitoring and coordination system with relevant offices, ensuring that personnel receive their salaries, allowances, and other compensation accurately and on time through proper documentation and timely submission of requirements.', 'The school implements a fair and transparent workload distribution system that considers teachers’ specialization, experience, and assigned responsibilities, ensuring equitable assignment of teaching loads, ancillary tasks, and other duties.', 'The school conducts regular inspection and assessment of its infrastructure and facilities through scheduled monitoring, safety checks, and coordination with relevant personnel to ensure that classrooms, buildings, and equipment are safe, functional, and conducive to learning.', 'The school actively initiates infrastructure and facility improvements through the prioritization of repair and upgrading needs in its annual plan, coordination with the LGU and stakeholders, and utilization of available funds and support to enhance the learning environment.', '', 'The school ensures the continuous functionality of its basic utilities such as water, electricity, and internet through regular monitoring, timely maintenance, and coordination with service providers and local stakeholders, ensuring uninterrupted support for teaching and learning activities.', '', 'The school has an efficient financial planning and procurement system that ensures timely identification, prioritization, and utilization of MOOE funds aligned with the approved Annual Implementation Plan (AIP), resulting in a 72–100% utilization rate.', 'The school has a well-organized financial management system with complete documentation, timely submission of liquidation reports, and strict adherence to accounting and auditing rules, ensuring 100% liquidation of utilized Maintenance and Other Operating Expenses (MOOE).', 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 3, 6, 1, 0, 1, 5, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 5, 1, 2, 2, 6, 1, 3, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 3, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'To address learners’ difficulty in transitioning from Mother Tongue to Filipino and English, the school shall implement a structured Language Transition Support Program that uses bridging instruction strategies such as code-switching, translation, and parallel vocabulary development, supported by contextualized and dual-language learning materials. This will be reinforced through daily vocabulary enrichment activities, guided reading sessions with gradual language shift, and differentiated instruction based on learners’ reading levels. Capacity building for teachers on MTB-MLE strategies and active parental engagement in reinforcing language use at home will also be prioritized to ensure improved comprehension, increased learner confidence, and a smoother transition to Filipino and English proficiency.', 'The school shall implement a targeted NAT Enhancement Program that integrates HOTS-based instruction, regular formative assessments, and test-taking strategies into daily lessons, supported by teacher training on 21st-century teaching approaches, use of contextualized learning materials, and data-driven remediation sessions to strengthen learners’ competencies and improve overall NAT performance.', 'N/A', 'The school shall sustain and strengthen collaborative practices through regular Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions, continuous capacity building on contextualization, and systematic monitoring of material utilization, ensuring that all teachers consistently produce and use high-quality, learner-responsive instructional resources.', 'The school shall sustain and strengthen data-driven remediation through consistent use of assessment results, scheduled intervention classes, and provision of appropriate instructional materials, while ensuring continuous teacher collaboration to effectively close learning gaps and improve learner achievement across all learning areas.', 'The school shall sustain the deliberate embedding of peace education and DepEd core values across all learning areas through contextualized lesson plans, value-laden activities, and continuous monitoring via classroom observation and LAC sessions to ensure meaningful internalization among learners.', 'The school shall implement a strengthened data utilization system through regular capacity building on test item analysis, standardized reporting templates, and scheduled collaborative planning sessions where teachers use analysis results to design focused remediation and enrichment activities, ensuring that assessment data directly informs teaching and improves learner performance.', 'N/A', 'The school shall sustain and strengthen its child protection program through continuous awareness campaigns, regular monitoring, prompt reporting mechanisms, and active engagement of teachers, parents, and learners to ensure that a bullying-free and child-friendly school environment is consistently maintained.', 'The school commits to sustain and strengthen its child protection policy implementation by continuously capacitating teachers and stakeholders on child protection guidelines, conducting regular monitoring and awareness activities, and ensuring a quick-response reporting system is always functional. It also commits to intensify partnerships with parents and community leaders to maintain a zero child abuse incidence and uphold a safe learning environment for all learners.', 'The school shall strengthen its early warning system by closely monitoring learners with frequent absences, intensifying home visitation activities, and strengthening collaboration with parents and community leaders to address attendance barriers. It will also implement targeted interventions such as remedial support, peer mentoring, and possible assistance programs to sustain learners’ engagement and further reduce drop-out incidence.', 'The school commits to continuously promote and strengthen culture-sensitive education by sustaining meaningful engagement with Indigenous community leaders, integrating local culture in teaching-learning activities, and ensuring that all school programs respect and celebrate cultural diversity. It also commits to regularly capacitate teachers on culturally responsive pedagogy to further deepen learners’ appreciation of their heritage.', 'The school commits to sustain and expand inclusive learning opportunities by strengthening partnerships with the ALS implementers and local community leaders, conducting regular mapping and profiling of OSYs and adult learners, and providing flexible and accessible learning interventions. It also commits to continuously design learner-centered programs that ensure no learner is left behind regardless of age, status, or circumstance.', 'N/A', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen the functionality of the Child Protection Committee by providing regular capacity-building activities, ensuring updated child protection policies are effectively implemented, and sustaining close coordination with parents, teachers, and stakeholders. It also commits to uphold a proactive safeguarding system that protects learners from all forms of abuse, exploitation, and neglect.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen the implementation of its DRRM plan by conducting regular drills, updating risk assessments, and enhancing coordination with local DRRM offices and stakeholders. It also commits to ensure that learners and staff are always well-informed, prepared, and responsive to any emergency situations to guarantee safety and resilience at all times.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen its mental wellness support mechanism by sustaining regular psychosocial support activities, enhancing the capacity of teachers on basic mental health care, and deepening coordination with health professionals and partner agencies. It also commits to promote a caring and supportive school environment that prioritizes the emotional well-being of all learners and staff.', 'The school commits to continuously improve and sustain inclusive and PWD-friendly facilities by regularly assessing accessibility needs, upgrading infrastructure when necessary, and strengthening awareness among staff on inclusive education practices. It also commits to ensure that all learners, regardless of ability, are provided with equal opportunities to learn in a safe, supportive, and barrier-free environment.', 'The school shall strengthen its strategic planning process by ensuring regular, inclusive stakeholder consultations and maximizing the use of updated school data in decision-making. It will also establish periodic review and monitoring mechanisms to ensure that plans remain responsive, relevant, and aligned with the school’s goals and learners’ needs.', 'The school commits to sustain and strengthen the engagement of its School-Community Planning Team by ensuring regular meetings, transparent decision-making, and continuous capacity-building of members. It also commits to deepen partnerships with stakeholders to co-create responsive, inclusive, and sustainable programs that support the holistic development of learners.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen the Supreme Pupil Government by providing regular leadership training, ensuring meaningful participation in school governance, and supporting learner-led initiatives. It also commits to nurture responsible and empowered student leaders who actively contribute to a positive, inclusive, and student-friendly school environment.', 'The school shall enhance the sustainability of its innovative frontline services by providing continuous orientation and technical assistance to stakeholders, improving offline and alternative service options, and strengthening ICT infrastructure support. It will also establish feedback mechanisms to regularly assess service effectiveness and ensure accessibility for all clients.', 'The school shall strengthen alignment between the strategic plan and implementation plan by conducting regular review and adjustment sessions, ensuring realistic scheduling and proper resource allocation. It will also reinforce monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to track progress and immediately address implementation gaps for timely and effective delivery of planned activities.', 'The school commits to sustain and further strengthen the School Governance Council by ensuring regular meetings, inclusive participation, and transparent decision-making processes. It also commits to deepen stakeholder engagement and collaboration to support school improvement initiatives and ensure that governance remains participatory, responsive, and effective for learner success.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen the Parent-Teacher Association by promoting active parental involvement, ensuring transparent planning and utilization of PTA resources, and sustaining regular communication between teachers and parents. It also commits to deepen partnership efforts to support learners’ academic, social, and emotional development.', 'The school commits to sustain and expand its collaborative partnerships by continuously engaging stakeholders in planning and implementation of school programs, strengthening inter-school cooperation, and formalizing partnerships through MOAs when necessary. It also commits to nurture a culture of shared responsibility to further enhance learner outcomes and school development.', 'The school commits to sustain and strengthen its monitoring and evaluation system by conducting regular progress reviews, ensuring data-driven decision-making, and actively utilizing evaluation results for program improvement. It also commits to enhance transparency and accountability in all school initiatives to ensure effective and efficient delivery of services for learners.', 'The school commits to sustain and further enhance personnel performance by strengthening continuous professional development, providing regular instructional supervision and feedback, and recognizing outstanding performance. It also commits to foster a culture of excellence, collaboration, and accountability to ensure that all personnel consistently deliver high-quality work.', 'The school commits to sustain and further improve office performance by strengthening strategic alignment of targets, enhancing teamwork and accountability among personnel, and continuously monitoring progress of key deliverables. It also commits to uphold efficiency, transparency, and innovation in office processes to consistently achieve or surpass performance targets.', 'The school commits to sustain and strengthen the conduct of needs-based LACs and L&D activities by systematically using data as basis for training topics, ensuring active participation of all teachers, and providing follow-through coaching and mentoring. It also commits to continuously align professional development initiatives with emerging instructional needs to improve teaching quality and learner outcomes.', 'The school commits to sustain and strengthen the professional growth of its personnel by continuously providing equal access to training and development opportunities, supporting career advancement through mentoring and coaching, and ensuring a culture of lifelong learning. It also commits to align professional development initiatives with both individual growth plans and organizational needs to enhance overall school performance.', 'The school commits to sustain and further strengthen its recognition and rewards system by ensuring timely and equitable acknowledgment of personnel achievements, expanding recognition opportunities, and fostering a culture of appreciation and motivation. It also commits to continuously encourage excellence, dedication, and commitment among staff through consistent and meaningful recognition practices.', 'The school commits to sustain and further improve the timely and accurate release of salaries, allowances, and other benefits by maintaining strict compliance with documentary requirements, strengthening coordination with concerned offices, and regularly monitoring payroll-related processes. It also commits to ensure transparency, accuracy, and efficiency in all financial transactions affecting personnel compensation.', 'The school commits to continuously uphold fair and equitable distribution of workload among teachers by regularly reviewing assignments, ensuring transparency in the assignment process, and considering teacher welfare and specialization. It also commits to promote collaboration and prevent workload imbalance to maintain efficiency and well-being among personnel.', 'The school commits to sustain and strengthen the regular inspection of its infrastructure and facilities by implementing a systematic maintenance schedule, promptly addressing identified issues, and coordinating with appropriate offices for repairs and upgrades. It also commits to ensure a safe, functional, and learner-friendly learning environment at all times.', 'The school commits to continuously prioritize and advocate for the improvement of its infrastructure and facilities by strengthening partnerships with stakeholders, ensuring proper planning and budgeting, and promptly addressing identified facility needs. It also commits to sustain efforts in creating a safe, accessible, and conducive learning environment for all learners and personnel.', 'The school shall improve library utilization by integrating regular reading programs and scheduled library periods per class, while also strengthening partnerships with stakeholders for the donation of updated books and reading resources. It will further promote reading engagement activities such as storytelling sessions, book clubs, and reading challenges to maximize learner use of the library and enhance literacy development.', 'The school commits to sustain and further improve the reliability of its water, electric, and internet facilities by implementing regular inspection and preventive maintenance measures, strengthening coordination with utility providers, and allocating resources for immediate repairs. It also commits to ensure uninterrupted access to essential services to support efficient school operations and quality learning delivery.', 'The school shall prioritize the establishment of a functional computer laboratory by including ICT equipment acquisition in its SIP/AIP, strengthening partnerships with LGU, stakeholders, and private donors for possible resource support, and coordinating with DepEd and other agencies for ICT program assistance. It will also explore phased procurement and utilization of available resources to gradually develop a fully functional computer laboratory that supports digital learning.', 'The school commits to sustain and further improve the efficient utilization of MOOE funds by strengthening financial planning, ensuring strict adherence to procurement schedules, and continuously aligning expenditures with priority programs and activities. It also commits to uphold transparency, accountability, and timely liquidation of funds to support effective school operations and learner development.', 'The school commits to continuously maintain 100% liquidation of MOOE by strengthening financial monitoring, ensuring complete and accurate supporting documents, and adhering to prescribed accounting and auditing procedures. It also commits to uphold transparency, accountability, and timeliness in all financial transactions to sustain compliance and trust.', 'The school commits to sustain and further improve stakeholder satisfaction by continuously enhancing service delivery, strengthening feedback mechanisms, and addressing concerns promptly and effectively. It also commits to uphold transparency, accountability, and participatory governance to ensure that stakeholder trust and confidence in the school are maintained and further strengthened.', 1, 39, 12, 58),
