(596, '2026', '306403', '', '', '', '1.Difficulty in ensuring that materials are both locally relevant and aligned with national standards.\r\n2. Teachers often juggle multiple responsibilities, leaving limited time for material development.\r\n3. Wide variation in learners’ abilities, backgrounds, and learning styles.\r\n4. Insufficient professional development on contextualization and localization strategies.\r\n5. Lack of systems to assess effectiveness of contextualized materials.\r\n\r\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '1. Occasional irregular attendance among learners due to socio-economic challenges.\r\n2. Health-related absences affecting participation and performance.\r\n3. Learners still at risk of dropping out due to poverty and family responsibilities.\r\n', '', '', '', '1. Inconsistent attendance or availability of CPC members during meetings and urgent cases.\r\n2. Occasional delays in response due to overlapping school responsibilities\r\n3. Limited documentation and systematic recording of minor incidents and preventive actions.', '', '', '1. Mobility challenges due to incomplete or improperly maintained infrastructure.\r\n2. Insufficient funding for assistive technologies and learning materials.', '', '', '', '', '', '1. Inconsistent attendance or participation of some SGC members in meetings and consultations.\r\n2. Varying levels of commitment among members in implementing agreed actions.\r\n3. Need for continuous capacity building for SGC members on governance roles and responsibilities.', '', '', '1. Need for continuous capacity building on data collection, analysis, and reporting.\r\n2. Incomplete documentation of program outputs, outcomes, and impact.', '1. Inconsistent feedback collection and analysis from stakeholders.\r\n2. Insufficient documentation of stakeholder concerns and satisfaction surveys.', '', '', '1. Difficulty retrieving documents during validation or evaluation.\r\n2. Sessions are sometimes postponed or not conducted as scheduled.\r\n3. ', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '1. No established computer laboratory to support ICT curriculum integration.\r\n2. Limited budget allocation for ICT infrastructure development.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '1. Use diagnostic, formative, and summative assessments to identify specific learning gaps.\r\n2. Group learners based on skill level (not just grade level).\r\n3. Track progress regularly to adjust interventions.', '1.Integrate peace and values education in daily lessons—not as a separate subject.\r\n2. Use examples, problems, and scenarios that highlight respect, empathy, and responsibility.\r\n3. Align activities with real-life situations learners can relate to.', '1. Identify poorly constructed or ambiguous test iteEnsure alignment between test items, learning competencies, and teaching strategies itemsProvide targeted interventions for identified learning gaps.\r\n3. \r\n2. ', '', '1. Clearly communicate policies, procedures, and consequences to learners, parents, and staff.\r\n2. Ensure consistent and fair application of rules across all grade levels.\r\n3. Address behavioral concerns early through counseling and intervention.', '1. Maintain zero tolerance for any form of abuse, neglect, or exploitation\r\n2. Ensure all school spaces are safe, well-supervised, and child-friendly.\r\n3. Conduct regular orientations for learners, parents, and staff on child protection and rights.', '', '1. Embed local traditions, beliefs, languages, and practices in lessons and school activities.\r\n2. Engage parents, elders, Indigenous Peoples, and community leaders in planning and implementation.\r\n3. Invite cultural experts to share authentic knowledge and practices.', '1. Provide printed modules, digital resources, and offline learning materials.\r\n2. Ensure accessibility in low-connectivity or remote areas.', '', '', '1. Keep accurate records of drills, trainings, and incidents.\r\n2. Conduct regular evaluation and use findings to improve DRRM practices.', '1. Strengthen partnerships with mental health professionals and institutions.\r\n2. Promote respect, kindness, and open communication among learners and staff.\r\n3. Strengthen teachers’ skills in handling learners with emotional and behavioral needs.', '', '', '', '', '', '1.Ensure that the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) is fully aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and strategic goals.\r\n2. Translate long-term objectives into clear, actionable yearly targets and activities.\r\n3. Ensure accountability by clearly identifying persons responsible for each activity.', '', '1. Promote open communication between parents and teachers regarding learner progress and concerns.\r\n2. Strengthen parents’ sense of ownership in school programs and initiatives.\r\n3. Ensure clear agenda setting, proper documentation, and dissemination of minutes.', '1. Recognize contributions of stakeholders and partner institutions.\r\n2. Establish formal agreements (MOA/MOU) to sustain long-term partnerships.', '', '', '1. Promote a culture of sharing resources and strategies.\r\n2. Support colleagues in achieving collective targets.\r\n3. Conduct mid-year self-assessments.\r\n4. Identify gaps early and implement improvements', '1. Clear understanding of OPCR indicators, targets, and expectations\r\n2. Regular monitoring and feedback mechanisms are in place.', '', '1. Conduct training needs analysis based on IPCR/OPCR results, classroom observations, and performance gaps.\r\n2. Guide personnel in meeting competency and qualification requirements.', '', '1.Maintain complete and updated employee master data (position, plantilla, step increment, deductions, etc.). 2. Regular validation of records with payroll requirements to avoid discrepancies provide proposed resolutions and commitment', '1. Maintain open communication between teachers and administration. 2. Follow DepEd guidelines on teaching hours and workload limits. 3. Regularly review policy updates affecting workload distribution', '1. Conduct routine inspections (monthly/quarterly) of all school buildings and facilities.\r\n2. Engage PTA, LGUs, and stakeholders in supporting facility improvement and repair initiatives.\r\n3. Conduct Brigada Eskwela and similar programs for collaborative maintenance.', '1. Identify and access multiple funding sources such as school MOOE, LGU support, and donations.\r\n2. Ensure transparent and efficient use of resources for infrastructure projects.', '1. Conduct regular reading programs, reading challenges, and book fairs.\r\n2. Encourage daily reading habits among learners through structured library time.', '1. Conduct routine checks of water systems, electrical wiring, and internet connectivity to ensure continuous functionality.\r\n2. Ensure proper maintenance of routers, modems, and network systems.', '', '1. Base MOOE planning on the School Improvement Plan (SIP), Annual Implementation Plan (AIP), and actual school needs.\r\n2. Maintain clear, accurate, and updated financial records.', '1. Ensure that all supporting documents (receipts, vouchers, purchase orders, and reports) are complete, accurate, and properly filed.\r\n2. Maintain a systematic filing system for easy tracking and retrieval of financial records.', 0, 0, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 1, 3, 3, 3, '', '', '', '1.Commit to aligning all contextualized materials with curriculum standards and learning competencies.\r\n2.Allocate dedicated weekly time for material development and review.\r\n3. Conduct regular learner profiling to better understand students’ needs, interests, and backgrounds.\r\n4. Participate in and advocate for continuous professional development on contextualization strategies.\r\n5. Seek regular feedback from school heads, master teachers, and peers.', '1. Commit to conducting regular diagnostic and formative assessments to identify specific learning gaps.\r\n2. Maintain updated learner progress records to guide interventions.\r\n3. Use assessment results to design targeted remediation plans', '1.Commit to maintaining a safe, inclusive, and respectful classroom atmosphere.\r\n2. Establish and reinforce clear classroom norms aligned with core values', '1. Commit to continuous training on test construction, item analysis, and data interpretation.\r\n2. Develop and maintain a validated test item bank aligned with curriculum standards.', '', '1. Commit to regularly orienting learners, parents, and school personnel on school rules, policies, procedures, and consequences related to behavior and discipline.\r\n2. Ensure that anti-bullying and child protection policies are clearly disseminated during assemblies, PTA meetings, and classroom discussions.\r\n3. Commit to the fair, consistent, and impartial enforcement of school rules across all grade levels.', '1. Ensure that all reported concerns are acted upon immediately, documented properly, and referred to appropriate authorities when necessary.\r\n2. Uphold accountability among all school personnel in safeguarding learners’ welfare at all times.', '1. Commit to continuous communication with parents and guardians regarding learner attendance and performance.\r\n2. Ensure timely and appropriate interventions for identified at-risk learners.\r\n3. Maintain accurate records to guide decision-making and support planning.', '1. Commit to inviting cultural experts, elders, and practitioners to share authentic knowledge, skills, and cultural practices.\r\n2. Ensure that cultural presentations and sharing sessions are accurate, respectful, and educational.', '1. Commit to providing printed modules, digital resources, and offline learning materials to ensure continuity of learning for all learners.\r\n2. Ensure that learning materials are aligned with curriculum standards and are learner-friendly and contextualized.', '', '1. Commit to establishing a fixed schedule of CPC meetings and activities that is agreed upon and communicated at the start of the school year.\r\n2. Commit to clearly defining and distributing CPC roles and tasks to avoid workload conflicts and ensure efficiency.\r\n3. Commit to maintaining complete, accurate, and systematic documentation of all CPC-related incidents, interventions, and preventive actions.', '1. Commit to utilizing documented records and evaluation findings in planning and decision-making.\r\n2. Commit to assigning clear responsibilities for documentation and evaluation among DRRM committee members.\r\n3. Commit to using evaluation results as a basis for enhancing DRRM plans, procedures, and preparedness strategies.', '1. Commit to fostering a school culture that promotes respect, kindness, empathy, and open communication among learners and staff.\r\n2. Reinforce school policies that support emotional safety and inclusivity.\r\n3. Use feedback from learners, teachers, and stakeholders to improve support systems and interventions.', '1. Actively explore donation drives, sponsorships, and grant opportunities to support SPED needs.\r\n2. Commit to prioritizing SNED and PWD learners’ needs in the school’s Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).', '', '', '', '', '1.Commit to ensuring that the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) is fully aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and the school’s strategic goals.\r\n2. Regularly review both plans to maintain consistency, relevance, and coherence in implementation.\r\n3. Ensure that all planned activities are specific, time-bound, and responsive to identified school needs.\r\n', '1.  Commit to establishing a fixed schedule of SGC meetings and consultations that is agreed upon at the beginning of the school year.\r\n2. Ensure timely communication and proper coordination to encourage full attendance and active participation.', '1. Commit to maintaining transparency in all PTA-related decisions and activities.\r\n2. Ensure timely dissemination of minutes and agreements to all stakeholders for transparency and follow-up actions.', '1. Strengthen stakeholder engagement by fostering a culture of gratitude and sustained collaboration.\r\n2. Commit to establishing formal agreements such as Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) or Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) with partner institutions and stakeholders.', '1. Commit to ensuring complete, accurate, and systematic documentation of all program outputs, outcomes, and impact.\r\n2. Ensure that documented data is utilized in planning, decision-making, and continuous school improvement.', '1. Utilize performance data, feedback, and self-assessment results to promptly identify gaps and design targeted interventions or action plans.\r\n2. Implement a systematic mid-year review process to evaluate individual performance against IPCR targets and identify areas for enhancement.', '1. Commit to engaging in regular monitoring activities, submitting required reports on time, and valuing feedback as a tool for improving my performance and achieving set targets effectively.', 'Establish a centralized and systematic documentation and filing system for all LAC and L&D records, both physical and digital. Use standardized folders, labeling, and indexing of documents (e.g., attendance, minutes, outputs, MOVs). Assign a documentation focal person to ensure proper filing, updating, and easy retrieval during validation or evaluation.', 'Strengthen coaching and mentoring support systems to assist personnel in understanding and complying with competency standards and qualification requirements for promotion and professional growth. Provide clear orientation, checklists, and continuous technical assistance for documentation and compliance.', '', '1.Establish a systematic updating protocol for employee master data, including scheduled quarterly reviews and immediate updates upon any personnel movement (e.g., promotion, transfer, step increment, deductions). \r\n2.Assign a designated focal person to ensure accuracy, completeness, and proper safekeeping of records.', '1. Strictly adhere to existing DepEd policies and guidelines on teaching hours, ancillary tasks, and allowable workload limits. \r\n2. Conduct regular monitoring and validation to ensure compliance and prevent overloading or underloading of personnel.', '1. Ensure that inspection results are properly documented, reported, and used as basis for maintenance planning and prioritization of repairs.\r\n2. ommit to actively engaging PTA, LGUs, and other stakeholders in supporting school infrastructure improvement and repair initiatives.', '1. Commit to identifying and accessing multiple funding sources such as school MOOE, LGU support, PTA contributions, and private donations to support infrastructure improvement projects.\r\n2. Strengthen partnerships with stakeholders and external agencies to supplement limited school resources.\r\n3. Ensure that funding proposals and requests are aligned with priority infrastructure needs identified through school assessments.', '1. Commit to conducting regular reading programs, reading challenges, and book fairs to promote literacy and a love for reading among learners.\r\n2. Commit to integrating structured library time into the school schedule to encourage consistent reading habits among learners.', '1. Commit to ensuring the regular maintenance and inspection of routers, modems, and network systems to guarantee stable internet connectivity.\r\n2. Designate ICT focal persons responsible for monitoring and addressing connectivity issues immediately.', '1. Commit to identifying and accessing additional funding sources such as LGU support, PTA contributions, donations, and external partners to support ICT infrastructure development.\r\n2. Coordinate with stakeholders and partner institutions for possible ICT equipment donations and technical assistance.', '1.Commit to ensuring that all expenditures are based on actual school needs and priorities.\r\n2. Avoid unnecessary or low-impact spending to maximize resource efficiency.', '1.Commit to maintaining a systematic, organized, and updated filing system for all financial records.', '1.Commit to maintaining complete, organized, and updated records of all stakeholder concerns, feedback, and satisfaction surveys.\r\n2. Ensure proper filing and safekeeping of both hard copy and digital documentation for easy retrieval and reference.', 0, 144, 12, 59),
