s, provide training on contextualizing peace education, and showcase best practices', 'Institutionalize item analysis in quarterly assessments, provide digital tools to ease analysis, and share results during LAC sessions', '', 'Sustain anti-bullying campaigns, strengthen peer mediation, and conduct quarterly monitoring', 'Continue awareness sessions, strengthen reporting mechanisms, and maintain coordination with LGUs and child welfare agencies', 'Intensify home visitation, provide financial assistance through partnerships, and strengthen feeding programs', 'Expand cultural activities, involve more community stakeholders, and integrate culture-sensitive practices in lessons', 'Explore partnerships with ALS providers, NGOs, and LGUs to extend access; document future initiatives', 'Explore partnerships with DepEd ALS coordinators, NGOs, and LGUs to establish an ALS program if demand arises', 'Strengthen committee operations, conduct regular meetings, and document activities for compliance', 'Update DRRM plan annually, conduct quarterly drills, and coordinate with LGUs for disaster preparedness', 'Partner with health agencies for counseling, conduct wellness programs, and integrate SEL (social-emotional learning) activities', 'Assess needs of PWD learners, plan for accessible facilities, and coordinate with DepEd SPED program for support', 'Regularly update the strategic plan, integrate monitoring tools, and ensure alignment with school improvement goals', 'Strengthen stakeholder engagement, schedule regular planning sessions, and document outputs for transparency', 'Provide leadership training, expand student-led initiatives, and integrate SSG/SPG activities into school programs', 'Explore digital platforms for communication, streamline processes, and gather stakeholder feedback for continuous improvement', 'Conduct mid-year and year-end reviews; strengthen monitoring and evaluation tools; provide training on adaptive planning; ensure documentation of implementation progress', 'Conduct stakeholder orientation; clarify roles and responsibilities; improve communication strategies; schedule meetings at convenient times', 'Provide flexible meeting schedules; enhance transparency in financial reporting; encourage volunteerism', 'Formalize Memoranda of Agreement (MOA); strengthen networking activities; maximize resource-sharing initiatives', 'Develop standardized monitoring templates; conduct quarterly evaluation meetings; integrate feedback mechanisms from teachers and learners', '', 'Streamline reporting processes; provide training on documentation; conduct regular internal audits', 'Allocate budget for professional development; integrate LACs into school calendar; encourage peer mentoring', '\r\nStrengthen linkages with DepEd and external partners; prioritize professional development in budget planning; provide equitable access to training opportunities', 'Develop a structured recognition program; allocate funds for incentives; ensure equitable recognition across all personnel', 'Strengthen coordination with division office; maintain updated payroll records; conduct regular audits to ensure accuracy', 'Regular workload review; rotate committee assignments; provide support mechanisms for teachers with heavier subject loads', 'Standardize inspection templates; conduct quarterly inspections; ensure timely follow-up on identified issues', 'Strengthen linkages with LGU and stakeholders; prioritize improvements in SIP; maximize school MOOE', 'Request support from DepEd and LGU; initiate book donation drives; designate teacher-librarian', 'Coordinate with service providers; allocate funds for ICT upgrades; establish backup systems', '\r\nRequest ICT packages from DepEd; strengthen partnerships with NGOs and LGUs; allocate funds for maintenance and upgrades', 'Streamline procurement procedures; strengthen financial planning; conduct quarterly utilization reviews', 'Maintain updated liquidation records; conduct regular internal audits; strengthen coordination with division finance office', 'Strengthen stakeholder feedback systems; improve transparency in reporting; conduct regular satisfaction surveys and follow-up actions', 1, 145, 12, 59);
INSERT INTO `sbm_ta` (`id`, `fy`, `school_id`, `q1`, `q2`, `q3`, `q4`, `q5`, `q6`, `q7`, `q8`, `q9`, `q10`, `q11`, `q12`, `q13`, `q14`, `q15`, `q16`, `q17`, `q18`, `q19`, `q20`, `q21`, `q22`, `q23`, `q24`, `q25`, `q26`, `q27`, `q28`, `q29`, `q30`, `q31`, `q32`, `q33`, `q34`, `q35`, `q36`, `q37`, `q38`, `q39`, `q40`, `q41`, `q42`, `qq1`, `qq2`, `qq3`, `qq4`, `qq5`, `qq6`, `qq7`, `qq8`, `qq9`, `qq10`, `qq11`, `qq12`, `qq13`, `qq14`, `qq15`, `qq16`, `qq17`, `qq18`, `qq19`, `qq20`, `qq21`, `qq22`, `qq23`, `qq24`, `qq25`, `qq26`, `qq27`, `qq28`, `qq29`, `qq30`, `qq31`, `qq32`, `qq33`, `qq34`, `qq35`, `qq36`, `qq37`, `qq38`, `qq39`, `qq40`, `qq41`, `qq42`, `a1`, `a2`, `a3`, `a4`, `a5`, `a6`, `a7`, `a8`, `a9`, `a10`, `a11`, `a12`, `a13`, `a14`, `a15`, `a16`, `a17`, `a18`, `a19`, `a20`, `a21`, `a22`, `a23`, `a24`, `a25`, `a26`, `a27`, `a28`, `a29`, `a30`, `a31`, `a32`, `a33`, `a34`, `a35`, `a36`, `a37`, `a38`, `a39`, `a40`, `a41`, `a42`, `f1`, `f2`, `f3`, `f4`, `f5`, `f6`, `f7`, `f8`, `f9`, `f10`, `f11`, `f12`, `f13`, `f14`, `f15`, `f16`, `f17`, `f18`, `f19`, `f20`, `f21`, `f22`, `f23`, `f24`, `f25`, `f26`, `f27`, `f29`, `f30`, `f31`, `f32`, `f33`, `f34`, `f35`, `f36`, `f37`, `f38`, `f39`, `f40`, `f41`, `f42`, `f28`, `stat`, `district`, `region`, `division`) VALUES
(642, '2026', '315808@deped.gov.ph', '', 'For Grade 10 and 12 learners of Ulip NHS who frequently achieve proficiency in all 21st-century skills and core learning areas in the National Achievement Test (NAT), several Concerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems, and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) are still observed, such as inconsistent mastery of higher-order thinking skills where learners perform well in assessments but show variability in applying concepts in complex or real-life situations; fluctuating academic performance across quarters due to differences in motivation, attendance, and study habits; moderate gaps in differentiated instruction that may not fully address the needs of both struggling and advanced learners; occasional limitations in access to updated instructional materials and technology-enhanced learning tools; varying effectiveness in the integration of 21st-century skills across subjects depending on teacher readiness and workload; and assessment practices that, while generally aligned, still rely heavily on traditional testing methods, resulting in limited opportunities for sustained formative feedback and continuous improvement.', '', '', 'Although teachers at Ulip NHS frequently conduct remediation activities to address learning gaps in reading comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics, several Concerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems, and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) are still observed, such as inconsistent learner attendance and participation in remediation sessions due to lack of motivation, time constraints, or competing responsibilities; limited instructional time that restricts the depth and continuity of remediation activities; varying effectiveness of remediation strategies depending on teacher expertise and available materials; insufficient individualized or differentiated remediation plans for learners with diverse needs; and occasional lack of updated or adequate learning resources and assessment tools to fully support targeted interventions, resulting in only partial closure of identified learning gaps despite frequent implementation of remediation programs.', 'Although teachers at Ulip NHS frequently integrate topics that promote peace and DepEd core values, several Concerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems, and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) are still observed, such as inconsistent depth of integration where values are sometimes treated as embedded concepts rather than explicitly taught and reinforced; limited instructional time that restricts deeper discussion and reflection on peace education and values formation; varying teacher readiness and confidence in effectively contextualizing and modeling core values across different learning areas; occasional difficulty in translating abstract values into measurable learner behaviors and performance tasks; and limited assessment tools that fully capture affective learning outcomes, resulting in frequent but not fully sustained or deeply internalized manifestation of peace education and DepEd core values among learners.', 'Although the school conducts test item analysis to inform its teaching and learning process, the concerns, issues, gaps, problems, and bottlenecks (CIGPBs) are rarely manifested and occur only on limited occasions, such as occasional delays in the completion and submission of item analysis results due to time constraints and workload; minimal inconsistencies in the depth of analysis where some test items are not fully reviewed for higher-order thinking skills alignment; limited utilization of results in instructional planning by a few teachers, resulting in partial translation of data into targeted interventions; and occasional lack of uniform templates or standardization in interpreting item analysis data, though overall implementation remains strong and functional in supporting teaching and learning improvements.', '', 'Although the school reports zero child bullying incidence, frequently manifested CIGPBs include underreporting of minor or hidden cases due to fear of retaliation, limited student understanding of subtle forms of bullying such as cyberbullying and social exclusion, inconsistent implementation and monitoring of anti-bullying policies, and weak reporting and documentation systems. There are also gaps in continuous teacher training on early detection, limited parental involvement in reinforcing positive behavior, insufficient monitoring of school “blind spots” and online spaces, and student reluctance to report or intervene due to peer pressure. In some cases, complacency may also develop when the school is perceived as already safe, affecting sustained vigilance and proactive prevention efforts.', 'Although the school reports zero child abuse incidence, frequently manifested CIGPBs include possible underreporting of sensitive cases due to fear, stigma, or lack of awareness among learners about what constitutes abuse and where to report it. There are also gaps in continuous training of teachers and staff on child protection policies and early warning signs, limited student and parent understanding of reporting mechanisms, and insufficient monitoring of potential risk situations in both school and online environments. In addition, inconsistencies in the strict implementation of child protection protocols and possible complacency due to the “zero incidence” status may affect proactive safeguarding efforts.', '', '', 'Frequently manifested CIGPBs include irregular attendance and low completion rates among disadvantaged learners, Out-of-School Youths (OSYs), and adult learners due to work commitments, financial constraints, and family responsibilities. There are also gaps in flexible learning delivery such as limited resources for modular or blended instruction, inconsistent monitoring and follow-up of learners, and difficulty in sustaining learner motivation. Other concerns include inadequate learning support materials tailored to diverse learning needs, limited availability of trained facilitators for alternative learning modalities, and challenges in coordinating schedules that accommodate adult learners’ time constraints.', '', '', '', '', 'Frequently manifested CIGPBs include inadequate or outdated SPED and PWD-friendly facilities, limited availability of assistive devices and specialized learning materials, and insufficient funding for continuous improvement and maintenance of accessible infrastructure. There are also gaps in trained personnel to handle diverse special education needs, inconsistent implementation of inclusive practices, and challenges in fully complying with accessibility standards. Additionally, limited awareness among stakeholders and difficulties in sustaining individualized support for learners with disabilities may affect the overall effectiveness of inclusive education efforts.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'At ULIP NHS, the CIGPBs encountered in the functional library being frequently manifested include the insufficient and outdated library resources such as books and reference materials, which limit learner access to updated information. There may also be inadequate budget allocation for the improvement and maintenance of library facilities and ICT resources. Limited staffing or lack of a full-time trained librarian can affect efficient library management and service delivery. In addition, low utilization of the library by learners and teachers due to lack of reading programs or integration in instruction, as well as limited space, poor ventilation, or inadequate learning environment, further hinder the full functionality of the library.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Facilitating factors for the consistent (always manifested) preparation of contextualized learning materials by Ulip NHS teachers include strong teacher competence and creativity in adapting lessons to learners’ needs, continuous participation in professional development focused on curriculum contextualization and learner-centered strategies, and a shared commitment among teachers to improve instructional quality. Supportive school leadership that encourages innovation, provides guidance, and recognizes effective teaching practices also strengthens this consistency. In addition, collaboration among teachers through sharing of instructional resources, availability of reference materials and curriculum guides, and a strong understanding of learners’ backgrounds and learning gaps further enable the regular and sustained production of relevant, contextualized learning materials.', '', '', '', 'Facilitating factors for the consistent (always manifested) engagement of local industries to strengthen TLE-TVL course offerings include strong and sustained partnerships between the school and industry stakeholders built on mutual trust and shared goals for learner development. Active support from school leadership in establishing, maintaining, and expanding linkages also ensures continuity of collaboration. Teachers’ proactive coordination and effective communication with industry partners further strengthen implementation, while the presence of clear DepEd guidelines on work immersion and industry partnerships provides a solid framework for engagement. In addition, the commitment of local industries to support skills development, combined with learners’ enthusiasm for hands-on training and real-world exposure, contributes to the continuous and sustained manifestation of this indicator.', '', '', 'The consistent reduction of dropout incidence is facilitated by strong school retention programs, effective learner support systems such as remedial classes and guidance counseling, and active monitoring of at-risk students through early warning mechanisms. It is further supported by strong teacher-student relationships, engaging and learner-centered instruction, and regular communication with parents or guardians to address attendance and performance concerns. In addition, the provision of financial assistance, feeding programs, and partnerships with stakeholders help address socio-economic barriers, while school-wide interventions and continuous follow-up strategies ensure learners remain motivated and actively participating in school.', 'The consistent implementation of culture-sensitive activities is facilitated by strong school leadership that prioritizes inclusivity and respect for diversity, as well as active collaboration with parents, Indigenous Peoples (IP) leaders, and community stakeholders in designing culturally relevant programs. It is further supported by teachers’ awareness and training on cultural sensitivity, integration of local traditions and values into the curriculum, and availability of school policies that promote respect for diverse beliefs and practices. Regular observance of cultural celebrations and inclusive classroom practices also strengthen learner engagement and foster a respectful and culturally responsive learning environment.', '', 'The consistent functionality of the school-based ALS program is facilitated by strong institutional support and commitment from school leadership, active collaboration with ALS implementers and community learning facilitators, and continuous alignment with DepEd guidelines and policies. It is further strengthened by the availability of learning materials and flexible instructional approaches suited for OSYs and adult learners, as well as strong community partnerships that help identify and encourage potential learners. Regular monitoring, dedicated ALS focal persons, and responsive learner support systems also contribute to the sustained effectiveness of the program.', 'The consistent functionality of the Child Protection Committee is facilitated by strong school leadership support, clear implementation of the Child Protection Policy, and well-defined roles and responsibilities among committee members. It is further strengthened by regular meetings, continuous capacity-building and training on child protection laws and protocols, and active collaboration with teachers, parents, and relevant stakeholders. The availability of reporting and monitoring systems, along with a shared commitment to safeguarding learners’ welfare, also ensures the committee operates effectively and proactively.', 'The consistent implementation of a functional DRRM plan is facilitated by strong leadership support and clear policy direction, active DRRM coordinators and committees, and regular training and drills for students and staff. It is further strengthened by the availability of updated risk assessments, emergency preparedness plans, and adequate resources such as first aid kits and safety equipment. Strong coordination with local government units and disaster response agencies, along with continuous monitoring, evaluation, and awareness campaigns, ensures that the school remains prepared, responsive, and resilient in times of emergencies.', 'The consistent functionality of the school’s mental wellness support mechanism is facilitated by strong leadership support and clear policies promoting mental health, the presence of trained guidance counselors or designated personnel, and regular implementation of wellness programs and activities. It is further strengthened by a supportive and inclusive school climate, active involvement of teachers and parents, accessible counseling and referral services, and continuous awareness campaigns that reduce stigma and encourage help-seeking among learners.', '', 'Ulip NHS develops a strategic plan which is always manifested” include strong and committed school leadership that actively drives the planning process, the active participation and collaboration of teachers and staff in setting goals and priorities, and the availability of reliable school data that supports evidence-based decision-making. The continuous conduct of planning activities and professional learning sessions strengthens alignment and understanding of goals, while strong stakeholder support from parents, LGUs, and community partners enhances implementation. In addition, clear DepEd guidelines, an established planning committee, effective communication among personnel, and a culture of accountability and continuous improvement all contribute to the consistent development and manifestation of the school’s strategic plan.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the indicator “The school has a functional school-community planning team” include strong and active leadership that organizes and sustains the planning team, active participation of committed teachers and community stakeholders, and clear roles and responsibilities among members that promote accountability and collaboration. The presence of supportive LGU and PTA involvement, regular meetings and consultations, and strong communication channels between the school and the community also strengthen coordination. In addition, the use of data-driven planning, adherence to DepEd guidelines, and a shared commitment to school improvement contribute to the team’s consistent and effective functionality.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested functionality of the Supreme Student Government include strong support and guidance from school administration and advisers, active student participation and leadership development opportunities, and clear policies and structures that define roles and responsibilities of officers. Regular meetings, planning sessions, and school-wide activities strengthen student engagement and governance, while continuous mentoring from teachers helps build leadership skills and accountability. In addition, strong collaboration with school programs and the presence of a culture that values student voice and participation contribute to the effective and sustained functionality of the Supreme Student Government.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested innovation in the provision of frontline services to stakeholders include strong and proactive school leadership that encourages creativity and continuous improvement in service delivery, as well as committed and customer-oriented personnel who prioritize responsiveness to stakeholders’ needs. The presence of ICT tools and digital platforms for faster communication and transactions, along with established feedback mechanisms, supports efficient service delivery. Continuous training and capacity-building of staff, strong collaboration with stakeholders, and a culture of openness to innovation and improvement further contribute to the school’s effective and consistent delivery of improved frontline services.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested operationalization of the school’s strategic plan through an implementation plan include strong and committed school leadership that ensures clear translation of goals into actionable activities, and active participation of teachers and stakeholders in planning and execution. The presence of a well-structured implementation framework with clear timelines, assigned responsibilities, and measurable targets supports effective execution. Regular monitoring, evaluation, and feedback mechanisms help track progress and address gaps promptly, while availability of resources, data-driven decision-making, and strong coordination among committees further ensure that the implementation plan is consistently carried out.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested functionality of the School Governance Council (SGC) include strong leadership support that actively engages and empowers council members, and the active participation of committed stakeholders such as parents, LGU representatives, teachers, and community partners. Clear policies, defined roles, and regular meetings ensure organized governance and decision-making, while effective communication and collaboration among members strengthen coordination. The presence of shared goals for school improvement, transparency in planning and implementation, and a strong culture of partnership and accountability further contribute to the SGC’s consistent functionality and effectiveness.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested functionality of the Parent-Teacher Association (PTA) include strong collaboration and open communication between parents and school personnel, active participation of parents in school programs and activities, and strong leadership from PTA officers and school advisers. Regular meetings, transparent financial management, and clearly defined roles and responsibilities help ensure organized operations. The support of school administration, shared commitment to learners’ welfare, and strong community involvement further strengthen the PTA’s continuous engagement and effective contribution to school development.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested collaboration with stakeholders and other schools in strengthening partnerships include strong and proactive school leadership that actively builds and maintains linkages, as well as the commitment of teachers and staff to engage in collaborative activities. Active participation of LGUs, parents, alumni, and community partners, along with established networks with nearby schools, supports shared learning and resource sharing. Regular communication, joint planning activities, and formal partnership agreements further strengthen coordination, while a shared vision for school improvement and learner development ensures sustained and meaningful collaboration.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested monitoring and evaluation of programs, projects, and activities include strong leadership that prioritizes accountability and evidence-based management, as well as the active involvement of teachers and committee heads in tracking implementation. The presence of clear monitoring tools, schedules, and performance indicators ensures systematic evaluation of activities. Regular reporting mechanisms, data-driven decision-making, and continuous feedback from stakeholders further support effective assessment, while a culture of transparency, collaboration, and commitment to continuous improvement strengthens the overall monitoring and evaluation process.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested satisfactory rating from internal and external stakeholders include strong and responsive school leadership that prioritizes quality service and continuous improvement, as well as the commitment and professionalism of teachers and staff in delivering effective programs and services. Strong collaboration and communication with parents, LGUs, and community partners help ensure stakeholder needs are addressed, while regular feedback mechanisms allow the school to respond promptly to concerns. The presence of a positive school culture, transparency in operations, and sustained implementation of school improvement initiatives further contribute to maintaining a satisfactory level of stakeholder satisfaction.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested very satisfactory rating in the Individual Performance Commitment and Review (IPCR) of school personnel include strong instructional and administrative leadership that provides clear performance targets and continuous guidance, as well as the commitment and professionalism of teachers and staff in fulfilling their duties. Regular coaching, mentoring, and performance monitoring support staff development, while access to training and capacity-building opportunities enhances competence and efficiency. Clear performance indicators, collaborative work culture, and constructive feedback mechanisms further contribute to consistent achievement of very satisfactory performance ratings among school personnel.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested very satisfactory rating in the Office Performance Commitment and Review (OPCR) include strong and effective leadership that ensures clear direction, well-defined office targets, and continuous supervision of performance. The commitment and collaboration of school personnel in achieving shared goals, along with efficient work systems and clearly assigned roles and responsibilities, support smooth office operations. Regular monitoring, data-driven decision-making, and constructive feedback mechanisms help maintain accountability and performance standards, while access to training, adequate resources, and a culture of teamwork and continuous improvement further contribute to the consistent achievement of very satisfactory office performance.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested conduct of needs-based Learning Action Cells (LACs) and Learning & Development activities include strong instructional leadership that prioritizes teacher growth and data-driven professional development, as well as the active participation and collaboration of teachers in identifying learning needs. The availability of training resources, clear planning schedules, and alignment with DepEd priorities ensure relevance and consistency of activities. Supportive school management, culture of continuous improvement, and effective feedback mechanisms further strengthen the implementation of LAC sessions and professional development programs, leading to sustained instructional enhancement.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested promotion and continuous professional development of personnel include strong and supportive school leadership that prioritizes staff growth and career advancement, as well as clear policies and guidelines for promotion and professional development aligned with DepEd standards. Active participation of personnel in training, seminars, and postgraduate studies, along with access to relevant learning and development opportunities, further strengthens professional growth. Regular performance monitoring, mentoring, and coaching support career progression, while a culture of continuous improvement and institutional support ensures sustained development of all school personnel.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested recognition and rewarding of milestone achievements of personnel include strong leadership commitment to valuing employee contributions, as well as established policies and systems for awards and recognition aligned with DepEd guidelines. Regular monitoring of performance achievements and accomplishments ensures that deserving personnel are identified and acknowledged in a timely manner. Active participation of the recognition committee, transparency in selection processes, and availability of incentives and reward mechanisms further support fair and consistent recognition practices. A positive organizational culture that promotes appreciation, motivation, and professional excellence also contributes to sustaining this practice.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested timely receipt of correct salaries, allowances, and other compensation include efficient coordination between the school, division office, and payroll personnel, as well as strict adherence to government accounting and disbursement guidelines. The presence of accurate and updated personnel records ensures correct computation of salaries and benefits, while strong administrative systems and ICT-based payroll processing support timely release of funds. Effective monitoring, verification procedures, and responsive communication among responsible offices further ensure accuracy, transparency, and punctuality in the release of personnel compensation.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested fair and equitable distribution of teacher workload include strong and transparent instructional leadership that ensures proper assignment of tasks based on qualifications, expertise, and teaching loads. Clear policies and guidelines from DepEd on workload standards support equitable distribution, while collaborative planning among school heads, department heads, and teachers ensures balanced assignments. Regular monitoring and consultation, accurate workload tracking, and a culture of fairness and teamwork further contribute to maintaining equity and preventing overload among teaching personnel.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested inspection of infrastructure and facilities include strong school leadership that prioritizes safety, functionality, and maintenance of school resources, as well as the presence of a designated inspection and maintenance team. Regular schedules for facility checks, adherence to safety standards and DepEd guidelines, and proper documentation of inspection results ensure systematic monitoring. Active involvement of stakeholders in reporting facility concerns, availability of maintenance support, and a culture of responsibility in caring for school facilities further strengthen the continuous inspection and upkeep of infrastructure.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested initiation of improvement of infrastructure and facilities include strong and proactive school leadership that prioritizes continuous school development and safety, as well as the presence of a functional school improvement planning process. Regular assessment of facility needs, availability of data-based planning inputs, and strong coordination with DepEd, LGU, and stakeholders support timely upgrading of facilities. Active stakeholder participation, proper allocation and utilization of resources, and a shared commitment to providing a safe and conducive learning environment further contribute to continuous infrastructure improvement initiatives.', '', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested functionality of water, electric, and internet facilities include strong coordination between the school administration and utility service providers to ensure continuous supply and quick response to issues, as well as regular maintenance and monitoring of facilities. The availability of allocated budget for utilities supports uninterrupted services, while the presence of ICT infrastructure management systems helps maintain stable internet connectivity. Proactive school leadership, prompt reporting and repair of technical issues, and stakeholder support further ensure that essential utilities remain functional and consistently available to support teaching, learning, and school operations.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested functionality of the computer laboratory/classroom include strong school leadership support in maintaining and upgrading ICT facilities, as well as the presence of trained personnel or ICT coordinators who manage and monitor laboratory use. Regular maintenance and technical support ensure that computers and equipment remain operational, while adequate allocation of resources supports software updates and repairs. Integration of ICT in teaching and learning, scheduled laboratory use, and adherence to proper utilization guidelines further enhance the consistent functionality and effective use of the computer laboratory.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested 72–100% utilization rate of Maintenance and Other Operating Expenses (MOOE) include strong financial planning and budgeting aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP), as well as active leadership that ensures proper prioritization of expenditures. Efficient procurement and disbursement processes, guided by DepEd financial policies, support timely and appropriate use of funds. Regular monitoring of budget utilization, transparent financial reporting, and active participation of school committees in planning and decision-making further ensure accountability. In addition, effective coordination among personnel and a culture of responsible fiscal management contribute to the optimal and consistent utilization of MOOE resources.', 'At ULIP NHS, the facilitating factors for the always manifested 100% liquidation of utilized MOOE include strict adherence to DepEd financial policies and guidelines, as well as strong leadership oversight in ensuring timely and accurate submission of liquidation reports. Efficient coordination between the school, accounting, and supply units supports proper documentation and validation of expenses, while the presence of trained administrative and finance personnel ensures compliance with accounting procedures. Regular monitoring of financial transactions, organized record-keeping, and a culture of accountability and transparency further contribute to the complete and timely liquidation of MOOE funds.', 0, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 2, 2, 2, 6, 5, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 6, 2, 6, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, '', 'To address these CIGPBs, Ulip NHS commits to strengthening the consistent integration of higher-order thinking skills and real-life application in daily instruction through enhanced lesson planning, contextualized activities, and performance-based tasks; intensifying differentiated instruction to better support both struggling and advanced learners; providing continuous teacher training and coaching focused on 21st-century skills integration and innovative assessment practices; improving access to updated instructional materials and ICT resources through stronger school resource planning and partnerships; and reinforcing the use of formative assessment and regular feedback mechanisms to monitor learner progress and ensure timely interventions for sustained academic improvement.', '', 'To sustain and further strengthen the consistent preparation of contextualized learning materials, Ulip NHS commits to continuously enhancing teachers’ competencies through regular training and upskilling on curriculum contextualization and innovative instructional design, while reinforcing collaborative practices such as Learning Action Cells (LACs) and peer sharing of best practices. The school also commits to providing strong instructional leadership and support systems that encourage creativity and recognize exemplary outputs, alongside ensuring the availability of updated curriculum guides, reference materials, and ICT resources. Furthermore, a sustained focus on understanding learners’ needs through regular assessment and feedback will be prioritized to ensure that all instructional materials remain relevant, responsive, and aligned with learners’ contexts.', 'To address these CIGPBs, Ulip NHS commits to strengthening the implementation of structured and well-scheduled remediation programs with improved monitoring of learner attendance and participation, alongside intensified learner motivation strategies and parental engagement to encourage consistent attendance. Teachers will be supported through continuous professional development focused on effective remediation strategies, differentiated instruction, and data-driven intervention planning. The school also commits to maximizing instructional time through well-planned remediation schedules and integrating targeted interventions within regular classes when necessary. In addition, Ulip NHS will enhance the provision and development of updated, context-based, and level-appropriate learning resources and assessment tools to better support individualized learning needs, ensuring more effective and sustained closure of learning gaps in reading comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics.', 'To address these CIGPBs, Ulip NHS commits to strengthening the consistent and intentional integration of peace education and DepEd core values across all learning areas through well-planned, explicit, and contextualized lesson integration. Teachers will be supported through continuous professional development, coaching, and Learning Action Cells focused on values education strategies, formative assessment of affective learning, and the use of performance tasks that reflect real-life application of core values. The school also commits to developing and utilizing appropriate tools for assessing learners’ values formation, enhancing instructional planning time for deeper integration, and promoting a whole-school culture that models peace, respect, and responsibility to ensure meaningful and sustained internalization of DepEd core values among learners.', 'To further strengthen the effective use of test item analysis, Ulip NHS commits to institutionalizing a standardized and timely process for the preparation, submission, and utilization of item analysis results across all subject areas. Teachers will be continuously guided and trained on deeper data interpretation to ensure that results are consistently translated into targeted instructional interventions and improved lesson planning. The school also commits to enhancing collaboration through regular Learning Action Cells (LACs) focused on data-driven instruction, as well as providing templates and digital tools to ensure uniformity and efficiency in analysis. Through strong instructional supervision and monitoring, Ulip NHS will ensure that test item analysis is fully maximized as a key tool for improving teaching quality and learner performance.', 'To further strengthen and sustain the engagement of local industries in enhancing the TLE-TVL course offerings, Ulip NHS commits to expanding and formalizing partnerships through strengthened Memoranda of Agreement (MOA) with more diverse industry stakeholders. The school will intensify coordination and networking activities to increase the number of partner industries and ensure alignment with updated TLE-TVL curriculum standards. Continuous collaboration meetings, joint planning, and regular monitoring of work immersion programs will be conducted to address scheduling and implementation concerns. Teachers will also be supported in building stronger industry linkages and ensuring effective supervision of learners during immersion. Furthermore, the school commits to continuously improving alignment between school-based instruction and industry practices to ensure learners gain relevant, updated, and employable skills.', 'To sustain a zero child bullying incidence, the school commits to strengthening the implementation of its anti-bullying policy through continuous awareness campaigns, regular orientation for students, parents, and staff, and capacity-building for teachers on early detection and intervention of bullying behaviors. It will enhance monitoring systems in both physical and digital spaces, establish a more accessible and confidential reporting mechanism, and conduct regular student climate surveys to validate safety conditions. The school also commits to intensifying guidance and counseling services, promoting values formation and peer support programs, and strengthening stakeholder collaboration to ensure a consistently safe, inclusive, and supportive learning environment.', 'o sustain zero child abuse incidence, the school commits to strengthening its Child Protection Policy through continuous orientation and education of learners, parents, and staff on child rights, prevention, and proper reporting procedures, as well as regular capacity-building for teachers and personnel on early detection and appropriate response to abuse cases. It will enhance accessible and confidential reporting systems, intensify monitoring of potential risk areas in school and online platforms, and strengthen guidance and counseling services. The school also commits to sustaining strong collaboration with parents and child protection agencies to ensure a safe, responsive, and fully protective learning environment for all learners.', 'To further sustain and improve the reduction of dropout incidence, the school commits to strengthening its learner retention programs through intensified early warning and tracking systems for at-risk learners, regular home visitation, and close coordination with parents and guardians. It will continue providing targeted academic support such as remediation and tutoring, strengthen guidance and counseling services, and enhance learner engagement through relevant and inclusive teaching strategies. The school also commits to expanding partnerships with stakeholders to provide financial, nutritional, and psychosocial support, ensuring that all learners are continuously motivated, supported, and retained in school.', 'To further strengthen the conduct of culture-sensitive activities, the school commits to continuously integrating local culture, traditions, and indigenous knowledge into teaching and learning activities, and ensuring that all programs are inclusive and respectful of diverse learners’ backgrounds. It will enhance teacher training on cultural responsiveness, strengthen partnerships with community elders and stakeholders, and regularly review school programs to ensure cultural appropriateness. The school also commits to sustaining meaningful cultural celebrations and promoting respect and appreciation of diversity among learners to foster an inclusive and harmonious school environment.', 'To strengthen access to learning experiences for disadvantaged, OSYs, and adult learners, the school commits to enhancing flexible learning modalities such as modular and blended learning, and strengthening alternative learning programs that accommodate varied schedules and learning needs. It will intensify monitoring and home-based follow-ups, provide targeted instructional support and learning materials, and strengthen coordination with parents, community leaders, and partner agencies. The school also commits to improving learner motivation through counseling and support services, ensuring inclusive and accessible education opportunities for all marginalized learners.', 'To further strengthen the school-based ALS program, the school commits to sustaining and enhancing program implementation through continuous coordination with ALS implementers, community learning facilitators, and local stakeholders to ensure wider reach and learner participation. It will improve monitoring and tracking of ALS learners, provide adequate learning resources and support materials, and intensify advocacy to encourage more OSYs and adult learners to enroll. The school also commits to strengthening learner support services, capacity-building for ALS personnel, and sustained community engagement to ensure effective, inclusive, and flexible learning opportunities for all.', 'To further strengthen the functionality of the Child Protection Committee, the school commits to sustaining regular meetings and continuous capacity-building of its members on updated child protection policies and response protocols, while ensuring strict and consistent implementation of all safeguarding measures. It will enhance coordination with parents, teachers, and external agencies, improve confidential reporting and monitoring systems, and intensify awareness campaigns for learners. The school also commits to regularly reviewing and improving its child protection strategies to ensure a safe, responsive, and child-friendly learning environment.', 'To further strengthen the implementation of the DRRM plan, the school commits to continuously updating and enhancing its disaster preparedness and response strategies through regular risk assessments, drills, and capacity-building activities for students and staff. It will ensure the availability and maintenance of emergency resources and safety equipment, strengthen coordination with local government units and disaster response agencies, and intensify awareness campaigns on disaster readiness. The school also commits to regular monitoring and evaluation of DRRM practices to ensure a proactive, responsive, and resilient school environment.', 'To further strengthen the school’s mental wellness support mechanism, the school commits to sustaining comprehensive mental health programs through continuous capacity-building of teachers and designated personnel, regular wellness activities, and accessible counseling and referral services. It will enhance early identification and intervention strategies, strengthen partnerships with parents and mental health professionals, and intensify awareness campaigns to promote a stigma-free environment. The school also commits to regularly monitoring and improving its mental wellness initiatives to ensure responsive, inclusive, and learner-centered support for all.', 'To strengthen SPED and PWD-friendly facilities, the school commits to continuously improving accessibility through the upgrading of ramps, comfort rooms, and learning spaces, as well as the provision of appropriate assistive devices and learning materials for learners with special needs. It will intensify capacity-building for teachers on inclusive education strategies, strengthen partnerships with LGUs and stakeholders for resource support, and ensure strict compliance with accessibility standards. The school also commits to promoting a more inclusive school culture and regularly monitoring and evaluating its facilities and services to better address the needs of learners with disabilities.', 'To further strengthen the consistent implementation of the school’s strategic plan, ULIP NHS commits to enhancing collaborative planning through regular sessions with teachers and stakeholders, strengthening data-driven decision-making through updated and accurate school data, and reinforcing monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to track progress effectively. The school also resolves to sustain strong leadership support, intensify stakeholder engagement, and provide continuous capacity-building activities for personnel to ensure full alignment and successful realization of the strategic plan.', 'ULIP NHS commits to further strengthen its school-community planning team by sustaining regular and well-documented meetings, enhancing stakeholder engagement through active participation of PTA, LGU, and community partners, and clearly defining roles and responsibilities for more efficient coordination. The school also resolves to strengthen data-driven planning, improve communication channels, and provide continuous capacity-building activities for team members to ensure more effective collaboration and sustained implementation of school programs and initiatives.', 'ULIP NHS commits to further strengthen the Supreme Student Government by sustaining active student participation through meaningful leadership opportunities, enhancing adviser support and mentoring programs, and ensuring regular, well-organized meetings and planning sessions. The school also resolves to provide continuous leadership training for student officers, strengthen coordination with school programs and activities, and promote greater student voice and involvement in school governance to ensure the SSG remains functional, responsive, and impactful.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain and further enhance its innovative frontline services by continuously improving digital and ICT-based systems for faster and more efficient transactions, strengthening feedback mechanisms to better respond to stakeholder needs, and providing regular training for personnel to ensure quality service delivery. The school also resolves to promote a culture of innovation and responsiveness among staff, strengthen collaboration with stakeholders, and ensure continuous monitoring and evaluation of services to maintain efficiency, accessibility, and client satisfaction.', 'ULIP NHS commits to further strengthen the operationalization of its strategic plan by ensuring that all programs and activities are clearly aligned with the implementation plan, supported by updated and accurate data, and reinforced through regular monitoring and evaluation. The school also resolves to enhance collaboration among committees, sustain strong leadership oversight, and provide continuous capacity-building for personnel to ensure efficient execution, timely adjustments, and full achievement of planned goals and targets.', 'ULIP NHS commits to further strengthen the School Governance Council by sustaining active and regular participation of all stakeholders, ensuring well-planned and documented meetings, and reinforcing clear roles and responsibilities among members. The school also resolves to enhance transparency and communication in all governance processes, strengthen collaborative decision-making, and continuously engage LGU, PTA, and community partners to support school programs and initiatives for sustained school improvement.', 'ULIP NHS commits to further strengthen the Parent-Teacher Association by sustaining active parent participation in school activities, ensuring regular and well-documented meetings, and promoting transparency and accountability in all PTA operations. The school also resolves to enhance collaboration between parents, teachers, and school leadership, strengthen communication channels, and continuously engage stakeholders in programs that support learner development and overall school improvement.', 'ULIP NHS commits to further strengthen collaboration with stakeholders and partner schools by sustaining active engagement through regular joint activities, meetings, and shared programs that support learner development. The school also resolves to enhance partnership-building initiatives, strengthen communication and coordination mechanisms, and formalize collaborative agreements to ensure continuity and effectiveness of partnerships for sustained school improvement.', 'ULIP NHS commits to further strengthen its monitoring and evaluation system by ensuring the consistent use of standardized tools and performance indicators in tracking all programs, projects, and activities. The school also resolves to enhance regular reporting and feedback mechanisms, strengthen data-driven decision-making, and sustain active involvement of all committees and stakeholders to ensure timely assessment, continuous improvement, and effective implementation of school initiatives.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain and further enhance the very satisfactory performance of school personnel by strengthening continuous coaching and mentoring, ensuring clear alignment of duties with performance indicators, and providing regular professional development opportunities. The school also resolves to reinforce performance monitoring and feedback mechanisms, promote a culture of accountability and excellence, and support collaborative practices that will help maintain and further improve individual performance ratings.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain and further improve its very satisfactory Office Performance Commitment and Review (OPCR) rating by strengthening strategic planning, ensuring clear alignment of office targets with DepEd priorities, and enhancing monitoring and evaluation systems. The school also resolves to promote efficiency and accountability among personnel, provide continuous capacity-building and professional development, and strengthen collaboration and communication within the organization to ensure consistent and improved office performance outcomes.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain and further strengthen its needs-based Learning Action Cells and Learning & Development activities by ensuring continuous identification of teachers’ development needs through data-driven assessment and feedback. The school also resolves to enhance the regular conduct of relevant LAC sessions, strengthen collaboration among teachers and facilitators, and provide adequate support and resources to ensure meaningful, responsive, and sustained professional development aligned with instructional improvement.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain and further strengthen the promotion and continuous professional development of its personnel by ensuring equal access to relevant training, scholarships, and career advancement opportunities. The school also resolves to enhance mentoring and coaching programs, strengthen performance-based development planning, and continuously support staff participation in professional growth activities to ensure sustained competence, motivation, and career progression.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain and further strengthen its recognition and reward system by ensuring timely, fair, and transparent acknowledgment of personnel achievements and milestones. The school also resolves to enhance existing incentives and recognition programs, strengthen the role of the awards committee, and continuously promote a culture of appreciation and excellence to motivate personnel and sustain high performance.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain the timely and accurate release of salaries, allowances, and other compensation by ensuring continuous coordination with the division office and relevant units, maintaining updated and accurate personnel records, and strengthening internal verification and monitoring processes. The school also resolves to further improve documentation and ICT-based payroll systems and promote efficient communication among responsible personnel to prevent delays and ensure accuracy and transparency in all financial transactions.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain the fair and equitable distribution of teacher workload by continuously adhering to DepEd guidelines, ensuring transparent planning and consultation in assigning tasks, and regularly reviewing workload distribution. The school also resolves to strengthen monitoring mechanisms, promote open communication among staff, and ensure that teaching assignments remain balanced to support teacher well-being, efficiency, and instructional quality.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain and further strengthen the regular inspection of its infrastructure and facilities by maintaining a systematic schedule of checks, ensuring prompt reporting and resolution of identified issues, and reinforcing the roles of designated maintenance and safety committees. The school also resolves to strengthen stakeholder involvement in facility monitoring, improve coordination for timely repairs, and uphold compliance with safety standards to ensure a secure and conducive learning environment.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain and further strengthen the continuous improvement of its infrastructure and facilities by prioritizing data-driven planning, strengthening coordination with DepEd, LGU, and stakeholders, and ensuring proper allocation and utilization of available resources. The school also resolves to intensify stakeholder engagement, regularly assess facility needs, and implement timely improvement projects to provide a safe, functional, and conducive learning environment for all learners and personnel.', 'ULIP NHS commits to strengthen the functionality of its school library by allocating resources for the acquisition of updated books and ICT-based learning materials, and by seeking support from stakeholders and partners for library improvement. The school also resolves to enhance library utilization through reading programs and integration of library resources in instruction, assign trained personnel or designate a competent library-in-charge, and improve the physical condition of the library to provide a more conducive learning environment for learners and teachers.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain the continuous functionality of its water, electric, and internet facilities by strengthening regular maintenance and monitoring systems, ensuring timely coordination with utility service providers, and allocating appropriate resources for immediate repairs and upgrades. The school also resolves to enhance ICT infrastructure management, promote efficient reporting of issues, and maintain strong stakeholder collaboration to ensure uninterrupted and reliable utility services that support effective teaching and learning.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain and further enhance the functionality of its computer laboratory by ensuring regular maintenance and timely repair of ICT equipment, continuous upgrading of software and hardware as resources allow, and strengthening coordination with ICT personnel and service providers. The school also resolves to maximize the use of the laboratory through structured scheduling, promote ICT integration in instruction, and allocate appropriate resources to ensure that learners and teachers have consistent access to functional and up-to-date computer facilities.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain and further improve the efficient utilization of its MOOE by ensuring that all expenditures are aligned with the School Improvement Plan and prioritized based on urgent school needs. The school also resolves to strengthen financial planning, monitoring, and reporting systems, uphold transparency and accountability in all transactions, and continuously enhance coordination among committees to ensure the proper, timely, and effective use of resources.', 'ULIP NHS commits to sustain the 100% timely liquidation of its MOOE by strictly adhering to DepEd accounting and auditing rules, ensuring complete and accurate documentation of all expenditures, and strengthening internal monitoring and validation processes. The school also resolves to enhance coordination among responsible personnel, maintain organized financial records, and uphold transparency and accountability to ensure continuous compliance and efficient financial management.', 'ULIP NHS commits to continuously improve its services and stakeholder engagement by sustaining high standards of teaching and school operations, strengthening feedback and grievance mechanisms, and ensuring prompt and appropriate responses to stakeholder concerns. The school also resolves to enhance collaboration with internal and external stakeholders, intensify quality assurance and monitoring practices, and implement continuous improvement initiatives to maintain and further elevate stakeholder satisfaction.', 1, 121, 12, 57);
