y of a designated School Learning Resource Center that is accessible, organized, and conducive to learning', 'Allocation of maintenance funds from MOOE for utility bills', '', 'Timely submission of financial reports, liquidation documents, and supporting documents', 'Strict compliance with financial policies and liquidation guidelines of the Department of Education and Commission on Audit (COA) rules', 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 6, 2, 2, 2, 6, 6, 5, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Conduct targeted literacy and numeracy intervention sessions for all struggling learners', '1. Use data analytics from test results to guide school-based remediation and/or interventions\r\n2. Strengthen reading comprehension across all learning areas', 'Not Applicable', '1. Sustain and strengthen SLAC sessions focused on the development of contextualized learning materials\r\n2. Allocate school funds from the MOOE for the reproduction and development of localized materials\r\n3. Promote inclusive practices ensuring learning materials are gender-responsive and culturally sensitive', '1. Strengthen school-based remediation programs with structured schedules per subject area\r\n2. Allocate resources from school MOOE for printing and reproduction of intervention materials\r\n3. Establish regular monitoring and evaluation of learner progress during remediation\r\n4. Engage parents and/or guardians through home-based reading and practice support activities', '1. Strengthen monitoring of lesson plans to ensure consistent values integration\r\n2. Strengthen integration of peace education and Core Values across all learning areas, not only Values Education subjects', '1. Utilize ICT tools (example: spreadsheets and automated forms) to streamline analysis and reporting\r\n2. Use item analysis results to redesign lesson plans and remediation activities', 'Not Applicable', '1. Enhance the functionality of the Child Protection Committee with clear roles and reporting systems\r\n2. Strengthen partnership with parents and community stakeholders in behavior monitoring', '1. Conduct regular capacity-building for all school personnel on child safeguarding and protection\r\n2. Enhance awareness campaigns for learners and parents on identifying and reporting abuse', '1. Conduct home visitation and parental counseling for at-risk learners\r\n2. Strengthen parent-teacher communication channels', 'Institutionalize regular culture-sensitive school activities integrated into the School Annual Implementation Plan', 'Implement regular monitoring and assessment of learner progress and program effectiveness', 'Not Applicable', 'Regularly convene the Child Protection Committee (CPC) for planning', 'Enhance coordination with local DRRM offices and emergency response units for rapid assistance', 'Conduct regular mental health awareness campaigns for learners, teachers, and parents', 'Improve and expand PWD-friendly infrastructure (ramps, signage, accessible toilets, pathways)', '1. Ensure alignment of budget allocation (MOOE and other funds) with strategic priorities\r\n2. Promote transparency and shared accountability in planning and implementation', '1. Promote transparency and shared decision-making in all planning activities\r\n2. Align school-community plans with SIP/AIP\r\n3. Ensure sustainability of initiatives through continuous stakeholder engagement', 'Increase student participation in school planning, policymaking, and program implementation', 'Enhance ICT infrastructure to support efficient and accessible service delivery', '1. Strengthen alignment between strategic goals and annual implementation activities\r\n2. Enhance monitoring and evaluation systems for regular tracking of progress and outcomes', 'Conduct regular SGC meetings with clear agenda and documentation', '1. Align PTA initiatives with School Improvement Plan (SIP) priorities\r\n2. Foster stronger school-community partnerships for sustainable education suppor