INSERT INTO `sbm_ta` (`id`, `fy`, `school_id`, `q1`, `q2`, `q3`, `q4`, `q5`, `q6`, `q7`, `q8`, `q9`, `q10`, `q11`, `q12`, `q13`, `q14`, `q15`, `q16`, `q17`, `q18`, `q19`, `q20`, `q21`, `q22`, `q23`, `q24`, `q25`, `q26`, `q27`, `q28`, `q29`, `q30`, `q31`, `q32`, `q33`, `q34`, `q35`, `q36`, `q37`, `q38`, `q39`, `q40`, `q41`, `q42`, `qq1`, `qq2`, `qq3`, `qq4`, `qq5`, `qq6`, `qq7`, `qq8`, `qq9`, `qq10`, `qq11`, `qq12`, `qq13`, `qq14`, `qq15`, `qq16`, `qq17`, `qq18`, `qq19`, `qq20`, `qq21`, `qq22`, `qq23`, `qq24`, `qq25`, `qq26`, `qq27`, `qq28`, `qq29`, `qq30`, `qq31`, `qq32`, `qq33`, `qq34`, `qq35`, `qq36`, `qq37`, `qq38`, `qq39`, `qq40`, `qq41`, `qq42`, `a1`, `a2`, `a3`, `a4`, `a5`, `a6`, `a7`, `a8`, `a9`, `a10`, `a11`, `a12`, `a13`, `a14`, `a15`, `a16`, `a17`, `a18`, `a19`, `a20`, `a21`, `a22`, `a23`, `a24`, `a25`, `a26`, `a27`, `a28`, `a29`, `a30`, `a31`, `a32`, `a33`, `a34`, `a35`, `a36`, `a37`, `a38`, `a39`, `a40`, `a41`, `a42`, `f1`, `f2`, `f3`, `f4`, `f5`, `f6`, `f7`, `f8`, `f9`, `f10`, `f11`, `f12`, `f13`, `f14`, `f15`, `f16`, `f17`, `f18`, `f19`, `f20`, `f21`, `f22`, `f23`, `f24`, `f25`, `f26`, `f27`, `f29`, `f30`, `f31`, `f32`, `f33`, `f34`, `f35`, `f36`, `f37`, `f38`, `f39`, `f40`, `f41`, `f42`, `f28`, `stat`, `district`, `region`, `division`) VALUES
(738, '2026', '501772', '', '', 'No learners enrolled in the School-Based ALS program, resulting in no candidates for elementary and junior high school completion certification. Limited community awareness and low learner participation affected program implementation.', '', '', '', '', 'Limited partnerships and linkages with local industries and business establishments to support TLE-TVL programs and provide learners with practical exposure and training opportunities.', 'There are still reported cases of verbal teasing, peer conflicts, and social bullying among learners. Limited awareness of anti-bullying policies and insufficient monitoring during break times contribute to the occurrence of incidents. Some learners hesitate to report bullying due to fear or lack of confidence.', 'There are isolated cases of bullying, verbal abuse, and lack of immediate reporting by learners due to fear or limited awareness of child protection policies. Some parents and learners have insufficient understanding of proper child safeguarding practices.', 'Some learners still experience absenteeism due to financial difficulties, family problems, lack of parental support, early employment, and distance from school. Limited monitoring and follow-up of at-risk learners also affect retention.', '', '', 'Lack of trained ALS teachers/facilitators, insufficient learning materials, limited funding support, and low community awareness on ALS implementation hinder the establishment of a functional school-based ALS program.', '', '', '', 'Lack of ramps, handrails, accessible comfort rooms, and learning facilities for learners with disabilities. Limited budget allocation for inclusive infrastructure and assistive devices.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Lack of Specialized Skills: School personnel conducting the inspections may lack the technical expertise to identify deeper structural or electrical hazards.', '', 'Insufficient or outdated reading materials, reference books, and multimedia resources.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Absence of a designated, full-time librarian or trained library coordinator.\r\n\r\n\r\n* No allocated budget for purchasing new books and maintenance.\r\nNo allocation for  library room', '', '', '', '', 'Strong support from teachers, active parental involvement, regular reading and numeracy interventions, and effective monitoring of learners’ progress.', 'Dedicated teachers, regular conduct of review and enrichment classes, strong school leadership support, active stakeholder participation, and continuous learner assessment and monitoring.', '', 'Teachers are creative and collaborative in developing localized and contextualized instructional materials with the support of school heads and stakeholders.', 'Strong support from school administration, commitment of teachers, active participation of parents, availability of intervention programs, and collaboration among teachers in preparing remediation materials and strategies.', 'Strong support from school leadership, teachers’ commitment to values integration, availability of DepEd learning materials, and active participation of learners in school activities promoting peace and values formation.', 'Strong support from school leadership, availability of assessment tools and templates, active participation of teachers, and regular Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions focused on assessment practices.', '', '', '', '', 'Active implementation of learner monitoring systems, support from teachers and parents, school interventions such as home visitation, feeding programs, and guidance services contributed to the reduction of drop-out cases.', 'Strong support from stakeholders, active coordination with the community and barangay officials, committed teachers, and implementation of flexible learning modalities helped ensure continuous access to education for disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adult learners.', '', 'Active participation of school personnel, support from parents and stakeholders, regular orientation on child protection policies, and strong coordination among committee members.', 'Strong support from school stakeholders, active DRRM coordinators, regular disaster preparedness activities, and cooperation from LGU and community partners.', 'Strong support from school administration, active guidance and counseling services, collaboration with parents and stakeholders, implementation of mental health programs and activities, and positive school environment promoting psychosocial well-being.', '', 'Active participation of stakeholders, strong leadership support, collaborative planning process, and regular monitoring and evaluation mechanisms.', 'Strong collaboration among school personnel, parents, LGU, community stakeholders, and School Governing Council; regular meetings and participatory planning activities support effective implementation of programs and projects.', 'Strong support from school administration, active student leaders, regular conduct of leadership activities, and guidance from teacher-advisers', 'Strong support from school leadership, active participation of stakeholders, effective communication systems, and commitment of teachers and staff in providing efficient and responsive services.', 'Strong leadership support, active participation of stakeholders, regular monitoring and evaluation, and clear alignment of programs and activities with the school strategic plan', 'Strong collaboration among school personnel, parents, LGU, community stakeholders, and supportive leadership of the school head contributed to the effective functioning of the SGC. Regular meetings, clear communication, and active stakeholder engagement strengthened school governance and decision-making processes.', 'Strong collaboration between parents and school personnel, active participation of PTA officers, regular PTA meetings, and continuous support for school programs and activities.', 'Strong support and cooperation from stakeholders, partner schools, LGU, parents, and community organizations; effective communication and regular coordination meetings.', 'Active participation of school personnel, availability of monitoring tools, strong leadership support, and regular conduct of meetings and evaluation activities.', 'Strong collaboration among school personnel, active support from stakeholders, effective school leadership, regular monitoring and feedback mechanisms, and transparent communication practices', 'Strong leadership support, commitment of school personnel, regular monitoring and coaching, teamwork, and continuous professional development activities contributed to the achievement of very satisfactory performance ratings.', 'Strong leadership support, collaborative teamwork among personnel, commitment of teachers and staff, effective monitoring and evaluation system, and compliance with DepEd policies and guidelines.', 'Strong support from school leadership, active participation of teachers, availability of school-based training plans, and collaboration among teaching personnel contribute to the successful implementation of needs-based LACs and L&D activities.', 'Strong support from school leadership; active participation of teachers in LAC sessions, INSET, and webinars; collaboration with DepEd and partner stakeholders for capacity-building opportunities', 'Strong support from school leadership, active participation of stakeholders, and established recognition programs that motivate personnel to perform effectively', 'Strong coordination between school personnel, finance office, and division office; timely submission of payroll requirements; effective monitoring and validation of records; support from digital payroll and communication systems.', 'Strong leadership support, collaborative planning, open communication, and adherence to workload policies ensure equitable distribution of teaching and ancillary tasks.', '', 'Strong Stakeholder Support: Active involvement of the Parents-Teachers Association (PTA) and local alumni association in fundraising and volunteer labor (Brigada Eskwela).\r\n\r\n\r\n* Proactive Leadership: The school administration consistently allocates a portion of the MOOE (Maintenance and Other Operating Expenses) and looks for external partnerships.', '', 'Strong support from the school administration, regular maintenance of facilities, active coordination with service providers, and proper allocation of school resources for utilities.', 'Strong support from school administration, availability of ICT coordinators and teachers, proper maintenance practices, and support from stakeholders and partners for ICT resources', 'Strong financial management practices, timely preparation of procurement and financial plans, active monitoring of expenditures, and support from school personnel and stakeholders contributed to the effective utilization of MOOE funds.', 'Strong financial management system, active coordination among school personnel, adherence to accounting and auditing guidelines, and timely submission of reports.', 1, 1, 2, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 6, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 5, 5, 5, 1, 3, 3, 'Sustain intervention programs, provide additional localized learning resources, strengthen home-school partnership, and continue capacity-building activities for teachers.', 'Continue intensive review and intervention programs, enhance access to digital and printed learning resources, strengthen stakeholder support, and sustain teacher training on innovative teaching strategies and assessment practices.', 'Strengthen advocacy campaigns and community mapping to encourage out-of-school youth and adults to enroll in the ALS program. Coordinate with barangay officials and stakeholders to support learner recruitment and retention for future certification completers.', 'Sustain the preparation of contextualized learning materials through continuous teacher collaboration, capacity-building activities, and strengthened stakeholder support for resources and reproduction of materials.', 'Continue strengthening remediation programs through regular monitoring, development of contextualized learning materials, conduct of parent-teacher collaboration, and scheduling of consistent remediation sessions to further improve learner performance.', 'Continue strengthening values integration through regular monitoring, classroom observations, and conduct of activities that promote peace, respect, and DepEd core values among learners and stakeholders.', 'Sustain the regular conduct of test item analysis through continuous capacity-building activities, strengthen collaborative review among teachers, and ensure timely utilization of results to improve instruction and learner performance.', 'Strengthen collaboration with local industries, LGUs, and private partners through MOAs and regular coordination meetings to support TLE-TVL implementation, learner immersion, and skills training opportunities.', 'Strengthen the implementation of the Child Protection Policy through regular orientations, anti-bullying campaigns, peer support activities, and close monitoring of learners. Encourage open communication and reporting mechanisms while engaging parents and stakeholders in promoting a safe and inclusive school environment.', 'trengthen the implementation of the Child Protection Policy through continuous orientation, advocacy campaigns, counseling services, and close coordination with parents and stakeholders. Establish regular monitoring and immediate intervention mechanisms to ensure learner safety and protection.', 'Strengthen learner intervention programs, intensify coordination with parents and stakeholders, conduct regular home visitation and counseling, provide financial and academic support to at-risk learners, and continuously monitor attendance and participation to further reduce drop-out incidence.', 'Strengthen learner intervention programs, intensify coordination with parents and stakeholders, conduct regular home visitation and counseling, provide financial and academic support to at-risk learners, and continuously monitor attendance and participation to further reduce drop-out incidence.', 'Sustain and strengthen community partnerships, continue flexible learning delivery, and enhance monitoring and support mechanisms to maintain inclusive and accessible learning opportunities for all learners.', 'Coordinate with the Schools Division Office for technical assistance and teacher training, strengthen advocacy campaigns to encourage ALS participation, allocate school funds and seek stakeholder support for learning resources, and establish partnerships with the community and LGU for program implementation.', 'Sustain the implementation of child protection programs, strengthen monitoring and documentation practices, and continue conducting orientations and advocacy activities to ensure a safe and child-friendly learning environment.', 'Sustain the implementation and regular updating of the DRRM plan, strengthen coordination with stakeholders, conduct periodic drills and trainings, and allocate resources for emergency preparedness and response activities.', 'Sustain and strengthen mental wellness programs through continuous capacity building, regular monitoring of learners’ well-being, strengthened stakeholder collaboration, and provision of inclusive and supportive activities for all learners and personnel.', 'Allocate funds for the construction of PWD-friendly facilities and coordinate with stakeholders, LGU, and partners for support in promoting inclusive and accessible education.', 'Sustain collaborative strategic planning practices, strengthen stakeholder engagement, and continuously review and update the strategic plan to ensure alignment with school goals and DepEd directives.', 'Sustain active stakeholder engagement through continuous collaboration, regular planning meetings, capacity-building activities, and strengthened partnerships to maintain effective school-community planning and decision-making.', 'Continue strengthening leadership capabilities through regular trainings, monitoring of programs and projects, and sustained support from stakeholders to ensure active and effective student governance', 'Sustain and strengthen innovative frontline services through continuous capacity-building, stakeholder collaboration, and improvement of communication and service delivery mechanisms.', 'Sustain the effective implementation and monitoring of the school implementation plan through continuous collaboration, periodic review, and timely submission of reports and accomplishments', 'Sustain and strengthen stakeholder participation through continuous coordination, regular meetings, capacity-building activities, and transparent implementation of school programs and projects.', 'Sustain active PTA engagement through regular communication, strengthen parent participation in school activities and decision-making, and continue collaborative programs that support learners’ welfare and school improvement.', 'ustain and strengthen partnership programs through continuous engagement, regular collaboration meetings, recognition of stakeholders’ contributions, and expansion of linkages with other institutions and community partners.', 'Sustain the regular monitoring and evaluation system, strengthen data management practices, and continue capacity-building activities for teachers and coordinators to ensure timely and accurate reporting.', 'Sustain effective performance management practices through continuous coaching, capacity-building activities, recognition of personnel achievements, and strengthening collaborative work culture to maintain and further improve performance ratings.', 'ustain and strengthen performance management practices through continuous capability-building activities, regular monitoring, teamwork, and timely accomplishment of targets and deliverables.', 'Sustain the regular conduct of needs-based LACs and Learning & Development activities, strengthen monitoring and evaluation mechanisms, and continue encouraging collaborative learning and professional growth among teachers.', 'Continue strengthening professional development programs through regular trainings, equitable access to learning opportunities, and sustained collaboration with stakeholders to support personnel growth and career advancement.', 'Sustain and strengthen the recognition and rewards system through continuous stakeholder support, proper allocation of resources, and regular implementation of incentive and appreciation programs for personnel achievements.', 'Sustain efficient payroll monitoring and timely submission of required documents; continue strengthening coordination with concerned offices to ensure uninterrupted and accurate release of salaries and benefits.', 'Sustain transparent workload distribution practices, regularly review task assignments, and continue promoting teamwork and collaboration among teachers.', 'Institutionalize an Inspection Calendar: Develop and strictly adhere to a monthly and post-calamity inspection checklist signed by the school head.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Capacity Building: Partner with the Municipal/City Engineer’s Office or DepEd Division Engineers to conduct a basic structural assessment training workshop for the school\'s facilities committee.', 'Commitment: We commit to strengthening partnerships with local government units (LGU) and private donors through formal Memorandums of Agreement (MOA) to secure continuous funding and resources for facility upkeep.', 'Transforming a non-functional space into a functional one relies heavily on Social (community drop-offs/donations) and Financial (MOOE allocation) interventions.', 'Sustain regular monitoring and maintenance of water, electrical, and internet facilities; strengthen coordination with utility providers; and allocate continuous budget for repair, upgrading, and uninterrupted operation of services.', 'Continue strengthening the maintenance and upgrading of ICT facilities, ensure regular monitoring of equipment functionality, seek additional funding and stakeholder support for modernization, and sustain effective utilization of the computer laboratory for teaching and learning.', 'The school commits to sustaining transparent, efficient, and timely utilization of MOOE through continuous monitoring, capacity-building on financial management, and strict adherence to government budgeting, accounting, and auditing policies.', 'Sustain accurate and transparent financial management practices, continue capacity-building on financial reporting, and ensure timely monitoring and submission of liquidation documents.', 'Sustain and strengthen stakeholder engagement through continuous improvement programs, regular consultation meetings, transparent reporting, and timely response to stakeholder concerns to maintain or further improve satisfaction ratings', 0, 123, 12, 57),
(739, '2026', '341526@deped.gov.ph', 'N/A', '', 'N/A', 'Limited time for materials development; lack of high-quality localized digital resources.  Some teachers have difficulty in contextualization of learning materials', 'Time constraints and overlapping of activities.                  Overloaded teacher schedules; learner fatigue during after-school sessions.', 'Difficulty in quantifying the impact of value integration on learner behavior.', '', 'Limited nearby industries for specific specializations', 'Occasional verbal bullying; lack of student reporting due to fear of retaliation.', 'Lack of awareness among parents/staff on the boundaries of \"positive discipline\" vs. abuse.', 'High absenteeism due to seasonal labor or financial instability at home.', 'Limited instructional materials that reflect local indigenous or minority cultures.', 'Overlapping schedules of OSYs who are working; lack of community mapping data.', 'No designated room for ALS; lack of a permanent ALS mobile teacher assigned to the site.', 'Committee meets only when a case arises rather than practicing proactive prevention.', 'DRRM equipment (extinguishers, first aid) is incomplete or expired; some students ignore drills.', 'Lack of a registered guidance counselor; stigma surrounding seeking mental health help.', 'Only ramps and comfort rooms are available facilities for PWD', '', '', '', 'Difficulty in gathering 100% of community stakeholders for Need for a more structured \"Customer Feedback\" mechanism to measure satisfaction levels accurately.', '', 'Lack of clear roles; members are inactive or unavailable for meetings.', '', '', '', 'Minor complaints regarding facility maintenance or response time.', '', '', 'Scheduling conflicts', '', '', '', '', 'Lack of a standardized checklist for technical inspections; limited expertise in structural integrity assessment', 'Budget allocation is insufficient', '', '', 'Computer Laboratory is available however, All desktops sets were condemned since i