(751, '2026', '304293', '', 'Even though Grade 6, 10, and 12 learners achieved proficiency in the NAT, challenges still exist such as unequal learner performance, gaps in higher-order thinking and real-life application of skills, limited learning resources and ICT access, large class sizes, limited time for remediation/enrichment, and teacher workload that may affect sustained improvement.\r\n', '', '', 'Challenges in conducting remediation include limited time, large class sizes, lack of resources, varying learner difficulties in key subjects, irregular attendance, and limited parental support, which affect the effectiveness of addressing learning gaps.\r\n', 'Challenges include limited time, lack of ready materials, difficulty integrating values across subjects, varying learner behavior, limited home reinforcement, and weak monitoring tools for evaluating values integration.\r\n', 'Challenges include limited time, lack of training and ICT tools, heavy teacher workload, and delayed or incomplete assessment data, which affect the effectiveness of test item analysis.\r\n', '', 'Occasional bullying cases, underreporting of incidents, limited learner awareness on anti-bullying policies, and inconsistent monitoring', 'Limited reporting due to fear or lack of awareness, weak community reporting system, and insufficient monitoring outside school premises', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Limited trained personnel, stigma on mental health, insufficient time for counseling, and lack of dedicated materials', 'Lack of ramps, assistive devices, trained SPED personnel, and accessible learning materials', '', '', '', '', 'Inconsistent alignment of activities with planned targets, delays in implementation due to workload, and limited monitoring tools', 'Irregular attendance of some members, limited participation in decision-making, and scheduling conflicts', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Facilitating factors include teachers’ commit