y education and learner development.', 'Support the programs and projects of schools for the welfare of the school children.', 'Perform my duties and responsibilities as a teacher with dedication , integrity and professionalismin accordance with the Department of Education standards.', 'The office commit to deliver quality , efficient , and timely services in accordance with the goals and standard  of the organization.', 'Effectively facilitate LAC  that support the continuous professional development of teachers and improve teaching and learning.', 'Uphold responsibilities of my new position with integrity and dedication.', 'Uphold the values and standards expected of the recognition received.', 'Fulfill my obligation in giving the required compensation as agreed upon by the program /institution.', 'Handle my assigned workload responsibly and to the best of my ability.', 'Making sure organization follow laws, regulations and standards.', 'Proper monitoring  to reduce corruption and ensure quality work.', 'Providing trustworthy and well-organized information.', 'Ensuring uninterrupted electricity and clean water for learners.', 'Allocating enough budget to support planned activities and projects.', 'Ensure funds are prepared based on  school needs.', 'Use the allocated MOOE responsibly ,transparently and in accordance with existing rules and regulations.', 'Support the school in achieving  its vision, mission and goals for the success and development of learners.', 1, 1, 12, 61),
(765, '2026', '128999', '', '•	Need for stronger home-based learning support', 'The school does not implement a School‑Based Alternative Learning System (ALS) program. Only Community - Based ALS Program located in the school campus', '', '', '', '', 'The school does not offer TLE‑TVL courses requiring industry immersion or partnership.', '•	Minor peer conflicts and behavioral issues occasionally reported', '', '', '', 'The school does not cater to out‑of‑school youth and adult learners under a school‑based Alternative Learning System (ALS).', 'The school has no established school‑based ALS program.', '', '', '•	Need for more structured mental wellness programs', '•	Limited availability of fully accessible facilities', '', '', '', '', '', '•	Limited understanding of roles and functions among identified members.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '•	Insufficient learning resources and reference materials.\r\n•	Limited space and lack of designated library personnel.\r\n', '', '•	Insufficient number of functional computers to cater to learners’ needs.\r\n•	Limited space and lack of updated ICT equipment.\r\n', '', '', '•	Regular conduct of remediation and intervention programs', '', '', '•	Collaborative development of learning materials during SLAC sessions', '•	Teachers’ commitment to implementing remediation programs', '•	Teachers’ commitment to values integration in daily lessons', '•	Regular conduct of quarterly and summative assessments', '', '', '•	Strict implementation of DepEd Child Protection Policy', '•	Early identification and monitoring of learners at risk', '•	Teachers’ awareness and respect for cultural diversity', '', '', '•	Regular orientation for teachers, learners, and parents', '•	Regular conduct of drills and preparedness activities', '', '', '•	Active School Planning Team with clear roles and responsibilities.', '•	Strong partnership with local government units, parents, and community organizations.', '•	Support from school administrators and teachers.', '•	Utilization of digital platforms (online forms, school social media, messaging groups) for communication and service requests.', '•	Approved Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) aligned with the SIP.', '', '•	Elected and recognized PTA officers.\r\n•	Regular PTA meetings and documented plans and activities.\r\n•	Strong collaboration between parents and teachers.\r\n', '•	Active engagement of stakeholders in school programs and projects.', '•	Regular conduct of school monitoring visits and progress review meetings.', '•	Responsive school personnel addressing concerns promptly.', '•	Regular coaching, mentoring, and performance review conferences.\r\n•	Supportive school leadership promoting professional growth.\r\n', 'learly defined office targets aligned with the School Improvement Plan and AIP.', '•	Conduct of regular needs assessment to identify priority LAC themes.', '•	Encouragement of personnel to pursue further studies and professional growth.', '•	Implementation of school based recognition and incentives programs.\r\n•	Supportive school culture that values appreciation and motivation.\r\n•	Regular acknowledgement of achievements during school activities and assemblies.\r\n', '•	Designated personnel assisting teachers and staff in the preparation and submission of requirements.', '•	Collaborative decision making involving teachers and school heads.\r\n•	Consideration of teacher expertise, skills, and capacity in workload distribution.\r\n', '•	Proper documentation of inspection results and identified needs.', '•	Availability of approved improvement plans based on inspection results.', '', '•	Existing functional utilities supporting daily school operations.', '', '•	Approved Annual Procurement Plan aligned with the School Improvement Plan and AIP.\r\n•	Proper financial planning and budgeting practices.\r\n•	Regular monitoring of MOOE utilization.\r\n', '•	Clear guidelines and timelines for MOOE liquidation.\r\n•	Regular coordination with Division finance offices.\r\n', 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 2, 6, 2, 6, 5, 2, 6, 6, 1, 2, 2, 6, 6, 1, 6, 2, 2, 1, 2, 6, 2, 6, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, '•	Enhance parent involvement through regular communication and orientation', '•	Engage parents and stakeholders in supporting learners’ academic needs', 'Ensure proper referral of potential ALS learners to nearby ALS centers.', '•	Sustain collaborative development and sharing of contextualized materials', '•	Sustain data driven instructional decisions', '•	Strengthen values based activities and school programs', '•	Sustain regular conduct and utilization of test item analysis', 'Refer learners to nearby schools offering TLE‑TVL programs with established industry partnerships, as applicable.', '•	Strengthen anti bullying awareness and values formation activities', '•	Maintain a safe, protective, and supportive school environment', '•	Continue targeted support for at risk learners', '•	Sustain implementation of culture sensitive and inclusive activities', 'Support community initiatives and information dissemination on available ALS programs.', 'Refer potential ALS learners to nearby accredited ALS centers.', '•	Conduct regular capacity building and orientation activities', '•	Strengthen disaster preparedness and response activities', '•	Build teachers’ capacity on basic psychosocial support', '•	Gradually improve accessibility and PWD friendly facilities', '•	Strengthen stakeholder participation through scheduled planning consultations and capacity-building activities.', '•	Institutionalize recognition of active community stakeholders to sustain engagement.', '•	Conduct regular leadership training and mentoring sessions for student officers.', '•	Improve information dissemination through multiple platforms to reach all stakeholders.', '•	Enhance coordination among implementers to ensure timely accomplishment of targets.', '•	Reconstitute the SGC ensuring complete and compliant stakeholder representation.\r\n•	Conduct orientation and capacity-building activities for SGC members.\r\n', '•	Sustain PTA-led initiatives supporting learners and school programs.', '•	Formalize partnerships through MOUs or MOAs.', '•	Sustain data driven decision making based on evaluation results.', '•	Sustain regular coaching and performance monitoring activities.\r\n•	Strengthen documentation and timely submission of IPCRF requirements.\r\n•	Continue professional development programs to maintain high performance standards.\r\n', '•	Use OPCRF results to continuously improve school management and operations.', '•	Strengthen documentation and sharing of LAC outputs and best practices.', '•	Continue supporting personnel participation in professional development activities.\r\n•	Promote equitable access to training and development opportunities.\r\n', '•	Explore partnerships and low cost initiatives to support incentive programs.', '•	Strengthen guidance and reminders on timely submission of compensation requirements.\r\n•	Sustain close coordination with concerned offices to address issues promptly.\r\n', '•	Promote a supportive work environment that ensures work life balance.', '•	Prioritize identified needs for repair and maintenance.\r\n•	Strengthen coordination with concerned offices and partners for technical support.\r\n', '•	Prioritize improvement projects based on urgency and impact.', '•	Develop a concrete plan for the establishment and improvement of the school library.\r\n•	Source learning resources through donations, partnerships, and available funds.\r\n•	Assign personnel to manage and sustain library operations.\r\n', '•	Sustain regular maintenance and monitoring of utility services.', '•	Develop a phased plan for the establishment and improvement of a functional computer laboratory/classroom.\r\n•	Source ICT equipment through partnerships, donations, and available school funds.\r\n•	Coordinate with LGUs and external partners to support ICT infrastructure development.\r\n', '•	Sustain efficient and transparent utilization of MOOE.\r\n•	Strengthen monitoring and documentation of expenditures.\r\n•	Ensure alignment of expenses with school priorities and needs.\r\n', '•	Sustain timely and accurate liquidation of all utilized MOOE.\r\n•	Strengthen document management and record keeping practices.\r\n•	Continue adherence to financial policies and accountability standards.\r\n', '•	Utilize survey results to continuously improve school programs and services.', 1, 29, 12, 60),
