(795, '2026', '128968', '', '', 'None Implementing', 'Heavy teaching load and administrative tasks limiting the time available for teachers to research and create high-quality contextualized modules.', '', '', '', 'Not Implementing', 'Under-reporting of bullying incidents due to learners\' fear of retaliation', '', '', 'Less number of Indigenous learners', 'Non implementing', 'Non implementing', '', '', 'Limited number of trained personnel to provide specialized mental health.', 'Limited budget allocation', '', '', '', 'Need of personnel to act as frontliner', '', 'Limited participation from some SGC members who are also involved in multiple community organizations.', '', '', 'Heavy reliance on manual tracking systems leading to delays in generating quarterly SMEA reports.', 'Limited participation of external stakeholders in school monitoring and evaluation (M&E) activities', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Limited School MOOE to cover major capital outlays.', 'Lack of a dedicated room/space for a library; insufficiency of updated and relevant reading materials; absence of a plantilla position for a School Librarian.', '', 'Absence of a standard-sized, secure room for a laboratory; insufficient number of working computer units to meet the 1:1 or 1:2 learner-to-computer ratio.', '', '', '\"Consistent implementation of the school\'s remedial reading program', 'Intensive implementation of the Unified School-Based Review Program for NAT-takers.', '', '', 'Utilization of pre-test and post-test data to identify specific students needing intervention', 'Visible integration of DepEd Core Values in school-wide activities, ceremonies', 'Institutionalized practice of submitting Item Analysis report, Proficiency Level and Least Learned Competencies alongside periodic examination grades.', '', '', 'Open communication lines between learners and the Guidance Office, fostering a culture where students feel safe to voice concerns', 'Effective implementation of the \'Home Visitation Program\'', '', '', '', 'Established referral protocol with local social welfare offices and health centers', 'Updated School Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (DRRM) Plan aligned with the local division standards.', '', '', 'Strong alignment of the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) with the Division’s strategic roadmap.', 'Sustained transparency in school operations, building high levels of trust and cooperation from the community.', 'Active guidance from a designated SPG Adviser who provides mentorship while allowing student autonomy', '', 'A well-defined Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) that clearly outlines specific activities, timelines, and budgets aligned with the SIP.', '', 'Active PTA officers who spearhead resource mobilization and volunteer programs like \'Brigada Eskwela.', 'Strong linkages with NGOs, LGUs, and private donors for supplemental school resources.', '', '', 'Regular LAC (Learning Action Cell) sessions, consistent monitoring by the School Head, use of standardized digital templates for MOV collection, and a strong culture of professional development.', 'Strategic alignment of the School Improvement Plan (SIP) with the OPCRF targets; quarterly internal monitoring and evaluation (SMEA) conducted by the School Quality Assurance team.', 'Presence of highly competent \"Master Teachers\" as LAC facilitators; supportive school leadership in providing time for L&D.', 'Consistent conduct of LAC sessions', 'Functional School PRAISE Committee', 'Efficient school personnel in charge of payroll and administrative records; timely submission of Form 7 and other supporting documents to the Division Office.', 'Strict adherence to the Magna Carta for Public School Teachers and DepEd Order no.005 s.2024 regarding teaching loads.', 'Regular conduct of the School Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (SDRRM) inspections.', '', '', 'Prompt payment of utility bills through MOOE', '', 'Transparent procurement process through the School BAC (Bids and Awards Committee); regular posting in the Transparency Board.', 'Transparent procurement process through the School BAC (Bids and Awards Committee); regular posting in the Transparency Board.', 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 6, 1, 2, 6, 2, 2, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 6, 3, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 6, 6, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 5, 3, 1, 3, 5, 3, 3, 'Allocate portion of the MOOE for the reproduction of localized \'Big Books\' and numeracy manipulative kits.', 'Strengthen the \'Teachers-Mentoring-Teachers\' initiative to share best practices in contextualizing core learning areas', 'Indorse qualified ALS learners to ALS implementing institution.', 'Conduct a workshop on the quality assurance of teacher-made materials.', 'Institutionalize the \'No Learner Left Behind\' policy through a structured remedial schedule integrated into the regular school calendar', 'Conduct a SLAC session on \'Creative Values Integration', 'Conduct a hands-on workshop on \'Automating Item Analysis\' using Microsoft Excel', 'Not Implementing', 'Revitalize the school’s \'Anonymous Reporting System\' (e.g., a physical drop-box ) to encourage victims and witnesses to speak up safely', 'Conduct Mental Health and Wellness\' sessions for students to build resilience and empower them with knowledge on their rights and personal boundaries', 'Strengthen the peer-support network where classmates act as \'attendance buddies\' for those with high absence rates.', 'Integrate in lessons', 'Not implementing', 'Indorse qualified learners to ALS implementing school', 'Track student welfare concerns while maintaining strict confidentiality protocols', 'Strengthen the school’s \'Early Warning System\' through updated emergency signage.', 'Partner with local health offices to conduct \'Mental Health workshops for parents to strengthen the home-school support system', 'Allocate a portion of the school\'s MOOE for the installation of temporary ramps.', 'Review strategic plan to make adjustment', 'Strengthen the \'Stakeholder Recognition Program\' to honor the contributions of community members who actively participate in school governance.', 'Mentoring', 'Identify specific areas for improvement.', 'Strengthen the \'Transparency  Board\' to give all personnel a visual representation of completed vs. ongoing implementation tasks.', 'Conduct an \'SGC Leadership Orientation to clarify the council\'s role in school policy formulation and stakeholder engagement.', 'Expand the \'Parents as Partners\' program to include parent-led beautification and safety initiatives on campus.', 'Conduct SGC/PTA meeting', 'Produce hard copy of monitoring tool', 'To sustain this, we will implement a Peer-Coaching Mentorship Program to help teachers aiming for \"Outstanding\" and automate the performance monitoring system to reduce administrative stress.', 'Maintenance of time Management  for OPCRF evidence and conduct of a \"Mid-year Performance Review and Calibration\" to ensure targets are consistently met.', 'Strengthen Teacher-to-Teacher Mentorship Activity', 'Establish a Career Pathing and Mentorship Activity to assist teachers in meeting the requirements for promotion.', 'Enhance the Localized School PRAISE System to include peer-to-peer recognition.', 'Implement a Pre-emptive Review of Service Records', 'Sustain the equitable distribution of ancillary tasks.', 'Produce hard copy of inspection reports for easier retrieval and historical tracking of building integrity.', 'Strengthen the School Resource Mobilization Plan', 'Convert vacant or temporary spaces into a functional School Reading Center', 'Maintain regular preventive maintenance of electrical and water systems; explore upgrading internet bandwidth through \"DepEd Computerization Program (DCP)\" support.', 'Prioritize the request for a New Building/Laboratory Room through the School Development Plan; coordinate with the Division IT Officer for the inclusion of the school in the next DCP batch.', 'Conduct regularly financial reviews to ensure MOOE is spent according to the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).', 'Conduct regularly financial reviews to ensure MOOE is spent according to the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).', 'Conduct quarterly Stakeholders’ Convergence to increase engagement in school-community programs.', 1, 26, 12, 60);
INSERT INTO `sbm_ta` (`id`, `fy`, `school_id`, `q1`, `q2`, `q3`, `q4`, `q5`, `q6`, `q7`, `q8`, `q9`, `q10`, `q11`, `q12`, `q13`, `q14`, `q15`, `q16`, `q17`, `q18`, `q19`, `q20`, `q21`, `q22`, `q23`, `q24`, `q25`, `q26`, `q27`, `q28`, `q29`, `q30`, `q31`, `q32`, `q33`, `q34`, `q35`, `q36`, `q37`, `q38`, `q39`, `q40`, `q41`, `q42`, `qq1`, `qq2`, `qq3`, `qq4`, `qq5`, `qq6`, `qq7`, `qq8`, `qq9`, `qq10`, `qq11`, `qq12`, `qq13`, `qq14`, `qq15`, `qq16`, `qq17`, `qq18`, `qq19`, `qq20`, `qq21`, `qq22`, `qq23`, `qq24`, `qq25`, `qq26`, `qq27`, `qq28`, `qq29`, `qq30`, `qq31`, `qq32`, `qq33`, `qq34`, `qq35`, `qq36`, `qq37`, `qq38`, `qq39`, `qq40`, `qq41`, `qq42`, `a1`, `a2`, `a3`, `a4`, `a5`, `a6`, `a7`, `a8`, `a9`, `a10`, `a11`, `a12`, `a13`, `a14`, `a15`, `a16`, `a17`, `a18`, `a19`, `a20`, `a21`, `a22`, `a23`, `a24`, `a25`, `a26`, `a27`, `a28`, `a29`, `a30`, `a31`, `a32`, `a33`, `a34`, `a35`, `a36`, `a37`, `a38`, `a39`, `a40`, `a41`, `a42`, `f1`, `f2`, `f3`, `f4`, `f5`, `f6`, `f7`, `f8`, `f9`, `f10`, `f11`, `f12`, `f13`, `f14`, `f15`, `f16`, `f17`, `f18`, `f19`, `f20`, `f21`, `f22`, `f23`, `f24`, `f25`, `f26`, `f27`, `f29`, `f30`, `f31`, `f32`, `f33`, `f34`, `f35`, `f36`, `f37`, `f38`, `f39`, `f40`, `f41`, `f42`, `f28`, `stat`, `district`, `region`, `division`) VALUES
(796, '2026', '128471', '-Significant number of learners exhibit low reading comprehension and decoding skills. \r\n-Presence of learning gaps in foundational numeracy skills such as basic operations and problem-solving. \r\n-Limited individualized and differentiated instruction due to large class sizes.  \r\n- limited parental support affecting learner progress. \r\n- Limited access to learning resources and ICT tools to support literacy and numeracy development. \r\n', '- Some  learners demonstrate low mastery of competencies in core learning areas (English, Mathematics, Science). \r\n-Gaps in higher-order thinking skills (HOTS) such as critical thinking, problem-solving, and analytical skills\r\n-Limited availability of review materials, ICT tools, and enrichment resources. \r\n-Time constraints in conducting intensive review and remediation programs. \r\n\r\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '- Occasional incidents of verbal ,physical. \r\n- Some learners show limited awareness or understanding of anti-bullying policies and consequences. \r\n- Instances of underreporting due to fear of retaliation, peer pressureOccasional gaps in parental involvement and reinforcement of positive behavior at home. ', '', '-Occasional cases of learners at risk of dropping out due to absenteeism and low engagement. \r\n-Socio-economic challenges such as poverty, child labor, and lack of financial support affecting school attendance. \r\n- Limited parental involvement and monitoring of learners’ academic progress. \r\n-Learners experiencing learning difficulties or low academic performance leading to disengagement. \r\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '-The school  organized  Governance Council (SGC)  \r\n-Inactive participation of diverse stakeholders ( parents, community leaders, alumni, and partners). \r\n-SGC meetings, consultations, and planning sessions are not conducted regularly \r\n-Limited commitment and collaboration among council members in supporting school programs and projects.\r\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'No existing library room\r\n- Lack of updated books aligned with the current curriculum\r\n-Limited variety of reading materials (fiction, non-fiction, reference books, multimedia resources)\r\n- Inadequate materials for diverse learners (e.g., struggling readers, advanced learners, learners with special needs)\r\n- No assigned librarian or teacher-librarian\r\n- Insufficient budget dedicated to library development and maintenance\r\n', '', '- Insufficient number of functional computers and ICT equipment to accommodate all learners. \r\n-Occasional malfunctioning or outdated computer units that need repair or replacement. \r\n-Minor internet connectivity interruptions affecting some ICT-based activities. \r\n-Limited availability of updated software and digital learning resources in some units. \r\n-Need for continuous technical maintenance and periodic system updates. \r\n-Minimal gaps in teacher proficiency in advanced ICT integration strategies. \r\n-Occasional scheduling conflicts that limit full utilization of the laboratory. \r\n-Need to strengthen data security, device management, and proper usage protocols. \r\n-Limited dedicated ICT support personnel for immediate troubleshooting\r\n', '', '', '', '', 'The school head consistently prioritizes the Alternative Learning System (ALS) program, ensuring it is integrated into the school improvement plan and regularly monitored.\r\nALS teachers/facilitators demonstrate dedication, competence, and consistent delivery of learning sessions aligned with curriculum standards.\r\nALS teachers/facilitators demonstrate dedication, competence, and consistent delivery of learning sessions aligned with curriculum standards.\r\nActive involvement of parents, local government units, and community partners strengthens program implementation and learner participation.\r\nThe program accommodates diverse learner needs through flexible schedules and varied instructional strategies.', '-Teachers have a strong understanding of learners’ needs, abilities, and learning contexts through assessment and observation. \r\n-Regular conduct of needs assessment and diagnostic activities to guide material development. \r\n-Active participation in Learning Action Cells (LACs) and collaborative planning sessions for sharing and improving instructional materials. \r\n', 'Teachers regularly conduct diagnostic assessments and formative evaluations to identify learners’ learning gaps. \r\n- Availability of school-based intervention programs such as ARAL program, remediation classes, tutorials, and catch-up sessions.\r\n-Strong instructional leadership and support in prioritizing remediation and learner support programs. -Collaboration among teachers in sharing strategies and designing intervention activities. \r\n-Access to learning materials and resources that support remediation in reading, science, and mathematics. \r\n-Engagement of parents and guardians in supporting learners’ remediation at home. \r\n', '- Teachers consistently integrate DepEd Core Values (Maka-Diyos, Makatao, Makakalikasan, Makabansa) in daily lesson plans and classroom activities. -  Use of values integration in all learning areas as part of curriculum implementation. -  Regular conduct of Learning Action Cells (LACs) focusing on values education and character formation strategies. \r\n- Supportive school culture that promotes respect, harmony, and inclusivity among learners and personnel. \r\n- Active participation of learners in school-wide peace-building activities and programs. \r\n- Collaboration among teachers in sharing strategies for effective values integration.\r\n', '-The school has an established system for conducting test item analysis (TIA) after every assessment period. \r\n-Teachers are equipped with knowledge and skills in item analysis and interpretation of results. \r\n-Availability of assessment data (quarterly exams)for analysis. \r\n-Strong instructional leadership and supervision in ensuring the conduct and utilization of TIA. \r\n-Regular conduct of Learning Action Cells (LACs) to discuss analysis results and improve test items. \r\n-Use of standardized templates and tools for item analysis and reporting. \r\n-Collaboration among teachers in reviewing test items and identifying least-mastered competencies. \r\n', '', '', '-The school strictly implements child protection policies (Child Protection Policy/CPP) in compliance with DepEd guidelines. -Strong awareness and orientation programs for teachers, learners, and parents on child protection and rights. \r\n-Presence of a designated Child Protection Committee (CPC) that monitors and addresses related concerns. \r\n-Strong collaboration with parents, LGUs, and partner agencies for child welfare and protection. - Promotion of a safe, inclusive, and child-friendly school environment.', '', '-The school recognizes and respects the diverse cultural backgrounds of learners and stakeholders. \r\n-Integration of culture-based and localized content in classroom instruction and school activities. \r\n- Active participation of Indigenous Peoples (IP) learners and community members in school programs\r\n- Strong support from school leadership in promoting cultural awareness and inclusivity. - Conduct of school celebrations and events that highlight local traditions and heritage. ', '-The school consistently implements inclusive education policies that ensure access for disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adults.\r\n- The Alternative Learning System (ALS) is fully operational, providing flexible and accessible learning opportunities.\r\n- The school head prioritizes inclusive education and allocates resources to support marginalized learners.\r\n- Learning sessions are conducted in accessible venues within the community to reach more learners.\r\n', '-The school  consistently provides direction, supervision, and administrative support to ensure the effective implementation of the ALS program.\r\n-A clear organizational structure is in place, including designated ALS coordinators/facilitators with defined roles and responsibilities.\r\n-The program offers flexible schedules, modular learning, and community-based sessions to accommodate OSYs and adult learners.\r\n-Regular community mapping and advocacy activities identify and engage potential ALS learners.\r\n-Learners demonstrate regular attendance, active participation, and commitment to completing the program\r\n', '-The school has a duly organized Child Protection Committee (CPC) with clearly defined roles and responsibilities. \r\n- Strict implementation of the DepEd Child Protection Policy (CPP) within the school\r\n- Regular conduct of meetings and case discussions to address child protection concerns. \r\n- Established reporting, referral, and response mechanisms for child protection cases. \r\n- Strong awareness campaigns and orientations for learners, parents, and personnel on child protection\r\n- Presence of a safe, supportive, and child-friendly school environment.', '- The school has a comprehensive and updated DRRM Plan aligned with DepEd and national DRRM guidelines. \r\n- Strong leadership support in implementing disaster preparedness, response, and recovery measures. \r\n- Organized School DRRM Committee/Team with clearly defined roles and responsibilities. \r\n- Regular conduct of disaster preparedness drills (e.g., fire drill, earthquake drill, evacuation drill). \r\n- Availability of emergency supplies and equipment such as first aid kits, emergency go-bags, and communication tools. \r\n- Established coordination with LGUs, barangay disaster units, and other agencies for emergency response. \r\n- Continuous risk assessment and hazard mapping of school facilities and surroundings. \r\n- Active participation of teachers, learners, and stakeholders in DRRM activities and trainings\r\n', '- The school has an established mental wellness program integrated into guidance and learners support services. \r\n-Presence of a designated guidance counselor/teacher or focal person for mental health and psychosocial support. \r\n-Regular conduct of mental health awareness activities, seminars, and campaigns for learners and personnel. \r\n-Availability of counseling services and referral systems for learners needing support. \r\n- Strong support from school leadership in promoting mental wellness initiatives. \r\n-Collaboration with parents, health professionals, and external agencies for comprehensive support. \r\n- Implementation of safe spaces and supportive environments for learners to express concerns. \r\n-Integration of social-emotional learning (SEL) in classroom instruction and school activities.\r\n', 'The school has established accessible infrastructure such as ramps, handrails, and widened pathways for learners with disabilities.\r\n\r\nPresence of designated classrooms or spaces for learners with special education needs (SPED).\r\n', '-The school has a clear vision, mission, and goals that guide the strategic planning process. \r\n-Active participation of school heads, teachers, stakeholders, and community members in plan development. \r\n- Availability of relevant data (performance indicators, needs assessment, school report card) to inform planning decisions. \r\n-Established School Planning Team/Committee that leads and coordinates the process. \r\n- Strong support from school leadership in ensuring collaborative and systematic planning. \r\n- Alignment of the school plan with DepEd policies, programs, and national education priorities. \r\n-Regular conduct of consultations, meetings, and workshops for planning and review. \r\n-Presence of a culture of shared responsibility and accountability among stakeholders.', '-The school has an organized and officially designated School-Community Planning Team with clear roles and responsibilities. \r\n- Active participation of internal and external stakeholders (school head, teachers, parents, community leaders, and partners). \r\n- Regularly conducted meetings, consultations, and planning sessions to discuss school programs and priorities. \r\n-Strong leadership and coordination from the school head in guiding the team’s functions. \r\n- Presence of collaborative decision-making processes that encourage shared ownership of plans and programs. \r\nEstablished communication channels that ensure transparency and dissemination of plans and updates. \r\n-Demonstrated commitment and cooperation among team members in achieving school goals.', 'The school has a duly organized and recognized Supreme Student Government (SSG) / Supreme Pupil Government (SPG) with elected officers. \r\n-Presence of a designated teacher-adviser who guides and supports student leaders. \r\n-Active implementation of student-led programs, projects, and activities aligned with school goals. \r\n- Regular conduct of meetings, planning sessions, and assemblies involving student officers. \r\n-Strong support from school administration and stakeholders in empowering student leadership. \r\n-Established communication channels between student government, learners, and school management\r\n-Demonstrated participation of students in decision-making and school improvement initiatives. ', '- The school implements innovative systems and processes ( digital communication, Facebook page, feedback mechanisms) to improve service delivery. \r\n-Strong support from school leadership in promoting innovation and continuous improvement. \r\n- Active engagement of stakeholders (parents, learners, community partners) in providing feedback and suggestions. \r\n- Availability of ICT resources and tools that enhance efficiency in delivering frontline services\r\n-Established clear procedures and service standards to guide frontline services. \r\n', '-The school has a clear and approved strategic plan that serves as the basis for implementation. \r\n-Development of a detailed implementation plan (SIP/AIP) with specific activities, timelines, and responsible persons. \r\n-Strong leadership and supervision from the school head to ensure proper execution of plans. \r\n-Regular coordination meetings and progress reviews to ensure alignment with targets. \r\n-Use of data and performance indicators to guide implementation and adjustments.\r\n', '', '-The school has a duly organized and recognized Parent-Teacher Association (PTA) with elected officers. \r\n-Active participation of parents and teachers in school programs, activities, and decision-making processes. \r\n-Regular conduct of PTA meetings, assemblies, and consultations with proper documentation. \r\n-Strong support and coordination from the school head and teachers in PTA initiatives. \r\n- Implementation of PTA-led programs and projects that support school improvement and learner development. \r\n-Established communication channels between parents, teachers, and school administration. \r\n- Presence of clear guidelines and policies governing PTA operations and financial management. \r\n-Demonstrated collaboration and shared responsibility among members in achieving school goals.\r\n', 'The school maintains strong linkages and partnerships with stakeholders such as parents, community leaders, LGUs, NGOs, and other schools. \r\n-Active participation in inter-school collaborations, programs, and activities (e.g., benchmarking, joint projects, trainings). \r\n-Supportive school leadership that promotes collaboration and external engagement. \r\n- Regular conduct of meetings, consultations, and coordination activities with stakeholders and partner schools. \r\n-Established communication channels that ensure continuous coordination and information sharing. \r\n-Stakeholders demonstrate commitment and shared responsibility in supporting school programs and initiatives. \r\n', 'The school has established monitoring and evaluation (M&E) systems and tools to assess programs, projects, and activities. \r\n-Regular conduct of monitoring visits, progress reviews, and evaluation meetings. \r\n-Availability of reliable data and performance indicators to guide assessment and decision-making. \r\n-Active involvement of school personnel and stakeholders in the monitoring and evaluation process. \r\n-Strong leadership and supervision from the school head in ensuring accountability. \r\n-Proper documentation and reporting of accomplishments, issues, and outcomes. \r\nCulture of continuous improvement and evidence-based decision-making within the school. ', '-The school consistently implements quality assurance mechanisms to ensure effective service delivery and performance\r\n-Presence of a responsive and client-centered school culture among personnel and administrators. \r\n- Regular conduct of stakeholder satisfaction surveys and evaluation activities. \r\n-Effective communication and transparency in school programs, policies, and decisions. \r\n-Continuous monitoring and improvement of school programs, projects, and services. \r\n-Strong leadership commitment to addressing concerns and improving performance. \r\n-Active participation of internal and external stakeholders in school improvement initiatives.\r\n', '-The school implements a clear performance management system (RPMS/IPCRF) with defined targets and indicators. \r\n-Strong instructional leadership and supervision provided by the school head and MTs to guide teachers performance. \r\n-Regular conduct of coaching, mentoring, and performance monitoring activities. \r\n-Active participation of school personnel in planning, implementing, and evaluating individual commitments. \r\n-Availability of capacity-building programs, trainings, LAC sessions, Collaborative Expertise sessions and professional development opportunities. \r\n-Established collaborative and supportive work environment among school personnel       - Commitment of personnel to quality teaching, accountability, and continuous improvement. \r\n', '-The school implements a clear and well-defined performance management system (OPCRF) aligned with DepEd goals and priorities. \r\n-Strong instructional and administrative leadership that ensures effective planning, implementation, and monitoring of office targets. \r\n- Regular conduct of performance review, coaching, and feedback sessions among school personnel. \r\n- Active collaboration and teamwork among school staff in achieving office targets and deliverables. \r\n-Continuous capacity-building and professional development activities for school personnel. \r\n-Effective resource management and utilization to support program implementation. \r\n-Commitment of personnel to accountability, efficiency, and quality service delivery.\r\n', '-The school has an established schedule and structure for LAC sessions and L&D activities throughout the school year. \r\n- Conduct of needs assessment and identification of priority training needs among teachers and personnel. \r\n-Strong instructional leadership and support from the school head in organizing professional development activities. \r\n-Active participation of teachers and school personnel in collaborative learning sessions. \r\n-Availability of relevant data and classroom-based experiences as inputs for LAC discussions. \r\n-Presence of resource speakers, master teachers, and experts who facilitate learning sessions. \r\n-Culture of collaboration, sharing of best practices, and reflective practice among teachers. \r\n- Integration of LAC/L&D outputs into instructional improvement and classroom application.\r\n', '-The school has a clear professional development plan aligned with DepEd priorities and personnel needs. \r\n- Strong instructional leadership and support in encouraging teachers and staff to pursue career advancement. \r\n-Regular conduct of trainings, seminars, workshops, and Learning Action Cells (LACs) for capacity building. \r\n-Active dissemination of information on promotion guidelines, requirements, and opportunities. \r\n-Availability of mentoring and coaching systems to support personnel readiness for promotion. \r\n-Encouragement of personnel participation in scholarships, graduate studies, and external trainings.               -Culture of continuous improvement, motivation, and professional growth among staff. \r\n-Supportive performance management system (IPCRF/OPCRF) that guides career development and promotion readiness.\r\n', '-The school has an established PRAISE a recognition and rewards system that acknowledges personnel achievements and milestones. \r\n-Regular conduct of programs and activities such as awards ceremonies, commendations, and appreciation events. \r\n-Strong support from school leadership in valuing and motivating personnel contributions. \r\n-Implementation of transparent criteria and guidelines for recognition and rewards. \r\n-Active involvement of stakeholders and colleagues in recognizing accomplishments of personnel. \r\n-Availability of documentation and monitoring systems to track achievements and milestones. \r\n-Culture of appreciation, motivation, and positive reinforcement within the school community. \r\n', 'The school has a clear and efficient payroll processing system aligned with DepEd and DBM guidelines. \r\n-Strong coordination between the school, division office, and finance personnel ensures accurate and timely processing of salaries and benefits. \r\n-Designated administrative and finance focal persons who monitor payroll concerns and updates. \r\n-Proper record-keeping and updating of personnel data (e.g., plantilla, deductions, allowances, and service records). \r\n- Active monitoring and verification of payroll reports to ensure accuracy before release. \r\n- Established communication channels for addressing payroll-related concerns and queries. \r\n-Compliance with government policies, issuances, and timelines on compensation and benefits.\r\n', '-The school has a clear workload distribution policy aligned with DepEd guidelines. \r\n-Strong instructional leadership ensures fair assignment of teaching loads and non-teaching tasks. \r\n-Availability of updated teacher profiles and workload records for proper assignment and monitoring. \r\n-Conduct of consultative meetings before finalizing teaching assignments and responsibilities. \r\n-Consideration of teacher specialization, expertise, and subject competency in workload distribution. \r\n-Regular review and adjustment of workloads based on actual needs and school priorities. \r\n-Open communication between school management and teachers regarding workload concerns\r\n', 'The school has a regularly scheduled inspection plan for infrastructure and facilities. \r\n-Strong leadership support in prioritizing safety, functionality, and maintenance of school facilities. \r\n- Designated school personnel and committees responsible for facility inspection and monitoring. \r\nActive involvement of stakeholders (PTA, LGU, SGC, and partners) in facility inspection and improvement. \r\n-Proper documentation and reporting system for identified issues, repairs, and maintenance needs. \r\n-Availability of maintenance and repair plans based on inspection results. \r\n-Continuous monitoring of safety, accessibility, and usability standards in school facilities', '-The school has a planned infrastructure development and improvement program aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP). \r\n-Strong leadership support in prioritizing facility upgrades, repairs, and development projects. \r\n-Active collaboration with stakeholders (LGUs, PTA, SGC, NGOs, and private partners) in supporting infrastructure improvement. \r\n-Presence of budget allocation and resource mobilization strategies for infrastructure projects. \r\n-Regular conduct of planning meetings and consultations for identifying facility needs and priorities. \r\n- Engagement of technical personnel and experts in planning and implementing facility improvements. \r\n', '', '-The school has established utility systems ensuring continuous access to water, electricity, and internet services. \r\n-Strong coordination with utility providers and service agencies for regular maintenance and uninterrupted service. \r\n-Presence of allocated budget for utility expenses and maintenance needs. \r\n-Regular monitoring and inspection of water, electrical, and ICT facilities to ensure functionality and safety. \r\n-Availability of designated personnel responsible for utility management and troubleshooting concerns. \r\n-Implementation of preventive maintenance measures to avoid service interruptions. \r\n-Support from stakeholders (LGUs, PTA, and partners) in sustaining utility services and improvements. \r\n-Compliance with safety standards and proper usage protocols for electrical and water systems.\r\n', '', '-The school has a clear Annual Budget Plan (Work and Financial Plan/WFP) aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP). \r\n-Strong financial planning and management system ensures proper allocation and utilization of MOOE funds.     Active leadership oversight and approval process for budget utilization and expenditures. \r\n-Presence of designated ADAS/AO ensuring accurate recording and monitoring of expenses. \r\n-Regular conduct of budget review and monitoring activities to track fund utilization. \r\n-Compliance with DepEd, DBM, and COA guidelines on procurement and fund management. \r\nStrong coordination among school personnel in identifying priority needs and expenditures. \r\n-Timely procurement and implementation of school programs, projects, and activities based on approved plans.\r\n   ', '-The school has a clear and organized financial management system for tracking MOOE expenditures and liquidation requirements. \r\n-Strong compliance with DepEd, DBM, and COA guidelines on liquidation and financial reporting. \r\n-Presence of a ADAS/AO responsible for timely preparation and submission of liquidation reports.    Regular monitoring of disbursements and documentation of supporting receipts and records. \r\n-Strong coordination between the school head, finance staff, and procurement committee to ensure complete documentation. \r\n-Established deadlines and internal control mechanisms for liquidation processes. \r\n Availability of proper filing and record-keeping systems for financial documents. \r\n-Continuous review and validation of liquidation reports before submission to concerned offices.\r\n    ', 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, '-The school commits to strengthening early grade literacy and numeracy programs to improve learner proficiency. \r\n- Implement intensive and systematic remediation and intervention programs for struggling learners. \r\n- Enhance teacher capacity through training on differentiated instruction and intervention strategies. Develop and utilize contextualized, engaging, and learner-centered instructional materials. \r\n-Promote active parental involvement in supporting learners’ literacy and numeracy development at home. \r\n', 'The school commits to improving learner proficiency in NAT through strengthened instruction and targeted interventions. \r\n-Implement structured review and enrichment programs focusing on least-mastered competencies. \r\n-Enhance integration of 21st century skills in daily teaching and learning processes. \r\n-Provide capacity-building for teachers on HOTS, assessment strategies, and differentiated instruction. \r\n-Develop and provide adequate review materials, mock tests, and ICT-supported learning resources. \r\n- Allocate dedicated time for remediation, intervention, and NAT preparation a Promote active involvement of parents and stakeholders in supporting learner preparation. \r\n', 'Commit to continuous capacity-building for school heads and coordinators to strengthen ALS program management and innovation.\r\nProvide regular training, mentoring, and upskilling opportunities to improve instructional delivery and assessment practices.\r\nIntroduce interventions such as remediation sessions, counseling, and motivational activities to sustain learner engagement.\r\nIncrease community awareness of ALS programs to encourage enrollment and reduce stigma among learners.\r\n', '-The school commits to strengthening the development and use of contextualized and learner-responsive learning materials. \r\n- Encourage continuous needs assessment to ensure relevance and appropriateness of instructional resources. \r\n-Provide capacity-building activities for teachers on instructional material development and contextualization strategies. \r\n-Strengthen collaborative culture among teachers for sharing best practices and learning resources. \r\n- Ensure adequate provision of resources and support (ICT, printing, time allocation) for material development. \r\n- Promote innovation and creativity in instructional design aligned with curriculum standards. ', 'The school commits to strengthening and sustaining effective remediation programs to address learning gaps in key subject areas. \r\n-Ensure regular identification and monitoring of struggling learners through assessment data. \r\n-Enhance teacher capacity through training and LAC sessions on intervention strategies and differentiated instruction. \r\n-Allocate time, resources, and learning materials specifically for remediation activities. \r\n-Strengthen home-school collaboration to support learners undergoing remediation\r\n-Continuously evaluate and improve remediation strategies to ensure learner improvement and mastery.', '-The school commits to strengthening the integration of peace education and DepEd Core Values across all learning areas. \r\n- Provide continuous training and capacity-building for teachers on values education and peace-building strategies. \r\n- Ensure consistent monitoring and evaluation of values integration in teaching and learning processes. \r\n-Encourage the use of contextualized and experiential learning activities that promote peace and positive behavior. \r\n-Strengthen school-wide programs and activities that reinforce DepEd Core Values. \r\n- Engage parents and stakeholders in reinforcing values formation at home and in the community. \r\n-Continuously improve instructional materials and strategies to deepen values integration\r\n', '-The school commits to sustaining and strengthening the conduct and utilization of test item analysis in improving instruction. \r\n-Ensure regular and systematic implementation of TIA after all major assessments. \r\n-Enhance teacher capacity through training on assessment design and data analysis. \r\n-Improve quality of test items to ensure validity, reliability, and alignment with MELCs, Curriculum Guide.\r\n-Strengthen collaborative review processes through LAC sessions and peer evaluation.', '', '-The school commits to achieving and sustaining a zero-bullying environment through strengthened policies and practices. \r\n-Intensify awareness campaigns and orientation programs on anti-bullying for learners, parents, and personnel. \r\n- Strengthen reporting, monitoring, and documentation systems for all bullying-related incidents. \r\n- Promote safe and confidential reporting mechanisms to encourage learners to report concerns. \r\n- Engage parents and stakeholders in reinforcing positive behavior and anti-bullying measures. ', '-The school commits to sustaining a zero-tolerance policy on all forms of child abuse within the school community. \r\n-Strengthen implementation and monitoring of the Child Protection Policy at all levels. \r\n- Conduct regular orientation and awareness campaigns for learners, parents, and personnel. \r\n-Enhance capacity-building for the Child Protection Committee and school personnel on handling cases- Promote a safe, supportive, and nurturing school environment for all learners. \r\n', '-The school commits to sustaining and further reducing dropout incidence through proactive and inclusive strategies. \r\n-Strengthen early identification and monitoring systems for learners at risk of dropping out.      -Enhance intervention programs such as remediation, mentoring, and catch-up classes. \r\n- Improve parent and community engagement in supporting learner retention. \r\n-Provide guidance and counseling services to address learners’ personal and academic concerns. \r\nStrengthen partnerships with LGUs and stakeholders to support learners facing socio-economic challenges. \r\n-Promote learner engagement through relevant and motivating school programs. \r\n-Ensure regular home visitation and follow-up mechanisms for at-risk learners. \r\n', 'The school commits to sustaining and strengthening culture-sensitive and inclusive school activities. \r\n-Ensure regular integration of culture-based education in teaching and learning processes. \r\n-Strengthen partnerships with cultural communities and stakeholders for authentic learning experiences. \r\n-Provide capacity-building for teachers on culturally responsive teaching strategies. \r\n-Institutionalize school programs that celebrate and preserve local culture and traditions. \r\n-Ensure equal participation of all learners, including IP learners, in school activities. \r\n', '- Commit to continuously improving strategies that address barriers to access, such as poverty, distance, and time constraints.\r\n- Increase mapping, recruitment, and retention efforts for OSYs and adult learners in the community.\r\n- Ensure availability of contextualized, relevant, and sufficient learning materials for diverse learners.\r\n- Conduct sustained community campaigns to encourage enrollment associated with ALS learners.\r\n', '-Commit to continuous improvement of program implementation through regular planning, review, and innovation.\r\n-Establish additional CLCs in underserved areas and upgrade existing facilities for better accessibility and learning conditions.\r\n-Strengthen advocacy campaigns, conduct regular mapping, and implement interventions to reduce dropouts.\r\n-Continue awareness campaigns to reduce stigma and increase community recognition of ALS as a viable education pathway\r\n', '-The school commits to strengthening the functionality and responsiveness of the Child Protection Committee. \r\n- Ensure regular training and capacity-building for CPC members on child protection policies and case management. \r\n- Strengthen reporting, documentation, and monitoring systems for all child protection concerns. \r\n- Conduct continuous awareness and advocacy programs on child rights and protection. \r\n- Ensure prompt and appropriate action on all reported cases in accordance with DepEd guidelines. \r\n- Continuously review and improve child protection systems and practices to ensure effectiveness and safety.\r\n', '-The school commits to sustaining and strengthening the implementation of a functional DRRM Plan. \r\n-Ensure regular updating and enhancement of the DRRM Plan based on new risks and assessment results. \r\n-Conduct frequent disaster preparedness training and simulation exercises for all stakeholders. \r\n-Strengthen coordination with external DRRM agencies and local government units for effective response. \r\n-Improve availability and accessibility of emergency resources and equipment in all school areas. \r\n-Enhance documentation and monitoring of DRRM activities and incidents for continuous improvement. \r\n-Promote a culture of safety, preparedness, and resilience within the school community. \r\nInstitutionalize continuous evaluation and improvement of DRRM systems and practices. ', '-The school commits to strengthening and sustaining mental wellness programs and support mechanisms. \r\n-Ensure continuous capacity-building for teachers and personnel on mental health and psychosocial support. \r\n-Enhance counseling services and referral systems for timely and appropriate interventions. \r\n-Conduct regular mental health awareness and advocacy activities for the school community. \r\n- Promote a safe, inclusive, and supportive school environment for all learners and personnel. \r\n-Strengthen partnerships with health professionals and organizations for expert support. \r\n- Institutionalize monitoring and evaluation of mental wellness programs to ensure effectiveness. \r\n-Encourage open communication and stigma-free discussions on mental health concerns.\r\n', 'The school commits to continuously upgrading and maintaining all PWD-friendly facilities to ensure safety, accessibility, and usability. \r\nExpand and improve learning resources and assistive devices for learners with disabilities. \r\n', '-The school commits to sustaining a participatory and inclusive strategic planning process involving all stakeholders. \r\n-Ensure regular review, updating, and alignment of the strategic plan based on current data and emerging needs. \r\n-Strengthen the use of data-driven decision-making in all phases of planning and implementation. \r\n-Allocate adequate resources and budget to support priority programs and activities in the strategic plan. \r\n-Enhance capacity-building initiatives for the School Planning Team on effective planning and monitoring. \r\n-Institutionalize monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to track progress and outcomes of the strategic plan. \r\n-Promote transparency and communication of the plan to all stakeholders to ensure shared understanding and support. \r\n-Foster stronger partnerships with external stakeholders to support strategic goals and initiatives. \r\n', '-The school commits to strengthening the functionality of the School-Community Planning Team through continuous engagement and collaboration. \r\n-Ensure regular and well-documented meetings with clear agendas, outputs, and follow-through actions. \r\n-Provide capacity-building activities for team members on planning, leadership, and community engagement. \r\n-Enhance stakeholder participation by encouraging broader representation and active involvement. \r\nInstitutionalize monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to assess the effectiveness of the team’s plans and initiatives. \r\n-Allocate sufficient resources and logistical support to sustain team activities and programs. \r\n-Promote open communication and transparency in all planning and decision-making processes. \r\n-Strengthen partnerships with community organizations and stakeholders to support school improvement initiatives.', '-The school commits to strengthening student leadership and participation through continuous support of SSG/SPG programs. \r\n-Provide capacity-building and leadership training for student officers to enhance their skills and competencies. \r\n-Ensure regular and well-documented meetings and activities of the student government. \r\n-Encourage greater student involvement in planning, implementing, and evaluating school programs. \r\n-Allocate resources and logistical support for student-led initiatives and projects. \r\n-Promote transparency, accountability, and inclusivity in all student government operations. \r\n-Strengthen partnerships between student leaders, teachers, and stakeholders to support school development. \r\n-Institutionalize monitoring and evaluation of student government performance and impact.\r\n', '-The school commits to continuously enhancing and innovating frontline services to better meet stakeholder needs. \r\n-Strengthen the use of technology and digital platforms for faster, more efficient service delivery. \r\n-Provide capacity-building and training for personnel on customer service and innovative practices. \r\n-Institutionalize feedback and grievance mechanisms to ensure stakeholder concerns are addressed promptly. \r\n-Allocate resources and budget to support innovation and modernization of services. \r\n-Promote transparency, efficiency, and accountability in all frontline service processes.          -Encourage stakeholder participation in co-creating solutions and improvements. \r\n-Conduct regular assessment and benchmarking of service delivery practices to sustain quality improvement.\r\n', 'The school commits to ensuring effective and timely implementation of all programs and activities in the strategic plan. \r\n-Strengthen the alignment between the strategic plan and implementation plans (SIP/AIP) to ensure coherence. \r\n-Enhance monitoring, evaluation, and reporting systems to track progress and outcomes. \r\n-Provide capacity-building for staff on planning, implementation, and project management. \r\n- Ensure efficient allocation and utilization of resources to support priority programs. \r\n-Conduct regular review and updating of implementation plans based on performance data and emerging needs. \r\n-Promote accountability and shared responsibility among all personnel and stakeholders. ', 'The school commits to strengthening the functionality of the SGC through active engagement and collaboration. \r\n-Ensure regular, well-documented meetings with clear action plans and follow-up mechanisms. \r\n- Provide capacity-building and orientation for SGC members on governance, leadership, and SBM practices. \r\n-Enhance stakeholder representation and participation to ensure inclusivity in decision-making. \r\n-Institutionalize monitoring and evaluation systems to assess the effectiveness of SGC initiatives. \r\n-Allocate adequate resources and logistical support for SGC operations and activities. \r\n- Promote transparency, accountability, and open communication in all council undertakings. \r\n-Strengthen partnerships and linkages with external stakeholders to support school improvement efforts.\r\n', '-The school commits to strengthening the functionality and sustainability of the PTA through continuous engagement. \r\n-Ensure regular, transparent, and well-documented PTA meetings and financial reporting. \r\n-Provide capacity-building and orientation for PTA officers on leadership, governance, and financial management. \r\n- Encourage greater parent participation and inclusivity in all PTA activities and initiatives. \r\n-Allocate and manage resources effectively to support PTA programs and projects. \r\n-Promote open communication and strong partnerships between parents, teachers, and the school.         -Institutionalize monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to assess PTA contributions and impact. \r\n-Strengthen collaboration with community stakeholders to support school development initiatives.\r\n\r\n', 'The school commits to strengthening and sustaining partnerships with stakeholders and other schools. \r\n- Expand and diversify linkages and networking opportunities to support school improvement goals. \r\n-Ensure regular communication, coordination, and feedback mechanisms with all partners. \r\n-Formalize partnerships through MOAs/MOUs and documented agreements. \r\n-Provide capacity-building activities for stakeholders to enhance collaboration and engagement. \r\n-Promote transparency, accountability, and mutual respect in all partnership activities. \r\n-Allocate resources and support for collaborative programs and joint initiatives. \r\n-Conduct regular monitoring and evaluation of partnership outcomes and impact.\r\n', '-The school commits to strengthening its monitoring and evaluation systems for more effective program implementation. \r\n-Ensure regular, systematic, and data-driven monitoring and evaluation activities. \r\n- Enhance capacity-building of personnel on M&E tools, data analysis, and reporting. \r\n-Utilize evaluation results to inform planning, decision-making, and program improvement. \r\n-Improve documentation, reporting, and feedback mechanisms for transparency and accountability. \r\n-Allocate adequate resources and support for M&E activities. \r\n-Promote stakeholder participation in evaluating programs and providing feedback. \r\n -Institutionalize continuous review and refinement of programs, projects, and activities based on findings. ', '-The school commits to sustaining and improving personnel performance ratings through continuous support and supervision. \r\n-Strengthen coaching, mentoring, and performance feedback mechanisms for all personnel. \r\n-Provide regular LAC sessions, Collaborative Expertise sessions, professional development and training opportunities aligned with RPMS indicators. \r\n-Ensure clear goal-setting and alignment of individual performance with school objectives. \r\n- Promote a culture of excellence, accountability, and continuous improvement among personnel. \r\n-Enhance monitoring and evaluation of performance targets throughout the school year. \r\n-Recognize and reward high-performing personnel to sustain motivation and productivity. \r\n-Strengthen collaboration and peer support systems to improve teaching and non-teaching performance.\r\n', '-The school commits to sustaining and improving OPCRF performance ratings through continuous quality improvement. \r\n-Strengthen performance monitoring, coaching, and feedback mechanisms for all offices and personnel. \r\n-Ensure alignment of office plans and targets with school and DepEd priorities. \r\n-Enhance data-based decision-making and reporting systems for more efficient performance tracking. \r\n-Provide regular training and capacity-building activities to improve office efficiency and effectiveness. \r\n-Promote a culture of excellence, collaboration, and accountability among school personnel. \r\n- Improve resource planning and utilization to support target achievement. \r\n-Institutionalize recognition and rewards systems to motivate high performance.\r\n', '-The school commits to sustaining and strengthening needs-based LAC and L&D programs aligned with teacher development needs. \r\n-Ensure regular, well-planned, and well-documented LAC sessions with clear objectives and outputs. \r\n-Strengthen data-driven identification of training needs to guide L&D activities. \r\n-Encourage active participation and engagement of all teachers in professional learning activities. \r\n-Provide continuous support and resources for effective conduct of LACs and trainings. \r\n-Promote application of LAC/L&D learnings in classroom instruction to improve learner outcomes. \r\n-Enhance monitoring and evaluation of LAC effectiveness and impact on teaching practice. \r\n-Foster a culture of continuous professional growth and collaboration among school personnel.\r\n', '-The school commits to sustaining and strengthening continuous professional development programs for all personnel. \r\n-Provide regular and needs-based training opportunities to enhance competencies and career growth. \r\n-Strengthen mentoring, coaching, and career guidance systems for promotion readiness. \r\n- Ensure equal access to professional development opportunities for all qualified personnel. \r\n-Encourage and support advanced studies and participation in external learning programs. \r\n-Improve information dissemination on promotion policies and requirements to all staff. \r\n-Align performance management systems with professional growth and promotion pathways. \r\n- Foster a culture of lifelong learning, excellence, and professional accountability within the school.\r\n', '-The school commits to sustaining and strengthening a fair and systematic recognition and rewards system for all personnel.  -Ensure regular and meaningful recognition activities that celebrate both small and major accomplishments. \r\n-Improve documentation and tracking of personnel achievements for accurate and timely recognition. \r\n-Strengthen transparency and inclusivity in the selection process for awards and incentives. \r\n-Provide non-monetary and innovative forms of recognition to motivate personnel. \r\n-Encourage a culture of appreciation and positive reinforcement within the school. \r\n-Allocate resources and support for recognition programs and milestone celebrations. \r\n-Continuously review and enhance recognition policies to ensure fairness and relevance\r\n', 'The school commits to ensuring the continuous accuracy and timeliness of salary, allowance, and compensation release for all personnel. \r\n-Strengthen coordination and communication with concerned offices to avoid delays and errors in payroll processing. \r\n-Maintain updated and accurate personnel records to support efficient payroll management. \r\n-Enhance monitoring and validation procedures before submission of payroll documents. \r\n-Provide prompt resolution mechanisms for payroll-related issues and concerns. \r\n-Ensure strict compliance with government rules and regulations on compensation and benefits. \r\n-Promote transparency and accountability in payroll processing and management\r\n', '- The school commits to maintaining fair, transparent, and equitable distribution of teacher workloads at all times. \r\n-Strengthen consultative processes in assigning teaching loads and ancillary responsibilities. \r\n-Ensure regular review and adjustment of workloads to address emerging needs and imbalances. \r\n-Maintain updated and accurate records of teacher assignments and responsibilities. \r\n-Promote transparency and accountability in workload planning and assignment. \r\n-Consider well-being, specialization, and capacity of teachers in workload distribution decisions. \r\n-Address workload concerns promptly and fairly through proper channels.  -Foster a collaborative and supportive school environment that values teacher welfare.\r\n', '-The school commits to conducting regular, systematic, and comprehensive inspections of all infrastructure and facilities. \r\n-Strengthen preventive maintenance systems to ensure safety and functionality of school buildings and equipment. \r\n-Ensure prompt action and resolution of identified defects and hazards. \r\n- Improve documentation and tracking of inspection findings and repair actions. \r\n- Allocate adequate resources and budget for maintenance and facility improvements. \r\n- Enhance stakeholder participation in monitoring and improving school facilities. \r\n- Promote safety, accessibility, and compliance with standards in all infrastructure. \r\n- Institutionalize a continuous improvement system for school facilities management.\r\n', '-The school commits to continuously initiating and implementing infrastructure and facility improvement projects based on priority needs. \r\n-Strengthen planning, coordination, and consultation processes with stakeholders for infrastructure development. \r\n-Ensure efficient utilization of funds and resources for school improvement projects. \r\n-Enhance documentation and monitoring of all infrastructure projects from planning to completion. \r\n-Strengthen partnerships and resource mobilization efforts to support facility upgrades. \r\n-Prioritize safe, inclusive, and learner-friendly learning environments in all improvement initiatives. \r\n-Conduct regular evaluation of completed projects to ensure quality and sustainability. \r\n- Institutionalize a continuous improvement system for school facilities and infrastructure development', 'The school commits to  have a functional and learner-friendly library. \r\n-Strengthen resource mobilization and partnerships to acquire updated books and reading materials. \r\n- Promote a strong reading culture through school-wide reading programs and activities. \r\n-Enhance the physical environment of the library to make it more conducive for reading and learning. \r\n-Assign or train competent library focal personnel for efficient management. \r\n-Integrate library use into classroom instruction and learning activities. \r\n-Develop and strengthen digital library or e-library resources for broader access. \r\n-Ensure regular monitoring and evaluation of library utilization and improvement initiatives.\r\n', '-The school commits to ensuring continuous functionality and reliability of water, electricity, and internet services at all times. \r\n-Strengthen preventive maintenance and timely repair mechanisms for all utility systems. \r\n-Improve coordination with utility providers to address issues promptly and efficiently. \r\n- Ensure proper allocation and utilization of funds for utility maintenance and improvement. \r\n-Enhance monitoring systems to quickly identify and resolve service disruptions. \r\n-Promote responsible and efficient use of utilities among school personnel and learners. \r\n-Strengthen stakeholder support and partnerships for infrastructure sustainability. \r\n- Institutionalize a contingency plan for emergency utility interruptions to ensure continuous operations\r\n', '-Ensure regular maintenance, repair, and upgrading of ICT facilities and equipment. \r\n- Improve internet connectivity and network infrastructure to support digital learning. \r\n- Provide capacity-building and training for teachers on ICT integration and digital literacy. \r\n-Establish efficient scheduling and utilization systems for equitable access to the computer lab. \r\n-Allocate adequate budget and resources for ICT development and sustainability. \r\n-Enhance technical support and management systems for ICT facilities. \r\n-Promote safe, responsible, and effective use of technology among learners and personnel.\r\n', '-The school commits to ensuring efficient, transparent, and timely utilization of MOOE funds within the 75–100% target range. \r\n-Strengthen planning, budgeting, and procurement processes aligned with priority school needs. \r\n-Ensure strict compliance with accounting, auditing, and procurement rules and regulations. \r\n-Enhance monitoring and reporting systems for budget utilization and financial accountability. \r\n-Conduct regular budget reviews and adjustments based on implementation progress and emerging needs. \r\n-Promote transparency and stakeholder awareness on MOOE utilization and priorities. \r\n-Strengthen capacity-building for personnel involved in financial management and procurement. \r\n-Ensure prioritization of learner-centered programs and school improvement initiatives in fund utilization.\r\n', 'The school commits to ensuring 100% timely and complete liquidation of all MOOE expenditures in compliance with regulations. \r\n-Strengthen financial monitoring and internal control systems to prevent delays and discrepancies. \r\n-Ensure complete, accurate, and organized documentation of all financial transactions. \r\n- Provide capacity-building and training for finance personnel on updated accounting and auditing procedures. \r\n- Improve coordination among school officials and staff involved in procurement and liquidation processes. \r\n- Strictly adhere to submission timelines and documentary requirements set by oversight agencies. \r\n- Conduct regular internal reviews and audits of financial records before external evaluation. \r\n- Promote transparency, accountability, and responsible financial management practices within the school.\r\n', '-The school commits to sustaining and improving stakeholder satisfaction ratings through continuous quality improvement. \r\n-Strengthen feedback mechanisms to ensure timely response to stakeholder concerns. \r\n-Regularly conduct and analyze stakeholder satisfaction surveys to guide decision-making. \r\n-Enhance service delivery standards to ensure efficiency, transparency, and responsiveness. \r\n-Provide capacity-building for personnel on customer service and stakeholder relations. \r\n-Institutionalize action planning based on evaluation results and feedback\r\n-Promote stronger collaboration with stakeholders in planning and implementation of school programs. \r\n-Ensure continuous monitoring and evaluation of school performance and services.\r\n', 1, 119, 12, 57);
