ession', 'Conduct of PRAISE annualy', '1. Strong Leadership Support 2. Clear Policies and Criteria 3. Adequate Funding and Resources', '1. Efficient Administrative Processes 2. Competent and Trained Personnel 3. Accurate Data Management', '1. . Clear Workload Policies and Guidelines 2. Consideration of Teacher Expertise and Experience 3. Adequate Staffing and Resource Allocation', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 0, 2, 0, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 6, 6, 6, 2, 6, 0, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', 'results shall be utilized as supplementary data rather than the sole basis for evaluating school performance.', '', 'it is resolved that schools, with the support of the Schools Division Office, shall prioritize institutional support systems and targeted technical capacity-building to enable teachers to consistently prepare quality contextualized learning materials, thereby ensuring learner-centered, relevant, and inclusive instruction aligned with DepEd standards.', 'the school shall strengthen institutional support for teachers conducting remediation activities to address identified learning gaps in reading and comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics by institutionalizing a structured remediation program integrated into the SIP and AIP', 'The integration of peace-promoting topics and DepEd core values can be enhanced through a combined institutional and technical resolution that strengthens leadership support, school policies, professional development, instructional resources, and teacher pedagogical competence.', 'To strengthen the conduct of test item analysis, the school shall enhance its technical capacity by providing standardized item analysis tools and building teachers’ skills in their effective use.', 'o strengthen the relevance and effectiveness of the school’s TLE–TVL course offerings, the school shall institutionalize partnerships with local industries through formal agreements and regular collaboration.', 'Conduct an online safety workshop for all students', 'Conduct an annual review of the child protection policy for regular awareness for teachers, staff, students and parents', 'To reduce school dropouts, the school should strengthen flexible learning options, strengthen school guidance and counseling programs, increase government funding for basic education', 'Institutionalized key culture-sensitive events like annual IP month', 'the use of appropriate social assessment tools, supported by technical monitoring systems, is essential in measuring access, participation, learning quality, and outcomes among marginalized learner groups', '', 'Institutionalize regular CPC meeting into the school calendar', 'The School DRRM Committee is directed to continuously implement, monitor, and update the plan to ensure the safety, preparedness, and resilience of learners, personnel, and school property.', 'Advocate for a dedicated budget line for school mental health programs', 'Facility assessment and audit with the School Admin, SPED Team, Facility upgrades by Admin, Maintenance Team, Procurement of assistive tools by Admin, Supply Officer, Teacher training by SPED Coordinators, Program evaluation', 'This commitment includes ensuring active involvement of key stakeholders, establishing clear goals and performance indicators, and institutionalizing monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to guide decision-making and support sustainable school improvement.', 'The school must participate regularly and meaningfully in school planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation activities.\r\nPromote shared decision‑making guided by the principles of School‑Based Management and transparency.\r\nAlign community initiatives and resources with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).', 'The Supreme Student Government commits to transparent governance, active student representation, and effective program implementation in partnership with the school community to promote student welfare and leadership.', 'The school commits to strengthening institutional innovation in the delivery of frontline services by continuously improving policies, systems, and processes to ensure accessible, efficient, transparent, and stakeholder-centered services', 'The school commits to improving learner achievement and instructional quality by:\r\n\r\nEnsuring effective implementation of the K–12/MELCs-aligned curriculum\r\nStrengthening teachers’ instructional strategies, assessment practices, and ICT integration, Enhancing school leadership and governance in line with SBM principles\r\nBuilding teachers’ and staff’s capacity through continuous professional development', 'The school commits to strengthening the functionality of the School Governance Council (SGC) by ensuring active stakeholder participation, transparent decision‑making, and regular monitoring of school programs and resources. The SGC shall consistently convene to support the development, implementation, and evaluation of the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)', 'The school commits to strengthening its Parent‑Teacher Association (PTA) by ensuring its formal organization and recognition, conducting democratic elections of officers, maintaining an approved constitution and by‑laws, holding regular and well‑documented meetings, actively supporting school programs and projects', 'To institutionalize and strengthen partnerships with stakeholders and other schools through structured collaboration, joint initiatives, and continuous engagement.', 'The school commits to establishing and sustaining a systematic, participatory, and evidence‑based monitoring and evaluation process to continuously assess the effectiveness, efficiency, and impact of its programs, projects, and activities.', '1. Enhance Continuous Professional Development 2. Strengthen Instructional Leadership and Monitoring 3. Ensure Availability of Resources and Support', '1. Strengthen Leadership and Monitoring 2. Enhance Staff Capacity Development 3. Sustain Efficient Work Systems ', '1. Institutionalization of LAC and L&D Programs 2. Capacity Building of Facilitators', 'Adequate resources will be allocated to ensure staff development, recognizing its vital role in improving teaching quality and student outcomes.', '1. Policy Institutionalization 2. Annual Budget Allocation 3.  Regular Implementation Schedule', '1. Strengthen Administrative Efficiency 2. Build Capacity of HR and Finance Personnel 3.  Improve Monitoring and Internal Controls', '1. Institutionalize Clear Workload Standards 2. Ensure Continuous Capacity Building 3.  Provide Equitable Support and Resources', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Institutional Commitment\r\nThe school commits to continuously sustaining and improving an average rating of at least “Satisfactory” from its internal and external stakeholders by implementing systematic feedback mechanisms, strengthening stakeholder engagement, ensuring responsive governance and support services, and using evaluation results as inputs to evidence‑based planning and continuous quality improvement.', 1, 123, 12, 57);
