(834, '2026', '128501', 'Limited vocabulary and difficulty expressing ideas clearly, weak listening comprehension, especially with longer instructions, Difficulty in basic operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division) and limited parental support in learning at home.', '', 'Irregular attendance of ALS learners due to work or family responsibilities, low motivation and inconsistent participation in sessions, limited literacy and numeracy foundation among learners and difficulty in mastering competencies. ', '', '', 'Limited time to fully integrate peace education and DepEd core values in all lessons,  difficulty in assessing learners’ attitudes and values formation and weak reinforcement of values at home and in the community .\r\n', 'Limited teacher training on test item analysis and data interpretation, limited use of results to improve instruction and interventions, insufficient ICT tools or templates for efficient data processing, gaps in aligning test items with learning competencies and standards, weak feedback loop between analysis results and classroom practice and bottleneck in translating data into actionable teaching strategies.', '', 'Possible cyberbullying not easily detected within school setting, limited documentation or tracking of minor conflicts among learners, bottlenecks in ensuring sustained school-wide child protection vigilance, limited student awareness on what constitutes bullying and reporting procedures and inconsistent monitoring of learner behavior in all areas of the school.\r\n\r\n', '', '', 'Limited understanding of diverse cultures among teachers and learners, lack of contextualized and culture-sensitive instructional materials, insufficient training on integrating culture in teaching and school activities and  limited participation of indigenous and minority groups', 'Irregular attendance of OSYs and adult learners due to work and family responsibilities, difficulty in sustaining engagement and motivation among disadvantaged learners, limited trained facilitators for handling OSYs and adult learners, geographic and transportation barriers affecting access to learning sessions ', 'Irregular attendance and participation of ALS learners due to work and personal responsibilities, learning gaps in basic literacy and numeracy among enrollees, difficulty in sustaining learner motivation and program completion and bottlenecks in reaching remote or hard-to-access learners', 'Limited orientation and capacity-building for CPC members on updated policies and protocols, inconsistent reporting and documentation of child protection concerns, and lack of regular monitoring and evaluation of CPC actions and effectiveness', 'Insufficient training of staff and learners on disaster preparedness and response, lack of adequate DRRM equipment and emergency supplies and gaps in learner awareness and readiness during emergency situations', 'Limited number of trained guidance counselors or mental health personnel, inconsistent implementation of mental wellness programs and activities, lack of awareness on available mental health support services and limited resources and materials for psychosocial support interventions.', 'Incomplete or limited PWD-friendly facilities (ramps, handrails, accessible toilets), lack of specialized SPED learning materials and assistive devices, Insufficient number of trained SPED teachers or support personnel, Limited budget for upgrading and maintaining inclusive facilities and limited coordination with external agencies for SPED support services ', 'Limited stakeholder involvement in planning, lack of accurate and updated data, insufficient training on strategic planning and weak implementation and sustainability.', 'Limited participation of community stakeholders and insufficient training on planning processes', 'Limited student participation in SSG/SPG activities,weak leadership skills among officers, irregular meetings and poor coordination and lack of clear plans and student-led initiatives.', 'Lack of centralized information and service system, no established online feedback or complaint system and inconsistent implementation of service procedures across offices.', 'Insufficient budget, resources, and materials, weak monitoring and evaluation mechanisms and   difficulty sustaining programs and initiatives.', 'Irregular or infrequent SGC meetings, limited participation of stakeholders (parents, community members), unclear roles and responsibilities of SGC members, weak coordination between SGC and school management and lack of training/orientation for SGC members ', 'Low attendance and participation in PTA meetings and activities, limited parental involvement in school programs and learner support, lack of clear understanding of PTA roles and responsibilities, inconsistent participation of PTA officers and limited training or orientation for PTA members ', 'Limited number of active partner institutions and stakeholders, insufficient resources to support collaborative programs, difficulty sustaining long-term partnerships and programs, lack of clear roles and expectations in collaborative activities and inconsistent monitoring of partnership outcomes and impact', 'Lack of clear and measurable indicators for some programs, limited skills of staff in M&E processes and weak documentation of program implementation results', 'Inconsistent satisfaction feedback from internal and external stakeholders, limited mechanisms for gathering regular stakeholder feedback and limited awareness of stakeholder feedback results among staff ', '', '', 'Strong support from school leadership in planning and implementation, clear identification of teachers’ learning needs through assessments and feedback, regular scheduling and integration of LAC sessions in the school calendar, active participation and engagement of teachers and staff \r\nand availability of competent resource persons and facilitators\r\n', 'Inadequate documentation of professional accomplishments and credentials and difficulty meeting required competencies and qualifications for higher positions', 'Minimal impact on motivation due to weak recognition system and Lack of clear and fair criteria for selecting awardees', 'Incomplete submission of required documents for processing', '', 'Limited budget for repair and maintenance needs, aging or damaged school buildings and facilities and safety hazards in some classrooms or school areas ', 'Limited budget for infrastructure projects and upgrades and aging or inadequate school buildings and facilities', 'Lack of available space/classroom for library', 'insufficient water supply, especially during the hot season and unstable internet connection', 'Lack of available classroom for computer laboratory', '', '', '', 'Effective remediation and enrichment programs, integration of 21st-century skills (critical thinking, collaboration, communication, creativity) in lessons, competent and well-trained teachers using varied, learner-centered strategies', '', 'Supportive school leadership and collaborative culture, availability of resources needed by teachers, availability of curriculum guides and reference materials, teachers’ understanding of learners’ needs and context and conduct of LAC session for effective instructional materials.\r\n\r\n', 'Strong teacher commitment to learner improvement, supportive school leadership and intervention programs, availability of learning materials and remediation tools, use of differentiated instruction strategies and collaboration among teachers for intervention planning \r\n\r\n', '', '', '', '', 'Strict implementation of the Child Protection Policy (CPP), continuous teacher vigilance and classroom supervision promotion of a safe, respectful, and values-based school environment and consistent values education and positive discipline practices', 'Strong learner tracking and monitoring system, effective early intervention and remediation programs, active guidance and counseling services and consistent parental involvement and home visits ', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Clear performance targets and well-defined KRAs, strong commitment and dedication of school personnel, effective planning and time management of tasks, Supportive leadership and coaching from school heads and Master Teacher, continuous professional development and training opportunities, collaborative teamwork among staff and teachers and availability of needed instructional materials and resources ', 'Effective planning, coordination, and delegation of tasks, regular monitoring, coaching, and performance feedback, strong teamwork and collaboration among personnel, high level of commitment and accountability of staff, efficient implementation of school policies and procedures, availability of resources and logistical support and continuous capacity building and professional development \r\n\r\n', '', '', '', '', 'Clear assignment of roles and responsibilities based on qualifications and expertise, effective scheduling and workload planning by school leadership, regular consultation and coordination among teachers, transparent criteria for assigning teaching loads and ancillary tasks and consideration of teacher strengths, experience, and specialization', '', '', '', '', '', 'Proper planning and budgeting of MOOE allocation, timely submission of liquidation and financial reports, efficient prioritization of school needs and expenses and transparency and accountability in fund management ', 'Proper planning and documentation of all MOOE expenditures , strong monitoring and supervision by school leadership and timely submission of liquidation reports and supporting documents', 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 2, 6, 2, 2, 2, 6, 6, 6, 2, 6, 1, 2, 1, 2, 2, 3, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Strengthen early grade intervention programs (reading and numeracy remediation), implement daily guided reading and structured literacy activities, use differentiated instruction to address diverse learning needs, integrate play-based and contextualized numeracy strategies, enhance teacher training on early literacy and numeracy strategies and promote parental involvement through home reading and practice activities.', 'Strengthen curriculum alignment with NAT competencies and 21st-century skills Implement targeted intervention and enrichment programs based on assessment results, integrate critical thinking, problem-solving, and ICT skills in daily lessons, provide continuous teacher training on effective strategies and assessment practices, conduct review sessions, drills, and mock NAT exams and ensure availability of updated learning resources.\r\n', 'Strengthen regular and flexible ALS learning sessions to accommodate learners’ schedules, provide contextualized and simplified learning materials for better understanding and implement intensive literacy and numeracy remediation activities.\r\n\r\n', 'Continue capacity building and training on contextualization of learning materials, strengthen collaboration among teachers for sharing localized resources, ensure strong school leadership support for material development, maximize ICT and community resources in preparing lessons, allocate regular time for lesson planning and material preparation and sustain learner-centered and context-based instructional practices', 'Sustain strong teacher commitment to improve learner performance, continue leadership support and intervention programs, maintain continuous provision of learning materials and remediation tools, continue collaborative planning among teachers for effective interventions, maintain a fixed schedule for remediation sessions and ensure continuous monitoring, documentation, and feedback on learner progress', 'Develop and use contextualized and value-rich learning materials, apply learner-centered and reflective activities to strengthen values formation, reinforce values through daily classroom routines and modeling and strengthen parent and community involvement in values development monitor and evaluate learner behavior and values application regularly. ', 'Strengthen teachers’ training on test item analysis and data interpretation, ensure regular and timely preparation of item analysis reports after every assessment, use results to design targeted remediation and enrichment activities, provide templates and ICT tools for efficient analysis and reporting, align test construction with learning competencies, conduct regular collaborative discussions (LAC sessions) on assessment results ', '', 'Sustain and strengthen the implementation of Child Protection Policy and Anti-Bullying measures, conduct regular orientation and awareness campaigns for learners, parents, and teachers, strengthen guidance and counseling services for early identification and intervention, maintain active monitoring and reporting systems for learner behavior, promote values education and positive discipline practices in all classrooms, encourage a safe, inclusive, and respectful school environment.', 'Sustain strict implementation of the Child Protection Policy (CPP), maintain regular orientation and awareness programs on child safety for all stakeholders, strengthen guidance and counseling services for early detection and intervention, ensure continuous monitoring and supervision of learners in all school areas, and maintain a safe, inclusive, and child-friendly school environment.', 'Sustain and strengthen the learner tracking and early warning system, intensify remediation, catch-up, and intervention programs, conduct regular home visits and parent-teacher conferences, enhance guidance and counseling services for at-risk learners  and provide flexible learning options (modular, ALS support, adjusted schedules)', 'Sustain implementation of culture-sensitive and inclusive school programs, integrate local culture and indigenous knowledge in teaching and learning activities, conduct regular teacher training on cultural responsiveness, strengthen stakeholder engagement, including indigenous leaders and community members and continuously monitor and evaluate culture-sensitive programs for improvement. ', 'Strengthen flexible learning delivery modes (modular, blended, ALS sessions), intensify community-based learning programs for OSYs and adult learners, provide contextualized and simplified learning materials, conduct regular learner tracking, monitoring, and follow-up and assign trained facilitators for adult and alternative learners.', 'Sustain and strengthen the implementation of the School-Based ALS program, Ensure regular and flexible learning sessions for ALS learners, provide adequate and updated ALS learning materials and modules, conduct continuous monitoring, tracking, and learner profiling, strengthen training of ALS implementers and facilitators, and intensify remediation for literacy and numeracy gaps', 'Sustain and strengthen the functionality of the Child Protection Committee (CPC) , conduct regular training and capacity-building for CPC members, ensure consistent implementation of child protection policies and procedures, improve reporting, documentation, and monitoring systems and maintain a safe, child-friendly, and protective school environment', 'Sustain and regularly update the DRRM plan based on current risks and needs, conduct regular disaster preparedness drills (fire, earthquake, evacuation) and strengthen training of teachers, learners, and staff on DRRM protocols', 'Sustain and strengthen school-based mental wellness programs and services, strengthen the role of guidance services and trained personnel in providing support, implement regular psychosocial activities for learners and staff, allocate time and resources for mental wellness activities and interventions, enhance teacher training on basic psychosocial support and identification of at-risk learners, promote safe, supportive, and inclusive school environment and strengthen parent and community involvement in mental health initiatives ', 'Develop a school inclusion plan aligned with SPED and accessibility standards, allocate budget and resources for accessibility improvements and assistive devices, strengthen training of teachers and staff on inclusive education and SPED support and procure and provide assistive learning materials and equipment for learners with special needs', 'Conduct inclusive stakeholder consultations (teachers, parents, community, use updated and reliable school data for planning, provide training/workshops on strategic planning for staff, allocate dedicated time for planning activities and align the plan with DepEd and division priorities.', 'Strengthen stakeholder engagement and participation, clearly define roles and responsibilities of members and provide orientation/training for planning team ', 'Strengthen leadership training for SSG/SPG officers, ensure regular meetings and active participation, provide continuous guidance from advisers, develop clear and student-centered action plans, increase student awareness and involvement in activities and monitor and evaluate implementation of student-led initiatives', 'Upgrade ICT equipment and improve internet connectivity,  train staff on digital tools and frontline service systems, establish online and on-site feedback mechanisms, reduce manual processes through digitization, and strengthen efficiency, responsiveness and customer-friendly services', 'Ensure alignment of all implementation activities with strategic goals, strengthen stakeholder engagement through regular consultations and collaboration, allocate and maximize resources efficiently; seek external support if needed and establish a clear monitoring and evaluation system with defined indicators\r\n\r\n', 'Conduct regular and well-planned SGC meetings, strengthen stakeholder participation and representation, clarify roles and responsibilities of all SGC members and provide orientation and capacity-building for SGC members', 'Strengthen parent engagement through regular meetings and consultations, improve communication using multiple channels (group chats, letters, and meetings), encourage active participation of parents in school programs and activities, conduct orientation and capacity-building for PTA officers and members and strengthen collaboration between PTA and school administration', 'Strengthen engagement with stakeholders through regular coordination meetings, expand linkages with LGUs, NGOs, and nearby schools, share best practices and conduct benchmarking with partner schools , establish clear roles, responsibilities, and expectations in partnerships, monitor and evaluate partnership activities and outcomes regularly and Sustain long-term collaboration through continuous engagement and feedback', 'Strengthen regular and systematic monitoring of all programs and activities, develop clear, measurable, and aligned indicators for evaluation and provide training for staff on M&E tools and processes', 'Sustain high performance through continuous improvement and self-assessment, strengthen regular coaching, mentoring, and feedback mechanisms, provide ongoing professional development and training opportunities, enhance goal-setting aligned with KRAs and school priorities, promote collaboration and sharing of best practices among personnel, encourage innovation and initiative in work performance and continuously monitor and evaluate individual performance results ', 'Sustain strong performance through continuous monitoring and evaluation of office outputs, strengthen alignment of office goals with school and DepEd priorities, maintain effective planning, coordination, and task delegation, continue regular coaching, mentoring, and feedback systems, promote teamwork, collaboration, and shared accountability among staff, ensure timely and quality submission of required outputs and reports and provide continuous professional development and capacity-building opportunities\r\n\r\n', 'Strengthen regular conduct of needs-based LAC sessions aligned with teacher needs, ensure consistent scheduling and full implementation of LAC activities, enhance quality of sessions through skilled facilitators and resource persons, monitor and evaluate the impact of LAC sessions on teaching practice and sustain a culture of continuous learning and professional growth among personnel', 'Support equal access to relevant trainings, seminars, and professional development opportunities, encourage and assist personnel in meeting qualification standards for promotion, improve documentation and updating of employees’ credentials and achievements , strengthen mentoring and coaching programs for career advancement', 'Establish clear, transparent, and fair criteria for recognition, explore alternative resources for incentives and implement a regular and well-planned recognition program', 'Ensure accurate and timely submission of payroll-related documents, strengthen coordination with division and finance offices and regularly update and verify employee records to avoid errors', 'Sustain transparent and data-driven assignment of teaching loads and tasks, continue regular review and adjustment of workload distribution as needed, maintain open communication for concerns related to workload fairness, strengthen collaborative planning among school leadership and teachers and consider teachers’ specialization, strengths, and welfare in assigning tasks', 'Aging or damaged school buildings and facilities and safety hazards in some classrooms or school areas, conduct regular and scheduled inspection of all school buildings and facilities, allocate available funds and seek external support for repairs, maintain complete documentation of inspection and monitor and evaluate infrastructure conditions for continuous improvement.', 'Prioritize infrastructure needs based on urgency and impact on learning, maximize available funds and seek support from LGU, PTA, NGOs, and partners and continuously assess school infrastructure needs for future improvements', 'Improve library space, furniture, and learning environment', 'Strengthen maintenance and regular monitoring of water, electric, and internet systems and install or improve backup systems (water storage tanks, and backup internet)', 'Establish classroom for computer laboratory', 'Sustain efficient and timely utilization of MOOE based on approved work and financial plans and strengthen planning and prioritization of school needs and expenditures', 'Sustain timely and complete liquidation of all MOOE expenditures and continuously improve efficiency in financial management processes', 'Strengthen regular feedback collection from internal and external stakeholders, develop clear indicators for monitoring stakeholder satisfaction, establish a systematic feedback and action-taking mechanism, conduct regular consultations and dialogue with stakeholders, implement continuous improvement based on feedback results, orient staff on customer-service mindset and standards and sustain efforts to maintain and improve stakeholder satisfaction ratings', 1, 110, 12, 57),
(835, '2026', '128647', 'High percentage of \"non-readers\" or \"frustration level\" readers in English and Filipino; learners struggle with basic multiplication and division; lack of localized reading materials; limited parental support in home-based follow-up.', 'Maintaining the high proficiency level amidst changing curriculum components; ensuring the consistency of 21st-century skill integration across all subject areas.', 'Absence of a dedicated ALS lead teacher or room; lack of updated mapping for out-of-school youth (OSY) in the immediate community (Barangay level).', 'Limited budget for high-volume printing of localized modules; need for more digital-based contextualized materials for ICT-integrated lessons.', 'Overlapping schedules of teachers making it difficult to sustain daily remediation; some learners miss sessions due to lack of transportation after regular hours.', 'Difficulty in finding explicit \"Peace Education\" entry points in technical subjects like Math or Science; need for more varied classroom posters and materials reflecting these values.', 'Time-consuming nature of manual item analysis for large classes; occasional delay in applying results to adjust next-day lesson plans.', 'No formal MOA (Memorandum of Agreement) with local businesses for EPP exposure; limited school garden (Gulayan sa Paaralan) tools or industrial arts equipment.', 'Occasional \"verbal teasing\" among younger pupils that requires constant monitoring; need for updated orientation for new parents on the Child Protection Policy (CPP).', 'Occasional \"verbal teasing\" among younger pupils that requires constant monitoring; need for updated orientation for new parents on the Child Protection Policy (CPP).', 'High incidence of \"Learners-at-Risk of Dropping Out\" (LARDOs) due to distance from school, seasonal farm work, or family financial instability.', 'Need for more instructional materials that specifically reflect local Annipot history or indigenous traditions; limited funds for cultural costumes/festivals.', 'Lack of a formal mapping system to identify out-of-school youth (OSY) in the immediate sitios; limited community awareness about alternative learning options.', 'Lack of a designated ALS teacher/facilitator and lack of a permanent space for adult learning sessions.', 'Need for refresher training for new committee members regarding updated DepEd Child Protection policies; ensuring consistent documentation of every meeting.', 'Need for more updated first-aid kits in every classroom; limited signage for \"Evacuation Routes\" that are weather-resistant.', 'Absence of a registered Guidance Counselor; limited teacher training on identifying early signs of mental health distress; lack of a dedicated \"Quiet Room\" or wellness space.', 'Lack of ramps for wheelchair access in older school buildings; comfort rooms not yet fitted with PWD handrails; absence of tactile or braille signage for visually impaired learners.', 'Aligning the 3-year SIP with rapidly changing post-pandemic learning needs; ensuring 100% of the teaching staff fully understands the Key Result Areas (KRAs) within the plan.', 'Difficulty in finding a common schedule for meetings that suits both working parents and LGU representatives; need for more orientation on their specific roles in SBM.', 'Limited budget for student-led projects; need for more leadership training for young student officers to handle responsibilities independently.', 'Limited digital infrastructure for paperless transactions; need for a more comfortable, dedicated waiting area for visiting parents and stakeholders.', 'Occasional delays in fund release affecting the timeline of specific projects; need for more frequent monitoring of target accomplishments.', 'Non-existence of a formal council structure; lack of orientation for potential members on the roles and responsibilities of the SGC.', 'Low attendance of some parents during general assemblies due to work conflicts; need to diversify PTA projects beyond infrastructure.', 'Limited benchmarking activities with neighboring schools due to logistical constraints; need for more formal MOUs with local NGOs.', 'Need for a more systematized digital tracking tool for real-time monitoring; ensuring that M&E results are consistently used to adjust the following year\'s budget.', 'Low retrieval rate of satisfaction surveys; perception of slow response times for certain administrative requests; lack of a formal \"Suggestion Box\" system.', 'Ensuring that the means of verification (MOVs) for performance reviews are organized and uploaded digitally on time; balancing administrative documentation with actual teaching time.', 'Ensuring that the means of verification (MOVs) for performance reviews are organized and uploaded digitally on time; balancing administrative documentation with actual teaching time', 'Limited budget for external experts or speakers for specialized topics; overlapping school activities that sometimes shorten the allotted time for SLAC sessions.', 'Limited slots for specialized regional or national training; need for a more structured tracking system for individual CPD (Continuing Professional Development) points.', 'Need for more diverse award categories (e.g., Most Creative Classroom, Most Punctual); limited budget for physical trophies or tokens of appreciation.', 'Occasional technical delays in the processing of step increments or loyalty pay at the division level; need for better orientation on tax updates or loan deductions.', 'Sudden vacancies or long-term leaves that occasionally force temporary teacher overloads; the need to better balance \"ancillary\" tasks (coordinatorship roles) with actual classroom teaching hours.', '', 'Limited school MOOE to cover major structural improvements; need for more sustained partnerships with external donors for \"Adopt-a-School\" projects.', 'Need for more updated reference books and digital e-resources to supplement printed materials; limited space to accommodate multiple classes simultaneously.', 'Unstable internet connectivity due to the school’s geographical location; insufficient water pressure during peak hours; high cost of monthly utility bills.', 'Lack of a dedicated room that meets the safety and cooling requirements for a computer lab; zero inventory of functional desktop or laptop units for pupil use.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Regular quarterly physical audits conducted by the School Facilities Coordinator and School Head; proactive reporting of minor damages by teachers.', '', '', '', '', 'Meticulous planning through the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP); monthly tracking of expenses by the school bookkeeper/accountant.', 'Strict adherence to COA (Commission on Audit) rules; transparent posting of the School Transparency Board (Transparency in Government); timely submission of liquidation reports to the Division Office.', 1, 1, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 6, 6, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 6, 6, 2, 6, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Launch an intensive \"Catch-Up Friday\" or remedial reading program; conduct a SLAC (School Learning Action Cell) for teachers on early numeracy strategies; strengthen the \"Brigada Pagbasa\" by involving community volunteers.', 'Continue the \"Project NAT-Brace\" (or your local review program); institutionalize an item analysis system to identify specific learning competencies that need reinforcement.', 'Coordinate with the District ALS Coordinator to conduct a community mapping and \"Child Find\" activity; propose the establishment of a dedicated ALS learning space if the number of OSY warrants it.', 'Conduct a school-level \"Write-shop\" to produce more localized Big Books; seek partnership with the LGU or Stakeholders for additional printing supplies.', 'Institutionalize a \"Buddy System\" (Peer-to-Peer tutoring); maximize the use of the 8:00 AM - 9:00 AM slot for intensive intervention programs; create a rewards system for consistent \"remediation attendees.\"', 'Conduct a SLAC on \"Values Integration Across the Curriculum\"; launch a \"Value of the Month\" campaign with school-wide recognition for exemplary student behavior.', 'Standardize the use of automated analysis tools for all quarterly exams; ensure that remediation plans are strictly based on the results of the LMCs identified.', 'Establish a partnership with the local Agricultural Office or a successful local farm for a \"Young Farmers\" mentorship; invite local artisans or bakers for a one-day \"Life Skills\" demonstration for Grade 6 pupils.', 'Conduct a \"Positive Discipline\" seminar for teachers and parents; strengthen the \"Barkada Against Bullying\" student group; maintain a strictly confidential reporting logbook.', 'Conduct a \"Positive Discipline\" seminar for teachers and parents; strengthen the \"Barkada Against Bullying\" student group; maintain a strictly confidential reporting logbook.', 'Intensify the \"Project SAGIP\" or Home Visitation program; implement a flexible learning option for students in crisis; coordinate with the Barangay for \"Libreng Sakay\" or transport assistance.', 'Collaborate with community elders to document local oral histories for classroom use; organize a \"Cultural Exchange Day\" where students showcase local traditions and crafts.', 'Conduct a \"Child Find\" and OSY mapping activity in coordination with Barangay officials; strengthen the referral system to the nearest functional ALS center.', 'Submit a request to the Division Office for the assignment of a mobile teacher or creation of an ALS plantilla; designate a specific corner of the school for future ALS learning resources.', 'Conduct a quarterly review of the school’s child protection protocols; create a digital \"Complaint Tracking System\" to ensure every issue is resolved and documented.', 'Conduct a \"Hazard Mapping\" activity with student leaders; procure additional emergency supplies through the MOOE or stakeholder donations; update the school\'s emergency contact directory.', 'Establish a \"Mental Health Awareness Month\" with localized activities; designate a \"Wellness Corner\" in the faculty or guidance office; conduct a SLAC on Psychological First Aid (PFA) for all teachers.', 'Include the construction of PWD ramps and accessible CRs in the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) for MOOE or SEF funding; conduct a \"School Accessibility Audit\" to prioritize which areas need immediate modification.', 'Conduct a mid-year SIP review to track progress of targets; simplify the SIP/AIP into a \"One-Page Infographic\" to be posted in the faculty room for better teacher awareness.', 'Institutionalize a \"Hybrid Meeting\" setup (virtual and face-to-face) to increase attendance; issue formal \"Certificates of Recognition\" to SPT members to boost morale and commitment.', 'Launch a \"Pupil-led School Improvement Project\" (e.g., a small waste management or garden project); organize a \"Leadership Camp\" for SPG officers and class presidents.', 'Create a \"QR Code\" system for feedback and satisfaction surveys; establish a \"One-Stop-Shop\" during enrollment to reduce waiting time; institutionalize a \"Citizen’s Charter\" prominently displayed at the school entrance.', 'Create a \"Project Dashboard\" in the principal\'s office to visualize the status of each project; ensure all project leads submit quarterly progress reports.', 'Initiate the formation of the SGC by inviting community leaders, alumni, and parents to an orientation; submit the council’s composition to the Division Office for approval.', 'Implement a \"Class-Based PTA\" meeting strategy to make discussions more personal; launch a \"Parent Volunteer Program\" for classroom-level assistance.', 'Propose a \"Sister-School\" benchmarking activity within the district to share best practices; reach out to local businesses for a \"Adopt-a-School\" partnership.', 'Capacity building for the M&E team on data interpretation; institutionalize the \"SMEPA Gallery Walk\" to present program accomplishments to all teachers.', 'Conduct a \"Portfolio Day\" to help teachers organize their IPCRF documents; institutionalize a peer-review system to provide constructive feedback before final ratings.', 'Conduct a \"Portfolio Day\" to help teachers organize their IPCRF documents; institutionalize a peer-review system to provide constructive feedback before final ratings.', 'Establish a \"Teacher-Expert Exchange\" where teachers with specific strengths (e.g., ICT, Reading) lead sessions; use digital platforms for flexible, self-paced learning modules.', 'Establish a \"Professional Growth Tracker\" for every teacher; conduct a school-level \"Career Guidance\" session to help teachers prepare their promotion folders.', 'Partner with local stakeholders or the PTA to sponsor rewards and incentives; hold an annual \"Gabi ng Parangal\" or Recognition Gala to honor outstanding staff performance.', 'Conduct a \"Financial Literacy\" SLAC to help teachers manage their salaries and understand their payslips; ensure the school clerk/personnel officer attends all division briefings on benefit updates.', 'Conduct a quarterly workload audit to ensure no teacher is disproportionately burdened; implement a \"Rotation System\" for ancillary duties to give all teachers a chance to lead and learn without burnout.', 'Institutionalize a monthly \"Facility Walkthrough\" with the PTA physical facilities committee; maintain a centralized \"Repair and Maintenance\" logbook for immediate action.', 'Draft and submit project proposals to the LGU or private stakeholders for the construction of additional handwashing stations or pathway roofing.', 'Launch a \"Donate-a-Book\" campaign among alumni and stakeholders; establish a \"Digital Reading Hub\" corner within the library with at least one functional computer.', 'Request the installation of a high-capacity water tank from the LGU; apply for a dedicated school internet line under the DepEd DCP program; implement a school-wide \"Energy Conservation\" policy.', 'Include the \"Computer Laboratory Construction\" in the school\'s Prioritized Project List (PPL); coordinate with the Division IT Officer for the possible allocation of a DCP (DepEd Computer Program) package.', 'Continue conducting monthly budget reviews to ensure zero-waste spending; prioritize the procurement of essential learning materials that directly impact student performance.', 'Maintain a \"Digital Archiving\" system for all financial documents to speed up the liquidation process; continue the \"Transparency Board\" updates to keep the community informed of school spending.', 'Launch a \"Stakeholder Feedback Day\" during PTA assemblies; establish a digital feedback link (via Google Forms or FB Messenger); conduct a \"Service Excellence\" workshop for frontline personnel to improve communication.', 0, 39, 12, 58),
