(842, '2026', '128541', 'Students struggling to catch up, impact on future learning, \r\nStudents needing extra support, varying learning paces, and \r\nDifficulty engaging students, assessing progress accurately', '•	Low proficiency levels in key subjects like Math, Science, and English\r\n•	Limited critical thinking and ', '', '', '', '', '', '', '•	Sustaining a culture of empathy and respect among students\r\n•	Ensuring new students are integrated into the positive school culture\r\n•	Addressing potential underreporting of incidents\r\n', '', '•	Identifying students at risk of dropping out early\r\n•	Addressing underlying reasons for remaining dropouts\r\n•	Sustaining student motivation and engagement\r\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '\r\n', '', '', '', '', '', 'SGC members lack training\r\n\r\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '•	No adequate water supply \r\n•	Limited backup systems for water supply\r\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '•	Regular workshops on contextualization and material development.\r\n•	Availability of diverse, relevant learning resources.\r\n•	Teachers collaborated with their best practices\r\n•	Have regular feedback from students on material \r\n•	Have encouragement and resources from school leadership\r\n', '•	Teachers are trained on identifying learning gaps and designing remediation strategies\r\n•	Have regular assessments to identify specific gaps.\r\n•	Teachers are provided with remediation materials and tools\r\n•	Parents have a strong support in reinforcing remediation at home\r\n', '•	Teachers are trained on integrating peace education and core values\r\n•	Alignment of peace and values topics with existing curriculum\r\n•	Teachers have access to relevant materials and activities\r\n•	School culture promotes peace and values\r\n•	Community support and involvement in value promotion\r\n', '•	Teachers skilled in test item analysis and interpretation\r\n•	Effective systems for collecting and analyzing test data\r\n•	Access to tools and expertise for advanced analysis\r\n', '', '', '•	Clear anti-child abuse policies and procedures\r\n•	Regular awareness programs for students and teachers \r\n•	Safe and confidential reporting mechanisms\r\n•	Counseling and support services for students\r\n•	Collaboration with parents and community on child safety\r\n', '', '•	Teachers understand and value diverse cultures\r\n•	Involvement of local communities in school activities\r\n•	Curriculum incorporates diverse cultural perspectives\r\n•	School promotes respect for all cultures\r\n•	Students encouraged to share their cultural experiences\r\n', '', '', '•	Committee members trained in child protection policies and protocols\r\n•	Established guidelines for reporting and addressing incidents\r\n', '•	Teachers are trained in Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (DRRM)\r\n•	Established protocols for disaster response and mitigation\r\n•	Regular conduct of disaster drills and simulations\r\n•	Regular risk assessments and updates to the DRRM plan\r\n', '•	Regular awareness programs on mental wellness\r\n•	School promotes a supportive and non-judgmental environment\r\n', '', '•	Teachers, students, parents, and community are involved in planning\r\n•	Have a clear vision and mission guide the strategic plan\r\n•	Plan is based on data and analysis of school\'s strengths and needs\r\n•	Plan includes specific, measurable, achievable goals\r\n•	Regular monitoring and evaluation of the plan\r\n', '•	Team includes representatives from school and community\r\n•	Clear roles and responsibilities for team members\r\n•	Team meets regularly to plan and review initiatives\r\n•	Team works collaboratively to address school needs\r\n•	Established channels for communicating with stakeholders\r\n', '•	Elected student leaders are active and engaged\r\n•	Clear roles and responsibilities for SSG/SPG officers\r\n•	Regular meetings with advisors and stakeholders\r\n•	Students are empowered to lead initiatives and projects\r\n•	Advisors provide guidance and support\r\n', '•	Regular feedback from stakeholders on services\r\n•	Teachers are trained in innovative approaches\r\n•	Regular review and improvement of frontline services\r\n•	Stakeholders are engaged in designing services\r\n', '•	Implementation plan breaks down strategic goals into actionable objectives\r\n•	Tasks and responsibilities are clearly assigned\r\n•	Specific timelines are set for each action\r\n•	Resources (budget, personnel) are allocated for implementation\r\n•	Regular monitoring and reporting on progress\r\n', '', '•	PTA has active members from parents and teachers\r\n•	PTA meets regularly to discuss school issues\r\n•	PTA has clear objectives aligned with school goals\r\n•	PTA facilitates communication between parents and school\r\n•	PTA supports school initiatives and activities\r\n', '•	School actively networks with stakeholders and other schools\r\n•	Collaboration is driven by clear goals and objectives\r\n•	Established channels for communication and coordination\r\n•	Partnerships are mutually beneficial for all parties\r\n•	Regular engagement with stakeholders and partners\r\n', '•	School has a system for regular monitoring\r\n•	Feedback is gathered from stakeholders\r\n•	Insights from monitoring lead to adjustments\r\n', '•	School gathers feedback from stakeholders regularly\r\n•	Actions are taken based on feedback received\r\n•	School communicates with stakeholders effectively\r\n•	School delivers quality services and programs\r\n•	School strives for continuous improvement\r\n', '•	Clear performance goals and expectations are set\r\n•	School provides necessary resources and support\r\n•	Regular feedback and coaching are given\r\n•	Achievements are recognized and rewarded\r\n•	Opportunities for growth and development are available\r\n', '•	Office goals are aligned with school objectives\r\n•	Staff are competent and motivated\r\n•	Regular monitoring and feedback on performance\r\n•	Leadership supports office operations\r\n', '•	LACs are based on identified needs of teachers\r\n•	Topics are relevant to teaching and learning\r\n•	Sessions are facilitated by experts or skilled teachers\r\n•	LACs promote sharing of best practices\r\n•	Actions are taken based on LAC outputs\r\n', '•	School provides relevant training and workshops\r\n•	Opportunities for career advancement are available\r\n•	Feedback is given to support growth\r\n', '•	School has programs to recognize achievements\r\n•	Recognition is given in a timely manner\r\n•	Recognition takes various forms (e.g., awards, certificates)\r\n•	Recognition is inclusive of all personnel\r\n', '•	Transparent compensation policies\r\n•	Prompt submission of required docs\r\n•	Regular updates on compensation\r\n', '•	Clear criteria for workload distribution\r\n•	Teachers are involved in decision-making\r\n•	Workloads are reviewed regularly\r\n•	Support is given to manage workload\r\n•	Tasks are distributed considering individual capacities\r\n', '•	Inspections are done on a regular schedule\r\n•	Feedback from stakeholders is considered\r\n•	Issues are addressed promptly\r\n', '•	Improvements are based on identified needs\r\n•	Stakeholders are involved in planning\r\n•	Funds are allocated for improvements\r\n•	Improvements are managed effectively\r\n•	Feedback is gathered on improvements\r\n', '', '', '', '•	Accurate budgeting for MOOE expense\r\n•	Prioritizing essential expenses\r\n•	Efficient procurement processes\r\n•	Regular monitoring of expenses\r\n•	Transparent financial reporting\r\n', '•	Accurate and timely reporting of expenses\r\n•	Complete documentation of expenses\r\n•	Streamlined liquidation processes\r\n•	Adherence to financial regulations\r\n•	Clear accountability for funds\r\n', 2, 2, 0, 1, 2, 2, 2, 0, 6, 6, 2, 6, 0, 0, 6, 1, 6, 2, 2, 6, 2, 6, 0, 2, 6, 6, 2, 6, 1, 2, 1, 1, 3, 3, 2, 5, 5, 0, 5, 0, 3, 3, 'Small groups for struggling students, Cater to varying learning paces,  and Make learning fun with activities, games',