(860, '2026', '128603', 'Inconsistent reading and numeracy levels\r\n• Limited ELLN instructional materials\r\n• Insufficient parental support', 'Limited integration of 21st century skills\r\n• Inadequate ICT resources\r\n• Low critical thinking and problem-solving skills', 'Insufficient learning materials and modules\r\n• Limited number of trained ALS facilitators\r\n• Low learner motivation and retention', '• Insufficient time for teachers to develop quality materials\r\n• Lack of available localized references and resources\r\n• Inadequate ICT tools and printing resources', '• Limited time for remediation due to packed class schedules\r\n• Insufficient instructional and remediation materials\r\n• Large class size affecting individualized instruction\r\n• Low learner motivation and inconsistent attendance', '• Lack of contextualized materials highlighting peace and core values\r\n• Inconsistent integration across subject areas', '• Lack of standardized tools/templates for item analysis\r\n• Insufficient time to analyze test results due to workload\r\n• Inconsistent practice across grade levels/learning areas\r\n• Limited use of results to improve instruction', '', '• Inconsistent monitoring and documentation of cases\r\n• Lack of structured reporting and response mechanisms\r\n• Limited parent involvement in addressing behavioral concerns', '• Presence of reported or suspected child abuse cases', '', 'Limited integration of cultural diversity in school activities\r\n• Lack of awareness and training on culture-sensitive approaches', '• Limited identification and profiling of out-of-school youth (OSYs) and adult learners\r\n• Lack of alternative delivery modes and flexible learning options', 'the school have a partnership with the ALS program', '', '', 'Limited awareness among teachers and parents, absence of trained personnel, lack of structured programs, minimal budget allocation', 'Lack of ramps and accessible toilets, absence of SPED-trained teachers, limited as