ive strategies\r\n• Implement enrichment activities', '• Strengthen attendance monitoring and flexible learning schedules\r\n• Provide adequate learning materials and resources\r\n• Conduct capacity-building for ALS facilitators\r\n• Implement motivation and retention strategies (incentives, recognition)', '• Provide time allocation for material development\r\n• Develop and share a repository of contextualized learning materials\r\n• Strengthen ICT support and provide needed resources\r\n• Encourage collaborative development and peer review of materials', 'Conduct regular diagnostic, formative, and summative assessments\r\n• Design structured remediation programs (reading, numeracy, science skills)\r\n• Allocate time for remediation (e.g., after class, pull-out sessions)\r\n• Provide adequate remediation materials and resources\r\n• Engage parents in supporting learners at home\r\n• Monitor and evaluate learners’ progress regularly', 'Develop and utilize contextualized instructional materials\r\n• Integrate values across all learning areas consistently\r\n• Strengthen monitoring through classroom observations and lesson plan review', '• Develop and provide standardized templates/tools for item analysis\r\n• Allocate time for collaborative data analysis during LAC sessions\r\n• Utilize results to revise test items and improve teaching strategies\r\n• Establish a school policy on regular conduct of item analysis', '', 'Strengthen awareness campaigns on anti-bullying and child protection policies\r\n• Establish clear, confidential, and accessible reporting mechanisms\r\n• Conduct regular orientations for learners, teachers, and parents\r\n• Enhance monitoring and documentation of incidents\r\n• Provide counseling and intervention programs for affected learners\r\n• Promote a positive, inclusive, and safe school environment', 'Strengthen implementation of Child Protection Policy and protocols\r\n• Conduct regular orientations for learners, parents, and teachers on child abuse prevention\r\n• Establish clear, confidential, and child-friendly reporting systems\r\n• Enhance coordination with DSWD, PNP, and LGU for proper referral and action\r\n• Provide counseling, support, and intervention programs for affected learners\r\n• Conduct continuous monitoring and documentation of cases', 'Sustain and strengthen DORP implementation\r\n• Conduct regular tracking of at-risk learners and provide timely interventions\r\n• Intensify home visitations and parent engagement activities\r\n• Provide support programs (feeding, school supplies, guidance services)\r\n• Strengthen partnerships with LGU and stakeholders for additional support\r\n• Recognize and motivate learners to stay in school', '• Integrate local culture, traditions, and languages in lessons and school activities\r\n• Strengthen partnerships with IP leaders and local cultural groups\r\n• Develop and utilize culturally relevant instructional materials\r\n• Organize regular cultural activities, events, and celebrations\r\n• Promote respect, inclusivity, and appreciation of diversity within the school', 'Conduct community mapping and profiling of OSYs and adult learners\r\n• Strengthen implementation of ALS and flexible learning delivery modes\r\n• Provide adequate learning materials and resources\r\n• Intensify advocacy and awareness campaigns in the community', 'Strengthen coordination with ALS focal person', '- Sustain regular meetings and monitoring\r\n- Provide refresher trainings on child protection policies\r\n- Strengthen coordination with barangay and local agencies', 'Sustain regular DRRM drills and simulations\r\n- Update emergency kits and first-aid supplies\r\n- Strengthen coordination with LGU and barangay DRRM units', '- Conduct orientation sessions on mental health awareness\r\n- Partner with local health units for counseling support\r\n- Integrate simple wellness activities (journaling, mindfulness, peer support) into school routines', 'Request LGU support for construc