(891, '2026', '304306', '', '', '', 'Limited time, insufficient localized resources, and varying teacher skills in material development hinder consistent preparation of contextualized learning materials responsive to learners’ needs in our school.', '', 'Limited instructional time, insufficient training on value integration, and lack of contextualized materials hinder consistent integration of peace education and DepEd core values in classroom teaching in our school.', '', '', '', '', '', 'Limited cultural resource materials, insufficient teacher training on cultural sensitivity, and occasional lack of integration in lesson activities may affect the consistent implementation of culture-sensitive activities in our school.', 'Limited flexible learning delivery options, insufficient tracking of out-of-school youth (OSY) and adult learners, and lack of adequate learning materials may hinder full access to learning opportunities for disadvantaged learners in our school', 'Limited learning materials, irregular attendance of ALS learners, and insufficient facilitators or training support may affect the effectiveness of the school-based ALS program in our school', '', 'Limited updated risk assessments, insufficient drills and simulations, and lack of adequate emergency resources may affect the full effectiveness of the school’s DRRM plan in our school.', 'Limited mental health personnel, low awareness among learners about available support, and occasional stigma in seeking help may hinder the effectiveness of the school’s mental wellness support mechanism in our school.', 'Limited accessibility features in some classrooms, insufficient assistive learning materials, and lack of fully trained personnel to support learners with special needs may affect the effectiveness of SPED and PWD-friendly facilities in our school', 'Limited stakeholder participation, insufficient data-driven inputs, and time constraints in planning hinder the full development and implementation of a comprehensive strategic plan in our school.', 'Limited active participation of stakeholders, irregular meetings, and unclear roles and responsibilities may affect the effectiveness of the school-community planning team in our school.', '', 'Limited ICT resources, inconsistent staff training on digital tools, and slow adoption of new processes hinder consistent innovation in frontline services for stakeholders in our school.', 'Limited alignment between activities and targets, insufficient monitoring of implementation, and delays in resource allocation may hinder the effective operationalization of the school’s strategic plan in our school.', 'Limited attendance of members, irregular consultation meetings, and unclear engagement of stakeholders in decision-making may affect the effectiveness of the School Governance Council in our school', '', 'Limited coordination schedules, lack of sustained partnership agreements, and weak communication channels with stakeholders and other schools may hinder effective collaboration and partnership strengthening in our school.', '', 'Inconsistent service delivery, limited stakeholder engagement in feedback mechanisms, and gaps in addressing identified concerns may affect the school’s ability to consistently maintain a satisfactory rating from internal and external stakeholders.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong instructional leadership, consistent use of differentiated and learner-centered strategies, regular NAT-aligned formative assessments, collaborative teacher planning, adequate learning resources, active parental support, and a positive school learning environment consistently enable our school’s Grade 6, 10, and 12 learners to achieve proficiency in 21st-century skills and core learning areas in the National Achievement Test.', '', '', 'Strong teacher collaboration, scheduled remediation time, available learning materials, and consistent monitoring of learner progress enable effective remediation to address learning gaps in reading comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics in our school.', '', 'Regular assessment practices, teacher collaboration in data analysis, and strong support for data-driven instruction enable effective test item analysis to inform teaching and learning in our school', '', 'Strong implementation of child protection policy, active classroom supervision, and consistent guidance and counseling programs support the maintenance of zero child bullying incidence in our school', 'Strong enforcement of child protection policies, active monitoring by teachers and staff, and effective guidance and reporting mechanisms support the maintenance of zero child abuse incidence in our school.', 'Strong learner support programs, close monitoring of attendance, and active intervention from teachers and parents contribute to the reduced drop-out incidence in our school.', '', '', '', 'Strong implementation of child protection policies, active involvement of trained committee members, and effective reporting and response mechanisms support the functional Child Protection Committee in our school.', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong student leadership support, active participation of learners, and effective guidance of advisers enable a functional Supreme Student Government/Supreme Pupil Government in our school', '', '', '', 'Active parent involvement, strong collaboration between teachers and parents, and regular PTA meetings support a functional Parent-Teacher Association in our school', '', 'Strong leadership support, regular data gathering practices, and active involvement of teachers in reporting and documentation enable effective monitoring and evaluation of programs, projects, and activities in our school.', '', 'Strong leadership supervision, clear performance targets, and continuous professional development opportunities enable school personnel to achieve a very satisfactory rating in their Individual Performance Commitment and Review in our school.', 'Strong leadership direction, effective teamwork among office personnel, and consistent monitoring of targets and accomplishments enable the school to achieve a very satisfactory rating in the Office Performance Commitment and Review in our school.', 'Strong instructional leadership, collaborative culture among teachers, and regular identification of learning gaps through classroom data enable effective needs-based LAC sessions and Learning & Development activities in our school.', 'Strong leadership support, access to professional development programs, and a culture of continuous learning among personnel facilitate the effective promotion and continuous professional development in our school.', 'Strong leadership appreciation practices, transparent criteria for recognition, and regular school programs that acknowledge employee achievements support the consistent recognition and rewarding of personnel milestone achievements in our school.', 'Strong coordination with finance offices, accurate payroll processing systems, and timely submission of personnel records enable the consistent and timely release of salaries, allowances, and other compensation in our school.', 'Clear workload distribution guidelines, transparent assignment of teaching loads, and strong coordination among school leadership and teachers ensure fair and equitable distribution of teacher workload in our school.', 'Regular maintenance schedules, active involvement of school property custodians, and strong coordination with stakeholders for facility upkeep support the consistent inspection of infrastructure and facilities in our school', 'Strong school leadership initiative, active stakeholder support, and regular identification of facility needs enable continuous improvement of infrastructure and facilities in our school.', 'Adequate library resources, active support from school leadership, and regular utilization by learners and teachers support the functional library in our school.', 'Reliable utility services, regular maintenance of facilities, and strong coordination with service providers ensure functional water, electricity, and internet facilities in our school.', 'Adequate computer units and ICT equipment, regular maintenance and upgrading of hardware and software, and active use of the laboratory in teaching and learning activities support the functional computer laboratory in our school.', 'Strong budget planning and monitoring, timely submission of procurement requirements, and efficient coordination among school committees support the high utilization rate of MOOE in our school.', 'Strict compliance with accounting and auditing guidelines, timely submission of liquidation reports, and strong coordination between school administration and finance personnel ensure 100% liquidation of MOOE in our school', 0, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 2, 3, 1, 1, 2, 3, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 3, 3, 3, 3, '', 'Implement a schoolwide NAT action plan that integrates 21st-century skills into daily lessons, uses regular NAT-aligned formative assessments, strengthens teacher collaboration through LAC, and provides targeted remediation and enrichment to sustain high proficiency in the National Achievement Test.', '', 'Establish a shared repository of contextualized materials, schedule dedicated LAC time for co-creation, and provide targeted training to strengthen teachers’ skills in developing learner-responsive resources.', 'Strengthen remediation programs through structured intervention plans, increased instructional support, and provision of updated, context-based learning materials to further improve learner performance in all subject areas.', 'Strengthening teacher capacity through targeted training, providing adequate instructional time, and developing localized materials can improve the consistent integration of peace education and DepEd core values in our school.', 'Strengthen regular LAC-based item analysis sessions, provide training on data interpretation, and establish a standardized feedback system to ensure assessment results are effectively used to improve instruction in our school', '', 'Sustain zero bullying incidence by strengthening continuous child protection policy orientation, enhancing teacher and learner awareness programs, and reinforcing regular monitoring and reporting through guidance services and class advisers.', 'Sustain zero child abuse incidence by regularly strengthening child protection policy orientation, intensifying teacher and staff vigilance through classroom and campus monitoring, and ensuring accessible, confidential reporting and response systems through the guidance office.', 'Strengthen drop-out prevention by intensifying home visitation for at-risk learners, improving early warning systems for absenteeism, and expanding learner support programs such as tutoring and counseling with active parent coordination.', 'Develop localized cultural learning materials, provide regular teacher training on cultural sensitivity and inclusive education, and ensure integration of culture-sensitive activities in lesson plans and school programs across all subjects.', 'Strengthen flexible learning programs (modular and blended), establish a systematic database and regular monitoring of OSY and adult learners, and provide appropriate contextualized learning materials with support from teachers and community partners.', 'Strengthen the ALS program by providing sufficient contextualized learning materials, improving learner tracking and follow-up for attendance, and conducting regular training and support for ALS facilitators in our school', 'Sustain the Child Protection Committee by conducting regular training and policy orientations, strengthening reporting and monitoring systems, and ensuring active coordination among committee members, teachers, and stakeholders in addressing child protection concerns.', 'Regularly update the school’s risk assessment, conduct scheduled earthquake and fire drills, and improve the availability of emergency kits and supplies through coordinated support from stakeholders and local DRRM offices.', 'Strengthen the school’s mental wellness program by conducting regular mental health awareness campaigns, training teachers as mental health first responders, and improving access to guidance services through clear referral and support systems', 'Improve SPED and PWD support by gradually upgrading school facilities for accessibility (ramps, handrails, signage), providing assistive learning materials through LGU/partner support, and conducting regular training for teachers on inclusive education and learner accommodation.', 'Strengthen participatory planning through regular stakeholder consultations, use data-driven decision-making in strategic planning, and allocate dedicated time for collaborative planning sessions to ensure a comprehensive and well-implemented strategic plan in our school.', 'Strengthen stakeholder engagement through scheduled quarterly meetings, clearly define roles and responsibilities via written guidelines, and encourage active participation by involving community members in priority-setting and decision-making activities.', 'Provide continuous leadership training for officers, strengthen adviser mentoring and monitoring, and encourage wider student participation through structured school activities and regular feedback mechanisms.', 'Allocate budget for ICT upgrading, conduct regular staff training on digital tools, and implement step-by-step process improvements to gradually strengthen innovation in frontline services in our school.', 'Strengthen alignment through clear cascading of goals per department, conduct regular quarterly monitoring and evaluation meetings, and ensure timely release and tracking of resources based on the implementation plan', 'Strengthen SGC effectiveness by setting a fixed meeting schedule, improving communication and attendance through official reminders, and clearly defining stakeholder roles to ensure active participation in school decision-making.', 'Strengthen PTA functionality by encouraging wider parent participation through flexible meeting schedules, improving communication channels (e.g., group chats and notices), and sustaining collaborative school–home programs.', 'Establish regular coordination meetings, formalize partnerships through MOUs or agreements, and strengthen communication via designated focal persons and digital platforms to sustain collaboration with stakeholders and partner schools', 'Strengthen monitoring and evaluation by standardizing tools for data collection, conducting regular review meetings per quarter, and providing capacity-building for teachers on accurate reporting and data analysis', 'Sustain high IPCR ratings by strengthening regular coaching and mentoring, aligning individual targets with school goals through periodic performance reviews, and enhancing professional development programs based on identified competency gaps.', 'Sustain and further improve OPCR performance by strengthening regular performance monitoring and feedback sessions, aligning office plans with school priorities through collaborative planning, and providing continuous capacity-building for office personnel to enhance efficiency and service delivery.', 'Sustain and improve needs-based LACs by strengthening data-driven planning from classroom assessments, scheduling regular and well-structured LAC sessions, and providing targeted professional development based on identified teacher and learner needs.', 'Strengthen continuous professional development by providing regular training aligned with career paths, supporting personnel in pursuing scholarships and certifications, and implementing a structured mentoring and performance-based promotion system.', 'Institutionalize a transparent and merit-based recognition system, regularly conduct formal recognition activities during school programs, and ensure systematic documentation and validation of personnel achievements for timely and fair awarding.', 'Strengthen payroll monitoring systems, ensure strict deadlines for submission of personnel documents, and maintain close coordination with accounting and finance offices to further improve the timely release of salaries, allowances, and benefits in our school.', 'Implement a standardized workload allocation system based on teacher specialization and class load limits, conduct regular consultations before assigning loads, and review workload distribution every grading period to ensure fairness and balance among teachers in our school.', 'Strengthen infrastructure inspection by implementing a regular preventive maintenance checklist, assigning clear responsibilities to facility custodians per area, and coordinating with LGU and stakeholders for timely repair and upgrading of school facilities.', 'Develop a prioritized school improvement plan based on facility assessments, strengthen partnerships with LGUs and stakeholders for funding and support, and implement phased infrastructure upgrades to address the most urgent needs in our school.', 'Strengthen the school library by continuously updating and expanding reading materials, improving the library space and accessibility, and promoting a reading culture through scheduled library periods and reading programs for learners', 'Strengthen utility reliability by establishing regular preventive maintenance schedules, coordinating closely with service providers for quick response to outages, and allocating funds for backup systems such as water storage, generators, and internet redundancy to ensure continuous services in the school.', 'Sustain and improve the computer laboratory by allocating budget for regular upgrading and repair of ICT equipment, conducting scheduled maintenance checks, and integrating ICT-based lessons across subjects to maximize utilization of the laboratory.', 'Strengthen MOOE utilization by improving annual procurement planning, ensuring strict adherence to timelines for request and liquidation, and enhancing monitoring and evaluation of expenditures through regular budget review meetings.', 'Strengthen MOOE liquidation by enforcing strict internal deadlines for documentation, providing regular training on updated accounting and auditing procedures, and implementing a monitoring checklist system to ensure complete and timely submission of liquidation reports', 'Strengthen service delivery through clear standards and staff coaching, improve stakeholder feedback systems with regular surveys and consultations, and ensure timely action on concerns through a documented response and monitoring system', 1, 11, 12, 61),
