(940, '2026', '129320', 'Grade 3 learners encounter gaps in foundational reading skills such as decoding, fluency, and comprehension, along with limited vocabulary development, which hinder their overall language proficiency. In numeracy, difficulties in mastering basic operations, number sense, and problem-solving are compounded by limited instructional resources, inconsistent learner support at home, and time constraints in reinforcing essential skills.', 'Learners in Grades 6, 10, and 12 face gaps in higher-order thinking, reading comprehension, and problem-solving skills, which affect their performance across core learning areas and 21st century competencies in the National Achievement Test (NAT). These challenges are compounded by curriculum misalignment, limited access to quality learning resources, inconsistent teaching strategies, and insufficient practice with test-based and real-world application tasks.', 'The school has no School-Based ALS offerings', 'Teachers face challenges in preparing contextualized learning materials due to limited time, insufficient training in localization and contextualization, and lack of access to relevant resources and references. These are further compounded by heavy workloads, inadequate technical support, and limited collaboration opportunities for sharing best practices and materials.', 'Teachers encounter challenges in conducting remediation activities due to limited time within the school schedule, large class sizes, and insufficient training in differentiated and targeted interventions across reading, comprehension, science, and mathematics. These are further hindered by a lack of appropriate remediation materials, inconsistent learner attendance, and limited support from parents or guardians.', '', 'The school faces challenges in conducting test item analysis due to limited teacher training in data analysis, lack of standardized tools or systems, and time constraints in reviewing assessment results. These issues are further compounded by insufficient technical support and inconsistent use of data to inform instructional decisions.', 'The school has no  TLE-TVL course offerings', 'Maintaining zero bullying incidence can be challenged by underreporting due to fear or stigma, limited awareness of reporting mechanisms, and inconsistent monitoring of learner behavior across school settings. Additionally, gaps in continuous values reinforcement, peer influence, and limited parent engagement may pose risks to sustaining a bullying-free environment.', 'Sustaining zero child abuse incidence can be challenged by underreporting due to fear or lack of awareness, unclear or inaccessible reporting mechanisms, and inconsistent monitoring across school and home environments. Additional gaps include limited training of personnel on child protection protocols, weak coordination with external agencies, and insufficient engagement of parents in safeguarding practices.', 'The school faces challenges in sustaining reduced drop-out incidence due to economic constraints of families, learner absenteeism, and competing responsibilities at home or work. Additional gaps include limited monitoring of at-risk learners, insufficient intervention programs, and inconsistent parent or community support.', 'The school encounters challenges in conducting culture-sensitive activities due to limited contextualized materials, insufficient teacher training on cultural responsiveness, and time constraints within the school calendar. These are further compounded by diverse learner backgrounds, limited community participation, and lack of sustained support for inclusive and culturally relevant programs.', 'The school has no OSYs, and adult learners', 'The school has a functional school-base ALS program', 'The school may face challenges in sustaining a fully functional Child Protection Committee due to irregular meetings, unclear roles and responsibilities, and limited training on updated child protection policies and procedures. Additional gaps include weak documentation and monitoring systems, inconsistent coordination with external agencies, and limited awareness among learners and parents about child protection mechanisms.', '', 'The school faces challenges in sustaining a functional mental wellness support system due to limited trained personnel, insufficient counseling resources, and stigma that discourages learners from seeking help. Additional gaps include weak referral systems, inconsistent program implementation, and limited engagement of parents and external mental health partners.', 'The school faces challenges in providing SPED- and PWD-friendly facilities due to limited funding, inadequate infrastructure, and lack of specialized equipment to support diverse learner needs. Additional gaps include insufficient training of personnel, absence of universal design features, and limited maintenance and monitoring of existing accessible facilities.', 'The school may encounter challenges in developing a strategic plan due to limited stakeholder participation, insufficient data for informed decision-making, and lack of technical expertise in planning processes. These are further compounded by time constraints, unclear priorities, and weak alignment with long-term goals and available resources.', '', 'The school may face challenges in maintaining a functional Supreme Student/Pupil Government due to limited leadership training, unclear roles and responsibilities, and inconsistent participation of student officers. Additional gaps include insufficient guidance from advisers, limited resources for activities, and weak coordination with school administration and stakeholders.', 'The school encounters challenges in innovating its frontline services due to limited resources, lack of technological tools, and insufficient training of personnel in customer service and digital systems. Additional gaps include resistance to change, weak feedback mechanisms, and limited stakeholder engagement in improving service delivery.', '', 'The school may face challenges in sustaining a functional School Governance Council (SGC) due to irregular meetings, unclear roles and responsibilities, and limited capacity of members in governance and decision-making. Additional gaps include weak stakeholder participation, insufficient communication, and lack of systematic monitoring and documentation of council actions.', '', 'The school encounters challenges in strengthening partnerships due to limited time for coordination, unclear collaboration frameworks, and inconsistent participation from stakeholders and partner schools. Additional gaps include weak communication channels, lack of formal agreements, and limited monitoring of partnership outcomes.', '', 'The school faces challenges in maintaining a satisfactory rating due to inconsistent service quality, limited feedback mechanisms, and gaps in addressing stakeholder concerns in a timely manner. Additional issues include resource constraints, communication gaps, and varying expectations among stakeholders, which affect overall satisfaction.', 'School personnel may face challenges in achieving a “very satisfactory” IPCR rating due to unclear or shifting performance indicators, heavy workload, and limited opportunities for professional development aligned with targets. These are compounded by inconsistent coaching and feedback, inadequate documentation of outputs, and varying levels of supervisory support and monitoring.', 'The school may encounter challenges in achieving a “very satisfactory” OPCR rating due to misalignment between targets and actual accomplishments, limited resources, and gaps in data collection and reporting systems. These are further compounded by weak coordination among personnel, inconsistent monitoring of outputs, and insufficient documentation of performance results.', 'The school encounters challenges in conducting needs-based Learning Action Cells (LAC) and Learning & Development (L&D) activities due to limited time, insufficient data to accurately identify priority needs, and lack of trained facilitators. These are further compounded by resource constraints, low participation or engagement, and weak monitoring and evaluation of the effectiveness of sessions.', 'The school faces challenges in facilitating promotion and continuous professional development due to limited training opportunities, budget constraints, and unclear career progression pathways. Additional gaps include heavy workload, limited access to relevant programs, and insufficient mentoring and support systems for personnel growth.', 'The school may encounter challenges in recognizing and rewarding milestone achievements due to limited budget for incentives, lack of clear and consistent criteria, and insufficient documentation of accomplishments. These are further compounded by irregular recognition programs, limited stakeholder involvement, and perceptions of inequity or bias in the selection process.', 'The school may encounter challenges in facilitating timely and accurate receipt of salaries and allowances due to delays in document processing, incomplete or incorrect submissions, and coordination gaps with payroll and higher offices. Additional issues include system inefficiencies, limited personnel handling payroll concerns, and delays in communication and verification processes. ', 'The school may face challenges in ensuring fair and equitable teacher workload distribution due to staffing shortages, uneven subject or class assignments, and unclear workload policies or criteria. These are further compounded by additional non-teaching tasks, limited coordination in scheduling, and varying teacher competencies and specializations.', '', '', 'The school may face challenges in maintaining a functional library due to outdated or insufficient reading materials, limited budget for acquisitions, and lack of a dedicated librarian or trained personnel. Additional gaps include low learner engagement, inadequate space or facilities, and limited integration of library resources into classroom instruction. ', 'The school may encounter challenges in maintaining functional water, electric, and internet facilities due to unstable supply, frequent service interruptions, and limited budget for maintenance and upgrades. Additional gaps include outdated infrastructure, delayed repairs, and limited technical support to address connectivity and utility issues promptly.', 'The school may encounter challenges in maintaining a functional computer laboratory/classroom due to outdated or insufficient equipment, limited budget for upgrades and maintenance, and unreliable internet connectivity. Additional gaps include lack of technical support, insufficient teacher training in ICT integration, and inconsistent utilization of the facility for learning. ', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong administrative support, availability of DepEd-guided values integration frameworks, and teachers’ commitment to holistic education facilitate the consistent integration of peace and core values in daily lessons. Positive school culture, active learner participation, and reinforcement from parents and the community further strengthen the sustained practice of these values.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong leadership support, regular training and drills, and clear policies enable the consistent implementation of a functional Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (DRRM) plan. Active participation of stakeholders, availability of resources, and effective coordination with local agencies further ensure preparedness and responsiveness.', '', '', '', 'Strong leadership support, clearly defined roles, and regular communication enable the consistent functioning of the school-community planning team. Active stakeholder participation, shared accountability, and established monitoring and feedback mechanisms further sustain effective collaboration and decision-making.', '', '', 'Clear alignment between goals and activities, strong leadership support, and well-defined roles enable the effective operationalization of the school’s strategic plan through an implementation plan. Regular monitoring, adequate resource allocation, and active collaboration among stakeholders further ensure consistent and successful implementation.', '', 'Strong leadership and active participation from parents and teachers, along with clear roles and regular communication, enable the PTA to function effectively. Consistent support from the school, transparent processes, and shared commitment to learner welfare further sustain its active involvement.', '', 'Strong leadership support, clear monitoring and evaluation systems, and availability of reliable data enable the school to consistently assess its programs, projects, and activities. Active participation of stakeholders, regular review processes, and a culture of accountability further ensure continuous improvement and effective implementation.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong leadership support, clear inspection schedules, and availability of standard checklists enable the school to consistently inspect its infrastructure and facilities. Active involvement of personnel, proper documentation, and coordination with maintenance teams further ensure timely identification and resolution of issues.', 'Strong leadership initiative, availability of funds, and clear improvement plans enable the school to consistently initiate infrastructure and facility enhancements. Active stakeholder support, effective coordination, and regular monitoring further ensure timely implementation and continuous improvement. ', '', '', '', 'Effective financial management systems, clear budgeting plans aligned with school priorities, and strong leadership oversight enable the school to consistently achieve a 72–100% utilization rate of its MOOE. Timely procurement processes, proper documentation, and active monitoring further ensure efficient and transparent use of funds.', 'Strong financial management practices, accurate record-keeping, and adherence to established accounting and auditing procedures enable the school to consistently liquidate 100% of its utilized MOOE. Timely submission of documents, clear guidelines, and effective coordination among responsible personnel further ensure full compliance and accountability. ', 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 6, 1, 2, 6, 6, 3, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 6, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Strengthen instructional quality through targeted teacher training, use of structured remediation programs, and regular formative assessments to address gaps in early language, literacy, and numeracy skills. Complement this with increased provision of learning resources, improved classroom conditions, and active engagement of parents and community stakeholders to support inclusive and consistent learning for all Grade 3 learners.', 'Improve teaching quality and alignment by providing targeted professional development, strengthening curriculum-to-assessment coherence, and integrating 21st century skills through consistent, data-driven instructional practices. Support this with structured remediation programs, increased access to learning resources, and active engagement of parents and communities to reinforce learner achievement and readiness for the National Achievement Test (NAT).', 'Strengthen the ALS program through improved instruction, flexible learning support, and sustained collaboration with stakeholders to ensure learners are fully prepared and successfully attain elementary and junior high school certification.\r\n', 'Provide targeted training, dedicated planning time, and access to quality resources and collaborative platforms to support teachers in developing effective, contextualized learning materials that meet learners’ needs.', 'Implement structured remediation programs supported by targeted teacher training, dedicated intervention time, appropriate learning materials, and strengthened coordination with parents to ensure consistent learner participation and progress.', 'Sustain and strengthen values integration by providing continuous teacher support, enriching contextualized materials, and reinforcing partnerships with parents and the community to consistently promote peace and DepEd core values.', 'Provide targeted training, standardized tools, and dedicated time for teachers to conduct test item analysis and consistently use the results to improve instruction.', 'Conduct a needs assessment and strengthen partnerships with industry and local stakeholders to establish relevant TLE-TVL course offerings, supported by teacher training, appropriate facilities, and necessary learning resources.', 'Strengthen a whole-school anti-bullying system by ensuring confidential reporting mechanisms, consistent monitoring, continuous values education, and active engagement of parents and students to sustain a safe, bullying-free environment.', 'Strengthen child protection systems by ensuring clear and confidential reporting mechanisms, continuous staff training, consistent monitoring, and active coordination with parents and relevant agencies to sustain a safe, abuse-free school environment.', 'Strengthen early identification and support systems for at-risk learners through regular monitoring, targeted intervention programs, and close collaboration with parents and community stakeholders to sustain reduced drop-out rates.', 'Strengthen culture-sensitive programming by providing teacher training, developing contextualized materials, and actively engaging community partners to ensure inclusive, relevant, and sustainable activities.', 'Strengthen community mapping, early identification, and inclusive outreach programs in partnership with local stakeholders to ensure all out-of-school youth and adult learners are engaged and provided access to appropriate learning opportunities.', 'Sustain and enhance the functional school-based ALS program by providing continuous training for facilitators, adequate learning resources, and strong partnerships with the community to ensure effective and inclusive delivery.', 'Strengthen the Child Protection Committee by ensuring regular meetings, clear roles, continuous training, effective documentation, and active coordination with parents and external agencies to maintain a responsive and well-functioning system.', 'Sustain and continuously improve the DRRM plan through regular drills, capacity-building, resource allocation, and strong coordination with stakeholders to ensure ongoing preparedness and effectiveness.', 'Strengthen the school’s mental wellness support system by training staff, expanding counseling resources, establishing clear referral pathways, and actively engaging parents and external partners to ensure accessible and stigma-free services.', 'Upgrade facilities using universal design standards, allocate dedicated funding for assistive equipment, train staff on inclusive practices, and establish regular maintenance and monitoring to ensure accessibility for all learners.', 'Strengthen strategic planning by ensuring inclusive stakeholder participation, using reliable data, building planning capacity, and aligning priorities with clear goals and available resources.', 'Sustain and strengthen the school-community planning team through regular engagement, clear role definition, continuous capacity-building, and effective communication and monitoring systems.', 'Strengthen the Supreme Student/Pupil Government by providing leadership training, clarifying roles, ensuring consistent adviser support, and improving coordination and resource allocation for student-led activities.', 'Enhance frontline service innovation by investing in digital tools, building staff capacity, strengthening feedback systems, and actively involving stakeholders in continuous improvement.', 'Sustain effective implementation by strengthening alignment, clarifying roles, ensuring adequate resources, and maintaining regular monitoring and stakeholder collaboration.\r\n', 'Strengthen the School Governance Council by ensuring regular meetings, clarifying roles, building members’ capacity, and improving stakeholder engagement, communication, and documentation systems.', 'The school commits to sustaining a strong and functional PTA through continuous engagement, transparent communication, and collaborative efforts that support learner development and school improvement.', 'he school commits to strengthening partnerships by establishing clear collaboration frameworks, improving communication, ensuring regular stakeholder engagement, and monitoring outcomes for continuous improvement.', 'The school commits to sustaining effective monitoring and evaluation by ensuring regular data-driven reviews, active stakeholder participation, and continuous improvement of its programs, projects, and activities.', 'propose 1 sentence resolution', 'Align targets with achievable outputs, strengthen data collection and documentation systems, and ensure regular monitoring and coordination to improve OPCR performance.', 'Strengthen needs-based LAC and L&D by using data-driven planning, providing facilitator training, allocating dedicated time and resources, and implementing regular monitoring and evaluation to ensure effectiveness.', 'Strengthen needs-based LAC and L&D by using data-driven planning, providing facilitator training, allocating dedicated time and resources, and implementing regular monitoring and evaluation to ensure effectiveness.', 'The school commits to establishing a fair, transparent, and consistent recognition system supported by clear criteria, proper documentation, and regular acknowledgment of personnel achievements.', 'Streamline payroll processes by ensuring timely and accurate document submission, strengthening coordination with payroll offices, and improving monitoring and communication systems to prevent delays.', 'Establish clear workload guidelines, optimize scheduling based on teacher expertise, and regularly review assignments to ensure equitable distribution and minimize non-teaching burdens.', 'The school commits to sustaining regular and systematic inspection of its infrastructure and facilities through clear schedules, proper documentation, and prompt coordination for maintenance and improvements.', 'The school commits to continuously improving its infrastructure and facilities through strategic planning, efficient use of resources, and active collaboration with stakeholders to ensure a safe and conducive learning environment.', 'The school commits to strengthening its library by updating resources, assigning trained personnel, promoting learner engagement, and integrating library use into teaching and learning processes. ', 'The school commits to ensuring reliable water, electricity, and internet services through regular maintenance, timely repairs, infrastructure upgrades, and strong coordination with service providers.', 'The school commits to upgrading and maintaining its computer laboratory through regular equipment updates, reliable connectivity, technical support, and continuous teacher training to maximize its use for learning. ', 'The school commits to sustaining efficient and transparent MOOE utilization through sound financial planning, timely implementation, and continuous monitoring aligned with school priorities. ', 'The school commits to maintaining full and timely liquidation of MOOE through accurate documentation, strict adherence to accounting procedures, and continuous coordination among responsible personnel.', 'Strengthen stakeholder satisfaction by improving service consistency, establishing responsive feedback systems, enhancing communication, and ensuring timely action on concerns.', 1, 11, 12, 61),
