advocacy programs.', 'Regular conduct of quarterly nationwide simultaneous earthquake drills (NSED); partnership with local health offices for mental health webinars; presence of a functional clinic.', 'Regular conduct of quarterly nationwide simultaneous earthquake drills (NSED); partnership with local health offices for mental health webinars; presence of a functional clinic.', '', 'Strong leadership commitment; active participation of the School Planning Team; data-driven decision-making processes.', 'Established rapport with the Barangay Council and PTA; transparent communication channels; clear definition of roles and responsibilities.', 'Supportive faculty advisers; high student interest in school governance; democratic election processes are strictly followed.', 'Adaptation of \"Ease of Doing Business\" protocols; use of social media and QR codes for faster information dissemination.', 'Use of an Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) aligned with the budget; regular monthly tracking of project milestones.', 'Clear institutionalization of SGC bylaws; active leadership from the School Head in convening the council.', 'Transparency in financial reporting; strong involvement of parents in Brigada Eskwela and school safety programs.', 'Open-door policy for donors; active networking with local businesses and NGOs.', 'Established Quality Assurance and M&E (QAME) team; use of standardized feedback forms for every school event.', 'Consistent \"Client Feedback Mechanism\" at the front desk; responsiveness of the administration to complaints.', 'Regular coaching and mentoring by the School Head; clear alignment of individual targets with school goals.', 'Strong teamwork among department heads; efficient data management and tracking of Key Result Areas (KRAs).', 'Results of the Training Needs Analysis (TNA); availability of competent local resource speakers within the staff.', 'Encouragement for teachers to pursue graduate studies; transparent dissemination of vacancy announcements and promotion criteria.', 'Active PRAISE (Rewards and Recognition) committee; strong support from the PTA for non-monetary incentives and tokens.', 'Efficient School Liaison Officer; well-maintained personnel files and service records.', 'Use of the Magna Carta for Public School Teachers as a guide for teaching loads; transparent deliberation during the assignment of tasks', 'Conduct of regular \"Brigada Eskwela\" inspections; presence of a dedicated School Facilities Coordinator.', 'Strong partnership with the LGU and Alumni Association; inclusion of facility improvement in the SIP.', '', '', '', 'Systematic Cash Program and Monthly Disbursement Plan; transparent procurement through the BAC (Bids and Awards Committee)', 'Strict adherence to COA (Commission on Audit) rules; efficient record-keeping by the School Bookkeeper/Disbursing Officer.', 1, 1, 6, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 6, 2, 6, 6, 2, 2, 6, 2, 5, 5, 2, 6, 2, 1, 2, 2, 6, 6, 1, 5, 2, 2, 1, 2, 6, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 1, 3, 3, 'Provide more learning resources; targeted remediation', 'Conduct assessment; gather and analyze data', 'Strengthen ALS promotion and monitoring', 'Share resources; schedule planning time', 'Adjust schedules; continuous intervention programs', 'Conduct INSET/training; develop and share lesson exemplars', 'Provide training on item analysis; use templates/tools; regular data review meetings', 'Establish partnerships/MOAs; conduct outreach and coordination meetings; strengthen work immersion programs', 'Maintain a 100% reporting rate and conduct quarterly orientation for students and parents on child rights.', 'Maintain a 100% reporting rate and conduct quarterly orientation for students and parents on child rights.', 'Strengthen the \"Adopt-a-Student\" program and provide flexible learning options for students with family financial difficulties.', 'Organize an annual \"Cultural Day\" showcase', 'Coordinate with the District Office to assign a mobile teacher; utilize community centers for ALS sessions.', 'Coordinate with the District Office to assign a mobile teacher; utilize community centers for ALS sessions.', 'Maintain a 100% reporting rate and conduct quarterly orientation for students and parents on child rights.', 'Upgrade first-aid kits in every classroom; establish a \"Peer Facilitator\" group to support student mental wellness.', 'Upgrade first-aid kits in every classroom; establish a \"Peer Facilitator\" group to support student mental wellness.', 'Include the construction of PWD ramps and accessible toilets in the next School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).', 'Regular quarterly reviews of the SIP to ensure it remains responsive; Conduct capacity-building workshops on strategic foresight for the planning team.', 'Implement flexible meeting schedules (virtual or hybrid); provide formal recognition/awards for active community partners to boost engagement.', 'Allocate a specific \"Student Initiative Fund\"; partner with local youth organizations for leadership mentoring programs.', 'Upgrade ICT infrastructure; develop a simplified \"One-Stop-Shop\" physical booth and a more robust offline-ready digital filing system.', 'Strictly follow the school calendar while maintaining a \"catch-up\" plan for displaced activities.', 'Issue meeting notices at least two weeks in advance; utilize digital platforms for policy voting and feedback.', 'Focus on \"sweat equity\" (labor/participation) rather than just financial help; hold regular general assemblies to present liquidation reports.', 'Create a standardized partnership handbook to streamline the legalities of collaborations; host a \"Stakeholders’ Appreciation Day.\"', 'Transition to digital M&E tools (Google Forms/Dashboards) for real-time data collection and automated report generation.', 'Conduct \"Portfolio Preparation Days\" to assist teachers in organizing their electronic portfolios and MOVs early.', 'Institutionalize a mid-year performance review to recalibrate targets and ensure the school remains on track for \"Outstanding\" ratings', 'Streamline LAC sessions to focus on high-impact classroom strategies; utilize micro-learning or \"bite-sized\" professional development modules.', 'Provide technical assistance for teachers applying for ERF (Equivalent Record Form) or reclassification to Master Teacher positions.', 'Strengthen the \"Employee of the Month\" program; issue formal commendations (Certificates of Recognition) that can be used for promotion points.', 'Create a digital tracking system for personnel benefits to remind the administration when a teacher is due for a step increment or bonus.', 'Regular review of the School Form 7 (SF7); ensure that teachers with heavy administrative ancillary tasks are given proportional reductions in teaching minutes.', 'Collaborate with the Municipal/City Engineer’s office for a professional annual structural audit.', 'Create a priority list of repairs and actively pitch these projects to private stakeholders and \"Adopt-a-School\" partners.', 'Establish a \"Reading Corner\" in every classroom as an interim library; request book donations from partner NGOs.', 'Propose the installation of a water tank (cistern) and a signal booster or Starlink/satellite internet for more reliable connectivity.', 'Implement a \"shifting schedule\" for computer use; seek partnerships for \"refurbished laptop\" donations.', 'Regular monthly meetings with the School Finance Team to monitor spending against the Annual Implementation Plan.', 'Orient regular suppliers on the required documentation; maintain a \"Liquidation Folder\" to organize receipts immediately upon purchase.', 'Conduct deeper \"Root Cause Analysis\" on dissatisfied ratings; improve school aesthetic and waiting areas to enhance visitor experience.', 1, 69, 12, 107);
INSERT INTO `sbm_ta` (`id`, `fy`, `school_id`, `q1`, `q2`, `q3`, `q4`, `q5`, `q6`, `q7`, `q8`, `q9`, `q10`, `q11`, `q12`, `q13`, `q14`, `q15`, `q16`, `q17`, `q18`, `q19`, `q20`, `q21`, `q22`, `q23`, `q24`, `q25`, `q26`, `q27`, `q28`, `q29`, `q30`, `q31`, `q32`, `q33`, `q34`, `q35`, `q36`, `q37`, `q38`, `q39`, `q40`, `q41`, `q42`, `qq1`, `qq2`, `qq3`, `qq4`, `qq5`, `qq6`, `qq7`, `qq8`, `qq9`, `qq10`, `qq11`, `qq12`, `qq13`, `qq14`, `qq15`, `qq16`, `qq17`, `qq18`, `qq19`, `qq20`, `qq21`, `qq22`, `qq23`, `qq24`, `qq25`, `qq26`, `qq27`, `qq28`, `qq29`, `qq30`, `qq31`, `qq32`, `qq33`, `qq34`, `qq35`, `qq36`, `qq37`, `qq38`, `qq39`, `qq40`, `qq41`, `qq42`, `a1`, `a2`, `a3`, `a4`, `a5`, `a6`, `a7`, `a8`, `a9`, `a10`, `a11`, `a12`, `a13`, `a14`, `a15`, `a16`, `a17`, `a18`, `a19`, `a20`, `a21`, `a22`, `a23`, `a24`, `a25`, `a26`, `a27`, `a28`, `a29`, `a30`, `a31`, `a32`, `a33`, `a34`, `a35`, `a36`, `a37`, `a38`, `a39`, `a40`, `a41`, `a42`, `f1`, `f2`, `f3`, `f4`, `f5`, `f6`, `f7`, `f8`, `f9`, `f10`, `f11`, `f12`, `f13`, `f14`, `f15`, `f16`, `f17`, `f18`, `f19`, `f20`, `f21`, `f22`, `f23`, `f24`, `f25`, `f26`, `f27`, `f29`, `f30`, `f31`, `f32`, `f33`, `f34`, `f35`, `f36`, `f37`, `f38`, `f39`, `f40`, `f41`, `f42`, `f28`, `stat`, `district`, `region`, `division`) VALUES
(955, '2026', '1296mapu', '', '', 'No enrolment rate in the ALS program', '', '', '', 'Some of the teachers lack of advanced knowledge and skills  in conducting proper statistical item analysis', 'Limited knowledge and skills  of teachers on how to establish and manage partnerships with industries', '', '', 'Drop-out rate is reduced but not fully eliminated, some learners  still leave school due to poverty, family problem,  or transfer of residence', 'Activities are conducted but are limited to special events or occasions  and not fully integrated into daily lessons and school routines', 'Low awareness among target beneficiaries (disadvantaged learners, out-of-school youth and adult) about available learning opportunities', 'No enrollment and participation in ALS Program', '', '', '', 'Not all school facilities are fully accessible (insufficient ramps, lack of tactile guide, limited accessible restrooms)', 'Updates to plan are done annually but not always aligned with emerging education policies or changing school community needs', 'Team members are identified but some lack clear understanding of their roles, responsiblities, and the scope  of their work', '', 'Innovative services are introduced but limited in scope and coverage (not applied to all service areas or stakeholder groups)', 'Implementation plans are developed but some lack detailed brrakdown of activities, timelines, responsible persons, and specific deliverables', 'SGC  is organized but some members have limited knowledge and understanding of their roles, functions, and legal mandates', '', 'Collaboration is mostly limited to  local stakeholders and nearby schools.', '', 'Feedback collection is inconsistent, not all stakeholders are reached', '', '', '', '', 'Criteria for recognition are somtimes vague, subjective , or not clearly communicated to stakeholders', '', '', '', '', 'No available space or room for functional library facility', '', 'No available space or room allocated for a computer laboratory/calssroom', '', '', 'Teachers use localized, indigenized and contextualized  teaching materials', 'Teachers are trained on integrating 21st  century skills in lessonf', '', 'School encourages and supports teachers in material development', 'School has established guidelines for the implementationof remediation program', 'Deped policies mandate the integration of values and peace education', '', '', 'Strict implementation of D.O No. 40, s. 2012 (Child Protection Policy)', 'Strict adherence to National Child Protection  laws and DepEd policies', '', '', '', '', 'Strict compliance with D.O No. 42, s. 2012 (Child Protection Policy)', 'The DRRM plan is aligned with DepEd and National Disaster management guidelines', 'School adheres to DepEd Mental health Policy  and guidelines', '', '', '', 'Compliant with DepEd Order No. 47, s. 2014 on the organization and operatrions of Supreme Pupil Government', '', '', '', 'Organized and operated in accordance with DepEd policies  and guidelines', '', 'The school has established moniotoring and evaluation systems aligned with DepEd standards and policies', '', 'Strict compliance with DEpEd Result-based Performance Management System(RPMS) guidelines', 'Adherence to DepEd standards and guidelines for office operations and performance management', 'Compliance with DepEd Order No. 35, s. 2016 which  LAC  as a key professional development  strategy', 'Strict adherence to Civil Service Commission(CSC) and DepEd policies, rules, and regulations on promotion and professional development', '', 'Srtict compliance with government financial rules, regulations, and DepEd policies', 'Compliance with  DepEd  guidelines and policies on teachers workload and assignment ', 'Designated personnel or committee responsible for facility inspection and maintenance', 'School Adminstration prioritizes facility improvement to create a safe and conducive learning environment', '', 'Basic water , electric and internet facilities are already established and operational', '', 'Strict compliance with DepEd guidelines, financial policies and accounting standards', 'compliance with government financial rules, regulations and accountig standards', 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 1, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 2, 3, 3, 'Suatain the implementation of intervention and remedial programs', 'Streamline lesson guides to ensure full coverage of required competenceis', 'Conduct intensive information campaign and orientation in barangays  and communities to enrol in the ALS program', 'Create a fromal validation and evaluation process for all developed learning materials', 'Adjust class schedules and teaching loads to ensure sufficient time for remediation activities', 'Develop lesson exemplar and activity guides specifically for integrating peace and  core values ', 'Develop and provide standardized template', 'Conduct a mapping and profiling of local inductries or business relevant to the School\'s TLE-TVL specializations', 'Sustain regular anti-bullying education and awareness activities', 'Expand information d community campaigns to iclude prnotection from abuse in home and community settings', 'Strengthen the system for identifying and monitoring at-risk learners at the start of every school year', 'Develop a comprehensive plan to integrate  culture-sensitive practices across all learning areas', 'Conduct information  campaigns and community dialogues to increase awareness and encourage enrollment of target beneficiaries', 'Conduct aggressive information and advocacy  campaigns in the community to promote  the ALS  program and increase enrollment ', 'Conduct quarterly traioning and reonrientation  for committee members on updated child protection guidelines and case management', 'Schedule regular emergency drills(earthquake) at least once in every quarter to ensure prerparedness', 'Conduct regular training for teachers and staff on basic mental health care ', 'Conduct a full assessment of all facilities to identify gaps in accessiblity and develop a prioritized improvement plan', 'Update the strategic plan regularly to align with new national/regional education policies and emerging school needs', 'Conduct orientation and capacity-building sessions for team members to clarify roles, responsibilities, and planning procedures', 'Conduct regular leadership training, seminars, and workshops for learners officers to build their capacity in planning, mangement, and decision making', 'Expand the scope of innovation to cover all key frontline services', 'Develop detailed activity matrix specifying timelines, assigned personnel, required resources, and expected outputs for all programs /projects', 'Conduct orientation and capacity-building sessions for SGC members to clarify roles', 'Establish multiple communication platforms( group chat, notice board, home visit) to ensure all parents are informed and involved', 'Expand partnership networks to include government agencies, NGOs, private sector organizations', 'Develop customized monitoring and evaluation tools for each program/project to ensure relevant and accurate data collection', 'Ensure that individual performance target are directly linked to the goals and activities in the school', 'Develop specific, measurable, achievable , relevant, and time-bound (SMART) performance targets for each office/unit', 'Conduct a comprehensive Training Needs Assessment (TNA) at the start of the school year to identify priority learning needs of personnel', 'Conduct regular orientation and informastion sessions to update personnel on promotion requirements, policies , and procedures', 'Develop clear objective, inclusive  and well-disseminated criteria  for recognizing exemplary performance and contributions', 'Simplify and standardize  requirements and procedures for claiming allowances and compensation  and disseminate these clearly to all personnel', 'Develop clear workload guidelines and standards aligned with DepEd policies considering teraching specialization and additional responsibilities hours, class size, subject', 'Create specific inspection checklist for different facility types aligned with safety standards and usage requirements', 'Prioritize facility improvement projects based on urgency, safety risks, and impact  on teaching and learning', 'Make a project proposal and plan for the establishment of functional school library', 'Coordinate with local  water and electric utility  providers to address supply interruptions and improve service reliability', 'Develop a detailed project proposal  and plan for the establishment of a functional computer laboratory /classroom', 'Conduct comprehensive financial planning and budgeting at the start of the school year, ensuring that allocation are realistic and aligned with actual needs', 'Ensure timely preparation and submission of complete, accurate and properly supported liquidation documents', 'Develop and implement a standardized system from regular collection and documentation of stakeholder feedback', 1, 69, 12, 107),
