(1040, '2026', '129670', 'A small percentage of learners still struggle with advanced reading comprehension.', 'Learners experience difficulty with higher-order thinking skills (HOTS) questions in Science and Mathematics.', '', 'Intellectual Property & Plagiarism', 'Limited time allocation for remediation due to heavy teaching loads', '', 'Time constraints as the process requires careful review and data organization', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Overloaded schedule of the guidance teacher, limiting one-on-one sessions.', 'Existing ramps in older buildings do not meet the standard slope requirements.', 'Lack of technical expertise among staff in strategic planning frameworks.', 'Irregular attendance of community members due to personal work schedules.', 'Student leaders struggle to balance academic workloads with leadership responsibilities.', 'Difficulty in aligning school curriculum with the needs and practices of local industries', 'Poor alignment between the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and the actual Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) activities.', 'Lack of regular meetings and unclear roles among newly appointed SGC members.', '', '', '', '', 'Some personnel struggle with providing diverse \"Means of Verification\" (MOVs) for specific objectives.', '(Very Satisfactory)	Challenges in meeting 100% of the timeline targets for infrastructure projects due to weather or funding delays.', 'Difficulty in scheduling LAC sessions that do not conflict with regular teaching hours.', '', 'Limited school funds to provide substantial or physical rewards for top performers.', '', '', 'Potential hazards from aging electrical wiring in older buildings or seasonal soil erosion near perimeter fences.', ' Limited school MOOE funds allocated for large-scale structural renovations or repairs.', '', 'Frequent power outages, weak network signals in the area, and lack of water source.', 'Insufficient number of working computer units; lacks a secure room with proper air conditioning and wiring.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Positive school culture that encourages respect, unity, and responsibility', '', '', 'Active Child Protection Committee (CPC), functional guidance office, and regular anti-bullying campaigns.\r\n', 'Strict implementation of DepEd Child Protection Policy and high teacher accountability.\r\n', 'Effective tracking via the Early Warning System (EWS) and active home visitation programs.', 'Inclusive school curriculum, diverse student population integration, and localized lesson plans.', '', '', 'Designated Child Protection Coordinator and active PTA officers.', 'Annual conduct of earthquake and fire drills with BFP assistance.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'High level of volunteerism during Brigada Eskwela and school events.', 'Strong alumni involvement and active participation from the Barangay Council.', 'Presence of a functional School Quality Management Team (SQMT).', 'High satisfaction levels reported during quarterly Parent-Teacher Conferences.', '', '', '', 'Presence of a functional School Personnel Selection Board (PSB) and transparent promotion criteria.', '', 'Efficient school clerk/administrative officer and updated personnel records.', 'Adherence to the Magna Carta for Public School Teachers and school-wide workload consultation.', '', '', '', '', '', 'Regular monthly tracking of the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) by the School Finance Team.', 'Efficient bookkeeping system and prompt assistance from the division accounting office.', 1, 1, 0, 2, 1, 2, 1, 0, 6, 2, 6, 6, 0, 0, 6, 5, 6, 5, 1, 6, 4, 1, 2, 4, 6, 2, 1, 6, 1, 2, 1, 2, 3, 3, 2, 5, 3, 0, 5, 1, 3, 3, 'Develop more interactive, localized digital and printed learning blocks for struggling readers.', 'Intensify the utilization of HOTS-formulated questions in quarterly examinations.', '', 'Provide official school or division-level administrative backing that clears teachers of personal liability, provided they adhere to the established school citation guidelines.\r\n', 'Allocate specific hours in the school schedule dedicated solely to remediation', 'Strengthen partnerships with community groups to organize activities that reinforce peace and core values outside the classroom', 'Establish a system where results are discussed during department meetings and action plans are formulated based on findings', '', 'Sustain a 100% safe environment by launching an anonymous digital reporting drop-box and conducting quarterly student awareness seminars on cyber-safety.', 'Conduct annual orientation on child protection laws for all teaching and non-teaching staff, and reinforce the zero-tolerance policy during stakeholder general assemblies.\r\n', 'Strengthen the Adopt-a-Student program through local NGO partnerships to provide school supplies and feeding assistance to students at risk of dropping out (SARDOs).\r\n', 'Establish a dedicated cultural resource corner in the school library and organize a localized annual cultural exchange festival involving community elders.\r\n', '', '', 'Maintain a digital repository for CPC minutes and incident reports for quicker tracking.', 'Lobby for additional MOOE or stakeholder donations for \"Go-Bags\" and emergency signage.', 'Establish a \"Peer Support Group\" system to assist students with minor social concerns', 'Retrofit older school entrances with standard-compliant ramps and grab bars.', 'Conduct a capability-building workshop on strategic planning for the School Planning Team (SPT).', 'Create a flexible, pre-scheduled quarterly meeting calendar utilizing hybrid/online options.', 'Provide time-management and leadership training specifically tailored for student officers.', 'Establish regular feedback channels (such as suggestion boxes, surveys, or consultation meetings) to gather input from parents, students, and community members', 'Conduct a mid-year review to realign current school projects with the 3-year strategic goals.', 'Formalize the SGC through an induction ceremony and schedule quarterly meetings for policy review.', 'Implement a \"Class-Level PTA\" system to make meetings smaller, more frequent, and more flexible.', 'Formalize existing verbal partnerships through written Agreements or Deeds of Donation for better documentation.', 'Transition to a digital M&E dashboard (using shared spreadsheets) for real-time tracking of project progress', 'Provide a standardized e-portfolio template and conduct a workshop on MOV collection and organization.', 'Enhance the school’s internal monitoring system to include early warning alerts for upcoming deadlines.', 'Schedule \"Cluster-Based LAC\" sessions or utilize asynchronous digital platforms for flexible teacher training.', 'Conduct an in-house \"Career Pathing\" seminar to help personnel align their professional goals with promotion requirements.', 'Institutionalize the \"PRAISE\" program with monthly \"Teacher of the Month\" recognition through social media and simple incentives.', 'Establish a \"Compensation Tracking Calendar\" to notify personnel 3 months before they are due for increments.', 'Regularly update the School Form 7 (SF7) and utilize a \"Points System\" for ancillary tasks to ensure no teacher is overloaded.', 'Conduct a quarterly \"Safety Audit\" and prioritize the repair of electrical systems and structural integrity in the Annual Improvement Plan (AIP).', 'Strengthen linkages with local government units (LGUs) and private donors for infrastructure funding.\r\n', '', 'Partner with utility providers for repairs; request alternative solar panels and rainwater collectors from DepEd/LGU.\r\n', 'Submit a proposal for the DepEd Computerization Program (DCP); allocate school funds to secure/renovate a room.', 'Maintain timely quarterly procurement scheduling and continue strict adherence to the project procurement management plan (PPMP).', 'Set an internal school deadline for liquidations 5 days ahead of the official Division office deadline.', 'Implement a QR-code based Client Satisfaction Survey to reach more external stakeholders via mobile.', 0, 68, 12, 107),
(1041, '2026', '304262', '', '', 'Challenges in tracking learner progress due to inconsistent participation and mobility of learner; Need for stronger coordination between ALS implementers and stakeholders for learner support', '', '', 'Time constraints due to heavy teaching load; Limited monitoring tools to assess the effectiveness of values integration in classrooms; eed for further capacity-building and training on peace education and values formation', 'Time constraints due to heavy teaching load reducing focus on data analysis; Weak feedback loop where analysis results are not fully communicated to all teachers for collaborative improvement', '', 'Some bullying incidents remain unreported due to fear, peer pressure, or lack of confidence in reporting mechanisms; Difficulty in monitoring incidents occurring through social media and online platforms (cyberbullying); Need for strengthened guidance and counseling interventions for learners exhibiting behavioral concerns.', '', 'Financial constraints and poverty continue to affect the regular attendance of some learners; Some learners are compelled to prioritize work or household responsibilities over schooling; Geographic distance and transportation challenges affect learner accessibility to school; Need for stronger intervention and retention programs targeting struggling and disengaged learners', '', 'Difficulty in identifying and reaching all disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adult learners within the community; Irregular participation of learners due to employment, family obligations, and personal responsibilities; Insufficient resources and facilities to fully support inclusive and alternative learning delivery.\r\nChallenges in maintaining learner engagement and completion in alternative learning program; ', '', '', '', '', '', 'needs to be revised  , some of the plans are not applicable anymore', 'due to time conflicts, some scheduled meetings were not conducted', '', '', 'Delays in translating strategic goals into specific, measurable, and time-bound action plan; Inadequate allocation of resources and budget support for priority programs; Need for stronger coordination among committees and personnel responsible for implementation; Difficulty in sustaining continuity of programs due to changes in schedules, priorities, or personnel assignments', 'Limited awareness among stakeholders regarding the roles and responsibilities of the School Governance Council; Difficulty in scheduling meetings convenient for all stakeholders due to conflicting commitments; Limited resources to support SGC-led initiatives and program', '', '', 'Delays in submission and consolidation of reports and supporting documents; Limited utilization of monitoring results in improving future programs and interventions; Time constraints and multiple workloads affecting regular monitoring activities', '', '', '', '', '', 'Limited availability of funds and resources for recognition and incentive programs; Absence of a structured and institutionalized recognition system for personnel achievements; Limited opportunities to acknowledge both teaching and non-teaching personnel equally; Need for clearer criteria and guidelines in identifying outstanding accomplishments and milestone achievements', '', '', '', '', 'Insufficient library space to accommodate the increasing number of learners and users; Inadequate budget allocation for procurement of new library materials and maintenance of facilities; Some learning materials and equipment require repair, replacement, or upgrading', '', '', '', '', '', 'Regular conduct of formative and summative assessments, including periodic tests and mock NAT; Provision of targeted intervention programs (e.g., remediation, enrichment classes); Continuous teacher capacity-building (LAC sessions, INSETs) focusing on assessment and pedagogy', '', 'Regular Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions promoting collaborative development of materials; ', 'Systematic identification of struggling learners through assessment results and progress monitoring; Implementation of structured intervention programs (e.g., reading programs, numeracy drills); Support from school heads in scheduling and monitoring remediation sessions; Availability of remediation materials and modules', '', '', 'Strong partnership and linkage initiatives with local industries and community stakeholders; Support from LGUs and external partners aligned with programs of the Department of Education', '', 'Regular orientation of learners, teachers, and parents on child rights and protection; Promotion of a safe, respectful, and inclusive school culture', '', 'Active participation of community members and cultural groups; Conduct of school-wide activities', '', 'Strong implementation of the Alternative Learning System (ALS) under the Department of Education; Provision of flexible learning schedules and delivery modes', 'Implementation of child protection protocols and reporting procedures; Strong coordination with external agencies (DSWD, LGU, PNP) when needed', 'Established and updated Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (DRRM) Plan; Coordination with local disaster response units and LGU offices', 'Conduct of wellness activities; Promotion of a positive, supportive, and stigma-free school environment', 'Implementation of programs aligned with inclusive education policies of the Department of Education; Teacher training on inclusive education and differentiated instruction', '', '', 'Strong implementation of student leadership programs guided by the Department of Education policies on learner governance; Active supervision and mentoring by designated SSLG advisers; Clearly defined organizational structure, roles, and responsibilities of officers', 'Adoption of technology-driven systems; Regular gathering of stakeholder feedback to improve service delivery', '', '', 'Active and organized Parent-Teacher Association (PTA) with clear roles and responsibilities; Strong collaboration between parents, teachers, and school leadership supported by the Department of Education guidelines on stakeholder engagement; Transparent communication between school and parents regarding learner progress and school concerns; Regular conduct of PTA meetings, assemblies, and planning sessions; ', 'Strong partnership-building initiatives with LGUs, NGOs, and community stakeholders; ', '', 'Strong communication and feedback mechanisms between school and stakeholders; Strong collaboration among teachers, parents, and community partners', 'Strong instructional and administrative leadership promoting a culture of accountability and excellence; Continuous coaching, mentoring, and technical assistance provided by school heads and master teachers; Regular monitoring of personnel performance and timely feedback mechanisms', 'Effective implementation of school plans, programs, and targets aligned with school improvement goals; Strong teamwork and collaboration among teaching and non-teaching personnel; Efficient leadership and management practices supporting organizational performance', 'Active participation and collaboration of teachers during LAC sessions and professional learning activities; Supportive school leadership promoting continuous professional growth and reflective practice; haring of best practices, teaching strategies, and classroom innovations among teachers', 'Strong support from school leadership in encouraging personnel to attend trainings, seminars, and graduate studies; Culture of lifelong learning and continuous improvement among school personnel; Alignment of professional development programs with personnel needs and school goals', '', 'Efficient coordination between school personnel and payroll/accounting offices;  Timely preparation and submission of payroll-related documents and reports; Proper communication channels for addressing compensation-related concerns and updates', 'Clear and transparent workload distribution policies implemented by school leadership; Proper consideration of teachers’ specialization, experience, and competencies in task assignments; Supportive work environment promoting teamwork and shared responsibility', 'Active participation of stakeholders in ensuring the safety and functionality of school facilities; Regular conduct of school facility inspection and monitoring by designated committees and school personnel; Supportive leadership prioritizing school safety, cleanliness, and facility maintenance; Collaboration with LGUs and stakeholders for infrastructure monitoring and improvement initiatives', 'Strong support from school leadership in prioritizing infrastructure development and maintenance; Participation of stakeholders in Brigada Eskwela and other school improvement initiatives; Active collaboration with stakeholders, LGUs, and community partners for school improvement projects', '', 'Continuous coordination with service providers and local stakeholders for maintenance of utilities and connectivity; Availability of budget allocation for utility expenses and minor repairs', 'Integration of technology and digital resources in classroom instruction; Growing digital literacy and technology integration among teachers and learners aligned with the programs of the Department of Education', 'Effective financial planning and budgeting aligned with school priorities and improvement goals; Strong adherence to government accounting and financial management policies and procedures; Active monitoring of fund utilization and expenditures by school leadership and finance personnel', 'Timely preparation and submission of liquidation reports and supporting documents; Organized record-keeping and systematic documentation of financial transactions; Effective coordination among school heads, property custodians, and finance personnel', 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 4, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 4, 2, 2, 6, 5, 2, 2, 2, 4, 2, 2, 2, 4, 2, 4, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''