ith the Local School Board (LSB); synergy with the Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH) for major projects.', '', 'Timely liquidation of MOOE allowing for uninterrupted utility payments', '', 'Systematic \"Cash Flow\" management; early liquidation of previous cash advances to trigger the immediate release of the next month’s allocation.', 'Established \"Internal Audit\" system where a school-based committee reviews vouchers for completeness before submission to the Division Office.', 1, 1, 0, 5, 3, 6, 1, 0, 5, 2, 6, 6, 6, 0, 2, 1, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 1, 1, 6, 2, 2, 1, 2, 6, 3, 1, 2, 2, 6, 2, 4, 4, 3, 1, 3, 2, 'Conduct regular remediation classes, literacy and numeracy intervention programs, and differentiated instruction strategies.', 'Conduct regular competency-based remediation, enrichment classes, and focused review sessions based on least mastered competencies.', '', 'Enhance ICT utilization and expand access to digital tools, repositories, and technological resources.', 'Continue prioritizing funds and stakeholder support for the development and reproduction of intervention materials.', 'Conduct parent orientation and strengthen school-home partnerships in promoting values formation among learners.', 'Sustain continuous professional development and mentoring on assessment literacy and data analysis.', '', 'Coordinate with stakeholders and LGUs for the installation and maintenance of school safety and monitoring facilities.', 'Sustain strict enforcement, regular review, and continuous orientation on Child Protection Policy among all stakeholders.', 'Strengthen coordination with LGUs and stakeholders for assistance programs (e.g., scholarships, school supplies, feeding programs).', 'Sustain cultural awareness programs and continuous orientation on inclusive and culture-responsive education.', 'Maintain inclusive, supportive, and non-discriminatory school culture.', '', 'Sustain clear delineation of roles and periodic review of CPC functions to ensure efficiency and accountability.', 'Maintain scheduled drills and improve simulation quality for better learner and staff readiness.', 'Maintain a positive school climate that encourages openness, respect, and psychological safety.', 'Sustain and strengthen inclusive education policies and ensure continuous implementation of SPED-related programs.', 'Sustain leadership development programs and continuous improvement in strategic planning practices.', 'Sustain participatory governance practices and regular strengthening of school-community planning structures.', 'Sustain institutional support through policies, supervision, and integration of student governance in school programs.', 'Improve ICT facilities and strengthen partnerships for internet connectivity and equipment support.', 'Sustain data-driven decision-making through improved data collection and utilization systems.', 'Provide training on school governance, planning, and data-driven decision-making.', 'Sustain strong parent engagement through regular meetings, consultations, and school activities.', 'Continue strengthening school-to-school partnerships and learning exchange programs.', 'Continue strengthening collaborative participation and shared accountability among personnel.', 'Sustain alignment of IPCR targets with SIP/AIP and continuously refine performance indicators.', 'Sustain a collaborative and supportive work environment across all offices.', 'Sustain budget allocation for professional development and capacity-building activities.', 'Continue implementing needs-based and competency-based L&D programs aligned with career progression.', 'Sustain and regularly enhance the school-based recognition and rewards mechanism.', 'Maintain clear coordination protocols and regular communication with finance and accounting offices.', 'Sustain collaborative decision-making and open dialogue in assigning responsibilities.', 'Continuous Capacity Building: Commitment to send the facilities coordinator to advanced seminars on disaster risk reduction and climate-resilient infrastructure.', 'Resolution to maintain a \"Resource Map\" visible to the public, showing exactly where donated funds and materials are being utilized to encourage further external investment.', 'Allocate a specific percentage of the annual budget for library enrichment and include library upgrades in the AIP/SIP.', 'Maintain a \"Utility Reserve Fund\" within the school\'s supplemental budget to cover emergency repairs without affecting instructional funds.', 'Conduct \"ICT Literacy Workshops\" for teachers to build confidence in using the lab for instructional purposes.', 'Maintain a 100% liquidation rate within the first five days of the succeeding month to ensure continuous funding.', 'Maintain a \"Document Tracking System\" to monitor the movement of liquidation folders from the school to the Division Office.', 'Sustain continuous training on frontline service excellence and stakeholder engagement.', 0, 25, 12, 60),
(1074, '2026', '128844', '-Presence of slow readers and non -numerate\r\n-Limited time for remediation due to class schedule \r\n- Irregular learnerattendance', '-Low mastery of competencies among some learners\r\n-Limited time for intensive review sessions\r\n-Lack of sufficient review materials\r\n-Learner absenteeism or low motivation', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '•	Financial constraints of families \r\n•	Learners helping in household or livelihood activities \r\n•	Irregular attendance due to distance \r\n•	Limited parental involvement in some cases\r\n', '', '', '', '', '-Policies and guidelines are present but not strictly followed or monitored\r\n-Teachers ,personnel and learners have insufficient knowledge and skills in disaster prepared and response\r\n-Weak linkages with local DRRM offices, rescue units and community stakeholders', '•	No trained mental health professional in school \r\n•	Limited knowledge on handling mental health concerns \r\n•	Stigma or hesitation in discussing mental health \r\n•	Limited time for activities\r\n', '•	Financial difficulties of families \r\n•	Learners needing to work or help at home \r\n•	Lack of parental support in some cases \r\n•	Distance of learners from school\r\n', '•	Limited stakeholder participation due to distance and availability \r\n•	Lack of updated or complete data for planning \r\n•	Time constraints of teachers during planning period\r\n', '•	Irregular attendance of community members due to work and distance \r\n•	Limited understanding of roles among some members \r\n•	Difficulty in scheduling meetings convenient for all\r\n', '', '•	Limited internet connectivity in the area \r\n•	Lack of dedicated personnel for frontline services \r\n•	Some stakeholders have limited access to digital communication\r\n', '', '•	Lack of organized SGC structure \r\n•	Limited awareness of stakeholders about SGC roles \r\n•	Low participation due to time constraints and distance \r\n•	Irregular or no scheduled meetings\r\n', '', '', '•	Limited time of teachers for monitoring and documentation \r\n•	Incomplete or inconsistent data collection \r\n•	Lack of standardized monitoring tools\r\n', '•	Limited participation of stakeholders in answering surveys \r\n•	Some feedback not clearly expressed or incomplete \r\n•	Lack of systematic recording of results\r\n', '', '', '•	Limited time due to teaching workload \r\n•	Inconsistent attendance of teachers \r\n•	Lack of available training materials/resources \r\n•	Limited access to expert resource speakers\r\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '38. \r\n•	No existing library facility or space \r\n•	Limited available reading materials \r\n•	Lack of funds for full library setup \r\n•	No designated librarian \r\n', '•	Occasional water interruption or low pressure \r\n•	Unstable or slow internet connection \r\n•	Limited funds for major repairs \r\n•	Delayed response from external service providers\r\n', '40. \r\n•	No existing computer laboratory or equipment \r\n•	Limited funds for purchasing computers \r\n•	Lack of stable internet connection (in some cases) \r\n•	Limited technical expertise for maintenance\r\n', '', '', '', '', '', 'Teachers consistently develop contextualized learning  materials by integrating familiar local contexts such as farming ,fishing, and community life into daily lessons. These materials are refined through regular LAC sessions  where teachers share ,review ,and improve each others outputs.\r\nThe school maximizes available and low cost resources ,including improvised and recyled materials to ensuresustainability and relevance', 'Teachers implemented targeted  remediation activities based on learners\' assessed needs in reading ,science , and mathematics. They use differentiated strategies  such as peer tutoring ,guided practices during designated intervention periods.', 'Teacher intentionally integrate themes of  themes of  peace , and Department of Education  core values into daily lessons and classroomsroutines. They use real life situations, stories ,and guided discussions to reinforce respect ,responsibility , and empathy among learners .', '-The school regularly conducts test item analysis to identify learners \' strength and areas needing improvement across subjects .Findings guide development of targeted interventions and remediation activites  the', '', 'The school maintains a proactive approach to child protection through clear policies, consistent monitoring, and immediate response to any concerns. Teachers integrate values formation and respectful behavior into daily routines, while learners are encouraged to report issues in a safe and supportive environment. Strong collaboration with parents and the community reinforces positive discipline and open communication. As a result, the school sustains a safe and nurturing environment with zero reported bullying incidents ', '10. The school strictly implements child protection policies and maintains clear reporting and response mechanisms to safeguard all learners. Teachers and staff are oriented on recognizing and addressing signs of abuse, ensuring vigilance in daily interactions. Strong partnerships with parents and the community support early intervention and open communication. As a result, the school has sustained a zero child abuse incidence.', '', 'The school conducts culture-sensitive activities that recognize and respect the diverse backgrounds of its learners and community. Teachers integrate local traditions, language, and practices into school programs and classroom instruction. Activities are planned with community participation to ensure authenticity and inclusivity. As a result, learners develop respect for cultural diversity and a stronger sense of identity and belonging', '13. The school ensures access to learning experiences for disadvantaged learners through flexible and inclusive delivery strategies. Teachers provide differentiated tasks, remediation, and alternative learning modalities to address varied needs and circumstances. The school also coordinates with stakeholders to support learners through available resources and community assistance. As a result, more learners are able to participate meaningfully and continue their education despite challenges.', '', '15. The school maintains a functional Child Protection Committee with clearly defined roles, regular meetings, and documented plans and actions. The committee actively monitors child protection concerns, responds promptly to reported cases, and ensures proper documentation and follow-through. It also conducts orientations for teachers, learners, and parents to strengthen awareness and preventive practices. As a result, the school sustains a safe and protective environment for all learners.', '', '', '', '', '', '21. The school maintains a functional Supreme Pupil Government with clearly defined roles and regular meetings that guide student-led initiatives. Officers actively participate in planning and implementing school activities, promoting leadership and responsibility among learners. Teachers provide guidance while allowing pupils to take active roles in decision-making and program implementation. As a result, learners develop confidence, accountability, and a strong sense of participation in school governance.', '', 'The school operationalizes its strategic plan through a clear and aligned implementation plan with defined targets, timelines, and responsible persons. Programs and activities are regularly monitored to ensure they are on track and responsive to emerging needs. Progress is reviewed during meetings, allowing timely adjustments and improvements. As a result, planned goals are translated into concrete actions that support continuous school improvement.', '', ' The school maintains a functional Parent-Teacher Association with regular meetings, clear communication, and active participation from parents and teachers. The PTA supports school programs and activities through collaboration, volunteerism, and shared decision-making. Open dialogue strengthens trust and ensures that concerns are addressed promptly. As a result, the partnership contributes to improved learner support and overall school development.', ' The school actively collaborates with stakeholders and nearby schools through regular coordination, joint activities, and resource sharing. Partnerships with the community, local agencies, and fellow schools support the implementation of programs and address common challenges. Communication is maintained to ensure alignment of goals and sustained cooperation. As a result, these partnerships strengthen support systems and enhance the delivery of basic education services.', '', '', 'School personnel consistently achieve a “Very Satisfactory” rating in the Individual Performance Commitment and Review through clear performance targets and regular monitoring. The school provides support mechanisms such as coaching, mentoring, and feedback sessions to help personnel meet expected standards. Professional development opportunities are also encouraged to strengthen competencies. As a result, personnel maintain quality performance aligned with school goals and expectations.', '30. The school consistently achieves a “Very Satisfactory” rating in the Office Performance Commitment and Review through clear alignment of targets, programs, and assigned responsibilities. Regular monitoring and team coordination ensure that activities are implemented as planned and outputs are delivered on time. Progress is reviewed during meetings, allowing timely adjustments and collective accountability. As a result, the school sustains efficient performance and meets its organizational goals.', '', ' The school actively supports the promotion and continuous professional development of its personnel through regular training, mentoring, and access to learning opportunities. Teachers are encouraged to pursue further studies, attend webinars, and participate in professional learning communities. School leadership provides guidance and recognition to motivate growth and career advancement. As a result, personnel continuously enhance their competencies and improve the quality of instruction and service delivery.', ' The school recognizes and rewards milestone achievements of its personnel through simple yet meaningful forms of appreciation such as certificates, acknowledgments during meetings, and commendations in school events. Achievements in performance, service, and professional growth are regularly highlighted to motivate staff. Recognition is done fairly and consistently to promote a culture of appreciation. As a result, personnel feel valued and are encouraged to sustain and improve their performance.', ' The school ensures the timely and accurate processing of salaries, allowances, and other compensation through proper documentation and coordination with concerned offices. School personnel are guided on required submissions to avoid delays and discrepancies. Any concerns are promptly addressed through clear communication and follow-up. As a result, personnel receive their benefits on time, contributing to their morale and overall work efficiency.', '. The school ensures fair and equitable distribution of teacher workload through clear assignment of classes, designations, and ancillary tasks based on capacity and expertise. Workload is reviewed regularly to maintain balance and prevent overburdening. Open communication allows teachers to raise concerns and adjustments to be made when necessary. As a result, teachers manage their responsibilities effectively while maintaining quality instruction.', 'The school initiates improvements of its infrastructure and facilities based on identified needs from regular inspections and feedback. It mobilizes available resources and coordinates with stakeholders to support repair, maintenance, and development projects. Priorities are set to address urgent concerns affecting safety and learning conditions. As a result, the school continuously enhances its facilities to provide a more conducive learning environment.', 'The school initiates improvements of its infrastructure and facilities based on identified needs from regular inspections and feedback. It mobilizes available resources and coordinates with stakeholders to support repair, maintenance, and development projects. Priorities are set to address urgent concerns affecting safety and learning conditions. As a result, the school continuously enhances its facilities to provide a more conducive learning environment.', '', '', '', '. The school ensures efficient use of its Maintenance and Other Operating Expenses (MOOE) through careful planning, prioritization of needs, and adherence to budgeting guidelines. Expenditures are aligned with school programs and regularly monitored to ensure proper utilization. Transparent documentation and reporting are consistently practiced. As a result, the school achieves a 72–100% utilization rate while supporting its priority needs.', '. The school ensures 100% liquidation of its utilized Maintenance and Other Operating Expenses (MOOE) through accurate documentation and strict adherence to financial guidelines. All expenses are properly recorded, supported with complete receipts, and submitted within the required timelines. Regular monitoring and coordination with responsible personnel help prevent delays and discrepancies. As a result, the school maintains full compliance with financial reporting requirements.', 2, 2, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 2, 2, 1, 3, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 6, 2, 6, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 3, 3, 5, 1, 1, 'Strengthen daily reading and numeracy routines\r\n- Provide continuous remediation for learners in need \r\n-Involve parents in supporting learning at home\r\n-Maximize available  materials and create improvised resources', 'Focus on least mastered skills through targeted interventions\r\n-Conduct regular and consistent review sessions\r\n-Engage parents in supporting review at home\r\n-Commit to gradual improvement of NAT performance through sustained efforts ', '', '-Learners demonstrate better understanding and engagement as lessons are directly connected to their  real life experiences', '-Progress monitored regularly and approaches  to address specific learning gaps', '-Learners demonstrate positive behavior and deeper understanding of values in both school and community settings', 'The school commit to conduct accurate ,objective test item analysis to improve assessment  quality and enhance student learning', '', 'The school commit to maintain zero incidence of child bullying in our school through vigilance,cooperation and active promotion of a safe and respectful environment', 'We ensure zero child abuse and protect every learners\' rights andsafety', '•	Strengthen early monitoring of attendance \r\n•	Continue consistent home visitation and follow-up \r\n•	Enhance communication with parents \r\n•	Provide supportive and flexible learning environment \r\n•	Commit to sustaining reduced drop-out incidence\r\n', 'We commit to holding culture-sensitive activities that respect diversity and promote inclusivity ', 'We provide equal learning access for disadvantaged, out of school youth, and adult learners', '', 'We commit to fully implement and sustain afunctional child protection policy to safeguard every learners safety and rights', '-Update and revise DRRM Plan\r\n-Conduct regular drills and trainings\r\n-Strengthen coordination with local DRRM Offices and stakeholders\r\n ', '•	Start with simple awareness and support activities \r\n•	Strengthen teacher capacity through available trainings/webinars \r\n•	Establish linkages with RHU and LGU for referrals \r\n•	Encourage open communication between learners and teachers \r\n•	Commit to building a supportive and safe school environment\r\n\r\n', '•	Strengthen early identification of at-risk learners \r\n•	Continue regular home visitations and follow-ups \r\n•	Enhance parent engagement and awareness \r\n•	Provide flexible and supportive learning environment \r\n•	Commit to sustaining zero or minimal drop-out rate\r\n', '•	Schedule planning activities earlier and inform stakeholders in advance\r\n•	Strengthen data collection and record-keeping practices\r\n•	Encourage more stakeholder involvement through flexible meeting options\r\n•	Commit to regular monitoring and simple mid-year review of plans\r\n', '•	Set meeting schedules in advance and keep them short and focused \r\n•	Clarify roles and responsibilities of each member \r\n•	Use simple communication (text/chat) to update absent members \r\n•	Continue strengthening partnership with barangay and parents\r\n', 'We commit to support \r\nand sustain a functional Supreme Student Government that leads , serves and represent learners effectively', '•	Continue using both online (chat/text) and offline (scheduled visits) methods \r\n•	Assign clear roles for handling inquiries and requests \r\n•	Improve record-keeping of transactions for better tracking \r\n•	Strengthen communication channels through PTA coordination\r\n', 'We commit to fully operationalize our school strategic plan through  an implementation plan', '•	Reorganize SGC with clearly defined roles and members \r\n•	Conduct orientation to build understanding and commitment \r\n•	Set regular but manageable meeting schedules (at least quarterly) \r\n•	Strengthen communication through PTA and barangay coordination\r\n', 'We commit to sustain a functional PTA that collaborates actively to support school programs and student welfare', 'We commit to collaborates with stakeholders and other schools in strengthening partnership', '•	Develop and use uniform and simple monitoring tools \r\n•	Allocate specific time for monitoring and evaluation activities \r\n•	Strengthen documentation and record-keeping practices \r\n•	Continue regular review meetings to improve programs\r\n', 'Attain  rating of very satisfactory in the individual performance commitment and review', 'We commit to attain very satisfactory rating in OPCR through consistent compliance ,quality ,performance and achievement of all targets', '•	Schedule LAC sessions during least busy days or inset days \r\n•	Ensure strict but supportive monitoring of attendance \r\n•	Utilize in-house experts to lead sessions \r\n•	Maximize free online resources (DepEd Commons, webinars) \r\n•	Commit to continuous improvement by aligning LAC topics with actual classroom needs\r\n', 'We commit to facilitate and promote continuous professional development to enhance staff competence and performance', '', 'Ensure timely receipt of correct salaries', 'ensure fair an equitable distribution of teachers\' workload', '-we commit to regularly inspect school infrastructure to ensure safety, proper  condition and compliance with standards', 'we commit to regularly inspect school infrastructure to ensure safety, proper  condition and compliance with standards', '•	Start with a reading corner instead of a full library \r\n•	Conduct book donation drives (Brigada Eskwela, PTA meetings) \r\n•	Assign a teacher as library focal person \r\n•	Gradually improve resources through partnerships and donations \r\n•	Commit to sustaining and expanding the mini-library annually\r\n', '•	Conduct regular inspection and preventive maintenance \r\n•	Establish quick coordination with LGU and service providers \r\n•	Allocate small MOOE funds for minor repairs \r\n•	Encourage responsible use of water, electricity, and internet \r\n•	Commit to sustaining and improving access for uninterrupted school operations\r\n', '•	Start with a small computer corner instead of a full laboratory \r\n•	Seek donations and partnerships for additional units \r\n•	Assign a teacher to oversee proper use and maintenance \r\n•	Gradually improve facilities as resources become available \r\n•	Commit to integrating basic ICT skills in teaching-learning processes\r\n', 'We commit to active and maintain 72-100 % of MOOE for efficient and timely fund use', 'We commit to active and maintain 100 % of  MOOE  utilization for efficient and timely fund use', '•	Develop and use uniform and simple monitoring tools \r\n•	Allocate specific time for monitoring and evaluation activities \r\n•	Strengthen documentation and record-keeping practices \r\n•	Continue regular review meetings to improve programs\r\n', 0, 30, 12, 60);
