(1095, '2026', '128300', 'Some learners have difficulty in reading comprehension and basic numeracy skills due to porr attendance and limited parental support', 'Limited access to learning resources and technology affects learners\' performance and participation in activities.', 'N/A', '', '', 'Some learners show behavioral issues and lack appreciation of values integration.', 'Limited teachers\' skills in test item analysis and data interpretation', 'N/A', '', '', '', 'Activities are regularly held but there is still room to further include more diverse cultural groups and traditions in the community; limited resources sometimes restrict scope and variety of activities.', 'N/A', 'N/A', '', '', 'Services are available and used, but limited number of guidance counselors makes it hard to accommodate all students needing help. Not all teachers are fully trained to identify early signs of mental health concerns.', 'N/A', '', 'Team is organized and meets regularly; challenge is limited participation from some sectors (e.g., private sectors, NGOs, minority groups). Meetings are sometimes delayed due to conflicting schedules; contributions vary among members', '', 'Innovations are present (e.g., online inquiries, simplified forms), but limited technology and internet access hinder wider adoption. Some parents/stakeholders prefer traditional methods, so adoption rate varies. Limited staff skills in digital tools is also a challenge.', ' Some activities lack clear timelines and assigned persons responsible\r\n- Budget allocation for certain planned activities is not fully aligned\r\n- Limited monitoring of whether planned outputs are achieved on schedule\r\n- Some stakeholders are not fully oriented on their roles in the plan', '- Members are not regularly attending meetings\r\n- Roles and functions of SGC members are not clear to all\r\n- Limited participation in planning, monitoring, and decision-making\r\n- Lack of regular meetings and documented minutes/action plans\r\n- Members lack knowledge/training on SGC mandates and functions', '', '', '- Monitoring tools are not standardized\r\n- Data collected is not always analyzed or used for improvement\r\n- Limited involvement of stakeholders in evaluation\r\n- No regular feedback mechanism to adjust activities\r\n- Reports are made but not always acted upon', '- Some stakeholders are not satisfied with facilities, sanitation, or support services\r\n- Feedback collection is irregular and not systematic\r\n- Gaps exist in communication between school and community\r\n- Expectations of some stakeholders are not clearly understood or manage', '', '', '', '', 'Recognition is occasional; limited budget for rewards; inconsistent criteria for awards.', '', '', '', '', 'Limited books/learning materials; no full-time librarian; space is small; rarely used by students; no organized system.', '', 'Few working units; outdated computers; no proper ventilation; limited internet connection; no dedicated technician.', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong teacher collaboration and support from school heads and stakeholders', 'Teachers\' dedication and support from parents/community volunteers', '', '', '', 'Regular conduct of anti-bullying campaigns and seminars\r\nStrict implementation of anti-bullying policies and guidelines\r\nActive monitoring of student behavior by teachers and guidance counselors\r\nOpen reporting system for students, parents, and staff.', 'Full implementation of Child Protection Policy\r\nAll school staff underwent child protection training\r\nFunctional child protection committee\r\nClear guidelines on proper student handling and discipline\r\nConfidential and accessible reporting mechanism', 'Regular tracking and monitoring of student attendance\r\nImplementation of alternative learning modes and remedial classes\r\nProvision of financial/scholarship support and learning materials\r\nStrong home-school partnership and regular parent-teacher meetings\r\nEarly identification and intervention for at-risk students', '', '', '', 'Committee is officially organized with designated members and clear roles\r\nRegular meetings are conducted (monthly/quarterly)\r\nFunctional reporting and response system is in place\r\nImplements child protection policies and conducts information campaigns\r\nMaintains records of cases, reports, and actions taken', 'Approved, updated DRRM plan aligned with national standards\r\nRegular conduct of drills (fire, earthquake, flood, etc.)\r\nIdentified safe zones, evacuation routes, and assembly areas\r\nDRRM team organized and trained.', '', '', 'Strong guidance from division/regional offices and existing policy frameworks\r\nActive participation of teachers, staff, and community members in planning\r\nRegular consultation and data gathering to identify needs and priorities\r\nClear guidelines and timeline for plan formulation and review', '', 'Democratic election of officers and clear constitution/by-laws\r\nActive guidance and supervision by designated teacher-adviser\r\nStrong support from school administration and student body\r\nRegular meetings, planning sessions, and reporting\r\nInvolvement in school activities, decision-making, and student welfare', '', '', '', '- Strong leadership of PTA officers\r\n- High enthusiasm and support from majority of parents\r\n- Regular activities are conducted (meetings, projects, fundraising)\r\n- Good communication channel between school and PTA', '- Good relationship with LGU, NGOs, alumni, and neighboring schools\r\n- Stakeholders are willing to support school programs\r\n- Communication lines are open and active.', '', '', 'Clear guidelines, regular coaching, supportive leadership, standardized assessment tools.', 'Defined office mandates, regular monitoring, team cooperation, established reporting systems.', 'Regular assessment of needs, supportive administration, available facilitators, policy compliance.', 'Support for training, dissemination of guidelines, assistance in application, recognition of qualifications.', '', 'Efficient finance staff, clear guidelines, coordination with division, Efficient finance staff, clear guidelines, coordination with division office, proper records. office, proper records.', 'Consultation with teachers, awareness of teaching loads, flexible scheduling, shared responsibilities.', 'Assigned maintenance staff; school head conducts regular rounds; support from stakeholders.', 'Identified needs from inspections; support from LGU/PTA; availability of MOOE; community help.', '', 'Connected to main utility lines; regular maintenance; service providers are accessible; backup power available.', '', 'Proper financial planning; trained bookkeeper/accountant; clear guidelines; regular monitoring.', 'Complete supporting documents; trained finance staff; clear liquidation guidelines; internal checking.', 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 6, 1, 0, 6, 2, 2, 6, 0, 0, 2, 2, 6, 0, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 6, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Strengthened reading and numeracy  intervention programs, conduct regular monitoring and encourage parental involvement through home learning activities', 'Provide additional learning materials and ICT resources. Conduct enrichment/remedial classes and stregnthened  teachers\'  training on 21st century teaching strategies', '', 'Conduct LAC sessions and workshops on contextualization and provide resource support/materials sharing', 'Strengthen remediation programs through scheduled intervention classes and parental involvement.', 'Intensify integration of peace education and core values through classroom activities and school programs.', 'Conduct training/workshop on test contruction, item analysis and utilization of assessment results', '', 'Sustain and strengthen anti-bullying programs, workshops, and activities\r\nContinue training for teachers and staff on early detection and intervention\r\nMaintain the safe and inclusive environment for all students\r\nRegularly orient parents on their role in preventing bullying', 'Sustain strict compliance with national and local child protection laws\r\nConduct annual refresher training for all personnel\r\nContinue information and education campaigns for students and parents\r\nRegularly review and update child protection policies and procedures', 'Strengthen the student monitoring and intervention system\r\nExpand scholarship and feeding programs to support vulnerable learners\r\nConduct regular home visits and close coordination with families\r\nProvide additional academic and psychosocial support services\r\nSustain programs that promote school retention and engagement', 'Develop a yearly cultural activity plan covering all groups in the community\r\nInvolve local leaders, elders, and cultural groups in planning and implementation\r\nAllocate sufficient budget and resources for cultural programs\r\nIntegrate culture and gender sensitivity in teacher training and curriculum\r\nRegularly evaluate activities to ensure inclusivity, relevance, and respect.', '', '', 'Sustain regular meetings and capacity-building/training for members\r\nConduct wider information campaigns for students, parents, and stakeholders\r\nUpdate guidelines and procedures based on latest policies\r\nMaintain transparency and confidentiality in all operations', 'Secure adequate budget for emergency supplies and facilities\r\nConduct annual refresher training and simulation drills for all personnel and students\r\nRegularly review and update the plan based on risks and new guidelines\r\nStrengthen partnership with LGU, OCD, and other agencies for support', 'Advocate for additional guidance personnel or trained focal persons\r\nConduct capacity-building on mental health awareness for all teachers\r\nIntegrate mental wellness in daily lessons and school activities\r\nEstablish strong referral links with health centers and mental health agencies\r\nSustain regular wellness programs and peer-support groups', '', 'Simplify the plan document and create a summarized version for easy reference\r\nEnsure all programs, projects, and activities directly link to strategic goals\r\nConduct orientation and consultation to ensure full understanding and ownership\r\nReview and update the plan annually based on results, feedback, and new policies', 'Expand membership to ensure full representation of all stakeholders\r\nSet fixed, convenient schedules and provide advance notices for meetings\r\nConduct capacity-building on planning, collaboration, and decision-making\r\nRecognize and reward active participation to sustain engagement\r\nStrengthen communication channels to gather inputs from all sectors.', 'Allocate sufficient budget and resources for SSG/SPG programs\r\nConduct annual leadership training, workshops, and seminars for officers\r\nStrengthen partnership with alumni, parents, and community for support\r\nEncourage inclusive representation of all grade levels and groups\r\nDocument and recognize contributions to motivate future leader', 'Upgrade facilities, internet connectivity, and digital tools\r\nTrain staff on digital systems, customer service, and process improvement\r\nProvide both traditional and digital options to serve all stakeholders\r\nCreate feedback channels to continuously improve services\r\nDocument and share best practices; seek partnerships for support', '- Revise implementation plan to include detailed timeline, responsible persons, and measurable outputs\r\n- Align budget directly with each activity in the plan\r\n- Conduct orientation/meeting with all staff and stakeholders to clarify roles\r\n- Establish monthly monitoring and reporting mechanism', '- Conduct orientation and training on SGC roles, functions, and legal mandates\r\n- Set fixed meeting schedule, issue notices in advance, and require attendance tracking\r\n- Develop clear terms of reference and work plan for SGC\r\n- Ensure regular documentation of meetings, decisions, and action items\r\n- Encourage active participation in school planning, monitoring, and resource mobilization', '- Design activities/schedules that accommodate working parents\r\n- Encourage and promote equal participation of both mothers and fathers\r\n- Strengthen coordination: all PTA projects must be aligned and approved by school\r\n- Publish financial reports regularly for transparency\r\n- Recognize and reward active PTA contributions', ' Formalize partnerships through Memorandum of Agreement/Understanding\r\n- Develop joint action plans with clear goals, activities, and contributions\r\n- Expand collaboration to include resource sharing, training, and student activities\r\n- Create a partnership database and evaluate results annually\r\n- Recognize partners’ contributions publicly', '- Develop and use standardized monitoring and evaluation tools\r\n- Train staff on data collection, analysis, and report writing\r\n- Include stakeholders in evaluation and feedback sessions\r\n- Use evaluation results to revise and improve programs\r\n- Submit and discuss monitoring reports during regular meetings', 'Conduct IPCRF orientation/workshops; simplify documentation; schedule quarterly performance check-ins', 'Align targets with school plan; set clear timelines; conduct team reviews and feedback sessions.', 'Conduct training needs analysis; secure internal/external resources; make sessions interactive and relevant.', 'Maintain promotion info board; assist in document preparation; partner with agencies for more development programs', ' Create formal recognition system; allocate small budget; include non-monetary awards; hold regular appreciation events.', 'Double-check computations; submit requirements early; maintain open communication with finance unit; update personnel on status.', 'Formulate clear workload policy; use standard allocation criteria; consult before assigning extra tasks; review distribution yearly.\r\n', 'Create standard inspection checklist; set monthly schedule; tag issues by urgency; log all findings and actions taken.', 'Prioritize urgent repairs; prepare detailed project proposals; streamline procurement; coordinate early with suppliers/partners.', 'Designate library coordinator; secure funds to add books/materials; arrange shelves properly; set regular opening hours; promote library use.', 'Install water storage tank; coordinate with providers for better signal; schedule preventive electrical checks; allocate budget for upgrades.', 'Repair/replace broken units; secure funds for new computers; install proper cooling; assign ICT coordinator; set usage guidelines.', 'Plan activities aligned with budget; submit requirements early; track spending monthly; adjust plans to fully utilize allocation.', 'Conduct orientation on liquidation rules; double-check all papers before submission; submit within deadline; maintain proper filing system.', '- Conduct regular, structured satisfaction surveys/feedback forms\r\n- Address identified concerns immediately and report back to stakeholders\r\n- Improve facilities and services based on feedback\r\n- Strengthen communication channels (meetings, newsletters, social media)\r\n- Manage expectations through clear information sharing', 0, 116, 12, NULL),
