(1146, '2026', '128549', 'Absenteeism', 'Least learned competencies in all subject areas', 'No enrolment', 'Time', 'Struggling learners', 'Technical assistance to the newly hired teachers', 'Technical Assistance to the newly hired teachers', 'Not applicable to elementary', 'Incidence reporting', 'Incidence reporting', 'Family Proble, health issues, attitudes towards education', 'Inclusion in the classes and activities in the school', 'No enrolment', 'No enrolment', 'For  re organization for SY 2026-2027', 'Revisit the SDRMM plan', 'Revisit the mental wellness program', 'No SNED program', '', 'Re- organize the planning team', '', 'Revisit frontline services', 'Unrealize plan  due to budget', 'Re organization', 'Failure to pay the voluntary contribution of some members', 'MOA or other docs', 'Time', 'satisfactory rating', 'Very Satisfactory', 'Very Satisfactory', 'Time and schedule issue', 'Funding', 'Funding', 'Discrepancy issue', 'Unfairly', 'Reporting system', 'Funding', 'No vacant room', 'For upgrade electrical supply', 'Re-installation/ rehabilitation', 'under spending', 'delayed liquidation', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'with approved SIP', '', 'with functional SPG', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 6, 1, 6, 2, 2, 1, 1, 0, 2, 2, 6, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 3, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 3, 3, 3, 2, 5, 3, 5, 3, 3, 3, 3, 'Tap and meet with the parents regarding the status of the concern learners\r\n>Sustain  the performance in achieving proficiency level', 'Conduct review  focusing on the least learned competencies', 'Encourage learners to enroll in the formal education', 'Monitor the preparation contextualize materials\r\n>Collaboration', 'Monitor regularly  conduct of remediation \r\n> Support the teachers need in the conduct of class remediation', 'Extent technical assistance to the new teachers  with the master teachers assistance\r\n> Monitor through class observation and check lesson plan\r\n>FGDs', 'FGDs', '', '>Re- Orientation of Child Protection\r\n>Strengthen anti bullying policy in the school', 'Strengthen information and dissemination campaign in the school on child abuse', '>Daily monitoring of attence\r\n>Conduct Home Visitation\r\n> Strengthen Flexible learning Program for learners at risks', 'Strengthen  culturally sensitive school environment for all  learners, teachers, parents and the whole community as well', 'No refusal of enrolment for those OSYs willing to enroll  in the school', 'The school will function if there is enrolment on ALS', 'Re organization of  Child Protection Committee', 'Convene for planning and revision of plan if needed', 'Convene for  revisiting the mechanism support for mental wellness program\r\n>Implementation of wellness leave or break', '> Orientation on SNED program to all teachers, NTPs and parents\r\n> Submit for assessment  learners with manifestation\r\n> Tag in LIS those learners with manifeatation\r\n>Send teachers to SNED training', 'Revisit SIP every quarter ', '> Re -organization SBM or SGC planning team', 'Strengthen SPG functionality', 'Revisiting frontline services', '>Source out of funds through IGP or partner stakeholders', '> Send invitation letters and conduct meeting for the re- organization of SGC', 'Encourage the Parents to pay their voluntary contribution\r\n> Look for a scheme with the PTA officials on how to convince some parents to pay their voluntary obligations', 'Have an agreement  or MOA with partner stakeholders\r\nInivite partner stakeholder for any gathering or activity in the school present them the situation of the through data and winning moments  as well', 'Allocation of time for monitoring of Dep ED PPAs', 'Motivate teachers to aim Outstanding rating if possible', 'Aim for an Outstanding  OPCRF rating if possible', 'Realization  of scheduled   activities in the LAC plan', '>Allocation of budget from MOOE or other source of fund\r\n>Encourage teachers to join credited online free webinar offered by NEAP, SEAMEO & others', 'Allocation of budget from MOOE for PRAISE\r\n>Look for other source of fund', 'Follow up for any discrepancies of salary and benefits of teachers', 'Fairly distribution of teachers workload', 'Properly reported in the BEIS/EBEIS', 'Allocation of budget in the MOOE for minor repair\r\n>Inform the to the concern authority for funding especially  need for bigger  allocation', 'Properly reported in the BEIS/EBEIS\r\n>For construction\r\n', '>Source out of funds for the installation of transformer', '>Allocation of funds for re- installation & rehabilitation computer lab\r\n>Inform the concern Division  personnel for the additional set of computer set and other accessories or DICT package', 'Utilize 100%  the allocated of school MOOE  ', 'Submit 100% school MOOE liquidation on or before due date', 'Aim for VS or Outstanding rating', 0, 108, 12, 57),
(1147, '2026', '128557', 'A small percentage of Grade 3 learners still struggle with transition from mother tongue to English/Filipino reading comprehension. There is also a minor gap in the mastery of basic multiplication and division concepts among at-risk learners, often exacerbated by irregular student attendance.', 'Low mastery levels in critical thinking and problem-solving items under Science and Mathematics.', '', '', 'Limited instructional time for conducting regular remediation sessions', '', 'Focus on urgent teaching tasks leaves minimal time for deep analysis and reflection', '', 'Minor bullying behaviors may still occur but remain unreported or unnoticed due to limited disclosure and monitoring constraints.', 'There is a minor gap in fully monitoring the domestic or home environments of learners, where invisible verbal or emotional distress may occur. Additionally, continuous updates are required to ensure all school stakeholders perfectly understand the fine line between strict classroom discipline and emotional distress.', 'Persistent financial/economic difficulties within families forcing some older learners to engage in seasonal labor or mining work to help their households. Family issues (such as lack of parental guidance due to working parents) and geographic or transportation challenges also contribute to chronic absenteeism, which leads to dropping out.', '', '', '', '', '', 'May not be fully maximized due to limited access to specialized mental health professionals and occasional reluctance of learners or staff to seek support.', 'Absence or inadequacy of physical infrastructure tailored for learners with special needs and PWDs (such as standard concrete ramps with handrails, tactile pathways, and PWD-accessible restroom cubicles) due to budgetary limitations and old school building designs.', 'Full implementation is occasionally affected by limited resources, shifting priorities, and the need to address emerging school concerns.', 'Conflicting schedules of external stakeholders (PTA and LGU) make full and consistent attendance difficult during urgent or unscheduled planning meetings.', '', 'Limited digital literacy among some stakeholders and occasional internet connectivity issues slow down the full implementation of online or digitized frontline service tracking.', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Personnel is still new and needs more improvement.', 'Attainment of higher performance ratings is occasionally influenced by workload demands, time constraints, and the need to address multiple administrative and instructional priorities simultaneously.', 'Schedule conflicts.', '', '', 'Funds sometimes are delayed. ', '', '', '', '', 'Frequent power interruptions disrupt school operations, resulting in unstable internet connectivity and water supply shortages, especially during extremely hot weather conditions.', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Active conduct of regular School LAC sessions focusing on localization and contextualization of lesson exemplars. Teachers utilize available local resources and community contexts to make lessons relatable.', '', 'Strict implementation of daily integration of core values in all lesson plans (Daily Lesson Logs/Exemplars) across all learning areas. Active conduct of values-driven programs (e.g., Homeroom Guidance, EsP initiatives, and peace education modules), supported by visible campus materials promoting the four DepEd Core Values.', '', '', '', '', '', 'Active implementation of the Indigenous Peoples Education (IPEd) framework and/or Madrasah Education Program (MEP), where applicable. Teachers regularly integrate culture-sensitive topics across learning areas, and the school consistently celebrates inclusive cultural milestones (e.g., IP Month, localized cultural festivals) with full community support.', '', '', 'Regular quarterly meetings, updated composition of committee members (including student and PTA representatives), and a clear localized intake system for handling student concerns. Strong administrative support and open communication lines between the school, parents, and local barangay stakeholders ensure immediate action on all child protection matters.', 'Active and organized School DRRM Committee with clearly defined roles for teachers and staff', '', '', '', '', 'Strong leadership guidance from the designated teacher-adviser, enthusiastic student participation, and full administrative support for student-led campus projects.', '', 'Consistent and timely preparation of the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP), coupled with strict monitoring of monthly activities.', 'Active, institutionalized participation of the SGC policy-making body, regular meetings, and strong cooperation between school heads and internal/external stakeholders.', 'Outstanding parental volunteerism, strong support for school projects (e.g., Brigada Eskwela), and open, transparent communication between teachers and parents.', 'Active participation in inter-school learning action cells (LAC sessions), strong linkages with local government units (LGUs), and collaborative community outreach programs.', 'Regular and systematic operationalization of the School Monitoring, Evaluation, and Adjustment (SMEA) mechanism, alongside complete and reliable verification data (MOVs).', 'Institutionalized distribution of Client Satisfaction Measurement (CSM) surveys, transparency in school operations, and prompt action on stakeholder feedback.', '', '', '', 'Active implementation of individual development plans, regular recommendation of personnel to district/division training, and timely processing of promotion and reclassification documents.', 'Active and institutionalized implementation of the school PRAISE committee program, consistent giving of certificates/tokens, and strong stakeholder sponsorship for awards.', '', 'Strict adherence to DepEd guidelines on teacher workloads (e.g., maximum teaching hours), utilization of an equitable school timetable, and an objective distribution of ancillary or administrative designations.', 'Routine conduct of school physical facility inspections (such as pre- and post-disaster assessments), active participation of the school inspectorate team, and utilization of standard facility checklists.', 'Proactive allocation of school MOOE funds for minor repairs, successful resource mobilization through Brigada Eskwela, and active partnerships with the LGU and private stakeholders for facility donations.', '', '', '', 'Systematic and timely preparation of the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP), prompt submission of monthly liquidation reports, and regular alignment meetings with the school head and staff to monitor fund spending against the approved budget.', 'Consistent and meticulous organization of official receipts, timely preparation of disbursement vouchers, and maintaining a strict internal schedule for submitting liquidation documents ahead of the division deadline.', 1, 1, 0, 2, 1, 2, 1, 0, 6, 2, 3, 6, 0, 0, 2, 5, 2, 5, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 6, 6, 1, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 5, 5, 0, 1, 0, 3, 2, 'Intensify targeted, localized reading and numeracy interventions for the remaining at-risk Grade 3 learners. Conduct regular home visitations for students with irregular attendance, and maximize the use of contextualized instructional materials during remedial classes.', 'Institutionalize a structured, data-driven NAT review program starting early in the school year. Enhance classroom assessment methods by incorporating higher-order thinking skills (HOTS) questions.', '', 'Sustain the regular monitoring and quality assurance of teacher-made contextualized learning materials through the School LR Committee.', 'Strengthen partnership with parents through regular dialogues to ensure the consistent attendance of remedial learners, and establish a digital tracking tool to closely monitor the progress of students undergoing intervention.', 'Sustain the seamless integration of peace education and DepEd core values in daily teaching practices. Enhance the school-home partnership by sharing value-focused materials with parents during PTA general assemblies to ensure character development is supported and reinforced at home.', 'Conduct a specialized School LAC session focused on data-driven instruction and the interpretation of item analysis results. Streamline the reporting timeline to ensure findings are immediately used to adjust subsequent lesson objectives, and institutionalize a simplified tracking system for least-mastered skills across all grade levels.', '', 'Strengthen the student-led peer mediation groups to help resolve minor conflicts early, and increase teacher presence/monitoring in corridors and common areas during recess and dismissal times.', 'Conduct annual refresher seminars on Child Protection Policies and Positive Discipline for all teaching and non-teaching personnel. Strengthen information campaigns for parents regarding positive parenting, and optimize the referral system to ensure any external signs of learner distress are immediately addressed by the guidance coordinator or proper authorities.', 'Maximize the utilization of Alternative Delivery Modes (ADM) to accommodate students facing unique family or financial situations, and coordinate with local barangay officials/4Ps coordinators to provide external support for at-risk families.', 'Sustain the regular conduct of culture-sensitive activities and strengthen collaboration with community elders/tribal leaders during school planning. Continue providing technical assistance to teachers on the localized contextualization of learning materials to ensure that respect for diversity remains deeply embedded in daily classroom instruction.', '', '', 'Sustain the regular operational rhythm and meetings of the Child Protection Committee. Enhance the capability of members by participating in advanced division-led child protection webinars, and digitize the committee’s information campaigns to make safety resources and reporting channels more accessible to students and parents alike.', 'Allocate a dedicated portion of the school\'s annual budget (MOOE) specifically for the regular maintenance, check-up, and procurement of emergency response and first-aid supplies.', 'Establish a clear, localized Mental Health Referral Pathway workflow; maximize partnership with the Division Office guidance coordinators for scheduled school visits; and integrate routine, brief wellness checks or psychosocial support activities into regular faculty and homeroom meetings.', 'Allocate a portion of the school physical facilities maintenance fund (MOOE) for basic accessibility modifications (e.g., constructing minor ramps); include PWD-friendly facility upgrades in the regular School Improvement Plan (SIP) for potential DepEd custom-building funding; and coordinate with the LGU or stakeholders/partners for donations of specialized learning/structural materials.', 'Integrate the school\'s strategic goals and SIP/AIP targets into the orientation phase for newly hired personnel and regular faculty meetings to ensure all staff members are consistently moving toward the same institutional targets.', 'Establish a fixed, year-round calendar for quarterly meetings ahead of time and maximize group chats or digital tools for quicker coordination.', 'Sustain the active status of the student government by providing continuous leadership training and ensuring smooth transition turnovers during annual elections.', 'Provide simplified, alternative offline or SMS-based communication channels alongside digital systems, and maintain clear, printed visual guides at the school\'s physical frontline desk.', 'Sustain the quarterly internal reviews of the implementation plan to ensure all programs and target schedules remain on track and adapt immediately to changing school needs.', 'Maintain the high level of functionality of the SGC through continuous advocacy of its roles and ensuring active stakeholder engagement in school policy implementation.', 'Sustain the strong partnership by holding regular, collaborative general assemblies and continuously recognizing active PTA officers and members for their contributions.', 'Sustain and expand existing partnerships through continuous benchmarking activities, signing of updated Memorandums of Agreement (MOA), and active involvement in community-led developmental programs.', 'Sustain the strict timeline for quarterly SMEA presentations to immediately identify intervention areas and continuously improve school performance outcomes.', 'Conduct regular mid-year IPCRF tracking and coaching sessions to ensure systematic electronic portfolio management and timely verification of targets.', 'Integrate the school\'s strategic goals and SIP/AIP targets into the orientation phase for newly hired personnel and regular faculty meetings.', 'Utilize electronic post-LAC monitoring trackers and tap Master Teachers to conduct brief, supportive mentoring during regular class observation periods.', 'Sustain support for professional growth by systematically tracking training hours, providing technical assistance on portfolio preparation, and mentoring personnel for career advancement.', 'Sustain and upscale the localized rewards system by exploring more diverse award categories and ensuring a stable funding source or partner support for annual recognition events.', 'Establish an internal, proactive monthly checklist for personnel document submissions and coordinate immediate electronic follow-ups with the division payroll unit to resolve discrepancies quickly.', 'Sustain fair distribution by reviewing teacher assignments and loads before the start of each school year, keeping open lines of communication for feedback during faculty adjustments.', 'Sustain the quarterly inspection timeline and institutionalize a preventative maintenance log to catch minor facility repair needs early before they worsen.', 'Sustain facility development initiatives by continuously updating the school\'s physical improvement plan and maximizing stakeholder coordination to secure funding for major infrastructure upgrades.', '', 'Coordinate with local service providers for bandwidth upgrades, explore alternative backup internet options, and allocate a portion of the maintenance fund to install secondary water storage tanks.', '', 'Sustain the high utilization rate by maintaining a strict, proactive monthly procurement timeline and continuing to update liquidation documents immediately after every school expenditure.', 'Sustain the 100% compliance rate by continuing to digitalize financial record-keeping and checking receipts immediately upon purchase to ensure prompt liquidation every month.', 'Sustain high satisfaction levels by continuously improving front-line service delivery, maintaining open communication channels, and addressing feedback from evaluation results immediately.', 1, 108, 12, 57),
