.', 'Conduct regular quarterly inspections with documented reports.\r\n\r\nRequest technical assistance from DepEd engineers and LGU.\r\n\r\nEstablish a monitoring logbook for minor repairs and follow-ups.', 'Strengthen resource mobilization through LGU and private partners.\r\n\r\nPrioritize projects in the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).\r\n\r\nAdopt transparent monitoring and evaluation frameworks for improvements.', 'Request additional book donations and ICT equipment.\r\n\r\nExpand library space through minor renovations.\r\n\r\nConduct regular literacy and reading programs to maximize library use.', 'equest installation of backup generator and water storage tanks.\r\n\r\nCoordinate with service providers for priority restoration during outages.\r\n\r\nStrengthen ICT support through DepEd and LGU initiatives.', 'Request additional ICT equipment through DepEd and LGU projects.\r\n\r\nEstablish a maintenance plan with ICT-trained staff.\r\n\r\nExplore partnerships with private organizations for computer donations.', 'Strengthen financial monitoring and reporting systems.\r\n\r\nConduct regular orientation for staff on allowable MOOE expenditures.\r\n\r\nEnsure timely submission of procurement requests.', 'Conduct capacity-building training for finance staff on liquidation procedures.\r\n\r\nAdopt digital tools for faster documentation and reporting.\r\n\r\nMaintain a checklist system to ensure completeness of liquidation documents.', 'egular reporting of school performance, programs, and accomplishments and  strong culture of shared responsibility and participatory decision-making ', 1, 124, 12, 57),
(1149, '2026', '204016', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Periodic delay in the submission and consolidation of item analysis results due to heavy teacher workloads, slowing down immediate instructional adjustments.', '', '', '', '', 'Limited instructional references and specialized localized templates designed explicitly for integrating contextualized culture-sensitivity across all learning subjects.', '', '', '', '', '', 'Absence of standard PWD infrastructure (such as access ramps with handrails, tactile pathways, and specialized PWD comfort rooms) due to historical fiscal limitations', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Minor delays or inconsistencies in gathering feedback from external partners due to non-digital/manual survey distribution methods.', '', '', '', '', '', 'Prompt and accurate preparation, consolidation, and online submission of personnel operational documents by the school\'s administrative', '', '', '', 'Absence of a dedicated library room or physical facility due to limited available classroom space and standard budgetary allocations for standalone library structures.', 'Inconsistent or slow internet connectivity caused by geographic/provider signal limitations, occasionally disrupting online administrative workflows or digital lessons. Water suppply is also limited  with insufficient volume and sometimes  intermittent availability  that affects daily operations and hygiene practice. ', 'Complete lack of a computer room and zero working computers or laptops available for our pupils and teachers to use.', '', '', 'Consistent implementation of the ELLN (Early Language, Literacy, and Numeracy) program, regular conduct of remedial and enhancement reading sessions, and active parental involvement in home-based reading.', 'Strategic conduct of intensive NAT diagnostic tests and review sessions, utilization of test-banking, and heavy integration of 21st-century critical thinking skills across core subject areas.', '', 'Active participation of teachers in LAC sessions focused on contextualization and localization; availability of local community resources to integrate into the lessons.', 'Institutionalized implementation of reading programs (e.g., ARAL PROGRAM, ELLN) and targeted remediation schedules; data-driven identification of struggling learners.', 'Strong integration of Maka-Diyos, Maka-Tao, Makakalikasan, and Makabansa in daily lesson logs (DLL/MATATAG Exemplars); active school-wide advocacy campaigns and values-driven student activities.', '', '', 'Consistent implementation of the Child Protection Policy (CPP), active operations of the School Child Protection Committee (CPC), and regular anti-bullying awareness campaigns during assemblies.', 'High teacher awareness of legal child protections (e.g., RA 7610), localized psycho-social orientation sessions for personnel, and a transparent, protective school environment.', 'Early identification of Students-at-Risk of Dropping Out (SARDOs) paired with effective home visitation practices and localized feeding programs.', '', 'Flexible learning delivery setups, active mapping of out-of-school youths (OSYs) within the community, and dedicated tracking schemes tailored for vulnerable learners.', '', 'Complete composition of committee members, quarterly regular meetings, visible posting of anti-bullying materials, and rapid handling of student concerns.', 'Updated Hazard Mapping, systemic conduct of quarterly nationwide simultaneous earthquake and drills, and a well-coordinated School DRRM Team.', 'Active institutionalization of psychological first aid during regular classes, dedicated mental wellness hours (e.g., Guidance or Homeroom intervals), and supportive peer-groups.', '', 'Collaborative development of the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) involving internal and external stakeholders; alignment with DepEd\'s strategic directions.', 'Active engagement and representation from the School Governing Council (SGC), PTA officials, LGU/BLGU partners, and school head leadership in decision-making processes.', 'Successful conduct of democratic and automated/orderly student elections, active leadership training for elected pupil leaders, and implementation of student-led school programs', 'Digitization of basic transaction inquiries, establishment of clear Citizen\'s Charter postings, and systematic setup of customer feedback mechanisms or help desks during peak periods.', 'Consistent preparation and approval of the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) tied closely to the school\'s fiscal tracking and monthly resource allocations.', 'Active participation of diverse stakeholder representatives ( youth, and civil society) in policy-recommendation processes and regular shared leadership initiatives.', 'Strong, harmonious partnership with General PTA and Homeroom PTA officers, visible transparency in managing localized projects, and robust parent attendance during school assemblies.', 'Active participation in district-level learning cells (LAC networks), inter-school resource/knowledge sharing, and extensive community linkages for programs like Brigada Eskwela.', 'Functional School Monitoring, Evaluation, and Adjustment (SMEA) team conducting regular reviews and data-driven adjustments of school initiatives.', '', 'Objective alignment of individual targets with the school\'s master plans, paired with systematic, periodic mentoring and technical coaching by the school head.', 'Outstanding teamwork and data-driven management tracking systems that ensure all key result areas (KRAs) of the school office are successfully met.', 'Utilization of the Electronic Self-Assessment Tool (e-SAT) results to directly design relevant, highly targeted monthly school LAC session topics.', 'Proactive dissemination of promotion openings, alongside immediate institutional assistance with tracking and documentation needs.', 'Consistent implementation of institutional PRAISE programs during year-end or milestone events.', 'Prompt, accurate, and early submission of the school\'s monthly payroll documents, ', 'Strict adherence to standard DepEd guidelines on instructional teaching hours; collaborative development of the school master schedule involving all faculty members during pre-opening planning.', 'Active and functional School DRRM team conducting routine quarterly inspections using standard DepEd facility checklists.', 'Strong resource-mobilization initiatives through Brigada Eskwela and continuous project collaboration with the General PTA and local stakeholders.', '', '', '', 'Transparent, systematic implementation of the approved Annual Implementation Plan (AIP), coupled with meticulous and compliant liquidations handled by the school head and finance team.', 'Submitting our liquefaction papers on time every month and keeping our receipts and records well-organized.', 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 2, 1, 0, 2, 2, 1, 6, 1, 0, 2, 5, 6, 5, 2, 4, 2, 3, 2, 4, 6, 6, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Sustain the regular conduct of focused learning interventions, continuous monitoring of student progress via ELLN assessment tools, and provisioning of localized reading materials.', 'Institutionalize the early implementation of NAT reviewers, continuously capacitate teachers on constructing analytical test items, and maintain data-driven remediation based on diagnostic results.', '', 'Sustain and continuous updating of the inventory of contextualized learning materials across all grade levels; share best practices during LAC sessions.', 'Sustain the implementation of structured remediation schedules; maximize the use of interactive learning tools and localized intervention modules to further reduce learning gaps.', 'Sustain the consistent integration of peace education and DepEd core values in all learning areas; document and feature exemplary student behaviors or values-driven initiatives.', 'Institutionalize a strict timeline and designated \"Data Days\" immediately following quarterly exams to finalize item analysis, ensuring prompt remediation or modification of teaching strategies.', '', 'Sustain the rigorous monitoring by the CPC, regular integration of positive discipline concepts in homeroom guidance, and maintenance of anonymous reporting channels.Sustain the rigorous monitoring by the CPC, regular integration of positive discipline concepts in homeroom guidance, and maintenance of anonymous reporting channels.', 'Sustain absolute zero-tolerance policies through continued legal re-orientation for old and new staff, and reinforce active stakeholder partnership for student welfare outside school walls.', 'Sustain real-time monitoring of chronic absenteeism through the tracking system and establish early, supportive intervention and tracking loops with parents.', 'Organically integrate culture-sensitive themes into quarterly school activities and host dedicated LAC sessions on culturally responsive teaching methods to ensure every class incorporates inclusive perspectives.', 'Sustain community mapping initiatives before enrollment periods and ensure continuous adjustments to flexible delivery models to keep these learners fully engaged.', '', 'Sustain functional operations by holding regular quarterly case reviews, updating the pupil registry, and conducting brief refresher orientations for old and new members.', 'Sustain regular hazard check-ups across school buildings, continually update response equipment, and enforce routine safety drills for all learners and personnel.', 'Sustain open advocacy programs for mental wellness, strengthen the referral pipeline to specialized guidance personnel, and continue fostering safe space initiatives across classrooms.', 'Formally integrate PWD facility updates into the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP); actively lobby for infrastructure subsidies from the LGU (Local Government Unit) through the Special Education Fund (SEF) while partnering with stakeholder donors to install basic transitional accessibility ramps.', 'Sustain data-driven planning processes through regular mid-year and year-end reviews of targets, and ensure the active participation of the planning team in continuous improvement projects.', 'Sustain strong institutional ties with community leaders through quarterly assemblies, regular transparency reporting, and collaborative planning for school-community welfare.', 'Sustain the youth leadership development pipeline by providing continuous mentorship from the SPG/SSG adviser and allocating ample avenues for student voices in school program reviews.', 'Sustain and continuously update digital channels for stakeholder queries (e.g., official school social media page or tracking systems) to reduce processing wait times and further optimize public service.', 'Sustain continuous alignment between the operationalized activities and the school budget, ensuring a quarterly assessment of targets achieved versus planned outcomes.', 'Sustain functional operations through scheduled quarterly council assemblies, collaborative policymaking, and clear communication of school performance reports to stakeholders.', 'Sustain regular accountability mechanisms, maintain an open-door communication policy for parent feedback, and co-manage infrastructure or student welfare initiatives.', 'Expanding the partner network to continuously support learner development programs.', 'Sustain the systematic conduct of  SMEA conferences and continue utilizing standardized evaluation tools to track program efficiency.', 'Sustain 100% submission compliance and high-quality ratings by providing clear guidance on portfolio evidence collection early in the school year cycle.', 'Sustain the exceptional operational standard through proactive monitoring of quarterly performance benchmarks and collaborative target tracking.', 'Sustain the regular conduct of responsive LAC sessions, focusing deeply on emergent areas like curriculum delivery variations and innovative diagnostic assessment tools.', 'Sustain full career growth support by systematically mapping professional qualifications and mentoring eligible personnel to advance through the career path structures.', 'Sustain the implementation of localized appreciation incentives, timely issuance of certificates of recognition.', 'Sustain this high operational standard by continuously conducting proactive monthly checking of personnel folders and maintaining immediate coordination pipelines with the Division payroll unit.', 'Sustain transparent and balanced loading distribution by using an automated tracking template for ancillaries, ensuring equitable division of non-teaching assignments across the staff.', 'Sustain the scheduled seasonal structural integrity assessments and ensure rapid logging of minor repair needs into the school\'s maintenance calendar.', 'Sustain proactive multi-stakeholder partnerships to continuously fund minor classroom repairs, beautification, and safety enhancements.', 'Maximize and upgrade classroom-based reading centers while actively proposing a dedicated space or reading hub in the next School Improvement Plan (SIP) revision, supplemented by stakeholder book-donation drives.', 'Allocate a portion of school maintenance funds to: upgrade to a more reliable network provider option or higher-bandwidth plan for smoother digital integration; and implement water conservation measures, explore alternative water sources, or develop a storage/distribution system to address limited and intermittent water supply.', 'Request the Division Office for complete DCP packages and computer allocations, while including a space for an ICT room in our next SIP/AIP.', 'Sustain 100% timely and compliant MOOE utilization by following rigid quarterly procurement workflows aligned explicitly with immediate school operational demands.', 'Sustain this by checking our receipts early and staying on track with our monthly submission schedule.', 'Transition to a hybrid feedback mechanism (combining physical drop-boxes with digital/QR-code-based evaluation forms) during major school events to maximize stakeholder survey participation.', 0, 116, 12, 57);
