(1157, '2026', '137062', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Some learners are hesitant to report bullying incidents due to fear or peer pressure. Limited awareness among some parents regarding anti-bullying policies.', 'Limited awareness of child protection protocols among some stakeholders. Difficulty in identifying unreported cases.', '', '', '', '', 'Limited participation of some committee members during meetings and activities.', 'Limited emergency equipment and insufficient funds for disaster preparedness activities.', 'Limited availability of mental health professionals and counseling resources.', 'Limited infrastructure and assistive devices for learners with disabilities.', '', '', '', '', '', 'Limited participation of some members due to conflicting schedules and commitments.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Limited availability of updated books, references, and reading materials.', '', '', '', '', 'Strong support from teachers and school administrators. Implementation of reading and numeracy intervention programs. Availability of learning resources and active participation of stakeholders. Conduct of remediation and enrichment activities.', 'Strong instructional leadership and continuous monitoring of learner performance. Active implementation of intervention, remediation, and enrichment programs in all learning areas. Teachers demonstrate competence in integrating 21st century skills such as critical thinking, communication, collaboration, and creativity in classroom instruction. Availability of learning resources, NAT reviewers, and technology-assisted learning materials. Strong partnership among school personnel, parents, and stakeholders supports learners’ academic achievement. Regular conduct of assessments, coaching, and data-driven instruction contributes to improved NAT performance.', '', 'Teachers demonstrate creativity and commitment in preparing learner-centered materials. Support from school heads and collaboration among teachers through LAC sessions enhance material development. Availability of reference materials and community-based resources supports contextualization.', 'Strong teacher commitment in conducting remediation and intervention classes. School support through reading and numeracy programs enhances learner improvement. Regular assessment and monitoring help identify learner needs.', 'Teachers consistently integrate peace education and DepEd core values across learning areas and classroom activities. Supportive school environment promotes positive discipline and learner engagement.', 'Teachers regularly conduct test item analysis to identify learners’ strengths, weaknesses, and least mastered competencies. School heads and academic coordinators provide support through monitoring, technical assistance, and data-driven planning. Collaboration among teachers during LAC sessions and meetings strengthens assessment practices and instructional adjustments. Availability of assessment tools, learner performance data, and intervention programs supports continuous improvement of teaching and learning processes.', '', '', '', 'Intervention programs, home visitation, and strong monitoring systems help retain learners in school.', 'Teachers integrate cultural awareness and inclusivity in school programs and classroom instruction.', 'Flexible learning modalities and support from ALS implementers and stakeholders improve access to education', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong leadership and collaborative planning among school personnel and stakeholders. Availability of school data and planning tools supports strategic planning.', 'Active collaboration between school personnel, parents, and community partners strengthens planning and decision-making', 'Active student participation and support from teacher-advisers enhance leadership development and school involvement.', 'School personnel demonstrate initiative and creativity in improving stakeholder services and communication systems.', 'Clear implementation guidelines and regular monitoring ensure alignment of programs with school goals.', '', 'Active PTA officers and supportive parents contribute to school programs and learner welfare.', 'Strong linkages and partnerships with stakeholders and neighboring schools support resource sharing and program implementation.', 'Regular monitoring and evaluation activities help improve program implementation and accountability.', 'School personnel maintain professionalism, transparency, and responsiveness in delivering services.', 'Personnel demonstrate commitment, competence, and accountability in accomplishing assigned tasks.', 'Strong teamwork and effective leadership contribute to the achievement of school performance targets.', 'Teachers actively participate in professional learning and collaborative sharing sessions.', 'Supportive school leadership encourages professional growth and career advancement.', 'Recognition activities boost morale, motivation, and productivity among personnel.', 'Coordination with concerned offices ensures proper facilitation of salaries and benefits.', 'School administration ensures equitable distribution of tasks and considers teachers’ competencies and capacities', 'Regular inspection and monitoring by school personnel help identify facility needs and ensure safety.', 'Support from stakeholders, LGUs, and community partners contributes to school improvement projects.', '', '', '', 'Proper financial planning and monitoring ensure effective utilization of MOOE funds.', 'School personnel demonstrate accountability and compliance with financial management procedures.', 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 6, 6, 3, 6, 6, 0, 2, 5, 6, 6, 1, 1, 6, 5, 1, 2, 6, 2, 1, 6, 1, 2, 3, 2, 3, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 0, 0, 3, 3, 'Strengthen reading and numeracy intervention programs. Conduct regular monitoring and assessment of learner progress. Provide additional instructional materials and learning resources. Enhance parental involvement through orientation and home learning support. Continue teacher capability-building activities and remediation programs.', 'Sustain and strengthen intervention and enrichment programs for Grade 6, 10, and 12 learners. Continue teacher training and professional development on 21st century teaching strategies and assessment practices. Provide updated instructional materials, ICT resources, and NAT review materials. Enhance stakeholder and parental involvement in supporting learner achievement. Conduct regular monitoring, evaluation, and feedback mechanisms to ensure continuous improvement in NAT performance and mastery of core learning competencies.', '', 'Continue capacity-building activities on contextualization and localization of learning materials. Provide sufficient instructional resources and printing support. Strengthen collaboration and sharing of best practices among teachers.', 'Sustain remediation and intervention programs with regular monitoring of learner progress. Provide additional remediation materials and ICT resources. Strengthen parental involvement to support learner attendance and participation.', 'Continue integration of peace education and core values in daily instruction and school activities. Conduct values formation programs and learner-centered activities that promote positive behavior and citizenship.', 'Sustain the regular conduct of test item analysis and data-driven instruction. Strengthen teachers’ assessment literacy through continuous professional development and training. Utilize results of item analysis in planning remediation, enrichment, and instructional strategies. Continue collaborative review and monitoring of learner performance to improve achievement outcomes.', '', 'Sustain anti-bullying campaigns, strengthen reporting mechanisms, and continue values formation activities.', 'Continue orientation and advocacy on child protection policies and reporting procedures.', 'Strengthen learner support programs, parental engagement, and attendance monitoring systems.', 'Continue conducting inclusive and culture-sensitive activities that promote diversity and respect.', 'Expand learning access programs and strengthen partnerships to support disadvantaged learners and OSYs.', '', 'Sustain regular meetings, capacity-building activities, and monitoring of child protection initiatives.', 'Strengthen disaster preparedness programs and provide additional DRRM resources and equipment.', 'Continue mental wellness programs, strengthen referral systems, and conduct regular wellness activities.', 'Improve accessibility facilities and provide additional resources and support for learners with special needs and disabilities.', 'Strengthen participatory planning and regular review of the strategic plan to ensure responsiveness to school needs.', 'Sustain stakeholder engagement through regular consultations and planning meetings.', 'Conduct leadership training and provide support for student-led programs and initiatives.', 'Improve ICT facilities and strengthen digital systems for efficient frontline services.', 'Strengthen monitoring and resource allocation to ensure timely implementation of planned activities.', 'Enhance communication and engagement strategies to encourage active SGC participation.', 'Strengthen parental involvement through regular communication and flexible engagement activities.', 'Expand partnerships and strengthen collaboration mechanisms for sustainable support and resource mobilization.', 'Strengthen monitoring systems, documentation, and timely submission of reports.', 'Provide continuous coaching, mentoring, and workload management support for personnel', 'Sustain collaborative practices and strengthen resource mobilization to support school performance goals.', 'Continue conducting relevant and needs-based LAC and professional development activities.', 'Strengthen access to training, seminars, and scholarship opportunities for personnel.', 'Sustain recognition programs and seek stakeholder support for incentives and awards.', 'Strengthen coordination and timely submission of required documents for compensation processing.', 'Review workload distribution regularly and provide support mechanisms to maintain teacher welfare and efficiency.', 'Continue regular inspection and preventive maintenance of school facilities and infrastructure.', 'Strengthen resource mobilization and partnerships to support infrastructure improvement initiatives.', 'Provide additional and updated learning resources and strengthen library improvement programs', '', '', 'Strengthen financial planning, procurement processes, and monitoring of fund utilization.', 'Ensure timely submission of liquidation reports and strengthen financial management practices and documentation.', 'Continue improving stakeholder relations and feedback mechanisms to enhance satisfaction.', 0, 25, 12, 60),
(1158, '2026', '128480', 'Some learners still have difficulty in reading comprehension, vocabulary development, and solving basic numeracy problems. Irregular attendance, limited parental support, and insufficient learning materials also affect learners’ performance. Remediation time is sometimes limited due to overlapping school activities.', 'Some learners demonstrate low mastery in higher-order thinking skills, reading comprehension, scientific inquiry, and problem-solving competencies assessed in the NAT. Limited access to updated instructional materials, inadequate review time, absenteeism, and varied learner readiness also affect performance. Teachers encounter challenges in addressing diverse learning needs due to large class sizes and limited intervention resources.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Limited physical infrastructure such as ramps, handrails, and accessible comfort rooms; insufficient assistive learning materials and resources for learners with disabilities; constrained budget for facility upgrades.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Limited availability of updated reading materials and insufficient modernization of the library room, including lack of ICT-based resources and improved learning spaces.', '', 'Limited number of functional computers and outdated units; insufficient ICT equipment for all learners; and need for improved maintenance and upgrading of laboratory facilities.', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong collaboration and sharing of ideas among teachers in preparing learning materials suited to learners’ needs.', 'Teachers show commitment and patience in providing continuous remediation and learner support.', 'Teachers consistently model and integrate peace education and DepEd core values during classroom instruction and school activities.', 'Teachers regularly collaborate in analyzing assessment results to improve instruction and learner performance.', '', 'Strong implementation of child protection policies and positive discipline practices by teachers and school personnel.', 'Strong adherence to Child Protection Policy and active involvement of teachers, parents, and school personnel in safeguarding learners', 'Strong monitoring and support system provided by teachers, parents, and school stakeholders for at-risk learners.', 'Teachers and school personnel actively promote respect for diverse cultures and traditions through inclusive school activities.', 'Strong commitment of teachers in providing flexible and inclusive learning opportunities for diverse learners.', '', 'Active and committed Child Protection Committee members who consistently respond to child safety concerns and school reports.', 'Strong commitment of the school DRRM team in implementing preparedness activities such as drills, hazard mapping, and safety orientations.', 'Teachers and school personnel actively provide emotional support and referrals, fostering a caring and supportive school environment.', '', 'Strong leadership of school management ensures collaborative planning and regular involvement of stakeholders in developing the school strategic plan.', 'Active collaboration and strong commitment of school leaders, teachers, and community stakeholders in participatory planning activities', 'Active guidance and mentoring provided by advisers and school administrators in strengthening student leadership and participation.', 'Strong initiative of school personnel in adopting simple, practical, and user-friendly innovations to improve service delivery.', 'Strong leadership and clear assignment of roles ensure that the implementation plan is consistently carried out and monitored.', 'Active participation and strong commitment of stakeholders in supporting school programs and decision-making through the SGC.', 'Active involvement and cooperation of parents and teachers in supporting school programs and learner development through the PTA.', 'Strong existing relationships and active engagement of stakeholders and partner schools in collaborative initiatives.', 'Strong culture of data-driven decision-making and regular conduct of monitoring activities by school leaders and teachers.', 'Strong commitment of the school to provide responsive, transparent, and quality services to internal and external stakeholders.', 'Strong commitment, professionalism, and dedication of school personnel in performing their duties and meeting performance targets.', 'Strong leadership and coordinated efforts of school personnel in ensuring timely and quality accomplishment of office targets.', 'Strong collaborative culture among teachers and school leaders in identifying and addressing instructional needs through LAC sessions.', 'Strong support of school leadership in encouraging and endorsing personnel participation in professional development activities.', 'Strong appreciation culture within the school that values and acknowledges personnel achievements through simple but meaningful recognition activities.', '', 'Strong collaborative planning among school leaders and teachers in assigning duties based on capacity, expertise, and availability.', 'Regular conduct of safety inspections and maintenance checks led by school management and designated personnel.', 'Strong initiative of school leadership in prioritizing facility improvement through planning, proposal development, and stakeholder engagement.', '', 'Strong coordination with utility providers and proactive school maintenance efforts ensure continuous availability of basic services.', '', 'Strong financial planning and budget monitoring by school leadership ensure proper and timely use of MOOE resources.', 'Strong adherence of school personnel to financial policies and proper documentation procedures ensures complete and accurate liquidation of funds.', 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 6, 1, 0, 6, 6, 1, 6, 6, 0, 6, 5, 6, 5, 2, 6, 6, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 1, 5, 3, 3, 1, 5, 3, 3, 'Strengthen reading and numeracy intervention programs, provide additional learning resources, intensify parental involvement, and conduct regular assessment and monitoring of learners needing remediation. Allocate more time for targeted intervention activities and seek support from stakeholders for instructional materials.', 'Strengthen intervention and remediation programs; intensify NAT review sessions and coaching activities; provide additional ICT resources and learning materials; conduct continuous teacher training on innovative teaching strategies and 21st century skills integration; strengthen parental involvement through regular communication and orientation; improve monitoring of learner progress using data-driven interventions; seek stakeholder support for resource augmentation.', '', 'Continue collaborative planning and material-sharing practices among teachers; allocate scheduled time for preparation of contextualized materials; and maximize available local resources to make learning materials more relevant, practical, and learner-friendly.', 'Sustain regular remediation activities through flexible schedules and differentiated learning approaches; strengthen coordination with parents to improve learner attendance and participation; and continuously monitor learner progress to address specific learning needs effectively.', 'Continue strengthening values integration across learning areas and school programs; encourage positive behavior through recognition and guidance; and sustain collaboration with parents and stakeholders in promoting peace, respect, and responsible citizenship among learners.', 'Continue conducting regular test item analysis after assessments; strengthen collaborative data-sharing and planning among teachers; and use analysis results to guide remediation, enrichment, and improvement of teaching strategies.', '', 'Continue strengthening awareness programs on child protection and positive behavior; sustain close monitoring and guidance of learners; and maintain active coordination among teachers, parents, and stakeholders to ensure a safe and supportive school environment.', 'Sustain implementation of child protection programs and awareness activities; continue strengthening coordination with parents and stakeholders; and maintain a safe, supportive, and learner-friendly school environment through regular monitoring and guidance.', 'Continue early identification and monitoring of at-risk learners; strengthen home visitation and parental engagement activities; and sustain intervention programs and stakeholder support to encourage learners to stay in school and complete their education.', 'Continue integrating culture-sensitive practices in school programs and classroom activities; strengthen participation of parents and community members; and maximize available local resources to promote inclusivity, respect, and appreciation of cultural diversity.', 'Continue offering flexible learning arrangements and alternative delivery modes; strengthen coordination with families and community leaders to encourage consistent participation; and sustain learner support mechanisms to help OSYs and adult learners complete their basic education.', '', 'Sustain regular monitoring and meetings of the Child Protection Committee; strengthen coordination among members through clear roles and communication; and continue capacity-building activities to ensure effective and timely response to child protection concerns. ', 'Continue regular conduct of disaster preparedness drills and safety orientations; strengthen coordination with LGU and stakeholders for resource support; and ensure periodic review and updating of the DRRM plan to maintain school safety and readiness.', 'Continue strengthening school-based mental health and psychosocial support activities; enhance coordination with trained guidance personnel and external partners; and promote a safe, non-judgmental environment where learners are encouraged to seek help when needed.