(1176, '2026', '128532', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '- No dedicated or appropriate room/space for a library\r\n- Insufficient number of books, references, and reading materials\r\n- Lack of proper furniture, shelves, and equipment\r\n- No designated or trained librarian or library-in-charge\r\n- No system for classification, cataloging, or lending of materials\r\n- Limited budget for library development and maintenance\r\n- No regular reading programs or activities to promote usage', '', '- Lack of computer units, equipment, and peripherals\r\n- No dedicated or suitable room/space to serve as laboratory\r\n- Insufficient funds to purchase equipment and furniture\r\n- Lack of trained personnel to manage and maintain the facility\r\n- No stable internet connection to support computer-based activities\r\n- Lack of necessary software and learning applications', '', '', '*Use of contextualized and localized learning materials suited to learners’ background- *Regular monitoring and assessment (formative and summative) to track progress- \r\n*Collaborative planning among teachers to align lessons with proficiency standards- Support from school head and allocation of time for remediation/enrichment', '- Integration of 21st century skills (critical thinking, communication, collaboration, creativity) in daily lessons\r\n- Conduct of regular practice tests and reviews using NAT-style questions\r\n- Data-driven instruction: using previous test results to address weak areas\r\n- Teachers attend trainings/workshops on teaching strategies for HOTS', '', '- School policy/guideline mandating use of contextualized and localized materials\r\n- Regular workshops and LAC sessions on material development\r\n- Resource sharing and collaboration among teachers\r\n- Support from school head in allocating time and small funds for materials', '- Early identification of gaps through regular assessments\r\n- Scheduled remediation hours built into the school calendar\r\n- Use of diagnostic tests to target specific needs\r\n- Teachers are trained in intervention strategies\r\n- Support from parents/guardians in encouraging attendance', '- Values Education is a core subject, and integration is part of lesson plan requirements\r\n- Teachers are oriented on DepEd core values (Maka-Diyos, Makatao, Makakalikasan, Makabansa)\r\n- School activities (flag ceremony, programs) reinforce values\r\n- Support from school in promoting peace and values education', '- Required practice in school and division policies\r\n- Standardized form/template provided by the school\r\n- Sharing of results and insights during LAC sessions\r\n- School head monitors and guides the process\r\n- Teachers are trained on how to conduct analysis', '', '- Strict implementation of child protection policies and anti-bullying guidelines\r\n- Regular orientation and education on respect, empathy, and positive behavior\r\n- Active involvement of teachers, parents, and student leaders in monitoring\r\n- Safe reporting mechanisms for learners to report incidents\r\n- Immediate intervention and counseling for involved parties', '- Strict adherence to DepEd Child Protection Policy\r\n- Functional Child Protection Committee that oversees prevention and response\r\n- Regular training for teachers and staff on child protection and reporting protocols\r\n- Collaboration with community leaders and LGUs for support\r\n- Clear procedures for reporting, investigating, and addressing abuse cases\r\n', '- Implementation of intervention programs (scholarships, feeding programs, educational assistance)\r\n- Regular monitoring and tracking of learners’ attendance and performance\r\n- Guidance and counseling services for at-risk learners\r\n- Home visitation programs by teachers and guidance counselors\r\n- Flexible learning options and alternative delivery modes when needed', '- Integration of cultural sensitivity in lesson plans and school programs\r\n- Involvement of community members and cultural leaders in planning activities\r\n- Use of local materials and traditions to design relevant activities\r\n- Regular training for teachers on cultural awareness and sensitivity\r\n- Recognition and celebration of diverse cultures and traditions', '', '', '- Formal establishment of the committee with defined roles and functions\r\n- Regular training and capacity building for committee members\r\n- Strict implementation of child protection policies and guidelines\r\n- Regular meetings and planning sessions to address concerns\r\n- Collaboration with child welfare agencies and authorities', '- Formal development and adoption of a comprehensive DRRM plan\r\n- Regular orientation and training on disaster preparedness and response\r\n- Conduct of periodic drills and simulations (earthquake, fire, flood, etc.)\r\n- Allocation of resources and facilities for disaster management\r\n- Collaboration with local disaster risk reduction offices and agencies', '- Integration of mental health and wellness in school policies and programs\r\n- Provision of guidance and counseling services\r\n- Regular activities and programs to promote positive mental health\r\n- Training for teachers and staff on recognizing and addressing mental health concerns\r\n- Collaboration with mental health professionals and agencies', '- Compliance with DepEd standards and guidelines for inclusive facilities\r\n- Planning and budgeting for accessibility upgrades and improvements\r\n- Collaboration with LGUs and community partners for support\r\n- Regular inspection and maintenance of facilities\r\n- Designated areas and spaces for learners with special needs', '- Strong leadership commitment and guidance\r\n- Systematic planning process involving key stakeholders\r\n- Alignment with DepEd mandates and educational goals\r\n- Regular review and monitoring of plan implementation\r\n- Clear documentation and communication of the plan', '- - Formal establishment of the team with defined roles and functions\r\n- Regular scheduled meetings and clear communication channels\r\n- Support and guidance from school and community leaders\r\n- Shared decision-making and collaborative approach\r\n- Recognition of team contributions', '- School support and guidance from advisers\r\n- Training / Meeting and development for student leaders\r\n- Opportunities for student voice and representation in school affairs\r\n- Access to resources and support for student projects\r\n- Recognition of student achievements and contributions', '- Support and encouragement from school leadership\r\n- Regular feedback and input from stakeholders\r\n- Willingness to adapt and improve existing processes\r\n- Collaboration with stakeholders to identify new solutions\r\n- Access to information, training, and best practices', '- Detailed planning framework linking strategic goals to operational tasks\r\n- Clear assignment of roles and responsibilities\r\n- Regular monitoring and review mechanisms\r\n- Leadership commitment and guidance\r\n- Documentation of progress and achievements', '- Legal basis and defined mandates for the SGC\r\n- Regular scheduled meetings and clear communication channels\r\n- Support and guidance from school leadership and division offices\r\n- Collaborative and inclusive decision-making\r\n- Capacity building for council members', '- Strong partnership and shared vision between school and parents\r\n- Regular communication and consultation channels\r\n- Support from school leadership and teachers\r\n- Recognition of parent contributions and achievements\r\n- Shared goals for learner development and school improvement', '- Open communication and trust among partners\r\n- Shared vision and common objectives for education improvement\r\n- Leadership support and encouragement for partnerships\r\n- Formal agreements (MOAs) to guide collaboration\r\n- Mutual benefits and value for all stakeholders', '- Clear indicators and success metrics for each program/activity\r\n- Standardized monitoring and evaluation tools\r\n- Trained personnel to conduct assessments\r\n- Leadership support for data-driven decision-making\r\n- Feedback mechanisms to gather input from stakeholders', '- Responsive and learner-centered services\r\n- Open communication channels to gather feedback\r\n- Continuous improvement practices based on input\r\n- Transparency in operations and decision-making\r\n- Commitment to quality and excellence', '- Clear DepEd guidelines, memoranda, and standardized IPCR forms and tools\r\n- Regular orientation, training, and re-orientation on performance management\r\n- Supportive supervision, coaching, and mentoring by school leaders\r\n- Transparent and objective evaluation processes and criteria\r\n- Regular monitoring and feedback mechanisms for performance improvement\r\n- Recognition and appreciation of high performance and achievements', '- Collaborative planning and target-setting aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)\r\n- Clear definition of roles, functions, and deliverables per office/unit\r\n- Regular coordination meetings, consultations, and information sharing\r\n- Strong leadership guidance and support from school management\r\n- Standardized monitoring and reporting systems for office performance\r\n- Shared commitment to school goals and culture of teamwork\r\n- Transparent evaluation and reporting processes', '- Clear policy for conducting regular LAC sessions\r\n- Needs assessment conducted to determine topics\r\n- Availability of competent LAC facilitators\r\n- Support from school leadership in providing time and resources\r\n- Collaboration among teachers in sharing best practices', '- Clear DepEd policies on promotion and professional development\r\n- Availability of various training programs (in-service, online, external)\r\n- Support for personnel to attend relevant courses and seminars\r\n- Fair and transparent promotion processes\r\n- Encouragement for higher education and advanced studies', ' Existing awards and recognition programs (e.g., PRAISE, service awards)\r\n- Support from school leadership in promoting positive work environment\r\n- Active participation of committees in selecting awardees\r\n- Open communication about criteria for recognition\r\n- Celebration of milestones during school events', '- Efficient and well-organized school administrative processes\r\n- Dedicated personnel for handling payroll and financial matters\r\n- Strong coordination with the Division Office and other relevant agencies\r\n- Clear communication of policies and requirements to personnel\r\n- Use of proper documentation and record-keeping	Institutional, Financial, Technical	- Ensure timely submission and accurate preparation of all payroll-related documents\r\n- Conduct regular checks and audits of salary and allowance computations\r\n- Establish a clear communication protocol for updates or issues regarding compensation\r\n- Provide personnel with clear information on their payslips and deductions\r\n- Continuously train administrative staff on updated financial policies and procedures\r\n35. Teacher workload is distributed fairly and equitably\r\nDegree of Manifestation: Always Manifested\r\nTable\r\nConcerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) Encountered	Facilitating Factors for Indicators with always manifested	Category	Proposed Resolutions/Commitment\r\n- Ensuring equitable distribution of teaching loads and extra-curricular duties\r\n- Balancing academic and administrative tasks\r\n- Managing teachers’ preferences and specializations\r\n- Preventing burnout due to excessive workload	- Clear guidelines and policies for workload distribution\r\n- Collaborative planning and assignment of duties\r\n- Regular consultation with teachers regarding their workload\r\n- Support from school leadership in balancing tasks\r\n- Recognition of varied contributions (academic, administrative, etc.)	Institutional, Technical, Social	- Develop a transparent system for assigning teaching loads and ancillary duties\r\n- Conduct regular consultations with teachers to assess workload balance\r\n- Provide support (e.g., administrative assistance) to ease non-teaching loads\r\n- Implement a fair rotation system for demanding tasks\r\n- Recognize and address concerns about workload promptly and equitably\r\n', '- Clear guidelines and policies for workload distribution\r\n- Collaborative planning and assignment of duties\r\n- Regular consultation with teachers regarding their workload\r\n- Support from school leadership in balancing tasks\r\n- Recognition of varied contributions (academic, administrative, etc.)', '- Designated inspection committee/team in place\r\n- Inspection activities included in the school’s annual plan\r\n- Clear checklists and guidelines for assessment\r\n- Strong support and supervision from school administration\r\n- Involvement of stakeholders (PTA, SGC) in monitoring\r\n- Findings used as basis for repair and improvement planning', '- Improvement projects based on results of needs assessment and inspection\r\n- Portion of MOOE allocated for maintenance and improvement\r\n- Financial, material, or labor support from LGU, NGOs, and private partners\r\n- Well-prepared project proposals and work plans\r\n- Active community and parental participation\r\n- School leadership prioritizes facility development	Infrastructure, Financial, Institutional, Technical	- Include all facility improvement projects in the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)\r\n- Maximize funding sources: MOOE, special grants, and community donations\r\n- Simplify procurement procedures while complying with government rules\r\n- Engage skilled parents, alumni, or community members for technical support\r\n- Ensure all projects adhere to DepEd infrastructure standards\r\n- Monitor project progress regularly and report updates to stakeholders\r\n- Document completed works for reference and reporting\r\n38. The school has a functional library\r\nDegree of Manifestation: Not Yet Manifested\r\nTable\r\nConcerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) Encountered	Facilitating Factors for Indicators with always manifested	Category	Proposed Resolutions/Commitment\r\n- No dedicated or appropriate room/space for a library\r\n- Insufficient number of books, references, and reading materials\r\n- Lack of proper furniture, shelves, and equipment\r\n- No designated or trained librarian or library-in-charge\r\n- No system for classification, cataloging, or lending of materials\r\n- Limited budget for library development and maintenance\r\n- No regular reading programs or activities to promote usage	- Strong recognition of the library’s importance for learning\r\n- Availability of vacant rooms/spaces that can be converted\r\n- Willingness of stakeholders to donate books or funds\r\n- DepEd policies and guidelines supporting school libraries\r\n- Teachers willing to manage or assist in the facility\r\n- Community interest in literacy and reading development	Infrastructure, Financial, Institutional, Technical	- Identify, prepare, and designate a suitable room for the library\r\n- Develop and submit project proposals to secure funds and resources\r\n- Launch book donation campaigns among parents, alumni, and partners\r\n- Include library development in the school’s AIP and budget proposals\r\n- Designate a teacher-in-charge and arrange training on library management\r\n- Adopt a simple classification, recording, and lending system\r\n- Start small reading activities and programs to build a reading culture\r\n- Coordinate with the Division Office for technical assistance and standards\r\n', '', '- Proper installation and regular maintenance of facilities\r\n- Allocation of budget specifically for utilities and repairs\r\n- Established contracts/agreements with service providers\r\n- Regular monitoring and reporting of facility status\r\n- Support from school administration and stakeholders for maintenance', '', '- Proper financial planning and budgeting based on school needs\r\n- Trained and competent school head, bookkeeper, and property custodian\r\n- Strict adherence to DepEd financial guidelines and circulars\r\n- Regular monitoring and updating of expenditure status\r\n- Timely submission and processing of requests for obligations', '- Trained and dedicated finance/administrative personnel\r\n- Standardized forms, templates, and filing systems\r\n- Clear guidelines and checklists for liquidation\r\n- Regular review and validation of documents before submission\r\n- Guidance and support from Division Office finance teams', 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 2, 2, 2, 'Develop and produce additional localized learning resources (storybooks, worksheets, games)- Conduct parent orientations/seminars on supporting learning at home- Allocate specific time for individualized coaching for struggling learners- Strengthen collaboration between Grade 1–3 teachers for continuity of skills', '- Create a school-wide NAT review program with scheduled sessions\r\n- Compile and share standardized review materials across grade levels\r\n- Conduct motivational activities/guidance to build learners’ confidence\r\n- Align lesson plans and assessments to NAT competencies and standards', '', '- Schedule regular collaborative planning days for material development\r\n- Allocate small budget for production and reproduction of materials', '- Implement small-group remediation for better focus\r\n- Develop a standardized tracking form to monitor progress of each learner\r\n- Create a bank of remediation activities and worksheets\r\n- Conduct parent meetings to explain importance of remediation and seek cooperation\r\n', '- Conduct LAC sessions on creative integration of peace education and values\r\n- 