\r\n- Home visitation programs by teachers and guidance counselors\r\n- Flexible learning options and alternative delivery modes when needed	Social, Financial, Institutional	- Expand assistance programs (scholarships, school supplies, transportation support) for needy learners\r\n- Conduct home visits to identify and address root causes of drop-out\r\n- Provide academic remediation and enrichment activities to improve learner performance\r\n- Strengthen guidance and counseling services to support learners’ well-being\r\n- Coordinate with community groups and LGUs for additional support and resources\r\n12. The school conducts culture-sensitive activities\r\nDegree of Manifestation: Always Manifested\r\nTable\r\nConcerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) Encountered	Facilitating Factors for Indicators with always manifested	Category	Proposed Resolutions/Commitment\r\n- Limited resources and materials for activities that reflect diverse cultures\r\n- Need to ensure activities are inclusive and respectful of all cultural groups\r\n- Balancing cultural practices with school policies and standards\r\n- Ensuring all learners feel represented and valued in school activities	- Integration of cultural sensitivity in lesson plans and school programs\r\n- Involvement of community members and cultural leaders in planning activities\r\n- Use of local materials and traditions to design relevant activities\r\n- Regular training for teachers on cultural awareness and sensitivity\r\n- Recognition and celebration of diverse cultures and traditions	Social, Institutional	- Plan and implement activities that highlight local and national cultures, as well as global diversity\r\n- Invite community members to share their cultural practices and traditions\r\n- Develop learning materials that reflect different cultural backgrounds\r\n- Organize cultural festivals, shows, and events to promote understanding and unity\r\n- Evaluate activities regularly to ensure they are inclusi