prove learning outcomes\r\n- Evaluate collaboration efforts regularly to ensure effectiveness and sustainability\r\n', '- Review and update the DRRM plan regularly based on local hazards and needs\r\n- Conduct regular information sessions and training for learners, staff, and parents\r\n- Perform scheduled drills and exercises to test the effectiveness of the plan\r\n- Ensure facilities and resources are prepared for emergency situations\r\n- Establish clear communication and coordination channels during disasters', '- Conduct information campaigns and seminars on mental health and well-being\r\n- Establish accessible guidance and counseling services for learners\r\n- Organize activities that promote stress management, emotional intelligence, and social connection\r\n- Train teachers and staff to identify and support learners with mental health needs\r\n- Develop a referral system to connect learners with professional support when needed\r\n18. The school has special education - and PWD-friendly facilities\r\nDegree of Manifestation: Always Manifested\r\nTable\r\nConcerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) Encountered	Facilitating Factors for Indicators with always manifested	Category	Proposed Resolutions/Commitment\r\n- Limited accessibility features (ramps, handrails, wide doorways) in some areas\r\n- Need for specialized facilities and equipment for learners with special needs\r\n- Challenges in maintaining and upgrading facilities to meet standards\r\n- Ensuring all facilities are safe and usable for PWD learners	- Compliance with DepEd standards and guidelines for inclusive facilities\r\n- Planning and budgeting for accessibility upgrades and improvements\r\n- Collaboration with LGUs and community partners for support\r\n- Regular inspection and maintenance of facilities\r\n- Designated areas and spaces for learners with special needs	Infrastructure, Institutional	- Conduct an assessment of facilities to identify areas for improvement\r\n- Allocate budget and resources to install accessibility features (ramps, handrails, etc.)\r\n- Provide specialized equipment and materials for SPED and PWD learners\r\n- Maintain and upgrade facilities regularly to ensure safety and usability\r\n- Ensure all areas of the school are accessible and welcoming for all learners\r\nOverarching Statement: School and Community Collaboration\r\nTable\r\nConcerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) Encountered	Facilitating Factors for Indicators with always manifested	Category	Proposed Resolutions/Commitment\r\n- Need to strengthen partnership and coordination between school and community stakeholders\r\n- Limited participation of community members in school programs and activities\r\n- Challenges in aligning community resources with school goals and needs\r\n- Ensuring equitable access to resources and opportunities for all learners	- Active engagement of community leaders, parents, and organizations in school governance and programs\r\n- Regular consultation and dialogue between school and community\r\n- Sharing of resources, knowledge, and skills for the benefit of learners\r\n- Collaborative planning and implementation of activities that support learner-centered education\r\n- Shared responsibility for creating a safe, healthy, and supportive learning environment	Social, Institutional, Political	- Establish formal partnerships and memoranda of agreement (MOA) with community groups and agencies\r\n- Organize regular community assemblies and meetings to discuss school needs and priorities\r\n- Involve community members in teaching, mentoring, and resource sharing\r\n- Develop joint programs and projects that address learner needs and improve learning outcomes\r\n- Evaluate collaboration efforts regularly to ensure effectiveness and sustainability\r\n', '- Conduct an assessment of facilities to identify areas for improvement\r\n- Allocate budget and resources to install accessibility features (ramps, handrails, etc.)\r\n- Provide specialized equipment and materials for SPED and PWD learners\r\n- Maintain and upgrade facilities regularly to ensure safety and usability\r\n- Ensure all areas of the school are accessible and welcoming for all learners', '- Conduct comprehensive needs assessments to guide plan development\r\n- Involve teachers, staff, parents, and community leaders in planning\r\n- Review and revise the plan annually to reflect new goals and challenges\r\n- Allocate resources and assign responsibilities for plan implementation\r\n- Communicate the plan clearly to all stakeholders to ensure ownership', '- Conduct orientation and capacity-building activities for team members\r\n- Encourage greater participation from diverse community groups\r\n- Set clear timelines and work plans for team activities\r\n- Establish mechanisms to monitor and evaluate team outputs\r\n- Strengthen linkages between the team and school management', '- Provide leadership training and workshops for student officers\r\n- Create platforms for students to share ideas and concerns\r\n- Allocate small funds or resources for student-led activities\r\n- Guide students in planning and implementing projects\r\n- Recognize and celebrate student contributions to school development', '- Conduct surveys and consultations to identify stakeholder needs\r\n- Explore new methods and technologies to improve service delivery\r\n- Train staff and personnel on innovative approaches\r\n- Allocate resources to support new initiatives\r\n- Monitor and evaluate the effectiveness of innovations; sustain successful practices', '- Develop a detailed implementation plan with specific activities, timelines, and responsible persons\r\n- Establish a monitoring system to track progress against targets\r\n- Allocate resources based on priority activities and needs\r\n- Conduct periodic reviews to update plans and address gaps\r\n- Communicate progress to all stakeholders to ensure alignment and support', '- Conduct orientation and training for SGC members on their roles and responsibilities\r\n- Hold regular meetings to discuss school concerns, plans, and policies\r\n- Establish clear procedures for decision-making and documentation\r\n- Promote inclusive participation from all sectors of the school community\r\n- Monitor and evaluate the council’s performance regularly to improve its functions\r\n', '- Organize regular PTA meetings and activities to keep parents informed and engaged\r\n- Provide opportunities for parents to contribute skills, resources, and ideas\r\n- Establish clear mechanisms for collaboration and decision-making\r\n- Recognize and appreciate parent involvement and support\r\n- Align PTA activities with school goals and priorities to ensure relevance and impact', '- Establish formal partnerships and memoranda of agreement (MOAs) with government agencies, NGOs, private sectors, and other schools\r\n- Conduct consultations and meetings to align goals and activities\r\n- Share resources, expertise, and best practices with partners\r\n- Organize joint activities and programs that benefit learners and the school\r\n- Evaluate partnership effectiveness and adjust strategies to strengthen collaboration', '- Collect data regularly through surveys, observations, and records\r\n- Analyze results to identify strengths, gaps, and areas for improvement\r\n- Use evaluation findings to adjust plans, strategies, and activities\r\n- Share results with stakeholders and report progress transparently', '- Refine performance targets to be more specific, measurable, and aligned with actual duties\r\n- Simplify documentation requirements while maintaining compliance\r\n- Conduct regular workshops to clarify indicators and ensure common understanding\r\n- Establish a system for continuous feedback and coaching throughout the rating period\r\n- Link performance results to professional development and career advancement plans\r\n- Create a clear schedule and checklist for timely submission of requirements\r\n', '- Conduct annual planning workshops to fully align OPCR targets with school strategic objectives\r\n- Strengthen inter-office coordination mechanisms and regular progress meetings\r\n- Develop clear work plans and timelines for each office/unit\r\n- Implement a centralized monitoring system to track collective and individual outputs\r\n- Allocate resources based on office priorities and needs\r\n- Conduct regular reviews and adjustments of plans to address challenges\r\n- Document and share best practices among offices to sustain good performance', '- Conduct a comprehensive training needs analysis for all personnel\r\n- Develop a LAC plan based on identified needs and priorities\r\n- Provide training for LAC facilitators and leaders\r\n- Document and disseminate best practices and outputs from LAC sessions\r\n- Allocate dedicated time slots in the school calendar for LACs', '- Create a comprehensive professional development plan linked to IPCR results and school needs\r\n- Seek funding opportunities for personnel training and scholarships\r\n- Develop mentorship programs for career growth and promotion\r\n- Provide clear information on promotion criteria and opportunities\r\n- Establish a system for tracking and recognizing personnel’s professional growth', '- Establish clear and transparent criteria for recognizing various achievements\r\n- Develop a diverse range of recognition (certificates, non-monetary rewards, special mention)\r\n- Conduct regular awards ceremonies or appreciation events\r\n- Create a system for personnel to nominate colleagues for recognition\r\n- Promote a culture of appreciation and celebration of successes', '- Ensure timely submission and accurate preparation of all payroll-related documents\r\n- Conduct regular checks and audits of salary and allowance computations\r\n- Establish a clear communication protocol for updates or issues regarding compensation\r\n- Provide personnel with clear information on their payslips and deductions\r\n- Continuously train administrative staff on updated financial policies and procedures\r\n35. Teacher workload is distributed fairly and equitably\r\nDegree of Manifestation: Always Manifested\r\nTable\r\nConcerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) Encountered	Facilitating Factors for Indicators with always manifested	Category	Proposed Resolutions/Commitment\r\n- Ensuring equitable distribution of teaching loads and extra-curricular duties\r\n- Balancing academic and administrative tasks\r\n- Managing teachers’ preferences and specializations\r\n- Preventing burnout due to excessive workload	- Clear guidelines and policies for workload distribution\r\n- Collaborative planning and assignment of duties\r\n- Regular consultation with teachers regarding their workload\r\n- Support from school leadership in balancing tasks\r\n- Recognition of varied contributions (academic, administrative, etc.)	Institutional, Technical, Social	- Develop a transparent system for assigning teaching loads and ancillary duties\r\n- Conduct regular consultations with teachers to assess workload balance\r\n- Provide support (e.g., administrative assistance) to ease non-teaching loads\r\n- Implement a fair rotation system for demanding tasks\r\n- Recognize and address concerns about workload promptly and equitably\r\n', ' Develop a transparent system for assigning teaching loads and ancillary duties\r\n- Conduct regular consultations with teachers to assess workload balance\r\n- Provide support (e.g., administrative assistance) to ease non-teaching loads\r\n- Implement a fair rotation system for demanding tasks\r\n- Recognize and address concerns about workload promptly and equitably', '- Develop and implement standardized inspection forms and documentation\r\n- Set fixed, regular schedules (monthly/quarterly) for inspections\r\n- Provide basic tools and simple training to the inspection team\r\n- Maintain a logbook/tracker for defects, repairs, and completed works\r\n- Conduct follow-up checks after repairs to ensure quality\r\n- Share results with stakeholders for transparency', '- Include all facility improvement projects in the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)\r\n- Maximize funding sources: MOOE, special grants, and community donations\r\n- Simplify procurement procedures while complying with government rules\r\n- Engage skilled parents, alumni, or community members for technical support\r\n- Ensure all projects adhere to DepEd infrastructure standards\r\n- Monitor project progress regularly and report updates to stakeholders\r\n- Document completed works for reference and reporting\r\n', '- Identify, prepare, and designate a suitable room for the library\r\n- Develop and submit project proposals to secure funds and resources\r\n- Launch book donation campaigns among parents, alumni, and partners\r\n- Include library development in the school’s AIP and budget proposals\r\n- Designate a teacher-in-charge and arrange training on library management\r\n- Adopt a simple classification, recording, and lending system\r\n- Start small reading activities and programs to build a reading culture\r\n- Coordinate with the Division Office for technical assistance and standards\r\n', '- Implement a regular preventive maintenance schedule for all facilities\r\n- Allocate sufficient funds for utility payments and immediate repairs\r\n- Coordinate closely with service providers for faster response to issues\r\n- Upgrade internet connection to meet digital learning needs\r\n- Conduct regular inspection to identify problems before they worsen\r\n40. The school has a functional computer laboratory/classroom\r\nDegree of Manifestation: Not Yet Manifested\r\nTable\r\nConcerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) Encountered	Facilitating Factors for Indicators with always manifested	Category	Proposed Resolutions/Commitment\r\n- Lack of computer units, equipment, and peripherals\r\n- No dedicated or suitable room/space to serve as laboratory\r\n- Insufficient funds to purchase equipment and furniture\r\n- Lack of trained personnel to manage and maintain the facility\r\n- No stable internet connection to support computer-based activities\r\n- Lack of necessary software and learning applications	- Strong need and demand for digital learning resources\r\n- Support and interest from stakeholders, LGU, and private partners\r\n- Availability of programs and funding opportunities from DepEd\r\n- Willingness of teachers to undergo training on ICT integration\r\n- Existing plans and proposals to establish the facility	Infrastructure, Financial, Technical, Institutional	- Develop and submit a project proposal to secure funding\r\n- Seek donations, sponsorships, or partnerships from LGU, NGOs, and private sectors\r\n- Identify and prepare a suitable room/space for the laboratory\r\n- Include ICT needs in the school’s Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)\r\n- Conduct training for teachers on basic computer operations and maintenance\r\n- Apply for DepEd ICT programs and grants\r\n41. The school achieves a 72-100% utilization rate of its Maintenance and Other Operating Expenses (MOOE)\r\nDegree of Manifestation: Always Manifested\r\nTable\r\nConcerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) Encountered	Facilitating Factors for Indicators with always manifested	Category	Proposed Resolutions/Commitment\r\n- Strict procurement and bidding procedures that delay spending\r\n- Delays in the release of funds from higher offices\r\n- Unforeseen or emergency expenses that alter planned allocations\r\n- Complex documentation and requirements for expenditures\r\n- Limited flexibility in reallocating funds between different budget items	- Proper financial planning and budgeting based on school needs\r\n- Trained and competent school head, bookkeeper, and property custodian\r\n- Strict adherence to DepEd financial guidelines and circulars\r\n- Regular monitoring and updating of expenditure status\r\n- Timely submission and processing of requests for obligations	Financial, Institutional, Technical	- Conduct thorough needs assessment before preparing the budget\r\n- Simplify and streamline procurement processes within allowed guidelines\r\n- Maintain a detailed monitoring tool to track utilization vs. plan\r\n- Attend regular trainings on financial management and MOOE utilization\r\n- Coordinate closely with the Division Office for timely release and guidance\r\n42. The school liquidates 100% of its utilized MOOE\r\nDegree of Manifestation: Always Manifested\r\nTable\r\nConcerns, Issues, Gaps, Problems and Bottlenecks (CIGPBs) Encountered	Facilitating Factors for Indicators with always manifested	Category	Proposed Resolutions/Commitment\r\n- High volume and complexity of supporting documents required\r\n- Strict compliance and reconciliation requirements\r\n- Challenges in retrieving and organizing receipts and records\r\n- Risk of errors or discrepancies in reporting\r\n- Limited time and personnel dedicated to documentation	- Trained and dedicated finance/administrative personnel\r\n- Standardized forms, templates, and filing systems\r\n- Clear guidelines and checklists for liquidation\r\n- Regular review and validation of documents before submission\r\n- Guidance and support from Division Office finance teams	Financial, Institutional, Technical	- Implement a systematic filing and recording system from the start of transactions\r\n- Use standard checklists to ensure complete and accurate documents\r\n- Conduct regular internal reviews before submission\r\n- Provide continuous training for staff on liquidation rules and updates\r\n- Submit reports early to allow time for corrections or adjustments\r\n', '- Strong need and demand for digital learning resources\r\n- Support and interest from stakeholders, LGU, and private partners\r\n- Availability of programs and funding opportunities from DepEd\r\n- Willingness of teachers to undergo training on ICT integration\r\n- Existing plans and proposals to establish the facility', '- Conduct thorough needs assessment before preparing the budget\r\n- Simplify and streamline procurement processes within allowed guidelines\r\n- Maintain a detailed monitoring tool to track utilization vs. plan\r\n- Attend regular trainings on financial management and MOOE utilization\r\n- Coordinate closely with the Division Office for timely release and guidance', '- Implement a systematic filing and recording system from the start of transactions\r\n- Use standard checklists to ensure complete and accurate documents\r\n- Conduct regular internal reviews before submission\r\n- Provide continuous training for staff on liquidation rules and updates\r\n- Submit reports early to allow time for corrections or adjustments', '- Conduct regular satisfaction surveys and feedback sessions with stakeholders\r\n- Address concerns and suggestions promptly to improve services\r\n- Communicate school achievements, improvements, and plans to stakeholders\r\n- Maintain consistent quality in programs, activities, and services\r\n- Recognize and appreciate stakeholder contributions to school success', 1, 108, 12, 57);
INSERT INTO `sbm_ta` (`id`, `fy`, `school_id`, `q1`, `q2`, `q3`, `q4`, `q5`, `q6`, `q7`, `q8`, `q9`, `q10`, `q11`, `q12`, `q13`, `q14`, `q15`, `q16`, `q17`, `q18`, `q19`, `q20`, `q21`, `q22`, `q23`, `q24`, `q25`, `q26`, `q27`, `q28`, `q29`, `q30`, `q31`, `q32`, `q33`, `q34`, `q35`, `q36`, `q37`, `q38`, `q39`, `q40`, `q41`, `q42`, `qq1`, `qq2`, `qq3`, `qq4`, `qq5`, `qq6`, `qq7`, `qq8`, `qq9`, `qq10`, `qq11`, `qq12`, `qq13`, `qq14`, `qq15`, `qq16`, `qq17`, `qq18`, `qq19`, `qq20`, `qq21`, `qq22`, `qq23`, `qq24`, `qq25`, `qq26`, `qq27`, `qq28`, `qq29`, `qq30`, `qq31`, `qq32`, `qq33`, `qq34`, `qq35`, `qq36`, `qq37`, `qq38`, `qq39`, `qq40`, `qq41`, `qq42`, `a1`, `a2`, `a3`, `a4`, `a5`, `a6`, `a7`, `a8`, `a9`, `a10`, `a11`, `a12`, `a13`, `a14`, `a15`, `a16`, `a17`, `a18`, `a19`, `a20`, `a21`, `a22`, `a23`, `a24`, `a25`, `a26`, `a27`, `a28`, `a29`, `a30`, `a31`, `a32`, `a33`, `a34`, `a35`, `a36`, `a37`, `a38`, `a39`, `a40`, `a41`, `a42`, `f1`, `f2`, `f3`, `f4`, `f5`, `f6`, `f7`, `f8`, `f9`, `f10`, `f11`, `f12`, `f13`, `f14`, `f15`, `f16`, `f17`, `f18`, `f19`, `f20`, `f21`, `f22`, `f23`, `f24`, `f25`, `f26`, `f27`, `f29`, `f30`, `f31`, `f32`, `f33`, `f34`, `f35`, `f36`, `f37`, `f38`, `f39`, `f40`, `f41`, `f42`, `f28`, `stat`, `district`, `region`, `division`) VALUES
(1177, '2026', '304213', 'N/A', 'No available NAT results and insufficient baseline data to determine learner proficiency levels.', 'Limited enrollment and lack of available data on ALS completers and certification results.', '', '', '', 'Limited time and technical skills in conducting in-depth item analysis among some teachers.', '', 'Occasional bullying incidents among learners and limited monitoring outside classrooms.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Manifested\r\nLimited availability of mental health professionals and counseling resources.', 'Insufficient PWD-friendly facilities such as ramps, accessible comfort rooms, and learning spaces.', '', 'Irregular participation of some stakeholders and scheduling conflicts during planning activities.', '', 'Limited technological resources, insufficient training, and lack of modernized systems for service delivery.', '', '', '', '', 'Insufficient monitoring tools and limited time for evaluation activities', 'Low stakeholder feedback and limited satisfaction survey participation', '', '', 'Limited time and resources for training and professional development activities', 'Insufficient funding and limited opportunities for advanced training', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Teachers are skilled in contextualization, availability of local resources, and administrative support.', 'Teachers’ commitment, regular assessment results, and support from parents and stakeholders.', 'Strong school culture, teacher commitment, and integration of values across learning areas.', '', 'Strong partnership with local stakeholders and industries supporting work immersion and skills training.', '', 'Functional Child Protection Committee, active stakeholder support, and implementation of child protection policies.', 'Strong learner monitoring system, home visitation, and stakeholder support.', 'Supportive school community, active participation of learners, and integration of cultural awareness activities.', 'Availability of ALS programs, community support, and inclusive learning opportunities.', 'Dedicated ALS teachers/facilitators and support from stakeholders and local community.', 'Active committee members, clear policies, and strong administrative support.', 'Active DRRM team, regular drills, and support from LGU and stakeholders.', '', '', 'Strong leadership, stakeholder involvement, and alignment of school programs with DepEd goals and priorities.', '', 'Active student leaders, supportive school administration, and participation of learners in leadership activities.', '', 'Strong leadership support, clear implementation guidelines, active participation of stakeholders', 'Active collaboration among school officials and community stakeholders', 'Strong support from parents and school administrators', 'Good relationship and cooperation with stakeholders and partner institutions', '', '', 'Strong commitment of teachers and effective performance monitoring system', 'Effective teamwork, proper planning, and administrative support', '', '', 'Positive school culture and supportive administration', 'Efficient coordination with payroll and finance offices', 'Proper workload planning and cooperation among personnel', 'Strong administrative monitoring and regular facility inspection schedules', 'Support from stakeholders and proper planning of improvement projects', 'Active support from school administration and proper library management', 'Regular monitoring and maintenance of utility facilities', 'Availability of ICT support and proper laboratory management', 'Efficient financial management practices and proper budget planning', 'Efficient financial management practices', 0, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, '', 'Conduct diagnostic assessments and implement intervention programs to improve learner readiness for NAT.', 'Strengthen ALS monitoring, encourage community participation, and provide support programs for ALS learners.', 'Sustain development of localized and contextualized learning materials through continuous training and sharing of best practices.', 'Continue remediation programs and strengthen parental involvement and learner monitoring mechanisms.', 'Continue integrating peace education and DepEd core values in daily classroom instruction and school activities.', 'Conduct capability-building activities on test construction and item analysis and institutionalize regular data review sessions.', 'Sustain and expand partnerships with local industries and strengthen work immersion opportunities for learners.', 'Strengthen anti-bullying campaigns, intensify monitoring, and conduct regular awareness and values formation activities.', 'Sustain strict implementation of child protection policies and continue advocacy programs for learners and parents.', 'Continue intervention programs, strengthen learner support mechanisms, and intensify collaboration with parents and community partners.', 'Sustain implementation of inclusive and culture-sensitive programs and strengthen partnerships with cultural groups and stakeholders.', 'Continue providing inclusive education opportunities and strengthen outreach and support services for disadvantaged learners.', 'Sustain ALS implementation and provide additional learning resources and learner support interventions.', 'Continue capacity-building activities and strengthen coordination among stakeholders regarding child protection issues.', 'Sustain disaster preparedness activities and seek additional resources for emergency response equipment and facilities.', 'Strengthen mental wellness programs, conduct regular psychosocial activities, and establish stronger partnerships with health professionals.', 'Prioritize development of PWD-friendly facilities and seek funding assistance from stakeholders, LGUs, and partner organizations.', 'Sustain collaborative strategic planning and regularly review and update plans based on school needs and performance data.', 'Strengthen stakeholder engagement through regular consultations, meetings, and capacity-building activities.', 'Continue leadership development programs and provide support for student-led initiatives and activities.', 'Enhance frontline services through digitalization, capacity-building, and resource mobilization to improve efficiency and accessibility of services.', 'Strengthen monitoring mechanisms and ensure timely submission of implementation reports', 'Conduct regular meetings and enhance communication among council members', 'Encourage greater parent involvement through continuous engagement activities and orientations', 'Sustain partnerships through regular coordination and collaborative programs', 'Improve monitoring and evaluation systems and provide capacity-building activities', 'Continue strengthening performance monitoring and provide coaching and mentoring to personnel', 'Sustain collaborative practices and improve efficiency in report preparation and submission', 'Increase access to relevant trainings and allocate sufficient resources for LAC and L&D activities', 'Strengthen partnerships and seek additional funding for continuous professional development', 'Continue recognition programs and explore additional incentives for outstanding personnel', 'Maintain accurate documentation and strengthen coordination with concerned offices', 'Regularly review workload distribution and ensure equitable assignment of responsibilities', 'Continue regular inspections and strengthen preventive maintenance programs', 'Seek additional funding and strengthen partnerships for infrastructure development', 'Acquire updated books and digital learning resources to improve library services', 'Coordinate with service providers and improve contingency measures for service interruptions', 'Upgrade ICT equipment and provide regular maintenance of computer facilities', 'Sustain proper utilization and strengthen monitoring of MOOE expenditures', 'Continue timely submission of reports and ensure compliance with financial guidelines', 'Strengthen stakeholder engagement, improve feedback mechanisms, and address concerns promptly', 0, 123, 12, 57),
