(1230, '2026', '305778', '', 'Learners continue to demonstrate low proficiency levels in core subjects, particularly in reading comprehension, science, and mathematics, despite remediation efforts.', '', 'Teachers need more time and collaborative opportunities to sustain the quality and updating of contextualized materials.', 'Remediation activities are effective but require stronger learner monitoring and documentation of progress.', 'Integration is practiced but may not yet be consistently measured in terms of learner behavioral outcomes.', 'Teachers have limited technical capacity and time to systematically conduct and interpret test item analysis after assessments.', '', '', '', 'Some learners remain at risk of dropping out due to poverty, family responsibilities, and transportation difficulties.', '', '', '', 'Need for continuous orientation and refresher training on child protection protocols among school personnel and stakeholders.', '', 'Limited access to professional counseling services and specialized mental health resources.', 'Lack of accessible infrastructure such as ramps, handrails, PWD-friendly comfort rooms, and learning spaces for learners with disabilities.', 'Limited stakeholder participation in periodic review and updating of the strategic plan, which may affect responsiveness to emerging school needs.', 'Inconsistent attendance or varying levels of participation among external stakeholders during planning meetings.', '', 'Limited resources and technological tools may constrain the implementation and expansion of innovative service delivery mechanisms.', 'While implementation plans are in place, there is a need to further strengthen alignment between planned activities, timelines, and stakeholder accountability to maximize effectiveness.', 'The School Governance Council has not been fully organized or activated, resulting in limited stakeholder participation in school governance and shared decision-making.', '', '', 'Monitoring and evaluation mechanisms are functional, but documentation and utilization of findings for continuous improvement may still need enhancement', 'Stakeholder satisfaction remains satisfactory, but there is a need to further improve responsiveness to stakeholder feedback to achieve higher satisfaction levels.', '', '', '', '', 'Recognition practices are present but may lack a standardized system for documentation, criteria, and regular scheduling of awards and incentives.', '', '', '', '', 'The school library is either limited in resources, lacks updated reading materials, or is not fully operational due to insufficient space, staffing, or equipment.', '', 'Insufficient number of functional computers, limited ICT equipment, and possible lack of stable internet connectivity restrict student access to digital learning resources.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong implementation of school rules, positive discipline practices, and active monitoring by teachers and school personnel.', 'Effective child safeguarding policies, awareness campaigns, and active coordination with parents and local protection agencies.', '', 'Inclusive school programs that recognize and celebrate learners’ diverse cultural backgrounds and traditions.', 'Strong commitment to inclusive education and flexible learning opportunities for marginalized learners.', '', '', 'Active DRRM committee, regular drills, risk assessments, and preparedness activities.', '', '', '', '', 'Active student leadership, strong teacher-adviser support, and consistent administrative guidance promote effective implementation of student-led programs and initiatives.', '', '', '', 'Strong parental involvement, regular PTA meetings, and active collaboration between parents and school personnel contribute to effective school support systems.', 'Established partnerships with community stakeholders and neighboring schools foster resource sharing, technical support, and collaborative problem-solving.', '', '', 'Strong individual accountability, effective coaching and mentoring, and consistent performance monitoring contribute to high individual performance ratings.', 'Strong leadership, coordinated planning, and effective implementation of school programs support high organizational performance.', 'Regular identification of training needs and active teacher participation ensure relevant professional development activities.', 'Supportive leadership and adherence to DepEd guidelines on promotion and professional growth encourage continuous staff development.', '', 'Efficient coordination with administrative offices and compliance with financial processes ensure timely release of personnel benefits.', 'Clear workload policies and collaborative scheduling among school leadership and teachers support equitable distribution of tasks.', 'Regular monitoring schedules, strong leadership oversight, and coordination among personnel ensure consistent facility inspection.', 'Proactive school leadership and available improvement plans support continuous infrastructure enhancement.', '', 'Established utility systems and coordination with service providers ensure continuous access to basic services.', '', 'Effective budget planning, prioritization of needs, and adherence to DepEd financial guidelines contribute to efficient fund utilization.', 'Strong financial compliance systems and timely documentation ensure complete liquidation of funds.', 0, 1, 0, 1, 2, 6, 1, 0, 2, 6, 6, 6, 6, 0, 2, 1, 6, 5, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 2, 6, 2, 1, 6, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 2, 2, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, '', 'Strengthen targeted intervention programs through data-driven remediation, intensified NAT review sessions, and continuous development of contextualized learning materials aligned with assessed learner needs.', '', 'Sustain Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions focused on collaborative development, sharing, and enhancement of contextualized instructional materials.', 'Strengthen learner progress tracking systems and regularly evaluate remediation outcomes to improve intervention strategies.', 'Develop simple monitoring tools and school activities that assess and reinforce learners’ application of peace education and core values in daily school life.', 'Conduct capacity-building sessions on test construction and item analysis, and institutionalize regular post-assessment data review meetings among teachers.', '', 'Sustain a safe and respectful school environment through continuous values formation, student engagement, and vigilance in reporting and addressing concerns.', 'Continue strict implementation of child protection measures and strengthen advocacy on children’s rights and safety.', 'Sustain and strengthen early warning systems, home visitation programs, and learner support interventions through active coordination with parents and community stakeholders.', 'Maintain and expand culturally responsive activities that promote inclusivity, respect, and community participation.', 'Continue developing accessible learning programs and strengthen outreach efforts to ensure no learner is left behind.', '', 'Conduct regular Child Protection Policy orientations, case simulations, and committee meetings to ensure readiness and responsiveness.', 'Sustain disaster preparedness initiatives, regularly update the DRRM plan, and enhance stakeholder participation in safety programs.', 'Strengthen partnerships with guidance counselors, health professionals, and local agencies, and institutionalize school-based mental wellness activities and referral systems.', 'Prioritize the inclusion of SPED- and PWD-friendly facilities in the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Procurement Plan (APP), and seek support from LGU, DepEd, and external stakeholders for funding and implementation.', 'Strengthen participatory planning by ensuring regular consultation and active engagement of teachers, parents, learners, and community partners in reviewing and refining the school strategic plan.', 'Enhance stakeholder commitment through regular communication, scheduling flexibility, and recognition of contributions to sustain active involvement in school-community planning.', 'Sustain and strengthen student leadership development by providing continuous mentoring, capacity-building activities, and opportunities for meaningful student participation in school governance.', 'Pursue resource mobilization and partnerships while continuously building staff capacity to improve and sustain innovative, accessible, and efficient frontline services.', 'Continuously refine implementation planning processes by assigning clear responsibilities, setting measurable targets, and regularly reviewing progress to ensure strategic goals are achieved efficiently.', 'Organize and officially constitute the School Governance Council through orientation and designation of representatives from key stakeholder groups, and ensure regular meetings and active participation in school planning and monitoring.', 'Sustain and strengthen PTA engagement by promoting inclusive participation, transparent communication, and collaborative initiatives that support learners’ welfare and school improvement.', 'Maintain and expand strategic partnerships through regular engagement, mutual accountability, and collaborative programs that advance educational quality and community development.', 'Strengthen data collection, documentation, and feedback systems to ensure that monitoring results inform timely interventions and evidence-based decision-making.', 'Sustain performance coaching and mentoring systems while strengthening individual target-setting and feedback mechanisms to maintain high performance levels.', 'Maintain strategic alignment of school plans and strengthen collaborative leadership practices to sustain high OPCRF ratings.', 'Continue strengthening needs assessment mechanisms and ensure LAC sessions remain data-driven, collaborative, and aligned with priority learning gaps.', 'Sustain transparent and merit-based promotion systems while encouraging continuous upskilling through structured professional development plans.', 'Strengthen and formalize a school-based rewards and recognition system with clear guidelines, scheduled recognition activities, and documented criteria for fairness and transparency.', 'Maintain efficient financial processing systems and strengthen coordination with relevant offices to ensure uninterrupted and timely compensation.', 'Sustain transparent workload planning and periodically review assignments to ensure fairness, equity, and teacher well-being.', 'Sustain systematic inspection protocols and strengthen reporting mechanisms for timely identification of facility needs and risks.', 'Continue prioritizing infrastructure improvement projects aligned with school development plans and safety standards.', 'Prioritize the establishment and strengthening of a functional library through allocation of MOOE/LGU support, acquisition of updated learning resources, and designation or training of a library focal person.', 'Maintain and regularly upgrade utility systems to ensure uninterrupted and reliable services for teaching and learning.', 'Develop a functional computer laboratory through phased procurement of ICT equipment, strengthen internet connectivity, and seek partnerships or donations from stakeholders and LGUs to support ICT enhancement.', 'Sustain transparent and needs-based budgeting practices to ensure optimal use of MOOE for school priorities.', 'Maintain strict compliance with financial liquidation policies and continue capacity-building on fiscal management.', 'Sustain regular stakeholder feedback mechanisms and implement responsive improvements in school services to increase trust, satisfaction, and engagement.', 1, 122, 12, 57),
