N/A', '', 'Limited number of functional computer units; outdated ICT equipment; insufficient maintenance and technical support; intermittent internet connectivity affecting ICT-based instruction.', '', '', '', 'Teachers continuously conduct remediation, review classes, and intervention programs such as the ARAL Program; school administrators and stakeholders support academic programs and learner development activities.', '', 'Teachers are skilled and collaborative in developing contextualized learning materials; strong support from school heads and stakeholders; availability of ICT resources and sharing of best practices among teachers.', 'Teachers consistently implement remediation and intervention programs such as the ARAL Program; strong commitment of teachers in addressing learners’ needs; support from school administration, parents, and stakeholders in sustaining intervention activities.', 'Teachers consistently integrate peace education and DepEd core values in classroom instruction and school activities; active support from school administrators and stakeholders in promoting positive values and inclusive learning environment.', '', '', '', '', 'Teachers conduct regular monitoring, home visitation, and learner intervention activities; strong support from parents, stakeholders, and school programs promoting learner retention and participation.', '', 'The school implements inclusive education programs and alternative learning opportunities; teachers and stakeholders actively support learner participation and access to education.', '', 'Active participation of committee members, school personnel, parents, and stakeholders; regular implementation of child protection policies, orientations, and learner welfare activities.', 'Active participation of school DRRM coordinators, teachers, learners, and stakeholders; regular conduct of disaster preparedness drills and orientations; support from local government units and community partners.', 'Teachers, guidance coordina