(1243, '2026', '128670', '', '1. learners struggle with higher-order thinking skills (HOTS) and complex problem-solving items.\r\n2. Limited access to NAT parallel review materials and digitized mock tests.\r\n3. Learning gaps carried over from previous grade levels in core subjects like Mathematics and Science.\r\n', 'No ALS enrollment in the school', '', '', '', '', '', 'Minimal cases of verbal bullying occurring during unstructured times (recess/dismissal).', 'Limited awareness among some stakeholders regarding the specific legal definition of child abuse.', 'Financial difficulties and domestic responsibilities among learners in high-risk categories.', '', '', 'No dedicated classroom or learning space available specifically for ALS sessions.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Lack of formal orientation for newly designated members on their roles and functions.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '1. Lack of a dedicated room or space specifically allocated for a library.\r\n2. Insufficient updated reference materials, books, and digital learning resources.\r\n3. Absence of designated Librarian or trained Library Hub coordinator.\r\n', '', '1. Insufficient number of functional computer units to accommodate the student population.\r\n2. lack of dedicated, air-conditioned space to secure and maintain IT equipment.\r\n3. Limited electrical load capacity to support a full laboratory setup.\r\n', '', '', '1. Consistent implementation of the Early Language, Literacy, and Numeracy (ELLN) program.\r\n2. Strategic use of Mother Tongue-Based Multilingual Education (MTB-MLE) materials.\r\n3. Regular conduct of school-based Learning Action Cells (SLAC) focusing on reading strategies.\r\n', '', '', '1. Contextualized learning activity sheets (LAS) or localized modules.\r\n2. Lesson Plans (DLL/DLP) showing integration of local heritage or community context.\r\n3. Teacher-made instruction materials using indigenous or locally available resources.\r\n4. Digitized contextualized materials uploaded in the school’s shared drive.\r\n', '1. Remedial Activity Plans and session logs.\r\n2. Pre-assessment and Post-assessment results of learners under remediation.\r\n3. Individual learner’s Progress Report (specifically for reading and numeracy).\r\n4. Attendance sheets for after-school or pull-out intervention sessions.\r\n', '1. Daily lesson logs (DLL) or lesson plans (DLP) showing integration of Maka-Diyos, Makatao, Makakalikasan, and Makabansa.\r\n2. Documentation of school-based celebrations (e.g. Values Education Month, Peace Day).\r\n3. Student output/ portfolios related to values-based lessons.\r\n', '1. Records of Item Analysis for Quarterly examinations.\r\n2. Minutes of LAC sessions discussing least learned competencies.\r\n3. Remedial plans or modified lesson plans based on examination results.\r\n', '', '', '', '', 'Inclusive school climate and celebrate of diverse cultural events (e.g. Indigenous Peoples Month).', 'Active coordination with the Barangay Council for learner mapping and advocacy.', '', 'Active involvement of the PTA and a functional student grievance mechanism.', 'Consistent conduct of quarterly earthquake and fire drills and a dedicated DRRM coordinator.', 'Presence of a functional Guidance Office and regular mental health awareness advocacies for staff and pupils.', 'Availability of basic PWD ramps and accessibility features in the school gymnasium and main building.', 'Availability of a comprehensive School Improvement Plan (SIP) aligned with division goals.', 'Strong representation and commitment from the School Planning Team (SPT) and local leaders.', 'Active participation of student leaders in school governance and decision-making processes.', 'Encouragement of an innovative culture among school personnel to improve service delivery.', 'Alignment of the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) with the School improvement Plan (SIP)', '', 'Strong cooperation from the General PTA officers in school programs and activities.', 'Attended Regular Coordinator meetings with the Barangay Council and NGOs for School improvement projects.', 'Conducted quarterly Project monitoring and Evaluation (PMER) sessions to adjust implementation strategies.', 'Administered annual client satisfaction surveys to parents, students, and community partners to gauge the quality of school services. Analyzed feedback to identify areas for service delivery improvement.', 'Regular technical assistance on IPCRF preparation and portfolio building.', 'Strong alignment of school targets with division goals and strategic plan.', 'Conducts monthly School Learning Action Cells (SLAC) based on consolidated teacher development needs.', 'Facilitates coaching and mentoring sessions for teachers to support career progression and professional growth.', 'Implements a school-based Rewards and Recognition (R&R) program that honors teachers for years of service and outstanding performance.', '*strong coordination between the school’s administrative/ clerical staff and the division personnel and finance sections.\r\n*Proactive preparation and immediate tracking of personnel documents (eg. Promotional papers, NOSI, NOSA).\r\n', '*Utilization of a collaborative scheduling process involving Master Teachers, Grade level chairs, and school administration.\r\n*adherence to standard Deped policies regarding maximum teaching loads and fair allocation of non-teaching/ ancillary duties.\r\n', '1. Regular conduct of school physical facilities audit by the school facilities coordinator.\r\n2. Adherence to the DepEd School Monitoring and Evaluation Plan (SMEP) schedule.\r\n3. Active participation of the School Planning Team in quarterly inspections.\r\n', '1. Effected utilization of School MOOE for minor repairs and maintenance.\r\n2. Strong partnership with stakeholders (PTA, LGUs, and private donors) for facility enhancement projects.\r\n3. Successful implementation of the “Brigada Eskwela” initiative throughout the year.\r\n', '', '1. Consistent payment of utility bills through the school MOOE.\r\n2. Successful installation of a rainwater harvesting system to supplement water supply. \r\n3. Provision of high-speed internet subscription for administrative and instructional use.\r\n', '', '1. Strict adherence to the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) and School Improvement Plan (SIP).\r\n2. Regular quarterly meetings of the School Planning Team to track expenditure.\r\n3. Timely procurement of school supplies and instructional materials.\r\n', '1. Efficient record-keeping and documentation by the School Bookkeeper/ Designated Disbursing Officer.\r\n2. strict compliance with COA (Commission on Audit) and Deped financial guidelines.\r\n3. Prompt submission of liquidation reports to the Division Office.\r\n', 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 2, 0, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 5, 2, 5, 6, 5, 1, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 1, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, '1. Continue the “Drop Everything and Read” (DEAR) program and sustain the intensive monitoring of learners’ literacy and numeracy progress through periodic assessments.', '1. Implement a Strategic Intervention Plan (SIP) specifically for NAT preparation.\r\n2. Conduct regular mock examinations and “cliniquing” sessions for students to familiarize them with the test format.\r\n3. Provide targeted remedial instructions focusing on the most essential learning competencies (MELCs) that were least mastered.\r\n', '', '1. teachers consistently adapt lessons to the learners’ environment, leading to better comprehension and higher participation rates.\r\n2. The use of localized examples in classroom discussions has made the abstract concepts more concrete and relatable for the students.\r\n', '1. Targeted remediation in reading and mathematics has significantly decreased the number of at-risk learners this quarter.\r\n2. Regular monitoring of learning gaps allows for immediate intervention, ensuring that no learner is left behind in core subject areas.\r\n', '1. Integration is evident in most subject areas, though there is room to strengthen the documentation of peace education in technical subjects.\r\n2. Students consistently demonstrate core values during flag ceremonies and group activities, showing the effectiveness of classroom integration.’\r\n', '1. Data-driven instruction is a priority; teachers use the results of item analysis to identify which competencies need to be re-taught or remediated.\r\n2. The systematic conduct of item analysis had led to a more targeted approach in preparing review materials for the National Achievement Test (NAT).\r\n', '', 'Intensify the “No Bullying” campaign through peer-mediation and increased adult supervision.', 'Conduct quarterly awareness seminars for parents and community members on positive discipline.', 'Strengthen the “Adopt-a-Learner” program and provide targeted academic interventions for at-risk pupils.', 'Collaborate with community elders to develop localized and culture-sensitive learning resources.', 'Strengthen ‘oplan Balik Paaralan” campaigns and conduct house-to-house mapping.', 'Request the establishment of a formal ALS center and secure modular materials from the SDO.', 'Conduct annual capacity building and orientation for all CPC members and stakeholders.', 'Procure additional emergency kits and update the school’s Hazard map annually.', 'Institutionalize a peer-mentoring program and conduct regular wellness sessions for both teachers and learners.', 'Enhance existing PWD-friendly facilities and request for more inclusive education (IE) learning resources.', 'Conduct semi-annual review of the strategic plan to adjust to emerging school needs.', 'Institutionalize a fixed quarterly meeting schedule for the planning team to ensure consistent attendance.', 'Provide continuous leadership training and mentoring for student government officers.', 'Expand the use of digital platforms for faster processing of school records and stakeholder requests.', 'Conduct monthly tracking of project milestones to ensure 100% completion rate.', 'Conduct a formal SGC induction and orientation session to make the council fully operational.', 'Utilize digital communication platforms (e.g social media group) to increase parent engagement.', 'Joined Inter-school learning Action Cells (LAC) to share best practices in teaching and governance.', 'Utilized standardized M & E Tools to track the progress of school projects (e.g. Brigada eskwela, feeding programs, and reading program and reading interventions).', 'Institutionalized quarterly performance reviews and coaching sessions.', 'Conduct monthly monitoring and evaluation of the school improvement Plan (SIP).', 'Maintains complete documentation including sessions guides, attendance sheets, and post-activity reports.', 'Provides technical assistance in the preparation of promotion folders and encourages enrollment in graduate studies or specialized training.', 'Issues certificates of recognition and plaques during formal ceremonies like Stakeholders’ Appreciation Day or Year-end Rites', '*Maintain an digital tracker for teacher increments and promotion dates to ensure prompt processing.\r\n*continue conducting regular check-ins with staff regarding payroll concerns to address any systemic issues immediately.\r\n', '*Review the workload distribution annually or every semester to adapt to changes in enrolment or teacher deployments.\r\n*Maximize the use of automated scheduling tools to ensure absolute mathematical fairness in time and task distribution.\r\n', '1. Sustain the monthly inspection routine and ensure all findings are documented in the School Facilities Maintenance Logbook for immediate action.', '1. Continue to craft detailed project proposals for major facility improvements and strengthen networking with external stakeholders for additional funding and support.', '1. Allocate a specific area for a “Reading Corner” or mini-library in each classroom as an initial step.\r\n2. include the procurement of library furniture and materials in the next Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).\r\n3. Conduct a book drive and seek donations from community partners to build the library collection.\r\n', '1. Ensure regular maintenance of electrical and plumbing systems to prevent service interruptions.', '1. Submit a request for additional DCP (DepEd Computerization Program) packages.\r\n2. Prioritize the repair or refurbishing of a dedicated room for ICT integration in the next school budget.\r\n', '1. Maintain the systematic tracking of expenses to ensure all funds are utilized according to the approved program of works.', '1. Sustain the practice of ‘zero-backlog’ in liquidation submission to maintain the school’s good financial standing.', 'Consolidated client satisfaction survey (CSS) results, summary of feedback reports, and action plans addressed to stakeholder concerns.', 0, 37, 12, 58),
(1244, '2026', '136925', 'The school frequently manifests achievement of Grade 3 learners in the expected proficiency levels across early language, literacy, and numeracy skill clusters.', 'Intensify curriculum implementation and competency-based instruction aligned with the National Achievement Test (NAT).', 'No ALS learners  enrolled in School', '', '', '', 'Lack of standardized tools or templates for item analysis documentation.', 'No TLE-TVL course offered', '', '', 'Some learners still experience absenteeism and are at risk of dropping out due to financial difficulties, family concerns, lack of parental support, and distance from school and poverty.', 'Limited resources and instructional materials related to cultural activities, minimal participation of some stakeholders, and insufficient opportunities for wider cultural exposure and integration in school programs.', 'No OSY at School', 'No ALS at School', '', '', 'Limited mental health resources, lack of trained personnel for psychosocial support, irregular conduct of wellness activities, and minimal stakeholder participation in mental wellness programs.', 'Limited availability of accessible facilities such as ramps, handrails, accessible toilets, and learning resources for learners with disabilities due to insufficient funding and infrastructure support.', '', '', '', 'Limited technological resources, insufficient training on innovative service delivery, and occasional delays in communication and coordination with stakeholders.', '', 'Limited participation and engagement of some stakeholders, lack of regular meetings and clear operational guidelines, and insufficient orientation on roles and functions of SGC members.', '', '', '', 'Inconsistent stakeholder feedback results due to varying service delivery experiences, limited responsiveness to some concerns, and occasional communication gaps between school and stakeholders.', '', '', '', '', 'Lack of formal recognition system, and irregular implementation of recognition activities for personnel achievements and milestones.', 'No direct school-level payroll processing or monitoring since salary, allowances, and compensation are managed at the division level; lack of consolidated feedback or tracking at the school level.', '', 'Irregular schedule of facility inspections, limited documentation of inspection results, and occasional delays in addressing identified repair and maintenance needs due to resource constraints.', 'Limited funding allocation for major infrastructure projects', 'No Library at School', '', 'No Computer laboratory at School', '', '', '', '', '', 'Availability and effective utilization of contextualized and localized learning materials.', 'Teachers’ commitment and competence in conducting remediation and differentiated instruction.', 'Strong commitment of teachers to values formation and peace education integration in daily lessons.', '', '', 'Strong implementation of Child Protection Policy, active teacher monitoring, and positive learner discipline practices.', 'Strict implementation of the Child Protection Policy, active supervision of teachers and school personnel, strong coordination with parents and stakeholders, regular guidance and awareness activities, and promotion of a safe and child-friendly learning environment.', '', '', '', '', 'Active participation and coordination among committee members, strong implementation of child protection policies, and continuous monitoring and support from school stakeholders.', 'Effective disaster preparedness planning, active participation of school personnel and stakeholders, regular DRRM drills and orientations, and strong coordination with local DRRM offices.', '', '', 'Strong leadership and collaborative participation of school personnel and stakeholders in planning, monitoring, and aligning school goals with DepEd priorities and programs.', 'Strong collaboration and active participation of school personnel, parents, community stakeholders, and local officials in school planning and decision-making processes.', 'Active participation of learners, supportive school administration and teachers, and effective implementation of student leadership programs and activities.', '', 'Effective school leadership, collaborative planning among stakeholders, clear implementation strategies, and regular monitoring and evaluation of school programs and activities.', '', 'Active participation and strong collaboration of parents and teachers, regular PTA meetings and activities, and strong support from school leadership in engaging stakeholders.', 'Strong linkages with LGU, PTA, community organizations, and nearby schools; active participation in school partnerships and joint activities; and supportive school leadership promoting collaboration.', 'Strong school leadership, established monitoring tools and processes, regular reporting and feedback mechanisms, and active participation of teachers and stakeholders in program implementation.', '', 'Strong performance management system, clear performance targets and indicators, regular coaching and mentoring from school leadership, and commitment of personnel to quality work and professional growth.', 'Strong leadership and management practices, clear alignment of school objectives with DepEd priorities, effective teamwork among personnel, and regular monitoring and evaluation of office performance targets.', 'Strong instructional leadership, regular training needs assessment, active teacher participation, and alignment of LAC sessions and L&D activities with identified classroom needs and DepEd priorities.', 'Strong leadership support for professional growth, access to training opportunities, encouragement for higher studies and specialization, and systematic implementation of development plans aligned with personnel needs.', '', '', 'Strong instructional leadership, transparent assignment of loads and responsibilities, collaborative planning among teachers, and regular review of workload distribution to ensure fairness and balance.', '', '', '', 'Reliable utility connections, regular monitoring and maintenance of facilities, strong coordination with service providers, and prompt reporting and resolution of technical issues.', '', 'Proper budget planning and allocation, adherence to procurement and financial guidelines, regular monitoring of fund utilization, and timely submission of liquidation reports.', 'Strict adherence to accounting and auditing rules, timely submission of liquidation documents, effective coordination with administrative and finance personnel, and proper documentation of expenditures.', 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 6, 6, 6, 6, 0, 0, 2, 2, 6, 3, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 6, 1, 6, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Strengthen the implementation of reading and numeracy intervention programs for struggling learners.', 'Intensify NAT review and intervention activities for Grades 6, 10, and 12 learners.', '', 'Encourage collaboration and sharing of best practices among teachers in developing innovative instructional materials.', 'Sustain and institutionalize regular remediation programs in reading, comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics.', 'Sustain the consistent integration of peace education and DepEd core values in all learning areas.', 'Strengthen the regular conduct of test item analysis after all major and periodic assessments.', '', 'Promote active participation, positive relationships, and shared responsibility among learners, parents, and stakeholders.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen child protection programs, conduct regular awareness campaigns and orientations, sustain close coordination with stakeholders, and maintain a safe, nurturing, and child-friendly learning environment for all learners.', 'The school commits to strengthen learner monitoring, intensify home visitation and intervention programs, enhance parental engagement, and collaborate with stakeholders to support at-risk learners and further reduce drop-out incidence.', 'The school commits to continuously implement culture-sensitive and inclusive activities that respect diversity, strengthen cultural appreciation, and promote unity among learners and stakeholders.', '', '', 'The school commits to sustain the effectiveness of the Child Protection Committee through regular meetings, continuous capacity-building activities, and strengthened implementation of child protection programs and policies.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen and update the DRRM plan, conduct regular disaster preparedness activities, and sustain coordination with stakeholders to ensure the safety and preparedness of all learners and personnel.', 'The school commits to strengthen mental wellness programs through regular psychosocial activities, capacity-building for teachers, enhanced stakeholder involvement, and establishment of sustainable learner support mechanisms.', 'The school commits to prioritize the improvement of inclusive and PWD-friendly facilities, strengthen partnerships with stakeholders for resource support, and promote an accessible and inclusive learning environment for all learners.', 'The school commits to continuously enhance strategic planning processes through data-driven decision-making, stakeholder engagement, and regular monitoring and evaluation of school targets and accomplishments.', 'The school commits to sustain and strengthen partnerships with stakeholders through continuous consultation, collaborative planning, and active participation in programs and projects that support school improvement and learner development.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen student leadership and participation through capacity-building activities, regular engagement in school programs, and promotion of responsible and active citizenship among learners.', 'The school commits to enhance frontline services through continuous innovation, capacity-building activities, improved communication systems, and strengthened stakeholder support to ensure efficient and responsive service delivery.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen the implementation of its strategic plan through data-driven monitoring, stakeholder engagement, and timely evaluation of programs and activities to ensure attainment of school goals and objectives.', 'The school commits to activate and strengthen the School Governance Council through regular meetings, clear delineation of roles and responsibilities, stakeholder orientation, and sustained collaboration to improve school governance and decision-making.', 'The school commits to sustain and strengthen PTA involvement through continuous communication, regular consultation meetings, and active partnership in implementing school programs, projects, and learner development activities.', 'The school commits to sustain and further strengthen partnerships through continuous coordination, regular stakeholder engagements, and collaborative programs and activities that support school improvement and learner development.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthen monitoring and evaluation systems through data-driven decision-making, regular program review, and sustained stakeholder feedback to ensure effective and efficient implementation of school programs, projects, and activities.', 'The school commits to sustain high performance by strengthening performance monitoring and feedback mechanisms, providing continuous professional development opportunities, and promoting a culture of excellence, accountability, and results-based performance among personnel.', 'The school commits to sustain high office performance by strengthening results-based management practices, continuous monitoring of OPCR targets, enhancing collaboration among personnel, and providing capacity-building activities to maintain and further improve performance outcomes.', 'The school commits to sustain and further strengthen needs-based LAC and L&D programs through continuous needs assessment, data-driven planning, and provision of relevant professional development activities to enhance teaching quality and learner outcomes.', 'The school commits to sustain and enhance continuous professional development by supporting participation in trainings, seminars, and graduate studies, strengthening mentorship programs, and ensuring equitable opportunities for career advancement among personnel.', 'The school commits to establish and strengthen a systematic recognition and rewards mechanism, maximize available resources and partnerships for incentives, and regularly conduct recognition activities to acknowledge personnel achievements and motivate continued excellence.', '', 'The school commits to sustain fair and equitable workload distribution through continuous consultation, transparent planning processes, and regular monitoring and adjustment based on teacher capacity and school needs.', 'The school commits to establish a regular and systematic infrastructure inspection schedule, improve documentation and reporting of findings, and strengthen coordination with stakeholders and concerned offices for timely repair and maintenance of facilities.', 'The school commits to strengthen resource mobilization by actively engaging stakeholders such as the LGU, PTA, and private partners to support infrastructure needs.', 'The school commits to establish a functional school library through phased implementation, starting with the organization of a reading corner or mini-library.', 'The school commits to sustain the functionality of water, electricity, and internet facilities through regular maintenance, efficient resource management, and continuous coordination with service providers to ensure uninterrupted school operations and learning activities.', 'The school commits to establish a functional computer laboratory or ICT learning space through phased implementation, prioritizing inclusion in the SIP/AIP and mobilizing resources from LGU, PTA, and other stakeholders.', 'The school commits to sustain efficient and transparent utilization of MOOE through strengthened financial planning, strict compliance with accounting and auditing rules, and continuous monitoring to ensure that funds are used effectively to support school operations and priorities.', 'The school commits to sustain full and timely liquidation of MOOE by maintaining accurate financial records, ensuring compliance with COA guidelines, and strengthening internal monitoring and review of all financial transactions and supporting documents.', 'The school commits to improve stakeholder satisfaction by strengthening communication systems, enhancing responsiveness to feedback and concerns, and continuously improving service delivery through regular monitoring and quality assurance mechanisms.', 0, 125, 12, 57),
