(1266, '2026', '129254', 'Many Grade 3 learners are still struggling with reading comprehension, vocabulary development, and basic numeracy skills.', 'Many learners have difficulty applying critical thinking, problem-solving, communication, and analytical skills required in 21st century learning and NAT assessments.', '', 'Lack of regular monitoring and evaluation of the effectiveness of contextualized learning materials.', 'Although remediation activities are regularly conducted, some learners still demonstrate persistent learning gaps in reading comprehension, mathematics problem-solving, and science concepts.', 'Some teachers have limited instructional materials and contextualized examples related to peace education and DepEd core values integration.', 'The school conducts test item analysis to inform its teaching and learning process; however, some teachers encounter difficulty in interpreting data results and utilizing the analysis to improve instructional strategies effectively.', '', 'The school aims to maintain zero child bullying incidence; however, isolated cases of misunderstandings, teasing, and peer conflicts among learners are occasionally observed within the school environment.', 'The school upholds zero child abuse incidence; however, there are occasional concerns related to learners’ emotional well-being, discipline issues, and limited awareness of child protection mechanisms among some stakeholders.', 'The school has reduced its drop-out incidence; however, there are still occasional cases of learners at risk of dropping out due to absenteeism, family-related concerns, economic challenges, and lack of academic motivation.', 'Conducts culture-sensitive activities; however, integration of indigenous peoples’ culture, local traditions, and contextualized cultural practices in classroom instruction and school activities is not yet fully maximized or consistently implemented across all learning areas.', '', '', 'Has a functional Child Protection Committee; however, there are occasional gaps in the consistency of documentation, monitoring of reported concerns, and strengthening of proactive child protection advocacy activities.', 'Has a functional DRRM (Disaster Risk Reduction and Management) Plan; however, there are occasional gaps in the regular updating of contingency plans, simulation drills, resource inventory, and full participation of all stakeholders in preparedness activities.', 'Has a functional support mechanism for mental wellness; however, there are still limitations in the availability of trained personnel, structured counseling schedules, and sustained mental health programs for both learners and staff.', 'Has SPED and PWD-friendly facilities; however, there are still gaps in the availability of complete accessibility features such as ramps, assistive learning materials, inclusive classroom adjustments, and specialized support services for learners with special needs.', 'School develops a strategic plan; however, there are occasional challenges in aligning stakeholder inputs, ensuring timely updating of targets, and strengthening the cascading of the plan to all implementers for full operationalization.', 'Absence of a structured and sustained mechanism for community engagement', 'Limited attendance of parents, LGU, and community leaders during planning sessions', 'No systematic system for collecting stakeholder feedback on services', 'Difficulty in tracking accomplishment of strategic goals\r\nInconsistent execution of programs and projects\r\nOverlapping or uncoordinated activities due to lack of structured planning flow', 'The School Governance Council (SGC) exists but is not fully active or consistently engaged in school governance functions\r\nLimited awareness among stakeholders on the role, scope, and responsibilities of the SGC\r\nGovernance participation is often informal rather than structured', 'The PTA is generally active and functional, but participation is sometimes uneven across parents\r\nPTA activities are often concentrated during school events rather than sustained year-round engagement\r\nSome parents remain passive participants despite regular PTA initiatives', 'Stakeholder participation is often event-based (e.g., Brigada Eskwela, school programs) rather than continuous.', 'Some programs use structured evaluation forms, while others rely on informal reporting.', 'atisfaction ratings may differ significantly between internal stakeholders (teachers, learners) and external stakeholders (parents, LGU).', 'While the overall rating is Very Satisfactory, some personnel occasionally fall below the target level.\r\nGap: Performance is not fully consistent across all teaching and non-teaching staff.\r\nBottleneck: Differences in workload distribution and varying levels of experience.', 'Concern/Issue: Some office outputs are achieved, but not all are fully aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).\r\nGap: Weak integration between OPCR targets and school strategic goals.\r\nBottleneck: Limited structured alignment sessions during planning.', 'Concern/Issue: Some LAC sessions are based on general priorities rather than fully data-driven needs.\r\nGap: Limited use of consolidated learner performance data and teacher competency gaps in planning LAC topics.\r\nBottleneck: Incomplete or delayed analysis of assessment results before LAC scheduling.', 'Concern/Issue: Not all personnel equally benefit from training, scholarships, or professional development activities.\r\nGap: Some teachers/staff receive more opportunities due to availability or priority areas.\r\nBottleneck: Limited slots, funding constraints, and scheduling conflicts.', 'Concern/Issue: Recognition activities are conducted, but records are sometimes incomplete or scattered.\r\nGap: Absence of a centralized tracking system for awards, citations, and milestones.\r\nBottleneck: Decentralized documentation practices across committees.', 'Concern/Issue: Timeliness is partly affected by external systems (e.g., division office, national payroll systems).\r\nGap: Limited control at the school level over final processing timelines.\r\nBottleneck: System constraints beyond school management authority.', 'Perception of uneven task distribution during peak school activities (e.g., examinations, school programs, and reporting periods).\r\nSome teachers feel assigned duties are based more on availability than specialization or expertise.\r\nOverlapping responsibilities among teachers holding multiple designations (e.g., class adviser + committee head).\r\nLimited delegation of non-instructional tasks to support staff.', 'Routine inspections are conducted, but follow-up actions on identified defects are sometimes delayed.\r\nSafety concerns may persist when minor damages are not immediately addressed.\r\nInconsistency in documentation of inspection results (some reports are incomplete or not standardized).\r\nLimited technical knowledge among staff conducting infrastructure assessments.', 'Improvement initiatives are often reactive (based on urgent needs) rather than fully planned preventive upgrades.\r\nSome infrastructure proposals may not immediately translate into approved or funded projects.\r\nStakeholders may have varying expectations on priority improvements.', 'No established library management system (cataloging, borrowing, tracking).\r\nLimited or no structured collection development plan for books and references.\r\nInsufficient budget allocation specifically for library establishment and maintenance.', 'Intermittent interruptions in water, electricity, or internet services affect teaching and learning continuity.\r\nDependence on external utility providers makes service stability beyond full school control.\r\nUnequal access to internet connectivity in different areas of the campus.', 'Absence of a dedicated and fully equipped computer laboratory/classroom.\r\nLimited number of functional computers or ICT equipment for student use.\r\nLack of structured ICT learning environment for digital skills development.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Facilitating Factors for Indicators with always manifested (give me this since The school achieves a 72–100% utilization rate of its Maintenance and Other Operating Expenses (MOOE) – Always Manifested.\r\nTimely release and disbursement of funds\r\nFunds from the Division Office are released without significant delays, allowing the school to implement planned activities within the fiscal year.\r\nStrong financial planning and budgeting practices\r\nThe school prepares a realistic Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) and corresponding budget aligned with priority needs, ensuring that MOOE funds are already assigned to specific programs and expenses. This reduces delays and underutilization.\r\n', 'The school consistently follows government accounting rules, COA guidelines, and DepEd financial procedures, ensuring that all disbursed funds are properly documented and liquidated.\r\nProcurement activities are completed on schedule, allowing expenses to be liquidated immediately after delivery and acceptance of goods or services.\r\nSuppliers comply with required documentation (official receipts, billing statements), and stakeholders assist in verifying deliveries and completion of activities.', 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 3, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Conduct intensive remediation programs such as reading intervention classes, numeracy drills, and after-class tutorials for struggling learners.', 'Integrate 21st century skills in daily classroom instruction through collaborative activities, project-based learning, and performance tasks.', '', 'Strengthen monitoring, feedback, and evaluation mechanisms to ensure quality, relevance, and effectiveness of instructional materials.', 'Intensify individualized and small-group remediation sessions based on learners’ specific needs and assessment results.', 'Develop and share localized learning resources, peace-themed activities, and contextualized lesson exemplars suited to the learners and community situation of the school.', 'Conduct continuous capacity-building activities and Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions on test item analysis, data interpretation, and data-driven instruction to further strengthen assessment practices and improve learner performance in the context of Judge Ernesto Nombrado Memorial School.', '', 'Strengthen the implementation of the Child Protection Policy through continuous values formation activities, guidance interventions, anti-bullying campaigns, peer support programs, and close coordination with parents and stakeholders to sustain a safe and peaceful learning environment in Judge Ernesto Nombrado Memorial School.', 'Intensify the implementation of the Child Protection Policy through regular orientations, advocacy campaigns, guidance activities, and strengthened coordination with parents, teachers, and community stakeholders to ensure a child-friendly and protective environment in Judge Ernesto Nombrado Memorial School.', 'Strengthen the implementation of the Dropout Reduction Program (DORP) through early identification of at-risk learners, regular home visitation, intensified guidance and counseling, remedial instruction, and stronger engagement with parents and stakeholders to sustain learner retention in Judge Ernesto Nombrado Memorial School.', 'Strengthen the integration of culture-sensitive education by contextualizing lessons, involving community elders and stakeholders, and aligning activities with learners’ cultural backgrounds. Conduct regular orientations and capacity-building for teachers to enhance culturally responsive teaching practices', '', '', 'Enhance the functionality of the Child Protection Committee by ensuring regular meetings, proper documentation, timely response to concerns, continuous monitoring, and strengthened advocacy campaigns on child rights and protection within the school.', 'Strengthen the implementation of the DRRM plan through regular updating of risk assessments, conduct of quarterly drills, proper maintenance of emergency supplies, and active involvement of teachers, learners, and stakeholders to ensure safety and preparedness.', 'Strengthen the school’s mental wellness support system by capacitating teachers and guidance personnel, establishing regular counseling and psychosocial support activities, and integrating mental health awareness programs into school-wide initiatives', 'trengthen inclusive education by improving accessibility facilities, providing assistive devices and learning materials, and enhancing teacher capacity in differentiated instruction and SPED strategies to better support learners with disabilities', 'Strengthen collaborative planning processes through regular stakeholder consultations, clear dissemination of strategic priorities, and continuous monitoring and evaluation to ensure effective implementation of the strategic plan', 'Institutionalize a School-Community Planning Team (SCPT) with clear membership, roles, and schedules', 'Strengthen stakeholder engagement through scheduled quarterly consultations and flexible meeting schedules', 'Implement feedback tools such as suggestion boxes, QR-based surveys, or SMS feedback', 'Strengthen the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) as the direct operational tool of the strategic plan\r\nEnsure all programs, projects, and activities (PPAs) are aligned with SIP goals\r\nConduct regular mid-year and year-end implementation reviews', 'Reactivate and formalize the SGC with updated membership and clear terms of reference\r\nEstablish a fixed annual calendar of SGC meetings and activities\r\nDefine clear roles, responsibilities, and decision-making authority of members', 'Implement more flexible meeting schedules (including blended or alternative formats if needed)\r\nEncourage class-level PTA strengthening to widen participation base\r\nRecognize active parent participation to encourage sustained engagement', 'Develop a School Partnership Development Plan (SPDP) with clear schedules, roles, and responsibilities.\r\nAssign a Partnership Coordinator/Committee to monitor engagement continuity.', 'Develop a school-wide M&E template package for all programs and projects.\r\nEnsure alignment with SBM indicators and DepEd reporting standards.', 'Strengthen Performance Alignment with SIP\r\nEnsure all IPCR targets are directly anchored to School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).\r\nConduct pre-IPCR alignment sessions at the start of the school year.', 'Strengthen Alignment of OPCR with School Plans\r\nEnsure all OPCR targets are directly anchored to SIP and AIP priorities.\r\nConduct annual OPCR planning and alignment workshops.', 'Use learners’ assessment results, classroom observations, and IPCR needs as basis for LAC topics.\r\nConduct pre-LAC needs analysis every quarter.', 'Strengthen Equal Access to CPD Opportunities\r\nDevelop a transparent selection system for training and scholarship opportunities.\r\nEnsure fair rotation of participants across all personnel.', 'Create a centralized recognition and awards database.\r\nMaintain annual recognition reports for transparency and continuity.', 'Strengthen coordination with Division Office and relevant agencies for faster processing.\r\nFollow up regularly on pending releases to minimize delays.', 'Develop a transparent workload matrix per grading period showing assignments per teacher.\r\nUse rotational assignment schemes for committees and major tasks.', 'Develop a standardized school infrastructure inspection checklist.\r\nSchedule monthly or quarterly structured inspection rounds with assigned personnel.\r\nEstablish a facility maintenance logbook or digital tracking system.\r\nRequire submission of inspection reports with photo documentation for transparency.\r\nC. Preventive Maintenance Planning', 'Develop a School Infrastructure Development Plan (SIDP) aligned with SIP/AIP.\r\nUse a priority ranking system (safety, urgency, learner impact, cost).', 'Allocate or designate a dedicated room/space for the school library or Learning Resource Center (LRC).\r\nGradually equip the area with basic furniture (shelves, tables, chairs).', 'Upgrade to more reliable internet service plans suited for school-wide use.\r\nEstablish redundant internet options (e.g., backup provider or mobile hotspot system).', 'Engage LGU, PTA, alumni, NGOs, and private partners for donation of computers and ICT equipment.\r\nInclude ICT lab development in the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).', 'Ensure that the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) and Work and Financial Plan (WFP) are fully aligned with priority school needs and updated based on actual conditions.', 'Ensure full adherence to COA rules, DepEd policies, and accounting procedures in all financial transactions and reporting.\r\nAll liquidation documents will be prepared and submitted immediately after the completion of each procurement or activity.', 'Develop a unified satisfaction survey tool for internal and external stakeholders.\r\nAlign indicators with SBM standards and DepEd quality assurance measures.', 1, 8, 12, 61),
