(1268, '2026', '128316', 'Learners absenteeism', 'Leaners absences, poor academic performance', '', '', '', '', 'Insufficient time for analysis', '', 'Underreporting of bullying incidents', '', 'Limited parental support and involvement', 'Financial constraints for cultural activities', '', '', 'Limited awareness of committee roles and responsibilities', 'Limited awareness of DRRM protocols and procedures', 'Insufficient guidance and counseling personnel', 'Limited accessibility of school facilities', 'Limited stakeholder participation in planning', 'Limited understanding of roles and responsibilities', 'Student officers may need further development in leadership, communication, and organizational skills.', 'The school may have insufficient computers, internet connectivity, and digital tools needed for efficient frontline services.', 'Financial and resource constraints', 'Scheduling conflicts and time constraints', '', 'Limited stakeholder participation and engagement', 'Insufficient time for monitoring and evaluation activities', 'Delayed or unclear dissemination of information may affect stakeholder understanding and satisfaction.', 'Limited time for preparation and accomplishment of targets', '', '', '', 'Insufficient documentation of personnel achievements', '', 'Overlapping schedules and responsibilities', '', 'Limited budget and financial resources', 'Limited budget and financial resources', 'Water interruptions and limited access to clean water may affect sanitation, hygiene, and daily school operations.', 'Lack of appropriate laboratory space', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong support from school administrators in providing resources and guidance.', 'Teachers demonstrate creativity, innovation, and commitment in preparing learning resources.', 'Presence of a positive, safe, and inclusive learning environment that supports harmonious relationships among learners and teachers.\r\nhow about its Proposed Resolutions/Commitment\r\n\r\nProposed Resolution/Commitment:\r\n\r\nThe school commits to strengthening the integration of peace education and DepEd core values in all teaching-learning processes and school activities. Teachers shall consistently promote Maka-Diyos, Maka-tao, Makakalikasan, and Makabansa through meaningful classroom discussions, learner-centered activities, and positive role modeling. School administrators, parents, and stakeholders shall work collaboratively to sustain a safe, inclusive, and values-oriented learning environment that nurtures respect, responsibility, unity, and active citizenship among learners.\r\n\r\nInsufficient guidance and counseling personnel what is the possible school commitment  or proposed resolution for this as rarely manifested\r\n\r\nProposed Resolution/Commitment:\r\n\r\nThe school commits to strengthening learner support services by maximizing the available human resources and collaborating with stakeholders to address the insufficient number of guidance and counseling personnel. Teachers, school heads, and designated coordinators shall work together in providing basic guidance activities, learner monitoring, and psychosocial support while advocating for additional guidance personnel, continuous training, and stronger partnerships with parents, LGUs, and external agencies to better respond to the needs of learners.', '', '', '', 'Strict implementation of the Child Protection Policy', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Active PTA Leaders', '', '', '', '', 'Commitment and teamwork among teaching and non-teaching personnel.', 'Active participation and collaboration among teachers during LAC sessions.', 'Strong support from the school head in encouraging professional growth and career advancement.', '', 'Timely preparation and submission of payroll-related documents and reports.', '', 'Regular implementation of school maintenance and inspection schedules.', '', '', '', '', 'Effective financial planning and budgeting by the school management.', 'Compliance with government procurement, disbursement, and liquidation procedures.', 2, 2, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 6, 6, 6, 6, 0, 0, 2, 1, 6, 5, 2, 2, 2, 1, 3, 6, 6, 6, 2, 6, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 3, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 3, 'Teachers, parents, and stakeholders shall work collaboratively in providing appropriate interventions, regular monitoring, and learner support to improve academic performance and promote quality learning outcomes for every child.', 'The school commits to intensifying academic support programs and strengthening the delivery of instruction to ensure that Grade 6, learners achieve the desired proficiency level', '', 'Continuously support the teachers  in providing resources and guidance.', 'Availability of sufficient instructional materials, ICT resources, and reference materials.', 'School administrators, parents, and stakeholders shall work collaboratively to sustain a safe, inclusive, and values-oriented learning environment that nurtures respect, responsibility, unity, and active citizenship among learners.', 'Allocate sufficient time for item analysis', '', 'Conduct regular anti-bullying awareness campaigns', 'Continue and enhance the implementation of the Child Protection Policy', 'Conduct regular home visitation and learner profiling', 'Allocate resources and budget support for cultural activities', '', '', 'Strengthen orientation on Child Protection Committee functions', 'Conduct regular drills and simulation exercises', 'Teachers and school personnel will participate in trainings on mental health awareness, stress management, and psychosocial support strategies.', 'Provide safe and supportive learning environments', 'Strengthen stakeholder participation in strategic planning', 'Clarify roles and responsibilities of planning team members', 'Provide continuous leadership training and capability-building', 'The school commits to maximizing digital tools, online platforms, and ICT resources to improve efficiency and accessibility of services.', 'Enhance resource mobilization and financial planning', 'The school will strengthen time management and coordination practices to minimize scheduling conflicts and ensure timely implementation of planned activities.', 'Continuously support the PTA activities and programs', 'The school commits to actively involving parents, community leaders, partner schools, NGOs, and organizations in collaborative programs and activities.', 'The school commits to implementing clear monitoring schedules, tools, indicators, and reporting mechanisms.', 'Promote effective time management and workload organization', 'The school administration shall also strengthen monitoring, coaching, capacity-building activities, and stakeholder collaboration to ensure continuous improvement and quality delivery of educational services.', 'The school commits to continuously conducting needs-based Learning Action Cells (LAC) and Learning and Development (L&D) activities that are responsive to the professional growth needs of teachers and personnel.', 'The school commits to continuously supporting the promotion and professional development of all personnel through relevant trainings, mentoring programs, Learning Action Cells (LAC), and other capacity-building activities.', 'The school commits to regularly recognizing and celebrating the achievements and contributions of school personnel.', 'The school commits to continuously ensuring the timely and accurate processing of salaries, allowances, and other benefits of personnel through efficient coordination, proper documentation, and compliance with existing DepEd and government policies.', 'Class schedules and school responsibilities will be carefully planned to avoid overlapping duties and workload conflicts.\r\nStrengthen monitoring and evaluation of workload distribution\r\nSchool leaders will regularly assess workload assignments and address concerns related to imbalance and overload.\r\nProvide support and assistance to teachers with heavy responsibilities\r\nTeamwork, collaboration, and administrative support will be encouraged to help manage workload demands.\r\nPromote teacher wellness and work-life balance\r\nThe school commits to implementing wellness programs and stress-management activities to support teachers’ well-being.\r\nEncourage collaborative planning and sharing of resources\r\nTeachers will be encouraged to work together in lesson preparation, instructional planning, and resource sharing.\r\nMaximize the use of technology and digital tools\r\nICT resources and digital platforms will be utilized to improve efficiency in teaching, reporting, and communication.\r\nAddress staffing needs and resource gaps promptly\r\nThe school will coordinate with higher offices and stakeholders to address teacher shortages and staffing concerns.\r\nRecognize and appreciate teachers’ efforts and contributions\r\nRecognition and appreciation activities will be conducted to motivate and acknowledge teachers’ hard work and dedication.\r\nProvide capability-building on time management and productivity\r\nTeachers will participate in trainings that enhance organization, prioritization, and efficiency in handling responsibilities.\r\nDevelop contingency plans for unexpected staffing changes\r\nFlexible work arrangements and support systems will be prepared for emergencies and personnel adjustments.\r\nSustain a culture of fairness, collaboration, and shared responsibility\r\nThe entire school community commits to maintaining a supportive and equitable working environment for all teachers.', 'The school commits to continuously strengthening the inspection, maintenance, and improvement of school infrastructure and facilities to ensure a safe, secure, and learner-friendly environment.', 'The school commits to maximizing available funds and seeking support from stakeholders, LGUs, NGOs, and partner organizations for infrastructure projects.', 'The school commits to maximizing available funds and seeking support from stakeholders, LGUs, NGOs, and partner organizations for infrastructure projects.', 'The school commits to conducting regular inspection, repair, and preventive maintenance of water, electrical, and internet systems.', 'The school will seek support from LGUs, NGOs, alumni, private organizations, and stakeholders for ICT equipment and infrastructure.', 'The school commits to continuously ensuring the efficient, transparent, and timely utilization of MOOE funds in accordance with DepEd policies and financial management guidelines.', 'The school commits to continuously ensuring the timely, accurate, and complete liquidation of all utilized MOOE funds in compliance with DepEd and government financial management policies.', 'The school will maintain clear, timely, and accessible communication channels for stakeholders.', 1, 116, 12, 57),
