(1284, '2026', '128741', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Absence of a centralized tracking and mapping mechanism to identify and enroll potential Alternative Learning System (ALS) learners within the immediate community catchment area', '', '', '', 'Absence of concrete ramps, PWD-accessible restrooms, and tactile pathways in the school buildings.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Absence of a dedicated room and shortage of updated reference books/reading materials for a functional library.', '', 'Lack of standard computer units and a secured laboratory room to facilitate ICT and digital literacy classes.', '', '', 'strong teacher collaboration', 'strong teacher collaboration', '', 'strong teacher collaboration', 'strong teacher collaboration', 'strong teacher collaboration', 'strong teacher collaboration', '', 'Active implementation of the DepEd Child Protection Policy, continuous advocacy during homeroom guidance, and visible anti-bullying campaigns around the school campus.', 'Conduct of seminars on child rights, strong implementation of the positive discipline policy, and an active, approachable Child Protection Committee (CPC).', 'Consistent home visitation programs (e.g., Project SARO/Dropout Reduction Program), early identification of students-at-risk, and regular communication with parents.', 'Integration of local culture, indigenous knowledge, and diverse traditions into school events (like Nutrition Month or United Nations Day) and lesson plans.', 'Proactive community mapping, open-door enrollment policies for over-aged learners, and flexible learning options tailored to student needs.', '', 'Regular quarterly meetings of the committee, a clear workflow for handling student welfare, and strong representation from teachers, parents, and barangay officials.', 'Conduct of regular multi-hazard drills (earthquake/fire), established and visible evacuation routes, and active coordination with the local BDRRMC.', 'Conduct of mental health awareness sessions for both students and teachers, and an active guidance counselor or designated teacher-coordinator providing basic counseling services.', '', 'Active participation of teachers, parents, and community leaders during the crafting and reviewing of the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).', 'Clear delineation of roles among SPT members, regular quarterly meetings, and strong administrative support from the school head.', 'Dedicated teacher-adviser providing leadership mentoring, clear student-led action plans, and active involvement of student leaders in school activities.', 'Standardized and visible Citizen\'s Charter, streamlined enrollment and document request processes, and the utilization of digital communication channels (like a dedicated school FB page) for quick updates.', 'Consistent, systematic alignment of the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) targets with the approved School Improvement Plan (SIP) priorities and quarterly tracking.', 'Active participation of diverse stakeholder representatives, clear adherence to the SGC functions, and the regular conduct of meetings to discuss school policies.', 'Strong collaborative relationship between the elected PTA officers and school administration, backed by regular, well-attended general assembly meetings.', 'Active networking with local government units (LGUs), private partners, and neighboring schools during Brigada Eskwela and shared technical assistance sessions.', 'Regular mobilization of the School Quality Assurance, Monitoring, and Evaluation (SMEA) team to assess program implementation and outcomes.', 'Consistent practice of gathering stakeholder feedback through client satisfaction surveys and maintaining transparent, accommodating frontline services.', 'Regular target setting and continuous mentoring by the school head.', 'Strong collaborative teamwork among teaching and non-teaching staff, and clear alignment of school programs with division goals.', 'Systematic administration of the Electronic Self-Assessment Tool (e-SAT) to pinpoint exact training needs, paired with a structured school LAC calendar.', 'Active dissemination of ranking guidelines, timely submission of promotion documents, and administrative support for staff attending external seminars or graduate studies.', 'Institutionalized school-level Rewards and Recognition (R&R) system (e.g., PRAISE committee) to celebrate perfect attendance, outstanding teaching, and milestones.', 'Prompt processing, verification, and submission of payroll attachments, service credits, and billing documents to the Division Office.', 'Strict adherence to DepEd guidelines on teacher workloads, consideration of ancillary assignments, and transparent consultation during the creation of the master schedule.', 'Active mobilization of the School Inspectorate Team and regular physical facility check-ups before the rainy season and school openings.', 'Productive collaboration with the PTA, LGU, and private donors during Brigada Eskwela to fund and execute minor school repairs.', '', 'Timely allocation and priority funding from the school MOOE to pay for monthly utility bills and regular maintenance contracts.', '', 'Strict adherence to the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) cash flow and proactive procurement scheduling by the school BAC.', 'Systematic record-keeping, prompt collection of receipts/receipt attachments, and adherence to the Division Office\'s strict liquidation deadlines.\r\n\r\n', 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 2, 1, 0, 2, 2, 6, 6, 6, 1, 2, 5, 6, 5, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 2, 6, 6, 1, 6, 1, 2, 1, 2, 2, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Consistent implementation of early literacy programs (such as Catch-Up Fridays or dedicated reading slots).', 'Regular conduct of NAT mock examinations and intensive review sessions.\r\n\r\nSeamless integration of 21st-century skills (critical thinking, communication) across core subject lesson plans.', '', 'Active participation of