(1298, '2026', '128736', 'Some Grade 3 learners are still identified as slow readers, affecting their comprehension and performance in literacy and numeracy activities.', 'Some learners still have difficulty in higher-order thinking skills, reading comprehension, and problem-solving competencies reflected in periodic assessments and NAT results.', 'Some ALS learners have irregular attendance due to work, family responsibilities, and financial difficulties, affecting their completion and certification.', 'Limited time and insufficient resources hinder teachers in developing more varied and localized contextualized learning materials.', '', '', 'The school has only one designated test analyzer who also handles teaching responsibilities, causing delays in the preparation and analysis of assessment results.', 'TLE–TVL (Technical-Vocational-Livelihood) course offerings are part of Senior High School (SHS) under the K–12 program.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'The school has limited structured mental wellness interventions and referral systems. An incident involving a teaching personnel who underwent psychological treatment highlights the need for stronger mental health support, early identification of stress indicators, and more accessible professional intervention services for staff and learners.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Uneven distribution of tasks and additional assignments due to insufficient number of teachers in the school, leading to some teachers having overload teaching loads.', 'Some minor delays in addressing identified maintenance needs due to limited budget and procurement timelines, which may affect the immediate repair of certain facilities.', 'Limited budget allocation and procurement processes may delay the immediate implementation of some infrastructure improvement projects and facility upgrades.', 'The school currently has no established library, limiting learners’ access to reading materials, reference books, and a dedicated space for independent learning and research.', '', 'The school has an existing computer laboratory, however most of the units are already outdated and insufficient, limiting learners’ access to functional ICT equipment for effective computer-based learning.', '', '', 'Consistent teacher monitoring and assessment of learners’ progress.', 'Effective implementation of competency-based teaching strategies and regular review sessions aligned with the National Achievement Test (NAT).\r\n', 'Strong implementation of Alternative Learning System (ALS) programs through regular learning sessions and learner support.\r\n', 'Teachers demonstrate creativity and collaboration in developing localized and contextualized learning materials.', 'Regular conduct of targeted remediation programs and close monitoring of learners with identified learning gaps.', 'Teachers consistently integrate peace education and DepEd core values in daily classroom instruction and activities.\r\n', 'Teachers regularly conduct test item analysis to identify learners’ strengths and areas for improvement.\r\n', '', 'Strict implementation of child protection policies and continuous promotion of a safe and inclusive school environment.', 'Strict enforcement of child protection policies and strong coordination among school personnel, parents, and stakeholders in safeguarding learners.', 'Effective learner monitoring and retention programs, including home visitation and intervention for at-risk learners.\r\n', 'Integration of culturally responsive practices and celebration of diverse cultural backgrounds in school activities.', 'Strong implementation of inclusive education programs and Alternative Learning System (ALS) initiatives for disadvantaged, OSY, and adult learners.', 'Strong implementation and regular conduct of Alternative Learning System (ALS) sessions with committed facilitators and active learner participation.\r\n', 'Active and well-coordinated Child Protection Committee ensuring continuous monitoring and enforcement of child safeguarding policies.', 'The school administration, DRRM coordinators, teachers, and stakeholders actively collaborate in implementing disaster preparedness activities, regular drills, and safety awareness programs.', 'The school provides guidance, counseling activities, psychosocial support, and wellness programs with the cooperation of teachers, parents, and stakeholders.', 'The school has existing SPED programs, inclusive classroom practices, and basic PWD-friendly facilities supported by school administration and stakeholders.', 'The school leadership, planning team, and stakeholders actively participate in the development and periodic review of the school strategic plan.', 'Active collaboration between school leaders, teachers, LGU representatives, parents, and community stakeholders in planning and decision-making activities.', 'Active support from school administration and teacher-advisers in guiding SSG/SPG officers in planning and implementing school activities and initiatives.', 'The school promotes initiatives such as improved service processes, use of digital platforms, and collaboration among personnel to enhance stakeholder services.', 'The school leadership ensures that the strategic plan is translated into actionable annual implementation plans with clear targets, monitoring systems, and assigned responsibilities among personnel.', 'Strong collaboration among school leaders, parents, LGU representatives, and stakeholders in supporting school governance functions and decision-making processes.', 'Active PTA officers and strong collaboration between parents, teachers, and school administration in supporting school programs and activities.', 'Strong linkages with LGU, parents, nearby schools, and community stakeholders who actively support school programs, projects, and activities.', 'The school implements regular monitoring schedules and assigns personnel to assist in data gathering and evaluation of programs, projects, and activities.', 'The school maintains strong relationships with stakeholders through regular communication, transparency, and consistent delivery of basic services and programs.', 'Strong performance monitoring system, regular coaching and mentoring from school leadership, and clear alignment of duties with IPCR targets contribute to high performance ratings.', 'Strong leadership and coordination among school personnel, clear performance targets, and regular monitoring and evaluation contribute to consistently high OPCR ratings.', 'Strong support from school leadership and active participation of teachers in identifying needs-based topics for LAC and professional development activities.', 'The school leadership actively supports and encourages participation in upskilling, graduate studies, trainings, and promotion-related requirements, with guidance provided for career development pathways.', 'The school leadership implements recognition programs, acknowledges personnel achievements during meetings and events, and conducts a yearly program entitled Gawad Parangal where the efforts and contributions of teaching and non-teaching personnel, as well as school stakeholders, are formally recognized and celebrated.', 'Strong coordination between school administration, payroll in-charge, and personnel ensures accurate computation, validation, and timely processing of salaries, allowances, and other compensation.', '', '', '', '', 'The school maintains functional water and electricity supply, with available internet connectivity that supports administrative tasks, teaching, and learning activities.', '', 'Strong financial planning and budgeting practices, guided by school leadership and supported by personnel involved in procurement and liquidation, ensure proper and efficient use of MOOE.', 'Strong financial management practices, close monitoring of expenditures, and active coordination among school personnel ensure complete and accurate liquidation of MOOE.', 1, 1, 6, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 2, 6, 6, 1, 2, 6, 6, 6, 1, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 0, 'Intensify reading intervention programs, provide differentiated learning activities, strengthen parental involvement, and conduct remedial classes and Summer Class/ARAL Program to improve learners’ reading and numeracy skills.', 'Strengthen reading and numeracy intervention programs and intensify NAT review and enrichment activities. Continue teacher training on 21st century teaching strategies and assessment practices. Enhance stakeholder partnership to support learning resources and learner attendance. Allocate funds for instructional materials, ICT resources, and learner support programs. Sustain monitoring and evaluation of learner performance to address gaps promptly.', 'Intensify learner monitoring, home visitation, and mentoring activities to encourage regular participation and completion of ALS requirements.', 'Strengthen teacher collaboration and provide additional training and resources for the development of quality contextualized learning materials.', 'Strengthen remediation initiatives and learner progress monitoring to improve achievement in reading comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics.', 'Continue promoting peace education and DepEd core values through meaningful integration in teaching strategies, classroom activities, and learner engagement.', 'Strengthen capacity-building activities for teachers on test item analysis to distribute responsibilities and ensure timely utilization of assessment results for instructional improvement.', '', 'Sustain child protection programs and strengthen school-wide awareness and monitoring to maintain a bullying-free learning environment.', 'Continue strengthening child protection mechanisms, awareness programs, and reporting systems to ensure a safe, secure, and abuse-free school environment.', 'Sustain and strengthen learner retention strategies and early intervention programs to further reduce drop-out incidence.', 'Continue promoting culture-sensitive and inclusive activities that respect and celebrate learners’ diverse cultural identities.', 'Sustain and strengthen inclusive education and ALS programs to ensure continuous access to learning opportunities for disadvantaged, OSY, and adult learners.', 'Sustain and further strengthen the school-based ALS program through continuous support, monitoring, and stakeholder engagement to ensure effective delivery and learner completion.', 'Sustain and strengthen the Child Protection Committee’s functions through regular monitoring, capacity building, and stakeholder collaboration to ensure a safe learning environment.', 'Sustain the implementation and regular updating of the DRRM plan through continuous coordination, capacity-building activities, and conduct of disaster preparedness drills and orientations.', 'Strengthen the school mental wellness program by establishing a clear referral pathway, regular psychosocial support activities, and coordination with trained mental health professionals. Conduct regular stress management and wellness programs for personnel and learners, and promote early intervention and confidential support mechanisms within the school.', 'Sustain and further improve SPED and PWD-friendly facilities through continuous upgrading of ramps, signage, learning materials, and assistive devices, and strengthen partnerships for additional support and funding for inclusive education.', 'Strengthen inclusive stakeholder engagement and regular review mechanisms to ensure that the strategic plan remains updated, data-driven, and aligned with school priorities and DepEd standards.', 'Strengthen scheduling flexibility and communication strategies to maximize stakeholder participation and sustain active engagement in school-community planning activities.', 'Strengthen leadership training and mentoring for SSG/SPG officers and encourage greater student participation in governance activities through structured programs and continuous guidance.', 'Strengthen ICT capacity-building for personnel and improve access to digital tools and systems to further enhance efficient, innovative, and responsive frontline services.', 'Strengthen regular monitoring, evaluation, and adjustment of the implementation plan to ensure alignment with priorities, efficient use of resources, and timely accomplishment of targets.', 'Strengthen scheduling coordination, communication, and engagement strategies to ensure regular participation of SGC members and sustain active and effective school governance.', 'Strengthen communication and scheduling flexibility for PTA activities and encourage greater parent engagement through regular consultation and inclusive participation strategies.', 'Strengthen coordination, communication, and scheduling of partnership activities and sustain engagement with stakeholders through regular consultation and collaborative planning.', 'Strengthen monitoring and evaluation system through streamlined reporting tools, task delegation, and capacity-building activities to ensure timely and accurate data analysis for decision-making.', 'Sustain performance monitoring and coaching mechanisms, provide workload rationalization where possible, and continue capacity-building to maintain and further improve personnel performance ratings.', 'Sustain strong performance monitoring and reporting systems, enhance task delegation and time management, and continue capacity-building activities to maintain and further improve OPCR results.', 'Strengthen regular scheduling of LAC sessions, ensure alignment with identified instructional needs, and sustain collaborative professional development activities to enhance teaching quality.', 'Sustain strong support for continuous professional development through proper scheduling, mentoring, and information dissemination on available training and promotion opportunities, and encourage equitable access to learning and development programs for all personnel.', 'Strengthen documentation and monitoring of personnel achievements and sustain recognition practices through planned activities and partnership support to ensure consistent and meaningful acknowledgment of milestones.', 'Sustain strict compliance with payroll requirements and ensure timely submission and validation of documents. Submission of Daily Time Records (DTR) is a must and strict deadlines must be followed; any DTR submitted beyond the deadline will no longer be accepted by the School HR to ensure timely payroll processing. Strengthen coordination with concerned offices to maintain accuracy and timeliness of compensation release.', 'Strengthen workload mapping and regular review of task distribution to ensure fairness and equity among personnel, and consider rationalization of assignments based on actual workload analysis and staffing capacity.', 'Strengthen regular monitoring and reporting system for facilities, prioritize urgent repairs, and enhance coordination with concerned offices and stakeholders to ensure timely maintenance and improvement of school infrastructure.', 'Strengthen prioritization of infrastructure projects, enhance partnership with stakeholders and LGU for resource generation, and continuously plan and advocate for facility improvement projects aligned with school development needs.', 'Prioritize the establishment of a school library through phased development, resource mobilization, and stakeholder support, including the provision of reading materials and designated space for a functional learning resource center.', 'Strengthen coordination with service providers to ensure stable utilities, maintain backup measures where possible, and regularly monitor facilities to minimize disruptions in school operations.', 'Prioritize upgrading and replacement of outdated computer units through resource mobilization and stakeholder support, strengthen partnerships for ICT donations, and ensure proper maintenance and maximized use of available ICT resources.', 'Sustain efficient financial planning and budgeting practices, strengthen timely submission of requirements, and ensure strict compliance with procurement and liquidation processes to maintain optimal MOOE utilization.', 'Sustain strict compliance with liquidation procedures, ensure timely submission of complete supporting documents, and strengthen monitoring of financial transactions to maintain 100% liquidation of utilized MOOE.', 'Sustain stakeholder engagement and continuously improve school services through feedback mechanisms, open communication channels, and regular review of performance to maintain and improve satisfaction ratings.', 1, 133, 12, 106),
(1299, '2026', '129758', 'Learners still struggle with advanced reading comprehension and word problems due to a lack of localized remedial materials.', 'Low mean percentage scores (MPS) in core subjects due to a lack of test-taking familiarity and gaps in critical thinking skills.', 'No available data since the school currently has no ALS learners.', '', '', '', 'Inconsistency in using item analysis results across all grade levels to actively modify day-to-day lesson delivery and remedial plans.', 'The school currently has no formal linkages with local industries. Learners have limited exposure to real-world applications of TLE-TVL skills, which affects competency development and industry readiness.', '', '', '', '', '', 'No available data since the school currently has no ALS learners.', 'Committee not fully organized', '', '', 'Absence of assistive devices, inadequate infrastructure such as ramps and accessible toilets', '', 'Irregular attendance of community representatives due to livelihood priorities, limited meeting schedules, and communication gaps with far-flung areas', 'No organized student government and lack of training on student leadership', 'Limited access to internet connectivity, lack of ICT resources, and difficulty in reaching stakeholders in remote areas', 'Limited resources affecting full implementation and  delays in activity execution due to distance and accessibility', 'SGC not fully organized, low participation of stakeholders due to livelihood priorities, and lack of awareness of roles and functions', '', '', '', 'Limited feedback collection due to stakeholders’ availability, lack of formal feedback mechanisms, and communication barriers in remote areas', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Intermittent electricity and weak or limited internet connectivity due to remote location', 'Lack of computers and ICT equipment, no dedicated laboratory space, and limited electricity and internet access', '', '', '', '', '', 'Regular conduct of sc