te analysis into regular LAC sessions', '', 'Sustain anti-bullying campaigns; strengthen peer mediation', 'Maintain reporting systems; conduct regular child protection seminars', 'strengthen home visitation', 'Institutional annual cultural events', 'Request LGU support for infrastructure', 'Provide flexible schedules ', 'Engage parents in awareness campaigns ', 'Conduct quarterly drills', 'establish peer support groups', 'Provide assistive devices', 'Conduct mid-year review', 'Expand stakeholder participation', 'Integrate student voice in school planning  ', 'Adopt digital platforms for efficiency', 'Strengthen monitoring and evaluation', '', 'Expand stakeholder involvement; conduct quarterly governance meetings', 'Increase parent engagement through regular assemblies', 'Forge stronger partnership with industries and NGO\'s', 'Provide continuous professional development; balance workload distribution', 'Streamline office processes; upgrade ICT tools', 'Institutionalized regular LAC sessions, invite external experts, integrate LAC outputs into school improvement plan', 'Institutionalize annual professional development plans, allocate funds for CPD activities', 'Conduct annual recognition ceremonies', 'strengthen coordination with DepEd finance offices', 'Strengthen equitable distribution through transparent workload planning', 'Strengthen reporting and documentation', 'Mobilize resources through LGU/PTA', '', 'Upgrade water system; request LGU support for water system', '', 'Conduct quarterly fund utilization reviews', 'Ensure timely liquidation reports', 'Strengthen feedback mechanism (surveys, forums);  conduct quarterly stakeholder satisfaction reviews', 1, 33, 12, 60),
(1307, '2026', '501555', 'Low reading readiness and foundational numeracy gaps; lack of localized, age-appropriate reading remedial tools in Mother Tongue/English/Math.', 'Low critical thinking and problem-solving skills among learners; unfamiliarity with the NAT assessment format and standard test-taking strategies.', 'High drop-out rates due to employment or family obligations; lack of learning centers or modular tracking systems for non-traditional learners.', 'Inconsistent quality assurance (QA) of teacher-made materials; lack of time/printing resources for mass distribution.', 'Teacher burnout due to ancillary tasks conflicting with remediation hours; overlapping schedules for struggling learners.', '', 'Difficulty of some teachers in utilizing test analysis software/spreadsheets; delayed utilization of results to adjust daily teaching plans', 'Weak or non-existent partnerships with local businesses; lack of matching between school TVL specializations and actual community market demands.', '', '', 'Poverty-related absences; family migration; lack of parental support; distance from school', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Incomplete ramps; lack of accessible restrooms; limited assistive devices; no designated SPED room', 'Lack of full attendance from all stakeholder groups during planning sessions.', '* Intermittent participation of community representatives due to conflicting work schedules.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Roles and responsibilities within the team are not fully documented or understood.', '', '', 'Some activities in the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) are delayed due to misalignment with the release schedules of downloaded funds (MOOE). And some unprogrammed needs and activities are being funded by the school MOOE.', '', '', '* Partnerships are often informal or lack structured Memorandums of Agreement (MOA).\r\n\r\n\r\n* Inter-school benchmarking or resource-sharing is rarely documented.', '', '* Feedback mechanisms are irregular (e.g., feedback drops are rarely filled out).\r\n\r\n\r\n* Low turn-around time on resolving minor complaints regarding frontline services.', '* A small percentage of teaching/non-teaching personnel struggle to meet outstanding ratings due to a lack of documented innovations or action research.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '* Lack of a dedicated room/space due to classroom shortages.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Deficiency in updated reading materials, references, and a designated school librarian.\r\n', '* Intermittent internet connectivity in rural building clusters.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Minor plumbing issues leading to low water pressure during peak hours.\r\n', '* No secure, air-conditioned room available to safely house technology assets.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Missing computer packages or uninstalled DCP (DepEd Computerization Program) batches.\r\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Strong administrative support, active integration of DepEd core values (Maka-Diyos, Makatao, Makalikasang, Makabansa) across all lesson plans (DLL/WHLP), and active EsP/Social Studies departments.', '', '', 'Strong anti-bullying policy; active peer mediation program; regular classroom guidance sessions; supportive school culture', 'Strong anti-child abuse policy; active peer mediation program; regular classroom guidance sessions; supportive school culture', '', 'Integration of local culture in curriculum; community involvement in school events; mother tongue-based instruction', 'Active ALS program; community mapping of out-of-school youth; flexible scheduling', 'Trained ALS teachers; community learning centers; stakeholder support; regular monitoring', 'Clear committee structure; trained members; regular meetings; known reporting protocols', 'Plans were crafted with the consultation of all concerned.', 'Designated guidance counselor/teacher; referral system; psychosocial activities; teacher training on mental health first aid', '', '', '', '* Strong leadership training programs.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Active mentorship from the faculty adviser.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Full administrative support and budget allocation for student-led initiatives.', '* Successful digitization of enrollment and request forms.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Well-trained, approachable administrative staff.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Clear Citizen’s Charter prominently displayed in the school lobby.', '', '* Clear definition of roles aligned with DepEd mandates.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Consistent quarterly meetings with high attendance.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Active participation in policy-making and school structural improvements.', '* High level of trust and open communication channels between school heads and PTA officers.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Prompt resolution of issues.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Active mobilization of parents during Brigada Eskwela and school events.', '', '* An active School Quality Management Team (SQMT).\r\n\r\n\r\n* Use of standard M&E templates and systematic data collection tools (e.g., SMEA/RMEA).', '', '', '* Clear alignment of school targets with division goals.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Strategic task delegation.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Regular mid-term performance reviews by the PMT (Performance Management Team).\r\n', '* Data gathered systematically from the Electronic Self-Assessment Tool (e-SAT).\r\n* Highly capable Teachers acting as LAC facilitators.', '* Transparent dissemination of ranking guidelines.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Active assistance from the school screening committee in checking personnel papers and requirements.\r\n', '* Institutionalized PRAISE (Rewards and Recognition) committee.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Allotment of local funds/donations for certificates, plaques, and incentives during world teachers\' day or end-of-year programs.\r\n', '* Efficient and prompt processing of paperwork by the school’s administrative/finance clerk.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Strong coordination with the Division payroll unit.\r\n', '* Strict adherence to DepEd guidelines on maximum teaching loads.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Collaborative scheduling during the programming phase before the school year starts.\r\n', '* Organized School Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (SDRRM) team.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Regular conducts of quarterly building inspections using standardized checklist forms.\r\n', '* Strong stakeholder support via Brigada Eskwela and minor repairs funded promptly through school MOOE allocation.', '', '', '', '* Clear, pre-approved Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) and Project Procurement Management Plan (PPMP) aligned directly with actual school expenditures.', '* Systematic record-keeping by the school bookkeeper/designated clerk.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Strict adherence to COA rules and division submission deadlines\r\n', 1, 1, 6, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5, 1, 2, 3, 5, 3, 2, 6, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 2, 6, 3, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 3, 3, 'Intensify the implementation of early literacy programs (e.g., Catch-Up Fridays, EGRA-based interventions); conduct targeted, regular tracking of struggling readers.', 'Institutionalize regular, diagnostic test-item analysis; integrate NAT-style parallel test questions in quarterly examinations; conduct targeted weekend or after-school review sessions for core subjects.', 'Formulate a flexible, localized home-visitation and hybrid modular tracking system; strengthen coordination with Barangay LGUs to provide financial/transportation mapping for ALS learners.', 'Establish a functional School Learning Resource Management Section (LRMS) committee to streamline the QA process; allocate school MOOE funds specifically for printing contextualized modules.', 'Designate a dedicated \"Remediation Hour\" in the class program; utilize peer-tutoring strategies (e.g., \"Big Brother/Sister\" system) to assist teachers in managing learning gaps.', 'Commitment: Sustain the practice by showcasing best practices in values integration during Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions; establish a school-wide reward system for exemplary learner behavior.', 'Conduct a targeted School LAC session on simplified digital test item analysis tools; require the submission of item analysis results alongside quarterly grades to immediately adjust lesson pacing.', 'Establish formal Memorandums of Agreement (MOA) with local industries for work immersion; invite local entrepreneurs and TESDA representatives for a stakeholder mapping and curriculum alignment summit. The school is not approved to offered such offerings.', 'Continue monitoring; sustain awareness campaigns\r\n\r\n', 'Continue monitoring; sustain awareness campaigns\r\n\r\n', 'Strengthen feeding programs; home visitation; coordinate with barangay for tracking at-risk learners', 'Sustain partnerships with cultural groups; document best practices', 'Continue outreach; expand mobile teacher deployment', 'Sustain program; seek additional learning materials', 'Continue capacity-building; update protocols annually', 'Continue for updating and improvement of the plan.', 'Sustain programs; strengthen referral network with community health units', 'Request MOOE allocation for accessibility improvements; coordinate with LGU/NGOs for assistive devices', 'Conduct weekend or hybrid (online/offline) planning workshops to increase stakeholder attendance.', '* Formalize membership through a Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) or official school order.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Provide orientation briefings and establish a predictable, quarterly meeting schedule.', 'Commitment: Sustain the program by institutionalizing an annual student leadership handover seminar and maintaining an open-door policy for student proposals.', 'Commitment: Continuous upgrade of digital infrastructure (e.g., school website/portal) and regular customer feedback surveys to maintain high service standards.', 'Conduct quarterly reviews of the AIP to realign timelines and adjust procurement paths based on actual fund releases. Then if there is a need to revise the AIP/APP, do the revision.', '* Commitment: Sustain active operations by institutionalizing a digital dashboard for tracking SGC resolutions and community feedback.25. The school has a functional Parent-Teacher Association (PTA)Always ManifestedN/A* High level of trust and open communication channels between school heads and PTA officers.* Prompt resolution of issues.* Active mobilization of parents during Brigada Eskwela and school events.Social / Financial* Commitment: Maintain strong engagement by continuing transparent financial transparency reporting of PTA collections and co-managed projects.26. The school collaborates with stakeholders and other schools in strengthening partnershipsFrequently Manifested [Assumed]* Partnerships are often informal or lack structured Memorandums of Agreement (MOA).* Inter-school benchmarking or resource-sharing is rarely documented.N/ASocial / Technical* Establish a dedicated Partnership and Linkages Committee to formalize local stakeholder agreements.* Create a structured calendar for inter-school learning action cells (LAC sessions).27. The school monitors and evaluates its programs, projects, and activitiesAlways ManifestedN/A* An active School Quality Management Team (SQMT).* Use of standard M&E templates and systematic data collection tools (e.g., SMEA/RMEA).Technical / Institutional* Commitment: Institutionalize mid-year and end-of-year School Monitoring, Evaluation, and Adjustment (SMEA) conferences to quickly pivot failing programs.28. The school maintains an average rating of satisfactory from its internal and external stakeholdersFrequently Manifested* Feedback mechanisms are irregular (e.g., feedback drops are rarely filled out).* Low turn-around time on resolving minor complaints regarding frontline services.N/A (Not Always Manifested)Technical / Social* Transition to digital feedback systems (such as QR-code based survey forms at exit points).* Implement a strict 3-day turnaround policy for handling non-complex stakeholder issues.', '* Commitment: Maintain strong engagement by continuing transparent financial transparency reporting of PTA collections and co-managed projects.', '* Establish a dedicated Partnership and Linkages Committee to formalize local stakeholder agreements.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Create a structured calendar for inter-school learning action cells (LAC sessions).', '* Commitment: Institutionalize mid-year and end-of-year School Monitoring, Evaluation, and Adjustment (SMEA) conferences to quickly pivot failing programs.', '* Conduct specialized mentoring and coaching sessions on action research, innovation development, and portfolio preparation prior to the phase 3 review.', '* Commitment: Maintain a data-driven tracking system for school targets to ensure timely adjustment of strategies during mid-year reviews', '* Commitment: Maximize the utilization of LAC sessions to address emerging gaps in digital literacy and localized instructional materials.', '* Commitment: Continue updating the personnel roster regarding their qualifications and actively encourage teachers to enroll in post-graduate studies.', '* Commitment: Sustain morale by diversifying recognition categories to include non-teaching staff achievements and perfect attendance.', '* Commitment: Ensure 100% accuracy and zero delay in the submission of Daily Time Records (DTRs) and Form 7 to prevent payroll discrepancies.', '* Commitment: Continue to utilize objective ancillary assignment matrices to balance teaching and non-teaching loads fairly among all personnel', '* Commitment: Maintain a monthly inspection routine and digitize logs to ensure rapid reporting of structural hazards to the division office.', '* Commitment: Continue to allocate emergency local funds for immediate minor repairs and maximize partnerships with the LGU for larger structural renovations', '* Establish a \"Reading Corner\" or localized mini-library in individual classrooms as an interim solution.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Submit a formal request to the division office for a non-teaching librarian position and source book donations via external stakeholders/NGOs.\r\n', '* Upgrade the internet subscription or procure additional signal boosters/routers for far buildings.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Allot a portion of the upcoming MOOE cycle for plumbing repairs and maintenance.\r\n', '* Retrofit an existing storage room with security bars and proper ventilation to act as a temporary computer lab.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Coordinate with the Division IT Officer to fast-track the deployment and setup of pending DCP packages.\r\n', '* Commitment: Sustain high utilization rates through systematic procurement planning and monthly internal tracking of cash advances against planned activities.', '* Commitment: Continue the practice of zero-backlog liquidation by finalizing financial documents within 5 working days following the end of each calendar month', '* Transition to digital feedback systems (such as QR-code based survey forms at exit points).\r\n\r\n\r\n* Implement a strict 3-day turnaround policy for handling non-complex stakeholder issues.', 1, 8, 12, 61),
