ness of the school-community planning team', 'Student leaders need more capacity-building activities and guidance from advisers.', '', 'Strong leadership support, active participation of stakeholders, and clear implementation guidelines', 'Active collaboration between school heads, teachers, parents, and community officials', 'Supportive parents and regular PTA coordination meetings', 'Strong community linkages and support from partner institutions', 'Availability of monitoring tools and cooperation of school personnel', 'Continuous delivery of quality services and open communication channels', 'Strong administrative support and commitment of personnel to performance standards', 'Cooperation among office personnel and availability of monitoring tools', 'Active participation of teachers and support from school leadership', 'Commitment of personnel to professional growth and support from school management', 'Positive school culture and appreciation from school leadership', 'Efficient coordination with finance and administrative offices', 'Clear workload policies, collaborative planning, and support from school administration', 'Regular conduct of quarterly school facility inspections by the School Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (SDRRM) committee and school head.', 'Strong partnership with the PTA, alumni, and local stakeholders through Brigada Eskwela and targeted donations.', '', 'Prompt payment of utility bills using MOOE funds and functional partnerships with the local electric cooperative and water district.', '', 'Systematic planning via the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP), alongside a proactive School Finance Team.', 'Regular updating of books of accounts, adherence to COA rules, and timely submission of liquidation reports to the division office.', 1, 1, 6, 3, 2, 2, 1, 3, 6, 6, 6, 6, 2, 5, 2, 5, 6, 5, 6, 6, 6, 5, 1, 6, 6, 2, 1, 6, 1, 2, 1, 3, 6, 3, 2, 5, 2, 5, 3, 1, 3, 3, 'Sustain remediation and enrichment activities: