esources through proper planning', 'Conduct regular meetings, improve communication, and encourage active participation of all SGC members', 'Increase parent engagement through flexible schedules, information drives, and recognition of active participation', 'Maintain regular communication, strengthen partnership agreements, and conduct periodic coordination meetings', 'Enhance monitoring systems, assign focal persons, and provide training on evaluation processes', 'Provide continuous coaching, streamline documentation processes, and strengthen monitoring of performance outputs', 'Improve work delegation, establish clear timelines, and enhance coordination among staff', 'Conduct regular needs assessment, maximize available training resources, and schedule LAC activities effectively', 'Allocate budget for professional development and encourage participation in free online and external trainings', 'Develop a structured recognition program and seek stakeholder support for incentive initiatives.', 'Strengthen coordination with concerned offices, ensure timely submission of documents, and improve tracking systems', 'Continue regular review of teaching loads, ensure equitable distribution of assignments, and maintain open communication among personnel.', 'To sustain weekly/monthly walkthroughs and institutionalize preventive maintenance checklists.', 'Continue active engagement with stakeholders and maximize the utilization of local school funds for minor repairs.', 'Allocate a dedicated room for the library, request reading materials from partners/DepEd, and assign a teacher-librarian.', 'Ensure prompt, priority allocation of monthly operational funds to maintain seamless utility and water bill.', 'Submit a proposal for the DepEd Computerization Program (DCP) and partner with local ICT stakeholders for technical support/donations.', 'Continue strict adherence to the procurement plan and quarterly cash program to maintain high utilization rates.', 'Maintain the regular practice of zero-backlog liquidation and undergo continuous financial management mentoring.', 'Improve feedback mechanisms, utilize online surveys, and strengthen stakeholder relations and communication.', 1, 133, 12, 106),
(1318, '2026', '304220', '', 'Low proficient in the recent result of NAT conducted', '', 'Insufficient budget ', 'Lacks interest or support of parents ', 'Only in selected subjects /topics such Values Education', 'Only in quarterly Exam but not in all assessment conducted such as daily quizzes', '', 'There are still reported cases of bullying but we immediately resolve the issue by calling the students and parents', 'There are reported cases of abuse with their own families. ', 'Disinterested to go to school . Lack of support of parents', 'Inclusion of learners and stakeholders through IP and Parents Day.', 'We offered Senior  ALS Program ', 'We produced ALS graduates for 2 consecutives years . Increase the number of enrollees for ALS ', '', 'Lack of facilities and equipment on its implementation', 'We rarely conducted mental wellness activities and programs', 'Limited facilities and  lack SNED Teachers', 'Insufficient budget , alignment of targets to other agencies , New Target Indicators', 'Unavailability of time of some stakeholders ', '', 'We adhere to our citizens charter in catering our services and having a feedback mechanism.', 'Change of Priorities and sometimes delayed downloaded of budget.', '', '', '', 'Conducts evaluation and feedback mechanism', 'Based on the results of our feedback mechanisms, mostly of our clients were satisfied of our services rendered  ', '', '', 'Lack of time or conflict of time in conducting learning action Cells', 'Through NSET , LAC Sessions and attended training and seminars , school , division , regional and national level.', 'Limited time for conducting recognition program .', '', 'There are teachers required to teach to subjects not their specialization', 'Lack expertise, sometimes request from LGU Engineering office delayed response  ', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Work Immersion and  JDVP Training 100% Passing Rate NCII', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Functional and Committed members of the program /organization ', '', '', '', '', '', 'Functional , Active Leaders ', '', '', 'Active and Supportive Stakeholders ', 'Active and Supportive parents', 'Through MOA and MOU signing.', '', '', 'Based on the results of their IPCRF and OPCR . Consistently achieved Very Satisfactorily ', 'Based on the results of their IPCRF and OPCR . Consistently achieved Very Satisfactorily', '', '', '', 'Updated Salaries and other benefits.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 0, 2, 0, 3, 2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 6, 6, 6, 2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 2, 3, 6, 2, 2, 3, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 0, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', 'To improve learners’ proficiency levels, we commit to strengthening intervention programs, conducting regular remediation sessions, and enhancing teaching strategies aligned with NAT competencies.”\r\n“The school commits to implementing intensive reading and numeracy programs, continuous assessment monitoring, and collaborative learning activities to address the low proficiency reflected in the recent NAT results.”\r\n“Teachers and stakeholders will work together to provide targeted interventions, enrichment activities, and close learner monitoring to improve academic performance in future NAT assessments.”\r\n“We resolve to intensify review classes, integrate competency-based instruction, and provide consistent learner support to increase proficiency levels in the next NAT administration.”\r\n“The institution commits to improving instructional delivery through teacher training, data-driven interventions, and active parental involvement to raise NAT performance outcomes.”', '', '“The school commits to maximizing available resources, strengthening partnerships with stakeholders, and seeking additional funding sources to address the insufficient budget.”\r\n“We resolve to prioritize essential programs and activities while exploring resource-generation initiatives and external support to supplement the limited budget.”\r\n“The institution commits to practicing efficient financial management and collaborating with stakeholders to ensure continuous support despite budget limitations.”\r\n“The school will intensify coordination with local government units, parents, and community partners to secure additional resources and sustain school programs.”\r\n“We commit to implementing cost-effective strategies and transparent budgeting to ensure that priority educational needs are adequately supported.”', 'The school commits to strengthening parent engagement through regular communication, meetings, and collaborative activities to encourage greater support for learners.”\r\n“We resolve to conduct parent orientation programs and awareness campaigns to emphasize the importance of parental involvement in students’ academic performance.”\r\n“Teachers and school personnel will work closely with parents through home visitations, conferences, and monitoring to improve learner support at home.”\r\n“The institution commits to building stronger partnerships with parents and stakeholders to foster a supportive learning environment for all learners.”\r\n“We commit to creating more inclusive and participatory school programs that encourage active parental involvement in school activities and learner development', 'The school commits to strengthening instruction and enrichment activities in selected subjects such as Values Education to improve learner understanding and engagement.”\r\n“We resolve to provide targeted interventions, contextualized learning materials, and regular monitoring in identified subject areas needing improvement, particularly Values Education.”\r\n“Teachers will enhance teaching strategies and integrate values formation activities across learning areas to reinforce competencies in Values Education.”\r\n“The institution commits to conducting focused review sessions and collaborative learning activities in selected topics and subjects to improve learner performance.”\r\n“We commit to promoting the importance of Values Education through school-based programs, learner participation, and strengthened classroom integration.”', 'The school resolves to strengthen the implementation of varied assessment tools such as daily quizzes, performance tasks, and periodic tests to promote continuous learner improvement and not rely solely on quarterly examination results.', 'The school commits to sustaining the 100% passing rate in Work Immersion and JDVP Training NC II through continuous skills enhancement, competency-based training, and close monitoring of learners’ performance.', 'The institution commits to enforcing the anti-bullying policy consistently and fostering open communication among learners, parents, and teachers to prevent and resolve bullying incidents effectively.We resolve to strengthen anti-bullying programs, conduct regular awareness activities, and ensure immediate intervention through conferences with students and parents whenever incidents are reported.', 'The school commits to providing immediate support and appropriate intervention for learners with reported cases of family abuse through proper coordination with parents, guidance personnel, and concerned authorities while ensuring the learners’ safety and well-being.', 'The school commits to strengthening learner motivation and parental involvement through regular counseling, home visitations, parent-teacher conferences, and school engagement activities to encourage consistent school attendance.”', 'The institution commits to sustaining inclusive programs and activities that recognize the importance of Indigenous Peoples and parental involvement in supporting learner development and school success.', '“The institution commits to expanding access and participation in the Senior ALS Program by strengthening partnerships with stakeholders and ensuring quality delivery of learning interventions for all ALS learners.', 'We resolve to build on the achievement of producing ALS graduates for two consecutive years by intensifying information campaigns, community partnerships, and recruitment activities to boost ALS enrollment.', 'The school commits to strengthening the functionality and commitment of program/organization members through continuous capacity building, clear role assignment, and regular monitoring of responsibilities.”', 'The school commits to addressing the lack of facilities and equipment by prioritizing resource allocation, improving procurement planning, and seeking support from stakeholders and partner agencies to enhance program implementation.', 'he institution commits to integrating mental wellness initiatives into school programs and ensuring consistent activities that promote resilience, self-care, and positive mental health among learners.”', 'The institution commits to improving inclusive education services by seeking partnerships with stakeholders, optimizing available resources, and advocating for the hiring or assignment of additional SNED teachers to better serve learners with special needs.”We resolve to strengthen support for SNED learners through the enhancement of available facilities, provision of appropriate learning materials, and continuous advocacy for additional trained SNED teachers.”', 'The institution commits to improving planning and performance management by aligning targets with partner agencies, integrating updated target indicators, and advocating for additional budget support to sustain program implementation', 'The institution commits to improving stakeholder involvement by implementing flexible participation arrangements, consistent updates, and stronger collaboration strategies to ensure continuous engagement even with limited availability.', 'The institution commits to promoting active and functional leadership by fostering accountability, teamwork, and consistent engagement of leaders in the implementation of school initiatives.”', 'he school commits to consistently adhering to the Citizens’ Charter in the delivery of services and strengthening the feedback mechanism to ensure transparency, accountability, and continuous improvement.”', 'The institution commits to enhancing budget management through proactive planning, strict adherence to approved priorities, and continuous coordination with funding agencies to address delays in budget download', 'The institution commits to building and sustaining active and supportive stakeholders by fostering strong linkages, regular consultation, and shared responsibility in achieving school goals.', 'The institution commits to sustaining active and supportive parents by fostering strong home-school partnerships, regular feedback mechanisms, and inclusive participation in school initiatives.”', 'The institution commits to establishing and maintaining strong linkages with stakeholders through MOA and MOU agreements to enhance cooperation and ensure the successful implementation of programs and initiatives.”', 'The institution commits to sustaining an effective evaluation and feedback mechanism to monitor performance, identify gaps, and enhance the quality of service delivery and school programs.', 'The school commits to sustaining the consistent Very Satisfactory performance in IPCRF and OPCRF results by continuously enhancing individual and organizational competencies through targeted professional development and performance monitoring.”', 'The school commits to sustaining the consistent Very Satisfactory performance in IPCRF and OPCRF results by continuously enhancing individual and organizational competencies through targeted professional development and performance monitoring.”', 'The school commits to improving the scheduling and implementation of Learning Action Cells (LAC) sessions by setting a fixed timetable and ensuring that activities are aligned with teachers’ availability to avoid conflicts of time.', 'he school commits to strengthening teacher competence through continuous participation in NSET, LAC sessions, and relevant trainings and seminars at the school, division, regional, and national levels to enhance instructional quality.”', 'he school commits to improving the planning and scheduling of recognition programs by setting a fixed timeline and integrating the activity into the annual school calendar to ensure proper implementation despite limited time.”', 'The institution commits to supporting personnel welfare by strengthening coordination with relevant agencies to facilitate the prompt updating and processing of salaries and other benefits.”', 'The school commits to improving teacher assignment by aligning teaching loads with subject specialization whenever possible, while providing necessary support and training for teachers handling non-specialized subjects', 'The institution commits to improving coordination and technical assistance processes through advance planning, stronger stakeholder engagement, and continuous follow-up with concerned offices to minimize delays in engineering-related requests', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'The school commits to sustaining high levels of client satisfaction by continuously improving service delivery based on feedback results and maintaining responsive and efficient transactions.”', 1, 132, 12, NULL);
