(1330, '2026', '128726', '', '', 'Not Applicable.', '', '', '', '', 'Not Applicable.', 'Occasional playground arguments or rowdy behavior among learners during recess which require close teacher monitoring to prevent potential bullying.', 'The constant need to reinforce positive classroom management techniques among teachers to ensure traditional disciplinary actions never cross into emotional distress for learners.', 'A small number of learners are at risk of dropping out due to seasonal absenteeism caused by family economic situations or long walking distances to school.', 'Limited readily available localized reading materials that explicitly highlight the distinct cultural backgrounds present within our local community.', 'Challenges in tracking and locating school-aged children in remote areas of the community who are not currently enrolled in formal education.', 'Not Applicable.', 'The need for routine re-orientation for committee members regarding their specific duties in handling learner behavioral adjustments.', 'Ensuring constant emergency preparedness and swift evacuation understanding among very young learners (Kinder to Grade 3) during sudden natural hazards.', 'Teachers have limited specialized training to fully address complex emotional anxieties or behavioral stress displayed by learners due to domestic issues.', 'The school lacks standardized concrete ramps or safety handrails in some older school buildings for learners with physical disabilities.', 'Aligning all specific targets in the school implementation plan with the shifting immediate learning priorities and available school maintenance resources.', 'Finding mutually convenient meeting schedules that match the personal work availability of community representatives and barangay partners.', 'The student leaders need constant guidance and structured mentoring to independently organize and run their school-wide student activities.', 'Occasional delays in releasing physical school records and answering stakeholder inquiries during peak enrollment periods.', 'Occasional difficulties in fully balancing school improvement targets with the immediate scheduling limitations of the regular school calendar.', 'Challenges in finding unified meeting schedules that match the varied personal work availability of the different council members.', 'Slight communication gaps in cascading general assembly agreements to parents who are unable to attend scheduled school meetings.', 'The need to continuously expand the school\'s local partner network to include more community-based resource supporters.', 'Time constraints for committee members who must balance manual tracking and consolidation of school data with their primary classroom teaching loads.', 'The need for a more consistent, routine method to capture and review feedback from occasional visitors and community transactors.', 'A few school personnel require continuous mentoring to help them smoothly gather and organize physical documentation for all their performance objectives.', 'The challenge of ensuring all separate school committees complete and submit their program reports on time to consolidate the final school performance review.', 'Finding open, uninterrupted time slots within the busy school calendar for teachers to hold long, deep professional development sessions without disrupting regular classes.', 'Limited local opportunities or resources for personnel to attend specialized external training or advanced professional seminars.', 'The need to establish a more regular, routine schedule to celebrate small, everyday teaching milestones alongside big annual awards.', 'Occasional delays in collecting and verifying physical daily time records and supporting papers due to overlapping school tasks at the end of the month.', 'The challenge of evenly balancing non-teaching administrative assignments among teachers while ensuring their primary classroom instruction hours are protected.', 'Conducting thorough, routine physical facility inspections can sometimes be delayed during periods of heavy administrative and classroom workloads.', 'Limited local maintenance funds to instantly cover larger, structural repairs or facility upgrades all at once.', 'The library space needs a continuous supply of updated, age-appropriate storybooks and reference materials across all elementary grade levels.', 'Occasional disruptions or weak signals in our local internet connectivity, which can temporarily limit online communication and research.', 'not applicable', 'Carefully balancing the pacing of month-to-month operational expenses with shifting or immediate school emergency needs.', 'Time constraints in consolidating and verifying all physical liquidation documents on time due to a heavy load of overlapping administrative tasks.', 'Consistent implementation of targeted reading programs like Catch-up Fridays and active utilization of early literacy learning resources.', 'onsistent implementation of structured NAT review drills, utilization of localized test item banks, and regular diagnostic tracking.', '', 'Active collaborative culture during weekly School Learning Action Cell (SLAC) sessions and readily available localized source materials within the community.', 'Teachers have high compliance and readiness to utilize open class schedules (such as Catch-up Fridays) for structured learning intervention.', 'Teachers display deep alignment with DepEd core values and strictly follow the explicit value-integration suggestions in the MATATAG curriculum guides.', 'The school utilizes standardized, automated Excel-based item analysis templates that generate rapid diagnostic summaries.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 0, 2, 5, 6, 5, 2, 6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 6, 6, 1, 6, 2, 2, 1, 5, 6, 2, 2, 5, 5, 5, 5, 1, 3, 3, 'Provide targeted, level-appropriate reading and numeracy intervention materials to help lagging learners achieve full baseline proficiency.', 'Expose learners to regular, timed test-taking simulations and localized practice item banks designed around higher-order thinking skills (HOTS).', 'Not Applicable.', 'Upskill teachers in digital material creation and software tools through hands-on ICT peer-coaching during School Learning Action Cells (SLAC).', 'Maximize collaborative teacher-planning sessions during regular grade-level meetings to co-create, share, and distribute standardized remedial worksheets.', 'Conduct collaborative lesson study and peer-mentoring sessions to help teachers develop and exchange seamless value-integration lesson exemplars.', 'Enforce a strict, uniform data-submission timeline right after every periodic examination to generate immediate, school-wide instructional adjustments.', 'Not Applicable.', 'Ensure teachers deliver daily positive behavior reminders before classes start and maintain active teacher supervision during recess.', 'Discuss positive discipline strategies during regular faculty meetings and strictly uphold the DepEd Child Protection Policy principles.', 'Conduct timely teacher-led home visitations or immediate parental dialogues for learners showing signs of chronic absenteeism.', 'Encourage teachers to integrate local history, community stories, and diverse cultural examples into their daily lesson discussions.', 'Coordinate closely with local barangay officials to locate out-of-school children and facilitate their standard enrollment into regular classes.', 'Not Applicable.', 'Convene regular committee meetings to review school safety conditions and update child protection posters in visible areas.', 'Conduct regular classroom evacuation drills and verify that all emergency exit paths are completely clear of obstructions.', 'Maximize the use of Homeroom Guidance periods to focus on emotional expression, self-care, and building a kind classroom environment.', 'Allocate a portion of available school maintenance funds to gradually install simple access pathways and wooden safety railings in high-priority zones.', 'Conduct regular mid-year reviews of our strategic planning targets to ensure all school projects remain practical, attainable, and responsive to learner needs.', 'Provide flexible communication updates and schedule planning consultations well in advance to ensure optimal stakeholder representation.', 'Implement simple leadership mentoring sessions for elected pupil officers to build their confidence in managing student-led campus initiatives.', 'Streamline the physical filing system and establish designated, clear public transaction hours to serve transacting parents and visitors more efficiently.', 'Conduct regular adjustments during monthly meetings to ensure implementation targets stay realistically aligned with school timelines.', 'Provide highly flexible meeting options and announce council schedules well in advance to ensure continuous stakeholder participation.', 'Strong parental volunteer spirit and constant support from elected PTA officers during school-led projects.', 'Actively present clear school needs to community stakeholders during advocacy meetings to secure stable partnership commitments.', 'Streamline the data consolidation schedule so the monitoring team can quickly provide actionable adjustments for school activities.', 'Conduct regular mid-year performance reviews and peer mentoring to guide personnel in maintaining organized portfolios.', 'Establish regular monthly progress checks with committee chairs to keep all school operational targets on track throughout the year.', 'Plan short, highly focused grade-level learning sessions during designated professional development hours to maximize learning without affecting class time.', 'Consistently support and recommend eligible school personnel for district or division training opportunities to enhance their career growth.', 'Institutionalize simple appreciation gestures, such as formal certificates of recognition during regular faculty meetings, to boost teacher morale.', 'Set a clear internal deadline for submitting complete monthly attendance papers to ensure the division office receives them on time.', 'Review the school ancillary list annually to redistribute extra duties fairly.', 'Establish a fixed, simple monthly schedule for routine classroom and facility walkthroughs to ensure timely tracking of maintenance issues.', 'Prioritize high-necessity safety and learning infrastructure repairs first in our physical development planning throughout the school year.', 'Organize existing reading materials clearly by grade level and safely allocate standard school resources over time to add fresh learning books.', 'Maintain basic utility systems carefully and coordinate with service providers to quickly report and resolve network connectivity issues.', 'not applicable', 'Review monthly project expenditures consistently to ensure funds are spent efficiently and on schedule for critical school needs.', 'Streamline the submission schedule and allocate dedicated, uninterrupted hours to focus purely on monthly liquidation reports.', 'Maintain an easily accessible physical suggestion box at the school\'s receiving area to routinely collect and address stakeholder feedback.', 1, 133, 12, 106),
