(69, 'Conduct Orientation on DepEd Order 7, series of 2024 for teachers and SPTA Officers', '*To familiarize the DepEd Order No. 7, s. 2025\r\n*To emphasize the role of internal and extenal stakeholders in School-Based Management\r\n*To plan for the organization of SGC', '*Shared commitment for School Improvement\r\n*No overlapping of functions\r\n*Strong partnership with unternal and external stakeholders', 'Face to face Orientation', 'September 15-30, 2025', 'Teachers, School Head, SPTA Officers', '3000.00', '', 2025, 128455, 57, 12, 121),
(70, '“Basa Para sa Kinabukasan: A Reading Development Program”', 'a.	Enhance reading comprehension and fluency among students at every grade level\r\nb.	Identify and assist students who are facing challenges with reading, implementing targeted remediation and intervention strategies.\r\nc.	Foster a culture of reading b', 'Remedial and guided reading sessions are structured to provide targeted support to struggling readers and to facilitate peer mentoring relationships between older and younger students.\r\n• The initiative \"Basa Ko, Share Ko\" entails weekly storytelling sessions conducted by teachers, students, or community elders featuring local and indigenous narratives.\r\n• Monthly Read-a-thons and Reading Camps are organized to host reading competitions and activities aimed at fostering a deeper interest in reading among participants.\r\n• The establishment of \"Aklat para sa Tribu\" Reading Corners involves setting up miniature reading spaces equipped with books in both local dialects and the Filipino language.\r\n• Parent and community engagement strategies encompass the implementation of home reading logs, parent-led storytelling sessions, and the solicitation of community book donations to further support literacy initiatives.\r\n', 'The daily implementation of the project has been allocated at least 50 minutes per day', 'From  June to march 2025', 'School Head, Teacher, Tutor', '20000', 'For implementation', 2025, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
(72, 'LAC sa Galing: Collaborative Learning for Teachers\r\n\r\n', 'To strengthen teacher competencies in lesson contextualization and IPED implementation.\r\n- To enhance technological proficiency among teachers, including the use of Artificial Intelligence and digital tools.\r\n- To foster collaboration and shared lear', '. Monthly LAC Sessions\r\nA dedicated vacant time once a month was institutionalized for LAC sessions. These sessions covered:\r\n- Contextualization of lesson plans using Bagobo-Tagabawa IKSP.\r\n- Integration of AI tools for grading, reporting, and instructional delivery.\r\n- Orientation on DepEd priority programs and school-based projects.\r\n2. Technology Integration\r\nTeachers were trained to use laptops issued by the DepEd Central Office. Sessions included:\r\n- Using AI for lesson planning and assessment.\r\n- Digital tools for ADM implementation and reading interventions.\r\n- Online collaboration platforms for resource sharing.\r\n3. IPED Capacity Building\r\nSpecial LAC sessions focused on:\r\n- Understanding Bagobo-Tagabawa history, values, and practices.\r\n- Designing culturally responsive learning materials.\r\n- Engaging with tribal elders and culture bearers for authentic learning experiences.\r\n4. Collaborative Culture\r\nThe project fostered a culture of shared leadership and peer mentoring. Teachers supported one another in navigating both technological and cultural learning curves.\r\n', 'Monthly implementation of the project at least 2 times every month', 'From  June to march 2025', 'School Head, Teacher, LAC Leder', '20000', 'for Implementation', 2025, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
(73, 'ARIEL', 'YEL', 'AA', 'A', 'A', 'AA', '2', '2', 2025, 129120, 60, 12, 25),
(74, ' Awareness and Capacity Building', 'Increase awareness of CPP among learners, teachers, parents, and community', 'Conduct orientation on DepEd Order No. 40, s. 2012 and Anti-Bullying Law\r\n- Integrate CPP in LAC sessions\r\n- Translate key CPP concepts into local dialect for IP learners', 'Conduct regular meetings with the focal persons, recording of incidents', 'From  June to march 2025', 'School Head, Teacher', '20000', 'for implementation', 2025, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
