(85, 'Electrification Project', 'To install electrical wiring for 5 classroom buildings and 1 Home Economics building by the 1st quarter of 2026.', 'Installed electrical wiring in 5 classroom buildings and the H.E. building.', '1. Procurement of wiring supplies\r\n2. Installation of electrical wiring.', 'January- March, 2026', 'MOOE TWGs/ Skilled electrician / Division Ins', '82,588.30', '1ST PHASE- ( 3 classroom buildings and the Home Economics building) will be implemented in the 1st quarter of SY 2025-2026 using JHS MOOE\r\n ( Php 82,588.30).\r\n2nd PHASE- ( 2 classroom buildings ) will be implemented in the 2nd quarter of SY 2025-2026 using JHS MOOE ( Php 80,000.00).', 2025, 501063, 107, 12, 89),
(87, 'Capacity Building for MGIS Teaching and Non-Teaching Personnel on Designing Reading Programs for Struggling Readers', 'To increase the reading proficiency level of MGIS across all grade levels and learning areas\r\nTo implement appropriate reading intervention program for the struggling readers of MGIS', 'Approved Reading Program Contextually Designed for the struggling readers of MGIS', 'Design activity proposal\r\nSubmit and seek approval for the designed activity\r\nImplement Activity\r\nEvaluate the Activity\r\nSubmit Accomplishment Report', 'Second Quarter of SY 2025-2026', 'School Head, All Teaching Personnel', '1500', '', 2025, 501060, 107, 12, 89),
(88, 'Capacitate Teachers on D.O 7 s 2024', '1.) Enhance Teaching Competencies Across Learning Areas  \r\n\r\n2.) Promote Effective Use of E-Learning Strategies \r\n\r\n3.) Support Learning Recovery in Literacy and Numeracy', '1.) Improved Teaching Skills and Competencies - Teachers demonstrate enhanced knowledge and mastery of subject content, teaching strategies, and classroom management techniques aligned with the Revised K-12 Curriculum. This leads to more effective lesson delivery and improved student engagement.\r\n2.) Increased Use of E-Learning and 21st Century Teaching Strategies- Teachers integrate digital tools and innovative e-learning strategies into their classrooms, creating more interactive and learner-centered environments that cater to diverse student needs.', '1.) Blended Learning Approach- Programs like the Master Classes for Kindergarten and Grades 1, 4, and 7 (K147) teachers aim to strengthen teacher collaboration and support the implementation of the Revised K-12 Curriculum. These master classes encourage educators to work together, share knowledge, and continuously improve outcomes through shared leadership and collective learning. By participating in such programs, teachers can enhance their subject matter knowledge and teaching techniques, leading to improved instructional quality.\r\n2.) Collaborative Learning and Peer Coaching- Encourage teachers to work in teams or professional learning communities where they can share experiences, co-develop lesson plans, and provide peer feedback to enhance teaching practices.', 'OCTOBER 5- NOVEMBER 5, 2025 ', 'SCHOOL HEAD , TEACHERS', 'MOOE - 5000.00 ', '', 2025, 502888, 107, 12, 89),
(91, 'Capacity Building of  Head Teachers, Master Teachers, and Teachers on DO7 S. 2024', 'To equip teachers with the knowledge and skills to implement the Revised SBM System ', 'Individual Development Plans for Teachers: Improved Teaching Competence, Enhanced Professional Development', 'Coaching and Mentoring, SLACs, In-service Trainings, Monitoring and Evaluation, Motivation and Recognition', 'October 31, 2025', 'School Head, Assistant to the School Principa', '2000', 'To be cascaded', 2025, 304379, 107, 12, 89),
(92, 'Capacity building of the teachers  of the DepEd order No. 07, s2023', 'to provide teachers the knowledge relevant for their professional development', 'All teachers will increase their individual skills and develop new goals on their career paths', 'Discussion, Workshops and Assessment', '1 Quarter', 'School Head, All Teachers', '1500', 'None', 2025, 305500, 107, 12, 89),
(93, 'Re orientation of the DO 7, s 2024- Policy Guidelines on the Implementation of the Revised School-Based Management System.', 'Strengthen capacity programs for school leaders and SBM Committees', 'Enhance the implementation of the School-Based Management', 'Developing school improvements plans, impowering stakeholders to lead and collaborate', 'June', 'School Head and All Teachers', '1000', '', 2025, 501069, 107, 12, 89),
(94, 'Tree Planting for a Greener Tomorrow', '- to involve learners in community-based projects \r\n- to promote environmental awareness and responsibilities \r\n- to strengthen school-community partnerships through collective action and sustainability projects', '- Plant at least 200 seedlings in school site and in the community ', '- preparation phase: planning and coordination\r\n    *identify the areas for tree planting\r\n    *coordinate with barangay officials as to the seedlings request\r\n    *involve the learners, teachers, and brgy officials \r\n    *orient learners as to the importance of the activity \r\n- implementation phase: \r\n    *tree planting \r\n    *documentation \r\n- post-planning phase  \r\n     *monitoring and maintenance \r\n     *evaluation of the event\r\n     *subject integration', 'December 2025', '- learners, teachers, school head, CSU, commu', '3000.00', '*Activity will be integrated to Earth Day, School-Based Environmental Projects to be led by YES-O, SELG/SSLG, BKD\r\n*Encourage to assign tree/plant adopters and provide tree guard/s', 2025, 501061, 107, 12, 89),
