(100, 'SY 2025-2026 NESTLÉ WELLNESS CAMPUS PROGRAM IMPLEMENTATION - HATAW SAYAW YEAR 3 PARTICIPATION', '1.	To participate in the Hataw Sayaw Year 3 Dance Competition organized by Nestlé Philippines.\r\n2.	To promote physical fitness and creativity among selected students through dance.\r\n3.	To submit a high-quality dance video entry by October 15, 2025 in', 'Successful submission of Hataw Sayaw Year 3 entry.\r\n1.	Increased student participation in wellness-related activities.\r\n2.	Strengthened implementation of the Nestlé Wellness Campus Program.\r\n3.	Promotion of active and healthy lifestyle among students.', 'September 15-30, 2025 (3:00 – 4:10pm)	\r\n- Daily rehearsals and choreography practice\r\n\r\nOctober 1, 2025	(1:00 – 4:10pm)\r\n- Costume fitting and props preparation\r\n\r\nOctober 2, 2025	(3:00 – 4:10pm)	\r\nTechnical rehearsal and video dry run\r\n\r\nOctober 3, 2025	(3:00 – 4:10pm)	\r\nFinal dance video recording\r\n\r\nOctober 6, 2025 (1:00 – 3:00pm)\r\nVideo editing and final review\r\n\r\nOctober 6, 2025 (3:00 – 4:10pm)\r\nOnline submission of final video entry', '4 weeks', 'Selected Student-Dancers , ICT Teacher/ Video', '1800.00', 'Activity proposal submitted and currently awaiting approval; implementation activities have commenced as scheduled.', 2025, 304349, 107, 12, 89),
(101, 'TAYO\'Y MAGDIWANG: MATH FESTIVAL - UNLOCK THE POWER IN NUMBERS', '1. To develop learners\' confidence and positive mindset toward mathematics by providing fun, engaging, and non-intimidating activities that showcase the practical and creative applications of mathematical concepts.\r\n2. To strengthen students\' logical', 'Students will develop their teamwork abilities and enhance their mathematical, logical reasoning, and problem-solving skills by actively participating in engaging games and challenges such as Sudoku, Tower of Hanoi, Rubik\'s Cube, Da Math board games, quiz bee, and critical thinking tasks. Through these activities, learners are expected to collaborate effectively with peers, apply strategies creatively, and build confidence in their mathematical abilities while fostering a positive and enjoyable learning experience.', 'September 29, 2025 (12:30-4:10pm)\r\n- Opening Program\r\nElimination game from Grade 7-12\r\n-Sudoku\r\n-Tower of Hanoi\r\n-Rubik\'s Cube\r\n- Da Math board games\r\n- Quiz Bee\r\n- Critical Thinking\r\n\r\nSeptember 30, 2025 (12:30-4:10pm)\r\nChampionship Game\r\n-Sudoku\r\n-Tower of Hanoi\r\n-Rubik\'s Cube\r\n-Da Math Board Games\r\n-Quiz Bee\r\n-Critical Thinking\r\n\r\nMath Track \'n Field', 'Not Applicable', 'Teachers, SSLG, Math Club Members', '5500.00', 'Activity duly approved and set for implementation on September 29–30, 2025, with preparatory activities in progress.', 2025, 304349, 107, 12, 89),
(102, 'TAYO\'Y MAGDIWANG: PAGDIRIWANG NG BUWAN NG WIKANG PAMBANSA 2025', 'a. Nahuhubog at nahahasa ang kasanayan ng mga mag-aaral sa paggamit ng wikang Filipino sa pamamagitan ng aktibong pakikilahok sa iba\'t ibang patimpalak at gawaing pangwika.\r\nb. Naiangat ang kamalayan ng mga mag-aaral hinggil sa kahalagahan, kasaysaya', 'Sa pagtatapos ng mga patimpalak para sa Buwan ng Wika, inaasahang higit na nahubog ang kasanayan ng mga mag-aaral sa paggamit ng wikang Filipino; naitaas ang kanilang kamalayan sa kahalagahan at kasaysayan ng ating wika; at naipamalas ang pagpapahalaga sa pagsasapanlipunan at nasyonalismo bilang bahagi ng kanilang pagkakakilanlang Pilipino.', 'August 4, 2025 (7:15-7:30am)\r\nBuwan ng Wika Kick-off \r\n\r\nAugust 14, 2025 (3:15-4:10pm)\r\nTagisan ng Talino\r\n\r\nAugust 20, 2025 (2:20-4:10pm)\r\nPaggawa ng Poster\r\n\r\nAugust 29, 2025 \r\nKulminasyon ng Buwan ng Wika\r\n- Parada ng mga katutubong kasuotan - 8:00-9:30am\r\n- Dagliang Talumpati - 10:00-11:30am\r\n- Interpretatibong katutubang awit at sayaw - 1:00-3:00pm\r\n- Pagbibigay parangal para sa mga mananalo at kalahok - 3:00-4:00pm\r\n', 'Not Applicable', 'Teachers, SSLG and SGC', '2860.00', 'Matagumpay na naisagawa ang aktibidad noong Agosto 29, 2025, alinsunod sa itinakdang iskedyul.', 2025, 304349, 107, 12, 89),
(103, 'NUTRITION MONTH CULMINATION', '1. To promote awareness and understanding of the importance of proper nutrition and healthy lifestyle practices.\r\n2. To showcase students talents and creativity in promoting nutrition and wellness through contest, and performances.\r\n3. To foster coll', '- Pre and Post-activity surveys showing increase in nutrition knowledge.\r\n- Participation and Feedback Forms with satisfaction ratings\r\n- Number of students joined contest or exhibit\r\n- Number of stakeholders involved\r\n- Varieties of entries such as slogan, cooking, poster\r\n- Accomplishment Report', 'July 29, 2025\r\n\r\n7:00-8:30am\r\n-Preliminaries\r\n\r\n8:30-9:30am\r\nPlanning and Coordination\r\n-Assign roles and responsibilities to each member\r\n-Set a detailed program flow\r\n\r\n8:30am-3:30pm\r\nContest Proper\r\n- Cooking Contest\r\n- Poster Making\r\n- Creative Costume\r\n- Table setting/Table Arrangement\r\n- Flower arrangement\r\n- Fruit and Vegetable Carving\r\n\r\n3:30-4:30pm\r\nAwarding of Certificates\r\n\r\n4:30-5:00pm\r\nClosing Ceremony', '1 day Activity', 'Teachers, Students and Stakeholders', '1000.00', 'The Nutrition Month Culmination was successfully implemented on July 29, 2025, promoting health and wellness among learners.', 2025, 304349, 107, 12, 89),
(104, 'INTRAMURALS 2025', '- To promote physical fitness, health, and wellness among students.\r\n- To develop leadership, teamwork, and sportsmanship.\r\n- To foster unity and school spirit through friendly competition.\r\n- To provide opportunities for students to showcase athleti', '- Successful and safe conduct of the Opening and Closing Intramurals 2025 Ceremonies.\r\n- Active participation of all year levels in sports and allied activities.\r\n- Strengthened bonds and camaraderie among students, faculty, and staff.\r\n- Identification and recognition of outstanding athletes and teams.\r\n-Documentation of the event through photos, videos, and post-activity reports.', 'July 17, 2025\r\n\r\n7:30-9:00am\r\n- Intramural\'s Parade\r\n\r\n9:00-10:00am\r\nOpening Program\r\n- Opening Salvo\r\n- Presentation of Participants\r\n- Banner Raising \r\n\r\n10:00am-4:00pm\r\nOutdoor and Indoor Games', '1 day Activity', 'Teaching and Non-Teaching Personnel, Students', '5000.00', 'Intramurals 2025 successfully conducted on July 17, 2025, promoting sportsmanship and physical wellness among learners.', 2025, 304349, 107, 12, 89),
(105, 'CONDUCT OF THE 2025 BRIGADA ESKWELA ACTIVITIES', 'A. Sustain partnership with the Local Government Unit, non-government organizations (NGOs) and private partners;\r\nB. Establish/Enhance a safe space child protection area for learners;\r\nC. Sustain a functional child protection committee; and\r\nD. Harmo', '1. Newsletter covering the Narrative Report\r\n2. Memorandum of Agreement (MOA),\r\n3. Deed of Donation/Acceptance (DOD/DOA)\r\n4. HGDG Checklist (GAD Mechanism) ', 'June 9, 2025\r\nSchool-Based Brigada Eskwela Kick-off\r\n\r\nJune 10, 2025\r\nCleaning of School ground\r\n\r\nJune 11, 2025\r\nClassroom beautification\r\n\r\nJune 12, 2025\r\nRepaint the School Roof & Gym/Repair of Gutter\r\n\r\nJune 13, 2025\r\nClean and prepare the Safe Space Child Protection Area/\r\nClosing Program', '5 days Activity', 'Teachers, Non-Teaching Personnel, SSLG, SGC &', '27500.00', 'Brigada Eskwela 2025 activities successfully conducted from June 9–13, 2025, with active involvement of stakeholders in preparing the school for the opening of classes.', 2025, 304349, 107, 12, 89),
(107, '3-DAY CLUSTER-WIDE SUPREME SECONDARY LEARNER GOVERNMENT LEADERSHIP TRAINING - EMPOWERING FUTURE LEADERS: SSLG LEADERSHIP TRAINING FOR A UNIFIED BAGONG PILIPINAS', '•	Equip SSLG\'s team with essential leadership skills, including communication, problem-solving, and teamwork, through interactive workshops and training sessions.\r\n•	Empower SSLG\'s team with a deep understanding of the organization\'s mission, values,', '•	Share the output and activities with other student leaders, fostering collaboration and knowledge sharing across various leadership roles and organizations.\r\n\r\n•	Offer technical assistance to student leaders, club officers, classroom officers, and utilizing their enhanced leadership and management skills to support peers effectively.\r\n\r\n•	Tackle: Implement the strategies and insights gained during the training to address challenges and enhance efficiency in their respective leadership roles within the school community.\r\n\r\n•	Grow: Contribute to the growth and development of the school community by actively applying leadership principles and fostering a culture of collaboration and continuous improvement among peers.\r\n', '       Ensuring the safety and well-being of our student leaders is our top priority during the Cluster-Wide SSLG Leadership Training.  We provide parents\' consent and waiver forms, orient parents, establish a Learner Rights and Protection Desk, assign a dedicated medical team, and coordinate with barangay officials and police for additional security. Together, we create a safe and empowering environment for our future leaders.\r\n\r\nFebruary 21, 2025 (Day 1)\r\n\r\n1:00 PM -2:30 PM\r\nArrival/Assembly Time/Registration\r\n\r\n2:30 PM -3:00 PM\r\n-Preliminaries\r\n-Induction of Newly Elected Cluster 12 SSLG Officers\r\n\r\n3:00 PM -5:00 PM\r\nSession I- DepEd Mandates on Student Government (CBL)\r\n\r\n5:00 PM- 6:30 PM\r\nDINNER (UNINTERRUPTED)\r\n\r\n\r\n6:30 PM -8:00 PM\r\nSession II- Writing Minutes of the Meeting\r\nWorkshop\r\n\r\nFebruary 22, 2025 (Day 2)\r\n\r\n6:30 AM – 7:30 AM\r\nBREAKFAST\r\n\r\n7:30 AM – 8:00 AM \r\nPreliminaries\r\n\r\n8:00 AM -9:30 AM\r\nSession III- Crafting of Resolutions\r\nWorkshop\r\n\r\n9:30 AM – 10:00 AM\r\nHEALTH BREAK (UNINTERRUPTED)\r\n\r\n\r\n10:00 AM -12:00 PM\r\nSession IV-Activity Proposal \r\n\r\n12:00 PM – 1:00 PM\r\nLUNCH BREAK (UNINTERRUPTED)\r\n\r\n1:00 PM – 2:30 PM \r\nWorkshop\r\n\r\n2:30 PM – 2:45 PM \r\nHEALTH BREAK (UNINTERRUPTED)\r\n\r\n2:45 PM – 5:00 PM \r\nTeam Building Activity\r\n\r\n5:00 PM – 6:30 PM \r\nDINNER\r\n\r\n6:30 PM – 8:00 PM \r\nTypes of Temperament\r\n\r\n8:00 PM – 10:00 PM \r\nBONFIRE ACTIVITY\r\n\r\nFebruary 23, 2025 (Day 3)\r\n\r\n8:00 AM -10:00 AM\r\nSession V-General Plan of Actions (SY: 2025-2026)\r\n\r\n10:00 AM -10 :15 AM\r\nHEALTH BREAK (UNINTERRUPTED)\r\n\r\n10:15 PM -11:30 AM\r\nDistribution of Certificates\r\n\r\nHOMEBOUND\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n', '3-Day Activity', 'Cluster 12, Principal In-charge, Cluster12 SS', '', 'Activity successfully conducted on February 21–23, 2025, with active participation of SSLG leaders from various schools within Cluster 12.', 2025, 304349, 107, 12, 89),
