(247, 'Conduct  Orientation for teachers, parents, and stakeholders on SBM principles\r\nAlways invite respective stakeholders in every school activity', 'To strengthen participatory governance and school performance through effective SBM Implementation', '*Improve stakeholder participation\r\n*Strengthened  community -school parnership', 'The implementation  of SBM  will  use a participatory, collaborative, and data-driven  approach. This ensures that all stakeholders are actively involved in planning, decision-making and monitoring school programs.', 'June 2026', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator', '1000.00', 'Improved stakeholder participation', 2026, 129770, 105, 12, 19),
(248, '- Organized School Governing Council (SGC)\r\n- Conduct leadership training for school heads and teachers\r\n-Develop/Review School  Improvement Plan(SIP)', 'To improve school performance and learner outcomes through participatory  governance, accountability, and efficient resource , management. ', '- Improved student achievement\r\n- Strong community participation\r\n- Transparent and accountable school management\r\n- Sustainable school improvement ', '- Monitor lesson plans and curriculum instruction\r\n- Implement intervention programs for struggling learners', 'Whole Year', 'School  Head, Property Custodian, Finance Off', 'MOOE', 'The implementation of School-Based Management (SBM) has significantly contributed to the improvement of school governance, instructional delivery, and stakeholder participation. Guided by the policies of the Department of education, and decentralizing decision-making and empowering stakeholders. ', 2026, 501779, 57, 12, 116),
(249, 'Assessment, development, and full ope-rationalization of the Library and Computer Laboratory/Classroom', 'To assess the current condition of the library and computer laboratory facilities \r\nTo identify gaps in resources, equipment, and usability \r\nTo establish a functional, accessible, and resource-efficient learning environment \r\nTo integrate technology', 'Fully functional library with organized and updated learning materials \r\nOperational computer laboratory with working units and internet access \r\nEstablished policies and guidelines for usage \r\nUtilization schedule for students and teachers \r\nMonitoring and evaluation report on usage and effectiveness ', 'Phase 1: Assessment\r\n               Conduct inventory of books, computers, and equipment \r\n               Evaluate current condition (working/non-working) \r\n              Identify missing resources (e.g., books, software, internet access) \r\nPhase 2: Planning\r\n               Develop improvement plan based on assessment \r\n               Allocate budget and resources \r\n              Coordinate with administration and stakeholders \r\nPhase 3: Resource Mobilization\r\n                Request procurement of needed materials (books, computers, peripherals) \r\n                 Seek partnerships/donations (LGUs, NGOs, private sectors) \r\n                  Install or upgrade internet connectivity \r\nPhase 4: Implementation\r\n                Organize and catalog library materials \r\n                 Repair/install computer units and necessary software \r\n                 Set up seating, layout, and workspace for usability \r\nPhase 5: Policy Development\r\n                 Create guidelines for borrowing books and using computers \r\n                 Develop class schedules for lab usage \r\n                 Assign personnel (librarian, lab custodian, IT support) \r\nPhase 6: Training & Orientation\r\n                 Train teachers and staff on system usage \r\n                 Orient students on proper use of facilities \r\nPhase 7: Monitoring & Evaluation\r\n                Track usage (logbooks, system records) \r\n                Gather feedback from users \r\n                Conduct periodic evaluation and improvements ', 'Q2–Q3', 'School Head / Administrator, Librarian / Libr', '35000', '', 2026, 128545, 57, 12, 109),
(251, 'Weekly monitoring of ALS Classes in CLCs and in School', 'To guide learners in completing the required competencies to receive the ALS certificate', '80% of the enrolled ALS learners received a certificate.', 'Weekly monitoring on their progress.  Employing a whole-school approach involving all teachers in review sessions/teaching-learning processes', 'June 2026-February 2027', 'ALS teacher, learners, SH and teachers of PVB', '', '', 2026, 129757, 105, 12, 20),
