(270, 'Conduct School-Based Management (SBM) orientation and capacity building for teachers and community stakeholders.', 'To strenghten collaboration among stakeholders, and to increase understanding of SBM principles and practices.', 'Improved stakeholder\'s participation and school programs, activities and projects, conducted SBM orientation and training sessions.', 'Used particiapatory approaches such as brainstorming and planning sessions, conduct seminar, workshop and group discussion.', 'June to August 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents', '5000', 'Activity will be monitored and evaluated regularly to ensure effective implementation and continuous improvement.', 2026, 129648, 107, 12, 67),
(271, 'Implementation of Enhanced Instructional Support, Child Protection Strengthening, and Stakeholder Engagement Program', '•	Improve Grade 10 and 12 learners’ proficiency in 21st-century skills and core learning areas as measured by NAT \r\n•	Increase teachers’ development and use of contextualized, learner-responsive materials \r\n•	Strengthen the functionality and visibili', '•	Developed and implemented contextualized learning materials in all key learning areas \r\n•	Conducted remedial/enrichment and 21st-century skill-focused programs for learners \r\n•	A fully functional and active Child Protection Committee with regular meetings and reports \r\n•	Established School Stakeholders’ Satisfaction Survey with improved rating (target: Satisfactory or higher) \r\n•	Quarterly progress monitoring reports ', '•	Facilitate professional learning sessions on contextualized teaching, assessment design, and 21st-century skills integration for all teachers \r\n•	Develop a school-based Learning Resource Repository (print, digital, and multimedia), ensuring materials meet learner needs and local context \r\n•	Implement targeted academic intervention programs, including after-class remediation and enrichment, and peer-assisted learning groups \r\n•	Strengthen Child Protection implementation through scheduled committee meetings, policy orientation, reporting protocols, and school-wide advocacy campaigns \r\n•	Establish a continuous stakeholder communication system through quarterly surveys, community assemblies, parent dialogues, and digital feedback platforms \r\n•	Forge partnerships with LGUs, NGOs, and community members to support school programs, learner-welfare initiatives, and resource development \r\n•	Conduct quarterly performance reviews using learner assessment data, teacher outputs, CPC reports, and stakeholder feedback to guide decision-making and improvements\r\n', 'June 2026-March 2027', '•	School Head  •	Teachers / Learning Area Coo', '50000', '•	Progress to be reviewed quarterly by the School Improvement Team \r\n•	Adjustments to be made based on learner performance, teacher feedback, and stakeholder responses', 2026, 304312, 61, 12, 1),
