(348, 'Implementation of Data-Driven Targeted Intervention Program for Non-Proficient Learners (Reading and Numeracy)', 'To increase the percentage of learners achieving proficiency in early language, literacy, numeracy, and core learning areas by addressing identified least learned competencies through targeted interventions.', 'List of identified non-proficient learners and least learned competencies, Intervention plans,LAC session reports and coaching logs\r\nPre-test and post-test results showing improvement\r\nMonitoring and Evaluation (M&E) reports ', 'Analyze NAT, CRLA, and classroom assessment data to identify gaps\r\nConduct targeted remediation through small-group instruction\r\nImplement differentiated teaching strategies\r\nConduct LAC sessions focused on intervention strategies\r\nProvide instructional coaching and classroom observation\r\nMonitor learner progress through regular assessment and feedback', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (Whole School Year, wi', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Teachers, Learn', '5000', 'This activity addresses the identified gap where “most learners are proficient but not all,” ensuring that interventions are targeted, monitored, and aligned with improving learner outcomes.', 2026, 129720, 107, 12, 74),
(349, 'Implementation of Learner Support and Safe School Environment Program (Dropout Prevention and Mental Wellness)', 'To ensure a safe, inclusive, and supportive learning environment by reducing dropout risks, strengthening mental wellness support, and sustaining zero incidence of bullying and child abuse.', 'List of at-risk learners (attendance, behavior, performance-based)\r\nHome visitation and intervention reports\r\nFunctional Child Protection Committee (CPC) and meeting minutes\r\nMental wellness activity reports and referral logs\r\nMonthly attendance and dropout monitoring reports', 'Identify at-risk learners through attendance and performance monitoring\r\nConduct home visitation and parent conferences\r\nImplement mentoring and peer support programs\r\nStrengthen Child Protection Committee (CPC) through regular meetings and case monitoring\r\nConduct mental wellness and socio-emotional learning (SEL) activities\r\nMonitor and track learner attendance and engagement monthly', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (Whole School Year wit', 'School Head, Teachers, Guidance/Designated Fo', '5000', 'This activity sustains “Always Manifested” indicators while addressing gaps in dropout reduction and strengthening mental wellness support to ensure all learners remain engaged and supported.', 2026, 129720, 107, 12, 74),
(350, 'Implementation of Data-Driven Instructional Leadership and School Improvement Monitoring System', 'To strengthen instructional leadership by ensuring that school plans, programs, and innovations are data-driven, collaboratively implemented, and focused on improving learner outcomes.', 'Updated SIP/AIP aligned with learner performance data\r\nSchool Planning Team (SPT) and SGC meeting minutes with action points\r\nInstructional supervision reports and coaching logs (PMCF)\r\nStudent leadership (SSG/SPG) project reports aligned to school priorities\r\nDocumented school innovations and best practices', 'Conduct data analysis (NAT, CRLA, assessment results) to guide planning\r\nFacilitate regular School Planning Team and SGC meetings with clear targets and deliverables\r\nImplement instructional supervision through classroom observations and coaching\r\nEngage SSG/SPG in learner-centered initiatives (e.g., reading campaigns, peer support)\r\nDevelop and monitor school innovations aligned to identified needs\r\nTrack implementation of plans through monthly monitoring and feedback', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (Whole School Year wit', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Teachers, Schoo', '5000', 'This activity sustains “Always Manifested” leadership indicators while ensuring that leadership practices are data-driven, outcome-focused, and directly linked to improvements in teaching and learning.', 2026, 129720, 107, 12, 74),
(351, 'Implementation of Results-Based Governance, Monitoring, and Stakeholder Engagement System', 'To strengthen transparency, accountability, and shared governance by ensuring that school plans, programs, and partnerships are effectively implemented, monitored, and aligned with improved learner outcomes.', 'SIP/AIP implementation tracking matrix and progress reports\r\nSGC and PTA meeting minutes with documented decisions and action points\r\nPartnership (MOA) and stakeholder engagement records\r\nMonitoring and Evaluation (M&E) reports of programs and projects\r\nStakeholder feedback and satisfaction survey results', 'Monitor implementation of SIP/AIP through regular tracking of targets and accomplishments\r\nConduct quarterly SGC and PTA meetings with data-driven agenda and decision-making\r\nStrengthen partnerships aligned to school priorities (e.g., reading, attendance, resources)\r\nImplement a monitoring and evaluation system comparing baseline and current performance\r\nConduct stakeholder feedback surveys and use results for continuous improvement\r\nEnsure transparency through regular reporting and public sharing of school performance', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (Whole School Year wit', 'School Head, School Governance Council (SGC),', '5000', 'This activity sustains “Always Manifested” governance indicators while ensuring that accountability systems are results-based, transparent, and directly linked to improved school and learner performance.', 2026, 129720, 107, 12, 74),
(352, 'Implementation of Data-Driven Teacher Development, Coaching, and Performance Enhancement Program', 'To enhance teacher competencies and team performance by aligning professional development, LAC sessions, and coaching interventions with identified learner needs and instructional gaps.', 'Consolidated Training Needs Analysis (TNA) based on classroom and learner data\r\nLAC session reports focused on least learned competencies\r\nCoaching and mentoring records (PMCF, observation notes)\r\nImproved IPCRF results aligned with learner performance\r\nDocumentation of best teaching practices and innovations', 'Analyze learner performance data (NAT, CRLA, formative assessments) to identify teacher development needs\r\nConduct targeted LAC sessions focusing on reading, numeracy, and differentiated instruction\r\nImplement regular classroom observation, coaching, and feedback cycles\r\nProvide mentoring support for teachers based on identified gaps\r\nAlign IPCRF objectives with learner outcomes and monitor progress\r\nRecognize and share effective teaching practices through LAC and peer learning', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (Whole School Year wit', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Teachers, Learn', '5000', 'This activity sustains “Always Manifested” indicators while ensuring that professional development is targeted, continuous, and directly linked to improved teaching practices and learner outcomes.', 2026, 129720, 107, 12, 74),
(353, 'Implementation of Strategic Resource Allocation and Learning Resource Enhancement Program', 'To ensure efficient and strategic utilization of financial and material resources to support priority learning needs, particularly improving access to learning materials and strengthening school facilities.', 'Resource inventory and needs assessment report\r\nImproved and functional library/reading corners\r\nMOOE utilization plan aligned with school priorities\r\nRecords of resource mobilization (donations, partnerships)\r\nMonitoring reports on utilization of ICT and learning facilities', 'Conduct resource mapping and needs assessment focusing on gaps (e.g., library resources)\r\nAllocate MOOE based on priority programs (reading, intervention materials, facility improvement)\r\nStrengthen partnerships with stakeholders for additional resources and support\r\nImprove and utilize library and ICT facilities to support teaching and learning\r\nMonitor usage and impact of resources on learner performance through regular evaluation\r\nEnsure transparency through proper documentation and reporting of resource utilization', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (Whole School Year wit', 'School Head, Property Custodian, Teachers, IC', '5000', 'This activity sustains “Always Manifested” indicators while addressing gaps in library functionality and infrastructure improvement, ensuring that all resources directly contribute to improved learner outcomes.', 2026, 129720, 107, 12, 74),
