(457, 'Recruit and/or assign librarian', 'Ensure proper management and supervision of library', 'Assigned librarian or teacher-in-charge; cataloged books', '- Identify qualified personnel\r\n- Train assigned librarian on cataloging and library management\r\n- Develop borrowing and return system', 'January 2027', 'School Head, Teachers', '2000.00', 'Librarian can be an existing teacher with library duties', 2026, 128503, 57, 12, 110),
(458, 'Orient learners and teachers', 'Promote reading culture and proper use of library', 'Learners and teachers trained; usage guidelines posted', '- Conduct orientation on library rules and policies\r\n- Demonstrate borrowing, returning, and ICT usage\r\n- Promote reading programs and book clubs', 'January 2027', 'Librarian, Teachers, School Head', '2000.00', 'Integrate library programs with literacy and curriculum activities', 2026, 128503, 57, 12, 110),
(459, 'Implement library activities', 'Facilitate reading, research, and learning programs', 'Learners actively using library; reading logs maintained; reading programs conducted', '- Schedule regular library periods\r\n- Conduct reading sessions, storytelling, and research projects\r\n- Encourage projects requiring library resources', 'Ongoing (monthly/quarterly)', 'Librarian, Teachers, Learners', '5000.00', 'Can partner with DepEd reading initiatives or local organizations', 2026, 128503, 57, 12, 110),
(460, 'Monitor and maintain library', 'Sustain library functionality and prevent deterioration', 'Maintenance logs; updated catalog; feedback collected', '- Regularly check furniture, books, and ICT equipment\r\n- Replace worn-out books and supplies\r\n- Collect feedback from learners and teachers', 'Ongoing (monthly/quarterly)', 'Librarian, School Head, Maintenance Staff', '5000.00', 'Ensure library remains functional and organized', 2026, 128503, 57, 12, 110),
(461, 'School Governing Council and School Planning Team Conference', 'To prioritize and map-out the needs of the school before the opening of classes', 'Minutes of Meeting, Matrix of Activities', 'Planning Conference', 'April - May 2026', 'School Governing Council, SH, Teachers', '3000', 'Activity Design should be approved before the conduct of the activity', 2026, 128743, 58, 12, 41),
(463, 'NAT Mastery Boosters', 'The main goal of this activity is to improve Grade 10 and 12 learners’ proficiency in the National Achievement Test (NAT), particularly in Mathematics, Science, and higher-order thinking skills. The school aims to raise proficiency rates to at least ', 'This program is expected to produce measurable improvements in learners’ NAT performance, including higher scores and reduced learning gaps. Documented results from quarterly NAT-style assessments and post-test reports will provide evidence of learners’ progress. Attendance and participation in remedial sessions will also be recorded, and item analysis reports will identify specific areas where learners have improved or still require support.', 'Learners will participate in structured review sessions, peer tutoring programs, and targeted remedial activities designed based on prior assessment data. Test item analysis will be used to identify weak areas, while subject teachers, the Academic Coordinator, and peer tutors will provide instruction and guidance. Continuous monitoring through pre-tests, post-tests, and progress tracking will ensure that the interventions are data-driven and responsive to learners’ needs.', 'This activity will be implemented throughout ', 'Subject teachers, the Academic Coordinator, t', '50000', '', 2026, 304328, 103, 12, 126),
(464, 'Teach Beyond the Book', 'The goal is to ensure that all lesson plans and instructional materials are contextualized to the learners’ needs and the local environment. The school aims to achieve 100% alignment of instructional materials with learner profiles and integrate loca', 'This activity will result in a complete set of contextualized lesson plans, documented classroom observations, and feedback from learners demonstrating the relevance and effectiveness of the materials. Teachers will also develop a repository of materials for sharing and reference.', 'Teachers will participate in quarterly workshops to develop, review, and refine learning materials. Mentoring will be provided for novice teachers, and classroom observations will monitor the effectiveness of the materials in improving learner engagement and understanding. Learner surveys will provide additional feedback to ensure materials are aligned with student needs and interests.', 'This activity will be ongoing throughout the ', 'ubject teachers, the SLAC Facilitator, and th', '30000', '', 2026, 304328, 103, 12, 126),
(465, 'Bridge the Gap Program', 'This program aims to address learning gaps in reading, comprehension, Mathematics, and Science among learners performing below proficiency. The goal is to reduce learning gaps by at least 15% after each term and ensure that all at-risk learners recei', 'Expected outputs include individualized learning plans, pre- and post-remediation test results, monthly progress reports for each learner, and records of participation in remedial sessions. These outputs will allow monitoring of both learner performance and program effectiveness.', 'Diagnostic tests will identify learning gaps, and small-group remedial sessions will be conducted to provide focused instruction. Individualized plans will be tailored to learners’ specific needs, and parents will be engaged to reinforce learning at home. Teachers will track attendance, participation, and improvements using learning trackers to ensure that interventions are responsive and effective.', 'The remedial sessions will occur biweekly thr', 'Classroom teachers, Master teachers, and the ', '20000', '', 2026, 304328, 103, 12, 126),
(466, 'Data-Driven Success', 'The goal of this activity is to ensure that all assessments undergo test item analysis and that the results are applied to improve lesson planning and instruction. This will increase instructional effectiveness and help close learning gaps identified', 'This program will produce item analysis reports after every major assessment, adjusted lesson plans based on the results, and documentation showing improved learner performance in previously weak areas.', 'Teachers will attend quarterly workshops to learn how to interpret item analysis data and identify recurring errors. Lessons will be adapted based on analysis outcomes, and progress will be tracked using pre- and post-test comparisons. Continuous feedback loops will ensure that teaching is responsive to identified gaps.', 'Item analysis and subsequent instructional ad', 'Subject teachers and the Master Teachers will', '10000', '', 2026, 304328, 103, 12, 126),
(467, 'Values in Action', 'The activity aims to strengthen learners’ understanding and practice of peace, social responsibility, and DepEd core values by integrating values education into 100% of lessons across subjects. The school targets at least 80% of learners demonstratin', 'Expected outputs include lesson plans that integrate values, documentation of values-related activities such as assemblies and projects, and observation logs showing learner behavior improvement. Learner participation and engagement in these activities will also be recorded.', 'Interactive activities such as role-plays, storytelling, and project-based learning will be implemented to contextualize values. School-wide campaigns, assemblies, and recognition programs will reinforce the learning of core values. Observation checklists, peer reports, and feedback will monitor adherence and behavior change.', 'SY 2026-2027', 'All teachers, the Guidance Advocate, SSLG off', '15000', '', 2026, 304328, 103, 12, 126),
(468, 'Library Lift-Off', 'The primary objective of this activity is to establish a fully functional school library that supports the academic and research needs of all learners. The library aims to provide access to a wide range of reading materials, reference books, digital ', 'The activity will produce a fully equipped library with organized shelves, a catalog of physical and digital resources, reading corners, and study areas. Learners’ borrowing and usage records will document active engagement, while teacher and student feedback will indicate the usefulness and relevance of materials. Library orientation sessions and research workshops will also be conducted to promote effective utilization.', 'The school will start by assessing existing spaces and materials, identifying gaps, and upgrading facilities to accommodate learners comfortably. Shelves, tables, chairs, and digital resources will be installed to provide a conducive reading and research environment. Teachers will collaborate to curate age-appropriate and subject-aligned resources. Library orientation programs will be conducted for both students and faculty to maximize usage, while a library monitoring system will track resource circulation, utilization, and feedback. Partnerships with local libraries, publishers, or donors may also be sought to enrich the collection.', 'The activity will be implemented in phases ov', 'The School Principal,  designated library tea', '100000', '', 2026, 304328, 103, 12, 126),
(469, 'Tech Lab Transformation', 'The objective of this activity is to maintain and enhance the functionality of the computer laboratory/classroom to ensure that all learners have access to digital tools for research, programming, and 21st-century skills development. The aim is for 1', 'The activity will result in a fully operational computer lab with updated computers, reliable internet access, and functional software for learning and research. Learner engagement and usage records will show increased participation in digital learning activities, while teachers will report improved integration of technology in lessons.', 'The school will conduct an initial assessment of the lab’s equipment and internet connectivity to identify outdated or malfunctioning resources. Upgrades will include hardware replacement, installation of relevant software, and ensuring reliable internet connections. Teachers will integrate lab use into lesson plans, and students will receive training on using digital resources responsibly. Regular monitoring and maintenance schedules will ensure continuous functionality.', 'This activity will be implemented in the firs', 'The ICT Coordinator, School Principal, Subjec', '80000', '', 2026, 304328, 103, 12, 126),
(470, 'Inclusive Learning Spaces', 'The activity aims to create special education- and PWD-friendly facilities that ensure equitable access to learning for all students, including those with physical disabilities or special needs. The goal is to have 100% of school facilities accessibl', 'The outputs include ramps, accessible toilets, adaptive classroom furniture, and specialized learning spaces. Learner participation and engagement in both regular and adapted programs will be documented, and feedback from students and teachers will demonstrate improved inclusivity.', 'The school will assess all current facilities to identify accessibility gaps. Upgrades will include constructing ramps, installing handrails, providing adaptive furniture, and arranging classrooms to accommodate learners with mobility needs. Teachers will be trained in inclusive teaching strategies, and individualized learning support will be provided for students with special needs. Regular monitoring and evaluation will ensure that the facilities meet the intended purpose.', 'Academic Year 2026–2027 ', 'The School Principal, Guidance Advocate, Teac', '70000', '', 2026, 304328, 103, 12, 126),
(471, 'Contextualized IM Development Workshop', '1. Develop teacher competence in creating contextualized instructional materials\r\n2. Produce usable learning materials', '- At least 1–2 contextualized IMs per teacher\r\n- Compiled school-based IM outputs', '- Hands-on workshop\r\n- Teachers create IMs (worksheets, modules, visual aids) using local context\r\n- Peer review of outputs', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '20000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(472, 'Peer Coaching and Mentoring', '- Provide continuous support to teachers\r\n- Improve classroom application of contextualization', '- Coaching notes and observation reports\r\n- Improved lesson delivery', '- Pairing/mentoring system\r\n- Classroom observation\r\n- Coaching sessions', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '5000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(473, 'Establishment of Learning Resource Bank', '- Ensure accessibility and sustainability of contextualized materials', '- Functional IM repository\r\n- Organized contextualized materials', '- Create Google Drive/physical repository\r\n- Organize by subject and grade level\r\n- Regular updating', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'Teacher', '3000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(474, 'Recognition and Incentive Program', '- Motivate teachers to innovate and sustain efforts', '- Awarded best IMs\r\n- Increased teacher participation', 'Identify best contextualized IMs\r\n- Recognition during meetings/INSET', 'First Quarter to 3rd Quarter', 'School Head and Administrative Officer', '10000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(475, 'Development of Standardized TIA Template', 'To ensure uniformity in analyzing test results across subjects', 'Standardized TIA template adopted by all teachers', 'Create and distribute a school-based TIA template (Excel/Google Sheets); include guide on how to compute and interpret results', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'Mathematics Teachers and ICT Coor', '3000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(476, 'Conduct of Quarterly Test Item Analysis', 'To regularly analyze learner performance and identify least learned competencies', 'Completed TIA reports per subject and grade level', 'After every quarterly assessment, teachers compute item analysis using test results; identify mastery and non-mastery items', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'Teachers', '1000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(477, 'LAC Session on TIA Results Utilization', 'To use TIA results in improving instruction and assessment practices', 'Documented LAC discussions; action points for improvement', 'Present TIA results during LAC; discuss difficult items, common errors, and misconceptions; share best practices', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '3000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(478, 'Revision and Enhancement of Test Items', 'To improve quality of assessment tools based on TIA findings', 'Improved test questionnaires; validated item bank', 'Revise or discard poor items (too easy/difficult, low discrimination); improve distractors; align with MELCs', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '3000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(479, 'Intervention Planning Based on Results', 'To address least mastered competencies identified through TIA', 'Intervention plans; list of target learners; progress monitoring records', 'Develop remediation plans (tutorials, differentiated instruction, enrichment activities); assign focus learners', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '3000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(480, 'Monitoring and Coaching by School Heads', 'To ensure proper implementation of TIA and its utilization', 'Monitoring reports; coaching notes; improved teacher practices', 'Conduct classroom observations; check TIA reports; provide technical assistance and feedback', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '00', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
