(501, 'Establish School Mental Wellness Committee', 'To create a dedicated team that will oversee mental health programs and interventions', '- Organized Mental Wellness Committee\r\n- Defined roles and structure', '- Designate members (Guidance Counselor, School Head, Teachers, Health Personnel, PTA representative)\r\n- Define roles and responsibilities\r\n- Conduct orientation on mental wellness policies', 'June 2026 ', 'School Head', '00', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(502, 'Conduct Mental Health Awareness Campaigns', 'To increase awareness and reduce stigma among learners and staff', 'Increased awareness on mental health\r\n- Active participation of school community', '- Conduct seminars/webinars on stress management, bullying prevention, and emotional resilience\r\n- Celebrate Mental Health Week\r\n- Distribute IEC materials', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '5000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(503, 'Implement Regular Counseling and Support Services', 'To provide accessible psychological support to learners and personnel', '- Functional counseling services\r\n- Documented counseling sessions', '- Schedule regular guidance counseling sessions\r\n- Provide one-on-one and group counseling\r\n- Establish referral system for serious cases', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '3000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(504, 'Set Up Safe Spaces / Wellness Corners', 'To provide a safe and calming environment for learners experiencing stress', 'Operational Teen Center\r\n- Increased student utilization', '- Identify and prepare a designated room/area\r\n- Provide calming materials (books, art supplies, etc.)\r\n- Assign personnel to supervise', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '50000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(505, 'Capacity Building for Teachers and Staff', 'To equip school personnel with skills in identifying and responding to mental health concerns', '- Trained teachers and staff\r\n- Improved response to mental health needs', '- Conduct training on Psychological First Aid (PFA)\r\n- Workshops on classroom-based mental health support\r\n- Partner with experts or agencies', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '5000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(506, 'Strengthen Peer Support Program', 'To encourage peer-to-peer support among students', 'Active peer support group\r\n- Increased student engagement', '- Organize peer facilitators or buddies\r\n- Train student leaders on basic helping skills\r\n- Monitor peer support activities', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Student', '5000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(507, 'Engage Parents and Community', 'To ensure holistic support for learners’ mental wellness', '- Increased parent involvement\r\n- Strengthened school-community partnership', '- Conduct parent orientation on mental health awareness\r\n- Establish communication channels for concerns\r\n- Collaborate with LGUs/health agencies', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '5000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(508, 'Monitoring and Evaluation of Mental Wellness Programs', 'To ensure effectiveness and sustainability of interventions', '- Monitoring reports\r\n- Improved mental wellness programs', '- Develop monitoring tools (surveys, feedback forms)\r\n- Conduct regular evaluation meetings\r\n- Adjust programs based on findings', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Head and Teachers', '1000', '', 2026, 325105, 103, 12, 128),
(509, 'Conduct intensive review sessions and diagnostic assessments for Grades 4-6 learners.', 'To improve the proficiency level of Grades 4-6 learners in all 21st century skills and core learning areas as measured by the NAT', 'Improved NAT scores; At least 75% MPS for Grades 4-6; Diagnostic assessment results', 'Conduct diagnostic tests; Form intervention groups; Administer weekly LAC sessions; Utilize DLP and Instructional  materials', 'June – March (S.Y. 2026-2027)', 'School Head, Subject Teachers', '5000.00', 'Not Yet Manifested – High Priority', 2026, 128324, 57, 12, 117),
(510, 'Implement strengthened anti-bullying and child abuse prevention programs', 'To achieve zero child abuse and sustain zero bullying incidences in the school', 'Zero child abuse/bullying incident reports; Updated Child Protection Policy; Awareness campaign materials.', 'Conduct quarterly orientations; Activate Child Protection Committee; Post anti-bullying materials in school; Conduct home visits for at-risk learners', 'June – March (quarterly)', 'School Head, Child Protection Committee, Guid', '3000.00', 'Frequently Manifested – For Strengthening', 2026, 128324, 57, 12, 117),
(511, 'Conduct regular Learning Action Cells (LAC) and Continuing Professional Development activities.', 'To upgrade teachers\' competencies and address identified learning and development needs.', 'LAC session plans and reports; Certificate of participation; Improved teaching strategies.', 'Conduct monthly LAC sessions; Identify L&D needs through IPCRF; Facilitate SBM-based CPD activities; Encourage participation in division/national trainings.', 'Monthly (June – March)', 'School Head, LAC Leader, All Teaching Personn', '5000.00', 'Frequently Manifested – For Strengthening', 2026, 128324, 57, 12, 117),
(512, 'Implementation of Inclusive Support Program for SNED ALS Learners', 'This activity aims to help SNED ALS learners become more confident, prepared, and ready for the A&E Test. Through continuous support and inclusive strategies, the goal is for at least 80% of the learners to show better participation, less anxiety, an', 'By the end of the implementation, all planned activities will be carried out. Learners are expected to participate more actively during sessions and show increased engagement. At least 80% of the SNED learners should be ready for the A&E Test, with noticeable improvement in their confidence and reduced anxiety based on observations and feedback.', 'The program will include regular PSYCHEGIP sessions to support the learners’ mental and emotional well-being. Diagnostic and progress assessments will be conducted to track their development. Individualized Learning Plans (ILPs) will be prepared to address specific learner needs. Teaching strategies will be adjusted to be more inclusive and learner-friendly. Practice exams and A&E Test simulations will also be given to help learners become familiar with the test. Peer support and mentoring will be encouraged, and coordination with parents/guardians and School Head will be maintained throughout the program.', 'entire School Year 2025–2026', 'ALS Teacher,ALS Focal Person, School Head', '10000', 'This activity is designed to support ALS SNED learners not only academically but also emotionally. By creating a safe and supportive learning environment, learners will feel more confident and prepared, helping them perform better in the A&E Test.', 2026, 128770, 104, 12, 129),
(513, 'Strengthening SGC Governance & Shared Leadership', 'Sustain high level stakeholder engagement and shared decision-making', 'Highly functional SGC with distributed leadership', 'Strategic planning session, policy review, role expansion', 'June 2026', 'School Head, SGC, Key Stakeholders', '3000', 'Focus on sustainability', 2026, 205504, 103, 12, 127),
(514, 'Advanced Capacity Building on SBM & Innovation', 'Enhance leadership and innovation skills of stakeholders', 'Trained SGC members with innovation initiatives', 'Training, benchmarking, LAC sessions', 'July–August 2026', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, External Partne', '8000', 'Include best practices sharing', 2026, 205504, 103, 12, 127),
(515, 'Conduct School Planning Workshop\r\n', 'Develop a collaborative and updated School Improvement Plan (SIP)', 'Approved SIP with stakeholder participation', 'Stakeholder meetings, workshops, data analysis', 'May 2026', 'School ', '10000', 'Involve PTA and community leaders', 2026, 129068, 60, 12, 32),
(516, 'Conduct School Planning Workshop\r\nReading Intervention Program', 'Develop a collaborative and updated School Improvement Plan (SIP)\r\nImprove reading proficiency of struggling learners', 'Approved SIP with stakeholder participation\r\n80% of identified learners improve reading level', 'Stakeholder meetings, workshops, data analysis\r\nRemedial classes, peer tutoring, use of reading materials', 'May 2026', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, SGC, PTA', '5000', 'Involve PTA and community leaders', 2026, 129068, 60, 12, 32),
(517, 'Conduct School Planning Workshop\r\nReading Intervention Program', 'Develop a collaborative and updated School Improvement Plan (SIP)\r\nImprove reading proficiency of struggling learners', 'Approved SIP with stakeholder participation\r\n', '	Stakeholder meetings, workshops, data analysis\r\n80% of identified learners improve reading level', 'May 2026', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, SGC, PTA', '10000', 'Involve PTA and community leaders', 2026, 129068, 60, 12, 32),
(518, 'Prepare and align MOOE Plan  with SIP and  AIP\r\nConduct Procurement planning and scheduling(APP & PPMP Preparation)\r\nOrganize and update financial documents (DV,OR,IAR liquidation\r\nPost MOOE utilization reports on transparency Board\r\nConduct repair a', 'Ensure 100% efficient utilization of MOOE\r\nImprove procurement efficiency\r\nStrengthen financial Management\r\nEnhance transparency and accountability\r\nimprove school facilities\r\nStrengthen monitoring and evaluation\r\nIncrease stakeholder Participation\r\n', 'Approved MOOE plan aligned with school  Priorities.\r\nTimely procurement of needed supplies and materials\r\nComplete and accurate financial records with no audit issues\r\nupdated and visible financial reports for stakeholders\r\nsafe, clean and functional classrooms\r\nUpdated SMEA REports\r\nCorrective actions Implemented\r\nActive involvement of stakeholder in school programs.\r\nFaster and more efficient service to parents and learners\r\nAvailable and functional learning Materials in classrooms\r\nSafe and Dissaster ready school environment', 'Conduct Documents review and audit of existing SBM files\r\nConduct Regular updating and Validation\r\nIntegrate Back up digital Filing System\r\nConduct Regular updating and validation meetings\r\nOrganized files into labeled folder\r\nuse checklist of required MOVs  per SBM principle\r\nAssign Focal Person per SBM area', 'April to August 2026', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, SGC, PTA', '10000', 'Ensure 100% completeness of MOVS\r\nFiles should be ready for SBM Validation\r\nMaintain both hard copy and soft copy\r\nAssign accountability per documents to avoid gaps', 2026, 129068, 60, 12, 32),
(519, 'To ensure the school has a functional library', 'Improve access to learning materials', 'Organized and updated book collection\r\nIncreased student use of library', 'Conduct inventory of books and materials\r\nRepair or replace damaged books and shelves\r\nAcquire new books and references (donations pr purchase)\r\nOrganize library system (cataloging and labeling)\r\nSet regular library schedule for students', '1-2 months', 'School librarian/assigned teacher, School Hea', '', '', 2026, 501417, 60, 12, 32),
(520, 'Water, Electricity and Internet Facilities', 'Ensure safe and continuous access to basic utilities', 'Continuous water supply\r\nSafe and stable electricity\r\nReliable internet access for teachers and students', 'Inspect current water system (pipes, tanks, supply)\r\nRepair leaks and install water storage if needed\r\nCheck electrical wiring and lightning; fix faulty connections\r\nCoordinate with service providers for stable electricity\r\nInstall or upgrade internet connection (Wi-Fi) access point\r\nRegular schedule maintenance ', '1-3 months', 'School Head, LGU/Utility providers, Maintenan', '', '', 2026, 501417, 60, 12, 32),
(521, 'Functional Computer Laboratory/Classroom', 'Provide students with access to digital learning tools\r\nEnhance ICT skills', 'Functional computers\r\nRegular ICT classes conducted\r\nIncreased student computer literacy', 'Access existing computers and equipment\r\nRepair usable units and dispose of irreparable ones\r\nProcure additional computers to reach target \r\nInstall necessary software and security systems\r\nEnsure proper ventilation and electrical setup\r\nAssign ICT coordinator/teacher\r\nSchedule regular computer classes\r\n', '2-4 months', 'School head, ICT Coordinator/teacher/LGU part', '', '', 2026, 501417, 60, 12, 32),
(527, 'SMART SKILLS DAY: Literacy and Numeracy Day ', 'Reinforce literacy and numeracy skills in an engaging way', 'Improved learner engagement, measurable gains in reading and numeracy competencies, active stakeholder participation, and strengthened instructional practices among teachers, as evidenced by assessment results, activity outputs, and program documentation.', 'The program will utilize a learner-centered activities and data-driven approach to enhance learners’ literacy and numeracy skills.', 'June 2026-April 2027', 'School Principal, Master Teachers, ELLNA Coor', '50000.00', '', 2026, 128798, 104, 12, 131),
(528, 'Gamified NAT Review', 'To enhance learners’ performance in the National Achievement Test through engaging, game-based review activities that reinforce mastery of key competencies in English, Mathematics, and Science.', 'The Gamified NAT Review Days resulted in improved learner performance, enhanced mastery of competencies, increased engagement, and strengthened test-taking skills, as evidenced by assessment results, participation records, and monitoring data.', 'The activity will utilize a learner-centered, competency-based, and game-based learning approach, integrating test simulation and immediate feedback to strengthen mastery of MELCs and improve test-taking skills.', 'June 2026-April 2027', 'School Principal, Master Teachers, Testing Co', '50000.00', '', 2026, 128798, 104, 12, 131),
(529, 'ACTION RESEARCH:  Developing contextualized learning materials and intervention program that are responsive to the needs of learners.', 'To improve learners’ academic performance by developing and implementing contextualized learning materials and targeted intervention programs based on identified learning needs.', 'Developed research-based contextualized learning materials and intervention program that address learners needs. ', 'The study will utilize a quasi-experimental action research design employing pre-test and post-test measures. Learners’ needs will be identified through diagnostic assessments and item analysis. Contextualized learning materials will be developed and implemented alongside targeted interventions such as remediation, gamified review, and peer tutoring. Data will be collected through assessments and monitoring tools, and analyzed to determine the effectiveness of the intervention in improving learner performance.', 'June 2026-April 2027', 'School Principal, Master Teachers, Research C', '100000.00', '', 2026, 128798, 104, 12, 131),
(530, 'ARAL PROGRAM: Intensive Pull-Out Remediation Program', 'To significantly improve learners’ reading proficiency by implementing structured, intensive, and data-driven ARAL interventions.', 'The Intensive Pull-Out Remediation Program resulted in measurable improvements in learners’ reading proficiency, including enhanced decoding, fluency, and comprehension skills, as well as a significant reduction in non-readers and increased learner confidence.', 'The program will utilize a data-driven, learner-centered, and differentiated remediation approach, focusing on systematic phonics instruction, guided reading, and continuous progress monitoring to address individual reading difficulties.', 'June 2026-April 2027', 'School Principal, Master Teachers, Research C', '100000.00', '', 2026, 128798, 104, 12, 131),
(531, 'School DRRM: Multi-Hazard Simulation', 'To enhance the preparedness, responsiveness, and safety of learners and school personnel by conducting realistic and systematic multi-hazard simulation drills, ensuring effective implementation of the school’s Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (', 'The conduct of the Multi-Hazard Simulation resulted in improved emergency response skills, validated DRRM protocols, reduced evacuation time, and increased preparedness among learners and personnel, as evidenced by drill performance and evaluation results.', 'The activity will use a simulation-based, participatory, and scenario-driven approach to ensure that learners and personnel actively practice and apply DRRM protocols in realistic emergency situations.', 'Every Quarter', 'School Principal, Master Teachers, School DRR', '50000.00', '', 2026, 128798, 104, 12, 131),
(532, 'Procurement and Utilization of SNED Materials', 'To ensure inclusive, equitable, and quality learning by procuring and effectively utilizing SNED-friendly instructional materials and assistive devices that address the diverse needs of learners with disabilities.', 'The procurement and utilization of SNED materials resulted in improved access to inclusive learning, increased learner participation, enhanced academic performance, and strengthened teacher capacity in delivering differentiated instruction.', 'The activity will employ a needs-based, inclusive, and data-driven approach, ensuring that procurement and utilization of SNED materials are responsive to the individual learning needs of learners with disabilities and aligned with inclusive education principles.', 'June 2026-April 2027', 'School Principal, Master Teachers, School SNE', '100000.00', '', 2026, 128798, 104, 12, 131),
(533, 'Alfresco Learning Hub Project', '1. Establish an outdoor library \r\n2. Provide the various clubs and organizations with safe and outdoor seating facility for meetings, study sessions, and activity planning', '1. Thirty sets of tables and benches for seating\r\n2. Book-boxes by the trees\r\n3. Literacy-responsive activities for students and community partners', '1. Realign saved school funds for the seating and paving of the walkways\r\n2. Conduct monthly Trivia Nights to create a reading culture at City High, encourage community partnerships, and afford the purchase of age-appropriate, contemporary books\r\n3. Orient teachers and students on the use and maintenance of the hub\r\n4. Conduct school literacy-responsive activities in the hub to reduce the learner\'s language anxiety and encourage a reading culture at City High', 'March 2026 to March 2027', 'School Head and the Coordinating Council', '88837.50', 'AD is SDO-approved.', 2026, 305680, 103, 12, 126),
(534, 'Classroom Repairs', '1. Complete the repair of the remaining 11 JHS classrooms', 'Improved and more easily maintained classrooms', '1. Have learners and teachers collaborate in the design and repair of their respective classroom in order to encourage ownership and care of their own space', 'April to December 2027', 'School Head, JHS advisers and learners', '462000', 'Repair is in APP 2026 as this is a target for SIP cycle 2025-2028', 2026, 305680, 103, 12, 126),
(535, 'Provision of sufficient classroom seating', '1. Tap schools with excess seating for donation\r\n2. Tap potential partners for donation\r\n3. Request additional log donations from DENR for the construction of benches and chairs', 'Sufficient classroom seating', '1. Exhaust potential for donors\r\n2. Repaint donated wooden chairs to improve aesthetics and user experience\r\n3. Utilize log donations for designing dynamic classroom chairs and benches ', 'April to December 2026', 'School Head', '20000', '', 2026, 305680, 103, 12, 126),
(536, 'Intensive Subject Remediation Sessions', 'To bridge learning gaps in Reading & Comprehension, Science, and Mathematics through focused small-group instruction.', '1. Individual Progress Reports\r\n2. Improved assessment scores (min. 3-5% increase)\r\n3. Portfolio of completed remedial modules', 'Differentiated Instruction: Grouping students by skill level.\r\nGamified Learning: Using interactive tools and hands-on Science kits.\r\nPeer Tutoring: High-performers assisting peers under teacher', 'Quarter 2 - Quarter 4 (Twice weekly, after cl', 'School Head, Subject Coordinators, Classroom ', '500', 'A comprehensive, multi-disciplinary approach that directly addresses the foundational gaps in literacy and numeracy.', 2026, 129420, 103, 12, 128),
(537, 'Conduct Leaderhip Training Workshops', 'Strengthen school leadership', 'Improved leadership evaluation results', 'Training Approach', 'June to July 2026', 'School Heads, Teachers and Staff', '3000', 'Stakeholders actively engaged; improvement in decision transparency', 2026, 129382, 103, 12, 127),
(538, 'Quarterly Quality Assurance & Item Analysis Workshop', 'To identify the least mastered competencies (LMCs) across all grade levels through systematic item analysis of quarterly exams.', '1. Detailed Item Analysis Reports per subject\r\n2. List of Priority Learning Gaps\r\n3. Validated Test Bank', 'Descriptive Statistical Mapping: Calculating Difficulty and Discrimination indices for each test item.\r\nCollaborative Review: Departmental focus groups to validate results.', 'End of every Quarter (Assessment Week)', 'School Principal, SBM Coordinator, Subject Ch', '150', 'This design demonstrates a transition from mere \'compliance testing\' to \'data-informed instruction,\' fulfilling the SBM requirement for evidence-based decision-making in the curriculum and learning strand', 2026, 129420, 103, 12, 128),
(539, 'Organization and Reconstitution of School Governance Council ', 'To establish functional SGC with defined roles and responsibilities.\r\nTo equip SGC members with knowledge on their roles in SBM implementation.\r\nTo ensure active participation in school planning and decision-making.', 'Organized SGC with approved composition and structure.\r\nSGC members trained and oriented on SBM principles.\r\nMinutes of meetings, approved plans and resolutions.', 'Conduct orientation and discussion of SBM roles and collaborative planning session. Selection of members and issuance of designation orders.', 'July 2026 & Quarterly ', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers, Barangay', '3000', 'Can be integrated with PTA Meeting', 2026, 129377, 103, 12, 127),
