(558, 'Reading Recovery Program', '*To help Grade 3 learners achieve grade-level reading proficiency.\r\n*To improve learners’ fluency, comprehension, and vocabulary skills.\r\n*To reduce and eliminate frustration and non-readers in Grade 3.', '*Zero non-readers in Grade 3\r\n*Majority of learners reading at grade level\r\n*Improved EGRA reading assessment results', '*Conduct EGRA pre-test and post-test\r\n*Daily remedial reading sessions for struggling readers\r\n*Small group guided reading activities\r\n*Use of phonics, sight words, and comprehension exercises\r\n*Peer tutoring (buddy reading)\r\n*Use of leveled reading materials and storybooks\r\n*Regular monitoring of learners’ progress', 'Whole Year-Round', 'School Head/Grade 3 Teacher/Reading Coordinat', 'Budgetary Requirement (for 25 learners):  Printing of reading materials (worksheets, passages) – ₱800 Flashcards / visual aids – ₱500 Basic storybooks / improvised reading materials – ₱1,000 Supplies (bond paper, markers, folders) – ₱400 Incentives (', 'Focus on early intervention and consistent reading practice at school and at home to ensure all Grade 3 learners become independent readers.', 2026, 128517, 57, 12, 118),
