(579, 'Mobilization and Strengthening of Stakeholder Partnerships to Support School PPAs and Improve Learner Proficiency', '1. To engage and mobilize stakeholders in supporting the implementation of school PPAs\r\n2. To improve literacy and numeracy proficiency levels of learners, especially among IP learners\r\n3. To establish sustainable partnerships with barangay officials', '1. Functional School-Community Partnership Program established\r\n2. At least 3–5 active stakeholders supporting school PPAs\r\n3. Conduct of remediation, enrichment, and literacy/numeracy programs with stakeholder support\r\n4. Improved learner proficiency levels (based on assessment results such as Phil-IRI, Numeracy Tests, etc.)\r\n5. Increased participation of parents and IP community in school activities', '1. Conduct stakeholder mapping within Barangay Palma Gil and nearby schools (cluster of 14 schools)\r\n2. Organize consultative meetings/dialogues with IP elders, parents, and barangay officials\r\n3. Launch advocacy campaigns on improving learner proficiency (reading and numeracy)\r\n4. Partner with stakeholders for resources (learning materials, feeding support, volunteer tutors)\r\n5. Implement targeted interventions such as:\r\n       a. Reading remediation sessions\r\n       b. Numeracy enhancement programs\r\n       c. Peer tutoring and community volunteer teaching\r\n6. Integrate culturally relevant and contextualized learning materials for IP learners\r\n7. Establish regular monitoring and feedback mechanism with stakeholders\r\n8. Recognize and incentivize stakeholder contributions through school recognition programs', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (Whole School Year)', 'School Head, Teachers, Learners, Parents/Guar', '10000', 'This action plan prioritizes inclusive education by strengthening collaboration with stakeholders and ensuring that interventions are culturally responsive to IP learners. Sustained stakeholder engagement is expected to significantly improve learner proficiency and overall school performance.', 2026, 137056, 58, 12, 40),
