(620, 'Rehabilitation of   Computer Laboratory/ Classroom ', '1. Assess and repair salvageable computer units\r\n\r\n2. Safely dispose of non-repairable ICT equipment\r\n\r\n3. Install necessary wiring and improve flooring for a safe ICT environment\r\n\r\n4. Acquire additional functional computers to complete the laborato', '1. Inventory report identifying functional, repairable, and condemned units\r\n\r\n2. Repaired and usable computer units\r\n\r\n3. Properly disposed non-repairable equipment (with documentation)\r\n\r\n4. Computer laboratory with installed wiring \r\n\r\n5. Minimum number of working computers ready for student use\r\n', '1. Conduct inventory and assessment of all existing computers\r\n\r\n2. Coordinate with technician for repair of salvageable units\r\n\r\n3. Prepare condemnation report for irreparable units\r\n\r\n4. Request approval for disposal following DepEd/property guidelines\r\n\r\n5. Improve laboratory room (electrical wiring, outlets, flooring)\r\n\r\n6. Mobilize support from LGU, PTA, alumni, NGOs for funding or donations\r\n\r\n7. Procure additional computers (brand new or refurbished)\r\n\r\n8. Install and test all equipment\r\n\r\n9. Develop laboratory usage schedule and policies', 'Assessment & Inventory: June  Repair  Condemn', 'School Head / Principal  ICT Coordinator / Co', '35,000.00', 'Subject for rehabilitation and restoration of ICT equipment.', 2026, 128719, 58, 12, 34),
