(725, 'ACTION PLAN ON INCREASING THE NATIONAL ACHIEVEMENT TEST (NAT) RATING IN GRADE SIX\r\n\r\n', 'To improve the National Achievement Test (NAT) Performance by Strengthening Instruction, Learner Support, Teacher Competence and Stakeholders Involvement.', '-Identified least mastered skills\r\n-Identified least mastered skills\r\n-NAT aligned lesson plans\r\n-Improve Mastery of Competencies and Skills\r\n-Learners\' familiarization and mastery of NAT-type questions\r\n-List of Priority Learners\r\n-Improved Learners’ Performance\r\n-Increased reading and numeracy levels\r\n-Learners prepared for NAT\r\n-Improved Teaching Strategies\r\n-Enhanced teacher\'s performance\r\n-Improved classroom instruction\r\n-Adequate review materials\r\n-Conducive learning atmosphere\r\n-Engaging lessons\r\n-Parents awareness, participation and support\r\n-Strong home-school partnership\r\n-Additional learning resources\r\n-Updated progress report.\r\n-Adjusted strategies\r\n-Basis for next improvement plan\r\n-\r\n-', '-Conduct item analysis of Previous NAT results\r\n-Align daily lesson plans with NAT Competencies\r\n-Use differentiated instruction and remediation strategies\r\n-Integrate HOTS questions in quizzes and exams\r\n-Identify slow learners and at risk-pupils\r\n-Conduct of remedial and enrichment classes\r\n-Implement weekly reading and numeracy programs\r\n-Conduct NAT simulation tests\r\n-In-school LAC sessions on NAT strategies\r\n-Coaching and Mentoring for teachers handling NAT Subjects\r\n-Sharing of Best Practices and Instructional Materials\r\n-Developed and reproduced NAT-based review materials\r\n-Improve Classroom Learning Environment\r\n-Utilize ICT and Audio-visual materials\r\n-Conduct parent orientation on NAT Importance.\r\n-Regular communication on learner’s progress\r\n-Seek support from BLGU and SGC\r\n-Weekly monitoring of learners’ progress.\r\n-Monthly evaluation and action plan implementation\r\n-Post-NAT analysis and documentation\r\n', '-December 1-3, 2025', '', '', '', 2026, 500846, 58, 12, 35),
