(737, 'BRIDGING GAPS, BOOSTING PERFORMANCE: A STRATEGIC INTERVENTION PLAN FOR IMPROVING\r\nNATIONAL ACHIEVEMENT TEST RESULTS IN GRADE 10 & 12\r\nSCHOOL YEAR 2026-2027\r\n\r\n', 'To improve the National Achievement Test (NAT) Performance by Strengthening Instruction, Learner Support, Teacher Competence and Stakeholders Involvement.', '-Minutes of the Meeting\r\n-Narrative Report\r\n-Attendance\r\n-List of possible topics/content -coverage to be included in the review\r\n-Compiled test items to be used as review materials\r\n-Conducted review session\r\nDocumentation\r\n-Feedback from monitoring\r\n-Result of mock test\r\n-Narrative report\r\n-Photo\r\n-Documentation\r\n\r\n', '-Identification of competencies:\r\n     *identify and note down least mastered competencies in the previous quarters\r\n-check competencies covered in the previous NAT to be utilized as additional basis for NAT review\r\n-Gather, prepare, and compile review materials from different sources\r\n-Conduct review sessions and strengthen instructional supervision\r\n-Conduct weekly assessment\r\n-Monitoring and feedback \r\nReview Schedule:\r\nMWF – content review (Eng., Sci., Math, AP, FIL.) at 3:15PM to 4:15PM.\r\nTTh – Practice/drill NAT processes at 3:15PM to 4:15PM\r\nSee attached review matrix  \r\n-Conduct mock test\r\n-NAT exam', '     December 1-3, 2026      ', '', '', '', 2026, 500846, 58, 12, 35),
(738, '1.Meeting to All Grade 6 Teachers\r\n2.Allocation of budget in the MOOE for the supplies and during the NAT exam\r\n3.Locate the NAT Like Tests in the test bank and if ever download and print activity sheets for practice in English,Science,Mathematics,Fi', 'to improve NAT proficiency level from 42.31% in SY 2024-25 to 75% in SY 2026-2027', '1.Planned of Action\r\n2.Allocated budget for the supplies and other materials needed\r\n3.Compiled folders per subject \r\n4.Results of daily review sessions\r\n5.Improved learner familiarity with NAT format\r\n6.Improved Instructional strategies of teachers', '1.Discussion of NAT results and planning  \r\n2.Included in the MOOE budget quarter 3\r\n3.Compiled NAT-like test materials and printed copies of the downloaded materials\r\n4.Daily review sessions implemented as schedule\r\n5.Practice test results item analysis\r\n6.Focus on Teaching strategies ', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'Grade 6 learners,Teachers and school Head', '5000', '75% proficiency level in NAT will be attained', 2026, 128590, 58, 12, 36),
