(818, 'School-Based Management Implementation Program', 'To empower school heads, teachers, and community members in planning and implementation.\r\nTo promote transparency and accountability in school operations.\r\nTo enhance collaboration between the school and the community.', 'Approved School Improvement Plan (SIP) aligned with SBM principles.\r\nIncreased stakeholder participation in school programs and activities.\r\nImproved school performance indicators (e.g., attendance, achievement, engagement).', 'Conduct orientation and capacity-building sessions on SBM.\r\nOrganize workshops for planning, implementation, and evaluation.\r\nFacilitate stakeholder meetings (teachers, parents, community leaders).\r\nImplement collaborative decision-making processes.\r\nMonitor progress through regular meetings and reporting.\r\nProvide feedback and continuous improvement strategies.', 'June - July 2026 ; Preparation Phase: 1–2 wee', 'School Head, Teachers and Stakeholders', '5000', 'Active participation of all stakeholders is highly encouraged.\r\nContinuous support from the school administration is essential.\r\nFlexibility in implementation may be applied depending on school needs.\r\nSustainability of SBM practices should be prioritized.', 2026, 204536, 58, 12, 40),
(819, 'Monitoring Evaluation and Reporting', 'To assess the impact of facility improvements and report achievements to stakeholders.', 'Monitoring reports, Terminal report highlighting achievements, challenges and lesson learned.\r\nEnhanced SBM level rating for School Facilities domain', 'Regular site visits and inspection.\r\nCollect feedback from users ( teachers, students )\r\nData analysis facility conditions before and after.\r\nPrepare and present progress reports during SGC/SPT Meetings and School Assemblies.', 'October to Dec. 2026', 'SBM Coordinator, School Head, SGC/SPT members', '1500', 'Ensure accountability and provides valuable insights for future SBM initiatives.\r\nCelebrates successes.', 2026, 128720, 58, 12, 34),
(820, 'Governance and Accountability-3. Feedback Mechanism', 'Improve school Services', 'Feedbacks Reports', 'Surveys, suggestion boxes,', 'Quarterly', 'Teachers, Parents', '2000', 'Continuous  Improvement', 2026, 128660, 58, 12, 0),
(821, 'Mobilization and Strengthening of Stakeholder Partnership to Support School PPA\'s and Improve Learners Proficiency', '1.To engage and Mobilized stakeholder in Supporting the Implementation of School Partnership Program. \r\n2.To Improve Literacy and Numeracy Proficiency Level of Learners , Especially among IP Learners.\r\n3.To Establish Sustainable Partnership with Bara', '1. Functional School-Community Partnership Program Established.\r\n2.At Least 3-5  Active Stakeholder Supporting School PPA\'s .\r\n3. Conduct of Remediation, Enrichment, and Literacy/ Numeracy Programs with the Support of External Stakeholder.', '1. Conduct Stakeholder Mapping Within the Barangay Dagohoy and Nearby Schools.\r\n2.Organize Consultative Meeting/ Dialogue with IP Elders, Parents, and Barangay Officials.\r\n3.Launch Advocacy Campaigns on Improving Learners Proficiency (Reading/Numeracy).\r\n4.Partnership on Stakeholder for Resources ( LMS, Feeding Support, Volunteer Tutors ).\r\n5. Implement Targeted Intervention such as Peer Tutoring, Reading Remediation Sessions, RPSB  Tutors on Reading.\r\n6.Integrate Culturally Relevant and Contextualized Learning Materials for IP Learners.\r\n7. Establish Regular Monitoring Feedback Mechanism based on Performance of the Learners.\r\n', 'June 2026- March 2027( Whole Year Round)', 'School Head, Teachers, Learners, Tribal Leade', '2000', 'This Action Plan Prioritized Inclusive Education by Strengthening Collaboration with Stakeholders and Ensuring that Intervention are Responsive and Sustainable to IP L earners.', 2026, 204515, 58, 12, 40),
(822, '1.Orientation on Mental Health and Psychosocial Support\r\n2.Strengthening the School Mental Health and Child Protection Programs\r\n3.Establishment of a School Counseling and Wellness Corner\r\n4.Integration of Social-Emotional Learning (SEL) in the Curri', '1.Increase awareness and understanding of mental health among learners, teachers, and parents.\r\n2.Establish a functional support system for mental wellness.\r\n3.Provide a safe space for learners to express emotions and seek support\r\n4.Develop learners', '1.Increased awareness and reduced stigma on mental health\r\n2.Functional and responsive support system\r\n3.Accessible and child-friendly wellness space\r\n4.Improved emotional resilience and positive behavior\r\n5.Supported and emotionally stable learners\r\n7.Improved well-being and reduced stress levels\r\n8.Empowered and supportive parents', '1.Conduct seminars and symposiums on stress management, emotional well-being, and resilience.\r\n2.Organize and activate the School Mental Health Team and Child Protection Committee.\r\n3.Set up a designated area for counseling, relaxation, and psychosocial activities.\r\n4.Integrate SEL concepts into EsP, Homeroom Guidance, and daily classroom routines.\r\n5.Offer one-on-one or group counseling and referrals when necessary.\r\n6.Organize mindfulness exercises, physical activities, and stress-relief sessions.\r\n7.Conduct parenting seminars on positive discipline and emotional support.\r\n8.Maintain records, conduct surveys, and coordinate with health professionals', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'Teachers, MAPEH Coordinator, SELG Officers', '3000.00', '', 2026, 128590, 58, 12, 36),
