(833, 'Establishment of School Computer Laboratory', '1. Provide learners with access to technology for digital learning. 2. Enhance students\' ICT skills and digital literacy. 3. Support teaching and learning through the use of computers. ', '1. Functional computer laboratory with complete basic equipment. Increased student access to ICT resources. 3. Improved digital skills among learners and teachers. ', 'Needs Assessment and Planning, identifies required number of computers and equipment and assess available space and facilities. Resource Mobilization, prepares budget proposals and seek fundings from internal and external stakeholders. ', 'June 2026 - March 2027', 'Amie Glee p. Duclayan- School Head, Charity H', '15000', 'Strong coordination with stakeholders as essential for the success of the programs, projects, and activities. ', 2026, 128808, 58, 12, 40),
(834, '1.Reconstitution and Orientation of School Governance Council (SGC)\r\n2.Development of SGC Annual Work and Financial Plan\r\n3.Regular Conduct of SGC Meetings\r\n4.Capacity Building on School-Based Management (SBM) and Governance\r\n5.Joint School Monitorin', '1.Reactivate and strengthen the functionality of SGC members\r\n2.Ensure clear direction and shared governance priorities.\r\n3.Ensure continuous participation and decision-making.\r\n4.Strengthen understanding of participatory governance.', '1.Fully oriented and reactivated SGC\r\n2.Approved SGC Work and Financial Plan\r\n3.Functional governance system with records of meetings\r\n4.Improved governance knowledge and participation\r\n5.Improved transparency and decision-making\r\n6.Active stakeholder participation in school programs', '1.Conduct orientation on roles, functions, and DepEd governance guidelines.\r\n2.Collaborative planning workshop for SGC members.\r\n3.Monthly or quarterly meetings with documented minutes.\r\n4.Training and workshops on SBM practices and leadership roles.', 'July 2026-April 2027', 'School Head, DepEd Resource Persons, SGC Memb', '3000.00', '', 2026, 128590, 58, 12, 36),
