(905, 'Conduct targeted review sessions, intervention programs, and enrichment activities for Grade 6 learners in preparation for the National Achievement Test (NAT).', 'Grade 6 learners achieve proficiency level in all 21st century skills and core learning areas in the National Achievement Test (NAT).', 'Increased NAT proficiency rates among learners\r\nImproved performance in core subjects (Math, Science, English, etc.)\r\nEnhanced critical thinking, communication, and problem-solving skills\r\nNAT results meeting or exceeding national standards', 'Diagnostic tests to identify learning gaps\r\nDifferentiated instruction and remediation sessions\r\nUse of interactive and learner-centered teaching strategies\r\nIntegration of 21st-century skills (collaboration, ICT, critical thinking)\r\nRegular formative assessments and feedback\r\nPeer tutoring and coaching sessions', '3–6 months prior to the scheduled NAT', 'School Head, Subject Teachers, Learners', '1000', 'Continuous monitoring and evaluation should be conducted to ensure effectiveness of interventions and to adjust strategies as needed.', 2026, 128622, 58, 12, 44),
