(914, 'STRATEGIC INTERVENTION PLAN FOR IMPROVING NATIONAL ACHIEVEMENT TEST RESULTS IN GRADES 6', 'Improved NAT 6 Performance from 41.46% to 52%  MPS', 'Identification of priority competencies\r\n\r\n\r\nData-driven and school-aligned NAT Action Plan\r\n\r\nShared understanding of learners performance gaps among teachers\r\nEstablished baseline learner Proficiency data\r\n\r\n\r\nAccurate identification of learning gaps/learning needs\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nOrganized learner grouping for remediation\r\nStrengthened stakeholder engagement\r\n\r\nSecured material, moral, and logistical support\r\n\r\nApproved and supported Intervention Plan\r\nImproved learner mastery of targeted competencies\r\n\r\n\r\nIncreased readiness for NAT-type assessments\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDocumented learner progress\r\nEnhanced learners test-taking skills and familiarity with NAT format\r\n\r\nReduced errors in filling out answer sheets and name grids\r\n\r\nIncreased learner confidence and endurance during long exams\r\nTrained learners to actual NAT examination conditions\r\n\r\nIdentification of remaining learning gaps before the actual NAT examination day\r\n\r\nIncreased learner motivation through rewards and recognition\r\nSmooth and orderly conduct of the NAT examination\r\n\r\nReduced absenteeism and test anxiety\r\n\r\nLearners able to focus and perform optimally during the exam\r\nIdentified strengths and areas for improvement\r\n\r\nInputs for future NAT intervention planning\r\nSustained stakeholder engagement\r\n\r\nInstitutionalized best practices for NAT preparation', 'Conduct of previous NAT results item analysis per learning area\r\n\r\nIdentify least learned competencies and performance trends\r\n\r\nConvene teachers to interpret data and set priority targets\r\n\r\nCraft a data-driven NAT Action Plan aligned to AIP\r\nAdminister diagnostic tests in a form of NAT like test.\r\n\r\n\r\nAnalyze results to validate least learned competencies\r\n\r\nGroup learners according to Proficiency Level in reference to conduct of remedial Instruction\r\n\r\nDevelop review and remediation schemes according to the least learned competencies. \r\nPresent diagnostic and NAT data to stakeholders\r\n\r\nDiscuss factors affecting low MPS \r\n\r\nMobilize stakeholder support for NAT interventions\r\nAcquire and formalize commitments through MOA/MOU\r\nImplement scheduled remedial/review classes based on learner needs & least learned competencies\r\n\r\nFocus instruction on least learned competencies\r\n\r\nIntegrate NAT-like questions during remedial activities\r\n\r\nMonitor learner progress regularly\r\nConduct intensive review sessions on the Least Learned Competencies across learning areas\r\n\r\nTrain learners on proper filling out of name grids and answer sheets\r\n\r\n\r\nAdminister simulated NAT exercises\r\n\r\n\r\nReinforce test-taking strategies and time management\r\n\r\nInclusion of the conduct of NAT Intensive Review with AIP/APP.\r\nProvision of Supplies\r\n\r\nProvision of supplemental snacks\r\n\r\nImplement reward system for Top scorers\r\n\r\nProvide Logistics Support (Hatid-Sundo)\r\nProvision of snacks and meals\r\n\r\nProvide Logistics Support (Hatid-Sundo)\r\nAnalyze NAT results to determine strengths, weaknesses, and trends across learning areas\r\n\r\nConduct post-assessment/ reflection with teachers to evaluate the effectiveness of implemented interventions\r\n\r\nIdentify successful strategies and gaps in instruction and assessment\r\n\r\nDocument lessons learned and best practices for future reference\r\nRecognize learners, teachers, and stakeholders who contributed to improved NAT performance\r\n\r\nInstitutionalize effective intervention strategies for continuous implementation through research-based initiative\r\n\r\nIntegrate successful practices into the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)', 'July 2026 to Feb 2027', 'Raul E. Consencino', '', '', 2026, 128678, 58, 12, 38),
