(997, '\"Bayanihan sa Paaralan: Brigada Eskwela 2026\"\r\n', '	* To record and putting up  BE info campaign tarpaulins.\r\n       * To make  and distribute school BE Tarpaulins in every purok.\r\n          * To inform community through social media networks, posting tarpaulins.\r\n', 'Accomplishment reports, Cleaned and repaired classrooms ready for opening of classes\r\nTeacher-led brigada activities documentation\r\n', 'Prepare and consigned people entrusted to facilitate the implementation through the Brigada Eskwela agreed scheme', 'June 9-13,2025', 'School Principal,BE coordinator, Teachers and', 'MOOE', 'Brigada Eskwela is a yearly program of the Department of Education Philippines that promotes bayanihan to prepare schoold before opening of classes.', 2026, 128656, 58, 12, 36),
(998, 'Health and Hygiene Education Campaign to address absenteeism for some Grade 3 pupils due to sickness', 'To promote proper hygiene and prevent common illnesses', 'Increased awareness and improved hygiene practices inside and outside classroom', 'Conduct sessions on handwashing, sanitation, and disease prevention; integrate in lessons\r\nPurchase health kits and sanitation materials such as hand soap, alcohol, and sanitizers', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers, School Clinic Coordina', '3000', 'Sustain through integration in the curriculum and consistent practice', 2026, 500449, 58, 12, 40),
(999, 'Attendance Monitoring and Intervention System', 'To track absenteeism and provide timely intervention', 'Reduced absenteeism rate among Grade 3 pupils', 'Daily attendance monitoring, home visits, and follow-up of frequently absent pupils', 'weekly/ monthly', 'Teachers, School Head,  School Guidance Coord', '3000', 'Help Grade 3 learners achieve the proficiency level for each cluster of early language, literacy, and numeracy skills.', 2026, 500449, 58, 12, 40),
(1000, 'Literacy& Numeracy Enhancement Program', 'To improve learners literacy and numeracy skills by implementing targeted intervention and remediation activities that address identified gaps, with the aim of increasing ELLNA performance  results to at least the expected proficiency level (75% and ', 'Increased percentage of learners in achieving at least 75% and above proficiency level  in ELLNA results; Identified gaps in literacy and numeracy competencies', 'The methodology is based on diagnosis/ learners needs assessment, targeted intervention , continuous monitoring  and stakeholders support to ensure measurable improvement in ELLNA performance', 'July 2026-February 2027', 'School Heads, teachers, parents, learners', '5000.00', 'The school\'s implementation of ELLNA intervention activities is responsive to learners\'  needs, as it is based on identified learning gaps in literacy  and numeracy', 2026, 128568, 58, 12, 35),
(1001, 'Intervention Strategies for Struggling Readers', '*To improve learners\' reading fluency  and comprehension skills\r\n* To develop phonemic awareness and word recognition skills \r\n*To increase learners\'  confidence and interest in reading\r\n', '-Attendance\r\n-Documentation\r\n', '-LAC Session about Intervention Strategies for Struggling Readers \r\n Tackle ways on redeveloping/developing strategies in reading instruction\r\n- Understanding the importance Reading Intervention Instruction Strategies\r\n', 'February 9,2025', 'School head, Teachers', '', 'The reading intervention program has been effective in supporting struggling readers. However, sustained practice and parental involvement are encouraged to ensure long-term improvement.', 2026, 128656, 58, 12, 36),
(1002, 'Capacity Building for Teachers on Mental Health', 'To equip teachers with basic skills in identifying and supporting learners with mental health concerns', 'Trained teachers on basic psychosocial support', 'Conduct LAC sessions, workshops, and webinars on mental health and psychosocial support', 'Whole year round', 'School Head, Master Teachers, External Expert', '10000', '', 2026, 500449, 58, 12, 40),
(1003, 'Learner Mapping and Community Profiling', 'To identify and locate OSYs and adult learners in the community', 'Updated master list of OSYs and adult learners', 'Conduct house-to-house survey and coordination with barangay officials and purok leaders', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers,', '1000', '', 2026, 500449, 58, 12, 40),
(1004, 'SCHOOL ACTION PLAN in ARALING PANLIPUNAN, COMPREHENSIVE SEXUALITY EDUCATION (CSE) and ALTERNATIVE DELIVERY MODE (ADM', '1. To conduct trainings on content and teaching-learning strategies \r\n2. To conduct enhanced trainings on CSE and Balik Kasaysayan \r\n3. To Integrate CSE, Balik Kasaysayan and Peace Education concepts\r\n4. To address the learning needs of the PARDO/LAR', 'List of conducted co- curricular programs \r\nList of accredited mode\r\nList of participated activities and contests in AP and CSE\r\nRenovated and revived Heroes Park \r\n-Updated Bulletin boards and information corner\r\n', '*Ensure trainings to teachers and facilitators of the teaching-learning delivery \r\n* Development of Lesson Plans with CSE, Balik Kasaysayan, and Peace Education   Integration\r\n* Intensify the Alternative Deliver Mode Program', 'October 2025- March 2026', 'School Head, School Coordinator', '', 'The learner demonstrates a good understanding of basic concepts in Araling Panlipunan and actively participates in class discussions.\r\nThe learner need to improve comprehension of concepts and requires additional support in analyzing historical events and their significance.', 2026, 128656, 58, 12, 36),
(1005, 'WINS( Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene in Schools)', 'To upgrade the school\'s WINS rating from 2-star to 3-star by ensuring safe, accessible,  sustainable, and sustainable water and sanitation facilities for all learners.', '* Achieved 3-star WINS Level\r\n* Improved learner health and hygiene practice\r\nFunctional and sustainable water and sanitation facilities', 'Assessment-Based Planning\r\n            Utilize WINS 3-STAR monitoring results to identify gaps\r\n            Prioritize needs based on urgency and impact on learners.\r\nCollaborative Implementation\r\n                 engaged stakeholders such as teachers, PTA, LGU and community partners\r\nMonitoring and Evaluation', 'June - August, Quarterly , ', 'School head, LGU, PTA, WINS Coordinator', '', 'Through strong stakeholder collaboration, continuous monitoring, and sustainable practice, the school aims to achieve and maintain a 3-Star WINS rating.', 2026, 128656, 58, 12, 36),
(1006, 'Implementation of School-Based Management (SBM) Programs', 'To effectively implement SBM principles in school operations and decision-making', 'Improved school performance, active stakeholder participation, and efficient resource management', 'Conduct regular meetings, execute planned school programs, involve stakeholders in decision-making, monitor progress through feedback and evaluation', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, Teachers, PTA O', '10000', 'For continuous implementation and monitoring', 2026, 315903, 58, 12, 43),
(1007, 'A1. Presentation and Analysis of the School NAT Results  (Baseline Data) ', 'Analyze previous NAT performance to identify least mastered skills and gaps', 'Data-driven NAT intervention plan', 'Conduct data analysis workshop, item analysis, and subject area breakdown', 'June - August 2026', 'School Head, Subject Coordinators, Teachers', '500', 'Basis for all intervention', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1008, 'A2. Setting of NAT Improvement Targets', 'Establish realistic and measurable performance targets per subject', 'Defined NAT targets and indicators', 'Benchmarking, goal-setting workshop', 'June - August 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Planning Team', '300', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1009, 'A3.1. Development and Implementation of NAT Intervention Program (Reading, Numeracy, Science) and NAT Review Materials', 'Improve learner performance in reading, numeracy and science through various programs and provision of adequate review tools', 'Improved learner performance and established intervention program, review materials ', 'Collaborative planning, intervention design, creation of worksheets, modules, reviewer compilation remediation, drills and exercises', 'July 2026 – February 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Planning Team', '300', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1010, 'A3. Orientation of Teachers and Students on NAT Framework and Test-Taking Strategies', 'Enhance teachers’ and students\' understanding of NAT structure and competencies', 'Enhanced instructional delivery, improved teacher and learner preparedness', 'Seminar-workshop, sharing of best practices, LAC Sessions, coaching and mentoring', 'July 2026 – February 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Planning Team, Student', '300', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1011, 'A5. Integration of NAT Competencies and NAT-like Assessments in Daily Lesson Plans', 'Ensure alignment of instruction with NAT competencies and exposure of learners to national-like assessment such as NAT', 'Enhanced mastery of competencies and readiness', 'Curriculum mapping, lesson integration, drills and exercises', 'July 2026 – February 2027', 'School Head, Teachers', '300', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1012, 'Stakeholder Orientation', 'To strengthen shared leadership and community ownership of the school’s vision.', '100% participation of key stakeholder groups.', 'Conduct annual SBM assessment and planning with parents/LGU.', 'June 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers', '1000.00', '', 2026, 204529, 58, 12, 39),
