(1027, 'A9. Post-NAT Evaluation, Review and Analysis', 'Evaluate effectiveness of interventions and identify best practices and areas for improvement', 'Evaluation report', 'Data analysis, review meetings', 'March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Planning Team', '300', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1028, 'Develop / Update School Strategic Plan (SSP)', 'To establish a clear, data-driven strategic direction for school improvement', 'Approved and documented SSP covering vision, mission, goals, and strategic priorities', 'Conduct school data analysis (SBM assessment, NAT, enrolment data); SWOT analysis; Stakeholder consultation; Draft SSP; Present to SBM Council for approval', 'June to August 2026', 'School Head, Department Heads, Master Teacher', '500', '', 2026, 128677, 58, 12, 38),
(1029, 'PROJECT AIM HIGH (Academic Intervention for Mastery on Holistic Improvement of grade 6 for High Achievement in NAT 6)', 'To improve  the academic performance  of Grade 6 learners in the National  Achievement Test by providing  targeted remediation, strengthening  skills and promoting mastery  of essential competencies', '*Improved NAT Performance-Increased mean percentage\r\n*Mastery of Least Learned Competencies\r\n*Establish remediation Materials and Plans', 'The program follows a data-driven remediation approach. It begins with assessing learners to identify least mastered skill followed by careful planning of targeted intervention activities. Learners are grouped baaed on their needs and teachers conduct focused , interactive remediation process.', 'July 2026-March 2027', 'School head, adviser, academic teacher, paren', '6000.00', 'The implementation of Project  AIM HIGH  highlights the importance of targeted and timely remediation in improving learners\' academic performance in NAT 6.  Through a structured and data-driven approach, the program effectively addresses learning gaps and supports the mastery of essential competencies among  Grade 6 pupils of Gavino e. Amoguis Elementary School.', 2026, 128568, 58, 12, 35),
(1030, 'Implement Electronic Records and Service Delivery Systems', 'To improve the efficiency, accessibility, and quality of school frontline services', 'Digitized enrollment process; Online request/release of school documents; Updated school website or social media page', 'Adopt DepEd\'s digital platforms; Train office staff; Set up school online communication channels; Develop frontline service feedback mechanism', 'July to October 2026', 'School Head, School Records Officer, ICT Coor', '500', '', 2026, 128677, 58, 12, 38),
(1031, 'Reconstitute and Organize School Governing Council (SGC)', 'To ensure a duly constituted, representative, and functional SGC per DepEd guidelines', 'Reconstituted SGC with officers; Organizational meeting minutes; SGC action plan', 'Issue election memorandum; Conduct SGC election; Conduct organizational meeting; Orient newly elected officers on roles and responsibilities', 'July to September 2026', 'School Head, All Stakeholder Sectors (Parents', '1000', '', 2026, 128677, 58, 12, 38),
(1032, 'Conduct Regular SGC Meetings', 'To ensure the SGC actively participates in school governance, planning, and monitoring', 'At least 4 SGC meetings per year; Documented resolutions and minutes of meetings', 'Schedule quarterly meetings; Prepare agenda and reports; Present school performance data; Act on resolutions', 'Quartetly (August, October, January, March)', 'School Head, SGC Officers and Members', '500', '', 2026, 128677, 58, 12, 38),
(1033, 'Conduct Reading and Numeracy Intervention Programs', 'To improve literacy and numeracy skills of learners', 'Increased proficiency rate of learners', 'Remediation classes, pull-out sessions, use of contextualized materials', 'Whole Year', 'Teachers, Reading Coordinators', '20000', 'Priority program', 2026, 501661, 58, 12, 34),
(1034, 'Conduct Regular School Monitoring, Evaluation and Adjustment (MEA)', 'To systematically track progress of programs, projects, and activities and make timely adjustments', 'Quarterly MEA reports; Updated SPT (School Planning Table); Documented adjustments and recommendations', 'Use DepEd MEA tools; Conduct classroom observation; Analyze school performance data; Present results to SGC and faculty; Apply adjustments', 'Quarterly (August, October, January, March)', 'School Head, , MEA Team, SGC team', '500', '', 2026, 128677, 58, 12, 38),
(1035, 'NAT Review and Enhancement Program', 'Increase NAT performance of Grades 6, 10, 12', 'Improved NAT results', 'Review classes, mock exams, coaching', 'Q3–Q4', 'Subject Teachers, School Head', '15000', 'For academic excellence', 2026, 501661, 58, 12, 34),
(1036, 'Strengthen Partnerships with LGU, NGO, and Private Sector', 'To harness external support for school programs, resources, and community engagement', 'Signed MOAs / MOUs with partners; Documented collaborative activities; Mobilized additional resources for school', 'Identify potential partners; Conduct stakeholder mapping; Conduct dialogues and consultation; Formalize partnerships through MOA/MOU; Recognize partners during School Anniversary', 'July – August (partnership building); Ongoing', 'School Head, SGC, PTA, Community Partners, LG', '1000', '', 2026, 128677, 58, 12, 38),
(1037, 'Conduct LAC Sessions and CPD Activities', 'Enhance teacher competencies', 'Improved teaching practices', 'Training, peer coaching, demo teaching', 'Quarterly', 'Teachers and School Head', '20000', 'Continuous development', 2026, 501661, 58, 12, 34),
