(1143, '1. Conduct intensive review on ELLN & NAT\r\n2.Conduct Test Item Analysis\r\n3.Campaign of zero bullying incidence\r\n4.Establish functional CPC\r\n5. Provide SNED facilities\r\n6. Provide Frontline Services\r\n7.Allocate budget for library/ reading  hub and com', '1. To improve literacy, numeracy and test performance in NAT\r\n2.To identify least mastered skills and adjust instructional delivery\r\n3. To ensure a safe, inclusive and learner-centered school climate\r\n4.To implement strict adherence to the CPP\r\n5.To ', '1. 10% increase in MPS\r\n2. Quarterly Item Analysis reports and modified lessons plans\r\n3.100% incident reporting and resolution, zero reported cases\r\n4. Functional CPC\r\n5. Supplies and Materials for learners with special needs\r\n6.Functional Citizen\'s Charter and Help Desk\r\n7.Functional Library/reading hub and computer room', '1. Conduct intensive remedial reading and \"Math-A-Day\" drills\r\n2.Regular SLC ( School Learning Center) workshops and teachers mentoring\r\n3.Value-laden integration in classes and peer mediation program\r\n4.Capacity building for teachers and community awareness campaigns\r\n5.Stakeholder mobilization (Brigada Eskwela) and LGU partnership\r\n6.Streamlining document requests via digital tracking or \"Express Lanes\"\r\n7.Resource mobilization from private partners and inventory maintenance', 'May 2026- April 2027', 'SH, AO, SBM TWG, Teachers', '30000.00', '', 2026, 128640, 58, 12, 43),
(1144, '1. Preparation of proposal and other documents                    \r\n2.  Policy Orientation & Awareness Campaign on Anti Bullying Act\r\n3. Peer Support / Buddy System\r\n4. Counseling & Intervention Program\r\n5. Monitoring & Evaluation', '1. To conduct a training and awareness seminar on anti bullying act.                      \r\n2.  To diminish  bullying cases in the school campus and reinforce school-wide commitment.\r\n3.  To prevent isolation and support vulnerable students.\r\n4.  To ', '1. School has zero bullying incidence.\r\n2. Increased student engagement and awareness.\r\n3. Strong peer relationships and early issue detection.\r\n4. Emotional recovery and behavior correction.\r\n5. Data-driven improvements.', '1. Training and campaign.\r\n2. Poster-making, slogan contests, assemblies.\r\n3. Assign buddies, peer mentoring programs.\r\n4. One-on-one counseling, behavior contracts.\r\n5. Surveys, incident reports review, feedback sessions.', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers/Advisers, Parents, Grad', '10000.00', 'Continue the program to have zero bullying in school campus.', 2026, 304359, 107, 12, 79),
