(1172, 'Conduct targeted review sessions, intervention programs, and enrichment activities for Grade 12 learners in preparation for the National Achievement Test (NAT).', 'Grade 12 learners achieve proficiency level in all 21st century skills and core learning areas in the National Achievement Test (NAT).', 'Increased NAT proficiency rates among learners Improved performance in core subjects (Math, Science, English, etc.) Enhanced critical thinking, communication, and problem-solving skills NAT results meeting or exceeding national standards', 'Diagnostic tests to identify learning gaps Differentiated instruction and remediation sessions Use of interactive and learner-centered teaching strategies Integration of 21st-century skills (collaboration, ICT, critical thinking) Regular formative assessments and feedback Peer tutoring and coaching sessions', '3–6 months prior to the scheduled NAT', 'School Head, Subject Teachers, Learners', '1000', 'Continuous monitoring and evaluation should be conducted to ensure effectiveness of interventions and to adjust strategies as needed.', 2026, 315901, 58, 12, 43),
(1173, 'Implementation of Reading intervention program for Grade 7-12 learners through structured reading, writing, and numeracy activities.', 'Grade7-12 learners achieve the proficiency level literacy and numeracy skills.', 'Improved reading comprehension and fluency levels Enhanced writing and communication skills Increased numeracy and problem-solving abilities Majority of learners meeting or exceeding proficiency standards Reduced number of non-readers and struggling learners', 'Conduct baseline assessment to identify learner needs Implement differentiated instruction and small-group interventions Use phonics-based and comprehension strategies in reading Integrate numeracy drills and real-life problem-solving tasks Utilize learning materials such as workbooks, flashcards, and ICT tools Conduct regular progress monitoring and feedback sessions Engage parents through home-based reading and numeracy activities', 'Whole school year (with quarterly monitoring)', 'School Head Grade 7-12 Teachers Reading Coord', '1000', 'Close monitoring and continuous intervention are necessary to ensure all learners reach the desired proficiency level. Collaboration with parents is highly encouraged.', 2026, 315901, 58, 12, 43),
