(1189, 'Policy formulation at school level', '1.Provide clear guidelines for teachers ,students and staff.\r\n2. Promote uniform implementation of rules and procedures.\r\n3. Avoid confusion and ensures everyone follows the same standard.\r\n4.Support policies that enhance instruction  and student per', '1 .Written school policies.\r\n2.Policies signed /approved by the school head and governing bodies.\r\n3. Minutes of meetings showing consultation and approval.\r\n4.Attndance sheets ,photos and reports    \r\nfrom meetings with parents , teachers and community members .\r\n6. Copies of policies shared to teachers ,parents and learners.', '1. Participatory Approach hich involves teachers, parents , students and community members that ensures the policy is inclusive and acceptable by the stakeholders.\r\n2. Data-driven approach herein school data are used like test results ,attendance and dropout rates . Identify the problems and base policies on evidence.\r\n3. Collaborative decision- making here  committees  and  working groups are formed for drafting the policies together to promote shared ownership and accountability.', 'June- September ,2026', 'Teachers ,Students, Parents, School Head, Sta', '5000.00', 'Effective policy formulation uses participatory ,data-driven ,collaborative and evaluative strategies to ensure the policy is relevant ,accepted and sustainable.', 2026, 128637, 58, 12, 43),
