(1246, 'Intensifying Stakeholders\' Engagement for Improved Learner Outcomes', 'a. Strengthen Stakeholder Engagement: To actively involve and mobilize parents, barangay officials, and the wider community in supporting the school\'s programs and activities.\r\nb. Improve Learner Proficiency: To enhance the literacy and numeracy skil', '1. A functional and active School-Community Partnership Program.\r\n2. Demonstrable improvements in learner literacy and numeracy, as evidenced by assessment results (e.g., Phil-IRI, NAT, formative assessments).\r\n3. Strengthened and sustained engagement with parents, barangay officials, and other community partners.', '1. Stakeholder Mapping: Identify key individuals and groups within Barangay Sta. Cruz who can contribute to the school\'s success.\r\n2. Community Dialogues: Organize regular meetings with parents and barangay officials to discuss school needs, share progress, and gather feedback.\r\n3. Advocacy Campaigns: Launch initiatives to raise awareness about the importance of improving learner proficiency in reading and numeracy.\r\n4. Partnership Development: Actively seek partnerships with stakeholders for resources such as learning materials, technology, and volunteer support.\r\n5. Formalizing Partnerships: Establish formal agreements (MOAs/MOUs, resolutions) with barangay officials and other stakeholders to solidify collaborations.\r\n6. Monitoring and Feedback: Implement a system for continuous monitoring of progress and gathering feedback from all stakeholders.\r\n7. Recognition and Rewards: Develop a program to acknowledge and celebrate the contributions of stakeholders to the school\'s achievements.', ' June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Administrative Officer', '10000', ' This action plan is designed to promote inclusive education by building strong collaborations and ensuring that all interventions are sensitive and responsive to the diverse cultural contexts of our learners. The anticipated outcome is a significant contribution to improved learner proficiency and overall school performance.', 2026, 128702, 58, 12, 34),
