(1279, 'Comprehensive NAT Preparation Program integrating 21st-century skills and mastery of core learning areas for Grades 6 learners', 'Improve learners’ performance in all core learning areas assessed in NAT (English, Math, Science, etc.)\r\nDevelop 21st-century skills such as critical thinking, communication, collaboration, and problem-solving\r\nIncrease the percentage of learners ach', 'Increased NAT proficiency rates for Grades 6\r\nImproved quarterly and mock test results\r\nLearner portfolios showcasing 21st-century skills (projects, presentations, outputs)\r\nConsolidated NAT review and intervention materials', 'Conduct diagnostic and baseline assessments aligned with NAT competencies\r\nImplement targeted remediation and enrichment programs per subject area\r\nIntegrate 21st-century skills through project-based learning (PBL), collaborative tasks, and inquiry-based activities\r\nConduct regular NAT simulation tests and drills\r\nUse data-driven instruction and learner progress tracking\r\nProvide coaching on test-taking strategies, time management, and critical analysis\r\nOrganize peer tutoring, mentoring, and study groups\r\nEngage parents through orientation and progress updates', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (with monthly monitori', 'Subject Teachers ,Grades 6, School Head, Mast', '1000', 'Sustained intervention, regular assessment, and integration of 21st-century skills in daily instruction are essential. Continuous stakeholder support will significantly impact learner achievement in NAT.', 2026, 128620, 58, 12, 44),
(1280, 'Implementation of School-Based Retention and Learner Support Program', 'Reduce the number of learners at risk of dropping out\r\nImprove learner attendance and engagement in school activities\r\nStrengthen support systems for struggling and disadvantaged learners\r\nPromote a positive and inclusive school environment', 'Decreased drop-out rate compared to previous school year\r\nImproved attendance and participation of learners\r\nEstablished database of at-risk learners with intervention plans\r\nIncreased parent and community involvement in learner support', 'Identify at-risk learners through attendance monitoring and academic performance tracking\r\nConduct home visits and regular parent-teacher conferences\r\nProvide counseling and psychosocial support services\r\nImplement remedial classes and flexible learning options\r\nEstablish peer support groups and mentoring programs\r\nOffer school-based incentives (recognition, awards, feeding programs if applicable)\r\nCollaborate with community stakeholders for additional support\r\nMonitor learner progress regularly and adjust interventions as needed', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (continuous implementa', 'School Head, Teachers, Guidance Counselor, Pa', '1000', 'Consistent monitoring, strong home-school collaboration, and timely interventions are critical in sustaining reduced drop-out rates. Flexibility in addressing learners’ needs will ensure continued participation and completion of schooling.', 2026, 128620, 58, 12, 44),
(1281, 'Implementation of Culture-Sensitive and Inclusive School Activities Program', 'Promote respect for diverse cultures, traditions, and beliefs among learners\r\nIntegrate cultural awareness and sensitivity into teaching and school activities\r\nStrengthen inclusivity and appreciation of local and indigenous cultures\r\nFoster a safe an', 'Increased learner awareness and appreciation of cultural diversity\r\nSuccessful conduct of culture-sensitive school events and celebrations\r\nIntegration of cultural elements in lesson plans and classroom activities\r\nStrengthened participation of community and cultural groups', 'Integrate culture-sensitive content in daily lessons across subject areas\r\nCelebrate cultural events, festivals, and heritage days in school\r\nInvite community members and cultural representatives as resource speakers\r\nConduct activities such as cultural presentations, storytelling, and exhibits\r\nUse inclusive and respectful language and practices in school policies\r\nProvide teacher training on cultural sensitivity and inclusive education\r\nEncourage learner participation in multicultural group activities\r\nMonitor implementation through feedback and reflection sessions', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (aligned with school c', 'School Head, Teachers, Learners, Parents/Guar', '1000', 'Continuous collaboration with the community and respect for cultural diversity are essential. Activities should be inclusive, age-appropriate, and reflective of the learners’ cultural backgrounds.', 2026, 128620, 58, 12, 44),
(1282, 'Development and Implementation of the School Strategic Plan', 'ormulate a clear and comprehensive strategic plan aligned with school goals and standards\r\nIdentify priority areas for improvement based on data and needs assessment\r\nStrengthen participatory planning involving all stakeholders\r\nEstablish measurable ', 'Approved School Strategic Plan document\r\nDefined vision, mission, goals, and key result areas (KRAs)\r\nAction plans with specific targets, timelines, and assigned responsibilities\r\nMonitoring and evaluation framework for implementation', 'Conduct situational analysis (SWOT, school data review, performance indicators)\r\nOrganize planning workshops with stakeholders (teachers, parents, community members)\r\nReview existing policies, programs, and school performance data\r\nSet SMART goals and align them with national and local education priorities\r\nDevelop implementation plans, including timelines and resource allocation\r\nValidate and finalize the strategic plan through consultation meetings\r\nDisseminate the plan to all stakeholders\r\nMonitor and evaluate progress regularly and update the plan as needed', 'June 2026 – September 2026 (planning phase), ', 'School Head, Teachers, Master Teachers, Schoo', '1000', 'A collaborative and data-driven approach ensures that the strategic plan is relevant, achievable, and responsive to the needs of the school community. Continuous monitoring is essential for successful implementation.', 2026, 128620, 58, 12, 44),
(1283, 'ACTION PLAN FOR STRENGTHENING SCHOOL-BASED MANAGEMENT (SBM) IMPLEMENTATION\r\nSchool Year 2026–2027', 'General Objective:\r\n\r\nTo strengthen the implementation of School-Based Management (SBM) in order to improve school performance and learner outcomes.\r\n\r\nSpecific Objectives:\r\nStrengthen shared leadership and governance structures.\r\nImprove curriculum ', 'EXPECTED OUTPUTS\r\nImproved SBM Level of Practice\r\nIncreased stakeholder participation\r\nEnhanced learner performance\r\nTransparent and accountable governance\r\nStrengthened school-community partnerships', 'The implementation of this Action Plan for strengthening School-Based Management (SBM) shall utilize a participatory, data-driven, and results-oriented approach anchored on continuous improvement principles.\r\n\r\nA. Participatory Approach\r\n\r\nThe school shall actively involve internal and external stakeholders including teachers, parents, learners, community leaders, Local Government Units (LGUs), and partner organizations in planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation. Mechanisms such as School Governing Council (SGC) meetings, PTA assemblies, and stakeholder consultations shall be conducted to ensure shared decision-making and collective accountability.\r\n\r\nB. Data-Driven Decision Making\r\n\r\nAll programs, projects, and activities shall be guided by relevant school data such as learner performance, attendance, SBM assessment results, and other key performance indicators. The School Monitoring, Evaluation, and Adjustment (SMEA) process shall be regularly conducted to analyze data, identify gaps, and formulate appropriate interventions.\r\n\r\nC. Capacity Building\r\n\r\nContinuous professional development activities shall be provided to school personnel and stakeholders to enhance their competencies in SBM implementation. This includes Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions, training workshops, coaching, and mentoring focused on leadership, curriculum delivery, and resource management.\r\n\r\nD. Collaboration and Partnership\r\n\r\nThe school shall strengthen linkages with stakeholders and partner institutions to support the delivery of quality education. Resource sharing, technical assistance, and community support shall be maximized to address school needs and sustain SBM practices.\r\n\r\nE. Transparency and Accountability\r\n\r\nThe school shall ensure transparency in all operations through regular reporting, posting of financial and program updates, and open communication channels. Accountability mechanisms shall be observed through proper documentation, monitoring, and evaluation of all implemented activities.\r\n\r\nF. Continuous Improvement Cycle\r\n\r\nThe implementation shall follow the Plan-Do-Check-Act (PDCA) cycle:\r\n\r\nPlan: Identify needs and develop interventions through SIP and AIP.\r\nDo: Implement planned activities effectively and efficiently.\r\nCheck: Monitor progress and evaluate outcomes using SBM tools.\r\nAct: Adjust strategies based on evaluation results.', 'SY 2026-2027', 'School Principal, Assistant School Principal.', '100,000.00', 'To be implemented.', 2026, 304206, 57, 12, 118),
(1284, 'Implementation of NAT Readiness and 21st Century Skills Enhancement Program', 'Improve learners’ mastery of competencies in core learning areas\r\nStrengthen critical thinking, problem‑solving, communication, and collaboration skills\r\nIncrease NAT proficiency levels of target learners', 'Conducted NAT readiness activities and review sessions\r\nImproved formative and summative assessment results\r\nEnhanced learner performance in simulated NAT assessments', 'Conduct diagnostic and item analysis to identify learning gaps\r\nImplement focused remediation, enrichment, and review sessions\r\nIntegrate 21st century skills through performance‑based tasks and activities\r\nDiscuss assessment results and strategies during LAC sessions', 'Conduct diagnostic and item analysis to ident', 'School Head; Subject Teachers; LAC Leaders; L', '25,000.00', 'High‑priority academic performance indicator', 2026, 128866, 59, 12, 139),
