(1326, 'Conduct Literacy and Numeracy  Enhancement Program', 'Improve reading skills and numeracy skills of pupils in Key Stage 1', '80% of pupils  improved reading and numeracy skills  in key stage 1', 'reading and numeracy remediation , DEAR, peer reading', 'June - August ', 'CRLA , Phil-Iri, RMA , reading Coordinators a', '2000.00', 'Monitor  pupils progress monthly, monitor CRLA, Phil-Iri and Aral Program Results', 2026, 128593, 58, 12, 35),
(1327, 'The school engages local industries to strengthen its TLE-TVL course offerings.', 'To have a memorandum of agreement between local industries for the different courses offered in a Techvoc School.', 'Signed Memorandum of agreement between local industries for the different courses offered in a Techvoc School.', 'Crafting of memorandum of agreement between local industries for the different courses offered in a Techvoc School.', '4th Quarter', 'School Head, Head Teachers and Master Teacher', '6000', 'Memorandum of agreement approved between local industries for the different courses offered in a Techvoc School', 2026, 304311, 61, 12, 7),
(1328, 'Conduct Phil IRI based reading intervention and Conduct Math intervention to stage 2 learners.', 'Improve learners\' reading comprehension and strengthen learners\' number sense, basic operations, and problem-solving skills in the numeracy cluster. Provide targeted intervention to learners who are performing below the proficiency level in Phil IRI.', '100 of grade 6 learners who took the NAT achieved proficiency level. ', 'Conduct reading remediation ( Catch Up Friday) and 12:30 reading intervention', 'within the school year of 2026-2027', 'Teachers, SH, Parents and guardians', '30000', 'Implement and monitor the plan religiously.', 2026, 128855, 59, 12, 139),
(1329, 'Establishment of TVL Program through Industry Linkages', 'To formally prepare and implement the offering of TVL strands in the school aligned with industry needs', 'Functional TVL program proposal, signed MOAs with industry partners, prepared facilities, and trained teachers', 'Conduct needs assessment, stakeholder consultation, curriculum planning, MOA signing, facility preparation, teacher training, and pilot implementation', '1 School Year (Phased: Planning–Implementatio', 'School Head, TLE Teachers, PTA, LGU, TESDA, I', '10000', 'For approval and implementation of TVL offering', 2026, 316017, 59, 12, 0),
(1330, ' Achieve the proficiency level in all 21st century skills and core learning areas in the National Achievement Test (NAT) of Grade 6 learners.', 'To improve the National Achievement Test (NAT) performance of Grade 6 learners by strengthening instruction, assessment, and learner support systems toward achieving proficiency in all core learning areas and 21st century skills.', 'Increased percentage of Grade 6 learners achieving Proficient and Advanced levels in the NAT\r\nImproved mean percentage score (MPS) in all core learning areas (English, Math, Science, Filipino, Araling Panlipunan)\r\nFunctional and implemented NAT review and enhancement program for Grade 6 learners', 'Data-Driven Instruction\r\nUse NAT results, formative assessments, and diagnostic tests to identify learning gaps and guide instruction.\r\nRemediation and Intervention Programs\r\nConduct daily or scheduled remediation sessions for struggling learners focusing on least mastered competencies.\r\nIntensive NAT Review Program\r\nImplement structured review classes covering all core learning areas with practice tests and drills.\r\nDifferentiated Instruction\r\nAdjust teaching strategies based on learners’ abilities, readiness, and learning styles.\r\nMastery-Based Learning Approach\r\nEnsure learners master competencies before moving to the next lesson through repeated practice and reinforcement.\r\nRegular Formative Assessment\r\nUse quizzes, exit tickets, and short tests to monitor progress and provide immediate feedback.\r\nReading and Numeracy Enhancement Program\r\nConduct daily reading sessions and numeracy drills to strengthen foundational skills.\r\nCollaborative Learning Strategies\r\nUse group work, peer tutoring, and cooperative learning to enhance engagement and understanding.\r\nICT-Integrated Instruction\r\nUtilize educational videos, online quizzes, and digital learning tools to reinforce lessons and improve engagement.\r\nTeacher Collaboration (LAC Sessions)\r\nConduct regular Learning Action Cells focused on improving instructional strategies and addressing learner difficulties.\r\nParent Involvement Strategy\r\nEngage parents through conferences, home support activities, and progress monitoring to reinforce learning at home.\r\nPerformance Monitoring and Feedback\r\nRegularly track learner progress and provide feedback to students, parents, and teachers for continuous improvement.', 'School Year 2026-2027', 'Teachers and School Head', '30000.00', '          The implementation of strategies to improve NAT performance among Grade 6 learners is ongoing and shows positive progress. Instructional interventions such as remediation, review sessions, and data-driven instruction have been consistently conducted. However, continuous strengthening is needed in reading comprehension, numeracy skills, and mastery of least learned competencies. Sustained collaboration among teachers, learners, parents, and stakeholders is essential to further improve learner outcomes and achieve the target proficiency level in all learning areas.', 2026, 128857, 59, 12, 139),
(1331, 'Strengthen Community Partnerships', 'To increase stakeholder support and involvement', 'Active partnerships and resource sharing', 'Meetings, MOA signing', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'School Head, SGC Members, Community Leaders', '1000', 'Sustain partnerships', 2026, 128667, 58, 12, 36),
(1332, 'Implement School-based Feeding and Health Programs', 'To improve learner health, nutrition, and school attendance', 'Program report, health records, photo documentation', 'Coordination with RHU, LGU, and parent volunteers', 'Year-round', 'District Nurse, Class Advisers, PTA, BHW', '15000.00', 'Ongoing, Beneficiaries identified per class advisory', 2026, 205007, 59, 12, 147),
(1333, 'Make a functional library', 'Establish a designated, organized, and well-maintained library space within the school premises.', 'A functional, organized school library\r\nA clean, well-arranged, and accessible library space with labeled bookshelves, a reading area, a librarian\'s desk, and a display board — ready for daily use by learners and teachers.', 'Form a library committee, Identify and prepare the library space, Conduct book and material inventory, Write a library development plan, Conduct book donation drive, Seek funding from MOOE and external partners, Procure basic library furniture and materials, Open the library for regular use, and Monitor and maintain the library regularly.', 'January- March 2027', 'Teachers, SHs, Parents, LGU', '50000', 'Needs assistance from stakeholders due to lack of resources.', 2026, 128855, 59, 12, 139),
(1334, 'Documentation and Reporting of SBM Practices', 'To maintain organized records and evidence', 'Complete and updated SBM portfolio', 'Assign focal persons, use templates', 'Monthly', 'School Head, SGC Members, Community Leaders', '1000', 'For validation and assessmen', 2026, 128667, 58, 12, 36),
(1335, 'MENTAL WELLNESS PROGRAM', 'To implement a school functional support mechanism for mental wellness to  learners and teachers for SY 2026-2027.', 'Functional support mechanism  for mental wellness (once a week)', 'Once a week (every Friday  from 4:00  PM-4:30 PM Zumba, sports activities)', 'From June 2026-March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers and Learners', '7500.00', 'For implementation and budgeting subject for approval.', 2026, 128931, 59, 12, 0),
