(1384, 'Anti-Bullying & Child Protection', 'To maintain zero bullying -incidence rate to ensure child protection', 'Zero reported cases', 'Conduct of anti-bullying symposium; \"No to Bullying\" campaigns; regular homeroom guidance.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Principal, Guidance Coordinator, Teach', '1000.00', 'M&E Protocol: Guidance Coordinator to submit RECORD OF BULLYING INCIDENCE to the School Principal monthly', 2026, 128836, 59, 12, 138),
(1385, 'F1. Baseline Assessment on Child Abuse Cases and Risk Factors', 'Assess, document, and analyze existing and potential child abuse cases, including physical, emotional, neglect, and exploitation, in order to identify risk factors and design appropriate preventive interventions', 'Comprehensive baseline report identifying risk factors, vulnerable learners, and priority intervention areas to prevent child abuse', 'School records, incident reports, and referrals; conduct confidential surveys and interviews; coordinate with guidance office and community stakeholders; analyze data to identify patterns, at-risk learners, and possible sources of abuse', 'June 2026', 'School Head, Child Protection Committee (CPC)', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1386, 'F2. Strengthening and Capacity Building of Child Protection Committee (CPC)', 'Enhance the capability of the Child Protection Committee to effectively implement, monitor, and respond to child abuse cases in accordance with child protection policies and legal frameworks', 'Functional and well-trained CPC capable of handling child protection cases effectively and responsibly', 'Reorganize CPC, clarify roles and responsibilities, conduct capacity-building workshops on child protection laws, reporting procedures, and case management; establish coordination with external agencies', 'June – July 2026', 'School Head, CPC Members, Teachers, External ', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1387, 'The school has zero child abuse incidence', 'To reduce child abuse incidence in school', ' Reduced child abuse incidence in school', 'Conduct extensive symposium and orientation about child abuse to learners and teachers.', 'Monthly', 'School Head, Head Teachers and Master Teacher', '8000', 'Provided avenue wherein child abuse cases in school will be reduced.', 2026, 304311, 61, 12, 7),
(1388, 'Integration of NAT like questions during regular classroom assessments', 'Improve proficiency level of Grade 6 learners in core learning areas and 21st century skills', 'Improved NAT results and mastery of competencies', '- Conduct NAT review sessions and drills \r\n- Integration of critical thinking, collaboration, and problem-solving activities \r\n- Mock tests and remediation classes\r\n', 'SY 2026-2027', 'Teachers, School head, parents', '5000', '', 2026, 128584, 58, 12, 35),
(1389, 'Implementation of a School-Based Dropout Reduction Program (Early Warning System, Learner Monitoring, and Intervention Support)', 'To identify learners at risk of dropping out through an Early Warning System (EWS)\r\nTo reduce dropout incidence through timely and targeted interventions\r\nTo strengthen school-home-community partnership in supporting at-risk learners\r\nTo sustain 100%', 'Functional Early Warning System (attendance, behavior, academic tracking)\r\nUpdated list of at-risk learners with intervention plans\r\nConducted home visitations and parent conferences\r\nEstablished learner support mechanisms (remediation, feeding, counseling)\r\nDecreased dropout rate (target: 0% or significant reduction)', 'Early Identification: Monitor daily attendance and performance; flag learners with frequent absences\r\nProfiling: Maintain individual learner profiles (academic, socio-economic, behavioral factors)\r\nIntervention:\r\nConduct home visitations\r\nProvide remediation classes and peer tutoring\r\nImplement feeding program for nutritionally at-risk learners\r\nOffer guidance and counseling sessions\r\nEngagement: Strengthen PTA involvement and community support (barangay officials, NGOs)\r\nMonitoring: Monthly tracking and case conferencing among teachers\r\nRecognition: Motivate learners through incentives and recognition for improved attendance', 'Whole Year Round, with monthly monitoring and', 'School Head, Class Advisers, Teachers, Guidan', '10000', 'This action plan aims to institutionalize a proactive and sustainable dropout reduction mechanism. Continuous monitoring, strong stakeholder collaboration, and learner-centered interventions will ensure that the indicator progresses from “Not Yet Manifested” to “Always Manifested.”', 2026, 205046, 59, 12, 144),
(1390, 'School Self-Assessment (SSA)', 'To evaluate current SBM level of practice', 'Completed SBM assessment tool', 'Use SBM assessment instruments, focus group discussions', 'July 2026', 'SBM Team, Teachers, External Stakeholders', '500', 'Basis for planning', 2026, 128745, 58, 12, 41),
(1391, 'F3. School-Wide Orientation on Child Protection Policy and Safeguarding Practices', 'Increase awareness and understanding among learners, teachers, parents, and stakeholders on child abuse prevention, reporting mechanisms, and safeguarding responsibilities to ensure a safe learning environment', 'Informed school community with heightened awareness and vigilance against all forms of child abuse', 'Seminars, assemblies, and classroom discussions; disseminate child protection policies; use IEC materials, role-playing, and scenario-based activities to reinforce understanding', 'June – July 2026', 'School Head, CPC, Teachers, Parents, Learners', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1392, 'Orientation of Stakeholders on the Implementation of SBM', 'To inform stakeholders about the principles and importance of SBM\r\nTo clarify roles and responsibilities of each stakeholder\r\nTo encourage active participation in school programs and decision-making', 'Increased awareness and understanding of SBM among stakeholders\r\nAttendance of parents, teachers, and community members\r\nSigned commitment or agreement of support', 'Conduct orientation seminar/workshop\r\nUse Powerpoint presentations and open forum discussions\r\nInformational materials (brochures/handouts)', 'June 10, 2026', 'School Head, teachers, PTA Officers,, Parents', '1000', '', 2026, 129130, 59, 12, 151),
(1393, 'Saving PARDO', 'To control and minimize drop-out rates through early intervention.', '95%+ retention rate', 'Home visitation; modular learning options (i.e. ADM)', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Principal; ADM Coordinator; Class Advi', '1000.00', 'For class advisers to focus on Pupils-at-Risk of Dropping Out.', 2026, 128836, 59, 12, 138),
(1394, 'School Improvement Plan (SIP) Enhancement', 'School Improvement Plan (SIP) Enhancement', 'School Improvement Plan (SIP) Enhancement', 'Workshops, collaborative planning', 'July–August 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Stakeholders', '500', 'Data-driven planning', 2026, 128745, 58, 12, 41),
(1395, 'Teachers prepare contextualized learning material responsive to the needs of learners', 'Strengthen relevance of academic content to community, workplace, and everyday contexts.', 'Increased learner engagement and participation', 'Integrate local examples, community issues, and familiar scenarios into lessons.', 'June-March 2026', 'School Head, Teachers', '1610.00', '', 2026, 128934, 59, 12, 144),
(1396, 'ICT Integration In Teaching', 'Enhance digital literacy of teachers and learners', 'Improved use of technology in classroom instruction', 'Training on ICT coordinator, school head', 'Whole school year', 'Teachers, ICT coordinator, school head', '2000', 'Support modern and engaging teaching methods', 2026, 205022, 59, 12, 147),
(1397, 'The School has a functional support mechanism for mental wellness', 'Promote and support the mental wellness and well-being of learners, teachers, and school personnel.', 'Functional mental wellness support system (e.g., guidance services, peer support groups, sports activities).', 'Conduct regular mental health awareness campaigns, seminars, and psychosocial support activities.', 'Whole Academic Year (June 2026-March 2027)', 'Teachers, School Heads , Learners, Stakeholde', '3000', '', 2026, 128935, 59, 12, 144),
(1398, 'D4. Implementation of Preventive and Values Formation Programs', 'Promote positive behavior, respect, empathy, and inclusivity among learners through structured values formation and preventive programs integrated into daily school activities', 'Improved learner behavior, increased empathy, and reduced risk of bullying incidents', 'Integrate anti-bullying lessons into curriculum (EsP/GMRC); conduct campaigns, poster-making, role-playing, peer mentoring, and SEL activities; implement buddy systems and student-led initiatives', 'July 2026 – March 2027', 'Teachers, SSLG Officers, CPC', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1399, 'Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) Preparation', 'To operationalize SIP for the year', 'Approved AIP', 'Planning sessions and consultations', 'July–August 2026', 'School Head, Planning Team', '500', 'Linked to budget', 2026, 128745, 58, 12, 41),
(1400, 'D5. Establishment of Confidential Reporting and Immediate Response Mechanisms', 'Provide safe, accessible, and effective reporting systems and ensure timely and appropriate response to all bullying incidents to prevent escalation and recurrence', 'Functional and accessible reporting system with timely response to incidents', 'Install suggestion boxes, hotlines, and reporting forms; designate focal persons; ensure confidentiality; conduct immediate investigation and intervention following standard procedures', 'July 2026', 'School Head, CPC, Guidance Coordinator', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1401, 'Implementation of School Mental Wellness Support Program', 'To support learners’ mental and emotional well-being\r\nTo identify learners needing psychosocial support\r\nTo provide safe and supportive school environment', 'Identified learners needing support\r\nConducted guidance sessions and activities\r\nFunctional referral and support system\r\nImproved learner behavior and well-being', 'Conduct regular check-ins and simple assessments\r\nProvide guidance sessions and classroom activities\r\nEstablish referral system (teacher–school head–health personnel)\r\nEngage parents through meetings and communication\r\nCoordinate with barangay/health workers if needed\r\nMonitor learners regularly', 'Whole Year Round', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents, Barangay/Heal', '1500', 'A supportive and safe environment, along with strong coordination with parents and community, will ensure sustained mental wellness support for learners.', 2026, 205046, 59, 12, 144),
(1402, 'D6. Conduct of Counseling, Intervention, and Parent Engagement Programs', 'Provide appropriate psychosocial support, corrective interventions, and parental involvement to address bullying behaviors and support both victims and offenders effectively', 'Supported learners, resolved cases, and improved behavior through collaborative intervention efforts', 'Provide individual and group counseling, restorative practices, and behavior interventions; conduct parenting seminars and case conferences; coordinate with stakeholders for support', 'August 2026 – March 2027', 'Guidance Coordinator, Teachers, Parents, CPC', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1403, 'Recognition and Awarding Program', 'Motivate learners and recognize achievements', 'Increased learner motivation and participation', 'conduct awarding ceremonies; prepare certificates and tokens', 'End of school year ', 'Teachers, school head, parents', '1500', 'Encourages excellence and positive behavior', 2026, 205022, 59, 12, 147),
(1404, 'The school has reduced its drop-out incidence', 'To minimize absences due to the target number of days present in school.', 'Monitored the attendance of 4Ps recipient .', 'Constant monitoring of all teachers and 4Ps by MSWDO personnel.', 'Monthly', 'School Head, Head Teachers and Master Teacher', '8000', 'Minimize absences due to the target number of days present in school.', 2026, 304311, 61, 12, 7),
(1405, 'D7. Monitoring, Evaluation, and Recognition for Zero Bullying Incidence', 'Monitor program implementation, evaluate effectiveness, and recognize positive behavior and contributions toward achieving and sustaining a zero-bullying school environment', 'Zero bullying incidence report, documented best practices, and recognized positive school climate', 'Conduct regular monitoring, inspections, and data reviews; evaluate program outcomes; document best practices; implement recognition programs for model learners and child-friendly classrooms', 'Monthly Monitoring; Year-End Evaluation (Marc', 'School Head, CPC, Teachers, SSLG', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1406, 'Computer Laboratory Improvement', 'Upgrade the computer laboratory to provide a modern, safe, and conducive learning environment that supports the integration of technology in teaching and learning, enhancing digital literacy and 21st century skills of students.', 'Improved Computer laboratory', '- Planning conference\r\n- Crafting letter request to Division ICT personnel for computer equipment repair\r\n- Crafting resolution to LGU Provincial asking for building repair\r\n- Submit letter request and resolution \r\n- Follow up\r\n- Procure materials if budget is available\r\n- inspection of materials\r\n- Repair and improvement implementation\r\n- Monitor progress\r\n\r\n', 'January - June 2027', 'SPT, SPTA and School Head', '100000.00', '', 2026, 128860, 59, 12, 139),
(1407, 'Cultural Heritage Sensitivity', 'To promote inclusivity and respect for local diversity.', 'Culturally diverse festivals; inclusive lesson plans.', 'Integration inclusivity values in Araling Panlipunan; Indigenous Peoples (IP) Month celebrations; IP costume every Friday', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Principal, IP Coordinator, Class Advis', '2000.00', 'Recognition  of all local ethnic groups.', 2026, 128836, 59, 12, 138),
(1408, ' Reorganization and Strengthening of the School Governance Council (SGC)', 'To organize and activate a functional SGC\r\nTo strengthen participation of stakeholders in school governance\r\nTo support school programs through shared decision-making', 'Organized and active SGC with members\r\nConducted regular SGC meetings\r\nApproved plans and programs with stakeholder participation\r\nDocumented minutes and resolutions', 'Identify and organize SGC members (parents, teachers, community leaders)\r\nConduct orientation on roles and responsibilities\r\nHold regular meetings and planning sessions\r\nInvolve SGC in school planning, implementation, and monitoring\r\nDocument all meetings and activities', 'Whole Year Round', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents, SGC Members, ', '1500', 'Active stakeholder participation and regular meetings will ensure a functional and sustainable SGC.', 2026, 205046, 59, 12, 144),
(1409, 'The school has functional school-community planning team', 'Strengthen collaboration between the school and community stakeholders in planning and decision-making.', 'Conducted planning meetings with active participation of stakeholders (parents, LGU, community members).\r\n\r\nDocumented minutes of meetings, attendance, and agreed action plans.', 'Organize and formalize the School-Community Planning Team through designation and orientation of members.\r\nConduct regular consultative meetings, focus group discussions, and planning workshops.', 'Whole Academic Year (June 2026-March 2027)', 'School Head, Teachers, Learner and Stakeholde', '2500', '', 2026, 128935, 59, 12, 144),
(1410, 'G1. Comprehensive Training Needs Assessment (TNA) for Teachers', 'Systematically determine teachers’ priority professional development needs based on learner performance data, classroom observations, and individual competency gaps to ensure relevant and targeted LAC and L&D interventions', 'Consolidated TNA report highlighting priority areas for LAC and L&D interventions aligned with school goals and learner needs', 'Conduct surveys, classroom observations, performance reviews (IPCRF), and analysis of learner achievement data; facilitate focus group discussions to validate identified needs; consolidate and prioritize training areas', 'June 2026', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1411, 'G2. Strategic Planning and Design of Needs-Based LAC and L&D Program', 'Develop a structured and responsive LAC and L&D plan that addresses identified teacher needs and supports improved instructional practices and learner outcomes', 'Approved LAC and L&D annual implementation plan with clearly defined topics, schedules, and expected outcomes', 'Conduct collaborative planning workshops; design LAC sessions and L&D activities aligned with TNA results; prepare annual calendar and session guides; integrate into SIP and AIP', 'June 2026', 'School Head, LAC Coordinators, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1412, 'The school conducts culture-sensitive activities', 'To conduct symposium on the child friendly school survey.', 'Conducted symposium on the child friendly activities.', 'Intensify the school child friendly culture-sensitive in all activities of the school.', 'Monthly', 'School Head, Head Teachers and Master Teacher', '10000', 'Conducted symposium on child friendly activities.', 2026, 304311, 61, 12, 7),
(1413, 'Mental Wellness Support System', 'To provide professional psychological support for students/staff.', 'Established Mental Health/ Teen  Hub; counseling logs', 'Routine wellness check-ins; stress management webinars; 24/7 help desk in Mental Health/Teen Hub', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Principal, Guidance Coordinator, Teach', '2000.00', 'Conduct of \"Psychological First Aid\" training for staff to help Guidance Counselor in help  desk', 2026, 128836, 59, 12, 138),
(1414, 'G3. Conduct of Regular LAC Sessions Focused on Priority Needs', 'Enhance teachers’ pedagogical knowledge and instructional practices through continuous, collaborative, and needs-based professional learning sessions', 'Improved teaching practices and documented LAC outputs addressing identified needs', 'Facilitate monthly LAC sessions using varied approaches such as lesson study, case discussions, demonstration teaching, and peer sharing; focus on priority topics like literacy, numeracy, assessment, and classroom management', 'Monthly (July 2026 – March 2027)', 'Teachers, LAC Coordinators, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1415, 'G4. Implementation of School-Based L&D Training Programs', 'Provide targeted professional development opportunities that address specific competency gaps and enhance teachers’ effectiveness in delivering quality instruction', 'Enhanced teacher competencies and improved instructional delivery as reflected in classroom performance', 'Organize workshops, seminars, and in-service trainings (INSET); invite resource speakers; utilize blended learning approaches; align training content with TNA results and DepEd priorities', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Resource Speakers, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1416, 'Establishment and Operationalization of a Functional School Library', 'To establish a functional school library that supports teaching, learning, and research needs of learners and teachers.\r\nTo improve learners’ reading skills, study habits, and academic performance through access to quality learning resources.\r\nTo str', 'A designated and organized school library room.\r\nAdequate collection of printed and non-printed learning resources (books, references, magazines, instructional materials).\r\nAssigned library-in-charge and library policies in place.\r\nIncreased utilization of library resources by teachers and learners.', 'Conduct an assessment of available space and existing learning resources.\r\nIdentify and allocate a room for the library.\r\nSolicit support and donations from stakeholders (LGU, PTA, alumni, NGOs).\r\nProcure and organize library materials and basic furniture.\r\nDesignate a library-in-charge and orient teachers and learners on library use and policies.\r\nMonitor and evaluate library utilization regularly.', 'School Year 2026–2027 (1st–2nd Quarter: Plann', 'School Head Teachers / Library-in-Charge SBM ', '400000.00', 'Library establishment will be implemented in phases depending on the availability of funds and stakeholder support.', 2026, 128835, 59, 12, 138),
(1417, 'Implementation of Needs-Based Learning Action Cells (LAC) and L&D Activities', 'To conduct at least 10 needs-based LAC sessions in a year\r\nTo improve teachers’ competencies based on identified needs\r\nTo ensure timely approval and implementation of LAC proposals', 'Approved annual LAC plan with at least 10 sessions\r\nConducted LAC sessions with attendance and documentation\r\nImproved teacher practices based on LAC topics\r\nComplete MOVs (minutes, photos, outputs)', 'Conduct needs assessment among teachers\r\nPrepare and submit annual LAC plan early for approval\r\nCoordinate with higher offices for timely approval\r\nSchedule regular LAC sessions (monthly/bi-monthly)\r\nAssign facilitators per topic\r\nDocument all sessions (attendance, minutes, photos)\r\nMonitor and evaluate implementation', 'Whole Year Round', 'School Head, Teachers, LAC Facilitators, Dist', '8000', 'Early planning and timely submission of proposals will ensure approval and completion of required LAC sessions, making the indicator “Always Manifested.”', 2026, 205046, 59, 12, 144),
(1418, 'Re-organize SGC with 5-7 active members only', 'To make governance manageable and active', 'Functional SGC with defined roles', 'Simple Election (Chair, Secretary, Members after giving its Terms of References', 'June-July 2026', 'School Head, Selected   Parents, Brgy. Offici', '500.00', 'Just this amount be allocated for this activity, as it is not included in the School Improvement Plan (SIP) to be taken from the Canteen Income', 2026, 128734, 106, 12, 133),
(1419, 'G5. Coaching, Mentoring, and Peer Support Mechanisms', 'Strengthen teachers’ instructional competence and professional growth through sustained coaching, mentoring, and collaborative support systems within the school', 'Improved teacher performance, strengthened mentoring culture, and enhanced instructional practices', 'Conduct classroom observations, post-observation conferences, peer mentoring, and coaching sessions; provide feedback and action plans for improvement; encourage reflective teaching practices', 'Quarterly / Continuous', 'School Head, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1420, 'Inclusive Infrastructure for PWD learners', 'To ensure physical accessibility for all  PWD learners.', 'Ramps installed', 'Facility audit; infrastructure upgrades by installing ramps', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Principal, Physical Facilities  Coordi', '10000.00', '', 2026, 128836, 59, 12, 138),
(1421, 'G6. Monitoring and Evaluation of LAC and L&D Effectivenes', 'Assess the impact of LAC and L&D activities on teaching practices and learner outcomes through systematic monitoring, evaluation, and data analysis', 'Evaluation reports showing effectiveness of LAC and L&D activities and areas for improvement', 'Use evaluation tools, feedback forms, and performance data; conduct review meetings; analyze improvements in teaching and learning; adjust plans based on findings', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, LAC Coordinators, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1422, 'G7. Documentation, Sharing of Best Practices, and Continuous Improvement', 'Document successful strategies and promote a culture of collaborative learning and continuous improvement through sharing of best practices and innovations among teachers', 'Complete documentation portfolio, shared best practices, and sustained culture of professional collaboration', 'Compile LAC minutes, outputs, and training materials; conduct sharing sessions, demo teaching, and portfolio presentations; recognize outstanding practices and integrate improvements into future plans', 'Monthly / Year-End (March–April 2027)', 'School Head, LAC Coordinators, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1423, 'Establishment of a Functional Computer Corner / Shared ICT Space', 'To provide basic ICT access for learners despite limited resources\r\nTo gradually establish a functional computer laboratory/classroom\r\nTo integrate ICT in teaching and learning', 'Identified space for ICT use (shared area/computer corner)\r\nAvailable computers or ICT devices (donated or procured)\r\nConducted basic ICT-integrated lessons\r\nIncreased learner exposure to technology', 'Identify available space (shared classroom corner, office space, or multipurpose area)\r\nRequest support from LGU, stakeholders, NGOs, and alumni for computer donations\r\nMaximize available devices (teacher laptops, tablets, mobile phones if applicable)\r\nSchedule ICT use per class (rotation system)\r\nIntegrate basic ICT activities in lessons\r\nEnsure proper maintenance and monitoring of devices', 'Whole Year Round', 'School Head, Teachers, LGU, PTA, Stakeholders', '50000', 'Due to limited classrooms and lack of equipment, the school will adopt a phased and resource-maximizing approach to gradually establish a functional ICT learning space.', 2026, 205046, 59, 12, 144),
(1424, 'The School has functional School Governance Council (SGC)', 'Strengthen participatory governance through an active and functional School Governance Council (SGC).\r\n', 'Functional SGC with organized structure, defined roles, and regular meetings.\r\n\r\nDocumented minutes of meetings, resolutions, and action plans.', 'Enhance collaboration among school leaders, parents, community members, and stakeholders in decision-making.', 'Whole Academic Year (June 2026-March 2027)', 'School Head, Teachers, Learner and Stakeholde', '2000', '', 2026, 128935, 59, 12, 144),
(1425, 'Provision and Utilization of a Functional Computer and ICT Learning Laboratory', 'To provide a functional computer and ICT learning laboratory that supports the effective delivery of computer and technology-related subjects.\r\nTo enhance learners’ digital literacy, ICT skills, and readiness for 21st-century learning.\r\nTo strengthen', 'A designated and equipped computer and ICT learning laboratory.\r\nAvailable and functional computers with basic software and internet connectivity (if applicable).\r\nAssigned ICT coordinator / laboratory in-charge with clear roles and responsibilities.\r\nIncreased utilization of ICT facilities by teachers and learners during classes and activities.', 'Conduct an assessment of existing ICT resources and identify gaps.\r\nIdentify and prepare a suitable classroom to serve as the ICT laboratory.\r\nProcure computers, peripherals, and essential software through MOOE, donations, or LGU support.\r\nCoordinate with stakeholders (PTA, LGU, private partners) for additional resources and technical assistance.\r\nAssign an ICT coordinator and orient teachers and learners on proper use, care, and policies of the laboratory.\r\nMonitor, evaluate, and maintain the laboratory regularly to ensure sustainability.', 'School Year 2026–2027 (1st Quarter: Planning ', 'School Head ICT Coordinator / Designated Teac', '500000.00', 'School Head\r\nICT Coordinator / Designated Teacher\r\nTeachers\r\nSBM Core Group\r\nPTA Officers\r\nLGU / Stakeholders\r\nLearners', 2026, 128835, 59, 12, 138),
(1426, 'The school provides access to learning experiences for the disadvantaged, OSYs, and adult learners', 'Provide equitable access to quality education for marginalized groups.', 'Learners achieve basic literacy and numeracy competencies.', 'Use modular instruction, blended learning , and alternative delivery modes ', 'June 2026', 'Teachers ,School Head', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128934, 59, 12, 144),
(1427, 'Putting up of Library & Learning Resource Hub ', 'To provide access to learning resources and  enhance literacy and research capabilities.', 'Existence of a functional library', 'Setting up of library; accepting book donations; cataloging', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Principal, LR Coordinator, Teachers', '30000.00', 'Access to library scheduled per grade daily ', 2026, 128836, 59, 12, 138),
(1428, 'H1. Development of School-Based Recognition and Incentive System (SRIS)', 'Establish a fair, transparent, and motivating recognition system that acknowledges personnel achievements, promotes excellence, and aligns with school goals and performance standards', 'Approved School-Based Recognition and Incentive System with clear criteria, categories, and guidelines', 'Conduct consultative meetings with school personnel; review existing DepEd policies on rewards and recognition; define criteria, categories, and guidelines; finalize and disseminate the SRIS framework', 'June 2026', 'School Head, HR Coordinator, Teachers, SGC', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1429, 'The school provides access to learning experiences for the disadvantaged, OSY and adult learners. ', 'To intensify OSYs in the school to focus on in formal education', 'Conducted school mapping for OSY learners', 'Conduct school mapping for OSY learners', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Head Teachers and Master Teacher', '8000', 'Conducted school mapping for OSY learners', 2026, 304311, 61, 12, 7),
(1430, 'Conduct 1- half day SGC Orientation during first PTA - Board Meeting or PTA Assembly ', 'To ensure parents understands SGC and their role', 'At least 80% of parents oriented', 'Short Talk (30 minutes) then open forum', 'June 2026', 'School Head, PTA - Officers and Homeroom offi', '', 'No allocated budget for this activity', 2026, 128734, 106, 12, 133);
INSERT INTO `sgod_action_plan` (`id`, `activity`, `objective`, `ex_output`, `metho_strategy`, `time_frame`, `person_involved`, `bud_req`, `remarks`, `fy`, `school_id`, `division`, `region`, `district`) VALUES
(1431, 'H2. Identification and Documentation of Personnel Achievements and Milestones', 'Systematically identify, validate, and document personnel achievements, contributions, and milestones in teaching, leadership, innovation, and service for recognition and reward purposes', 'Updated database and documented records of personnel achievements and milestones', 'Collect accomplishment reports, IPCRF results, and supporting documents; validate achievements through committees; maintain a database of personnel accomplishments throughout the year', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Committee Membe', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1432, 'Conduct regular meetings with teachers, parents, and stakeholders for shared decision-making', 'To enhance participatory and transparent school leadership', 'Improved collaboration and stronger leadership within the school', 'Use participatory approach by allowing open forums, suggestions, and feedback during meetings\r\nApply focus group discussions (FGD) to gather specific insights from different stakeholder groups\r\nUtilize structured meeting agendas and minutes to ensure organized and transparent discussions\r\nIncorporate survey or feedback forms after meetings to evaluate effectiveness', 'Quarterly ', 'School Head, teachers, parents, stakeholders', '500', '', 2026, 129130, 59, 12, 151),
(1433, 'The school has special education- and PWD-friendly facilities.\r\n', 'To install ramps, handrails, and accessible toilets in school buildings within the school year.\r\n', 'Ramps, handrails, accessible restrooms, and widened pathways installed in all major school facilities', '1. Identify learners with disabilities and assess their specific needs.\r\n2. Evaluate existing facilities and resources to determine accessibility gaps.\r\n3. Prioritize construction of ramps, handrails, accessible toilets, and pathways. ', 'July to September 2026', 'School Head, SNED Focal Person/Guidance Advoc', '85000.00', 'The implementation of SPED and PWD-friendly facilities is aligned with national policies such as Republic Act 7277, promoting equal access to quality education.', 2026, 306403, 59, 12, 144),
(1434, 'H3. Implementation of Quarterly Recognition Activities', 'Regularly recognize and reward personnel for outstanding performance and contributions, thereby fostering motivation, professional growth, and a culture of excellence within the schoo', 'Recognized and motivated personnel with increased engagement and job satisfaction', 'Conduct quarterly recognition ceremonies; provide certificates, commendations, and tokens; highlight achievements during meetings and assemblies; use bulletin boards and social media for recognition', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA, SGC', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
(1435, 'Out-of-School Youth and Adult Learners (OSYAL) Program Implementation', 'Improve literacy, numeracy, and life skills in OSY and adult learners.', 'Improved literacy and numeracy skills.', 'Coordination with barangay officials and stakeholders.', 'School Year 2025–2026', '• School Head , Barangay Officials and stakeh', '5000.00', 'Strong partnership with community stakeholders is vital for sustainability', 2026, 128958, 59, 12, 145),
(1436, 'H4. Conduct of Annual Awards and Incentives Program', 'Formally acknowledge exemplary personnel who have demonstrated outstanding performance, innovation, and dedication throughout the school year in alignment with school and DepEd priorities', 'Successful conduct of annual awards program with recognized outstanding personnel and documented best practices', 'Organize year-end awarding ceremony; select awardees based on established criteria; provide plaques, certificates, and incentives; invite stakeholders to witness recognition program', 'March – April 2027', 'School Head, Awards Committee, Teachers, Stak', '', '', 2026, 304224, 58, 12, 36),
