(1622, 'Building a School Library to Enhance Learners’ Learning Experience', 'To establish a functional and accessible school library that supports teaching and learning.\r\nTo improve students’ reading comprehension, research skills, and independent learning habits.\r\nTo provide teachers and learners with adequate reference mate', 'A designated and organized library area within the school.\r\nBasic library furniture (shelves, tables, chairs) installed.\r\nAdequate collection of textbooks, reference books, and reading materials.\r\nA library management system and inventory of books.\r\nIncreased student utilization of library resources.', 'Conduct a needs assessment to determine space, materials, and resource requirements.\r\nCoordinate with stakeholders (school governing council, PTA, LGU, NGOs) for funding and donations.\r\nIdentify and prepare a suitable room or space for the library.\r\nProcure and organize library materials and furniture.\r\nAssign a teacher‑in‑charge or librarian to manage daily library operations.\r\nOrient teachers and students on proper library use and policies.', 'Short‑term: 1st–2nd Quarter (planning, sourci', 'School Head SBM Coordinator Teachers PTA Offi', '400000.00', 'Implementation subject to availability of funds and stakeholder support.\r\nContinuous monitoring and evaluation to ensure sustainability.\r\nLibrary to be gradually improved based on pupils’ needs.', 2026, 128824, 59, 12, 138),
(1623, 'Building a Computer Laboratory for Quality Education', 'To enhance the quality of teaching and learning through the integration of information and communication technology (ICT).\r\nTo provide learners with equitable access to digital resources that support 21st-century skills.\r\nTo strengthen teachers’ inst', 'To enhance the quality of teaching and learning through the integration of information and communication technology (ICT).\r\nTo provide learners with equitable access to digital resources that support 21st-century skills.\r\nTo strengthen teachers’ instructional competencies through technology-assisted instruction.\r\nTo support School-Based Management (SBM) initiatives by improving learning facilities and resources.', 'Conduct a needs assessment to determine equipment, space, and budget requirements.\r\nCoordinate with school stakeholders, LGU, and partners for funding and technical support.\r\nProcure computers, furniture, and necessary peripherals following proper procurement procedures.\r\nInstall and configure hardware, software, and internet connectivity.\r\nConduct orientation and training sessions for teachers and students on proper use and maintenance of the computer laboratory.\r\nMonitor and evaluate the utilization and impact of the computer laboratory on learning outcomes.', 'Planning and Coordination: 1–2 months Procure', 'School Head / Principal ICT Coordinator Teach', '500000.00', 'Sustainability plan includes proper maintenance, regular monitoring, and possible expansion of ICT resources.\r\nSupports SBM principles of shared governance, stakeholder participation, and continuous improvement in learning delivery.', 2026, 128824, 59, 12, 138),
