(1628, '*Conduct community mapping to identify potential ALS learners.\r\n*Tap ALS teacher to organize orientation and enrollment\r\n*Delivery of learning session(modular & blended learning)\r\n*Holds monthly progress monitoring  and portfolio reviews\r\n*prepare le', 'Provide accessible, flexible and quality education to out-of-school youth and adults.', 'Accessible, Flexible and quality education to out- of- youth will be provided.', 'Use Individual Learning Agreement(ILA); Employ flexible schedules; Integrate real-life applications; Partner  with LGUs and NGOs; Provide recognition and motivation program', 'Year Round', 'ALS Focal Person, ALS teacher, School head, l', '20000', 'Strengthen monitoring through learner portfolios and SBM reports.', 2026, 129031, 59, 12, 147),
(1629, 'Enhancing 21st-Century learning strategies to improved NAT Performance', 'To develop learners’ critical thinking, communication, collaboration, and creativity skills to improve performance in the National Achievement Test (NAT).', 'Increased NAT performance and mastery level\r\nImproved learner proficiency in 21st-century skills\r\nEnhanced student engagement and participation', 'Integration of 21st-Century Skills\r\nDiagnostic and Data Analysis\r\nContinuous Assessment and Feedback\r\nCapacity Building and Stakeholder Support', 'June 2026 -March 2027', 'All teachers, School Heads, ', 'Printing of test questions- 5000.00', '', 2026, 128648, 58, 12, 36),
(1630, 'Review and validate teacher-made materials', 'Enhance quality of instructional materials', 'Improved quality and relevance of materials', 'Teachers prepare contextualized learning materials through learner needs assessment, collaborative planning in LAC sessions, and integration of local context and real-life situations in lessons. They ensure quality through regular review and validation by school leaders and master teachers. ICT tools are also utilized to enhance and innovate learning materials, while continuous feedback from learners is used to further improve instructional resources.', 'monthly', 'Master Teachers, Department Heads and Teacher', '10,000', 'Continuous improvement the quality of learning materials that respond to the needs of learners.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
(1631, 'Conduct of Learning Action Cell (LAC) Sessions', 'To enhance teachers\' competencies based on identified learning needs. To improve learner achievement through collaborative professional development.', 'Improved teaching strategies applied in classrooms, LAC sessions reports and action points.', 'Needs assessment through class observation and assessment result. Coaching and mentoring by Master Teachers/School Heads.', 'August 2026- February 2027', 'Gretchen Joy J. Flores, Melona M. Pongase, Ar', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128657, 58, 12, 36),
(1632, 'Early Language, Literacy, and Numeracy (ELLN) Enhancement Program', 'To improve Grade 3 learners’ proficiency in reading, writing, and numeracy through targeted, engaging, and skills-based interventions.', 'Learners’ reading portfolios (reading logs, comprehension worksheets, and assessment results)\r\nProgress monitoring charts per learner\r\nParent participation records and signed home activity guides', 'Conduct diagnostic tests to identify learners’ strengths and least mastered skills in reading, writing, and numeracy.\r\nProvide tailored activities such as remediation for struggling learners and enrichment for advanced learners.\r\nEngage parents through take-home activities and regular communication.\r\nImplement pull-out sessions or after-class interventions for learners needing additional support.', 'June 2026 -March 2027', 'All teachers, School Heads, ', '5000.00', '', 2026, 128648, 58, 12, 36),
(1633, 'Conduct Monitoring and Evaluation of School Programs', 'Ensure effective implementation of school programs. Support data-driven decision making.', 'M&E reports and Program improvement plan', 'Regular monitoring, Data analysis and Feedback sessions', 'August 2026, December 2026 and March 2027', 'Gretchen Joy J. Flores, Melona M. Pongase, Ar', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128657, 58, 12, 36),
(1634, 'Remediation and Intervention Programs', 'Address learning gaps in reading, Math, Science and other core subjects. Improve NAT and Classroom assessment performance.', 'Improved learners performance, NAT results and Academic achievements per learner', 'Diagnostic testing, constant review, Small-group tutoring and differentiated instructions', 'July 2026- March 2027', 'Gretchen Joy J. Flores, Melona M. Pongase, Ar', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128657, 58, 12, 36),
(1635, 'Conduct regular remediation sessions (reading, science, and mathematics)', 'Sustain effective remediation programs for learners with learning gaps', 'Continuous improvement in learner performance', 'Teachers implement diagnostic assessment-based remediation, focusing on identified learning gaps. They use differentiated instruction, small-group tutoring, and targeted intervention activities in reading, Science, and Mathematics. Continuous progress monitoring, feedback, and reinforcement activities are conducted to ensure mastery of competencies.', 'Whole Year', 'Reading coordinator English and Filipino, Tea', '5,000', 'Sustained practice to ensure continuous improvement and mastery of essential learning competencies across key subject areas.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38);
