(1669, 'The school has a functional support mechanism for mental wellness.', 'To integrate mental wellness concepts into contextualized learning materials that promote emotional resilience and a supportive school environment through culturally responsive activities.', '1.Localized Wellness Modules: Activity sheets that use local metaphors and language to discuss stress management and self-care.\r\n\r\n2.\"Hingahan\" (Breathing Space) Corners: Physical or digital spaces in the classroom supported by materials that encourage student reflection.\r\n\r\n3. Mental Health Resource Directory: A list of local community health workers and school counselors integrated into the students\' notebooks or handbooks.', 'Methodology Strategy: The \"CARE\" Framework\r\nThis strategy connects your mental wellness mechanism directly to classroom instruction:\r\nCheck-in-Start lessons with a \"Kumustahan\" (Check-in) using a \"Mood Meter\" contextualized with local emojis or cultural expressions of feelings.\r\nAffirm-Use learning materials that feature local stories of resilience, showing how community heroes overcame adversity.\r\nRefer-Explicitly include instructions in the learning materials on how to access the school’s wellness support mechanism if a student feels overwhelmed.\r\nEmpower-Create activities where students design their own \"Mental Wellness Toolkit\" using indigenous materials (e.g., stress balls made of local seeds or weaving).', 'Year round', 'Teachers, School Head, MT, pupils, parents', '', '', 2026, 128933, 59, 12, 144),
(1671, 'The school has special education - and PWD-friendly facilities.', 'To develop inclusive and accessible contextualized materials that utilize the school’s PWD-friendly facilities to ensure learners with disabilities have equal access to culturally relevant and grade-level appropriate instruction.', 'Modified Learning Materials (MLMs): Braille-transcribed, large-print, or simplified-text versions of localized stories and activities.\r\n\r\nInstructional Map of Facilities: A visual or tactile guide showing how students can use ramps, tactile paths, and accessible labs for specific learning tasks.\r\n\r\nInclusive Assessment Tools: Tests that allow for alternative response modes (e.g., oral exams, sign language, or digital interfaces).', '1. Identify which localized activities might be difficult for PWDs (e.g., a \"community walk\" might need a specific wheelchair-friendly route).\r\n2. Use the school\'s specialized facilities as the \"learning lab.\"\r\n3. Provide the same contextualized content in multiple formats: Visual (images), Auditory (recordings), and Kinesthetic (tactile materials).', 'Year round', 'Teachers, School Head, MT', '', '', 2026, 128933, 59, 12, 144),
(1672, 'The school has a functional school-community planning team.', 'To conduct regular conferences/meetings  to functionalize the SCPT.', 'Conducted regular meetings\r\nSubmitted accomplishment reports', 'Send communication to the members.\r\nMake an strategic plan .\r\nAllocate funds.\r\nConduct activities and programs\r\nSubmit accomplishment reports', 'Year round', 'Teachers, School Head, MT', '', '', 2026, 128933, 59, 12, 144),
