(1765, '  Activities\r\n*Orientation and capacity-building workshops for teachers, parents, and community leaders.  \r\n*Establishment of SBM committees (finance, curriculum, monitoring).  \r\n* Development of School Improvement Plan (SIP).  \r\n*Regular monitoring ', 'Objectives\r\n\r\n*Strengthen participatory decision-making in schools.  \r\n\r\n* Improve accountability and transparency in resource management.  \r\n\r\n*Enhance teaching-learning processes through localized initiatives.  \r\n\r\n* Foster collaboration among stak', 'Expected Outputs\r\n*Functional SBM committees with clear roles.  \r\n*Approved and operational School Improvement Plan.  \r\n* Increased stakeholder participation in school governance.  \r\n*Transparent financial and resource management system.  \r\n* Improved student performance indicators (attendance, achievement scores).  \r\n', 'Methodology / Strategy\r\n* Participatory Approach: Engage all stakeholders in planning and decision-making.  \r\n* Capacity Building: Provide training on leadership, financial management, and monitoring.  \r\n* Transparency Mechanisms: Public posting of budgets, reports, and decisions.  \r\n* Continuous Monitoring: Use performance indicators and feedback loops.  \r\n*Community Partnership: Collaborate with LGUs, NGOs, and private sector for support', 'Time Frame | Activity | Time Frame | |-------', 'Persons Involved * School Head / Principal (o', '5000', 'Remarks\r\n* Budget may be sourced from MOOE, LGU support, and community contributions.  \r\n*Flexibility in timeline depending on school readiness.  \r\n*Sustainability depends on continuous stakeholder engagement.  \r\n* Regular feedback mechanisms should be institutionalized.  ', 2026, 128897, 59, 12, 142),
(1766, 'Create/Organize SBM Task Force', 'Designate specific teams for each SBM Dimension', 'School/Office Order & Designation of Task Force Members', 'Meeting and formal appointment of committee chairmanship and membership', 'June 2026', 'School Head, SBM Chair, SBM Task Force', '1500.00', '', 2026, 128751, 58, 12, 41),
(1767, 'Activities\r\n- Conduct baseline assessment of current school management practices.  \r\n- Organize stakeholder consultation meetings (teachers, parents, barangay officials).  \r\n- Draft and approve a School Governance Framework.  \r\n- Launch transparency ', 'Objectives\r\n- Institutionalize shared governance in school operations.  \r\n- Ensure efficient use of resources aligned with student learning needs.  \r\n- Promote inclusivity and equity in decision-making.  \r\n- Strengthen monitoring and evaluation for c', 'Expected Outputs\r\n- Clear baseline data on school management gaps.  \r\n- School Governance Framework adopted by stakeholders.  \r\n- Transparent reporting system established.  \r\n- Enhanced capacity of school committees.  \r\n- Improved stakeholder trust and participation.  \r\n', 'Methodology / Strategy\r\n- Evidence-Based Planning: Use baseline data to guide priorities.  \r\n- Inclusive Participation: Ensure representation of marginalized groups.  \r\n- Transparency Tools: Public disclosure of financial reports and decisions.  \r\n- Capacity Development: Training sessions, peer learning, mentoring.  \r\n- Adaptive Management: Adjust strategies based on quarterly reviews.  ', 'Time Frame | Activity | Time Frame | |-------', 'Persons Involved - Principal (lead coordinato', '3000', 'Remarks\r\n- Budget allocation should prioritize training and transparency tools.  \r\n- Strong LGU support is critical for sustainability.  \r\n- Flexibility in implementation is encouraged to adapt to local needs.  \r\n- Documentation of best practices will help replication in other schools.  ', 2026, 128912, 59, 12, 142),
