(1815, 'The school has special education and PWD-friendly facilities', 'To establish functional special education (SPED) resources and PWD-friendly infrastructure (e.g., ramps, accessible restrooms, learning materials) to ensure equitable access to education for learners with special needs.', 'Improved inclusive, accessible, and PWD-friendly school facilities that support the learning needs of all students, including those with disabilities', 'The school will conduct a needs assessment to identify gaps in existing facilities and services for learners with disabilities, followed by collaborative planning with stakeholders such as teachers, parents, local government units, and community partners. The school will allocate resources and seek external support or funding for the construction and improvement of PWD-friendly infrastructure (e.g., ramps, handrails, accessible restrooms) and the acquisition of SPED instructional materials. Capacity-building activities, including training for teachers and staff on inclusive education and disability awareness, will also be implemented. Regular monitoring and evaluation will be carried out to ensure that facilities and services remain functional, inclusive, and responsive to the needs of all learners, with continuous feedback used to guide further improvements.', 'School Year 2026 - 2027', 'School Head, Teachers ', '', 'Leaners with special needs (based on assessment conducted) are mainstreamed', 2026, 128941, 59, 12, 144),
(1816, 'Monitoring and Evaluation Program', 'To strengthen the systematic monitoring, evaluation, and alignment of school programs and activities with the School Improvement Plan through regular data analysis and performance tracking', 'Updated reports', 'Quarterly M&E', 'School Year 2026–2027', 'School Head, Planning Team', '3000', 'Continuous improvement', 2026, 128902, 59, 12, 142),
