(1837, 'The school collaborates with stakeholders and other schools in strengthening partnership', 'To establish sustainable linkages and active collaboration mechanisms with internal and external stakeholders, including other schools, to enhance resource sharing, capacity-building initiatives, and community engagement for continuous school improve', 'Established and sustained partnerships with stakeholders and nearby schools, evidenced by signed agreements or memoranda of understanding (MOUs), regular coordination meetings, and documented collaborative activities such as joint programs, trainings, and resource-sharing initiatives, leading to improved school programs, strengthened community engagement, and enhanced learner outcomes.', 'The school will identify and map potential stakeholders and partner schools, then initiate communication through meetings, consultations, and networking activities to establish mutual goals and areas of collaboration. Formal agreements such as memoranda of understanding (MOUs) will be developed to define roles and responsibilities. The school will organize and participate in joint activities, including trainings, projects, and resource-sharing initiatives, while maintaining regular coordination through scheduled meetings and communication channels. Documentation of all partnership activities will be ensured, and continuous monitoring and evaluation will be conducted to assess effectiveness, strengthen relationships, and sustain collaborative efforts for ongoing school improvement.', 'School Year 2026 - 2027', 'School Head, Stakeholders (Internal and Exter', '', '', 2026, 128941, 59, 12, 144),
(1838, 'Stakeholder Feedback Forum', 'To transparently share successes and areas for improvement.', 'SBM corner updates; Feedback summary.', 'General Assembly; Suggestion boxes', 'Every 6 months', 'Entire School Community', '500.00', '', 2026, 304299, 61, 12, 2),
(1839, 'Functional Child Protection Committee (CPC)', 'To ensure a fully functional, responsive, and sustainable Child Protection Committee (CPC) that effectively safeguards learners’ welfare and implements child protection policies.', 'Trained teachers on the proper handling of child abuse cases', '*Implement standard procedures for handling child protection cases.\r\n*Reconstitute and activate the school Child Protection Committee  with clear roles and functions.', 'Year round', '*School Head, Class Advisers, Child Protectio', '30000.00', 'The Child Protection Committee (CPC) shall be fully activated and institutionalized in accordance with DepEd Child Protection Policy (D.O. 40, s. 2012).', 2026, 304217, 58, 12, 35),
