(1855, 'Monitoring and Evaluation of SBM Practices', 'To assess progress and effectiveness of SBM implementation', 'Monitoring reports and evaluation results', 'Regular meeting, use of SBM assessment tools', 'June, Aug, Dec 2026 and March 2027', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator', '6000', '', 2026, 128673, 58, 12, 0),
(1856, 'Implement “Tulong Mo Para sa Pag-aaral Ko”', 'Support learners’ educational needs.\r\n', 'Increased learner support and resources.\r\n', 'Stakeholder engagement, donation drives, partnership building.', 'April 2026 - June 2026', 'John Holden I. Medina ', '220', '', 2026, 128628, 58, 12, 43),
(1857, 'Home Visitation and Family Engagement Program\r\nAcademic Bridging and Alternative Learning Support\r\nCommunity Partnership and Reintegration Drive\r\nQuarterly Monitoring, Review, and Adjustment of Interventions', '1. Reach out to frequently absent or struggling learners at their homes to understand barriers and build trust.\r\n2. Help learners who are behind academically catch up to reduce frustration and shame that lead to dropout.\r\n3. Bring back learners who h', '- Home visitation schedule (at least 2 visits per at-risk learner)\r\n- Family needs assessment form\r\n- Log of parent commitments and support provided\r\n- Remedial classes schedule (for over-aged or low-performing learners)\r\n- Individualized Learning Activity Sheets (LAS)\r\n- Peer tutoring partnership record\r\n- Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) with barangay for dropout tracking\r\n- List of re-enrolled dropouts (target: at least 50% of previous year’s dropouts)\r\n- Community mapping of out-of-school youth (OSY)\r\n- Quarterly dropout rate report (compared to previous year)\r\n- Minutes of DRPC review meetings\r\n- Revised intervention matrix based on what worked', '- Train teachers on respectful, non-judgmental home visit protocols\r\n- Visit during agreed hours (afternoons or weekends)\r\n- Listen to family concerns (lack of school supplies, distance, child labor, illness)\r\n- Co-create a simple support plan with the family\r\n Identify learners with 2+ failing grades or 2+ years behind age-appropriate level\r\n- Offer after-class or remedial sessions focusing on basic literacy and numeracy\r\n- Train advanced learners as peer tutors (with simple incentives)\r\n- Use modular or blended learning for flexible pacing\r\n- Conduct a “Dropout Re-enrollment Campaign” using house-to-house visits, social media, and barangay announcements\r\n- Partner with barangay to identify OSY and offer flexible enrollment (modular, night classes if feasible)\r\n- Establish a “Second Chance” orientation for returning learners and their parents\r\n', 'Whole year round', 'School Head, Teachers, BLGU', '5000', 'Never visit alone; always go in pairs. Document but maintain confidentiality.\r\nShare progress with the whole school community during flag ceremony or PTA assembly to build collective responsibility.', 2026, 128950, 59, 12, 145),
(1858, 'Recognition and Feedback Mechanism', 'To sustain motivation and continuous improvement', 'Feedback reports and recognition activities', 'Surveys, suggestion box, awarding ceremonies', 'March 2027', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator', '10000', '', 2026, 128673, 58, 12, 0),
