(1868, 'Leadership & Governance-Conduct orientation on SBM principles and practices.', 'To familiarize school personnel, parents, and stakeholders with the core concepts, principles, and practices of School-Based Management (SBM).', 'Increased awareness and commitment', 'Interactive Orientation Sessions: Use presentations, workshops, and open forums to explain SBM principles.', 'Quarter 1', 'School Head, Teachers, SGC, PTA', '1500', 'Participants were able to attend and actively engage in discussions on SBM principles and practices.', 2026, 129097, 59, 12, 150),
(1869, 'The school has a functional Supreme  Secondary Learner Government', 'To organize and have a functional SSLG throughout the school year', 'Organized a functional SSLG throughout the school year.', 'Attended series of trainings, seminars and conduct activities aligned to the DepEd mandates', 'Monthly', 'School Head, teachers, SSLG Adviser and Learn', '10000', 'Functional and organized SSLG that support all schools programs and activities.', 2026, 304311, 61, 12, 7),
(1871, 'The school has functional computer/laboratory classroom', 'To temporarily restore and ensure the operational functionality of the school’s computer/laboratory classroom by implementing interim repair, refurbishment, and utilization of available ICT resources while awaiting DepEd funding allocation for full r', 'A temporarily functional and safe computer/laboratory classroom with repaired or reconfigured available units, properly documented inventory of damaged and usable equipment, implemented interim rehabilitation measures, and continued utilization of ICT resources for instruction while awaiting DepEd funding allocation for full restoration and upgrading of facilities.', 'The school will conduct a rapid assessment and inventory of all computer/laboratory equipment and facilities to determine the extent of earthquake damage and identify units that are still usable. Based on the assessment, immediate minor repairs, reconfiguration, and safe utilization of functional equipment will be carried out to allow continued instructional use. The school will implement temporary safety measures such as proper layout adjustments, electrical safety checks, and basic workstation rehabilitation to ensure a safe learning environment. Teachers will be oriented on the proper use of available ICT resources under limited conditions, while coordination with DepEd and other partners will be maintained for possible support. All actions and conditions will be properly documented to guide future rehabilitation once funding becomes available.', 'School Year 2026 - 2027', 'School Head, Teachers ', '', 'Laptops and other ICT related facilities (TV)  are issued to teachers which are utilized during the teaching-learning process', 2026, 128941, 59, 12, 144),
(1872, 'Advocacy and Resource Mobilization for Additional Computers', 'Acquire more computers through donations, partnerships, or low-cost alternatives.', '- List of potential donors (alumni, local businesses, NGOs, LGU)\r\n- Donation request letters and MOA drafts\r\n- At least 5 additional functional computers acquired within 6 months', ' Form a resource mobilization sub-team\r\n- Write a one-page proposal highlighting learner needs and DepEd computer-to-student ratio gap\r\n- Meet with Barangay Council, alumni association, and local businesses\r\n- Explore government programs (e.g., DICT’s PC for Public Schools)', 'Whole year round', 'School Head, PTA President, Barangay Captain,', '1000', 'Offer donor recognition (e.g., engraved plaque, naming of computer lab corner).', 2026, 128950, 59, 12, 145),
(1873, 'SBM Level of Practice Assessment', 'To determine the school\'s current SBM level of practice (Developing, Maturing or', 'Self-Assessment Results; SBM Level Certification', 'Self-Survey Tool (SST) and external validation', 'March 2027', 'School Head, SBM Team, SDO DavNor Validation ', '1000', 'To be accomplished.', 2026, 128751, 58, 12, 41),
