(2022, 'School Governing Council (SGC) Formation and Training', 'To establish a robust governance structure with clear roles, responsibilities, and decision-making processes.', '1. Functional School Governing Council (SGC) with diverse representation.\r\n2. Defined leadership roles and succession plans.\r\n3. Regular SGC meetings with documented minutes and action points.', '1. Elections/appointments for SGC members.\r\n2. Leadership training and capacity building for SGC members and school heads.\r\n3. Development of SGC operational guidelines.', 'July 2026', 'School Head , Master Teacher /SBM Focal Perso', '3000.00', 'A well-trained and representative SGC is the backbone of SBM. Focus on building trust and ensuring members understand their fiduciary and governance responsibilities. Clear communication channels between the SGC and the wider school community are crucial.', 2026, 128681, 58, 12, 38),
(2023, 'Conduct awareness campaign on anti-bullying\r\nStrengthen Child Protection Committee (CPC)\r\nIntegrate values education in lessons\r\nEstablish reporting and monitoring system\r\nConduct guidance and counseling sessions\r\nParent education and engagement\r\nPee', 'Strengthen awareness of learners on anti-bullying policies and respectful behavior\r\nEnsure effective implementation of child protection policies\r\nPromote positive behavior and respect among learners\r\nEnsure immediate reporting and resolution of bully', 'Increased awareness and understanding of anti-bullying laws and school policies\r\nFunctional CPC with active monitoring system\r\nImproved learner behavior and values formation\r\nEfficient reporting mechanism and zero unresolved cases\r\nImproved learner behavior and emotional well-being\r\nIncreased parental awareness and cooperation\r\nReduced negative behavior and improved peer relationships\r\nSafe school environment reports\r\n', 'Orientation, assemblies, IEC materials dissemination\r\nRegular meetings, case monitoring, reporting system\r\nDaily integration of DepEd core values, class discussions\r\nSuggestion boxes, confidential reporting channels, monitoring logs\r\nCounseling, peer support groups, individual interventions\r\nParent orientations, meetings, IEC dissemination\r\nPeer mentoring, SSG/SPG activities\r\nSurveys, observation, feedback mechanisms\r\n', 'Start of school year and quarterly Whole scho', 'Teachers, Guidance Coordinator, School Head, ', 'Printing of IEC materials Minimal operational costs Instructional materials Logbooks, communication materials Counseling materials Printing of materials Activity materials Printing and documentation', '', 2026, 129095, 59, 12, 150),
(2024, 'Project SMART-LAC (Strategic Management and Relevant Training through Learning Action Cells)', '1. To conduct monthly needs-based LAC sessions aligned with the results of the Electronic Self-Assessment Tool (e-SAT).\r\n2. To ensure 100% of teachers apply learned competencies in their classroom observations (COT)', '1. Approved LAC Plan and Completion Reports for 10 sessions.\r\n2. Documented increase in teacher proficiency levels in targeted KRAs (Key Result Areas).\r\n3. Portfolio of localized instructional materials developed during LAC sessions.', '1. Data-Driven Planning: Analyze e-SAT results to identify the top 3 priority competencies for the year.\r\n2. Expert Mentoring: Utilize \"Internal Experts\" (Master Teachers) and invite \"External Resource Persons\" for specialized topics.\r\n3. Differentiated LAC: Group teachers by grade level or department to ensure the training is subject-matter relevant.', 'School Year 2026-2027 (Monthly, July to May)', 'School Head, LAC Coordinator, and All Teachin', '12000', 'Success will be monitored through the Individual Performance Commitment and Review Form (IPCRF) and classroom observation notes.', 2026, 204527, 58, 12, 39),
(2025, 'Conduct orientation on Child Protection Policy (CPP)\r\nStrengthen Child Protection Committee (CPC)\r\nEstablish confidential reporting mechanisms\r\nConduct regular guidance and counseling services\r\nHome visitation and parent engagement activities\r\nIntegr', 'Increase awareness of child protection laws and policies\r\nEnsure effective monitoring and implementation of child protection measures\r\nEnsure immediate reporting of abuse cases or concerns\r\nProvide psychosocial support to learners\r\nStrengthen parenta', 'Learners, teachers, and parents oriented on CPP\r\nFunctional CPC with active case monitoring system\r\nFunctional reporting system (hotline/logbook/box)\r\nImproved learner well-being and early intervention cases\r\nIncreased parental involvement in child protection\r\nImproved learner behavior and values formation\r\nRegular monitoring reports and safe school environment\r\n', 'Orientation sessions, IEC dissemination\r\nRegular meetings, case tracking, reporting system\r\nSuggestion boxes, confidential reporting channels\r\nCounseling sessions, referral system\r\nHome visits, parent orientations, PTA meetings\r\nDaily integration of core values in lessons\r\nClassroom observation, surveys, reporting system review\r\n', 'Start of school year and quarterly Whole scho', 'Teachers, Guidance Counselor, School Head, Pa', 'Printing of IEC materials Minimal operational costs Printing of forms and logbooks Counseling materials Transportation and communication allowance Instructional materials Documentation materials', '', 2026, 129095, 59, 12, 150),
