(2028, 'Project BUILD (Better Infrastructure and Facilities for Unified Learning and Development)', '1. To institutionalize a systematic School Facilities Improvement Plan (SFIP).\r\n2. To secure external funding/support for at least two major facility enhancements (e.g., PWD ramps, library, or computer lab, water supplies and stable electric supplies', '1. Updated School Physical Facilities Inventory and prioritize Needs List.\r\n2. Completed minor repair projects and at least one major facility improvement.', '1. Facility Audit: Conduct a comprehensive walkthrough with the School Inspection Team to categorize needs into \"Immediate Repair,\" \"Minor Improvement,\" and \"Major Capital Investment.\"\r\n2. Stakeholder Pitching: Develop a \"Project Proposal Portfolio\" with 3D visualizations or clear floor plans to present to the PTA, Alumni, and LGU.', 'School Year 2026-2027 (Quarter 1: Planning; Q', 'School Head, Physical Facilities Coordinator,', '50000', 'Heavy emphasis on the \"Adopt-a-School\" program is necessary as MOOE funds are typically insufficient for major infrastructure improvements.', 2026, 204527, 58, 12, 39),
