(2096, '*Create and establish a mini library', '*To create a conducive space for learning and study\r\n*To provide access to educational and recreational reading materials\r\n*To improve literacy and comprehension skills, especially among young learners', 'A functional and accessible mini library space established\r\nOrganized shelves, reading area, and seating available\r\nAt least ___ number of books collected, sorted, and displayed Conducted reading activities (e.g., storytelling, reading sessions)\r\nImproved basic literacy and comprehension skills of users', 'Plan the layout and design of the mini library\r\nOrganize a book donation drive\r\nGather materials (shelves, tables, chairs, labels)\r\nSeek support from local partners or donors, Organize reading programs:\r\nStorytelling sessions\r\n*Reading circles\r\n*Reading challenges', 'May 25, 2026- July 2026', 'School Head, English Department and Reading C', '3000.00', '', 2026, 316004, 59, 12, 0),
(2097, 'Conduct regular meetings with teachers, parents, and stakeholders for shared decision-making', 'To enhance participatory and transparent school leadership.', 'Improved collaboration and stronger leadership within the school', 'Use participatory approach by allowing open forums, suggestions, and feedback during meetings. Apply focus group discussions (FGD) to gather specific insights from different stakeholder groups . Utilize structured meeting agendas and minutes to ensure organized and transparent discussions . Incorporate survey or feedback forms after meetings to evaluate effectiveness.', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, teachers, parents, stakeholders', '500', '', 2026, 613019, 59, 12, 151),
(2098, 'Curriculum Relevance and Delivery Enhancement', 'To ensure the curriculum is responsive to local needs and effectively delivered to meet student learning outcomes.', '1. Curriculum adapted to local context and needs.\r\n2. Improved teaching methodologies and learning resources.\r\n3. Positive trends in student academic performance.', '1. Curriculum review and adaptation workshops.\r\n2. Professional development for teachers on innovative pedagogy.\r\n3. Integration of technology in teaching and learning.', 'Whole ye3ar Round', 'School Head , Master Teacher /SBM Focal Perso', '1000.00', 'his activity is central to ensuring that education provided by the school is not just academic but also deeply practical and meaningful to the students\' lives and their future. By localizing the curriculum and improving teaching methods, the school directly addresses the core SBM principle of responsiveness to community needs and enhances student engagement and outcomes. It requires a collaborative effort between educators, curriculum developers, and community members to ensure relevance and effectiveness.', 2026, 128681, 58, 12, 38),
