(2132, 'Project READ (Reading Enhancement and Academic Development)', 'To identify the space, current book inventory, and furniture needs.\r\nTo secure funding and book donations from stakeholders.\r\nTo create a functional, comfortable, and well-lit reading environment.\r\nTo organize books by category (Dewey Decimal System)', 'Situational analysis report and floor plan design.\r\nIncreased book collection and budget for library fixtures.\r\nRenovated library room with shelves, tables, and chairs.\r\nSystematic catalog and labeled book sections.\r\n2-3 computer stations with educational software/e-books.\r\nFormal opening; 100% of students issued library cards.\r\nWeekly \"Storytelling Hour\" and \"Top Reader\" awards.\r\nMonthly utilization reports and inventory updates.', 'Survey of existing materials; consultation with teachers on curriculum needs.\r\n\"Adopt-a-Shelf\" program; letters to NGOs, Alumni, and LGU.\r\nPainting, carpentry work, and installation of proper lighting/ventilation.\r\nSorting, accessioning, and labeling of books (Fiction, Science, History, etc.).\r\nSetup of digital workstations and installation of offline encyclopedias.\r\nLaunching ceremony (Ribbon Cutting); Library Hour orientation per grade level.\r\nImplementing scheduled reading sessions and literacy contests.\r\nMaintenance of logbooks and quarterly satisfaction surveys.\r\n', 'Second Term 2026-2027', 'All Students, Teachers, School Head, School Q', '50000', 'Draft Joint Resolution by the School Faculty Club/Association, SPTA and Barangay Council', 2026, 128947, 59, 12, 145),
