(2164, 'Project BASA: Build, Assess, Strengthen, and Achieve', 'To improve the reading proficiency of Junior High School learners through a structured, cost-efficient, and sustainable reading intervention program.', 'Functional school reading program (Project BASA) \r\nImproved reading proficiency levels \r\n', 'The implementation of Project BASA follows a systematic, data-driven, and learner-centered approach anchored on School-Based Management (SBM) principles. It ensures that interventions are responsive to learners’ reading needs through continuous assessment, targeted support, and stakeholder collaboration.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'School Reading Focal', '20000', 'In essence, Project BASA serves as a strategic intervention program that contributes directly to the objectives of the National Aral Program by ensuring that every learner is given the opportunity to read, understand, and succeed', 2026, 304289, 59, 12, 147),
(2165, 'SCHOOL BASED MANAGEMENT IMPLEMENATION', 'To strengthen school governance, improve learning outcomes, and promote stakeholder \'s participation through effective SBM implementation.', '\r\n•	Functional School Governing Council (SGC) \r\n•	Approved SIP and AIP \r\n•	Improved learner performance \r\n•	Increased stakeholder participation \r\n•	Achieved SBM Level (Developing/Maturing/Advanced) \r\n', 'Organize/strengthen School Governing Council (SGC)\r\nConduct SBM orientation for stakeholders\r\nDevelop/review School Improvement Plan (SIP)\r\nConduct Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions\r\nMonitor learner performance\r\nImplement intervention programs\r\nConduct quarterly monitoring and evaluation\r\nPresent school performance to stakeholders\r\nAdjust plans based on feedback\r\nPrepare Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)\r\nMobilize community resources\r\nEnsure proper liquidation/reporting of funds\r\n', 'May 2026- March 2027', 'internal and external stakeholders', '60000', 'This action plan should be reviewed regularly and aligned with DepEd policies and school priorities.\r\n\r\n', 2026, 128718, 58, 12, 34),
