(2362, 'Collaborative Partnership Program and Inter-School Networking.', 'To establish formal linkages with external stakeholders and neighboring educational institutions.\r\nTo secure additional resources and technical support for school improvement.\r\nTo foster a community-based learning environment through shared expertise', 'Signed Memoranda of Agreement (MOA) or Understanding (MOU).\r\n\r\nResource sharing schedules (e.g., laboratory use, sports facilities).\r\nDocumentation of stakeholder-led workshops or donations.', 'Stakeholder Mapping: Identifying potential partners in the local government, NGOs, and private sector.\r\n\r\nConsultative Meetings: Conducting regular forums to align school needs with partner capabilities.\r\n\r\nBenchmarking Visits: Observing best practices at partner schools to adopt successful strategies.\r\n\r\nRecognition Programs: Acknowledging partner contributions during school events.', 'Annual cycle (Strategic planning at the start', 'School Head/Principal, Partnership Coordinato', '5000', 'Success will be measured by the sustainability of the partnerships and the direct impact of shared resources on student performance.', 2026, 137013, 58, 12, 39),
(2363, 'Conduct of Needs-Based Learning Action Cells (LAC) and Learning & Development (L&D) Programs.', 'To address specific pedagogical challenges identified through teacher performance reviews.\r\n\r\nTo facilitate collaborative professional growth through the sharing of best practices and instructional innovations.\r\nTo enhance teacher competence in integ', 'Accomplished LAC Plan and Session Guides.\r\n\r\nTeacher-made instructional materials or updated lesson exemplars.\r\n\r\nPost-activity evaluation reports and individual professional development plans.', 'Needs Assessment: Utilizing surveys or classroom observation results to identify priority topics.\r\n\r\nCollaborative Mentoring: Senior teachers or subject experts leading workshops and \"demo-teaching\" sessions.\r\n\r\nAction Research: Integrating research-based solutions into classroom practices.\r\n\r\nBlended Learning Workshops: Combining face-to-face discussions with online resource sharing.', 'Monthly (Scheduled LAC sessions) or Semi-annu', 'School Head, LAC Coordinator, Master Teachers', '10000', 'The focus of these sessions remains flexible to adapt to any emerging educational trends or urgent instructional needs identified mid-year.', 2026, 137013, 58, 12, 39),
(2365, 'Conducting targeted remediation activities for identified students to bridge academic performance gaps.', 'To improve student proficiency in reading fluency and literacy comprehension.\r\n\r\nTo strengthen foundational skills in Science, Technology, and Mathematics.', 'Improved assessment scores in Reading, Science, and Math.\r\n\r\nDocumented progress reports for each participating student.\r\n\r\nIncreased student confidence and engagement in classroom activities.', 'Differentiated teaching tailored to specific learning levels.\r\n\r\nHands-on Drills: Interactive Science and Math exercises.\r\n\r\nPeer Tutoring: Pairing struggling learners with student mentors.\r\n\r\nTechnology Integration: Using educational software and digital tools for interactive learning.', 'Quarterly / After-school sessions / Remedial ', 'Subject Teachers (English/Reading, Science, M', '10000', 'Continuous monitoring and post-remediation evaluations will be conducted to ensure the effectiveness of the strategy and determine if further intervention is required.', 2026, 204531, 58, 12, 0),
(2366, 'Implementation of Intensive Remediation Sessions (Reading & Comprehension, Science & Technology, and Mathematics).', 'To bridge identified learning gaps through targeted, subject-specific interventions.\r\n\r\nTo improve student proficiency in literacy and numeracy to meet grade-level standards.\r\n\r\nTo strengthen analytical skills and conceptual understanding in Science ', 'Improved post-test scores and quarterly grades for identified \"at-risk\" learners.\r\n\r\nCompleted remediation logs and progress monitoring charts.\r\n\r\nIndividualized instruction plans for students with persistent difficulties.', 'Diagnostic Testing: Identifying specific competencies where students struggle most.\r\n\r\nSmall Group Instruction: Providing focused attention to learners with similar gaps.\r\n\r\nContextualized Materials: Using simplified modules, localized stories for reading, and hands-on science kits.\r\n\r\nGamified Learning: Using math drills and interactive comprehension games to increase engagement.', 'Weekly (Scheduled remedial hours or \"Zero-Per', 'Subject Teachers, Remediation Coordinators, S', '10000', 'Progress will be tracked monthly; students who meet the mastery threshold will graduate from the remediation program to regular enrichment.', 2026, 137013, 58, 12, 39),
(2367, 'The school maintains an average rating of satisfactory from its internal and external stakeholders', '1. Determine stakeholders’ level of satisfaction on school programs and services\r\n2. Improve school services based on feedback\r\n3. Strengthen communication and engagement with stakeholders\r\n4. Enhance school programs and service delivery', '1. Completed survey results and consolidated report\r\n2. Action plan addressing identified gaps and concerns\r\n3. Documented meetings, resolutions, and agreements\r\n4. Improved school services and programs', '1. Conduct stakeholder satisfaction surveys\r\n2. Conduct feedback analysis and action planning sessions\r\n3. Conduct regular PTA meetings, community assemblies, and feedback forums\r\n4. Implement improvement initiatives based on stakeholder feedback', 'Whole Year', 'School Personnel, stakeholders', '500.00', 'Results of surveys shall be used as basis for decision-making and improvement.\r\nContinuous stakeholder engagement is encouraged to sustain satisfaction levels.', 2026, 205023, 59, 12, 144),
(2368, 'Collaborative Partnership Program and Inter-School Networking.', 'To establish formal linkages with external stakeholders and neighboring educational institutions.\r\n\r\nTo secure additional resources, technical expertise, and community support for school improvement.\r\n\r\nTo foster a synergistic learning environment th', 'Signed Memoranda of Agreement (MOA) or Understanding (MOU).\r\n\r\nActive Partnership Directory and Resource Sharing Schedule.\r\n\r\nDocumented stakeholder-led projects ', 'Stakeholder Mapping: Identifying potential partners in local government units (LGU), NGOs, and the private sector.\r\n\r\nStakeholder Forums: Conducting regular consultative meetings to align school goals with partner capabilities.\r\n\r\nInter-School Benchmarking: Visiting high-performing schools to exchange instructional strategies and administrative models.\r\n\r\nAdvocacy Campaigns: Utilizing social media and community events to showcase school needs and successes.', 'Annual cycle (Strategic planning at the start', 'School Head/Principal, Partnership Coordinato', '10000', 'Emphasis will be placed on \"Mutual Benefit\" to ensure partnerships are sustainable and not merely one-time donations.', 2026, 137013, 58, 12, 39),
