(2380, 'Implementation of a Culture-Sensitive Integration Program in Instruction and School Activities.', 'To promote inclusivity by integrating Indigenous Peoples (IP) knowledge and local cultural heritage into the curriculum.\r\n\r\nTo ensure all school programs, ceremonies, and frontline services respect the diverse traditions and beliefs of the community.', 'Contextualized lesson plans incorporating local cultural elements.\r\n\r\nSuccessful celebration of cultural heritage months/events with high community participation.\r\n\r\nZero reported incidents of cultural insensitivity or discrimination within the school campus.', 'Reviewing instructional materials to ensure they are culturally relevant and bias-free.\r\nStakeholder Consultation: Engaging community elders and cultural leaders in planning school activities.\r\n\r\nCapacity Building: Conducting seminars for teachers on cultural sensitivity and inclusive pedagogy.', 'ear-round integration with specific intensive', 'School Head  Araling Panlipunan (Social Studi', '2000', 'This plan strengthens the \"School and Community Partnership\" dimension of SBM, ensuring the school serves as a safe and respectful hub for all cultural identities.', 2026, 204531, 58, 12, 0),
(2381, 'Implementation of the K-3 Proficiency Mastery Program (Literacy and Numeracy).', 'To ensure all Grade 3 learners meet or exceed the required proficiency levels in Mother Tongue, Filipino, and English literacy.\r\n\r\nTo achieve 100% mastery of foundational numeracy clusters (number sense, operations, and geometric shapes) among Grade ', 'Verified assessment results (e.g., CRLA, Phil-IRI, or School-Based Numeracy Tests) showing \"Proficient\" or \"Advanced\" status for Grade 3 clusters.\r\n\r\nIndividual Learner Progress Folders documenting the mastery of specific skill clusters.\r\n\r\nDecrease in the number of \"at-risk\" learners transitioning to Grade 4.', 'Organizing lessons based on specific skill gaps identified in pre-assessments.\r\nThe \"3B’s\" Initiative: Bawat Bata Bumabasa (Every Child a Reader) through dedicated daily reading slots.\r\n\r\nConcrete-Pictorial-Abstract (CPA) Approach: Using manipulatives and visual aids to teach abstract math concepts to young learners.\r\n\r\nDifferentiated Learning Centers: Establishing classroom corners dedicated to specific literacy and numeracy games.', 'Ongoing throughout the academic year, with in', 'Grade 3 Class Advisers  School Reading and Ma', '10000', 'This plan is a core component of SBM Level 3, as Grade 3 proficiency is a leading indicator of long-term school success and a primary metric for the \"Learning Environment\" and \"Curriculum\" standards.', 2026, 204531, 58, 12, 0),
(2382, 'Implementation of Needs-Based School Learning Action Cells (SLAC) and Targeted Learning & Development (L&D) Programs.', 'To enhance teacher competencies in pedagogical content knowledge based on identified professional gaps.\r\n\r\nTo provide a collaborative platform for teachers to share best practices in remediation and classroom management.\r\n\r\nTo align teacher professio', 'Individual Professional Development Plans (IPDP) updated for all teaching staff.\r\n\r\nMonthly SLAC session reports and documented teaching strategies.\r\n\r\nImproved teacher performance ratings (RPMS-PPST) and corresponding increase in student achievement scores.', 'Using Self-Assessment Checklists (SAT) to identify the specific topics needed for LAC sessions.\r\nMentoring and Coaching: Pairing master teachers with proficient teachers for \"on-the-job\" professional development.\r\n\r\nResource Person Engagement: Inviting subject matter experts for specialized workshops on literacy, numeracy, and technology integration.', 'Monthly SLAC sessions (Year-round) with mid-y', 'School Head / LAC Leader  LAC Facilitator and', '3000', 'Needs-based L&D ensures that professional development is not just \"routine\" but is a purposeful intervention to improve the quality of frontline instructional services.', 2026, 204531, 58, 12, 0),
