(2385, '21st Century Skills Integration for Learners', 'To embed critical thinking, collaboration, communication, creativity, and digital literacy into classroom instruction and learner activities, ensuring proficiency in NAT core learning areas', 'At least 80% of Grade 6 learners demonstrate proficiency in formative assessments, project-based tasks, and mock NAT exams.', 'The methodology for embedding 21st century skills into classroom instruction is anchored on constructivist, project-based, and collaborative learning approaches. Strategies include lesson integration, skill-focused activities, technology utilization, teacher capacity-building, and stakeholder involvement. These ensure learners develop critical thinking, collaboration, communication, creativity, and digital literacy, leading to proficiency in NAT core learning areas.', 'Year Round', 'School Head, Teachers', 'MOOE', 'Successful implementation requires stakeholder support, provision of ICT resources, and continuous monitoring through formative assessments and mock exams. Sustainability will be ensured by embedding skills into daily instruction, while challenges such as digital access will be addressed through remedial and differentiated strategies', 2026, 128904, 59, 12, 142),
(2386, 'Facilitates Teacher Promotion ', 'To develop professional strength of teachers. ', 'Trainings attended by teachers; Expanded Professional Network; Professional Development', 'Teacher attendance to training. ', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'School Principal, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 500855, 58, 12, 40),
(2387, 'Inclusive Learning Facilities Program ', 'To ensure the school provides SPED- and PWD-friendly facilities that promote accessibility, equity, and quality learning for all learners.', 'Upgraded accessible facilities, inclusive classrooms, and provision of assistive devices. Teachers demonstrate readiness in inclusive practices, while SPED and PWD learners show active participation and improved achievement. Stakeholders are engaged in sustaining a barrier-free, equitable, and supportive learning environment.', 'The methodology for ensuring SPED- and PWD-friendly facilities is anchored on needs assessment, inclusive design, participatory planning, and capacity building. Strategies include infrastructure enhancement, assistive technology integration, inclusive classroom arrangements, stakeholder collaboration, and advocacy campaigns. These approaches guarantee accessibility, equity, and quality learning for all learners.', 'Year Round', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents', 'MOOE, PTA, PRIVATE PARTNERS', 'Successful implementation requires stakeholder collaboration, resource mobilization, and continuous monitoring. Sustainability will be ensured through integration into the school improvement plan, while teacher training will maximize the use of SPED- and PWD-friendly facilities.', 2026, 128904, 59, 12, 142),
(2388, 'Conduct Brigada Eskwela 2026', '1. Prepare school facilities for the opening of classes\r\n2. Mobilize stakeholder participation and Bayanihan\r\n3. Promote Conducive Learning Environment', '-100% school Readiness on the opening of classes\r\n-Brigada Eskwela Approved Activity Design and Accomplishment report', '1. Pre-Implementation Phase\r\n    * Conduct school facilities assessment and identify repair/cleaning needs\r\n    * Organize Brigada Eskwela steering committee with teachers, PTA, LGU, and partners\r\n    * Map stakeholders and send advocacy/invitation letters for donations, volunteers, and services\r\n    * Prepare activity design and BE Forms\r\n2. Implementation Phase\r\n    *Kick-Off program with orientation of volunteers on safety and assigned tasks\r\n    *Form task groups: (cleaning, minor repair, painting, gardening)\r\n    *Check daily attendance, work done, and donations received\r\n    *Document activities with photos for transparency and reporting\r\n  3. Post-Implementation Phase\r\n     *Conduct Final Inspection of completed work \r\n     *Consolidate accomplishment report and acknowledge partners/donors\r\n     *Evaluate outcomes and gather feedback for improvement of the next year\'s Brigada Eskwela', 'June 1-5, 2026', 'Jaylord L. Marsamolo- Brigada Coordinator', '5000.00', 'This activity will be implemented to promote collaborative planning, bayanihan system, resource pooling, and transparency in documentation between the school, community and stakeholders/partners.', 2026, 102008, 58, 12, 40),
(2389, 'Frontline Service Innovation Program ', 'To strengthen and innovate the school’s frontline services by integrating technology, inclusivity, and stakeholder-centered approaches, ensuring efficient, equitable, and quality service delivery.', 'Digitalized service systems, streamlined processes, and inclusive facilities that ensure accessibility for all stakeholders. Staff demonstrate readiness through training, while parents and community partners report improved satisfaction. Sustainability measures and stakeholder engagement guarantee continuous innovation in frontline service delivery.', 'The methodology for strengthening and innovating frontline services is anchored on process review, stakeholder consultation, technology integration, and capacity building. Strategies include establishing digital service platforms, creating a one-stop service center, implementing inclusive practices, and mobilizing partnerships. These approaches ensure efficient, equitable, and quality service delivery to all stakeholders.', 'Year Round', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents', 'MOOE', 'Successful implementation requires stakeholder collaboration, resource mobilization, and continuous monitoring. Sustainability will be ensured by embedding innovations into school systems, while staff training will strengthen readiness to deliver efficient, inclusive, and quality frontline services.', 2026, 128904, 59, 12, 142),
(2390, 'Partnership Strengthening Program', 'To foster collaboration between the school, stakeholders, and other schools, ensuring shared responsibility, resource mobilization, and continuous improvement in learner outcomes.', 'Formalized partnerships with stakeholders and other schools, implementation of joint programs, and mobilization of resources. Stakeholders actively engage in school activities, while best practices are shared across institutions. Capacity-building initiatives and sustained collaboration lead to improved learner outcomes and stronger school-community relationships.', 'The methodology for strengthening partnerships is anchored on stakeholder mapping, needs assessment, participatory planning, and formal agreements. Strategies include implementing joint programs, mobilizing resources, fostering inter-school collaboration, and maintaining transparent communication. These approaches ensure sustainable partnerships that enhance school improvement and learner success.', 'Year Round', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents', 'MOOE', 'This activity is aligned with DepEd’s priorities on shared responsibility and community engagement. Effective implementation requires active stakeholder involvement, resource mobilization, and continuous monitoring. Sustainability will be ensured by integrating partnerships into the school improvement plan, while capacity-building initiatives will strengthen collaboration among schools and stakeholders.', 2026, 128904, 59, 12, 142),
(2391, 'Milestone Achievement Awards ', 'To recognize and reward the contributions, loyalty, and achievements of school personnel, fostering motivation, morale, and a culture of excellence.', 'Establishment of a recognition program, distribution of awards and incentives, and acknowledgment of service loyalty. Personnel morale and motivation are improved, fostering a culture of excellence and appreciation. Recognition events are institutionalized, contributing to enhanced retention and performance of school staff.', 'The methodology for recognizing personnel achievements is anchored on achievement tracking, criteria development, and stakeholder consultation. Strategies include annual recognition ceremonies, incentive programs, public acknowledgment, and professional growth rewards. These approaches foster morale, motivation, and a culture of excellence among school personnel.', 'Year Round', 'School Head, Teachers', 'MOOE', 'Effective implementation requires stakeholder support, resource mobilization, and inclusivity. Sustainability will be ensured by institutionalizing recognition programs in the school calendar, thereby fostering morale, motivation, and a culture of excellence among personnel.', 2026, 128904, 59, 12, 142),
(2392, 'Computer Laboratory Enhancement Program ', 'To establish and maintain a functional computer laboratory/classroom that supports ICT integration, digital literacy, and technology-based learning for all students.', 'A fully operational computer laboratory, integration of ICT in instruction, and improved digital literacy among students. Maintenance systems and resource mobilization ensure sustainability, while teacher training and inclusive access foster equitable and effective use of ICT facilities.', 'The methodology for establishing a functional computer laboratory is anchored on needs assessment, resource mobilization, infrastructure setup, and capacity building. Strategies include ICT integration in the curriculum, digital literacy programs, inclusive access, and sustainability partnerships. These approaches ensure that the computer laboratory supports effective teaching, learning, and digital transformation in the school.', 'Year Round', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents', 'MOOE, PTA, PRIVATE PARTNERS', 'Effective implementation requires resource mobilization, teacher readiness, and inclusive access. Sustainability will be ensured through regular maintenance and integration of computer lab use into the curriculum and school improvement plan.', 2026, 128904, 59, 12, 142),
(2393, 'Conduct Oplan Balik Eskwela 2026', '1. Address enrollment concerns and provide public assistance;\r\n2. Conduct information campaigns on school opening and DepEd policies; and\r\n3. Ensure school readiness and inter-agency coordination for safe reopening.', '-Functional Public Assistance Command Centers\r\n-Resolved enrolment and school opening concerns\r\n-Widely disseminated information materials on school opening\r\n-School readiness assessment report\r\n-Activated Inter-Agency Task Force support\r\n-Consolidated OBE accomplishment report', '1. Pre-Implementation Phase\r\n  *Establish the OBE Public Assistance Command Center\r\n  *Conduct School Readiness Assessment of teachers, classrooms, seats, etc.\r\n  *Prepare information materials, advisories on enrolment, school policies, and safety protocols\r\n2. Implementation Phase\r\n  *Activate Public Assistance and Command Center to receive, log, and track concerns from parents, learners, and stakeholders in real time\r\n  *Resolve at least 80% of issues immediately\r\n  *Run for Information campaign via media, school postings, and online platforms to address DepEd policy Questions\r\n 3. Post-Implementation Phase\r\n   *Consolidate data on concerns received, resolved, and referred\r\n   *Prepare and Submit OBE accomplishment report to higher offices\r\n   *Evaluate Public Assistance Command Center Operations and stakeholder feedback as basis for improvements', 'June 1-8, 2026', 'Jomela Ann D. Arango', '0', 'This activity promotes real-time response system, transparency and proactive information dissemination.', 2026, 102008, 58, 12, 40),
(2394, 'Establish and operationalize a functional school library for Kindergarten to Grade 5 learners', '1. Provide learners with access to age-appropriate reading and reference materials\r\n\r\n2. Promote literacy and love for reading across all grade levels\r\n\r\n3. Support teachers with instructional resources for contextualized learning', '1. A designated library space within the school\r\n\r\n2. Collection of books, storybooks, reference materials, and digital resources\r\n\r\n3. Library management system (basic cataloging and borrowing process)\r\n\r\n4. Regular library-based activities (storytelling, reading clubs)', '1. Convert an existing classroom corner or unused space into a mini-library\r\n\r\n2. Solicit book donations from LGU, NGOs, alumni, and parents\r\n\r\n3. Allocate part of MOOE for shelves, tables, and basic cataloging materials\r\n\r\n4. Assign a teacher-librarian or designate a library-in-charge\r\n\r\n5.  Launch literacy programs (e.g., “Drop Everything and Read,” storytelling sessions)', 'June 2026 – March 2027 (initial setup and pil', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers, Barangay', '₱30,000 (for shelves, tables, cataloging materials, and starter book collection) Additional resources through donations and partnerships', 'This action plan addresses a critical gap in school infrastructure. A functional library will directly support literacy and numeracy programs, enhance learner engagement, and strengthen SBM compliance.', 2026, 128956, 59, 12, 145);
INSERT INTO `sgod_action_plan` (`id`, `activity`, `objective`, `ex_output`, `metho_strategy`, `time_frame`, `person_involved`, `bud_req`, `remarks`, `fy`, `school_id`, `division`, `region`, `district`) VALUES
(2395, 'Set up and operationalize a computer laboratory/classroom/space to support ICT integration in teaching and learning', '1. Provide learners with access to basic computer literacy and digital learning tools\r\n\r\n2. Support teachers in integrating ICT into lessons and instructional materials\r\n\r\n3. Strengthen learners’ readiness for 21st-century skills and future TLE-TVL e', '1. A designated computer laboratory/classroom/space equipped with functional ICT devices\r\n\r\n2. At least 3-5  computers or laptops available for learners and teachers\r\n\r\n3. Basic ICT curriculum integration in Grades 3–5\r\n\r\n4. Regular ICT-based activities (typing practice, educational software use, digital storytelling)', '1. Identify and prepare a classroom space for ICT use\r\n\r\n2. Request ICT equipment from DepEd, LGU, NGOs, and community stakeholders\r\n\r\n3. Allocate part of MOOE for minor ICT purchases (e.g., printers, routers, projectors)\r\n\r\n4. Train teachers on basic ICT integration and classroom management in computer labs\r\n\r\n5. Launch pilot ICT activities (e.g., “Digital Literacy Week,” coding basics for kids)', 'July 2026 – March 2027 (initial setup and pil', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Teachers, PTA O', '₱100,000.00 (for computers, furniture, internet setup, and basic ICT tools) Additional resources through donations and partnerships', 'This action plan addresses a critical gap in school infrastructure. A functional computer laboratory will enhance learners’ digital literacy, support teachers’ instructional innovation, and strengthen SBM compliance under ICT readiness.', 2026, 128956, 59, 12, 145),
(2396, 'CURRICULUM AND TEACHING\r\nImplementation of Targeted Academic Intervention and Skills Enhancement Program', '1. To improve the Early Language, Literacy, and Numeracy (ELLN) proficiency of Grade 3 learners through focused remediation and enrichment activities.\r\n2. To enhance the mastery of core learning areas and develop 21st‑century skills among Grade 6 lea', '1. Improved ELLN assessment results among Grade 3 learners.\r\n2. Increased mastery level in core learning areas and observable improvement in 21st‑century skills among Grade 6 learners.\r\n3. Conducted remediation and enhancement sessions with documented lesson plans and attendance.\r\n4. Completed test item analysis, progress monitoring records, and intervention reports.\r\n5. Improved overall learner performance in formative and summative assessments.', '1. Conduct baseline assessments and analyze results (ELLN assessments for Grade 3 and NAT item analysis for Grade 6) to identify specific learning gaps.\r\n2. Implement regular remediation and enrichment classes using differentiated, contextualized, and learner‑centered strategies.\r\n3. Integrate higher‑order thinking skills, collaborative learning, and problem‑based activities to strengthen 21st‑century skills.\r\n4. Utilize formative assessments, quarterly tests, and Test Item Analysis to monitor progress and adjust instruction accordingly.\r\n5. Engage teachers in collaborative planning through Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions and provide instructional coaching and feedback.\r\n6. Involve parents and guardians in supporting learners through home‑based learning activities and regular communication.', 'June - December 2026', '1. Teachers 2. Reading Coordinator 3. School ', 'MOOE (approved AIP) 45,000.00', '', 2026, 128919, 59, 12, 142),
(2398, 'LEARNING ENVIRONMENT\r\nCommunity‑Based Learning Access and ALS Referral Program', '1. To increase access to learning opportunities for disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adult learners in the school community.\r\n2. To identify and profile potential OSYs and adult learners who may benefit from alternative learning opportunities.', '1. Conducted community mapping and profiling of disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adult learners.\r\n2. Established referral system or coordination with nearby ALS providers or Schools Division Office.\r\n3. Implemented learning activities such as orientation sessions, literacy programs, or bridging classes.', '1. Conduct community mapping and coordination with barangay officials to identify disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adult learners.\r\n2. Organize orientation and advocacy activities to raise awareness of available learning opportunities, including ALS and school‑based initiatives.\r\n3. Coordinate with the Schools Division Office, ALS implementers, and partner stakeholders for referrals and support.', 'June 2026 - March 2027', '1. Teachers 2. School Head', '0.00', '', 2026, 128919, 59, 12, 142),
(2399, 'ADM/LARDOs Intervention  Program', 'To establish and implement intervention program for Learners At Risk of Dropping Out.\r\n', 'LARDOs  intervention program established and implemented', 'Establishment and implementation of intervention program for LARDOs.', 'January-December 2026', 'School Head, ADM Focal, Teachers, learners, P', '10000', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2400, 'Rewards and Recognition System', 'To recognize the performances of learners, parents and  teachers   in every quarter, yearends and in any culminating programs and activities done in school through medals, ribbons, or certificates.', 'Performances of learners, parents and  teachers   in every quarter and in any culminating programs and activities done in school through medals, ribbons, or certificates', 'Conduct quarterly recognition and Program or Activity culmination Recognition to learners, parents and teachers with excellent and commendable performance.', 'January-December 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, SPT, Program Coordinat', '23150', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2401, 'Learners performance and Progress', 'To track, record, assess and update the  attendance, performance, learning and development and progress of the 100% enrolled learners.', 'Attendance, Performance, learning and  development and  progress of 100% enrolled learners were  tracked, assessed, recorded, assessed, and updated', 'Tracking, Recording,Assessing,  and updating the attendance,  performance, development and progress of 100% enrolled learners ', 'January-December 2026', 'School Head, Teachers', '35020', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2402, 'IPEd Implementation', 'To implement IP related programs and activities in school i.e beadsmaking, basket weaving, IP Day, ', 'IP related programs and activities implemented.', 'Implementation of IP programs and activities.', 'January-December 2026', 'School Head, SPT, SPTA, IPEd Focal', '1500', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2403, 'ARAL-READING PROGRAM', 'To decrease the numbers of non-reader and frustration level reader in English and Filipino into at least 75% by the end of the school year through the ARAL-Reading Program and help of BEWs( Barangay Education', 'Decrease the numbers of non-readers and frustration level readers in English and Filipino into at least 75% by the end of the school year through the ARAL-Reading Program and help of BEWs', 'Intense implementation of school reading program and reading remediation.', 'January-December 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, School Reading Coordin', '49980', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2404, 'NUMERACY', 'To decrease the number of non-numerate learners in school into at least 75% by the end of the school year', 'Decrease the numbers of non-numerate learners in school into at least 75% by the end of the school year', 'Implement a numeracy remediation program in school.                             Intense monitoring and evaluation.', 'January-December 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, School Math Coordinato', '20100', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2405, 'Culture -sensitive Activities', 'To conduct culture-sensitive activities in school to be participated by different ethnic groups.\r\n', '90% of the total ethnic students enrolled in school participated the prepared contests and activities.', '1. Assign a Teacher to do the planning and to act as coordinator\r\n2. Invite interested students to join the group.\r\n3. Name and conduct some of the events that could enhance their culture.\r\n4. Invite external stakeholders to join and as speaker during the event', 'Nov.  20, 2026', 'Arlyn Limama-TI, Elizabeth C. Agbay, P-IV,  L', 'Php 2,500.00', 'The date can be moved according to our new grading terms.', 2026, 316003, 59, 12, 144),
(2406, 'Curriculum and Implementation', 'To contextualize/ localize curriculum designs by crafting, developing and reproducing 100% of learners materials, activity sheets, school forms and using other teaching materials/ICT integration within the school year  to be', 'Contextualized and localized learners materials and activity sheets were 100% crafted, developed and reproduced within the school year', 'Curriculum designs contextualized/localized.', 'January-December 2026', 'School Head, Teacher, Subject Coordinators, P', '107150', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2407, 'Early Identification of At-Risk Learners', 'To identify learners with frequent absences and learning difficulties', 'Master list of identified at-risk learners', 'Review of attendance records, teacher observation', 'Beginning of School Year and Ongoing', 'Class Advisers, Teachers', '00', 'Preventive intervention', 2026, 129030, 59, 12, 147),
(2408, 'Institutional Support and Training', 'To strengthen content knowledge and pedagogy of teachers and improve learners\' learning skills  by submitting them to all DepEd related trainings, meetings and activities with the provision of registration fee and travel allowance and technical assis', 'Technical assistance, Registration fee and travel allowance were  provided to any school personnel or learners attending DepEd related training, meetings and activities.', 'Provision of registration fee and travel allowance to any school personnel or learners attending DepEd related trainings, meetings and activities', 'January-December 2026', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Teachers, SPT, ', '90750', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2409, 'DRRM and WASH in School', 'To procure and provide DRRM and Health and sanitation supplies and materials  in school for safety and preparation/mitigation', 'DRRM and Health supplies and materials procured and provided In school', 'Procurement and provision of DRRM and Health supplies and materials in school.', 'January-December 2026', 'School Head, SPT, DRRM coordinator, Teachers', '46936', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2410, 'Identification and Profiling of Target Learners', 'To identify disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adult learners in the community', 'Master list and learner profiles', 'Survey, coordination with barangay officials, school records review', 'Beginning of School Year', 'School Head, Teachers, Barangay Officials', '00', 'Basis for intervention', 2026, 129030, 59, 12, 147),
(2411, 'CLASSROOM REPAIR', 'To repair the wall of Grade 1, Grade 2, Grade 5 and Grade 6  room infested with termites.', 'Grade 1,  Grade 5 and Grade 6 room repaired.', 'Repair the wall of Grade 1,  5 and Grade 6 room.', 'Quarter 3 2026', 'School Head, SPT, SPTA, Teachers, Carpenter, ', '63700', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2412, 'GRADE 2 FLOOR PAVEMENT REPAIR', 'To repair the floor pavement of Grade 2 class to avoid being drowned in water flood.', 'Grade 2 floor pavement repaired.', 'Repair the Grade 2 floor pavement.', '\'Quarter 4 2026', 'School Head, SPT, SPTA, Teachers, ', '38500', '', 2026, 129086, 59, 12, 149),
(2413, 'Capability Building for CPC Members', 'To strengthen skills in handling and managing child protection cases', 'Trained and confident CPC members', 'Trainings, workshops, case simulations', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, CPC Members', '2000', 'Capacity enhancement', 2026, 129030, 59, 12, 147),
(2415, 'Orientation on Mental Health Awareness', 'To raise awareness on mental health and emotional well-being', 'informed teachers, learners, and parents', 'Orientation sessions, short talks, discussions', 'Beginning of School Year and As Needed', 'School Head, Teachers, Guidance Designee', '1000', 'Preventive strategy', 2026, 129030, 59, 12, 147),
(2416, 'School Mental Health Program', 'To promote the overall physical, mental, and emotional well-being of participants by providing activities, resources, and education that encourage healthy lifestyle choices, stress management, and personal development.  ', '1. Increased awareness and knowledge of healthy lifestyle practices among participants\r\n2. Improved physical health indicators (e.g., fitness levels, nutrition habits)\r\n3. Enhanced mental and emotional well-being (reduced stress, improved coping skills)', '1. Needs Assessment - identify the needs and concerns of participants.\r\n2. Program Planning-design activities and interventions  and nutrition education.\r\n3. Implementation of Activities- carry out planned activities such as exercise programs, wellness seminars, stress management sessions, and counseling services.', 'At least once a month- ( First Friday of the ', 'Lilian Arranguez, T-II, Christine Presores', '500', 'A Speaker can be invited', 2026, 316003, 59, 12, 144),
(2417, 'Reconstitution & Activation of SGC', 'Achieve 10/12 functionality indicators.', 'SGC functionality tool; resolutions; minutes', 'Designation; TOR; quarterly meetings; participation in planning & resource mobilization', 'School Year 2026–2028', 'School Head; SGC Members; PTA', '3000', 'Use existing assemblies for SGC sessions', 2026, 129020, 59, 12, 146),
(2418, 'Identification of Personnel Milestone Achievements', 'To identify personnel who reached service, performance, and professional milestones', 'List of personnel with milestone achievements', 'Review of service records, IPCRF results, accomplishments', 'Beginning of School Year and Ongoing', 'School Head, Administrative Staff', '00', 'Basis for recognition', 2026, 129044, 59, 12, 147),
(2419, 'Conduct SBM orientation and re-echo sessions', 'Strengthen understanding and implementation of SBM principles among stakeholder', 'Stakeholders oriented on SBM levels and indicators', 'Seminar-workshop, LAC discussion, presentation of SBM framework', 'June–July (Start of School Year)', 'School Head, Teachers, SGC, PTA Officers', '1000.00', 'Funded through PTA support', 2026, 129039, 59, 12, 147),
(2420, '1. SBM Orientation for Stakeholders\r\n2. School Needs Assessment (Resource Gaps Focus)\r\n3. SIP Enhancement (2026–2029)\r\n4. Resource Mobilization and Partnership Building\r\n5. Instructional Resource Development\r\n6. Implementation of Priority Programs\r\n7', '1. To strengthen understanding of SBM among school and community stakeholders\r\n2. To identify priority needs, especially on limited learning resources\r\n3. To align SIP with identified needs and SBM principles\r\n4. To augment school resources through p', '1. Stakeholders oriented and actively engaged in SBM\r\n2. Comprehensive needs assessment report\r\n3. Updated and approved School Improvement Plan\r\n4. MOAs/MOUs and increased material support\r\n5. Locally developed and improvised instructional materials\r\n6. Completed programs (eg. reading, remediation, ICT integration)\r\n7. Quarterly M&E and SBM assessment reports\r\n8. Accomplishment reports and recognition of stakeholders\r\n', '1. Conduct school-based orientation, distribute SBM manuals and guides\r\n2. Surveys, classroom observations, FGD with teachers and learners\r\n3. Collaborative planning workshop with stakeholders\r\n4. Coordination with LGU Hagonoy & Barangay Guihing, alumni, NGOs, private partners\r\n5. LAC sessions, peer collaboration, material development workshops\r\n6. Program implementation, classroom monitoring\r\n7. Classroom observations, data tracking, SBM tool utilization\r\n8. Meetings, presentations, awarding/recognition activities\r\n', 'Whole Year Round (2025-2026)', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, Teachers, SGC &', '35500', '1. Use school MOOE\r\n2. Printing and data gathering\r\n3. Workshop materials\r\n4. Communication & transport\r\n5. For materials and supplies\r\n6. Depends on projects\r\n7. Documentation\r\n8. Certificates & materials\r\n', 2026, 304275, 59, 12, 140),
(2421, 'SIP/AIP planning workshop', 'Improve school planning', 'Updated SIP/AIP', 'Collaborative planning', 'July–August', 'School Head, Teachers, Stakeholders', '1000.00', 'Annual activity', 2026, 129039, 59, 12, 147),
(2422, 'LAC sessions and training', 'Improve teaching quality', 'Improved instruction', 'Coaching and mentoring', 'Monthly', 'Teachers, School Head', '1000.00', 'Continuous', 2026, 129039, 59, 12, 147),
