(2428, 'Implement academic support programs e.g. literacy and numeracy\r\nCarry out infrastructure  and facility improvements\r\nLaunch community engagement activities', 'Execute approved plans effectively\r\nEnsure efficient use of resources', 'Projects completed on time\r\nTargets and outcomes achieved\r\nResource utilization efficient', 'Assign task leaders and timelines \r\nMonitor progress regularly\r\nCoordinates with partners and stake holders ', 'August to March', 'All implementors and partners', '5000.00', '', 2026, 129077, 59, 12, 149),
(2429, 'Special Education', 'To provide educational support to learners with special needs by implementing appropriate interventions, and resources that promote their academic achievement and social development', 'Enhanced academic performance and skill development among learners with disabilities\r\nImproved social, emotional, and behavioral competencies', '1. To identify learners with special needs and determine their strengths and areas for support.\r\n2. To develop tailored Individualized Education Plans based on learners needs and apply instructional strategies for each learner.\r\n3. Prepare appropriate teaching materials,  suited to the needs of the learners.', '2026-2027', 'Elizabeth C. Agbay, P-IV,  April Rose Nazarit', '1000', 'The school can\'t provide ramp because it\'s utilizing TLS as classroom.', 2026, 316003, 59, 12, 144),
(2430, 'Preparation and Orientation, Assessment and Baseline Setting, Capacity Building, Planning and Resource Mobilization, Implementation of SBM Practices, Monitoring and Evaluation, Sustainability and Continuous Improvement', '-Promote participatory governance by involving teachers, parents, learners, and community stakeholders in school decision-making.\r\n-Strengthen accountability and transparency in resource management and school operations.\r\n-Enhance teaching and learni', '-Functional SBM Core Team established with clear roles and responsibilities.\r\n-Baseline Assessment Report using the SBM Assessment Tool (SAT).\r\n-Capacity-Building Workshops conducted for teachers, staff, and stakeholders.\r\n-School Improvement Plan (SIP) developed and aligned with DepEd priorities.\r\n-Transparent Resource Management System in place with stakeholder oversight.\r\n-Active Stakeholder Participation through PTA, student councils, and community partners.\r\n-Quarterly Monitoring Reports documenting progress and challenges.\r\n-School Report Card shared with stakeholders to ensure accountability.\r\n-Recognition of Best Practices in SBM implementation.\r\n-Sustained Partnerships with LGUs, NGOs, alumni, and other community supporters.', 'Orientation & Awareness\r\nConduct school-wide orientations and stakeholder meetings to explain SBM principles.\r\nDistribute DepEd guidelines and localized materials for clarity.\r\nAssessment & Planning\r\nAdminister the SBM Assessment Tool (SAT) to establish baseline data.\r\nIdentify priority areas and integrate them into the School Improvement Plan (SIP).\r\nCapacity Building\r\nOrganize training workshops for teachers, staff, and community partners.\r\nProvide mentoring and peer-sharing sessions to strengthen leadership and governance skills.\r\nImplementation of SIP\r\nExecute planned activities with clear timelines and assigned responsibilities.\r\nMobilize resources from LGUs, NGOs, alumni, and local stakeholders.\r\nMonitoring & Evaluation\r\nConduct quarterly reviews of SIP progress using performance indicators.\r\nShare results through school report cards and stakeholder assemblies.\r\nFeedback & Continuous Improvement\r\nCollect feedback from parents, learners, and community partners.\r\nAdjust strategies annually to ensure sustainability and responsiveness.', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'School Head, Non-teaching Personnel, Teachers', '5000', 'none ', 2026, 128929, 59, 12, 143),
(2431, 'Intensive Remedial Reading and Numeracy \"Power Hour\"', 'To move 100% of Grade 3 learners from \"Frustration\" to \"Instructional/Independent\" reading levels and master basic multiplication/division.', 'Improved post-test scores in Phil-IRI and numerical literacy assessments.', 'Small-group differentiated instruction; peer-tutoring (\"Big Brother/Sister\" reading program); localized instructional material development.', 'Year-round (Quarter 1 to Quarter 4)', 'School Head, K-3 Teachers, Parent Volunteers,', '5000', 'Progress to be monitored through monthly formative assessments and quarterly SMEA (School Monitoring and Evaluation Adjustment).', 2026, 137007, 58, 12, 39),
(2432, 'Average rating of SATISFACTORY from stakeholders', 'To maintain a satisfactory level of satisfaction among stakeholders by consistently delivering quality services, ensuring effective communication, and continuously improving programs based on feedback and evaluation.', 'Consistently achieved satisfactory or higher stakeholder satisfaction ratings\r\nIncreased positive feedback from stakeholders regarding services and programs\r\n', 'To develop  regular communication platforms (e.g., meetings, emails, feedback systems) to keep stakeholders informed and engaged.\r\nTo delivery of Quality Services that meet services standards and stakeholder expectations.\r\n To conduct regular surveys, and feedback sessions to gather stakeholder opinions and satisfaction levels.', 'SY2026-2027', 'Augjie Dave D. Ambayan, ADAS II, Mary Ann L. ', '1500', 'To use Client Satisfaction Survey', 2026, 316003, 59, 12, 144),
(2433, 'Project GIGHA (Guidance and Intervention for Growth, Health, and Advancement)', 'To provide accessible mental health support to 100% of students and personnel.\r\n\r\nTo reduce student behavioral referrals by 20% through proactive wellness interventions.\r\n\r\nTo equip teachers with \"Psychological First Aid\" skills.', 'Operational Wellness Nook; 100% of teachers trained in mental health basic protocols; monthly wellness activity reports.', 'Small-group counseling sessions; monthly wellness webinars; peer-mentoring through the SSG/SPG.', 'Year-round (Monthly implementation)', 'School Head, Guidance Designate, All Teachers', '2000', 'This program shall be monitored through the quarterly SMEA (School Monitoring and Evaluation Adjustment) to assess its impact on learner behavior and academic focus.', 2026, 137007, 58, 12, 39),
(2434, 'Strategic Planning and School Improvement Plan (SIP) Development', 'To formulate a comprehensive 3-year SIP that addresses the current gaps in learner achievement and school facilities.\r\n\r\nTo involve 100% of internal and external stakeholders in the situational analysis and goal-setting process.', 'Approved 3-year School Improvement Plan (SIP); Annual Implementation Plan (AIP); Signed commitment of support from stakeholders.', 'Vision-Mission-Core Values (VMV) workshops; SWOT (Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, Threats) Analysis; Community mapping and consultative assemblies.', 'Pre-planning (Quarter 1); Actual Planning (Qu', 'School Head, School Planning Team, SGC, PTA O', '2000', 'This plan serves as the primary roadmap for all school activities and must be monitored through the quarterly SMEA.', 2026, 137007, 58, 12, 39),
(2435, 'Strengthening SMEA and Program Evaluation (Project TRACK)', 'To achieve 100% timely submission of accomplishment reports for all school projects.\r\n\r\nTo utilize evaluation data to adjust at least 90% of underperforming programs during the mid-year review.', 'Updated SMEA Dashboard; Quarterly Evaluation Reports; Adjusted Project Procurement Management Plans (PPMP).', 'PDCA Cycle (Plan-Do-Check-Act) integration; peer-validation of reports; digital submission portals via cloud storage.', 'Quarterly (End of each grading period)', 'School Head, SMEA Team, Program Coordinators,', '5000', 'Success will be measured by the school\'s ability to present data-driven adjustments during the Division Monitoring and Evaluation Adjustment (DMEA).', 2026, 137007, 58, 12, 39),
(2436, 'Project DEVELOP (Dynamic Education via Learning Opportunities for Professionals)', 'To conduct at least two (2) targeted LAC sessions per month based on identified teacher gaps in the TNA.\r\n\r\nTo ensure 100% of teachers apply at least one new instructional strategy per quarter as evidenced by classroom observations (COT).', 'Monthly LAC Plan; Completion Reports with Narrative and Photos; Improved COT ratings for teaching staff.', 'Collaborative Professionalism; Mentoring and Coaching; Demonstration Teaching; Workshop-style sessions with immediate output creation.', 'Year-round', 'School Head, Master Teachers (Facilitators), ', '5000', 'The success of these activities will be validated during the year-end IPCRF (Individual Performance Commitment and Review Form) evaluations.', 2026, 137007, 58, 12, 39),
(2437, 'Implement literacy and numeracy programs', 'To reduce the number of non readers and non numerates by 20% through targeted implemented literacy and numeracy programs', 'Pretest and post test of Phil IRI, CRLA, RMA an LEGNA, individual progress report, and functional school reading and numeracy center', '20-30 minutes pull out session with the Barangay Education Worker (parents, volunteers)/a day, CLASSROOM- Utilization of advance learners paired with the struggling pupils during vacant hours, recess or lunch break.', 'June 2026- March 2027 ( Year-round)', 'School Reading and Math Coordinator, All Grad', '15000.00', 'Progress report should be monitored monthly and presented during the Mid-year review and evaluation', 2026, 129082, 59, 12, 149),
(2438, 'Conduct ELLN remediation and enrichment sessions for Grade 3 learners', 'To improve learners’ proficiency in early language, literacy, and numeracy skills and address learning gaps', 'Increased number of Grade 3 learners achieving proficiency level; improved reading and numeracy skills', 'Diagnostic assessment (pre-test), small group remediation, differentiated instruction, peer tutoring, use of ELLN materials, post-assessment', 'June – March (weekly sessions)', 'Grade 3 Teachers, School Head, Reading Coordi', '3000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2439, 'LEADERSHIP\r\nRegular Convening and Capacity‑Building of the School–Community Planning Team.', '1. To institutionalize the regular convening of the school–community planning team for collaborative planning and decision‑making.\r\n2. To strengthen stakeholder participation in school planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation.\r\n3. To ensu', '1. Established annual or quarterly meeting schedule for the school–community planning team.\r\n2. Conducted regular planning and monitoring meetings with documented minutes and attendance sheets.', '1. Develop and disseminate a fixed meeting calendar approved by the school head and stakeholders.\r\n2. Clearly define roles, responsibilities, and expectations of planning team members.\r\n3. Prepare meeting agendas and relevant data in advance to ensure productive discussions.\r\n4. Conduct regular meetings focused on planning, monitoring, and evaluation of school programs.\r\n5. Document proceedings through minutes, photos, and reports as means of verification.\r\n6. Monitor attendance and participation and provide feedback to sustain stakeholder engagement.', 'June 2026 - March 2027', '1. School Planning Team 2. School Head ', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128919, 59, 12, 142),
(2440, 'Conduct NAT Review and Enhancement Program (core subjects and 21st century skills integration)', 'To improve learners’ mastery in core learning areas and develop 21st century skills for NAT proficiency', 'Increased NAT MPS results; improved learner proficiency in tested competencies', 'Diagnostic test, focused remediation sessions, weekly review classes, contextualized learning activities, mock NAT exams, data-driven instruction', 'June – March (weekly and monthly review sessi', 'Subject Teachers (Grade 6) School Head, Maste', '5000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2441, 'Set up classroom-based reading corners and conduct book solicitation and donation drives to provide accessible reading materials for learners.', 'Provide learners with accessible reading materials by establishing classroom-based reading corners', 'Established and functional classroom-based reading corners serving as the primary reading resource in the absence of a school library.', 'Convert available classroom spaces into organized reading corners by allocating a small section with mats, shelves, or improvised book racks for easy access to reading materials.', 'July-October,2026', 'School Head, Reading Coordinator, Teachers, P', '1500.00', 'Regular monitoring of classroom reading corners to ensure effective use of reading materials in the absence of a formal school library.', 2026, 129427, 61, 12, 15),
(2442, 'Development and utilization of contextualized learning materials (modules, worksheets, and activity sheets)', 'To design and produce learning materials suited to learners’ context, needs, and abilities', 'Completed contextualized learning materials per subject/grade level; improved learner engagement', 'Collaborative lesson planning, LAC sessions, curriculum alignment workshops, peer review of materials, use of local context/examples in lessons', 'June – March (continuous per quarter)', 'Subject Teachers, Master Teachers, School Hea', '6000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2443, 'Conduct test item analysis of quarterly examinations and periodic tests', 'To identify least mastered competencies and improve instruction based on assessment results', 'Item analysis reports per subject; improved test quality; identified learning gaps', 'Collection of test results, computation of item difficulty and discrimination index, collaborative analysis during LAC sessions, data-driven instructional planning', 'Quarterly (after every periodic test)', 'Subject Teachers, Master Teachers, School Hea', '3000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2444, 'SGC Empowerment and SIP/AIP Participatory Planning', 'To institutionalize a functional School Governing Council (SGC) that actively participates in the development, implementation, and monitoring of School Improvement Plan', 'Updated SGC Constitution and By-Laws, Minutes of Quarterly Meetings, and a Community-validated Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)', 'Training of SGC members on school policies./ Transparent presentation of school targets and financial reports to gain community consensus.', '(Quarterly) July, 2026-Sept 2026, Oct,2026-De', 'School Head, SGC Chairperson, PTA President, ', '4500', 'School Governing Council includes diverse members (not just teachers)', 2026, 129088, 59, 12, 149),
(2445, ' Utilization of available laptops for Classroom-Based ICT Learning', 'Provide learners with ICT-based learning experiences using available laptops despite the absence of a computer laboratory and other ICT equipment', 'Regular use of laptops in instructional activities; improved learner ICT exposure; integration of digital learning tasks in lessons', 'Classroom-based rotational use of laptops; integration of ICT activities in lesson plans; teacher-guided computer literacy sessions; offline digital learning materials utilization', 'June-April,2026', 'School Head, Teachers, ICT Coordinator, Learn', '0', 'Focus on optimizing limited laptop resources for ICT integration in teaching and learning', 2026, 129427, 61, 12, 15),
(2446, 'Implementation of Alternative Learning System (ALS) and inclusive learning sessions for OSYs and adult learners', 'To provide learning opportunities and access to education for disadvantaged learners, OSYs, and adults', 'Enrolled OSYs/adult learners; conducted ALS/inclusive learning sessions; improved literacy and numeracy skills', 'Community mapping and profiling, coordination with ALS coordinators, modular learning sessions, blended learning approach, home-based and community-based instruction', 'June – March (continuous implementation)', 'ALS Coordinator, School Head, Teachers, Baran', '6000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2447, 'Enhancement of Grade 6 Learners\' Proficiency in 21st- Century Skills and Core Learning Areas', 'Grade 6 learners achieve proficiency in 21st -century skills and core learning areas in National Achievement Test (NAT)', '1. NAT performance reports\r\n2. Lesson Plans with 21st-century skills integration\r\n', '1. Sustain reading and Numeracy programs\r\n2. Conduct quarterly formative assessments\r\n3.  Strengthen parent involvement through meetings and  home-based support activities\r\n4. Integrate critical thinking and problem-solving tasks in classroom instruction', 'SY 2025-2026', 'Subject Teachers,  Testing Coordinator, Paren', '750.00', 'Ongoing implementation with continuous monitoring and evaluation; results to be reviewed quarterly for adjustments.', 2026, 129041, 59, 12, 147),
(2448, 'Establishment and implementation of School Mental Wellness Program (counseling, psychosocial support, and awareness activities)', 'To support learners’ mental and emotional well-being and provide appropriate intervention for at-risk students', 'Functional referral system; conducted mental health awareness sessions; counseling records; reduced behavioral and emotional issues among learners', 'Orientation on mental health awareness, regular homeroom guidance sessions, teacher training on basic counseling, referral system for at-risk learners, coordination with health professionals (RHU/DOH), peer support activities', 'June – March (continuous implementation)', 'School Head, Guidance Counselor/Designate, Te', '5000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2449, 'Establishment and improvement of SPED and PWD-friendly facilities (ramps, accessible comfort rooms, handrails, and learning support materials)', 'To provide safe, accessible, and inclusive learning environment for learners with special needs and PWDs', 'Installed ramps and handrails; improved accessible CR; availability of SPED support materials; inclusive school environment', 'Site inspection and needs assessment, coordination with LGU/engineers, construction and retrofitting of facilities, procurement of SPED learning materials, stakeholder consultation', 'June – March (phased implementation)', 'School Head, LGU Engineer, SPED Coordinator/T', '20000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2450, 'Implementation of ICT-based frontline service innovations (online enrollment, e-feedback system, and digital request processing)', 'To improve efficiency, accessibility, and responsiveness of school frontline services to stakeholders', 'Functional online systems for enrollment and feedback; faster processing of requests; improved stakeholder satisfaction', 'Development of simple digital forms (Google Forms/Microsoft Forms), orientation of stakeholders on ICT systems, establishment of help desk support, use of SMS/social media updates for announcements', 'June – March (continuous implementation and u', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Administrative ', '10000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2451, 'GOVERNANCE AND ACCOUNTABILITY\r\nRevitalization and Regular Convening of the School Governance Council (SGC).', '1. To institutionalize the regular convening of the School Governance Council for shared decision‑making and school governance.\r\n4. To strengthen stakeholder participation in school planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation.\r\n3. To ensure ', '1. Established annual or quarterly SGC meeting schedule approved by council members.\r\n2. Conducted regular SGC meetings with documented minutes, attendance sheets, and resolutions.\r\n3. Updated school plans, policies, or action items reflecting SGC inputs and decisions.\r\n4. Increased participation and engagement of SGC members and stakeholders.\r\n5. Improved SBM practices in leadership, governance, and accountability.', '1. Review and reorient SGC members on their roles, responsibilities, and importance in school governance.\r\n2. Develop and disseminate a fixed meeting calendar and clear meeting protocols.\r\n3. Prepare agendas, school data, and issues for discussion prior to each meeting.\r\n4. Conduct regular SGC meetings focused on planning, policy‑making, and monitoring of school programs.\r\n5. Document proceedings through minutes, resolutions, and reports as means of verification.\r\n6. Monitor attendance and implementation of agreed actions to sustain regular convening and active participation.', 'june 2026 - March 2027', '1. SGC Members 2. School Head ', '0.00', '', 2026, 128919, 59, 12, 142),
(2452, 'Organization and operationalization of School Governance Council (SGC) through stakeholder engagement and capacity building', 'To establish a functional SGC that supports shared governance and participatory decision-making in school programs and policies', 'Functional SGC with elected/selected members; regular meetings conducted; approved SGC plans and resolutions', 'Stakeholder mapping, orientation on SBM and shared governance, selection/election of members, drafting of SGC constitution and by-laws, conduct of regular quarterly meetings and planning workshops', 'June – March (initial organization and quarte', 'School Head, PTA Officers, LGU Representative', '5000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2453, 'Conduct regular monitoring and evaluation (M&E) of school programs, projects, and activities (PPAs)', 'To ensure effective implementation, assess progress, and improve school programs based on data-driven results', 'M&E reports per quarter; improved implementation of PPAs; evidence-based decision-making', 'Development of M&E tools, classroom and program observations, quarterly program reviews, data collection and analysis, feedback mechanisms from stakeholders, post-implementation evaluation', 'June – March (quarterly and ongoing monitorin', 'School Head, M&E Coordinator, Master Teachers', '4000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2454, 'Conduct stakeholder satisfaction survey and feedback analysis (internal and external stakeholders)', 'To measure stakeholder satisfaction and identify areas for school improvement', 'Survey results with average satisfactory rating; consolidated feedback report; action points for improvement', 'Development and distribution of survey questionnaires (online and printed), focus group discussions, data analysis and interpretation, presentation of results during school planning sessions', 'June – March (semi-annual or annual conduct)', 'School Head, M&E Coordinator, Teachers, PTA O', '4000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2455, 'Establishment and improvement of school library services (organization, cataloging, and reading programs)', 'To provide learners access to reading resources and promote literacy development', 'Functional school library with organized book collection; reading corner established; increased learner library usage', 'Inventory and classification of available books, setting up library space, procurement of additional reading materials, implementation of reading programs (e.g., Drop Everything and Read), librarian/teacher assignment, student orientation on library use', 'June – March (continuous implementation)', 'School Head, Library Coordinator/Teacher, Tea', '10000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2456, 'Establishment, upgrading, and maintenance of school computer laboratory/classroom for ICT-based learning', 'To provide learners access to functional ICT facilities and integrate technology in teaching and learning', 'Functional computer laboratory; available working computer units; ICT-integrated lessons; improved digital literacy of learners', 'Inventory and assessment of ICT equipment, procurement/repair of computer units, installation of basic software, internet connectivity setup, scheduling of lab use, ICT training for teachers and learners, maintenance and security system', 'June – March (continuous implementation and m', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Teachers, PTA, ', '20000', '', 2026, 129140, 59, 12, 151),
(2457, 'HUMAN RESOURCE AND TEAM DEVELOPMENT\r\nImplementation of a Comprehensive Professional Development and Career Advancement Program', '1. To support and facilitate the continuous professional growth and promotion of school personnel.\r\n2. To enhance teachers’ and staff competencies through needs‑based Learning and Development (L&D) activities.\r\n3. To ensure that personnel are equippe', '1. Conducted needs assessment for professional development and promotion requirements.\r\n2. Implemented Learning Action Cells (LAC), trainings, seminars, workshops, and coaching sessions.\r\n3. Updated Individual Professional Development Plans (IPDPs) of personnel.\r\n4. Increased number of personnel qualified for promotion or higher professional responsibilities.\r\n5. Improved teaching performance and service delivery as reflected in IPCR/OPCR results.', '1. Conduct a needs assessment based on performance reviews, IPCR results, and personnel development plans.\r\n2. Organize and implement needs‑based LAC sessions, in‑service trainings, mentoring, and coaching activities.\r\n3. Encourage and support personnel participation in division, regional, and national professional development programs.\r\n4. Provide guidance and technical assistance on promotion requirements, documentation, and career pathways.\r\n5. Monitor and evaluate the impact of professional development activities through performance assessments and feedback mechanisms.', 'JUne 2026 - March 2027', '1. Teachers 2. LAC Coordinator 3. School Head', '3500.00', '', 2026, 128919, 59, 12, 142),
(2458, 'FINANCE AND RESOURCE MANAGEMENT AND MOBILIZATIONEstablishment of Alternative Learning Spaces and Phased Development of Library and ICT Facilities', '1. To provide learners with access to library and ICT learning resources despite limited classroom space.\r\n2. To maximize existing school spaces through alternative and shared learning setups.\r\n3. To gradually establish a functional library and compu', '1. Established classroom‑based reading corners and/or mobile library system.\r\n2. Implemented temporary or rotational ICT learning sessions using available devices.\r\n3. Identified and documented potential spaces for future library and computer laboratory use.\r\n4. Inclusion of library and computer laboratory development in the School Improvement Plan.\r\n5. Increased learner access to reading materials and basic digital learning experiences.\r\n6. Reports, photos, inventory lists, and utilization schedules as means of verification.', '1. Conduct an inventory of available spaces, learning materials, and ICT equipment.\r\n2. Set up classroom‑based libraries, reading corners, or mobile book carts to address immediate library needs.\r\n3. Implement scheduled or rotational ICT sessions using available computers, laptops, or tablets within classrooms or shared spaces.\r\n4. Integrate library use and ICT‑supported activities into lesson plans across learning areas.\r\n5. Coordinate with the PTA, LGU, and other stakeholders for donations, support, and future infrastructure development.\r\n6. Include the construction or allocation of dedicated library and computer laboratory spaces in the School Improvement Plan for phased implementation.\r\n7.  Monitor utilization and learner participation to guide continuous improvement.', 'June 2026 - March 2027', '1. Teachers 2. ICT Coordinator 3. School Head', '45000.00', 'MOOE (approved AIP) ', 2026, 128919, 59, 12, 142),
(2460, 'Functional Reading Hub/Corner', 'To establish a reading hub/corner that promotes a culture of reading by providing accessible, engaging, and age-appropriate materials that enhance learners’ literacy skills, comprehension, and love for reading.', '1. Improved reading comprehension and literacy skills among learners\r\nDevelopment of positive reading habits and a love for reading', '1. Identify learners’ reading levels, interests, and preferences through PHIL-IRI  or reading assessments.\r\n2. Select an appropriate and design a comfortable reading space.\r\n3. Gather and organize a variety of culturally relevant reading materials such as books, magazines, and digital resources.\r\n', 'SY 2026-2027', 'Class Advisers, Arlyn L. Limama, T-I', '2000', 'Ask donation of reading Materials', 2026, 316003, 59, 12, 144),
(2462, 'SBM Orientation and Awareness Raising', 'Orient school personnel, stakeholders, and learners on SBM principles, processes, and benefits; foster shared understanding and commitment.', 'Attendance sheets, presentation materials, minutes of meeting, feedback forms.', 'Conduct seminar/workshop, distribute information materials, hold open forum.', 'June to July 2026', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, Teachers, PTA O', '5000.00', ' To be implemented', 2026, 304280, 59, 12, 149),
(2465, 'Conduct Situational Analysis and Needs Assessment', 'Orient school personnel, stakeholders, and learners on SBM principles, processes, and benefits; foster shared understanding and commitment.', 'SWOT Analysis Matrix, Needs Assessment Report, Priority Areas Matrix.', 'Use survey questionnaires, conduct Focus Group Discussions (FGD), review and analyze data.', 'July to September 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA', '3000', 'To be implemented', 2026, 304280, 59, 12, 149),
(2467, 'Establish and operationalize School Governance Council (SGC)', 'To strengthen shared leadership and stakeholder participation in school governance', 'Functional SGC with approved organizational structure and meeting records', 'Stakeholder orientation, election of members, regular meetings', 'First Quarter', 'School Head, PTA, LGU, Teachers, Community Le', '2000', 'The school demonstrates active efforts to strengthen shared governance through stakeholder participation. However, the full functionality of the School Governance Council (SGC) is still being developed. Continuous organization and engagement of stakeholders are necessary to fully institutionalize participatory school leadership and improve accountability mechanisms.', 2026, 128920, 59, 12, 142),
(2468, 'Strengthening instructional delivery through remediation and 21st century skills integration', 'Improve learner performance in core subjects and develop critical thinking, communication, and collaboration skills', 'Improved NAT performance and enhanced learner competencies', 'Remedial classes, LAC sessions, contextualized lesson planning', 'Whole School Year', 'Teachers, School Head', '8000', 'The school shows consistent implementation of instructional strategies, particularly in remediation and integration of 21st century skills. Nevertheless, challenges remain in learner mastery of core subjects and test-taking skills. Sustained instructional support and capacity-building activities are essential to further improve learning outcomes.', 2026, 128920, 59, 12, 142),
(2469, 'Strengthen monitoring, evaluation, and data-based decision making', 'Ensure effective implementation of school programs through evidence-based planning', 'Regular monitoring reports and improved program implementation', 'Monthly monitoring, data analysis, feedback sessions', 'Monthly', 'School Head, M&E Team, Teachers', '3000', 'The school has established mechanisms for monitoring and evaluation, but implementation is not yet fully maximized in all programs. Strengthening data utilization and consistent feedback mechanisms will enhance evidence-based decision-making and continuous improvement processes.', 2026, 128920, 59, 12, 142),
(2470, 'Activity	Objective	Expected Output	Methodology/Strategy	Time Frame	Persons Involved	Budget\r\nEstablish and improve learning resource facilities (library and ICT room)', 'Provide adequate learning resources to support instruction', 'Functional library and ICT learning space', 'Resource mobilization, LGU partnership, MOOE allocation', 'Whole Year', 'School Head, LGU, Stakeholders', '20000', 'Efforts to manage and mobilize resources are evident, particularly in financial utilization. However, limitations in infrastructure such as library and ICT facilities remain a major concern. Increased resource generation and strong partnerships with stakeholders are needed to support facility improvement.', 2026, 128920, 59, 12, 142);
