(2539, 'Empo-Women Contest', 'The primary objective of this project is to celebrate Women’s Month 2026 by organizing a series of events that raise awareness about women’s rights, promote gender equality, and empower women from all walks of life. The project will aim to foster dia', '1. Increased Awareness – A rise in public understanding of women’s rights, gender-based violence, and the need for gender equality, measured by participation in discussions and educational sessions.\r\n2. Empowerment of Women – Workshops, seminars, and networking events will help equip women with the knowledge, confidence, and resources to overcome systemic barriers and pursue leadership roles.\r\n3. Increased Visibility of Women’s Achievements – Highlighting successful women across various fields through awards, showcases, and media coverage to inspire others.\r\n', 'To effectively perform the activity, the process begins with forming an organizing committee consisting of teachers and student representatives to oversee the event. Clear objectives and themes are set (e.g., promoting creativity or awareness on specific issues). Detailed guidelines are created for each competition, including rules on format, word limits, design requirements, and judging criteria. Promotion of the event is done through announcements, flyers, and digital platforms to encourage participation. Judges are selected, and evaluation criteria are clearly communicated to ensure fairness. Finally, winners are awarded based on creativity, adherence to the theme, and overall quality.', '1 month', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '15414.00', '', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2540, 'School Improvement Plan (SIP) Review and Enhancement', 'To update and align SIP with current needs and SBM standards', 'Revised and approved SIP', 'Data gathering, planning workshops, and consultations', 'September 2026', 'School Planning Team, Teachers, Stakeholders', '1700', 'Use school data and reports', 2026, 128926, 59, 12, 143),
(2541, 'Monitoring and Evaluation of SBM Practices', 'To assess effectiveness of SBM implementation', 'Monitoring reports and recommendations', 'Classroom observations, surveys, and document reviews', 'Quarterly (April - June, July-September 2026)', 'School Head, Master Teachers, SBM Coordinator', '1000', 'Continuous improvement focu', 2026, 128926, 59, 12, 143),
(2542, 'BASA-TALINO: Read, Reflect, Respond', '1.	Enhance Reading Comprehension Skills Learners will be able to identify main ideas, supporting details, and infer meaning from various texts appropriate to their grade level.\r\n2.	 Develop Critical Thinking Through Text Analysis Learners will analyz', '1.	 Improved Reading Comprehension Scores Learners will demonstrate increased proficiency in understanding texts through post-activity assessments, showing progress in identifying main ideas, details, and making inferences.\r\n2.	 Learner-Created Reading Journals or Reflection Logs Each participant will produce a personal reading journal or log containing summaries, vocabulary notes, and reflections on selected texts, showcasing engagement and comprehension.\r\n3.	Oral Reading Performance with Enhanced Fluency Learners will participate in a guided oral reading session, exhibiting improved fluency, pronunciation, and confidence in reading aloud.\r\n', 'To go about this activity, the following processes shall be observed:\r\n•  Guided Reading Sessions\r\nLearners read selected texts with the facilitator’s support..\r\n•  Interactive Text Discussions\r\nSmall group or whole-class discussions to explore themes, characters, and messages\r\n•  Reading Journals and Reflection Logs\r\nLearners maintain personal journals to summarize readings, note unfamiliar words, and reflect on insights.\r\nPromotes metacognition and ownership of learning.\r\nFacilitators provide feedback to guide improvement.\r\n•  Vocabulary and Fluency Drills\r\nUse word walls, flashcards, and context-based exercises to strengthen vocabulary.\r\nConduct timed oral reading practices to improve fluency and confidence.\r\nIntegrate peer reading and echo reading techniques.\r\n•  Performance-Based Tasks\r\nLearners present book reviews, dramatizations, or visual interpretations of texts.\r\nEncourages creativity, comprehension, and public speaking skills.\r\nTasks are tailored to learners’ interests and abilities\r\n', 'School Year - round', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '106950.00', 'Continuous improvement focus', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2543, 'Resource Mobilization Program', 'To generate resources to support school programs and projects', 'Increased funds and in-kind donations', 'Partnership building, fundraising activities, proposal writing', 'Whole Year', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA, Community Partner', '2500.00', 'Transparency is essential', 2026, 128926, 59, 12, 143),
(2544, 'Development and Validation of Contextualized Learning Materials', '1. Enable teachers to design and implement contextualized learning materials responsive to learners\' needs, interests, and local culture.\r\n2. Strengthen instructional relevance and learner engagement through localized content.', '1. Validated and pilot-tested contextualized materials \r\n2.  Documented LAC Sessions highlighting best practices and reflections\r\n2. Compilation of learner feedback and improvement reports', '1. Continue development of localized modules aligned with curriculum standards\r\n2. Conduct peer review validation through SLAC Sessions.\r\n3. Integrate community culture, language and experiences into learning materials\r\n4. Gather learner feedback and adjust materials based on performance data\r\n5. Document processes and share outputs during SLAC and SBM review meetings', 'Monthly', 'Teachers, SLAC Facilatator', '13000.00', 'Sustain the development and refinement of contextualized learning materials throughout the school year. Ensure integration of community culture and learner feedback to enhance and effectiveness.', 2026, 129041, 59, 12, 147),
(2545, 'Conduct of Remedial and Enhancement Classes for NAT', 'Improve learners’ mastery of competencies.', 'Increased learner performance', 'Small group instruction; differentiated teaching; peer tutoring', 'WHOLE YEAR ROUND', 'Teachers', '2,500.00', 'Focus on struggling learners', 2026, 204530, 58, 12, 39),
