(2548, 'Kulminasyon ng Pagdiriwang sa Buwan ng Wika', 'Layunin ng Buwan ng Wika 2026 ang sumusunod:\r\n     a. Ganap na maipatupad ang Panguluhang Proklamasyon Blg. 1041; \r\n     b. Maiangat ang kamalayan ng mga mamamayang Pilipino ukol sa wika at kasaysayan nito;\r\n     c. Mahikayat ang iba’t ibang ahensiya', '1.Sariling Pag-unlad\r\n2. Pagdadamayan at Pakikipagkaisa\r\n3. Interaksiyong sosyal \r\n4. Pagbuo ng karakter\r\n5. Pakikipagkaibigan at pakikipag-ugnayan\r\n6. Habambuhay na mga Alaala\r\n', 'Ang tagapangasiwa ay makikipag-ugnayan sa mga guro, Supreme Secondary Learner Government (SSLG), Barkada Kontra Droga (BKD), Math Club Officers and Youth for Environment in Schools Organization (YES-O) ng paaralan na makilahok mula sa pagpaplano hanggang sa pagsasagawa ng mga gawain. Ang mga mag-aaral ay inaasahang aktibong makikilahok sa nasabing programa hanggang sa matapos ito.', '1 day (7:40-12:00/1:00-4:30)', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '5455.00', '', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2549, 'Strengthening School-Community Partnerships', 'To build strong collaboration between school and community', 'Established partnerships and signed MOA with stakeholders', 'Conduct meetings with LGU, NGOs, and community leaders', 'June–July 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, LGU Officials, Communi', '2000.00', 'Continuous monitoring.', 2026, 204530, 58, 12, 39),
(2550, 'Recognition &Graduation Awards JHS/SHS ', 'This end-of-the-school year rites aim to commemorate the academic achievement of students, particularly, these seek to: \r\n1.	Recognize the educational accomplishment of students;\r\n2.	Acknowledge the students’ transition to another phase of the educat', 'At the end of the end-of-the school year rites, it is expected that:\r\n1. Students would have received diplomas and certificates, medals, and other forms of recognition   \r\n2. Students would have been sent to the next educational level\r\n3. Parents, stakeholders, and school personnel would have gathered to create a strong community\r\n', 'To go about this activity, the following processes shall be observed:\r\n1. Conduct of Homeroom PTA Meetings\r\n- Within the month of April, parents shall be called for a meeting and be informed on the schedule of graduation/completion, things to prepare. They shall also be asked to suggest or recommend activities/preferences on the conduct of the activity, given that it still follows the measures provided by the department.\r\n2. Conduct of Practices\r\n        -Graduation/Completion rites practices shall be done from May 6-28, 2024. This shall be facilitated and supervised by the class advisers.\r\n      3. Canvass/Purchase of Necessary Materials\r\n	- ADAS, Class advisers, and the administration shall work together to canvass and purchase all necessary materials (diploma/certificates, medals, ribbons, etc.) \r\n      4. Create Committees\r\n	-To ensure that the activity shall run smoothly, the school personnel shall be assigned to different committees (decoration, food preparation, hall preparation, etc.)\r\n', 'Two (2) day', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '82605.00', '', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2552, 'Establishment and Operationalization of the School Governance Council (SGC)', '1. To gather stakeholders and organize SGC that promote shared leadership\r\n2. To strengthen stakeholder participation in school decision-making', '1. Officially recognized SGC\r\n2. Approved SGC Constitution and By-Laws (CBL)\r\n3. School Improvement Plan (SIP) aligned with SGC inputs\r\n4. Documented meetings and resolutions', '1. Conduct orientation on SGC roles, functions, and legal bases\r\n2. Identify internal and external stakeholders\r\n3. Elect or appoint representatives from various sectors\r\n4. Develop Constitution and By-Laws\r\n5. Conduct regular meetings\r\n6. Engage SGC in SIP, AIP, and school programs', 'June - August 2026', 'Principal, Head Teacher, Teachers’ League Pre', 'P10,000.00', '1. Ensure alignment with DepEd policies on School-Based Management (SBM).\r\n2. Encourage active participation and shared accountability among stakeholders.', 2026, 129099, 59, 12, 150),
(2554, 'Creation/Strengthening of School Governing Council (SGC)', ' Establish or reinforce participatory governance', 'Expected Outputs: Functional SGC with defined roles', 'Meetings, elections, planning sessions', 'June–July 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Community Leaders', '3000.00', 'Objectives achieved within the given timeframe.', 2026, 205024, 59, 12, 147),
(2555, 'Charting Paths to a Purposeful Future: Career Development Support Program 2026', 'The program will focus on enhancing students\' decision-making skills, career readiness, and understanding of labor market trends. This event is vital to help students align their academic pursuits with their career goals and equip them with the neces', '•	Increased student awareness of career options and opportunities.\r\n\r\n•	Better alignment of academic choices with future career goals.\r\n\r\n•	Improved decision-making skills and readiness for the world of work.\r\n\r\n•	Establishment of career guidance programs and resources in the school.\r\n\r\n•	Student outputs such as career plans and reflections on future goals\r\n', 'The following activities will be done during the one week program:\r\nCareer Orientation Seminars – Interactive talks by invited professionals and alumni highlighting various career paths and success stories.\r\n\r\nCareer Fair – Booths and exhibits featuring representatives from industries and higher education institutions.\r\n\r\nWorkshop on Resume Writing and Interview Skills – Practical sessions for developing job application skills with HR professionals.\r\n\r\nCareer Coaching Activity – Individual or group coaching sessions guiding students in career planning based on interests and strengths.\r\n\r\nSearch for Career Ambassador and Ambassadress 2025 – A contest to select student models exemplifying professionalism and purpose.\r\n\r\nPosting of Students’ Pictures in Career Attire – Visual displays promoting enthusiasm for chosen careers.\r\n\r\nParticipation in the Municipal CDSP Summit 2025 – Representation of the school in municipal-level contests, career coaching, and job fair organized by PESO.\r\n', '5 days', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '12305.00', '', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2558, 'Nutrition Month: Talent Leads to Excellence”', 'To celebrate the Nutrition month as per PD. No. 491 s. 1974\r\n2. To showcase the skills and talents of students in this institution.\r\n3. To select qualified students for the competition outside the school.\r\n', 'The Nutrition Month celebration was successful and the coaches selected qualified students to participate in the competition outside the school.', 'Nutrition month celebration is composed of series of activities from July 1-31, 2026. Below are the activities to be conducted during the nutrition month.\r\nJuly 1: Kick off Ceremony                                               July 28-31: Booth Making and Skills\r\nJuly 3: Gulay cooking per section                                                      Presentation\r\nJuly 3: Poster and Slogan Contest                                  July 31: Student and Parent Cooking\r\nJuly 7: Indigenous and Recyclable Decorations                               Tandem\r\nJuly 9: Landscaping Competition                                     July 31: Culmination Day\r\nJuly 10: Gulay cooking per section                                                Table Display\r\nJuly 15: Nutrition Feud                                                                   Mr. & Ms. Fit 2026\r\nJuly 17: Gulay cooking per section                                                Nutri-jingle Competition\r\nJuly 24: Gulay cooking per section\r\n', '1 MONTH', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '111525.00', '', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2559, 'Development and management of a functional library ', 'To establish a well-organized library with adequate learning resources that is accessible to all learners and personnel', 'A school library should have adequate and updated books and conducive learning area.', 'Repair / renovate  a room and transform it into a library\r\nConduct inventory of books and other learning resources\r\nAcquire new books through partnership with stakeholders  ', 'Year Round', 'School Head,  Reading Coordinators, Teachers ', '8000', 'A functional library becomes a source of knowledge especially for learners. It encourages learners to explore and develop reading habits and literacy skills. It also provides a conducive learning environment  and serves as resource center for all. ', 2026, 129151, 59, 12, 151),
(2560, 'School Numeracy Intervention (Early Language Literacy and Numeracy)', '1.   This Communication Arts Festival aims to showcase the communication skills and the students’ ability to integrate language to other activities, particularly, this seeks to: \r\n•	Provide a platform for students to showcase their communication skil', 'At the end of the CommArts Fest, it is expected that:\r\n1. Students would have showcased their language and communication skills\r\n2. Students would have integrated their language and communication skills with other 21st century skills \r\n3. The school community would have valued the spirit of cultural awareness, social responsibility, and cooperation achieving  common goals.\r\n', 'To go about this activity, the following processes shall be observed:\r\n1. Planning Conference\r\n- English teachers will conduct planning conference for the activities that will be conducted. Teachers will be assigned to different committees.\r\n\r\n2. Choosing Participants to Different Activities\r\n        -English teachers and/or classroom advisers shall choose the participants in different activities. They shall start training/practicing for the different competitions.\r\n\r\n      3. Preparing Programs, Medals, Certificates, and Other Materials\r\n	- All the necessary documents, certificates and other materials shall be prepared for the conduct of the different contesting events and closing program.\r\n', '2 weeks', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '7470.00', '', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2561, 'School Improvement Plan (SIP) Review and Updating', 'Align school goals with current needs', 'School Improvement Plan (SIP) Review and Updating', 'Workshop, data analysis, collaborative planning', 'July 2026', '', '3000.00', 'Program implemented effectively with minimal challenges encountered.', 2026, 205024, 59, 12, 147),
(2562, 'Organize and Strengthen School Governance Council (SGC)', 'To establish a functional SGC with defined roles and responsibilities.', 'Organized SGC; SGC Resolution.', 'Orientation; Election of Officers; Workshop', 'June -July 2026', 'School Head, SPTA President, Barangay Officia', '1500.00', '', 2026, 129028, 59, 12, 147),
(2563, 'Library-Book Protected', '1.	To enhance the aesthetic appeal and functionality of the school ibrary, ensuring it becomes more conducive environment for both students and learners.\r\n2.	To protect the library resources by covering books withplastic cellophane before distributio', 'A.	Improved Library Aesthetic: The library will have an enhanced visual appeal with a more organized and inviting layout, making it a more comfortable space for students and teachers.\r\nB.	Functional Design: The library\'s design will be optimized for better accessibility and flow, allowing users to easily navigate and access resources.\r\nC.	Preserved Library Resources: Books and other materials will be covered with plastic cellophane, ensuring better preservation, prolonged usage, and increased availability of resources   for the school community.\r\n\r\n', '•	Assessment and Planning: Conduct a preliminary assessment of the library’s current condition, including its layout, resources, and aesthetic appeal. Formulate a detailed plan outlining the necessary improvements, including design changes and book preservation needs.\r\n•	Resource Gathering: Collect materials needed for the project, such as plastic cellophane for book covering, new shelves or furniture (if needed), organizational supplies, and decorative items to enhance the library’s appearance.\r\n•	Book Preservation: Organize a team to cover all books and important resources with plastic cellophane. This step will protect the books from wear and tear, prolonging their usability.\r\n•	Library Reorganization: Rearrange bookshelves, furniture, and reading areas to create a more functional and accessible layout. Ensure that the new design supports easy navigation and fosters a more engaging learning atmosphere.\r\n•	Final Inspection and Feedback: Conduct a final review of the revamped library. Gather feedback from students and teachers regarding the improvements, and make adjustments as needed to further enhance the library\'s usability and appeal\r\n', '2 weeks', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '6125.00', '', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2564, 'End of the School Year Rites (EOSY)', 'To successfully conduct the End of School Year (EOSY) Rites that recognize the achievements, growth, and completion of learners in a meaningful and organized manner.', 'Strengthened collaboration and support between the school, parents, and community.\r\nEnhanced sense of pride, discipline, and responsibility among learners.', 'systematic and collaborative approach', '4th Quarter of the School Year', 'All Stakeholders', '10000', 'Consistently and successfully conducted in accordance with DepEd Orders.', 2026, 129147, 59, 12, 151),
(2565, 'Capacity Building for Teachers on SBM Practices', 'Enhance teacher competencies in SBM implementation', 'Trained teachers; training certificates', 'Training sessions, coaching, mentoring', 'August 2026', 'Trainers, Teachers, School Head', '3000.00', 'Strong collaboration observed among school and community stakeholders.', 2026, 205024, 59, 12, 147);
INSERT INTO `sgod_action_plan` (`id`, `activity`, `objective`, `ex_output`, `metho_strategy`, `time_frame`, `person_involved`, `bud_req`, `remarks`, `fy`, `school_id`, `division`, `region`, `district`) VALUES
(2566, 'Building the Basics: Mastering the Fundamentals of Journalism', '1. Introduce participants to the core principles and practices of journalism, including news writing, research, interviewing, and ethical reporting.\r\n2. To develop the communication skills of novice writers, enabling them to express ideas clearly, re', '1.	 A Completed News Article Draft\r\nEach participant will produce at least one original straight news article, following proper structure (lead, body, conclusion) and applying the principles of factual, ethical reporting.\r\n2.	A Portfolio of Journalism Exercises\r\nParticipants will compile outputs from various training activities, including news lead writing, headline creation, source evaluation, and mock interviews.\r\n3.	Peer and Self-Evaluated Works\r\nParticipants will engage in peer editing and self-assessment, helping them understand how to improve their own writing and give constructive feedback to others.\r\n4.	Participation in a Mini Journalism Contest or Simulation (\"Journalympics\")\r\nParticipants will take part in a friendly, skills-based activity or competition where they apply what they’ve learned in a real-time writing or reporting challenge.\r\n5.	Certificate of Participation and Recognition\r\nTo acknowledge their learning and participation, students will receive a certificate they can include in their academic or extracurricular records.\r\n', 'To go about this activity, the following processes shall be observed:\r\n1. Conducting a planning conference\r\n- SPAs and coaches will conduct planning conference for the training and activities that will be conducted. Teachers will be assigned to different committees.\r\n2. Securing approval of the activity\r\n- A formal proposal will be submitted to the school head, PSDS, and relevant authority for review and approval, in compliance with institutional guidelines.\r\n3. Carrying out information dissemination and campaign\r\n	– Announcements, posters, and digital notices will be distributed to inform and encourage 	participation among the students.\r\n      4. Preparing training materials and resources\r\n	– All necessary materials such as handouts, activity sheets, presentations, and evaluation tools will 	be developed and finalized before the event.\r\n', 'SIX (6) DAYS ', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '127770.00', 'Use school data and reports', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2567, 'The school monitors and evaluates its programs, projects and activities.', 'To conduct orientation on different tools for monitoring and evaluation of the implemented programs, activities and projects.', 'Oriented and monitored  implemented programs, activities and projects.', 'Orientation on different tools for monitoring and evaluation of the implemented programs, activities and projects.', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Accounting personnel, teachers a', '10000', 'Constant orientation and monitoring of all implemented programs, activities and projects through SMEA.', 2026, 304311, 61, 12, 7),
(2568, '1.2 Integrate topics in PEACE and DepEd Core Values in lesson plans.', '1.2 To promote the essence of PEACE and DepEd Core values to learners.', 'Lesson Plan, COT with TA Form in Pre and Post Observation Conference.', 'Checking Lesson Plans,\r\nConducting CO with TA in Pre and Post Observation Conference.\r\n', 'June, 2026 to March, 2027', 'School Head, MT’s,  Teachers', '500.00', 'Learners are potent players in promoting  PEACE and DepEd core values in the school community. ', 2026, 204520, 58, 12, 37),
(2569, 'Improving classroom ventilation through installation of ceiling fans', 'Create a conducive learning environment by ensuring proper airflow and reducing heat stress', 'All classrooms equipped with adequate ventilation; improved student focus and reduced absenteeism', 'Conduct needs assessment; coordinate with LGU,  SPTA, DASURECO and other stakeholders  for funding; phased installation and repair; monitor classroom conditions quarterly', 'June–August 2025', 'School head,  Teachers, SPTA officers, LGU en', '29750', 'Supports DepEd’s initiative for safe and learner-friendly school environments', 2026, 316009, 59, 12, 143),
(2570, 'Community Partnership and Engagement Program', 'Strengthen school-community collaboration', 'Active partnerships; MOAs signed', 'Meetings, outreach programs', 'September 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Barangay Officials', '3000.00', 'Outputs delivered as planned and aligned with SBM goals.', 2026, 205024, 59, 12, 147),
(2571, 'Reading interventions to frustration level learners', '1.	Promote Literacy\r\n2.	Encourage a Love for Reading\r\n3.	Highlight the Importance of Books\r\n4.	Foster Community Engagement\r\n5.	Support Educational Development \r\n6.	Celebrate Diversity in Literature', '1.	Increased Reading Engagement\r\n2.	Enhanced Literacy Skills\r\n3.	Positive Attitudes Toward Reading\r\n4.	Diverse Literary Exploration\r\n5.	Enhanced Literacy Resources\r\n6.	Community Engagement\r\n', 'The proponent will follow the following methodology for the activity implemetation\r\n   Form a Committee: - Assemble a team of volunteers, librarians, teachers, and community members to oversee the planning and execution of the parade.\r\n\r\nb. Set Objectives: - Define clear goals for the parade, such as increasing reading engagement, fostering community spirit, and celebrating literary characters.\r\n\r\nc. Determine Scope: - Decide on the scale of the event, including the target audience (e.g., children, families, or the entire community), the location, and the duration of the parade.\r\n\r\nd. Create a Timeline: - Develop a detailed schedule with key milestones, such as planning meetings, promotion deadlines, and the event day.\r\n', 'Month – long activity', 'Students/ Participants for the various events', '20300.00', '', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2572, 'Conduct School Planning Workshop', 'To formulate initial comprehensive School Improvement Plan (SIP) for the next Cycle Years.', 'Prepared School Improvement Plan (SIP) for the next Cycle Years.', 'Workshop/FGD; Situational Analysis, Participatory Planning.', 'August-October 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, SGC, SPTA, LGU, SELG P', '3000.00', '', 2026, 129028, 59, 12, 147),
(2573, '\"PROJECT TEAM WORK”', '1.	To enhance Collaborative Planning among teachers to work together to develop and implement cohesive lesson plans that integrate diverse teaching methods and address the varying needs of students.\r\n2.	To improve Communication and Conflict Resolutio', '1.	Conducted Training for teamwork\r\n2.	Improved collaboration among teachers', 'The methodology for conducting training on teamwork and collaboration involves a blend of interactive activities, group discussions, and practical problem-solving tasks. Participants will engage in team-building exercises designed to enhance trust, communication, and cooperation. Case studies and role-playing scenarios will be used to address real-world challenges, encouraging collaborative decision-making. Reflective discussions will follow each activity to reinforce key concepts and promote self-awareness. By incorporating a mix of theory and hands-on experience, the training ensures practical application and lasting impact', '(2) DAYS ', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '20300.00', 'Continuous improvement focus', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
(2574, 'Brigada sa Eskwela sa Tagolilong ES', 'To prepare Tagolilong Elementary School for the opening of classes through a safe, clean, and conducive learning environment by engaging stakeholders in the spirit of volunteerism and collaboration.', 'A clean, safe, and fully prepared learning environment at Tagolilong Elementary School, with active participation from stakeholders, ready for the opening of classes.', 'collaborative “bayanihan” strategy', 'Every Quarter of the School Year.', 'All Stakeholders', '500', 'Participated by all possible partners in education such private, LGU, BLGU, and parents.', 2026, 129147, 59, 12, 151),
(2575, '“One School, One Family: Fostering Unity and Shared Responsibility”', '1.	To promote active parental and family involvement in school programs and learner development.\r\n2.	To enhance communication and collaboration among learners, parents/guardians, teachers, and school staff.\r\n3.	To instill positive family and social v', 'Personal Growth\r\n2. Leadership Skills\r\n3. Teamwork and Collaboration\r\n4. Outdoor Skills\r\n5. Social Interaction\r\n6. Character Building\r\n7. Friendships and Camaraderie\r\n8. Life-long Memories\r\n9. Sense of Achievement\r\n10. Physical Fitness\r\n', 'The proponent will tap the Supreme Secondary Learner Government (SSLG), Barkada Kontra Droga (BKD), Math Club Officers and Youth for Environment in Schools Organization (YES-O) in the school to participate the planning and be included as the working committee together with the PTA officers who will be participating. The students will be encouraged to participate in the said activity.\r\nThe participating parents, SSLG, BKD,WATCH, Math club officers and YES-O will be grouped and assigned to different committee to serve until the end of the activity\r\n', '(1) DAY ', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '62630.00', '', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
