(2602, 'Strengthening School Governance through Evaluation', '1.	To assess the level of implementation of the School-Based Management (SBM) system across all school governance dimensions—curriculum and teaching, learning environment, leadership, governance and accountability, human resource and team development', '1.	Conducted SBM evaluation\r\n2.	Verified and validated SBM assessment results indicating the school’s current level\r\n', 'The program begins with an orientation to familiarize stakeholders with the goals, process, and indicators of the SBM Evaluation. The SBM Working Committee will be organized, and evaluation tools and templates will be prepared. Data gathering follows, where documents and evidences are collected and reviewed based on the six SBM dimensions. The school then conducts the evaluation using the SBM assessment tool, followed by validation from district or division validators. Afterward, results and findings will be presented through an SBM Conference, highlighting strengths and areas for improvement. Finally, a Post-Evaluation Action Plan will be developed and integrated into the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) to guide continuous improvement efforts.', '(1) DAY', 'Teaching Personnel (Teacher I-III, MT I-IV, H', '12545.00', '', 2026, 304284, 59, 12, 143),
