(3028, 'Grade 3 learners achieve proficiency level for each cluster of early language literacy and numeracy skills', '1. Improve Grade 3 learners’ reading proficiency\r\n2. Enhance numeracy skills of learners\r\n3. Strengthen delivery of literacy and numeracy instruction\r\n4. Integrate literacy and numeracy across subjects\r\n5. Enhance teachers’ capacity in teaching liter', '1. 80–90% of learners reach proficiency level in reading\r\n2. 80–90% of learners achieve proficiency in numeracy\r\n3. Improved learner performance across varied ability levels\r\n4. Learners demonstrate skills in multiple contexts\r\n5. Teachers demonstrate improved strategies in teaching\r\n6. Availability and utilization of materials in class\r\n7. Data shows continuous improvement in learner performance\r\n8. Increased parental involvement and learner support\r\n9. Decrease in number of non-proficient learners', '1. Conduct daily structured reading sessions (phonics, comprehension, fluency)\r\n2. Implement daily numeracy drills and problem-solving activities\r\n3. Utilize differentiated instruction and contextualized learning materials\r\n4. Conduct cross-curricular activities (e.g., reading in Math, counting in English tasks)\r\n5. Conduct LAC sessions, INSET, and peer coaching\r\n6. Develop and reproduce reading materials, worksheets, and manipulatives\r\n7. Conduct baseline, midline, and endline assessments\r\n8. Conduct parent orientation and reading/numeracy support programs at home\r\n9. Implement remediation programs (pull-out sessions, tutoring, peer support)', '1. June-March, Quarterly, Monthly', 'Adviser, ARAL Tutors, School Head', '5000', '', 2026, 128973, 60, 12, 26),
(3029, 'Grade 6 learners achieve proficiency level in all 21st Century Skills and Core Learning Areas in the National Achievement Test (NAT)', '1. Identify learning gaps of Grade 6 learners in a multigrade context\r\n2. Improve mastery in core learning areas\r\n3. Strengthen critical thinking, collaboration, communication, creativity\r\n4. Track Grade 6 NAT readiness in a shared classroom setup\r\n5', '1. Baseline data on Grade 6 performance established\r\n2. Targeted remediation plan prepared\r\n3. Improved engagement and participation\r\n4. Learners show increased mastery\r\n5. Improved test scores\r\n6. Demonstrated 21st century skills\r\n7. Completed learner projects\r\n8. Improved quarterly scores\r\n9. Reduced least-mastered skills\r\n10. Availability of self-learning materials\r\n11. Increased parent support at home\r\n12. Stakeholder contributions generated\r\n13. Continuous improvement in performance', '1. Conduct diagnostic assessment for Grade 6 learners while Grades 1–5 engage in independent/seatwork tasks\r\n2. Develop Individualized/Group Intervention Plan for Grade 6 learners\r\n3. Use differentiated instruction within multigrade grouping (small group instruction, peer tutoring)\r\n4. Rotational learning stations (teacher-led, peer-led, independent work)\r\n5. Conduct focused remediation sessions for Grade 6 before/after class or during free periods of other grade groups\r\n6. Use group tasks combining Grades 5 & 6 for cooperative learning activities\r\n7. Implement simple project-based learning integrated across grade levels\r\n8. Conduct quarterly assessment specifically for Grade 6 while other grades do independent tasks\r\n9. Provide item analysis and remediation per competency\r\n10. Develop reusable learning materials (modules, task cards, learning kits)\r\n11. Conduct parent orientation on home-based support for Grade 6 NAT preparation\r\n12. Mobilize community support for review materials and snacks during review sessions\r\n13. Conduct monthly monitoring of Grade 6 progress while managing multigrade classes', '1. June-March, Quarterly, Monthly', 'Adviser, ARAL Tutors, School Head', '5000', '', 2026, 128973, 60, 12, 26),
