(3170, 'Maintaining the accuracy of early langguage, literacy and numeracy skills', '-Strengthen Grade 3 learners’ proficiency in oral language, reading comprehension, writing, and numeracy.\r\n-Provide engaging, contextualized activities that build foundational skills.\r\n-Ensure learners achieve expected competency levels across langua', '-Improved learner performance in reading fluency, comprehension, and vocabulary.\r\n-Enhanced writing skills through structured and creative exercises.\r\n-Increased accuracy in basic mathematical operations and problem-solving.\r\n-Documented progress reports and assessment results showing proficiency gains.', '-Early Language: Story retelling, vocabulary charades, picture talk, oral news sharing.\r\n-Literacy: Shared reading, word sorts, sentence building, journal writing, comprehension games.\r\n-Numeracy: Math bingo, number line races, contextual story problems, skip counting songs, math journals.\r\n-Integrated Activities: Math storytelling, shopping role play, board games combining word and number challenges.\r\n-Use formative assessments to monitor progress.\r\n-Incorporate peer learning and group activities to encourage collaboration.', 'Throughout the school year', 'Teachers, Sch. Head, SBM coordinator, learner', 'Instructional materials from MOOE Budget and training sessions for teachers.', '-Continuous monitoring and evaluation are essential.\r\n-Activities should be adapted to learners’ diverse needs.\r\n-Collaboration between teachers and parents will reinforce learning at home.\r\n-Success indicators will be measured through improved literacy and numeracy test scores and classroom performance.', 2026, 137057, 58, 12, 40),
(3171, 'Quarterly monitors and evaluates its programs, projects, and activities', 'To assess the progress and effectiveness of school programs; to identify implementation gaps and provide immediate technical assistance or adjustments.', 'Quarterly M&E Reports; SMEA (School Monitoring and Evaluation Plan) accomplishment folders; and Adjusted Project Implementation Plans.', 'Conduct of School Monitoring, Evaluation, and Adjustment (SMEA) conferences; use of standardized M&E tools/checklists; and Focus Group Discussions (FGD) with program coordinators.', 'Every last week of the Quarter (Quarterly)', 'School Head, School M&E Coordinator, Program/', 'P5,000 - for printing of M&E tools, communication expenses, and light refreshments during the SMEA conference.', 'This activity is crucial for the Accountability and Continuous Improvement dimension of SBM, ensuring data-driven decision-making.', 2026, 137057, 58, 12, 40),
(3172, 'Maintaining the accuracy of early langguage, literacy and numeracy skills', '-Strengthen Grade 3 learners’ proficiency in oral language, reading comprehension, writing, and numeracy.\r\n-Provide engaging, contextualized activities that build foundational skills.\r\n-Ensure learners achieve expected competency levels across langua', '-Improved learner performance in reading fluency, comprehension, and vocabulary.\r\n-Enhanced writing skills through structured and creative exercises.\r\n-Increased accuracy in basic mathematical operations and problem-solving.\r\n-Documented progress reports and assessment results showing proficiency gains.', '-Early Language: Story retelling, vocabulary charades, picture talk, oral news sharing.\r\n-Literacy: Shared reading, word sorts, sentence building, journal writing, comprehension games.\r\n-Numeracy: Math bingo, number line races, contextual story problems, skip counting songs, math journals.\r\n-Integrated Activities: Math storytelling, shopping role play, board games combining word and number challenges.\r\n-Use formative assessments to monitor progress.\r\n-Incorporate peer learning and group activities to encourage collaboration.', 'Throughout the school year', 'Teachers, Sch. Head, SBM coordinator, learner', 'Instructional materials from MOOE Budget and training sessions for teachers.', '-Continuous monitoring and evaluation are essential.\r\n-Activities should be adapted to learners’ diverse needs.\r\n-Collaboration between teachers and parents will reinforce learning at home.\r\n-Success indicators will be measured through improved literacy and numeracy test scores and classroom performance.', 2026, 137070, 58, 12, 40),
(3173, 'Culture-sensitive activities', 'To promote inclusivity and respect for diverse cultural backgrounds among students and staff; to integrate indigenous and local knowledge into the school environment.', 'A school-wide \"Cultural Exchange Day\" event; updated localized lesson plans; and a published documentation of local community traditions and heritage.', 'Collaborative workshops with community elders; peer-led cultural presentations; and the integration of contextualized learning materials (MTB-MLE where applicable).', 'Quarter 2 - Quarter 3 (August to December)', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, Teachers, Paren', 'P5,000.00 - for materials, guest speaker honorariums, and refreshments.', 'This activity aligns with the \"School-Community Partnership\" dimension of SBM and ensures no learner is marginalized due to cultural identity.', 2026, 137057, 58, 12, 40),
(3174, 'Conduct Orientation on Strengthening Reading and Learning Resources', 'Improve access to reading and learning resources for Kindergarten to Grade 6 learners, particularly low-emerging and frustration level learners', '• Established classroom reading corners\r\n• Increased number of available contextualized reading materials', '• Develop teacher‑made and IP‑contextualized reading materials\r\n• Solicit book donations from stakeholders and partners\r\n• Organize reading corners in each classroom', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers, Barangay', '', 'Priority given to IP‑responsive and culture‑sensitive materials', 2026, 128672, 58, 12, 38),
(3175, 'Conduct needs-based Learning Action Cells and Learning & Development activities', 'To enhance teacher pedagogical skills based on identified professional gaps; to promote collaborative teaching strategies; and to improve overall learner performance through updated instructional methods.', 'Monthly LAC Session Reports; individual Professional Development Plans (PDP); and updated contextualized instructional materials.', 'Conduct of Training Needs Analysis (TNA); peer-to-peer coaching and mentoring; expert-led workshops; and collaborative lesson planning.', 'SY 2026-2027', 'School Head, LAC Coordinator, Master Teachers', 'P5,000.00- for training materials, office supplies, and technical resources.', 'This activity ensures continuous professional growth of staff, directly impacting the quality of classroom instruction and student achievement.', 2026, 137057, 58, 12, 40),
(3176, 'To install rainwater collector for functional school water facility.', 'To provide an alternative and sustainable water source for school gardening and toilet sanitation; to reduce water utility costs; and to promote environmental conservation awareness among learners.', 'Installed and operational rainwater harvesting system; maintenance schedule for the facility; and documented reduction in monthly water consumption.', 'Site identification and technical assessment; procurement of materials (drums, PVC pipes, filters); collaborative labor through \"Brigada Eskwela\" or community volunteers; and orientation of students on proper usage.', '3rd - 4th quarter (July-December)', 'School Head, School Facilities Coordinator, P', 'P32,000.00 - school MOOE funds or LGU grants.', 'This facility directly supports the WinS (Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene in Schools) program and contributes to a disaster-resilient school environment.', 2026, 137057, 58, 12, 40),
(3177, 'Launch enhanced Anti-Bullying Campaigns (posters, symposiums, role-playing activities)', 'Reduce and eliminate bullying incidents in school.', 'Increased awareness among learners, teachers, and parents on Child Protection and Anti-Bullying policies', 'Intensify awareness campaigns on Child Protection and Anti-Bullying policies.', 'Whole School Year (with quarterly monitori', 'School Head Guidance Counselor / Designated T', '5,000', 'Bullying prevention programs are implemented but need strengthening to achieve zero incidence.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38);
