(3192, 'Improve capacity to retain learners in school', 'To minimize absenteeism and drop-out cases', '1. Improved attendance rate\r\n2. Reduced dropouts', '1. Implementation of feeding program\r\n2. Engaging classroom activities\r\n3. Recognition/incentives for attendance', 'January 2026 to December 2026', 'School Head, Teachers & Parents', '1829.00', '', 2026, 128684, 106, 12, 134),
(3193, 'Strengthen schools’ capacity to ensure learners’ continuity to next stage', 'To support learners in completing grade level and transitioning to next stage', 'Increased promotion/completion rate', '1. Remediation programs\r\n2. Academic support\r\n3. Coordination with parents \r\n4. Guidance services', 'January 2026 to December 2026', 'Irah D. Guartero', '2724.00', '', 2026, 128684, 106, 12, 134),
(3194, 'Strengthen mechanisms for providing access to relevant opportunities for all school age children', 'To ensure inclusive and equitable access to education', '1. Increased participation of disadvantaged learners\r\n2. Inclusive programs implemented', '1. Collaboration with LGU/NGOs\r\n2. SPED support\r\n3. Flexible learning options', 'January 2026 to December 2026', 'School Head & All Teachers', '660.00', '', 2026, 128684, 106, 12, 134),
(3195, 'Conduct of School-Based Management (SBM) Self-Assessment and Strengthening of SBM Implementation through Stakeholder Engagement', 'To strengthen SBM implementation by utilizing SBM self-assessment results, improving school practices across SBM dimensions, and enhancing participatory governance through active engagement of the School Governance Council (SGC) and other stakeholder', 'Completed SBM Self-Assessment Tool with validated results; identified gaps and priority areas; enhanced School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) aligned with SBM indicators; documented stakeholder participation and SGC resolutions.', 'Conduct SBM orientation for school personnel and stakeholders; administer and validate the SBM Self-Assessment Tool; organize consultative meetings and planning workshops with the SGC; align SIP and AIP based on assessment results; implement, monitor, and evaluate programs using SBM indicators and continuous improvement mechanisms.', 'April 2026 - December 2026', 'School Head, Administrative Officer II, Teach', '3000', '', 2026, 239501, 106, 12, 133),
(3196, 'Review of Previous Year SBM Outcomes', 'To analyze the previous year’s results in order to identify strengths and areas for improvement.', 'A documented report outlining key performance indicators (KPIs) and a gap analysis.', 'Conduct reflection workshops with SBM Team and stakeholders; use first‑year M&E data', 'January 2026', 'School Head, SBM Team, Stakeholders', '2000', '', 2026, 129441, 61, 12, 16),
(3197, 'Re‑orientation of Stakeholders on DO 007 s. 2024', 'To reinforce understanding of School-Based Management (SBM) policies among key partners.', 'Summary of insights and updated commitment agreements', 'Conduct orientation sessions with Teachers, Parents, SPT on core SBM principles and continuous improvement', 'February 2026', 'School Head, SBM Focal, Stakeholder Represent', '3000', '', 2026, 129441, 61, 12, 16),
(3198, 'Strengthening SBM Committees & Functions', 'To ensure effective governance through clearly defined roles and responsibilities.', 'An updated SBM organizational structure with clearly defined roles and responsibilities.', 'Review and reassign committee roles; clarify responsibilities and functions via workshops', 'March 2026', 'SBM Team, Committee Chairs', '3000', '', 2026, 129441, 61, 12, 16),
(3199, 'Mid‑Year Self‑Assessment', 'To assess SBM practices at mid-year to guide necessary course corrections.', 'Completed self‑assessment checklist with action notes', 'SBM Team conducts self‑assessment with internal/external stakeholders', 'June 2026', 'SBM Team, Stakeholders', '2000', '', 2026, 129441, 61, 12, 16),
(3200, 'SIP Adjustment & Action Planning', 'To enhance and update the School Improvement Plan using assessment results as basis.', 'Revised SIP with SMART targets', 'Host planning workshop; assign responsibilities and timelines', 'July to August 2026', 'School Head, SBM Team, Stakeholders', '5000', '', 2026, 129441, 61, 12, 16),
(3201, 'Capacity Building: Leadership & Management', 'To strengthen leadership and promote participatory governance skills.', 'At least one training session delivered; post‑training evaluation report', 'Facilitate training for SBM Team and teachers on leadership, planning, and data use', 'September 2026', 'SBM Team, Teachers, External Trainer', '3000', '', 2026, 129441, 61, 12, 16),
(3202, 'Community Engagement & Feedback Mechanism', 'To enhance stakeholder participation and improve feedback mechanisms.', 'Quarterly stakeholder survey and focus group summary', 'Conduct quarterly consultations, surveys, FGDs with all stakeholder groups', 'Quarterly (March, June, September, December)', 'School Head, SBM Team, Stakeholders', '2000', '', 2026, 129441, 61, 12, 16),
(3203, 'Project \"DU-AW PAGPANGGA\" (Home Visitation)', 'To reach out to learners with irregular attendance and identify root causes.', '100% of at-risk learners visited; Signed intervention agreements.', 'Physical/Virtual Visits: Teachers & Brgy. Officials visit homes to discuss attendance barriers.', 'Monthly (Every 3rd Friday)', 'Class Advisers, Guidance Focal Person', '500.00', 'Priority for learners with 5+ days of absence.', 2026, 204516, 58, 12, 44),
(3204, 'Monitoring & Evaluation (Mid & Year‑end)', 'To monitor progress and identify challenges through the use of KPIs.', 'Mid‑year and year‑end M&E reports with performance metrics', 'Administer surveys, KPI tracking tools, feedback sessions, review meetings', 'Mid-year (June), Year-end (December)', 'M&E Team, SBM Team', '2000', '', 2026, 129441, 61, 12, 16),
(3205, 'Continuous Capacity Development Program', 'To maintain and strengthen internal SBM capabilities.', 'Ongoing webinars or coaching sessions; summary documentation', 'Conduct at least two refresher sessions or peer mentoring.', 'October to November 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, SBM Members', '3000', '', 2026, 129441, 61, 12, 16),
(3206, 'Recognition & Awards Ceremony (Year‑End)', 'To encourage stakeholder engagement and recognize good practices.', 'Organized ceremony with awardees and recognition cards', 'Design criteria; select recipients; hold celebratory event', 'December 2025', 'SBM Team, School Head, Stakeholders', '3000', '', 2026, 129441, 61, 12, 16),
(3207, 'Project \"Power-Up\" (Skills Swap)', 'To address individual needs through 1-on-1 mentoring.', 'Peer Coaching Log (Simple Checklist).', 'The Buddy System: Pairing teachers with opposite strengths (e.g., Tech-savvy + Master in Content).', 'Monthly Check-In\'s', 'All Teaching Personnel', '300.00', 'Turns workload into a team effort.', 2026, 204516, 58, 12, 44),
(3208, 'Contextualized MG-DLL\r\nDevelopment', 'To adapt K-6 curriculum for multigrade\r\nclasses in a flood-prone IP community.', 'Localized Daily Lesson Logs\r\n(DLL) with DRRM integration.', 'Collaborative planning sessions; LAC on\r\ncontextualization and indigenization.', 'Quarterly', ' School Head, MG Teachers', '12000.00', '', 2026, 128558, 57, 12, 108),
(3209, 'Project C.O.R.E. (Collaborative Oversight for Resilient Education)', 'Ensure active participation of stakeholders in governance', 'Functional SBM Team with defined roles', 'Regular meetings; role clarification; leadership training', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers, Communit', '2,000', 'Shared leadership', 2026, 204516, 58, 12, 44),
(3210, 'Project L.I.N.K. (Local Identification of Needs and Knowledge)', 'Identify priority needs with stakeholder involvement', 'Consolidated needs assessment report', 'Surveys, FGDs, community consultations', 'June to July,2026', 'SBM Team, Teachers, Parents', '1500', 'Inclusive planning', 2026, 204516, 58, 12, 44),
(3211, 'Project FLOOD (Waterproof\r\nModules)', 'To ensure learning continuity for\r\nstudents in remote sitios during\r\nflooding.', 'Procurement of plastic bins/zip locks for\r\nmodules; sitio delivery.', 'Pre-positioning of materials in \"Sitio Learning\r\nHubs\"; Use of Modular Distance Learning Modalities.', 'Jun-Oct', 'Teachers, Parents, LGU', '25000.00', '', 2026, 128558, 57, 12, 108),
(3212, 'The school has a functional school-based ALS program.', '1.Identify and enroll out-of-school youth (OSY) and adults in IP community\r\n2. Deliver contextualized and culture-responsive ALS instruction\r\n3. Provide appropriate and localized learning materials \r\n4. Strengthen teacher/implementer competence in AL', '1. Increased number of ALS enrollees (at least 20% increase)\r\n2. 80% attendance rate; learners actively participate\r\n3. Availability of localized learning materials\r\n4. Improved teaching strategies observed\r\n5. 75% retention rate of ALS learners\r\n6. At least 60% pass rate in A&E\r\n7. Active stakeholder participation\r\n8. Timely reports and program adjustments', '1. Conduct community mapping and survey- Coordinate with tribal leaders and barangay officials- Advocacy campaign (house-to-house, assemblies)\r\n2. Develop weekly learning sessions (flexible schedule)- Integrate IP culture, traditions, and local knowledge in lessons- Use multigrade strategies\r\n3. Develop/collect Indigenous Knowledge-based materials- Utilize ALS modules and contextualize content- Partner with stakeholders for materials support\r\n4. Attend ALS and IPED trainings- Conduct LAC sessions focused on ALS strategies- Peer coaching among teachers\r\n5. Conduct home visits for at-risk learners- Provide guidance and counseling- Set up peer support groups\r\n6. Conduct regular formative assessments- Review sessions before A&E test- Mock exams\r\n7. Engage LGU, NGOs, and IP leaders- Conduct regular meetings and reporting- Resource mobilization\r\n8. Monthly monitoring of classes- Quarterly program review- Feedback from learners and community', 'Whole year, monthly, quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers, ALS Focal', '5000', '', 2026, 128973, 60, 12, 26),
(3213, 'Operation \"Safe Haven\"', 'To maintain a flood-resilient and child-friendly school environment.', 'Elevated pathways and hazard-free classrooms.', 'Regular school grounds maintenance via\r\nBrigada Eskwela; Hazard mapping with pupils.', 'Year-round', 'SDRRM Team, PTA, Pupils', '45000.00', '', 2026, 128558, 57, 12, 108),
(3214, 'Project A.L.I.G.N.\r\n(Active Linkage for Integrated Governance and Networks)', 'Align School Improvement Plan with SBM principles', 'Updated SIP with stakeholder inputs', 'Planning workshop; data-based decision-making', 'July,2026', 'School Head, SBM Team, Stakeholders', '500', 'Key Level 2 indicator', 2026, 204516, 58, 12, 44),
(3215, 'Project E.X.E.L. (Executing eXcellence for Enhanced Learning)', 'To ensure all school projects are executed on time and achieve their goals.', 'Completed activities; progress reports', 'The \"Check-Point\" System: Instead of waiting for the end of the year, the team holds monthly \"Sprint Checks\" to see which programs need more support.', 'Whole Year Round', 'School Head,Teachers, SBM Team, Stakeholders', '2,000', 'Core SBM function', 2026, 204516, 58, 12, 44),
(3216, 'The school has special education and PWD-friendly facilities', '1. To ensure accessibility of school facilities for learners with disabilities\r\n2. To improve physical access for PWD learners\r\n3. To make classrooms inclusive and learner-friendly\r\n4. To provide assistive learning materials\r\n5. To strengthen teacher', '1. Accessibility needs identified and documented\r\n2. At least 1 ramp and basic access structures installed\r\n3. Classrooms adapted for diverse learners\r\n4. Availability of SPED support materials\r\n5. Teachers trained on inclusive strategies\r\n6. Active participation and resource support', '1. Conduct accessibility audit of school buildings and pathways\r\n2. Install ramps, handrails, and PWD-friendly pathways\r\n3. Arrange SPED-friendly seating, lighting, and learning corners\r\n4. Procure visual aids, large print materials, and basic assistive tools\r\n5. Conduct training on SPED and inclusive education\r\n6. Engage PTA, LGU, and donors for support', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, SNED Focal, Teachers', '10000', '', 2026, 128973, 60, 12, 26),
(3217, 'WASH in Schools (WinS)\r\nEnhancement', 'To provide clean water and sanitation\r\ndespite remote location.', 'Functioning handwashing\r\nstations with water filtration.', 'Community \"Bayanihan\" for water system\r\nrepair; Health education integration.', 'Quarter 1', 'WinS Coordinator, Brgy. Health Worker/s', '15000.00', '', 2026, 128558, 57, 12, 108),
(3218, 'SGC Re-activation &\r\nEmpowerment', 'To strengthen the School Governing\r\nCouncil\'s role in far-flung school\r\nmanagement.', 'Active SGC with clearly defined\r\nroles and regular meetings.', 'SGC Induction and Training; Monthly\r\nconsultative meetings with stakeholders.', 'Quarter 1', 'School Head, Community Leaders', '2500.00', '', 2026, 128558, 57, 12, 108),
(3219, 'Project LEAD (Local Educators\'\r\nAction)', 'To foster shared leadership among\r\nmultigrade teachers.', 'Teachers leading specific SBM\r\npillars and community outreach.', 'Mentoring and coaching; Designation of focal\r\npersons per SBM dimension.', 'Year-round', 'School Head, Teachers', '7500.00', '', 2026, 128558, 57, 12, 108),
(3220, 'Conduct school-based orientation with internal and external stakeholders about DepEd Order No. 007, s.2024.', 'To conduct school-based orientation with internal & external stakeholders about the implementing guidelines of the revised SBM system', 'Accomplished attendance Sheet, Minutes of Meeting and School memorandum', 'Discussion & Sharing', '2nd week of June 2026', 'eachers & School Principal', '500.00', '', 2026, 502246, 61, 12, 13),
(3221, 'The school has a functional School Governance Council (SGC)', '1. To ensure the formal organization of a functional School Governance Council\r\n2. To define roles, functions, and responsibilities of SGC members\r\n3. To ensure active participation and collaborative decision-making\r\n4. To strengthen participatory sc', '1. SGC is formally organized with complete composition\r\n2. Approved CBL and clear TOR per member\r\n3. At least 4 functional meetings conducted per year\r\n4. SGC actively participates in planning and approval\r\n5. Increased support (cash/kind/donations/projects)\r\n6. At least 2 monitoring activities conducted\r\n7. SGC members trained and oriented', '1. Organize/renew SGC membership (PTA, LGU, teachers, community leaders, stakeholders)\r\n2. Formulate SGC Constitution and By-Laws and operational guidelines\r\n3. Conduct regular SGC meetings (monthly/quarterly)\r\n4. Conduct consultation meetings for SIP/AIP and school priorities\r\n5. Initiate partnerships and resource generation activities\r\n6. Conduct SGC monitoring visits and evaluation of projects\r\n7. Attend training/orientation on SBM and school governance', 'Quartery, Whole Year', 'School Head, Teachers, SGC Members', '5000', '', 2026, 128973, 60, 12, 26),
(3222, 'Transparency Board Updating', 'To maintain public trust through\r\nfinancial and academic transparency.', 'Updated \"School Report Card\"\r\nand MOOE liquidation posts.', 'Regular posting of school accomplishments\r\nand fund utilization in the Brgy. Hall/School.', 'Monthly', 'School Head, SGC, PTA', '3000.00', '', 2026, 128558, 57, 12, 108),
(3223, 'Convene internal & external stakeholders for the conduct pre assessment using the SBM self-assessment checklist.', 'To assess the current situation of the school using the SBM self-assessment checklist in order to identify the SBM priority improvement area.', 'Accomplished SBM self-assessment checklist, Activity Design & Activity Completion Report', 'Discussion & Sharing', '3rd week of June 2026', 'eachers, School Principal & identified Parent', '2000', '', 2026, 502246, 61, 12, 13),
(3224, 'Incorporate results of SBM self-assessment in the AIP as identified improvement areas.', 'To integrate and prioritize those SBM indicators which not yet manifested or rarely manifested by the school.', 'Approved AIP, WFP & APP', 'Discussion & Workshop', 'November 2026', 'School Principal & School Planning Team', '1000', '', 2026, 502246, 61, 12, 13),
(3225, 'Assessing the Practice', 'Conduct Self-Assessment on School-Based Management', 'Accomplished Self-Assessment on School-Based Management', 'Access the Assessment tool on MIS, Accomplish the Self-Assessment Tool', 'April 20, 2026', 'School Head, Department Heads', '500.00', '', 2026, 304316, 61, 12, 1),
