(3308, 'Project LibREAD: Establishing a Functional School Library', '1Resource Mobilization\r\n2.Physical Transformation\r\n3. Inventory & Classification\r\n4. Library Integration\r\n5. Literacy Programs\r\n', '1. Sufficient collection of storybooks, reference materials, and digital tools.\r\n2. A conducive, organized, and \"child-friendly\" library space.\r\n3. A systematic cataloging of all available reading materials.\r\n4. Scheduled \"Library Hours\" for every grade level.\r\n5. Increased reading comprehension scores among learners.', '1. \"Adopt-a-Shelf\" Program: Partner with alumni, NGOs, and local stakeholders for book donations.\r\n2. Implementation: Repainting, installing shelves, and creating a \"Reading Nook\" using localized materials.\r\n3. Dewey Decimal Simplified: Sorting books by genre/level and creating a digital or manual logbook.\r\n4. Curriculum Mapping: Embedding library visits into the English and Filipino weekly schedules.\r\n5. \"Read-a-Thon\" & Storytelling: Monthly contests and peer-tutoring sessions (Big Brother/Sister Read).', 'June 2026-March 2027, ', 'School Head, Adopt-a-School Coordinator,  Sch', '₱20000', 'The establishment of the Biao Elementary School Library will give a positive impact not only for school but for the learners. By leveraging community involvement (Stakeholders) and aligning with DepEd literacy goals,  the school plans to create a sustainable environment that directly addresses reading gaps. ', 2026, 128963, 60, 12, 27),
