(3321, 'Cake making and decorating skills enhancement activity anchored on the technolympics  2025', 'To enhance participants proficiency in baking techniques, creativity and presentation. encourage the application of theoretical knowledge in a practical setting. To foster confidence, professionalism,  and time management skills as they showcase thei', 'Learner demonstrate improve cake baking and decorating skills. increased readiness and competitivness of students for the technolympics. Production of safe high quality and well presented  baked products. Documented outputs (photos, evaluation sheets , sample products ) for school records.', 'Preparation and orientation, Hands on training, Skill enhancement, Monitoring and evaluation, showcase and documentations.', 'November 21-26, 2025', 'Selected techpro students from grade 11 quart', '2400.00', 'Conducted as per schedule', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3322, 'PROJECT LUPAD: Leading Universal Progress through Alternative Delivery', '1. Advocacy & Social Mobilization\r\nTo inform the community about the newly established ALS program.\r\n2. Learner Profiling & Assessment\r\nTo identify the literacy level and learning needs of enrollees.\r\n3.Program Operationalization\r\nTo deliver standard', '1. Increased awareness; list of potential Out-of-School Youths and Adults (OSYA).\r\n2.  Accomplished Functional Literacy Test (FLT) results and Individual Learning Agreements (ILA).\r\n3. Conduct of weekly learning sessions for Basic Literacy and A&E learners.\r\n4. Functional CLC equipped with basic furniture and learning resources.\r\n5. Monthly learner progress reports and updated Presentation Portfolios.', '1. Conduct house-to-house literacy mapping and community advocacy campaigns in Sitio Biao, Pinalpalan.\r\n2. Administration of the revised FLT and Assessment for Basic Literacy (ABL)\r\n3. Implementation of flexible learning modes (face-to-face, blended, or distance).\r\n4. Partnership with the Local School Board (LSB) and Local Government Unit (LGU).\r\n5. Regular review of the ILA and conduct of formative/summative assessments.', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'District Supervisor, School Head, Teachers, A', '25000', 'This action plan is a highly feasible and strategically sound roadmap that will effectively address the educational gap in sitio Biao, Pinalpalan by leveraging community partnerships and flexible learning delivery to ensure no learner is left behind.', 2026, 128963, 60, 12, 27),
