(3332, 'Enhancing School Leadership and Governance', '1. To strengthen the capacity of school heads and governing bodies in decision-making and resource management.\r\n2. To promote a shared vision and collaborative leadership within the school community.\r\n', '1 A clearly defined leadership structure and roles.\r\n2 Regularly held and effectively managed school board meetings.\r\n3 Development of a strategic school improvement plan.', '1 Conduct leadership training workshops for school heads and key personnel.\r\n2 Establish functional school governing councils with clear mandates.\r\n3 Implement participatory planning and decision-making processes.\r\n4 Develop and disseminate school policies and guidelines.', 'August 2026', 'School head, Teachers, PTA, SGC and Stakehold', '2000', 'Requires commitment from all stakeholders, including teachers, parents, and community members. Ongoing professional development is crucial.', 2026, 108926, 58, 12, 0),
(3333, 'Senior high school Science Day Challenge', 'To enhance students  understanding of scientific concepts and application  in daily life.\r\nTo provide opportunities for students to demonstrate their knowledge , creativity, and critical thinking through various activities , exhibits and compititions', 'Students actively demonstrate knowledge, creativity, and critical thinking.\r\nSuccessful exhibits and competitions showcasing STEM skills.\r\nStrengthened collaboration and teamwork among Senior high school learners.\r\nRecognition of outstanding projects and performances\r\nDocumented results , photos and evaluation reports for school records.', 'Orientation and Preparation\r\nHands on Activities\r\nCompetition and Presentation\r\nCoaching and mentoring\r\nMonitoring and Documentation', 'September 29, 2025', 'Senior high school students and science teach', '2500.00', '', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3334, 'Improving Curriculum and Instruction Delivery.', '1 To align the curriculum with local needs and national standards.\r\n2 To enhance the quality of teaching and learning through innovative pedagogical approaches.\r\n3 To ensure that assessment methods are fair, valid, and reliable.', '1 Contextualized curriculum materials.\r\n2 Improved student engagement and learning outcomes.\r\n3 A robust system for monitoring and evaluating student progress.', '1Curriculum review and adaptation workshops involving teachers.\r\n2Implementation of differentiated instruction and project-based learning.\r\n3Provision of professional development on effective teaching strategies.\r\n4Development and use of diverse assessment tools (formative and summative).', 'June 2026 - March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, and Students ', '3000', 'Teacher buy-in and adequate resources for instructional materials are essential for success.', 2026, 108926, 58, 12, 0),
(3335, 'Enhancing Community Engagement and Partnerships', '1 To foster strong relationships between the school and its community.\r\n2 To mobilize community support for school programs and initiatives.\r\n3 To ensure that the school is responsive to the needs of its stakeholders.\r\n', '1 Active participation of parents and community members in school activities.\r\n2 Established partnerships with local organizations and businesses.\r\n3 Increased community support for school improvement.', '1 Regular parent-teacher association meetings and school events.\r\n2 Creation of a school-community liaison committee.\r\n3 Volunteer programs involving community members.\r\n4 Seeking feedback from parents and community members on school performance.', 'June 2026 - March 2027', 'School head, Teachers, PTA, SGC and Stakehold', '1500', 'Consistent communication and mutual respect are key to building strong community partnerships.', 2026, 108926, 58, 12, 0),
(3336, 'Together we thrive: Reigniting our collective purpose ', 'To foster a thriving staff community by strengthening camaraderie and promoting sustainable, fulfilling teaching practices.\r\nTo Facilitate a reflective process for educators to re connect with their individual and shared purpose in the profession.\r\nT', 'Inspired and motivated personnel with renewed sense of purpose\r\nstrengthen culture of collaboration and mutual support.\r\ndocumented reflections and feedback for continuous improvement. ', 'Orientation and motivation.\r\nCollaborative Activities.\r\nEngagement and reflection. ', 'October 27, 2025', 'all MNCHS personnel', '20400.00', '', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3337, 'Monitoring, Evaluation, and Continuous Improvement', '1 To establish a system for regularly monitoring the implementation of the SBM plan.\r\n2 To evaluate the impact of SBM initiatives on school performance.\r\n3 To use data and feedback for continuous improvement.', '1 Regular progress reports on SBM implementation.\r\n2 Data-driven insights into school performance.\r\n3 Adjusted strategies and action plans based on evaluation finding', '1 Development of a monitoring and evaluation framework.\r\n2 Collection and analysis of performance data (academic, financial, operational).\r\n3 Regular review meetings to discuss progress and challenges.\r\n4 Feedback mechanisms for stakeholders.', 'November 2026, April 2027', 'School head, Teachers, PTA, SGC and Stakehold', '1000', 'A culture of continuous improvement should be embedded in the school\'s operations.', 2026, 108926, 58, 12, 0),
(3338, 'Capacity Building for School Personnel', '1. To equip teachers and staff with the necessary skills and knowledge for SBM.\r\n2. To foster a professional learning community within the school.', '1 Enhanced skills in areas such as instructional leadership, financial management, and community engagement.\r\n2 A more collaborative and supportive work environment.', '1 In-service training programs and workshops.\r\n2 Peer coaching and mentoring.\r\n3 Study visits to exemplary schools.', 'December 2026', 'School head and Teachers', '6000', 'Training should be needs-based and ongoing to ensure sustained development.', 2026, 108926, 58, 12, 0),
(3339, 'Science investigatory Project Fair. Exploring eco-friendly innovations.', 'To provide platform for students to apply scientific principles and methods in conducting investigatory projects related to real-world environmental issues.\r\nTo enhance science teaching learning process by showcasing students innovations through spec', '1. Students present eco-friendly investigatory projects applying scientific principles.\r\n2. Documented fair proceedings and evaluation results for SBM monitoring.', '1. Facilitate project development and mentoring sessions for Grade 8 S.T.E.  students.\r\n2. Conduct school-level fair with presentation, exhibits, and panel evaluation.', 'September 1 to October 24, 2025', 'Junior High School grade 8 STE students and s', '6000.00', '1. Activity promotes environmental awareness and scientific innovation among learners.\r\n2. Budget allocation ensures materials, logistics, and documentation are adequately supported. ', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3340, ' Developing a School Improvement Plan (SIP)', '1 To create a comprehensive roadmap for school development based on SBM principles.\r\n2 To set clear goals, targets, and strategies for achieving school improvement.', '1 A well-articulated and actionable 2 School Improvement Plan.\r\n3 Alignment of school activities with the SIP.', 'Conducting a thorough school self-assessment.\r\n1 Consultation with all stakeholders to identify priorities.\r\n2 Setting SMART (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound) goals.\r\n3 Assigning responsibilities and allocating resources for SIP implementation.', 'May 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Stakeholders ', '1500', 'The SIP should be a living document, reviewed and updated regularly.', 2026, 108926, 58, 12, 0),
(3341, 'Establishing a School Data Management System', '1 To collect, organize, and analyze relevant school data.\r\n2 To use data for informed decision-making and school improvement.', '1 A functional and accessible school data management system.\r\n2 Regular data reports for various stakeholders.', '1 Identifying key data indicators (student performance, attendance, resources, etc.).\r\n2 Selecting or developing appropriate data management tools.\r\n3 Training staff on data collection and management procedures.\r\n4 Establishing protocols for data analysis and reporting.', 'June 2026 - March 2027', 'School head, Teachers, PTA, SGC and Stakehold', '2000', 'Data privacy and security must be ensured.', 2026, 108926, 58, 12, 0),
(3342, 'Filipino Values Celebration: HEME: BAGONG PILIPINAS, BAGONG PAG-ASA . Pagkakaisa para sa makabuluhang pagbabago.', '1. To promote Filipino values emphasizing unity and positive societal change.\r\n2. To foster reflection on personal actions and their impact in contributing to meaningful change .\r\n3. To encourage active participation in initiatives to support social ', 'Active participation of students and teachers in values-centered activities.\r\n2.  Learners demonstrate understanding and practice of Filipino values aligned with the theme Bagong Pilipinas.\r\n3. Documented outputs ( reflections, presentations, exhibits ) showcasing unity and positive societal change.\r\n4. Strengthen integration of values education in both curricular and co-curricular  program.', '1. Organize values-based activities such as essay writing, poster-making, and role-playing.\r\n2. Facilitate classroom discussion and reflection sessions guided by values education teachers.\r\n3. Conduct department -led exhibits and presentations highlighting Filipino values.\r\n4. Encourage student-led initiatives that promote unity and responsible citizenship.\r\n5. Document activities through reports, photos, and and evaluation forms for SBM monitoring.', 'November 17-30,2025', 'Department heads, Values education Teachers a', '4920.00', 'Activity supports the natiional thrust of Bagong Pilipinas by instilling values of unity and transformation.\r\n2. Budget allocation ensures materials, logistics, and prizes are adequately supported.\r\n3. Outputs will be consolidated into reports for BM documentation and future planning.\r\n4. Expected to foster stronger apprecciation of Filipino identity and values among learners. ', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3343, 'Promoting a Positive School Culture', '1 To foster a safe, inclusive, and supportive learning environment.\r\n2 To promote positive values and behaviors among students and staff.', '1 Reduced instances of bullying and disciplinary issues.\r\n2 Increased student and staff morale.\r\n3 A strong sense of community and belonging.\r\n', '1 Implementing school-wide positive behavior support systems.\r\n2 Conducting character education programs.\r\n3 Promoting student leadership opportunities.\r\n4 Celebrating achievements and recognizing positive contributions.', 'June 2026 - March 2027', 'School head, Teachers, PTA, SGC and Stakehold', '1000', 'A positive school culture is foundational for effective SBM and overall school success.', 2026, 108926, 58, 12, 0),
(3344, 'Senior High School Career coaching program.', '1. To conduct various activities on  career planning in order to prepare the grade 10 students to a career path that they are going to follow.', '1. Grade 10 students gain awareness of career planning and future pathways.\r\n2. Documented coaching outputs and students reflections for SBM monitoring.', '1. Conduct structured career coaching sessions with interactive activities.\r\n2. Facilitate student participation through workshops, counseling and guided discussions.', 'March 4, 2026', '826 grade 10 students.', '4400.00', '1. Activity supports informed career decision-making and readiness for senior high school.\r\n2. Budget allocation ensures logistics, materials, and resource persons are adequately covered.', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3345, 'Developing and Implementing School Safety and Security Plans\r\n', '1 To ensure a safe and secure environment for students, staff, and visitors.\r\n2 To prepare for and respond effectively to emergencies.', '1 A comprehensive School Safety and Security Plan.\r\n2 Regular safety drills and emergency preparedness exercises.\r\n3 Visible security measures and protocols in place.\r\n', '1 Conduct a thorough risk assessment of the school premises.\r\n2 Develop emergency contact lists and communication protocols.\r\n3 Train staff and students on safety procedures and emergency response.', 'June 2026 - March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Stakeholders ', '1000', 'Regular review and updating of safety plans are crucial.', 2026, 108926, 58, 12, 0),
