(3398, 'SIP Robotic Competition Individual and Group ', '1. Design and develop cost Effective Robotic prototype tat addresses specific real-life problem using STEM principle.\r\n2. Test and evaluate the functionality , efficiency and reliability of the robotic prototype through experiments and observation.\r\n', '1. Students design and present cost-effective robotic prototypes addressing real-life problems.\r\n2. Documented competition results and innovation for SBM monitoring.', '1. Facilitate individual and group project development guided by STEM principles.\r\n2. Conduct competition with presentations, evaluations and feedback from coaches and panels.', 'October 2025', 'Selected Students and Coahes', '9671.00', '1. Activity promotes innovation, problem solving, and application of STEM in real-world contexts.\r\n2. Budget allocation ensures materials, logistics and proper conduct of the competition.', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3399, 'Brigada Eskwela', '1. To conduct brigada Eskwela and promote spirit of voluntarism .\r\n2. To bring together all education stakeholders to participate the BAYANIHAN SA PAARALAN program to ensure accessible and quality basic education.\r\n3. To prepare the school facilities', '* Clean, safe, and well- prepared school facilities before the opening of classes.\r\n* Active participation of teachers, parents, learners, and stakeholders in volunteer work.\r\n* Strengthen partnership between school and community through shared responsibilitity.\r\n* Proper utilization of resources and budget for maintainance and improvement.\r\n* Documented activities ( attendance, photos, reports ) for SBM compliance and evaluation. ', '1. Preparation\r\n* Form committees for logistics, safety and documentation.\r\n* Announce Brigada Eskwela schedule and invite stakeholders,\r\n* Gather cleaning materials, tools, and donations.\r\n2. Implementation\r\n* conduct daily cleaning, repair, and maintainance activities.\r\n*promote teamwork and bayanihan spirit during activities.\r\n3. Documentation and Reporting\r\n* Record attendance and contribution of stakeholders.\r\n* Take photos and prepare reports of completed task.\r\n* Submit consolidated report to school governance and DepEd.\r\n', 'june 9-13, 2025', 'shool personnel, teachers, parents, students ', '17840.00', 'Successful conduct of Brigada Eskwela. ', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3400, 'School Governing Council (SGC) Formation and Training', 'To establish a strong governance structure with a clear decision-making, clear roles and responsibilities', '1.Have a regular SGC meetings with documented minutes/pictures and action points.\r\n2.Defined leadership succession plans and leadership roles .\r\n3. Functional School Governing ( SGC ) with diverse representation.', '1. Leadership training and Capacity Building for SGC members and School heads\r\n2.Elections/appointments  for SGC members\r\n3.Improvement of SGC operational guidelines.', 'July  2026', 'School Head,Teacher/ SBM Focal person', '2500.00', 'Clear communications channels between the SGC and wider school school community are crucial. Focus on building trust and ensuring members understand  their roles and governance responsibilities . Well-trained and  representative of the SGC is the  backbone of SBM', 2026, 128676, 58, 12, 0),
(3401, '1. SBM orientation and awareness campaign.', '1. To increase awareness and understanding of SBM principles among teachers and stakeholders.', '1. Conducted orientation sessions; attendance; records', '1.conduct orientation; distributes brochures, use presentations and open forum.', 'May 2026', 'Schoolhead, teachers, community leaders', '1000.0', 'essential first step', 2026, 129334, 61, 12, 12),
(3402, 'CAPACITY BUILDING PROGRAM AND LEADERSHIP TRAINING for MNCHS schoo project W.A.T.C.H.  officers, SSLG , Club officers.', '1. To enhance leadership and interpersonal skills of students officers.\r\n2. To promote time-consciousness and the value of punctuality in leadership roles.\r\n3. To install honesty and integrity as core principles in students governance.\r\n4. Foster tea', '1. Student officers demonstrate improved leadership and interpersonal skills.\r\n2. Increased punctuality and time-consciousness among participants.\r\n3. Strengthen teamwork and collaboration  within W.A.T.C.H. and SSLG clubs. \r\n4. Documented training outputs ( attendance, evaluation forms, activity reports. )\r\n5. Sustainable leadership practices applied in school activities. ', '1. Preparation \r\n* Identify training needs and design modules on leadership and time management.\r\n* Invite resource speakers or facilitators.\r\n* Prepare venue, materials, anf Schedule.\r\n* prepare venue, materials, and schedule.\r\n2. Implementation\r\n* Conduct interactive workshops, lectures, and group activities. \r\n* Facilitate role-playing and problem-solving exercises. \r\n*  Emphasize punctuality through time-bound task and activities.\r\n3. Documentation and evaluation\r\n* Record attendance and participation\r\n* Collect feedback from student officers.\r\n* Prepare consolidated report highlighting skills gained and areas for improvement.', 'August 4, 2025', 'W.A.T.C.H. officers, SSLG, Club Officers.', '1580.00', 'Training successfully conducted with active participation of W.A.T.C.H. and SSLG officers.\r\nStudent leaders showed improved confidence, punctuality, and teamwork.\r\nResource speakers and facilitators provide relevant leadership insights.\r\nBudget utilized appropriately for materials, venue, and logistics.\r\nDocumentation ( attendance, evaluation forms, photos) submitted for SBM compliance..\r\n', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3403, 'FOOD AND BEVERAGE SERVICES SKILLS AND COMPITITION', '1. To showcase and assess the technical skills and competencies of senior high school students in various home economics discipline  based on industry standards.\r\n2. To promote  excellence , innovation and creativity among students through hands-on ,', 'Senior high school students showcase technical skills in food and beverage service.\r\n2. Documented competition results and outputs for SBM monitoring.', '1. Conduct skills-based competitions supervised by TechPro teachers.\r\n2. Evaluate performances using industry-aligned rubrics and criteria.', 'August 25,2025', 'Teachpro teachers of grade 11 and 12, teachpr', '2520.00', '1. Activity highlights industry-relevant competencies and strengthens student readiness\r\n2. Budget allocation ensures proper logistics, materials, and competition standards.', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
