(3482, 'Conduct of the PSYSC Celebration activities in the month of September 2025', '1. To promote public understanding of Science, Technology and Environment. (PUSTE).\r\n2. To foster camaraderie and develop leadership skills among the science clubbers through different contest and engaging activities.  ', '1. Increased awareness and appreciation of science, Technology , environment among learners.\r\n2. Active participation of students in PSYSC activities( quizzes, exhibits, contest). \r\n3. Strengthen collaboration among science teachers and learners. \r\n4. documented reports and outputs showcasing student engagement and learning.', '1. Organize science-related contests ( quiz bee, poster-making, slogan-writing.\r\n2. Conduct exhibits and demonstrations highlighting environmental and technological innovations.\r\n3. Facilitate interactive lectures and workshops led by science teachers.\r\n4. Encourage student-led initiatives and peer-to-peer learning activities.\r\n5. Monitor and evaluate participation and outcomes through attendance sheets, photos, and reports.', 'September 2-30, 2025', 'All Science Teachers and all Learners.', '5500.00', '1. Activity aligns with the school\'s thrust to promote scientific literacy and environmental awareness.\r\n2 Budget allocation ensures materials, prizes, and logistics are adequately supported.\r\n3. Outputs will be consolidated into a report for SBM documentation and future reference.\r\n4. Positive engagement expected to foster enthusiasm for science and technology among learners.', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3483, 'Learning Action Cell (LAC) Session an the adaption and Implementation of the project MindSpring: Literacy integration for Senior High School Students.  ', '1. Deeper teachers\' understanding of project MindSpring as a literacy integration rogram.\r\n2. Guide teachers in adapting the READ FRAMEWORKS to their respective areas.\r\n3. Develop concrete strategies and sample activities for effective implementation', '1. Teachers gain deeper understanding of project MindSpring as a literacy integration program.\r\n2. Documented session outputs and reflection for SBM monitoring.', '1. Conduct structured LAC sessions facilitated by senior high school teachers.\r\n2. Provide guided discussions, resource sharing and collaborative planning activities.', 'September 5, 2025', 'MNCHS Senior High School Teachers.', '27744.00', '1. Activity strengthens literacy integration and supports curriculum enrichment\r\n2. Budget allocation ensures materials, logistics and documentation are adequately covered.', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3484, 'LEARNING ENVIRONMENT\r\n\r\nIndicator 15\r\n\r\n1.  Organization of CPC\r\n2. Orientation on Child protection Policy (CPP)\r\n3. Development of Child Protection plan\r\n4. Implementation of preventive programs\r\n5. Case management documentation', '1. Establish school CPC with defined roles\r\n2. Increase awareness of CPP among stakeholders\r\n3. Create a clear plan addressing child protection issues\r\n4. Reduce cases of bullying, abuse, and neglect\r\n5. Properly handle and document child protection ', '1. Approved list of CPC members\r\n2. Oriented teachers, parents and learners\r\n3. Written school Child Protection Plan\r\n4. Decreased incidents reported\r\n5. Case reports and resolution records', '1. Issue school order, assign roles (chairperson, guidance, teachers, PTA rep)\r\n2. Conduct seminars on CPP\r\n3. Planning workshop with CPC members\r\n4. Anti-bullying campaigns, values formation activities\r\n5. Follow standard protocols, maintain case folders', 'July to march', 'School Head and AO', '2000.00', '1. Ensure gender balance and representation\r\n2. Use real-life scenarios for better understanding\r\n3. Integrate into SIP\r\n4. Integrate into curriculum\r\n5. Strict confidentiality required', 2026, 128990, 60, 12, 27),
