(3486, 'Inter-School Symposium on Women and Child Protection ,Bridging gaps : Legal and Social Protection for Women and Children.', '1. To raise awareness among students about the laws and social support system  protecting women and children.\r\n2. To educate participants about pressing issues such as bullying , online sexual abuse , rape and gangsterism. \r\n3. To empower youth throu', '11. Students gain awareness of laws and support system protecting women and children.\r\n2. Documented symposium proceedings and student reflections for SBM monitoring.', '1. Conduct symposium sessions with resource speakers and interactive discussions.\r\n2. Facilitate student participation through Q & A and guided reflection activities.', 'September 29, 2025', '889 grade 7 students', '4700.00', '1. Activity strengthens advocacy for child and women protection within the school community.\r\n2. Budget allocation ensures logistics, resource materials, and speaker honoraria are covered.', 2026, 304325, 103, 12, 0),
(3487, 'Baseline Assessment( ELLN)', 'Determines learners\' current proficiency level in language, literacy, and numeracy', 'Consolidated assessment results, learner profiles', 'Conduct pre-test using ELLN tools; analyze results', 'June', 'Grade 3 teachers, Master Teacher and School H', '5000', 'This plan supports the improvement of Grade 3 learners\' ELLN proficiency through targeted interventions, regular assessment, and active stakeholders involvement.\r\nAims to ensure that all Grade 3 learners achieve the required proficiency level in early language, literacy, and numeracy skills.', 2026, 128602, 106, 12, 132),
