(3525, 'implementation of School Greening and Cleaning Programs', 'To maintain a safe, clean, green and child-friendly learning space that is conducive to learning', 'Clean classrooms, improved school sanitation and functional Gulayan sa Paaralan', '*Proper Waste Segregation and Disposal\r\n\r\n*Having Gulayan sa paaralan\r\n\r\n*Ensuring availability of water and clean toilets\r\n\r\n*Availability of drinking water\r\n\r\n*School beautification and regular weeding ', 'June 2025-March 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents, Learners', '20000.00', '', 2026, 501608, 61, 12, 7),
(3527, 'School Monitoring and Evaluation ', 'To systematically assess the implementation of school programs and activities in order to ensure efficiency, effectiveness, and continuous improvement of school performance', 'A comprehensive monitoring and evaluation report with data-driven findings and recommendations for school program improvement and decision-making', '*Conduct of SMEA ', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, SMET, Project owners, external s', '4000.00', '', 2026, 501608, 61, 12, 7),
(3528, 'GOVERNANCE AND ACCOUNTABILITY\r\n\r\nIndicator 27\r\n\r\n1.Development of monitoring and evaluation plan\r\n2. Creation of monitoring tools and templates\r\n3. ', '1. Establish a systematic process for tracking PPAs\r\n2. Standardize data collection and reporting', '1. Approved M&E plan with tools and indicators\r\n2. Monitoring forms, checklist and templates', '1. Conduct planning workshop, align with SIP and DepEd standards\r\n2. Develop and validate tools', 'July to February', 'SCPT members', '2000.00', '1. Include clear KPIs\r\n2. Use digital tools if possible', 2026, 128990, 60, 12, 27),
(3529, 'GOVERNANCE AND ACCOUNTABILITY\r\n\r\nIndicator 28\r\n\r\n1. Development of stakeholder satisfaction survey tool\r\n2. Conduct baseline survey and analyze survey results\r\n3. Implementation of feedback mechanism', '1. Establish a standard tool to measure satisfaction\r\n2. Determine current satisfaction level of stakeholders and identify strengths and areas for improvement\r\n3. Provide flatform for suggestions and complaints', '1. Approved survey questionnaire\r\n2. Baseline satisfaction rating report and data analysis report with key findings\r\n3. Functional feedback system', '1. Design survey align with DepEd survey standards\r\n2. Administer survey to learners, parents, teachers , partners and use simple statistical analysis and feedback review\r\n3. Suggestion box, online forms', 'June to March', 'School Head, AO Teachers', '5000.00', '1. Include clear rating scale\r\n2. Ensure anonymity and highlight priority concerns\r\n3. Ensure promt response', 2026, 128990, 60, 12, 27),
(3530, 'HUMAN RESOURCE AND TEAM DEVELOPMENT\r\n\r\nIndicator 31\r\n\r\n1. Planning of LAC sessions\r\n2. Conduct of regular LAC session\r\n3. Monitoring of LAC implementation', '1. Design relevant needs-based LAC activities\r\n2. Strengthen teaching practices through collaboration\r\n3. Ensure the effectiveness of sessions', '1. Annual LAC plan\r\n2. Annual LAC Plan\r\n3. Monitoring reports and attendance records', '1. Collaborative planning among school head and teachers\r\n2. Collaborative planning\r\n3. Observation, documentation, feedback forms', 'June to March', 'School Head, LAC Leader, LAC Faciltator', '10000.00', '1-2 Align with DepEd policies\r\n3. Regular evaluation\r\n', 2026, 128990, 60, 12, 27),
(3531, 'Stakeholders’ Planning and Improvement Workshop', 'To engage key stakeholders in identifying school needs, setting priorities, and collaboratively developing program for the school.', '1. Identified priority needs of the school\r\n2. Consolidated issues and root causes\r\nProposed solutions and strategies\r\n3. Draft inputs for the School Improvement Plan (SIP)\r\nStakeholders’ commitment and partnership agreements', 'Participatory Approach – Active involvement of all stakeholders\r\nData-Driven Decision Making – Use of school performance data\r\nCollaborative Group Work – Workshops, brainstorming, and reporting\r\nConsensus Building – Prioritization through voting or agreement\r\nAction Planning – Structured planning using templates', 'June-August 2026', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, Teachers, Paren', '22000.00', 'None', 2026, 128447, 57, 12, 121),
(3532, 'Orientation and Planning, Preparation of Materials,\r\nAdministration of CRLA (Beginning of school year) and PHIL - IRI (Pretest), Data analysis and interpretation, Development of Intervention Programs\r\n6. Implementation of Reading Interv', 'To conduct CRLA and PHIL - IRI at the beginning of the school year and end of the school year', '- Updated learner reading profile\r\n-Functional intervention program\r\n- Improved reading levels of learners\r\n- Data - driven instructional decisions', 'Standardized Assessment Approach, Baseline Intervention -Post Assessment, Individualized Assessment Method, Level - Based Classification, Data Driven Analysis, Collaborative Implementation Strategy', 'Whole Year Round', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Teachers', '25,000.00', '', 2026, 128841, 60, 12, 0),
