(3537, 'Conduct orientation on SBM to teachers and stakeholders ', 'To capacitate teachers and stakeholders on the policy guidelines on the revised SBM implementation.', 'Conducted orientation, attendance sheet, minutes of meeting and reports', 'Orientation and advocacy', '1 month', 'School Principal, Teachers and identified Sta', 'A4 bond paper, Tarpaulin, snacks', 'To be integrated during General Assembly', 2026, 129323, 61, 12, 0),
(3538, 'Orient teachers on the provisions of DO 7s.2024 or the Guidelines on the Implementation of the Revised School-Basesd Management System', 'Establish a Shared Understanding: To provide teachers with a definitive understanding that the revised SBM is the \"gateway to school effectiveness\" and a preparation phase for continuous improvement\r\n.\r\nFamiliarize with the New Framework: To orient p', 'Well-Informed Personnel: Teachers who are fully aware of the revised guidelines and are prepared to observe the three-year transitory period for full institutionalization\r\n.\r\nInitial Self-Assessment Results: Drafted entries for the SBM Self-Assessment Checklist (Annex A), where teachers provide input on the \"Degree of Manifestation\" of practices in their respective departments or grade levels\r\n.\r\nIdentification of Improvement Areas: A list of \"improvement areas\" identified through self-reflection to be integrated into the school’s strategic or implementation plans\r\n.\r\nEnhanced Commitment: A collective commitment to a school culture that prioritizes learner-centeredness, inclusion, and holistic development over administrative compliance', 'School-Based Learning Action Cell (LAC) Sessions: Utilizing existing LAC structures to conduct in-depth \"needs-based\" professional development on specific SBM dimensions\r\n.\r\nWorkshop and Self-Reflection Exercises: Facilitating sessions where teachers use the SBM Self-Assessment Checklist to analyze current school practices, identifying what is \"frequently\" or \"always\" manifested\r\n.\r\nCascading Strategy: Employing \"cascading strategies\" to ensure clear communication of policy goals from the School Head to all teaching and non-teaching personnel\r\n.\r\nCollaborative Stakeholder Engagement: Inviting teachers to participate in the school\'s self-assessment process alongside internal and external stakeholders to analyze observed school practices and achieved learning outcomes\r\n.\r\nIntegration with Planning: Using the orientation as a springboard to integrate self-assessment results into the school\'s Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) or School Improvement Plan (SIP)', '2nd week of May and as scheduled', 'School Head, Master Teachers, PDO, and AOII', '5000', '', 2026, 129548, 107, 12, 57),
(3539, 'Conduct of Comprehensive SBM Self-Assessment using Annex A Checklist', 'To determine the school\'s current degree of manifestation in the six SBM dimensions and identify areas for improvement.', 'Accomplished SBM Self-Assessment Checklist with verified remarks and identified priority improvement areas.', 'Internal and external stakeholders meeting, focus group discussions, and document review based on DepEd Order No. 007, s. 2024 indicators.', '4th Grading Period (Year 1)', 'School Head (SBM Coordinator), Teachers, PTA ', '5000.00', '', 2026, 129548, 107, 12, 57),
