(3587, 'Project ELLN Boost: bridging gaps in Language, Literacy and Numeracy for grade 3 Learners.', '- To assess the current literacy and numeracy levels of grade 3 learners to identify learning gaps.\r\nTo implement targeted instructional interventions and remediation activities for identified non-readers , slow readers, and low numerates.\r\n-to enhan', '-Complete pre-test ,  Mid-Test , and Post-Test results showing improvement in scores.\r\n-individual learning progress Charts for every learner.\r\n-Compilation of localized and contextualized instructional materials(IMS),worksheets, and activity sheets.\r\n-Accomplishment report s on conducted trainings, workshops,and remedial classes.\r\n-increase percentage of learners reaching the profeciency level based on the division/regional standards.\r\n-Attendance records of parents during meeting and workshops.', 'DIAGNOSIS AND ASSESSMENT\r\n-Administration of ELLN , Pre-assessment tools, Grouping of learners according to ability levels(Beginner, Developing, Proficient)\r\nINSTRUCTIONAL DELIVERY\r\n-Explicit Instruction: Direct teaching of skills\r\n-Differentiated Instruction: Activities suited to different learning speeds.\r\n-Multisensory Approach: Use of visual, auditory and kinesthetic materials.\r\n-Peer Tutoring/Buddy system: pairing advanced learners with those needing help.\r\nREMEDIATION AND ENHNCEMENT\r\n-Catch-up Fridays and implementation/provision of take-home activity sheets.\r\nCAPACITY BUILDING\r\n-Attendance to LAC(Learning Action cell)sessions focused on ELLN. and mentoring/coaching by master Teacher and school head.\r\nCOMMUNITY INVOLVEMENT\r\n-PTA meetings and orientation, distribution of learning guides for parents.', '-Planning assessment,IImplementation , Monito', 'Principal, Master Teachers, Grade 3 Teacher, ', 'Instructional materials, Trainings and recognition-3,0002,000.00', '', 2026, 128610, 106, 12, 132),
(3588, 'Orientation of Non-Teaching and Teaching Personnel and Organization of SBM Structures', 'a. To orient teachers on the new guidelines in the implementation of the School-Based Management System\r\nb. Establish or strengthen the School Governance Council (SGC) and core teams\r\nc. Designate SBM coordinators and working committees', 'Create Committees on the different pillars of the School-Based Management', 'Gather teachers before the start of the School Year ', 'May 2026', 'School Head ', '2000', 'To be implemented within the time frame of Brigada Eskwela Implementation', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
(3589, 'Orientation and Advocacy of the Internal and External Stakeholders and the creation of the different Teams under different Pillars.', 'a. Conduct orientation on SBM principles, framework, and DepEd guidelines\r\nb. Raise awareness among teachers, staff, and stakeholders (PTA, SGC, LGU, partners)', 'To Create Team under different Pillars and assigned task to empower the School-Based Management Implementation', 'Send invitation letters to the internal and external stakeholders', 'April-May 2026', 'School Head and Administrative Officer II', '2000', 'To be implemented within the period of implementation of Brigada Eskwela', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
(3590, 'Baseline Data Gathering and Situation Analysis', 'a. To Identify the magnitude of priority with regard to the Physical Plant and Facilities that needs improvement or rehabilitation.\r\nb. Collect school data (enrolment, performance indicators, resources, issues)\r\nc. Conduct SWOT analysis or school ass', 'List Down Physical Plant and Facilities and rank them in accordance to the priority improvement areas.', 'Roam around the premises of the school together with the teaching, non-teaching and stakeholders and identify the Physical Plant and Facilities for repair and rehabilitation.', 'May 2026-June 2026', 'School Head , Teaching and Non-Teaching Perso', '0', 'It should be implemented as the stakeholders have the unity walked around the school premises.', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
(3591, 'Creation of the School-Based Management Center', 'To establish a functional School-Based Management (SBM) Center that will serve as a hub for planning, implementation, monitoring, and documentation of school governance initiatives aligned with DepEd standards.', 'a. A fully established and organized SBM Center with designated space and resources\r\nb. Updated and accessible SBM documents (e.g., SIP, AIP, reports, MOVs)\r\nc. Functional display of school data, performance indicators, and best practices\r\nd. Strengthened stakeholder engagement and participation in school governance\r\ne. Improved compliance with SBM assessment indicators', 'a. Identify and prepare a designated space within the school for the SBM Center\r\nOrganize and compile all relevant SBM documents and Means of Verification (MOVs)\r\nb. Assign a focal person or team responsible for SBM Center management\r\nc. Conduct orientation and capacity-building for teachers and stakeholders on SBM processes\r\nd. Utilize visual management tools (charts, dashboards, portfolios) for easy monitoring\r\ne. Engage stakeholders (PTA, SGC, LGU) in contributing to and sustaining the center\r\nf. Regularly update and evaluate the SBM Center for continuous improvement', 'June 2026-October 2026', 'School Head , Teaching and Non-Teaching Perso', '10000', 'The SBM Center should not only function as a compliance mechanism but also as a dynamic learning and collaboration space that reflects transparency, accountability, and shared governance. Sustainability may be ensured through continuous stakeholder support, proper maintenance, and integration into the school’s regular operations.', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
(3592, '•	Conduct an intensive Reading and Numeracy Enhancement Program for Grade 3 learners.\r\n•	Organize teacher capacity-building workshops on differentiated instruction and formative assessment.\r\n•	Implement parental engagement sessions to support literac', '•	Strengthen learners’ foundational skills in reading comprehension, vocabulary, and numeracy.\r\n•	Equip teachers with effective strategies for early literacy and numeracy instruction.\r\n•	Foster home-school collaboration to reinforce learning continui', '•	At least 80% of Grade 3 learners reach proficiency in language, literacy, and numeracy clusters.\r\n•	LAC action plans\r\n•	Improved teaching strategies\r\n•	Teachers demonstrate improved instructional practices through classroom observations and learner performance.\r\n•	Parents actively participate in supporting learners’ reading and numeracy activities at home.', '•	Intensify ARAL Program\r\n•	Small-group remediation and peer-assisted learning for struggling learners.\r\n•	Use of diagnostic tests and regular progress monitoring (monthly assessments).\r\n•	Integration of games, storytelling, and manipulatives to make learning engaging.\r\n•	Community partnerships (e.g., local libraries, NGOs) to provide supplemental resources.\r\n•	Recognition programs for learners and parents to sustain motivation.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Grade 3 Teachers; Master Teacher', '20000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(3593, 'Resource Mobilization Management ', 'To secure and strengthen the commitment of internal and external stakeholders in supporting the establishment, development, and sustainability of the School-Based Management (SBM) Center.', 'a. Formalized stakeholder commitments (e.g., MOA, resolutions, pledges of support)\r\nb. Active participation of stakeholders (PTA, SGC, LGU, alumni, partners) in SBM Center development\r\nc. Mobilized resources (financial, material, and technical support) for the SBM Center\r\nd. Strengthened partnership and collaboration mechanisms\r\ne. Increased sense of ownership and shared accountability among stakeholders', 'a. Conduct stakeholder meetings, consultations, and orientation on SBM and the purpose of the SBM Center\r\nb. Present the SBM Center plan, including needs and potential areas for support\r\nc. Establish partnerships through formal agreements (MOA/MOU)\r\nd. Organize resource mobilization activities (donations, Brigada Eskwela support, community drives)\r\ne. Assign stakeholder representatives to take part in planning, implementation, and monitoring\r\nf. Maintain regular communication and feedback mechanisms (meetings, reports, updates)\r\ng. Recognize and acknowledge stakeholder contributions to sustain engagement', 'June 2026-October 2026', 'School Head , Teaching and Non-Teaching Perso', '2000', 'Sustained stakeholder support is crucial to the success of the SBM Center. Building trust, transparency, and continuous engagement will ensure long-term collaboration. The school should institutionalize stakeholder participation as part of its governance culture to promote shared responsibility and accountability.', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
