(3607, 'School Planning', 'a. Develop or update the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)\r\nb. Align plans with SBM principles and DepEd priorities', 'a. Approved School Improvement Plan (SIP) aligned with DepEd goals and SBM principles\r\nb. Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) derived from the SIP\r\nc. Prioritized Programs, Projects, and Activities (PPAs) with defined targets and timelines\r\nd. Consolidated school data profile (enrolment, performance indicators, resources, issues)\r\ne. Stakeholder-validated plans reflecting community needs and participation', 'a. Conduct data gathering (school report card, learner performance, resources, needs assessment)\r\nb. Facilitate school planning workshop with teachers and stakeholders (SGC, PTA, partners)\r\nc. Perform situational analysis (SWOT, gap analysis, root cause analysis)\r\nd. Set goals, objectives, and performance targets based on evidence\r\ne. Identify and prioritize PPAs aligned with identified needs\r\nf. Develop SIP (3-year plan) and translate it into AIP (annual targets and activities)\r\ng. Validate and finalize plans through stakeholder consultation and approval\r\nh. Disseminate the approved plans to all concerned and ensure alignment in implementation', 'May 2026-July 2026', 'School Head , Teaching and Non-Teaching Perso', '2000', 'Effective school planning should be data-driven, participatory, and responsive to learners’ needs. Continuous review and adjustment of plans ensure relevance and alignment with school performance goals.', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
(3608, 'Implementation of Programs, Projects, and Activities (PPAs)', 'a. Execute planned activities based on SIP and AIP\r\nb. Ensure participation of stakeholders in implementation', 'a. Successfully implemented PPAs aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)\r\nb. Increased learner performance and improved school outcomes (e.g., participation, achievement, retention)\r\nc. Efficient utilization of resources (MOOE, stakeholder support, materials)\r\nd. Active involvement of teachers, learners, and stakeholders in program delivery\r\ne. Documented accomplishments, reports, and Means of Verification (MOVs)', 'a. Communicate clearly the implementation plan, roles, and timelines to all involved personnel\r\nb. Organize implementation teams and assign specific responsibilities\r\nc. Execute PPAs based on the approved AIP and set schedules\r\nd. Integrate PPAs into regular school activities and classroom practices\r\ne. Ensure availability and proper use of resources and logistical support\r\nf. Engage stakeholders (PTA, SGC, LGU, partners) in implementation and support activities\r\ng. Conduct regular monitoring through meetings, progress tracking, and site observations\r\nh. Provide technical assistance and address challenges encountered during implementation\r\ni. Document all activities, outputs, and best practices for reporting and evaluation', 'May 2026-March 2027', 'School Head and Administrative Officer II', '100000', 'Effective implementation of PPAs requires strong coordination, accountability, and adaptability. Continuous communication and stakeholder engagement are essential to ensure that activities remain responsive to learners’ needs. Proper documentation and reflection on outcomes will support evidence-based improvements and sustainability of programs.', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
(3609, 'Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E)', 'a. Regularly track progress using indicators and tools\r\nb. Conduct internal assessments and review meetings', 'a. Regular M&E reports (monthly, quarterly, annual)\r\nb. Updated progress tracking tools and performance indicators\r\nc. Identified gaps, issues, and corresponding interventions\r\nd. Evidence-based decisions for school improvement', 'a. Use monitoring tools (checklists, dashboards, scorecards)\r\nb. Conduct regular review meetings and classroom observations\r\nc. Analyze data against targets in the AIP/SIP\r\nd. Provide feedback and technical assistance', 'May 2026-March 2027', 'School Head , Teaching and Non-Teaching Perso', '0', 'M&E should be continuous, data-driven, and participatory to ensure timely interventions and accountability.', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
(3610, 'Documentation and Reporting', 'To ensure accurate, organized, and timely recording of all SBM processes, outputs, and accomplishments.', 'a. Complete and updated Means of Verification (MOVs)\r\nb. Organized SBM Center with accessible records\r\nc. Periodic accomplishment and narrative reports\r\nd. Consolidated data for decision-making and validation', 'a. Assign documentation focal persons\r\nb. Use standardized templates and reporting formats\r\nc. Compile and organize documents in physical and digital formats\r\nd. Submit reports regularly to concerned offices', 'May 2026-March 2027', 'School Head , Teaching and Non-Teaching Perso', '0', 'Proper documentation supports transparency, validation, and continuity of school initiatives.', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
(3611, 'Recognition and Feedback', 'To acknowledge contributions and gather insights for improving school programs and stakeholder engagement.', 'a. Recognition programs/activities for stakeholders and personnel\r\nb. Feedback reports and stakeholder satisfaction results\r\nc. Increased motivation and sustained participation', 'a. Conduct recognition ceremonies and appreciation activities\r\nb. Gather feedback through surveys, meetings, and consultations\r\nc. Integrate feedback into planning and implementation', 'May 2026-March 2027', 'School Head , Teaching and Non-Teaching Perso', '0', 'Recognition and feedback strengthen partnerships and promote a culture of appreciation and continuous learning.', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
(3612, 'Continuous Improvement and Sustainability', 'To ensure that SBM practices and PPAs are continuously enhanced and sustained over time.', 'a. Improved SIP and AIP based on evaluation results\r\nb. Institutionalized best practices and innovations\r\nc. Sustained stakeholder support and resource generation\r\nd. Enhanced school performance indicators', 'a. Conduct periodic reviews and planning adjustments\r\nb. Adopt best practices and innovations\r\nc. Strengthen stakeholder partnerships and capacity-building\r\nd. Integrate successful PPAs into regular school operations', 'May 2026-March 2027', 'School Head , Teaching and Non-Teaching Perso', '0', 'Sustainability depends on strong leadership, stakeholder ownership, and the institutionalization of effective practices.', 2026, 129008, 60, 12, 29),
(3613, 'Parent orientation on reading and numeracy,  Home - based learning tasks, Community support for learning materials.', 'To conduct parent orientation for stakeholders\' support', '- Parents increased awareness.\r\n- Improved parents awareness.\r\n- Enhanced parents engagement.\r\n- Strengthened School - Home partnership.', '- Parent empowerment approach\r\n- Positive parenting technique\r\n- Continuous  support and follow up', 'Whole Year Round', 'School Head, School Reading Coordinator, Mast', '0.00', '', 2026, 128841, 60, 12, 0),
(3614, 'Conduct Test Analysis Workshop, Conduct Competency Mapping, Collaborative Reflection among teachers (Group Data Discussion - Data Talk),\r\nConduct Student  Self-Analysis Activity, Evaluate quality of multiple choice items', 'To conduct test item analysis to inform its teaching and learning process.', '- Data - Driven understanding of student performance\r\n- Identified strengths and weaknesses.\r\n- Improved assessment tools\r\n- Targeted remediation strategies\r\n- Adjusted teaching methods', '- Collect Data\r\n- Analyze Scores and Items\r\n- Map Competencies\r\n- Identify Errors\r\n- Group Learners\r\n- Plan Interventions\r\n- Adjust Teaching\r\n- Reassess Progress', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Teachers', '25,000.00', '', 2026, 128841, 60, 12, 0),
