(3849, 'Provide regular coaching, mentoring, and technical assistance to teachers and staff;\r\nConduct periodic performance monitoring and feedback sessions (quarterly review)', 'Results-based performance management system (RPMS) implementation; Data-driven monitoring and feedback system', '100% of school personnel achieving at least Very Satisfactory IPCRF rating\r\nImproved teaching and work performance outcomes\r\nStrengthened professional competence of personnel\r\nDocumented performance monitoring and coaching reports', 'Results-based performance management system (RPMS) implementation; Data-driven monitoring and feedback system\r\nCollaborative coaching and mentoring approach', 'Whole School Year (with quarterly monitoring ', 'School Head', '1000', 'The school consistently maintains high performance among personnel through effective monitoring, mentoring, and professional development. Continuous strengthening of performance management practices is recommended to sustain excellence and support professional growth. ', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
(3850, 'Conduct Training Needs Assessment (TNA) to identify priority learning and development needs of teachers', 'To sustain and enhance the implementation of needs-based LAC and L&D activities that strengthen teachers’ competencies, improve instructional practices, and support learner achievement.', 'Sustained implementation of needs-based LAC and L&D programs', 'Needs-based and data-driven planning (based on TNA, classroom observations, and learner outcomes), Reflective practice and sharing of experiences among teachers', 'Whole School Year (with scheduled monthly or ', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Teachers', '3000', 'The school consistently implements effective and needs-based LAC and L&D activities. Continuous enhancement of training programs, alignment with emerging educational needs, and strengthening of collaborative practices are recommended to sustain professional growth and improve teaching quality.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
(3851, 'Disseminate updated guidelines on promotion, ranking, and career progression', 'To sustain and strengthen systems that support the promotion and continuous professional development of school personnel, ensuring career growth, improved competencies, and enhanced performance.', 'Increased number of personnel promoted or qualified for promotion', 'Competency-based and needs-driven professional development\r\nCoaching and mentoring system for continuous improvement, Alignment with DepEd professional standards and career progression policies and\r\nMonitoring and evaluation of personnel development plans', 'Whole School Year (with scheduled trainings, ', 'School Head, HR', '1000', 'The school consistently promotes and supports the professional growth of its personnel.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
(3852, 'Identify and document personnel achievements (e.g., promotions, awards, years of service, outstanding performance)', 'To sustain and enhance a systematic and motivating recognition and rewards program that acknowledges the milestone achievements and exemplary performance of school personnel.', 'Sustained implementation of a functional recognition and rewards system\r\nIncreased motivation and job satisfaction among personnel', 'Transparent and merit-based selection and recognition system\r\nInclusive and participatory nomination process\r\nMotivation and reinforcement approach to improve performance\r\nContinuous documentation and dissemination of achievements\r\nAlignment with DepEd recognition and incentive guidelines', 'Whole School Year (with scheduled recognition', 'School Head, Teachers and School Personnel', '5000', 'The school consistently recognizes and rewards the achievements of its personnel. Continuous strengthening of the recognition system and expansion of incentives are recommended to further motivate staff and sustain high performance.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
(3853, 'Ensure accurate and updated submission of payroll requirements and personnel records                                            Conduct regular validation of plantilla positions, salary grades, and employee data\r\nCoordinate with the Division Office f', 'To sustain an efficient, accurate, and timely payroll and compensation processing system ensuring that all school personnel receive correct salaries, allowances, and benefits without delay.', 'Timely and accurate release of salaries and allowances\r\nZero or minimized payroll discrepancies\r\nUpdated and well-organized payroll records\r\nImproved personnel satisfaction regarding compensation', 'Strict adherence to government payroll policies and procedures\r\nData accuracy and verification system before submission\r\nClose coordination between school, division, and finance offices\r\nPreventive monitoring of payroll-related concerns\r\nTransparent communication with personnel regarding salary updates', 'Whole School Year (with monthly payroll monit', 'School Head, Administrative Officer', '1000', 'The school consistently ensures the accurate and timely release of salaries, allowances, and other benefits. Continuous improvement in records management, coordination, and verification processes is recommended to sustain efficiency and accuracy.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
(3854, 'Conduct annual review and assignment of teaching loads based on qualifications, specialization, and workload standards', 'To sustain a fair, transparent, and equitable distribution of teacher workload that promotes efficiency, well-being, and improved instructional delivery.', 'Fair and balanced distribution of teaching and non-teaching workloads\r\nImproved teacher efficiency and job satisfaction\r\nReduced workload-related concerns and conflicts\r\nUpdated and documented workload assignments', 'Data-driven workload allocation based on teacher specialization and performance\r\nParticipatory decision-making with teachers and department heads\r\nTransparent consultation and communication process\r\nContinuous monitoring and adjustment of assignments\r\nEquity-based workload balancing approach', 'Every School Year', 'School Head, Department Heads / Master Teache', '1000', 'The school consistently ensures fairness and equity in the distribution of teacher workload. Continuous consultation, monitoring, and adjustment are recommended to maintain efficiency, harmony, and productivity among personnel.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
(3855, 'Conduct regular school facility inspection (classrooms, comfort rooms, pathways, laboratories, etc.)               Prepare and update facility maintenance and improvement plan              ', 'To sustain a systematic inspection, maintenance, and improvement program for school infrastructure and facilities to ensure safety, functionality, accessibility, and conducive learning environment for all learners and personnel.', 'Well-maintained and safe school facilities\r\nCompleted minor repairs and prioritized infrastructure improvements\r\nUpdated facility inspection and maintenance records\r\nImproved learning environment for learners and staff', 'Preventive maintenance system (regular inspection schedule)\r\nData-based prioritization of facility improvements', 'Whole School Year (with monthly inspections a', 'School Head School Property Custodian, DRRM C', '500', '', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
(3856, 'Maintain an organized and updated school library system                                                  Conduct regular inspection and maintenance of water systems, electrical lines, and internet connectivity                                         ', 'o sustain and continuously improve the functionality, accessibility, and reliability of school learning resources and basic facilities (library, utilities, and ICT resources) in support of quality teaching and learning.', 'Fully functional and organized school library\r\nStable and reliable water, electricity, and internet services\r\nOperational and well-maintained computer laboratory/classroom\r\nImproved access to learning resources and ICT tools\r\nEnhanced teaching and learning experience', 'Preventive maintenance and regular facility inspection\r\nResource management and documentation system\r\nStakeholder collaboration (LGU, PTA, private partners)\r\nICT integration in teaching and learning\r\nContinuous monitoring and feedback system\r\nPrioritization of repairs and upgrades based on need', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head Library In-Charge / Teacher Libra', '5000', 'The school consistently ensures the functionality and accessibility of its learning resources and basic facilities. Continuous improvement, preventive maintenance, and strong stakeholder support are recommended to sustain quality service delivery and enhance learning opportunities.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
(3857, 'Maintain an organized and updated school library system                                                  Conduct regular inspection and maintenance of water systems, electrical lines, and internet connectivity                                         ', 'o sustain and continuously improve the functionality, accessibility, and reliability of school learning resources and basic facilities (library, utilities, and ICT resources) in support of quality teaching and learning.', 'Fully functional and organized school library\r\nStable and reliable water, electricity, and internet services\r\nOperational and well-maintained computer laboratory/classroom\r\nImproved access to learning resources and ICT tools\r\nEnhanced teaching and learning experience', 'Preventive maintenance and regular facility inspection\r\nResource management and documentation system\r\nStakeholder collaboration (LGU, PTA, private partners)\r\nICT integration in teaching and learning\r\nContinuous monitoring and feedback system\r\nPrioritization of repairs and upgrades based on need', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head Library In-Charge / Teacher Libra', '5000', 'The school consistently ensures the functionality and accessibility of its learning resources and basic facilities. Continuous improvement, preventive maintenance, and strong stakeholder support are recommended to sustain quality service delivery and enhance learning opportunities.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
(3858, 'Prepare annual and quarterly Work and Financial Plan (WFP) aligned with SIP/AIP\r\nEnsure timely implementation of planned activities funded by MOOE', 'To sustain efficient, transparent, and compliant utilization of MOOE funds in support of school operations, programs, and priorities aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).', '72–100% efficient utilization of MOOE funds\r\nFully implemented school programs and activities\r\nComplete and updated financial records and reports\r\nImproved transparency and accountability in fund management', 'esults-based budgeting aligned with school priorities\r\nTransparent and participatory financial planning\r\nRegular monitoring and evaluation of fund utilization', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head Administrative Officer / Finance ', '1000', 'The school consistently demonstrates efficient and transparent utilization of MOOE funds. Continuous financial planning, monitoring, and compliance with DepEd and COA regulations are essential to sustain effective resource management and support quality school operations.', 2026, 304241, 58, 12, 38),
