(3884, 'SBM Orientation & Capacity Building', 'To capacitate and empower school stakeholders with a clear understanding of School‑Based Management (SBM) principles, structures, roles, and processes in order to strengthen participatory leadership, improve shared decision‑making, and enhance collec', '• Oriented school stakeholders • Increased awareness and understanding of SBM • Improved participation in school governance', 'Lectures and presentations on SBM principles • Group discussions and workshops • Sharing of roles, responsibilities, and best practices • Open forum and reflection', 'QUARTER 1', 'School Head/Teachers/SPT/PTA', '500', 'once a year', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
(3885, 'Project TRANPARENCY-Quarterly School Report Card(SRC) and Stakeholder\'s Forum', '1. Strengthen transparency\r\n2. Increase stakeholder\'s participation', '1.Quarterly SRC posted\r\n2. 4 SGC meeting done\r\n3. 85% client satisfaction rating\r\n', 'Data-driven reporting\r\nOpen forum\r\nSuggestion box\r\nOnline feedback', 'Quarterly: August, November, February, May', 'School Head, SGC, SBM Team, LGU, AO', '2000', 'Improved Stakeholder Trust. Posted on FB gained 200+ engagements. SGC actively involved in Planning', 2026, 128962, 60, 12, 26),
(3886, 'Reorganization of SBM Structures (SGC, SPT)', 'To capacitate and empower school stakeholders with a clear understanding of SBM principles, structures, roles, and processes.\r\nTo strengthen participatory leadership, shared decision‑making, and collective accountability toward continuous school impr', 'School stakeholders oriented on SBM principles and processes.\r\nIncreased awareness of roles and responsibilities of SGC, SPT, and stakeholders.\r\nStrengthened participation in school governance and planning activities.\r\nAttendance sheets, program, minutes, and documentation of the activity.', 'Interactive lectures and presentations on SBM principles and frameworks.\r\nGroup discussions/workshops on roles, responsibilities, and SBM practices.\r\nCase sharing and reflection activities.\r\nOpen forum and feedback session.', 'Quarter 1 (June–August) or at the start of th', 'School Head Teachers and Non‑Teaching Personn', '500', 'Foundational activity for effective SBM implementation.\r\nSupports all SBM Principles, with emphasis on Leadership and Governance (Principle I).\r\nOutputs serve as Means of Verification (MOVs) for SBM Level II–III validation.', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
(3887, 'Reorganization of SBM Structures (School Governing Council & School Planning Team)', 'To ensure functional, representative, and policy‑compliant SBM structures through the reorganization of the School Governing Council (SGC) and School Planning Team (SPT).\r\nTo strengthen participatory governance, collaborative planning, and shared dec', 'Reconstituted and duly approved SGC and SPT with clear representation.\r\nIssued designation orders defining roles and responsibilities.\r\nApproved organizational structure and terms of reference.\r\nDocumentation (minutes, attendance, memos).', 'Review of DepEd policies and SBM guidelines on governance structures.\r\nStakeholder consultation and nomination/selection of members.\r\nIssuance of designation orders and orientation of members.\r\nValidation of roles, functions, and reporting lines.', 'Quarter 1 (June–August) or at the start of th', 'School Head Current and Newly Appointed SGC M', '500', 'Prerequisite activity for effective SBM implementation.\r\nSupports SBM Principle I (Leadership and Governance).\r\nOutputs serve as key Means of Verification (MOVs) for SBM Level II–III validation.', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
(3888, 'SIP Review and AIP Planning Workshop', 'To review and analyze the implementation status and results of the current School Improvement Plan (SIP).\r\nTo collaboratively formulate an Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) aligned with school priorities, learner needs, and SBM principles.', 'Reviewed and updated SIP with identified gaps, accomplishments, and priority areas.\r\nApproved Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) aligned with SIP targets.\r\nDocumented stakeholder inputs and agreed action points.\r\nWorkshop documentation (attendance sheets, minutes, photos).', 'Presentation and analysis of school performance data and accomplishments.\r\nGroup workshops and collaborative planning sessions.\r\nStakeholder consultation and consensus‑building.\r\nValidation and approval of SIP revisions and AIP outputs.', 'Quarter 1 to Quarter 2 (June–September) or at', 'School Head School Planning Team (SPT) Member', '300', 'Critical planning activity for operationalizing SBM at the school level.\r\nSupports SBM Principle I (Leadership and Governance) and Principle IV (Management of Resources).\r\nOutputs serve as primary Means of Verification (MOVs) for SBM Level II–III validation.', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
(3889, 'Learning Action Cells (LACs)', 'To continuously improve teaching practices through collaborative learning and professional dialogue among teachers.\r\nTo address identified instructional gaps and learner needs using shared experiences, best practices, and evidence‑based strategies.', 'Regularly conducted and documented LAC sessions.\r\nImproved lesson plans, teaching strategies, and classroom practices.\r\nIdentified instructional solutions and action plans addressing learner needs.\r\nLAC documentation (attendance, session notes, action plans, photos).', 'Professional learning discussions and peer collaboration.\r\nSharing of best practices, lesson demonstrations, and classroom observations.\r\nProblem‑solving sessions based on learner performance data.\r\nReflection, feedback, and action planning.', 'Monthly / Throughout the School Year', 'School Head LAC Leaders/Facilitators Teachers', '4000', 'Supports SBM Principle II (Curriculum and Learning) and Principle III (Accountability and Continuous Improvement).\r\nRequired professional development activity under DepEd guidelines.\r\nOutputs serve as Means of Verification (MOVs) for SBM Level II–III validation.', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
(3890, 'Instructional & Program Implementation', 'To effectively implement instructional and school programs aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).\r\nTo improve teaching–learning processes and learner performance through well‑planned, needs‑based, and out', 'To effectively implement instructional and school programs aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).\r\nTo improve teaching–learning processes and learner performance through well‑planned, needs‑based, and outcomes‑focused programs.', 'Execution of planned instructional and support programs based on AIP timelines.\r\nClassroom‑based instruction using appropriate strategies and instructional materials.\r\nCoordination among teachers, coordinators, and school leaders.\r\nContinuous monitoring and documentation of program implementation.', 'Throughout the School Year', 'School Head Teachers Program Coordinators Sch', '500', 'Core activity in achieving school and learner performance targets.\r\nAnchored on SBM Principle II (Curriculum and Learning) and supported by Principle III (Accountability and Continuous Improvement).\r\nOutputs serve as essential Means of Verification (MOVs) for SBM Level II–III validation.', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
(3891, 'Teachers\' INSET Plus Revised MATATAG Curriculum Implementation and ICT capacity building', '1. Upgrade Teaching Competency of 100% teachers\r\n2. Improve morale retention', '1. 1 INSET-100% attendance\r\n2. All Teachers VS on IPCRF\r\n3. LRs uploaded on LRMDS', 'Scholarship Tie-up, Peer coaching', 'October 2026', 'School Head, MT,  All Teachers, Speaker', '5000', '100% compliance to MATATAG training. IPCRF increased by 0.30. LRs Quality assured by PSDS', 2026, 128962, 60, 12, 26),
(3892, 'Strengthening School Governing Council (SGC)', 'To enhance shared leadership and decision-making.', 'Functional and active SGC', 'Conduct Regular meetings.\r\nInitiate trainings to improve leadership and to have role clarification activities.', '1st quarter', 'School Governing Council ', '5000', '', 2026, 129749, 105, 12, 20),
(3893, 'Monitoring & Evaluation Activities', 'To regularly track the implementation and performance of school programs, projects, and activities (PPAs) based on the AIP.\r\nTo identify gaps, issues, and areas for improvement to support evidence‑based decision‑making and continuous school improveme', 'Regular monitoring and evaluation reports.\r\nIdentified strengths, gaps, and action points in program implementation.\r\nUpdated implementation status of PPAs.\r\nDocumentation such as monitoring tools, accomplishment reports, and minutes of meetings.', 'Use of monitoring tools, checklists, and performance indicators.\r\nCollection and analysis of quantitative and qualitative data.\r\nConduct of review meetings and feedback sessions.\r\nDocumentation and reporting of findings for corrective and improvement actions.', 'Quarterly / Throughout the School Year', 'School Head School Planning Team (SPT) Progra', '2000', 'Supports SBM Principle III (Accountability and Continuous Improvement).\r\nResults serve as basis for program adjustment, AIP refinement, and School Report Card (SRC) preparation.\r\nOutputs are key Means of Verification (MOVs) for SBM Level II–III validation.', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
