(3900, 'Action Research Activities', 'To address identified learning, instructional, and school management issues through systematic, evidence‑based inquiry.\r\nTo promote reflective practice and use research findings to improve curriculum delivery, learner outcomes, and school performance', 'To address identified learning, instructional, and school management issues through systematic, evidence‑based inquiry.\r\nTo promote reflective practice and use research findings to improve curriculum delivery, learner outcomes, and school performance.', 'Identification of priority problems based on monitoring and assessment data.\r\nPreparation and approval of action research proposals following DepEd guidelines.\r\nImplementation of interventions and data gathering.\r\nAnalysis, reflection, documentation, and sharing of results through LACs, INSETs, or school forums.', 'Throughout the School Year (Proposal developm', 'Teachers (Teacher‑Researchers) School Head Ma', '3000', 'Supports SBM Principle III (Accountability and Continuous Improvement) and strengthens SBM Principle II (Curriculum and Learning).\r\nResearch outputs inform instructional improvement, planning, and policy decisions.\r\nCompleted studies serve as key Means of Verification (MOVs) for SBM Level II–III validation.', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
(3901, 'Resource Inventory & Programming', 'To systematically identify and document available financial, human, physical, and learning resources of the school.\r\nTo ensure proper programming and allocation of resources aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Pla', 'Updated and validated inventory of school resources (financial, human, physical, learning, and ICT).\r\nIdentified resource gaps and priority needs.\r\nResource programming plan aligned with SIP/AIP priorities.\r\nDocumentation such as inventory lists, matrices, and minutes of meetings.', 'Conduct of annual inventory using standard checklists and tools.\r\nValidation of inventory results through consultations with coordinators and stakeholders.\r\nAnalysis of gaps and prioritization of needs.\r\nPreparation of a resource programming plan linked to SIP/AIP targets.', 'Annually (usually Quarter 1 of the School Yea', 'School Head Property Custodian School Plannin', '2000', 'Supports SBM Principle IV (Management of Resources).\r\nInventory and programming results serve as basis for budgeting, procurement, and partnership building.\r\nOutputs are important Means of Verification (MOVs) for SBM Level II–III validation.', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
