(3904, 'Brigada Eskwela', 'To mobilize community stakeholders in preparing, repairing, and improving school facilities prior to the opening of classes.\r\nTo strengthen school–community partnership and shared responsibility in providing a safe, clean, and conducive learning envi', 'Improved school facilities, classrooms, and grounds.\r\nIncreased stakeholder participation and volunteerism.\r\nIdentified and addressed minor repair and maintenance needs.\r\nBrigada Eskwela accomplishment report with documentation (photos, attendance sheets, inventory of donations).', 'Organization of a Brigada Eskwela Committee and task groups.\r\nCommunity mobilization through meetings, announcements, and coordination with LGUs and partners.\r\nConduct of cleaning, minor repairs, repainting, and maintenance activities.\r\nDocumentation and reporting of accomplishments and donations received.', 'May – June (Prior to the opening of the Schoo', 'School Head Teachers and Non‑Teaching Personn', '500', 'Key community‑based initiative under SBM Principle IV (Management of Resources).\r\nPromotes shared ownership, transparency, and partnership.\r\nOutputs serve as vital Means of Verification (MOVs) for SBM Level II–III validation and stakeholder engagement indicators.', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
(3905, 'Recognition of Stakeholders & Personnel ', 'To acknowledge and appreciate the contributions, milestone achievements, and exemplary performance of school personnel and stakeholders.\r\nTo motivate continued participation, commitment, and ownership in school programs and SBM implementation.', 'Recognized and awarded school personnel and stakeholders.\r\nIncreased morale, motivation, and engagement of personnel and partners.\r\nDocumentation of recognition activities (certificates, program, attendance sheets, photos).', 'Identification and validation of awardees based on clear criteria and accomplishments.\r\nConduct of recognition ceremonies during assemblies, meetings, or school programs.\r\nIssuance of certificates, tokens, or commendations.\r\nDocumentation and dissemination of recognition highlights.', 'Annually (usually Quarter 4) or during culmin', 'School Head School Governing Council (SGC) Me', '4000', 'Supports SBM Principle I (Leadership and Governance) and Principle IV (Management of Resources).\r\nReinforces a culture of appreciation, motivation, and shared accountability.\r\nOutputs serve as Means of Verification (MOVs) for SBM Level II–III validation.', 2026, 129305, 61, 12, 11),
