(3959, 'THE MORE, THE MERRIER PALAN\r\n', '\"To increase at least 10% of the enrolled learners for SY 2026-2027 from the baseline SY 2025- 2026 of 70.\r\n Learners to be registered in school ages from 12 – 16   \"\r\n', '- 10% increase on the learners’ population for SY 2026-2027\r\n', '\"1.	Conduct Barangay Mapping with partner BHW and Prk. President\r\n2.	Orientation of teachers assigned during the Early Enrolment \r\n3.	Campaign for enrolment during local activities  \r\n-	Advocacy Campaign \r\n-	PTA Assembly \r\n-	4Ps Meeting \r\n4.	Joined Barangay functionary session.\r\n5.	Print /Hang tarpaulin and other campaign ads \r\n6.	Social Media Campaign\r\n7.	Mobile Enrollment Booth\"\r\n', 'January to December 2026', '\"School Head,  Teachers, Parents, Stakeholder', '29200.00', '', 2026, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
(3960, '\"Project S.M.A.R.T\r\n\r\n(Science and Math Advancement\r\nFor Real World Thinking)\"\r\n', '100% school-based participation to the documentation and showcasing the students’ capabilities through science and Mathematics fun activities.\r\n\r\n', '\"100% school-based participation in the documentation and showcasing the students\' capabilities through science and mathematics fun activities.\r\n\r\n*Attendance in the Division science and Math competition\r\n\r\n', '\"1.Crafting of Program for Science and Mathematics Celebration\r\n2. Purchase of Tower of Hanoi, Rubik’s Cubes, Scientific Calculators, graphing board, Tokens and Certificates, Tarpaulin, and Science Experiment Materials.\r\n3. Program Implementation\r\n4. Assessment and Evaluation     5.Listing of Laboratory Apparatus. \r\n6.Purchase of science and math instructional materials and supplies\r\n7.Conduct class observation and monitoring\r\n8.Participation in all Science and math activities\"\r\n\r\n', 'September 2026', 'School Head, Science and Mathematics Coordina', '27000.00', '', 2026, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
(3961, 'PROJECT SILANG\r\n', ' To keep at-risk learners in school and ensure their completion by strengthening ADM-(SII) support and targeted interventions under Project SILANG.\r\n', '100% promotion and completion rites.\r\n', '\"*Crafting of Project SILANG Work Action Plan (WAP)\r\n*Identification of LARDO\'s \r\n*Purchase of instructional materials to support SII program participants   and the teacher’s adviser                    \r\n*SLAC Session \r\n*Teachersorientation\r\n*Conduct monitoring and evaluation \r\n*Submission of report\r\n*LIS Tagging                  \r\n* Parents orientation                 \r\n*Conduct Home Visitations                     \r\n*Module Distribution and Retrieval    \r\n*Establish stakeholders’ partnership \"\r\n', 'January 2026 to December 2026', '\"School Head ADM Coordinator Teachers        ', '7150.00', '', 2026, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
(3962, 'Build Our Better School', 'Help participants understand and apply the principles of School-Based Management by collaboratively identifying school issues and creating realistic action plans.', 'Participants will:\r\n\r\nUnderstand SBM principles in practice\r\nDevelop collaboration skills\r\nCreate actionable school improvement ideas\r\nRecognize the importance of stakeholder involvement', '1. Warm-Up (15 minutes): “Our Ideal School”\r\nAsk participants:\r\n“If resources were not a problem, what would your ideal school look like?”\r\n\r\n2. Identify Key Issues (20 minutes): “Reality Check”\r\nEach group lists:\r\n3–5 major problems in the school (e.g., low reading levels, absenteeism, lack of facilities)\r\nWrite each issue on sticky notes.\r\n\r\n3. SBM Connection (15 minutes)\r\nIntroduce or review key SBM principles:\r\nLeadership and Governance\r\nCurriculum and Learning\r\nAccountability and Continuous Improvement\r\nResource Management\r\nGroups categorize their identified issues under these areas.\r\n\r\n4. Action Planning (40 minutes): “From Problem to Plan”\r\nEach group selects one priority issue and fills out this template:\r\nProblem:\r\nRoot Cause:\r\nProposed Solution:\r\nPeople Involved: (teachers, parents, LGU, students)\r\nResources Needed:\r\nTimeline:\r\nSuccess Indicators:\r\n\r\n5. Presentation and Feedback (20 minutes)\r\nEach group presents their plan (3–5 minutes)\r\nOthers give constructive feedback\r\n\r\n6. Reflection (10 minutes)\r\nAsk:\r\nWhat did you learn about shared decision-making?\r\nHow can SBM improve your school?\r\nWhat role will you personally take?', '1.5 to 2 hours', 'Teachers School heads Parents / PTA members S', '2490', 'This activity highlights the importance of collaboration and shared responsibility in improving our school through School-Based Management. By working together, we can turn identified challenges into practical solutions that benefit our learners and the entire school community.', 2026, 129320, 61, 12, 11),
(3963, '\"Project G.R.O.W Hub     ( Green Resources and Opportunities for Wellness)\r\n\r\n\"\r\n', 'To create a sustainable garden space where students can engage in hands-on learning activities on Crop Production and advocate environmental stewardship, and promote wellness\r\n', '\"established gulayan sa paaralan\r\n-sustained feeding program\"\r\n', '\"*Purchase of Instructional Materials for Crop Production \r\n*Crafting Work Action Plan \r\n*Preparation of Lesson Plans\r\n*Conduct class monitoring and observation\r\n*Preparation of the “Gulayan sa Paaralan” Implementation\r\n*Pasundayag\r\n*Monitoring and Evaluation\"\r\n', 'January 2026 to December 2026', '\"School Head, Class Adviser, Teachers,  PTA O', '55400', '', 2026, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
