(3987, 'Project “KUSINA SANDAWA”\r\n', '\"To enhance the quality of hands-on learning experience.\r\n \r\n- To foster student engagement and interest in food preparation.\r\n \r\n- To integrate local and sustainable practices in food preparation.\"\r\n', '\"Students can independently prepare simple dishes.\r\n\r\n- Increased participation and enthusiasm in class activities.\r\n 3. improved student performance in practical assessment.                4. conduct minor repair for TLE room \"\r\n', '\"*Purchase of instructional materials and kitchenware supplies\r\n*Crafting of Work Action Plan\r\n* Minor repair of TLE room/Kitchen\r\n*Conduct of Class monitoring and coaching\r\n*Pasundayag\"\r\n', 'January to December 2026', '\"School Head,  TLE Coordinator Class Advisers', '46400.00', '', 2026, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
(3988, '\"Project “KABÁKKÁRAN” \r\n(Sports Development Program)\"\r\n', '\"*To promote physical fitness, nurture athletic talents, and instill discipline and teamwork among students.\r\n\r\n*To provide structured opportunities for learners to engage in various sports activities, enhance their skills, and develop a healthy life', '\"*Produce competitive athletes \r\n\r\n*Holistic development of athletes\r\n\r\n*Enhance camaraderie and sportsmanship in all learners and athletes\"\r\n', '\"* Craft Work Action Plan\r\n* Conduct PTA meetings\r\n*Implementation of daily training habits\r\n*Conduct school athletic program\r\n*Conduct medical monitoring\r\n*Purchase of sports equipment and activities\r\n*Participation in the higher-level competition \r\n*3 o’clock Training habit\"\r\n', 'January to December 2026', 'School Head and Sports Coordinator Teachers', '45800.00', '', 2026, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
(3989, 'Enclosure and Securing of the School Activity Center with Yellow CAUTION Markings; NOW THE INITIALLY COMPLETED SCHOOL ACTIVITY CENTER UNDER SCHOOL PROJECT BANGON SENTRO', 'Ensure learner safety and call for urgent rehabilitation or replacement of unsafe facility', 'Secured activity center and increased stakeholder awareness for rehabilitation support.  NOW THE INITIALLY COMPLETED SCHOOL ACTIVITY CENTER UNDER SCHOOL PROJECT BANGON SENTRO', 'Safety inspection, enclosure marking, stakeholder mobilization', 'January 2026', 'School Head, SGC, Stakeholders, Parents', '', 'We reach the initial completion of the repair of our School Activity Center - PROJECT BANGON SENTRO. Despite limited materials, we made it possible by reusing old roofing, with only 17 new sheets generously provided by our Barangay Officials.  We remain hopeful that new roofing materials will soon be available for the full restoration of our Activity Center.', 2026, 128452, 57, 12, 120),
(3990, 'Project BRIDGE – Building Resources for Inclusive Digital Growth in Education\r\n', 'To help students and educators develop the necessary skills for navigating and utilizing technology responsibly and effectively.\r\n', 'Students and educators demonstrate improved digital literacy, showing competence in using online platforms, applying technology in learning and teaching, and practicing responsible and ethical use of digital tools.\r\n', '1. Needs Assessment                                    2. Platform Selection and Procurement           3. Capacity Building/Training                        4. Deployment and Integration                            5. Monitoring and Support                                 6. Evaluation and Improvement\r\n', 'January 2026 to December 2026', 'School Head                   ICT Coordinator', '25000.00', '', 2026, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
(3991, 'SMART LEARNERS\r\n', 'To develop students’ critical thinking, creativity, and problem-solving abilities by exposing them to hands-on, experiential, and learner-centered training /activities/competition.\r\n', '100%  selected and qualified learners join Festival of talent\r\n', 'Conduct school-based selection of learners in different discipline for Festival of talent                         *Conduct orientation of parents *Conduct weekly assessment in preperation for competition *Corroborate with other schools for training of learners and teachers\r\n', 'January to December 2026', 'Teachers        School Head Learners', '26900.00', '', 2026, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
(3992, 'Project EQUITY+ (GAD)\r\n', '\"Raise Gender Awareness and Foster Inclusivity.\r\n\r\nEncourage Gender-Responsive Teaching and Curriculum Development.\r\n\r\nProvide Safe, Supportive, and Equitable Learning Environments\"\r\n', '\"Learning materials, modules, and assessments revised to include gender-sensitive language and equity-focused content.\r\n\r\nActive GAD Focal Point System (GFPS) at the school level, supported by regular meetings, functioning GAD corners, and updated sex-disaggregated data.\r\n\r\nSuccessful execution of GAD-related events.\"\r\n', '\"Capacity-Building: GAD Seminars and Trainings.\r\n\r\nAction Planning: School GAD Committees & Data Systems.\r\n\r\nGender-Focused School Events & National Campaigns.\"\r\n', 'June - December 2026', 'School Head, GAD focal person', '36650.00', '', 2026, 306176, 105, 12, 23),
