(3997, 'Re-activation of the School Governing Council (SGC)', 'To strengthen participatory leadership and involve stakeholders in decision-making.', 'Signed SGC Resolutions, Minutes of Meetings, and Election Reports.', 'Conduct of SGC Elections, Orientation on Roles, and Quarterly Meetings.', 'June - July 2025', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents, LGU Reps', '2000', 'Essential for Leadership & Governance pillar.', 2026, 302077, 61, 12, 11),
(3998, 'The Blueprint Project: Building Stronger Literacy and Numeracy Foundations.', 'To improve learner performance in reading and math through data-driven tracking.', 'Monthly Progress Reports and Learners\' Profiles (PHIL-IRI and RMA Reports)', 'Pre-Test & Post-Test, Regular Reading Remediation, and \"Numeracy Habit\" drills.', 'Aug 2025 - March 2026', 'Coordinators, Teachers, and School Head ', '5000', 'Directly addresses the Curriculum & Instruction pillar.', 2026, 302077, 61, 12, 11),
(3999, 'Building Future for ALS learners', 'Assist ALS learners in strengthening their skills that would help them be prepared for certification as elementary or high school completers', '100% of ALS learners obtain certification as elementary and high school completers', '* Expose them to literacy and numeracy-focused activities as well as integrated and life skills like mock comprehension tests, essay writing practice and vocabulary builders, numeracy workshops                                                                                                                                                             * examination simulation ', 'year round', 'School head, ALS teacher and Coordinator', '2000.00', 'Focus on indicator 3', 2026, 129549, 107, 12, 57),
(4000, 'Stakeholders in Action: SBM Simulation', 'To help participants experience shared decision-making and understand the roles of different stakeholders in implementing School-Based Management.', 'Participants will understand stakeholder roles in SBM, practice collaborative decision-making, appreciate diverse perspectives and strengthen accountability and teamwork', 'I. Introduction (10 minutes)\r\nThe participants will have short discussion about Shared leadership, Transparency, and Community participation. \r\nII. Role Assignment (10 minutes)\r\nParticipants are grouped and assigned roles such as School Head, Teacher, Parent, Student Leader, Community Member / LGU, \r\nIII. Scenario Simulation (30 minutes): “The School Challenge”\r\nEach group is given a scenario, for example:\r\nLow student attendance\r\nPoor reading performance\r\nLack of school facilities\r\n\r\nIV. Decision-Making Output (30 minutes)\r\nEach group prepares:\r\n\r\nIdentified problem\r\nAgreed solution\r\nRoles of each stakeholder\r\nPlan of action\r\n\r\nV. Presentation and Reflection (30 minutes)\r\nGroups present their solutions\r\nDiscuss:\r\nWas it easy to agree?\r\nWhich roles were most challenging?\r\nHow did collaboration help?\r\n', '1.5 to 2 hours', 'Teachers School head / administrators Parents', '2300', 'This activity emphasizes the value of shared decision-making by allowing stakeholders to actively participate in solving real school issues. It strengthens collaboration, accountability, and mutual understanding, which are essential for effective School-Based Management.', 2026, 129320, 61, 12, 11),
(4001, 'SBM Scorecard Workshop: Measuring Our Progress', 'To help participants assess current school practices and develop improvement strategies using an SBM-based scorecard.', 'Participants will:\r\n\r\nUnderstand how to assess school performance using SBM tools\r\nIdentify strengths and areas for improvement\r\nDevelop data-based action plans\r\nStrengthen a culture of accountability and continuous improvement', '1. Introduction (10 minutes): “Why Measure?”\r\n\r\nDiscuss the importance of:\r\n\r\nMonitoring school performance\r\nData-driven decision-making\r\nContinuous improvement in SBM\r\n\r\n2. Grouping and Distribution (10 minutes)\r\n\r\nDivide participants into groups and provide each with an SBM scorecard covering areas like:\r\n\r\nLeadership and Governance\r\nCurriculum and Learning\r\nAccountability\r\nResource Management\r\n\r\n3. School Self-Assessment (30 minutes): “Where Are We Now?”\r\nGroups rate the school based on the scorecard:\r\nIdentify strengths\r\nIdentify gaps or weak areas\r\n\r\n4. Analysis and Planning (40 minutes): “How Do We Improve?”\r\nEach group selects one weak area and develops:\r\nImprovement goal\r\nSpecific actions\r\nResponsible persons\r\nTimeline\r\nSuccess indicators\r\n\r\n5. Presentation (20 minutes)\r\nGroups present:\r\nKey findings\r\nProposed improvements\r\n\r\n6. Reflection (10 minutes)\r\nAsk participants:\r\nWhat did the data reveal about our school?\r\nWhat should be prioritized?\r\nHow can we sustain improvement?', '1.5 to 2 hours', 'School head / administrators Teachers PTA rep', '3150', 'This activity highlights the importance of using data and structured assessment tools to guide school improvement under School-Based Management. It empowers stakeholders to identify gaps, set priorities, and collaboratively plan strategies for continuous progress.', 2026, 129320, 61, 12, 11),
(4002, 'Develop and implement SBM monitoring tools', 'Improves learning outcomes', 'A regular monitoring report on SBM shall be submitted', 'Group discussion or role play', 'Whole year', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA', '2000', 'A well organized reports is being submitted to the central office.', 2026, 129319, 61, 12, 11),
(4003, 'Quarter SMEA (School Monitoring & Evaluation) Conference', 'To assess school performance vs. targets and address (Bottlenecks).', 'SMEA Reports and other supporting documents on the conduct of activities', 'Data presentation, Root Cause Analysis, and Adjustment of AIP/SIP', 'Every end month of the every Quarter of the S', 'School Head, SMEA Team and Other Teachers Inv', '3000', 'Core of the Accountability & Continuous Improvement pillar.', 2026, 302077, 61, 12, 11),
(4004, 'Educational Content Creation', 'Provide engaging learning resources that build strong reading, writing, and basic math skills, supporting learners in achieving proficiency level expected of them', 'Quality-assured localized/indigenized teaching modules', 'Workshop on contextualization and localized resource mapping', 'semestral', 'Teachers, LRMDS coordinator', '5000.00', 'Focus on indicator 4', 2026, 129549, 107, 12, 57),
(4005, 'Conduct LAC session', 'To build strong capacity and camarra deri with teachers and parents,', ' To be able to improve teachers and parents knowledge with regards to SBM.', 'Call and set a date for the LAC session. Send a memo to all concern to participate the session.', 'June 2026 and March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA', '2000', 'Teachers and parents have already the knowledge on how the SBM is undertaken.', 2026, 129319, 61, 12, 11),
(4006, 'Transparency Board & E-Liquidation Posting', 'To ensure fiscal transparency and 100% liquidation of school funds.', 'Updated Transparency Board (Physical & Digital) and Audit Reports.', 'Regular posting of MOOE allocation, expenses, and donation reports (Brigada Eskwela) and other donation for other activities supported by stakeholders.', 'Monthly  or Quarterly (Year-round) of 2026', 'School Head, School Administrative Officer, P', '000', 'Aligned with Resource Management pillar. Budgetary requirements has no specific amount due to unforeseen donations and other sources of funds. ', 2026, 302077, 61, 12, 11),
