(4134, '1. Re-orientation on Enhanced SBM Framework and Digital SBM Tools', 'To re-align stakeholders with the 2026 SBM principles (Leadership, Curriculum, Accountability, Resource Management) and introduce digital platforms for SBM', '1. Updated SBM Team composition\r\n2. 100% of members trained on digital SBM tools (e.g., SBM Dashboard, e-IPCRF)\r\n3. Signed Commitment Wall', 'Hybrid seminar-workshop (face-to-face + LMS modules). Pre-assessment and post-assessment done via digital forms.', 'Week 1–2 (June 2026)', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, ICT Coordinator', 'PHP 8,000 (Food, internet load, printing of modules)', 'Partnership with LGU ICT office for free digital tools training', 2026, 129672, 107, 12, 69),
(4135, '2. Participatory Assessment of Current SBM Level (Levels 1–3)', 'To determine the school’s current SBM level based on the revised 2026 Access indicators', '1. Completed SBM Level Assessment Tool\r\n2. Identified gaps in 4 SBM dimensions\r\n3. Priority Improvement Plan', 'Focus group discussions (FGDs) per stakeholder group + self-assessment checklist using mobile devices. External validator from Division Office.', 'Week 3–4 (June 2026)', 'School Head, Teachers, Non-teaching staff, PT', 'PHP 5,000 (Snacks, printing, mobile load)', 'Secure permit from Division SBM Coordinator', 2026, 129672, 107, 12, 69),
(4136, '3. Development of 2026-2027 School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP)', 'To co-create evidence-based, community-driven SIP/AIP anchored on SBM principles', '1. Approved 2026–2027 SIP\r\n2. 2026 AIP with budget matrix\r\n3. Results-based M&E plan', 'Workshop using PESTLE analysis and problem tree. Voting via mentimeter.', 'Month of July 2026 (3 Saturdays)', 'School Planning Team, SBM Core Group, PTA, ba', 'PHP 12,000 (Materials, meals, reproduction of SIP)', 'SIP to be uploaded to the school’s SBM portal for transparency', 2026, 129672, 107, 12, 69),
(4138, '4. Establishment of SBM Communication and Feedback Hubs', 'To ensure transparent, real-time flow of SBM-related information and grievances', '1. Physical SBM Bulletin Board (updated weekly)\r\n2. Digital SBM Feedback Hub (e.g., FB page, Google Site, or SMS channel)\r\n3. Monthly SBM E-Report posted', 'Install QR codes for anonymous feedback. Assign SBM Secretary to collate responses. Weekly flag ceremony updates.', 'August–September 2026 (ongoing)', 'SBM Secretary, ICT Coordinator, PTA Informati', 'PHP4,500 (Tarpaulin, QR code printing, domain/hosting optional)', 'Link feedback system to School Governing Council (SGC)', 2026, 129672, 107, 12, 69),
(4139, '5. Quarterly SBM Performance Review and Coaching', 'To monitor progress of SBM implementation and provide technical assistance to low-performing areas', '1. Quarterly SBM Progress Report (June, Sept, Dec, March)\r\n2. Coaching logs for 3 identified challenge areas\r\n3. Revised action issues matrix', 'Use PDSA cycle (Plan-Do-Study-Act). SBM Leads present data dashboard. Coaching by Master Teachers.', 'Last week of Sept, Dec, March', 'SBM Coordinator, Master Teachers, School Head', 'PHP6,000 (Coaching materials, transportation, performance board)', 'Integrate into regular INSET and LAC sessions', 2026, 129672, 107, 12, 69),
(4140, '6. Stakeholders’ Accountability Assembly (General Assembly)', 'To present evidence of SBM outcomes and gather feedback for continuous improvement', '1. Signed accountability report\r\n2. New stakeholder suggestions logged\r\n3. Reaffirmation of resource contributions', 'Open forum + presentation of accomplishment vs. targets using SBM Scorecard. Distribution of stakeholder satisfaction survey.', 'Mid-November 2026', 'School Head, All teachers, Parents, Alumni, B', 'PHP10,000 (Venue setup, snacks, certificates, sound system)', 'Secure LGU support for venue and sound to reduce cost', 2026, 129672, 107, 12, 69),
(4141, '7. Mid-Year SBM Assessment and Level-Up Intervention', 'To move the school from current SBM level to next level (e.g., Level 2 to Level 3) by year-end', '1. Mid-year SBM gap analysis report\r\n2. Triage plan for weakest indicator\r\n3. Cluster benchmarking activity', 'Internal validation using ACCESS tool. Benchmarking with a Level 3 SBM school in the division. Division SBM team to provide TA.', 'December 2026', 'SBM Core Team, School Head, Division SBM Foca', 'PHP7, 000 (Fuel for benchmarking, meals, documentation)', 'Benchmarking requires prior MOA with host school', 2026, 129672, 107, 12, 69),
(4142, '8. Annual SBM Report, Documentation, and Award Readiness', 'To consolidate accomplishments and prepare for Division SBM Validation and Awards', '. End-of-year SBM Portfolio (digital + physical)\r\n2. 2026 SBM Accomplishment Report\r\n3. Video documentation of best practices', 'Rubric-based portfolio organization. Use of Canva for e-portfolio. ', 'February–March 2027', 'SBM Documentation Team, School Head, ICT', 'PHP15,000 (Binding, printing, video editing)', 'Target: Gold level SBM award or at least Level 2 validated', 2026, 129672, 107, 12, 69),
(4143, '9. Student-Led SBM Innovation Fair', 'To empower learners as co-leaders in school governance and innovation', '1. At least 5 student-proposed SBM projects (e.g., waste-to-cash program, peer tutorial hub)\r\n2. Student Innovation Grant awarded\r\n3. SBM Student Council Charter', 'Student proposal writing competition. Selection via SGC panel. Mentoring by teachers. Implementation of top 3 projects with mini-grants.', 'October 2026 (Fair Week)', 'Student Government, SBM Coordinator, Youth Fo', 'PHP8,000 (Prizes, materials for student projects, tokens)', 'Link to DepEd’s Youth Formation and Learner Governance Program', 2026, 129672, 107, 12, 69),
(4144, '10. Sustainability and Exit Protocol Planning for SBM Transitions', 'To ensure continuity of SBM gains beyond SY 2026 (e.g., change in school head or leadership)', '1. SBM Sustainability Plan for SY 2027–2028\r\n2. SBM Exit Document with turnover checklist\r\n3. Digital archive of all SBM artifacts', 'Workshop with SGC and next-in-line leaders. Document all processes, logins, partnerships. Develop simplified SBM continuity manual.', 'January–February 2027', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, SGC Chair', 'PHP 6,000 (Printing of manual, binding, storage device, snacks)', 'Highly recommended for schools with frequent leadership changes', 2026, 129672, 107, 12, 69),
(4147, 'Needs Assessment and Initial Planning', 'To assess the current state of school management; to identify areas for improvement and define the needs of the school community; and to create a baseline for the implementation of SBM.', 'Clearly defined priorities for SBM implementation.', 'Focus group discussions and brainstorming sessions.', '6 months', 'School Head, School Management Team, Teachers', '3000', 'Successful assessment requires active participation from all stakeholders.', 2026, 502785, 60, 12, 26),
