(4277, 'Pre-Implementation:\r\nActivities:\r\n1. Conduct SBM self-assessment using the 42 indicators\r\n2. Analyze indicators with “Rarely Manifested” and “Not Yet Manifested”\r\n3. Prioritize interventions per SBM dimension\r\n4. Conduct strategic planning workshop (', 'Pre-Implementation:\r\nObjectives:\r\n1. Establish baseline status across 6 SBM dimensions\r\n2. Identify priority improvement areas\r\n3. Focus planning on weak areas\r\n4. Develop SBM-based improvement plan\r\n5. Strengthen governance structure\r\n6. Strengthen ', 'Pre-Implementation:\r\nExpected Outputs:\r\n1. Comprehensive SBM Baseline Profile Report\r\n(with ratings across 6 dimensions and validated MOVs)\r\n2. Gap Analysis Report\r\n(list of “Rarely” and “Not Yet Manifested” indicators per dimension)\r\n3. Prioritized Intervention Matrix / Action List\r\n(ranked based on urgency, impact, and feasibility)\r\n4. Draft SBM Action Plan aligned with SIP/AIP\r\n(with timelines, persons involved, and resources)\r\n5. Organized and Functional School Governance Council (SGC)\r\n(with defined roles and meeting structure)\r\n6. Reorganized and Active PTA Structure\r\n(with elected officers and engagement plan)\r\n7. Revised SIP aligned with SBM Findings\r\n(evidence-based and responsive to gaps)\r\nImplementation and Monitoring:\r\nDimension 1: CURRICULUM AND TEACHING (Indicators 1–8)	\r\nExpected Outputs:\r\n1. Improved learner achievement in Math, Science, and Reading based on quarterly assessments and NAT results.\r\n2. 100% of teachers produce and utilize contextualized instructional materials aligned with MELCs.\r\n3. At least 4 documented test item analysis reports with improved test validity and reliability.\r\n4. Increased number of ALS learners completing and passing certification requirements.\r\nDimension 2: LEARNING ENVIRONMENT (Indicators 9–18)\r\nExpected Outputs:\r\n1. Zero reported cases of bullying and child abuse within the school year.\r\n2. Fully functional DRRM system with quarterly conducted drills and updated preparedness plans.\r\n3. Established and operational guidance and counseling services with documented learner support cases.\r\n4. Improved and more inclusive facilities accommodating PWD and SPED learners.\r\nDimension 3:  LEADERSHIP (Indicators 19–22)\r\nExpected Outputs:\r\n1. Updated and SBM-aligned SIP based on data and stakeholder consultation.\r\n2. Active and functional school-community planning team with documented meetings and outputs.\r\n3. Functional SSG/SPG with active participation in school governance and programs.\r\n4. At least 1–2 innovations\r\nDimension 4:  GOVERNANCE AND ACCOUNTABILITY (Indicators 23–28)\r\nExpected Outputs:\r\n1. Ensured SIP implementation through AIP\r\n(100% implementation of approved PPAs based on AIP.)\r\n2. Improved governance participation\r\n(Functional SGC and PTA with regular meetings and active involvement in school programs.)\r\n3. Strengthen monitoring and evaluation\r\n(Four (4) quarterly M&E reports completed and submitted.)\r\n4. Improved stakeholder satisfaction\r\n(Increased stakeholder satisfaction rating based on survey results.)\r\nDimension 5: HUMAN RESOURCE AND TEAM DEVELOPMENT (Indicators 29–35)\r\nExpected Outputs:\r\n1. Improved teaching quality through LAC\r\n(Monthly LAC outputs with documented instructional improvements.)\r\n2. Enhanced teacher competencies\r\n100% participation of teachers in professional development activities.\r\n3. Improved personnel motivation\r\n(Quarterly recognition system implemented with documented awards/acknowledgments.)\r\n4. Ensured equitable workload distribution\r\n(Balanced and documented teacher workload schedule implemented.)\r\nDimension 6: FINANCE AND RESOURCE MANAGEMENT (Indicators 36–42)\r\nExpected Outputs:\r\n1. Improved facility safety and condition\r\n(Complete quarterly facility inspection reports with compliance to safety standards.)\r\n2. Improved school infrastructure\r\n(Functional upgraded facilities (library, laboratories, classrooms, and learning spaces).\r\n3. Strengthened ICT systems\r\nFully functional ICT infrastructure supporting teaching and learning processes.\r\n4. Ensure financial accountability\r\n(100% MOOE liquidation compliance with complete and clean financial records.)\r\nPOST-IMPLEMENTATION\r\nExpected Outputs:\r\n1. Measured SBM improvement\r\n(Completed SBM end-line evaluation showing improved ratings across all six dimensions.)\r\n2. Document SBM implementation\r\n(Completed SBM accomplishment report with consolidated MOVs and evidence.)\r\n3. Improved school planning system\r\n(Revised SIP aligned with SBM results and priority improvement areas.)\r\n\r\n', 'PRE-IMPLEMENTATION (SBM ACTION PLAN)\r\nStrategies:\r\n1. Use SBM assessment tool and validation workshop\r\n3. Conduct data analysis workshop per dimension\r\n3. Rank and cluster indicators\r\n4. Facilitate participatory planning with stakeholders\r\n5. Select and orient  members\r\n6. Conduct election and orientation meetings\r\n7. Review SBM results and integrate into SIP\r\nIMPLEMENTATION AND MONITORING\r\nDimension 1: CURRICULUM AND TEACHING (Indicators 1–8)\r\nStrategies:\r\n1. Conduct intervention classes\r\n2. Implement LAC-based development\r\n3. Conduct quarterly review\r\n4. Coordinate with ALS implementers\r\nDimension 2: LEARNING ENVIRONMENT (Indicators 9–18)\r\nStrategies:\r\n1. Conduct campaigns and monitoring\r\n2. DRRM drills\r\n3. Provide counseling services\r\n4. Conduct facility planning\r\nDimension 3:  LEADERSHIP (Indicators 19–22)\r\nStrategies:\r\n1. Implement data-based planning\r\n2. Conduct regular meetings\r\n3. Conduct Leadership training\r\n4. Implement Digital systems\r\nDimension 4:  GOVERNANCE AND ACCOUNTABILITY (Indicators 23–28)\r\nStrategies:\r\n1. Execute programs	SIP/AIP\r\n2. Conduct Regular meetings	Governance plan\r\n3. Conduct Quarterly monitoring	Reports\r\n4. Conduct Surveys	Feedback tools\r\nDimension 5: HUMAN RESOURCE AND TEAM DEVELOPMENT (Indicators 29–35)\r\nStrategies:\r\n1. Conduct Needs-based LAC\r\n2. Conduct Trainings\r\n3. Implement award system Award system\r\n4. Implement Scheduling system\r\nDimension 6: FINANCE AND RESOURCE MANAGEMENT (Indicators 36–42)\r\nStrategies:\r\n1. Conduct Quarterly inspection\r\n2. Conduct Facility development\r\n3. Upgrade systems\r\n4. Monitor system\r\nPOST-IMPLEMENTATION\r\n1. Re-assess SBM Practice\r\n2. Consolidation of MOVs\r\n3. Data-based revision\r\n\r\n', 'June 2026 to April 2027', '1. School Head, Teachers, Planning Team, SGC ', '12,760.00', '1. Ensures accurate baseline data through participatory validation and complete MOV documentation\r\n2. Provides clear evidence-based identification of priority improvement areas\r\n3. Supports focused and strategic planning based on identified gaps\r\n4. Remarks:\r\nEnsures participatory planning and alignment of school improvement priorities\r\n5. Strengthens shared governance and accountability in school management\r\n6. Enhances community involvement and sustained stakeholder participation\r\n7. Ensures data-driven and needs-responsive school improvement planning\r\n', 2026, 304216, 106, 12, 134),
(4278, '1. Presence of non-readers/frustration-level readers and learners with low numeracy skills; limited parental support in home-based reading\r\n2. Gaps in higher-order thinking skills (HOTS); limited structured review and enrichment programs\r\n3. Time con', 'To improve learners’ reading and numeracy skills; reduce non-readers\r\nEnhance critical thinking and problem-solving skills\r\nProvide differentiated instruction\r\nStrengthen teacher professional development\r\nImprove ICT integration\r\nImprove monitoring a', 'Improved reading levels; reading progress records; remediation reports\r\n-HOTS-based activities and improved learner performance\r\n-Group-based remediation and improved learner support\r\n-Teachers with updated skills and CPD credits\r\n-Functional ICT resources and improved digital lessons\r\n-Organized inspection records and reports\r\n-Teacher-made contextualized modules', 'Remedial reading sessions, home-based reading program, peer tutoring, parent involvement activities\r\n-LAC sessions, PBL, enrichment activities, test analysis\r\n-Grouping strategies, station teaching, peer tutoring\r\n-Online trainings, webinars, DepEd-led seminars\r\n-Repair, inventory, request for LGU/donation support\r\n-Standardized forms, digital encoding, filing system\r\n-LAC sessions, collaboration, MELC-based material development', 'Whole yeat round', 'Teachers, Reading Coordinator, Parents, ICT c', '150000', 'Priority concern\r\n-Needs strengthening\r\nOngoing concern\r\nNeeds improvement\r\nNeeds upgrading\r\nNeeds system improvemen', 2026, 129676, 107, 12, 68),
(4279, 'Project SBM \r\n(School-Based Management)\r\n', 'To increase SBM level of Practice from 2 to 3', 'Upskilling teachers on SBM level of practice  \r\nProvision of materials for SBM Corner \r\nConduct TA to teachers on gathering artifacts for SBM pillars  \r\nConduct Monitoring and Evaluation to the teachers on the artifacts gathered on three pillars of SBM', 'Face to Face Lac session, TA program, constant monitoring and evaluation', 'June 2026-April 2027', 'School Head and teachers', '16,000.00', 'To be implemented this SY 2026-2027', 2026, 128787, 104, 12, 131),
