(4291, 'Reactivation and Strengthening of School Governance Council (SGC) of Tapak Elementary School', 'To reactivate the School Governance Council and ensure regular meetings and participation\r\nTo clarify roles and responsibilities of each SGC member\r\nTo strengthen collaboration between school, parents, and community stakeholders\r\nTo support effective', 'Conducted orientation and reorganization of SGC members\r\nApproved SGC Annual Work and Financial Plan\r\nRegular quarterly SGC meetings conducted with minutes\r\nIncreased participation of stakeholders in school programs and decision-making', 'Conduct orientation on SBM and roles of SGC members\r\nReview and update SGC composition and assign clear roles\r\nSchedule and conduct regular meetings (monthly/quarterly)\r\nDevelop Annual Implementation Plan aligned with School Improvement Plan (SIP)\r\nStrengthen communication through group chats and coordination meetings\r\nMonitor and evaluate SGC activities and participation', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head (Chairperson) SGC Members (Teache', '10000.00', 'Sustain active participation and continuous monitoring to ensure functionality of the SGC and support school improvement initiatives.', 2026, 129677, 107, 12, 69),
(4292, 'Conduct Stakeholders Satisfaction Assessment', 'To gather a feedback from internal and external stakeholders to measure satisfaction levels.', '-Survey instruments\r\n-Consolidated Result Reports', '-Develop survey tools\r\n-Distribute online and paper surveys\r\n-Conduct FGD (parents, teachers, students, community)', 'June 2026 to September 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Master Teachers, Paren', '500', 'Ensure at least 80% response', 2026, 128618, 58, 12, 44),
(4293, 'Strengthening Partnerships with Local Industries for TLE-TVL Exposure', 'To establish sustainable partnerships with local industries and business establishments that can provide learners with relevant TLE(for Elementary) exposure and workplace-based learning experiences.', '1. Signed Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) with partner industries \r\n2. List of partner institutions \r\n3. Student exposure activities conducted \r\n4. Improved learner skills and career awareness', '1. Identify possible local industries, enterprises, and business partners within the community. \r\n2. Conduct meetings and consultations with prospective partners. \r\n3. Prepare and sign partnership agreements. \r\n4. Organize educational visits, immersion, demonstrations, and career talks. \r\n5. Monitor and evaluate the effectiveness of the partnership activities.', 'June–August 2026 (Planning); Whole SY (Implem', 'School Head, TLE Teachers, SBM Coordinator, P', '5000', 'Continuous monitoring shall be conducted to ensure sustainability of partnerships and alignment with learner needs.', 2026, 128618, 58, 12, 44),
(4294, 'Development of an Enhanced Stakeholder Service Delivery System', 'To improve the efficiency, accessibility, and responsiveness of school frontline services through innovative and technology-supported systems for stakeholders.', '1. Improved stakeholder assistance process\r\n2. Digital and manual feedback system established\r\n3. Faster response time to stakeholder concerns \r\n4. Increased stakeholder satisfaction', '1. Assess current frontline services and identify service gaps.\r\n2. Constant monitor digital communication platforms such as online inquiry.\r\n3. Develop a feedback mechanism to gather suggestions for service improvement.', 'June–September  2026', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Teachers, SBM C', '1000', 'Continuous improvement shall be based on stakeholder feedback and monitoring results.', 2026, 128618, 58, 12, 44),
(4295, 'Establishment and Operationalization of a Functional School Library', 'To establish a fully functional, accessible, and resource-equipped school library that supports teaching and learning', '- Functional library space established\r\n- Library equipped with adequate books and learning materials\r\n- Library system (cataloging, borrowing) implemented\r\n- Increased learner access to reading resources', 'Phase 1: Assessment & Planning\r\n- Conduct inventory of existing materials\r\nPhase 2: Resource Mobilization\r\n- Request support from LGU, PTA, NGOs, alumni\r\n- Conduct book donation drives (Brigada Eskwela, Adopt-a-Book Program)\r\nPhase 3: Establishment\r\n- Prepare library space (cleaning, minor repairs)\r\n- Install shelves, tables, chairs\r\nPhase 4: Capacity Building\r\n- Assign/designate teacher-librarian\r\nPhase 5: Implementation & Monitoring\r\n- Launch library use program (reading time, class visits)\r\n- Implement borrowing system', 'June 2026 - December 2026', '- School Head - Teacher-Librarian / Assigned ', '50000', 'Sustainability plan needed (continuous book sourcing and maintenance). Encourage stakeholder partnerships for long-term support.', 2026, 128618, 58, 12, 44),
(4296, 'Organization of SBM-TWG', 'To organize School-Based Management Technical Working Group ', 'Organized SBM-Technical Working Group ', 'Organized SBM-TWG with different functions and responsibilities', 'March 2026', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, Teaching Staff', '0', '', 2026, 128778, 104, 12, 130),
(4297, 'Reorientation on the Revised School Management Framework, Assessment Process and Tool (APAT)', 'To conduct reorientation of the School-Based Management-Technical Working Group (SBM-TWG) on the Revised School Management Framework, Assessment Process and Tool (APAT)', 'Reoriented SBM-TWG and teachers on the Revised SBM Framework and APAT', '100% of school personnel reoriented on School-Based Management (SBM) by the School Head and SBM-TWG within the specified timeline.', 'March-June 2026', 'School Head, SBM Coordinators, SBM-TWG, Teach', '0', '', 2026, 128778, 104, 12, 130),
(4298, 'Updating compilation of reports and other documents on the different pillars/dimensions', 'To ensure standard implementation of SBM through gathering of reports and documents', 'Updated status of school-based SBM', 'Updating compilation of reports and other documents on the different pillars/dimensions', 'Year round', 'School Head, School SBM Coordinator, SBM-TWG,', '0', '', 2026, 128778, 104, 12, 130),
(4299, 'Conducting a SBM School Monitoring Evaluation and Assessment', 'To conduct monitoring and evaluation of SBM implementation ', 'Reported status of School SBM Monitoring and Evaluation Assessment', 'Division/Regional Evaluation Team will conduct school-based SBM monitoring and evaluation assessment', 'Year round', 'Division/Regional SBM-TWG, SBM Coordinator, S', '0', '', 2026, 128778, 104, 12, 130);
INSERT INTO `sgod_action_plan` (`id`, `activity`, `objective`, `ex_output`, `metho_strategy`, `time_frame`, `person_involved`, `bud_req`, `remarks`, `fy`, `school_id`, `division`, `region`, `district`) VALUES
(4300, 'Establishment of a Functional Computer Learning Room', 'To provide a functional computer learning room by equipping the existing classroom with operational computers and basic ICT facilities to support digital learning', '- Existing classroom converted into a computer learning room\r\n- Functional computers installed\r\n- Basic ICT equipment operational\r\n- Learners gain access to digital learning resources', 'Phase 1: Assessment and Planning\r\n- Inspect the existing classroom for suitability and assess electrical connections and internet readiness\r\nPhase 2: Resource Mobilization\r\n- Prepare project proposal for stakeholders\r\nPhase 3: Room Preparation\r\n- Repair classroom if needed\r\n- Install electrical outlets, wiring, and safety devices\r\nPhase 4: Equipment Installation\r\n- Install computers, printer, and basic networking equipment\r\n- Test all units for functionality\r\nPhase 5: Implementation and Monitoring\r\n- Assign ICT coordinator or computer teacher\r\n- Develop schedule for class use', 'June 2026- October 2026', '- School Head - ICT Coordinator - Teachers - ', '50000', 'Prioritize partnerships and donations to reduce cost. Sustainability plan for maintenance and upgrading should be included.', 2026, 128618, 58, 12, 44),
(4301, 'Conduct seminar/workshops/meetings on bullying prevention, respect, and empathy', 'PREVENTION AND AWARENESS: To ensure 100% awareness among students, teachers, parents, and staff regarding what constitutes bullying, its forms, and its consequences.', 'Positive school culture, Strong partnership', 'Conduct orientations, seminars, and  campaigns to ensure everyone knows the rules and consequences. (Information Dissemination)', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Guidance Designate, Teachers, Pa', '0.00', '', 2026, 128841, 60, 12, 0),
(4302, 'Engage students in creating visual reminders against bullying (Poster Making and Slogan Contest)', 'PREVENTION AND AWARENESS: To ensure 100% awareness among students, teachers, parents, and staff regarding what constitutes bullying, its forms, and its consequences.', 'Empowered students, \r\nSafe, secure and positive  environment, confident learners', 'Create welcoming atmosphere through decorations, slogans, and activities that promote friendship and inclusions.', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Guidance Designate, Teachers, Pa', '5,000.00', '', 2026, 128841, 60, 12, 0),
(4303, 'Include anti - bullying  topics in Values Education, Social Studies, or Homeroom periods.', 'PREVENTION AND AWARENESS: To ensure 100% awareness among students, teachers, parents, and staff regarding what constitutes bullying, its forms, and its consequences.', 'Positive school culture', 'Integrate lessons on respect, empathy, and emotional intelligence into the curriculum and homeroom activities (Values Formation)', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Guidance Designate, Teachers, Pa', '0.00', '', 2026, 128841, 60, 12, 0),
(4304, 'Show educational videos showing the effects of bullying and the importance of kindness.', 'PREVENTION AND AWARENESS: To ensure 100% awareness among students, teachers, parents, and staff regarding what constitutes bullying, its forms, and its consequences.', 'Confident learners, positive school environment', 'Integrate lessons on respect, empathy, and emotional intelligence into the curriculum and homeroom activities (Values Formation)', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Guidance Designate, Teachers, Pa', '0.00', '', 2026, 128841, 60, 12, 0),
(4305, 'Formulate/Update Anti - Bullying Policy', 'POLICY AND IMPLEMENTATION: To strictly implement and enforce the Anti - Bullying Policy and Child Protection Policy in accordance with existing laws and regulations.', '100% compliance of students, teachers, and staff with the Anti - bullying policy.', 'Whole school approach \r\n- Administration makes and enforces policies.\r\n- Teachers monitor and educate.\r\n- Students practice respect and speak up.\r\n- Parents support and cooperate at home.', 'June, 2026', 'School Head, Guidance Designate, Teachers, Pa', '0.00', '', 2026, 128841, 60, 12, 0),
(4306, 'Conduct Policy Orientation', 'POLICY AND IMPLEMENTATION: To ensure 100% awareness among students, teachers, parents, and staff regarding what constitutes bullying, its forms, and its consequences.', '100% awareness rate among the school community regarding anti - bullying rules and reporting procedures.', 'Orientation Dissemination', 'July, 2026', 'School Head, Guidance Designate, Teachers, Pa', '0.00', '', 2026, 128841, 60, 12, 0),
(4307, 'Establish Reporting Systems.', 'POLICY AND IMPLEMENTATION: To establish clear, accessible, and safe mechanisms for reporting incidents without fear of retaliation.', 'Positive feedback from parents and stakeholders\r\nEasily address the bullying incidence among learners.', 'Established easy and safe ways to report (Drop Boxes, Google forms, Designated Guidance, and Trusted Teachers)', 'Whole Year Round', 'School Head, Guidance Designate, Teachers, Pa', '0.00', '', 2026, 128841, 60, 12, 0),
(4308, 'CURRICULUM AND TEACHING:   * NAT REVIEW ', 'To achieve 2% increase in the proficiency level in all 21st century skills and core learning areas', '2% increased in the proficiency level of the NAT results ', 'Quarterly NAT REVIEW ', 'Quarterly ', 'SH, Core Subject Teachers, School Testing Coo', '2500', '', 2026, 301526, 57, 12, 114),
(4309, 'FINANCE AND RESOURCE MANAGEMENT: *Construction of Functional Library ', 'To construct a functional library ', 'Constructed functional library ', 'Make request to the LGU/PLGU for budget allocation ', 'July 2026', 'SH, Library Incharge, SGC, PTA, Faculty Club ', '1000000', '', 2026, 301526, 57, 12, 114),
(4310, '1. Conduct SBM Orientation for Stakeholders\r\n2. Review and Update School Improvement Plan (SIP) aligned with SBM\r\n3. Strengthen School Governance through Stakeholder Participation\r\n4. Implement Learning Improvement Programs\r\n5. Establish Transparent ', '1. To enhance awareness and deepen understanding of SBM principles among stakeholders\r\n2. To ensure SIP reflects SBM domains and school priorities\r\n3. To increase stakeholder involvement in decision-making\r\n4. To improve learner performance based on ', '1. Attendance sheet, photos, orientation materials\r\n2. Revised SIP document\r\n3. Meeting minutes, signed resolutions\r\n4. Intervention reports, learner progress data\r\n5. Financial reports, transparency board postings\r\n6. M&E reports, SBM assessment results\r\n', '1. Face-to-face orientation, presentation, and open forum\r\n2. Workshop with stakeholders, data review, and planning session\r\n3. Regular SGC meetings and consultations\r\n4. Remediation classes, peer tutoring, and monitoring\r\n5. Monthly financial reporting and stakeholder orientation\r\n6. Classroom observations, document review, feedback sessions\r\n', 'June 2026, June–July 2026, Quarterly, Whole S', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator and team, Teache', '10000', 'Ensure active and inclusive participation of all stakeholders by providing necessary reference materials to support understanding, align plans with current data and existing policies with proper validation before finalization, promote collaboration, shared accountability, and transparency in all processes, focus on key learning priorities while continuously improving strategies based on results, ensure that reports are readily available, accessible, and regularly updated, and involve concerned personnel and relevant stakeholders in all implementation and monitoring activities.\r\n', 2026, 128433, 57, 12, 121),
(4311, 'Conduct Test Item Analysis', '1. To determine the validity and reliability of assessment items through item analysis techniques.\r\n2. To identify difficult, easy, and poorly constructed test items for revision and improvement.\r\n3. To formulate interventions and improve future asse', '1. Accomplished test item analysis matrix/table and computed difficulty and discrimination indices.\r\n2. List of identified easy, difficult, and non-discriminating items and revised and improved test questions.\r\n3. Intervention/remediation plan for least-mastered competencies.', 'The activity will use workshops through LAC, collaborative analysis, peer review, and data-driven planning to help teachers analyze test items, improve assessment tools, and develop instructional interventions based on learners’ performance data.', 'June 2026 to April 2027', 'Teachers-17, School Head-1', '', 'To be conducted', 2026, 501410, 58, 12, 40),
(4312, 'Implementation of ARAL Daily Reading Sessions', 'Improve reading fluency, comprehension, and vocabulary', 'Improved reading performance of learners\r\n', 'Guided reading, shared reading, repeated reading', '1hr G1-3, 30min. Gr,4-6', 'Teachers, Learners', '3000', '', 2026, 128784, 104, 12, 130),
(4313, '*Strengthen implementation of the Academic Recovery and Accessible Learning (ARAL) Program\r\n*Implement intervention programs for learners who are lagging across all learning areas.\r\n', '*To increase proficiency level in all learning areas by 10% ( at 1% increase in 2 consecutive years and 2% in the remaining  4 years) from 50% to 60%', 'Increased proficiency level by 2% from 54% to 56% for SY 2026-2027', '*Conduct baseline periodic assessment to monitor learners\' proficiency levels.\r\n*Implement data-driven instruction through regular analysis of test results and identification of least mastered competencies\r\n*Integrate HOTS-based questioning techniques in daily lessons across all learning areas\r\n*Utilize SOLO Taxonomy in lesson planning\r\n*Use NAT-like questions in formative and summative assessments', 'Year-round', '*School Principal     * Asst. School Principa', '10,000.00', '', 2026, 304261, 104, 12, 129),
(4314, '*Conduct at least 2 LAC sessions on peace education and values integration\r\n*Demo teaching showcasing best practices in integration\r\n*Lesson plan review and enhancement  through peer critiquing                                               ', 'Enhance teachers’ competence in integrating values and peace education across learning areas.', '*Enhanced and revised lesson plans with integrated peace education and values\r\n*LAC session reports and attendance sheets\r\n*PMRF and observation notes', '*Learning Action Cell (LAC)-based collaborative learning\r\n*Demonstration teaching and reflection sessions\r\n*Use of contextualized and localized teaching strategies', 'Year-round', 'Master Teachers and Subject Teachers', '5000.00', '*To be monitored through classroom observations and LAC documentation\r\n*Technical assistance to be provided to teachers needing further support', 2026, 304261, 104, 12, 129),
(4315, 'Project PEACE', 'To standardize value and peace integration across subjects.', 'Integrated Lesson Plans; Improved behavior.', 'LAC Sessions: Collaborative mapping of peace concepts.', 'Quarter 1 (Ongoing)', 'School Head, Coordinators, Teachers', '2000', '', 2026, 304211, 57, 12, 108),
(4316, 'Contextualization Workshop', 'To enhance skills in creating localized learning materials.', 'Contextualized LRs per grade level.', 'Workshop: Hands-on training using local resources.', 'Month 2', 'School Head, LRMDS Coord, Teachers', '5000', '', 2026, 304211, 57, 12, 108),
(4317, 'Project READ', 'To improve literacy and reading comprehension.', 'Increased reading proficiency levels.', 'Scaffolded Instruction: Peer-tutoring and DEAR sessions.', 'Year-Round', 'Reading Coord, Teachers, Parents', '10000', '', 2026, 304211, 57, 12, 108),
(4318, '*Conduct school-wide orientation on RA 10627 and Child Protection Policy\r\n*Integrate anti-bullying in homeroom guidance sessions \r\n*Organize peer support groups / anti-bullying ambassadors\r\n*Conduct parent orientation and seminars on bullying awarene', '*Strengthen awareness and understanding of anti-bullying policies among learners, teachers, and parents.\r\n*Promote a safe, inclusive, and child-friendly school environment.\r\n*Reduce and prevent bullying incidents through early detection and intervent', '*Increased awareness of anti-bullying policies among stakeholders\r\n*Reduced number of bullying incidents\r\n*Improved learner behavior and school climate\r\n*Active student participation in anti-bullying initiatives', '*Whole-school approach (teachers, parents, learners, stakeholders)\r\n*Preventive and proactive strategies (awareness, values integration)\r\n*Guidance-based interventions and counseling\r\n*Peer mentoring and student leadership involvement\r\n*Collaboration with stakeholders (PTA, barangay, community partners)\r\n*Regular monitoring and documentation of incidents', 'Year - round', 'All Teaching Personnel, Guidance Counselors', '5000.00', 'Implementation to be monitored by the Child Protection Committee (CPC)', 2026, 304261, 104, 12, 129),
(4319, '*Conduct school-wide reorientation on DepEd Order No. 40, s. 2012\r\n*Hold parent education sessions on child protection and positive discipline\r\n*Display IEC materials (posters, tarpaulins) on child protection policies\r\n*Establish or reinforce confide', '*Strengthen awareness and understanding of child protection policies among school personnel, learners, and parents.\r\n*Ensure proper implementation of child protection mechanisms in the school.\r\n*Prevent cases of abuse, violence, exploitation, and dis', '*Increased awareness and understanding of child protection policies\r\n*Functional and active Child Protection Committee\r\n*Established and utilized a reporting and referral system\r\n*Reduction or zero incidence of child abuse cases\r\n*Improved school safety and learner well-being', '*Capacity-building for teachers and staff \r\n*Integration of child protection concepts in classroom instruction and guidance sessions\r\n*Coordination with external stakeholders (LGU, DSWD, PNP Women and Children Protection Desk)', 'Year - round', 'All Teaching Personnel, Guidance Counselors', '5000.00', '*Implementation to be monitored by the Child Protection Committee (CPC)\r\n*Ensure strict compliance with DepEd Child Protection Policy', 2026, 304261, 104, 12, 129),
(4320, '*Regularly monitor the attendance, academic performance, and behavior of students at risk of dropping out\r\n*Conduct parent-teacher conferences \r\n*Implement a home visitation program for at-risk learners\r\n*Provide one-on-one counseling and mentoring s', '*Reduce and prevent learner drop-out through early identification and intervention.\r\n*Strengthen parental involvement and home-school collaboration.\r\n*Improve learner engagement, attendance, and academic performance.\r\n*Provide holistic support to at-', '*Reduced drop-out rate\r\n*Improved attendance and retention rate\r\n*Increased parental involvement and participation\r\n*Documented intervention records (monitoring sheets, home visitation reports)\r\n*Improved learner engagement and academic performance\r\n', '*Early Warning System (EWS) for identifying at-risk learners\r\n*Data-driven decision-making (attendance, grades, behavior tracking)\r\n*Collaborative approach (teachers, parents, guidance)\r\n*Individualized intervention plans for learners\r\n*Counseling and psychosocial support\r\n*Continuous monitoring and follow-up', 'Year - round', 'All Teaching Personnel, Guidance Counselors', '3000.00', '*To be monitored by the School Head, Guidance Counselors, and Class Advisers\r\n*Maintain updated at-risk learner profiling and intervention records', 2026, 304261, 104, 12, 129),
(4321, '*Conduct a planning workshop for the development of PAPs Implementation Matrix\r\n*Identify specific PAPs, timelines, persons responsible, and required resources\r\n*Develop and finalize the PAPs Implementation Matrix\r\n*Conduct orientation for school per', '*Develop a detailed and structured PAPs (Programs, Projects, and Activities) Implementation Matrix aligned with the SIP/AIP.\r\n*Strengthen planning, monitoring, and accountability mechanisms.\r\n*Improve coordination among personnel in implementing scho', '*Completed and approved PAPs Implementation Matrix\r\n*Aligned SIP, AIP, and operational plans\r\n*Monitoring and evaluation reports\r\n*Improved implementation of school programs and activities', '*Participatory and collaborative planning among the school planning team and stakeholders\r\n*Alignment of PAPs with DepEd policies and SBM principles\r\n*Use of a standard monitoring tool like PMRF \r\n*Continuous monitoring, evaluation, and feedback mechanism', 'Year - round', 'School Principal, ASP, Program Owners', '5000.00', 'To be led by the School Head and School Planning Team', 2026, 304261, 104, 12, 129),
