(4490, 'Results of tests are not fully used to improve instruction.', 'To ensure test results are analyzed and used to guide instruction\r\nTo improve student performance through data-driven teaching strategies\r\nTo enhance teachers’ skills in interpreting assessment data', 'Regularly updated assessment analysis reports\r\nRevised lesson plans aligned with test results', 'Conduct Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions focused on data analysis\r\nUse item analysis to identify least mastered skills', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head/Principal Teachers Master Teacher', '500.00', 'Continuous monitoring and support are necessary to ensure sustainability. Adjustments should be made based on quarterly evaluation results.', 2026, 129678, 107, 12, 68),
(4491, 'Remediation sessions are often shortened or not conducted regularly.', 'To ensure remediation sessions are conducted regularly and consistently\r\nTo provide targeted support for learners with least mastered skills\r\nTo improve learners’ academic performance through structured intervention', 'Regular and documented remediation sessions\r\nIndividual learning improvement plans for struggling learners\r\nIncreased mastery level in targeted competencies', 'Prepare a weekly remediation schedule and strictly implement it\r\nIdentify learners needing support through assessment data\r\nUse differentiated and learner-centered remediation activities\r\nEngage parents/guardians to support remediation at home', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head/Principal Teachers Master Teacher', '1000', 'Strict adherence to the remediation schedule is essential. Administrative support and regular monitoring will help ensure consistency and effectiveness.', 2026, 129678, 107, 12, 68),
(4492, 'Occasional bullying cases due to peer conflict, lack of consistent reporting, underreporting of incidents, limited learner awareness on anti-bullying policies', 'o reduce incidents of bullying through awareness and preventive measures\r\nTo ensure consistent and accurate reporting of bullying cases\r\nTo increase learners’ awareness of anti-bullying policies and proper behavior\r\nTo promote a safe, inclusive, and ', 'onduct of regular anti-bullying awareness activities\r\nLearners demonstrate improved understanding of school policies\r\nDecrease in bullying cases over time', 'Conduct orientation sessions on anti-bullying policies for students and parents\r\nIntegrate values education and anti-bullying topics in lessons and homeroom guidance\r\nMonitor and evaluate incidents regularly', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head/Principal Teachers Guidance Couns', '2000', 'Confidentiality and sensitivity in handling cases must be strictly observed. Continuous collaboration among school personnel, learners, and parents is vital to sustain a bullying-free environment.', 2026, 129678, 107, 12, 68),
(4494, 'Strengthening Parental Engagement and Home Learning Support', 'o increase parental involvement in learners’ academic activities\r\nTo provide accessible learning resources for use at home\r\nTo strengthen school-home collaboration in supporting student learning\r\nTo improve learners’ performance through guided home s', 'Increased parent participation in school programs and meetings\r\nAvailability of take-home learning materials and guides\r\nImproved communication between teachers and parents\r\nObservable improvement in learners’ homework completion and performance', 'Encourage reading programs and simple home-based learning activities\r\nUse communication platforms (e.g., SMS, chat groups) for regular updates and guidance', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head/Principal Teachers Parents/Guardi', '5000', 'Active and consistent communication is key to sustaining parental involvement. Flexibility should be considered to accommodate parents’ availability and varying home situations.', 2026, 129678, 107, 12, 68),
(4495, 'Provision and Support for Alternative Learning System (ALS) Implementation', 'To ensure access to ALS for out-of-school youth and adult learners\r\nTo provide a designated or trained teacher to handle ALS classes\r\nTo strengthen coordination with the Division Office and stakeholders for ALS support\r\nTo promote inclusive education', 'Designated or trained ALS implementer assigned\r\nConduct of regular ALS sessions\r\nIncreased enrollment of out-of-school youth and adult learners\r\nImproved completion rate of ALS learners', 'Conduct community mapping to identify potential ALS learners\r\nCoordinate with the Schools Division Office for the deployment of an ALS teacher or mobile teacher.\r\nProvide learning materials and modules for ALS learners', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head/Principal Schools Division Office', '5000', 'Close coordination with the Schools Division Office is essential for teacher deployment. Sustainability can be supported through strong community partnerships and continuous monitoring.', 2026, 129678, 107, 12, 68),
