(4517, '*Conduct SBM orientation for stakeholders\r\n• Organize School Governing Council (SGC) and PTA meetings\r\n• Implement teaching improvement programs (remediation, INSET, LAC)\r\n• Prepare SIP and AIP and conduct resource inventory\r\n• Conduct Brigada Eskwel', 'To effectively implement School-Based Management (SBM) to improve school governance, teaching and learning, resource management, and community engagement', '• Increased stakeholder participation\r\n• Improved learner performance\r\n• Transparent and efficient resource utilization\r\n• Strengthened school-community partnerships\r\n• Regular monitoring reports and improved implementation', '• Stakeholder engagement and shared decision-making\r\n• Data-driven instruction and continuous assessment\r\n• Participatory planning and financial transparency\r\n• Community partnership and collaboration\r\n• Continuous monitoring and feedback mechanisms', 'May 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers, SGC Memb', '30000', ' Funds may be sourced from MOOE, PTA, and stakeholders; subject to liquidation and auditing', 2026, 304314, 103, 12, 0),
(4519, 'Implementation of structured ELLN Remediation Program for Grades 1-3 with leveled Reading Materials', '1. Increase % of Grade 3 learners achieving proficiency in ELLNA from 10% to 25% by March 2027\r\n2. Provide 30  minutes daily remediation for identified non-readers/frustration level readers.\r\n3.  Develop and reproduce leveled reading materials for mu', '1. Functional Reading corners with leveled books in 6 classrooms\r\n2. 100% of identified at-risk learners enrolled in remediation.\r\n3. Pre/post ELLNA results showing improvement.', '1. Conduct LAC on ELLN toolkit and Marungko approach\r\n2. Schedule daily 30-min \'Catch-up Fridays\" + pull-out sessions\r\n3. Partner with barangay for reading volunteers\r\n4. Utilize DMEA results for grouping', 'June 2026 - March 2027', 'School Head, All Teachers, PTA, Barangay Educ', '15000', 'Request TA from Division on: 1.) ELLN toolkit training, 2.) Provision of leveled readers, 3.) Guidance on multigrade remediation scheduling', 2026, 128328, 57, 12, 115),
(4520, 'Project NUMERATES - Numeracy and Science Mastery Enhancements for Grades 4-6', '1. Enhance NAT Math/Science Scores from below average to moving towards average by March 2027\r\n2. Conduct weekly numeracy drills and hand-on Science activities\r\n3. Train teachers on contextualized Math/Science DLLs for Multi-grade Classes', '1. Improved quarterly assessments results in Math/Science by 15%\r\n2. I set of teacher-made Math manipulatives + Science IMs per grade Level\r\n3. 100% of Math/Science teachers trained via LAC', '1. LAC on 4As in Math + 5Es in Science\r\n2, Use of Local materials for experiments/Manipulatives\r\n3. Peer tutoring via \"Math Buddy\" and \"Science Club\"\r\n4. Quarterly DMEA analysis for remediation grouping', 'July 2026- February 2027', 'School Head, Math/ Science Teachers, Master T', '7000', 'Request TA from Division on 1) Numeracy intervention strategies, 2) Science Equipment provision, based on TANA Priority #3, urgency 4', 2026, 128328, 57, 12, 115),
(4521, 'Address gaps in mastery of higher-order thinking skills; limited exposure to NAT-type test items; learning losses due to absenteeism; and inadequate review/intervention programs prior to NAT.', 'Improve learners’ mastery of higher-order thinking skills (HOTS).\r\nIncrease familiarity with NAT-type test items and performance-based assessments.', 'Increased NAT Mean Percentage Score (MPS).\r\nImproved learner performance in formative and summative assessments.', 'Increased NAT Mean Percentage Score (MPS).\r\nImproved learner performance in formative and summative assessments.', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, Grade VI Adviser,  NAT Task Forc', '500.00', 'Continuous monitoring and evaluation required.\r\nCollaboration with stakeholders is essential for success.', 2026, 129654, 107, 12, 68),
(4522, 'Project DIGITAL-BAYANIHAN ICT - Upskilling and Manual System Enhancement for School Frontline Services', '1. Train 100% of admin staff on basic ICT and data management\r\n2. Establish offline/manual backup systems for enrollment, SFs and MOOE\r\n3. Secure I additional DCP package for admin use', '1. 2 Admin Staff trained on excel/ google sheets offline\r\n2. Manual logbooks and templates for frontline services during outages\r\n3. DCP request endorsed to Division', '1. LAC on digital literacy for teachers/staff\r\n2. Develop printed forms and tracking sheets as backup\r\n3. Schedule data encoding during strong signal hours\r\n4. Partner with Barangay for internet access during reports/', 'August 2026 - March 2026', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Admin Officer, ', '10000', 'Request TA from Division on: DCP allocation, 2) Offline LIS/SF training. Based on TANA Priority #20, urgency 4', 2026, 128328, 57, 12, 115),
(4523, 'Risk of underreporting due to fear or lack of awareness among learners Need for continuous orientation on Child Protection Policy (CPP)', 'Increase learners’ awareness of their rights and the Child Protection Policy (CPP).\r\nEncourage safe and timely reporting of abuse, bullying, and other protection concerns.', 'Increased number of reported and properly documented cases (as appropriate).\r\nImproved awareness level of learners on CPP (based on surveys).', 'Conduct regular orientation sessions on CPP for learners, teachers, and parents.\r\nIntegrate CPP awareness in Homeroom Guidance and classroom discussions. Establish child-friendly reporting mechanisms (suggestion box, hotline, focal person)', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, Child Protection Committee, Teac', '500', 'Strict confidentiality must be observed at all times.\r\nImmediate action is required for reported cases.\r\nContinuous advocacy is key to sustaining awareness and trust.', 2026, 129654, 107, 12, 68),
(4524, 'Project LIGTAS SILID - Partnership Drive for Safe and Resilient School Infrastructure', '1. Secure LGU/External funding for repair of 2 damaged classrooms\r\n2. Conduct minor repairs via Brigada Eskwela Plus\r\n3. Complete hazard mapping and retrofitting plan', '1. Project proposal submitted to LGU\r\n2. 100% minor repairs completed via Brigada\r\n3. Updated School DRRM contingency plan with infra needs', '1. Stakeholder convergence meeting with LGU, PTA, Alumni\r\n2. Documentation of infra Gaps with photos fro proposals\r\n3. Mobilize community labor during Brigada\r\n4. Endorse to Division for BEFF prioritazation', 'May 2026 - December 2026', 'School Head, SGC, PTA, LGU,', '8000', 'For endorsement to LGU, Low feasibility due to budget, Based on TANA Priority #18, urgency 4\r\n(Major repairs is for external funding)', 2026, 128328, 57, 12, 115),
(4525, 'Limited mental health professionals or trained guidance personnel in some cases Insufficient dedicated time for structured mental wellness activities', 'Strengthen the provision of basic mental health and psychosocial support services in school.\r\nEquip teachers with essential skills in mental health awareness and psychological first aid.', 'Increased number of trained teachers in mental health and psychosocial support.\r\nRegularly conducted mental wellness activities integrated into school schedules.', 'Conduct Mental Health and Psychosocial Support (MHPSS) training for teachers.\r\nIntegrate mental wellness activities (e.g., mindfulness, journaling, check-ins) in Homeroom Guidance.', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, School Guidance Coordinator / De', '500', 'Prioritize teacher upskilling due to limited professionals.\r\nEnsure safe, inclusive, and non-judgmental spaces for learners.\r\nStrengthen referral pathways for serious mental health concerns.', 2026, 129654, 107, 12, 68),
