(4532, 'Implementation of School-Based Anti-Bullying Program (SBABP): Awareness, Prevention, and Intervention Campaign', 'To promote a safe, inclusive, and child-friendly learning environment free from bullying.\r\nTo increase awareness among learners, teachers, and parents about anti-bullying policies and child protection.\r\nTo strengthen reporting, monitoring, and respon', 'Conducted school-wide Anti-Bullying Orientation and Campaign\r\nFunctional School Child Protection Committee (CPC)\r\nEstablished and utilized reporting system (drop box/online reporting)\r\nDocumented cases with appropriate interventions\r\nReduced number of bullying incidents (based on quarterly monitoring)\r\nIEC materials (posters, flyers, videos) displayed and disseminated', '-Conduct orientation seminars for teachers, learners, and parents on Anti-Bullying Act and Child Protection Policy\r\n-Integrate anti-bullying themes in classroom instruction (Values Education, Araling Panlipunan, etc.)\r\n-Organize peer support groups and student-led advocacy campaigns\r\n-Set up confidential reporting mechanisms (suggestion box, hotline, digital forms)\r\n-Immediate response and intervention through CPC (investigation, counseling, mediation)\r\n-Monitoring and evaluation through surveys and incident reports\r\n-Recognition of positive behavior through rewards system', 'School Year 2026-2027', 'School Head Child Protection Committee (CPC) ', '12000', 'This action plan supports the School-Based Management (SBM) principles by promoting stakeholder participation, ensuring learner protection, and fostering a positive school climate conducive to learning.', 2026, 129063, 60, 12, 33),
