(4658, 'Flashcard relays or interactive board games featuring Grade 3 vocabulary and common sight words. Learners take turns reading words aloud rapidly to build automaticity and speed.', 'Identify and recognize Grade 3 high-frequency sight words instantly.\r\nIncrease oral fluency through high-speed repetitive reading drills.\r\nBuild confidence when reading aloud in front of peers.', 'Enhanced Reading Fluency: Observable increase in Words Correct Per Minute (WCPM) baseline scores.\r\nSight Word Mastery: Immediate (within 3 seconds) automatic recognition of targeted Grade 3 high-frequency words without halting to decode phonetically.\r\nReduced Reading Anxiety: Active, self-assured verbal participation during whole-class reading aloud and peer-group activities.', 'The Sight Word Shuttle (Relay Format): Divide the class into small, heterogenous teams lined up behind a starting line. A set distance away, face-down flashcards are placed on a table. One by one, learners sprint to the table, flip a card, read it aloud instantly, and rush back to tag the next classmate.', 'This strategy is designed as a highly structu', 'Grade three learners and Teachers', 'MOOE Fund', 'Conducted 3 to 4 times a week across an instructional quarter (8–9 weeks) to move target high-frequency words from short-term working memory into permanent, automatic cognitive recall.\r\n', 2026, 129670, 107, 12, 68),
(4659, 'Administer localized, contextualized pre-tests aligned with the Most Essential Learning Competencies (MELCs).', 'Identify Knowledge Gaps: Pinpoint which specific MELCs students have already mastered and which competencies require urgent, intensive instruction.\r\nEstablish a Learning Baseline: Obtain quantifiable pre-instruction data to measure academic growth an', 'Validated Localized Assessment Tools: Copy-ready pre-tests aligned with MELCs, complete with answer keys, TOS (Table of Specifications), and 21st-century skill tags.\r\nStudent Diagnostic Profiles: Individual and class-wide matrices mapping mastered vs. unmastered MELCs.\r\n21st-Century Skill Baseline Dashboard: A statistical summary ranking student proficiency in Critical Thinking, Problem-Solving, and Information Literacy.\r\nTargeted Remediation Roadmap: A data-driven list of priority MELCs earmarked for urgent intervention during daily classes and Catch-Up Fridays.\r\n', 'Blueprint Construction: Map pre-test items against DepEd\'s MELCs using a TOS that balances cognitive levels (Remembering to Creating).\r\nContextualization: Rewrite test prompts using local landmarks, provincial industries, community traditions, and native scenarios.\r\nSkill Tagging: Categorize each question under specific 21st-century skill pillars (e.g., Tag a Math problem as Problem-Solving: Executing Methods).', 'Weeks 1–2 (Pre-Implementation): Development &', 'Grade 6 Learners and Teachers', '', 'The Remarks column functions as an ongoing monitoring, accountability, and verification tracker for school heads, supervisors, and teachers. It details implementation status, constraints, variances, and actionable next steps.', 2026, 129670, 107, 12, 68),
