(4888, '10. Reorganization and Activation of the School Governance Council (SGC).', '1.To organize and activate a functional School Governance Council\r\n2. To orient members on their role sand responsibilities\r\n3. To Strengthen stakeholders participation in school governance ', '-Organized and updated list of SGC members\r\n- Orientation conducted for SGC members\r\n-Initial SGC meeting with documented minutes', '-Identify and invite potential SGC members \r\n-Conduct simple orientation on SGC roles and functions\r\n-Schedule initial and follow up meetings\r\n-Encourage participation through open discussion and clear task assignment ', 'June-October 2026', 'School Head ,teachers ,PTA Officers ,Barangay', '1000.00', '', 2026, 128844, 60, 12, 30),
(4889, 'Catch-Up Acceleration\r\n-Pinpoint specific areas where students lag\r\n-Create short, focused modules for key topics\r\n-Use games, quizzes, projects to make learning fun\r\n-Regular check-ins to adjust support', 'Help students catch up and engage with personalized support.\r\nIdentify and address specific learning gaps.\r\nProvide flexible support to help students catch up.\r\nBoost engagement with interactive learning activities.\r\nImprove student progress and conf', '-Students show improved understanding and grades in key subjects.\r\n\r\n-Learning gaps narrow as students get targeted support.\r\n\r\n-Increased student engagement and motivation.\r\n\r\n-Teachers can track progress more accurately.', '-Identify specific learning gaps.\r\n-Create short, focused modules for key topics.\r\n-Offer support via after-school help or online resources.\r\n-Use games, quizzes, projects to boost engagement.\r\n-Track progress and adjust support as needed.', 'Whole year round', 'Teachers and Learners', '10000', 'Acceleration activity is designed to be flexible and engaging, helping students overcome learning gaps and boost confidence.', 2026, 128541, 57, 12, 108),
(4890, 'Respect Connect, Building a Positive Vibe\r\n\r\n-Foster empathy and respect among students.\r\n-Integrate new students smoothly into the school culture.\r\n-Encourage incident reporting and address underreporting.\r\n-Create a safe and supportive environment ', '-Foster empathy and understanding among students.\r\n-Integrate new students into the school community.\r\n-Encourage open communication and incident reporting.\r\n-Strengthen a culture of respect and inclusivity.', '-Improved student relationships and empathy.\r\n-Smoother integration of new students.\r\n-Increased incident reporting and resolution.\r\n-A more supportive and inclusive school environment', '-Introduce new students to the school culture.\r\n-Pair new students with peer mentors.\r\n-Conduct empathy and respect-building activities.\r\n-Establish anonymous reporting and feedback systems.\r\n-Reward positive behaviors and contributions.', 'Whole year round', 'Teachers and Learners', '10000', 'Respect Connect\" can really help build a positive school culture. ', 2026, 128541, 57, 12, 108),
(4891, 'Stay Connected\r\n\r\n-Flag students showing signs of disengagement.\r\n-Understand underlying issues.\r\n-Address specific needs.\r\n-Pair students with trusted adults.\r\n-Offer relevant and fun learning experiences.', '-Identify and support students at risk of dropping out.\r\n-Identify students at risk of dropping out early.\r\n-Address underlying reasons for potential dropouts.\r\n-Boost student motivation and engagement.\r\n-Provide targeted support for at-risk students', '-Reduced dropout rates.\r\n-Improved student engagement and motivation.\r\n-Timely support for at-risk students.\r\n-Stronger teacher-student connections.', '-Use data and teacher referrals to flag at-risk students.\r\n-Assign mentors or counselors for one-on-one support.\r\n-Create personalized intervention plans.\r\n-Offer relevant activities and monitor progress.\r\n-Regularly assess and adjust support.', 'Whole year round', 'School Head, Teachers, and Learners', '10000', ' Stay Connected tackles the root causes of dropout risks. By building trust and support, students are more likely to stay engaged and succeed.', 2026, 128541, 57, 12, 108),
(4892, 'H2O Secure. Let\'s get water wise!\r\n\r\n-Evaluate current water supply and usage.\r\n-Implement water-saving measures.\r\n-Develop alternative water sources (e.g., rainwater harvesting through water tanks).\r\n-Regularly check and fix leaks.\r\n-Educate student', '-Ensure reliable water supply for school needs.\r\n-Ensure reliable water supply for school operations.\r\n-Procurement of Water Tanks.\r\n-Implement effective water conservation measures.\r\n-Develop sustainable backup systems for water supply.\r\n-Promote wa', '-Reliable water supply for school needs.\r\n-Reduced water consumption through conservation.\r\n-Functional backup water systems (e.g., rainwater harvesting).\r\n-Increased awareness on water conservation among students.', '-Evaluate current water supply and usage patterns.\r\n-Develop water conservation and backup plans.\r\n-Install water-saving fixtures and backup systems (e.g., rainwater tanks).\r\n-Regularly check water usage and system performance.\r\n- Conduct water conservation awareness campaigns.', 'Whole year round', 'School Head, Property Custodian, Teachers, an', '120000', 'Secure addresses water supply issues and promotes sustainability. By conserving water and having backups, the school ensures continuity and teaches students valuable lessons on resource management.', 2026, 128541, 57, 12, 108),
(4894, 'SGC Empower\r\n\r\n-Identify gaps in SGC members\' skills.\r\n-Organize training on roles, governance, and leadership.\r\n-Provide access to relevant materials and best practices.\r\n-Regularly check progress and address concerns.\r\n', 'Equip SGC members with necessary skills and knowledge.', '-SGC members are confident and skilled in their roles.\r\n-Improved governance and decision-making in the school.\r\n-Stronger collaboration among SGC members.\r\n-Enhanced school-community partnerships.', '-Identify training needs of SGC members.\r\n-Design targeted training workshops and resources.\r\n-Conduct workshops and pair members with mentors.\r\n-Provide ongoing guidance and resources.\r\n-Regularly assess SGC performance and feedback.', 'Whole year round', 'School Principal/Head, Teachers\' Representati', '5000', 'Empowering SGC members boosts school governance and collaboration. With the right skills, they can drive positive change and strengthen school-community ties.', 2026, 128541, 57, 12, 108),
(4895, 'Conduct baseline assessment and item analysis in English, Math, Science, Filipino, and Araling Panlipunan.', 'Improve learners’ proficiency in NAT core learning areas', '• Baseline assessment results per subject area\r\n• Item analysis report\r\n• List of least mastered skills/competencies\r\n• Intervention and remediation plan', '• Administration of standardized baseline tests\r\n• Checking and tabulation of results\r\n• Conduct item analysis and data interpretation\r\n• Collaborative review of results during LAC/department meetings\r\n• Development of intervention and enrichment activities', 'June – July 2026', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Subject Teacher', '', 'Results will serve as basis for intervention programs, remediation activities, and instructional planning for NAT preparation.', 2026, 316018, 60, 12, 24),
(4896, 'Conduct LAC sessions and INSET on critical thinking, communication, collaboration, and creativity integration', 'Strengthen teachers’ capability in teaching 21st century skills', '• Conducted LAC sessions and INSET activities\r\n• Teachers trained on 21st century teaching strategies\r\n• Session plans, attendance sheets, and documentation', '• Conduct Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions and INSET workshops\r\n• Demonstration teaching and peer coaching\r\n• Collaborative lesson planning and sharing of best practices\r\n• Workshops on innovative and learner-centered strategies\r\n• Monitoring and feedback sessions', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, MTs, Teachers', '', 'Activities will support teachers’ professional growth and improve delivery of instruction aligned with 21st century learning standards.', 2026, 316018, 60, 12, 24),
(4897, 'Conduct orientations, homeroom guidance sessions, and seminars on Anti-Bullying Act and Child Protection Policy', 'Strengthen awareness and understanding of the Anti-Bullying Policy among learners, teachers, and parents', '• Conducted orientations and seminars\r\n• Increased awareness on learners’ rights and responsibilities\r\n• Attendance sheets, program documentation, and reports\r\n• Reduced bullying incidents and improved school discipline', '• Conduct school-wide orientations and advocacy campaigns\r\n• Integrate discussions during Homeroom Guidance sessions\r\n• Invite guidance counselors, PNP officers, or child protection advocates as resource speakers\r\n• Use interactive activities, role-playing, and open forums\r\n• Disseminate informational materials and policies\r\nTime Frame	June 2026 – March 2027', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, Guidance Coordinator, Teachers, ', '', 'Activity supports the promotion of a safe, child-friendly, and bullying-free learning environment in accordance with DepEd policies.', 2026, 316018, 60, 12, 24),
(4898, 'Conduct orientations, seminars, and advocacy campaigns on Child Protection Policy and child abuse prevention', 'Strengthen awareness on Child Protection Policy and child abuse prevention among learners, teachers, and parents', '• Conducted orientations, seminars, and advocacy activities\r\n• Increased awareness and understanding of child protection and abuse prevention\r\n• Attendance sheets, documentation, and accomplishment reports\r\n• Strengthened implementation of child protection measures in school', '• Conduct seminars and orientations for learners, parents, and teachers\r\n• Organize advocacy campaigns, poster-making, and information drives\r\n• Invite guidance counselors, social workers, health personnel, and PNP officers as resource speakers\r\n• Integrate child protection topics in Homeroom Guidance and school programs\r\n• Distribute IEC materials and conduct open forums/discussions', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, Guidance Coordinator, Teachers, ', '', 'Activity promotes a safe, secure, and child-friendly learning environment aligned with DepEd Child Protection Policy and child welfare programs.', 2026, 316018, 60, 12, 24),
