(4948, 'Conduct regular remediation classes, literacy and numeracy intervention programs, and differentiated instruction strategies.', 'Improve learners’ literacy and numeracy skills through targeted intervention programs and strengthen teachers’ capacity in differentiated instruction strategies.', 'Increased reading comprehension and numeracy performance of struggling learners.', 'Conduct reading and numeracy assessments; implement pull-out remediation classes and intervention sessions.', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Reading Coordinators, ', '15000', 'To be monitored quarterly', 2026, 129116, 60, 12, 25),
(4949, 'Structured Reading Enhancement and Remedial Intervention Program', 'To improve learners’ reading fluency, comprehension, and vocabulary skills through intensified daily structured reading activities, remedial reading sessions, and the use of leveled reading materials.', 'Improved reading fluency and comprehension among learners.\r\nReduced number of struggling and non-readers.\r\nIncreased learner interest and engagement in reading.', 'Structured Reading Approach\r\nRemedial Reading Intervention\r\nInteractive Learning Activities', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'Teachers/Learners/ Reading Coordinator', '10000', 'The success of this action plan depends on the consistent implementation of reading interventions, active learner participation, and support from parents and stakeholders. Intensifying the daily structured reading program, conducting remedial reading sessions, and utilizing leveled reading materials will significantly improve learners’ reading fluency, comprehension, and overall academic performance.', 2026, 129103, 60, 12, 25),
(4950, 'Conduct regular competency-based remediation, enrichment classes, and focused review sessions based on least mastered competencies.', 'Identify least mastered competencies among learners through assessment results and classroom performance and improve learners’ mastery of identified competencies through remediation classes.', 'Consolidated list of least mastered competencies per grade level and subject area.', 'Analyze quarterly test results, formative assessments, and diagnostic tests.', 'June 2026 and every quarter', 'School Head, Teachers, Academic Coordinators', '38000', 'Prioritize learners at risk of failing.', 2026, 129116, 60, 12, 25),
(4951, 'Conduct Group Screening Test(GST) and Pre-test, Post -test utilizing the PHIL-IRI and CRLA', 'Identify essential beneficiaries of ARAL Program', 'Identified learners needing intervention under the ARAL Program, Baseline reading and numeracy levels of learners using PHIL-IRI and CRLA Tools, Categorized list of learners(Frustration , Instructional , Independent levels) , Intervention priority list for remediation sessions and Consolidated assessment report per grade level.', 'Administration of Group Screening Test (GST) to identify to identify at-risk learners, Conduct of PHIL-IRI (oral and silent reading assessment for reading level profiling, Pre-test administration before intervention activities, Post-test after intervention period to measure progress and Consolidation and validation of results for ARAL Program inclusion.', 'GST administration: 1-3 days, PHIL-IRI & CRLA', 'Adviser, School head , Principal, Master Teac', '3000', 'Results shall serve as basis for targeted ARAL Program Intervention groups, continuous monitoring is recommended to track learners progress.', 2026, 128846, 60, 12, 30),
(4952, 'Reading Enhancement and Higher-Order Thinking Skills (HOTS) Integration Program', 'To improve learners’ reading comprehension and critical thinking abilities through intensified reading programs and the integration of Higher-Order Thinking Skills (HOTS) in classroom instruction.', 'Improved reading comprehension and fluency among learners.\r\nEnhanced critical thinking and problem-solving skills.\r\nIncreased performance in comprehension and HOTS-based assessments.', 'Structured Reading Program\r\nHOTS Integration', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'Teachers/Learners', '10000', 'The successful implementation of this action plan requires the active participation of teachers, learners, parents, and school stakeholders. Intensifying reading programs and integrating Higher-Order Thinking Skills (HOTS) in lessons will help learners become more analytical, reflective, and confident in processing information and solving problems. Continuous monitoring and support are essential to ensure sustained learner improvement.', 2026, 129103, 60, 12, 25),
(4953, 'Conduct parent orientation and strengthen school-home partnerships in promoting values formation among learners.', 'Strengthen collaboration between parents and the school in promoting positive values among learners and promote learners’ moral development, discipline, and positive behavior.', 'Improved parent participation and stronger school-home partnership and learners demonstrating improved behavior, respect, and responsibility.', 'Conduct regular parent orientation meetings and values formation seminars and integrate values formation activities in classroom instruction and school programs.', 'Throughout the School Year', 'Teachers, Guidance Coordinator, Parents', '30000', 'Encourage active parental involvement.', 2026, 129116, 60, 12, 25),
(4954, 'Capacity Building of Teachers and school communities in the Implementation of School Projects, Activities, and Programs for SY 2026-2027', 'To capacitate and empower teachers and communities in implementing the school projects, activities, and programs for SY 2026-2027', 'Submitted Plans of Action for the implementation of different  school PAPs', '-Inclusion in Teacher Conferences\r\n-Conduct convergence of stakeholders', 'May - June 2026', 'School Principals, Teachers, Parents, SGC', '5000.00', 'This plan is subject for adjustment considering the overlapping of schedules of activities in the Department of Education.', 2026, 129764, 105, 12, 19),
(4955, 'ALS Learner Monitoring, Home Visitation, and Mentoring Program', 'To improve ALS learners’ attendance, participation, retention, and completion rate through strengthened learner tracking, regular home visitations, and mentoring programs.', 'Improved attendance and participation of ALS learners.\r\nReduced absenteeism and dropout cases among ALS learners.\r\nStrengthened learner tracking and monitoring system.\r\nIncreased learner motivation and engagement in ALS sessions.', 'Learner Tracking System\r\nHome Visitation Program\r\nMentoring and Guidance', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'ALS Teacher, Parents, Barangay Officials', '10000', 'The success of this action plan depends on the active collaboration of ALS teachers, learners, parents, barangay officials, and community stakeholders. Strengthening the learner tracking system, conducting regular home visitations, and implementing mentoring programs will help improve learner attendance, motivation, retention, and completion rates among ALS learners.', 2026, 129103, 60, 12, 25),
(4956, 'Selebrasyon ng Buwan ng Wika\r\n-School-based na patimpalak at paligsahan \r\n-paggawa ng poster\r\n-pagbigkas ng tula \r\n-kasuotang Panlarangan \r\n-Pagbaybay \r\n-Tagisan ng Talino\r\n-Pag-awit', 'To provide learners the opportunity to demonstrate their skills and talents in various competitions and contests.', 'Learners actively participating in various language-related competitions.\r\n-Quality outputs such as posters, poems, spelling results, performances, and songs\r\n-Winners per category (Poster Making, Poem Recitation , Spelling Bee, Quiz Bee, Singing Contest \r\n-Recognition certificates and awards for participation and winners', '-Orientation of learners and teachers regarding contest mechanics and criteria.\r\n-Formation of committees per contest \r\n-School-based finals for each competition\r\n-Judging by selected competent and impartial evaluators \r\n-Use of rubrics for objective scoring\r\n-Awarding ceremony after all contests', 'Preparation and Orientation: 1-2 days, Classr', 'Learners, Adviser, School head, Master Teache', '4000', 'All contests should promote Filipino language, creativity, and cultural appreciation', 2026, 128846, 60, 12, 30),
(4957, 'Implementation of Targeted Reading and Numeracy Enhancement Program for Grade 3 Learners', '•	Improve learners’ reading comprehension and numeracy skills \r\n•	Sustain proficiency level of learners through regular monitoring', '•	Conducted remediation sessions \r\n•	Assessment results showing progress\r\n', 'minutes) \r\n•	Conduct remediation for struggling learners (after class or scheduled time) \r\n•	Use localized and simple instructional materials \r\n', 'School year 2026-2027', 'Teachers, School head, and Pupils', '5000', 'This ensures that struggling learners receive consistent support and gradually improve their foundational skills.', 2026, 128840, 60, 12, 30),
(4958, 'Conduct of Earthquake Drill', '-To increase awareness and preparedness of learners and personnel during an earthquake drill.\r\n- To practice proper \"Drop, Cover, and Hold\", procedure.\r\n', '-All participants demonstrate correct earthquake safety procedures. \r\n-Identified strengths and gaps in the school emergency plan.\r\n-Organized and timely evacuation of learners and teachers.', '-Orientation on earthquake safety procedures\r\n-Simulation of earthquake scenario \r\n-Headcount and reporting of participants\r\n', 'Orientation: 20 minutes, Drill Proper: 10-15 ', 'Learners, DRRM Coordinator, Teachers, Master ', '4000', 'Participation of all stakeholders is highly encouraged.\r\nDrill should be conducted at least twice  a year for effectiveness.', 2026, 128846, 60, 12, 30),
(4959, 'Conduct SBM Re-Orientation Session', 'To ensure shared understanding of SBM framework, principles, standards, and indicators among all stakeholders and personnel', '- Personnel and Stakeholders oriented on SBM  framework, principles, standards, and indicators\r\n- Minutes and Attendance', 'SLAC and Focus Group Discussion', 'June - July, 2026', 'School Head, TP and NTP, Learners, PTA, Exter', '1500', 'Continuous strengthening of awareness and compliance', 2026, 128842, 60, 12, 30),
