(4967, 'Conduct GSP and BSP Joint Camporal', '•	Promote camaraderie, leadership, discipline, and teamwork among Girl Scouts and Boy Scouts. \r\n• Develop survival, environmental, and life skills through outdoor activities. \r\n• Strengthen values formation, responsibility, and community service.\r\n', 'Improved scouting skills and leadership abilities among participants. \r\n• Successful completion of camp activities and teamwork exercises. \r\n• Strengthened cooperation and friendship between GSP and BSP members. \r\n', '• Orientation and registration of participants. \r\n• Setting up campsites and patrol grouping. \r\n• Conduct of scouting activities such as knot-tying, first aid, cooking, hiking, campfire program, and team-building games. \r\n• Environmental and community service activities. \r\n• Awarding and closing program.\r\n', '•	2 days', 'School Head, BSP Coordinator, GSP Coordinator', '6000', '• Ensure safety and security measures during the camporal. \r\n• Secure parental consent and coordination with local authorities.\r\n', 2026, 128846, 60, 12, 30),
(4969, 'Conduct of SELG Campaign and Leadership Advocacy Program', '•	To promote responsible leadership, encourage student participation, and inform learners about the SELG election and campaign platforms.', '• Increased awareness of SELG roles and responsibilities\r\n • Active participation of learners in campaign activities\r\n • Organized and peaceful SELG campaign period\r\n • Improved leadership and communication skills among candidates', '• Orientation on SELG election rules and campaign guidelines\r\n • Posting of campaign materials and platforms\r\n • Classroom-to-classroom campaign and leadership talks\r\n • Conduct of Meeting de Avance and campaign presentations\r\n • Election\r\n', '•	Orientation •	Campaign Period  • Meeting de', 'School Head, SELG Adviser, Teachers, SELG Can', '-Tarpaulin:300, Printing Materials: 500, Decorations: 200 =1000 ', '• Ensure equal opportunity for all candidates \r\n • Promote clean and honest elections among learners\r\n', 2026, 128846, 60, 12, 30),
