(5047, '1. Conduct diagnostic tests to identify learners’ learning gaps.\r\n2. Implement regular remediation sessions per subject area (reading, Math, Science).\r\n3. Conduct small group tutoring and peer-assisted learning activities.\r\n4. Develop differentiated ', '1. Address learning gaps in reading, comprehension, Science and Technology, and Mathematics.\r\n2. Improve learners’ mastery of least learned competencies through targeted remediation.\r\n3. Strengthen teachers’ capacity in designing differentiated remed', '1. Improved learner performance in identified weak competencies.\r\n2. Functional remediation plans per grade level and subject.\r\n3. Increased reading comprehension and numeracy skills.\r\n4. Documented progress monitoring reports of learners.', '- Diagnostic assessment-based grouping\r\n- Targeted remediation sessions\r\n- Differentiated instruction\r\n- Peer tutoring and collaborative learning\r\n- LAC-based teacher capacity building\r\n- Continuous progress monitoring', 'School Year 2026–2027 (Weekly remediation ses', 'School Head, Subject Teachers, Master Teacher', '15000', 'This activity aims to strengthen learner mastery and reduce learning gaps through consistent, data-driven, and targeted remediation interventions in key learning areas.', 2026, 129114, 60, 12, 25),
(5048, '1. Conduct orientation/training on test item analysis procedures.\r\n2. Perform item analysis after quarterly examinations and major assessments.\r\n3. Identify least mastered competencies per subject area.\r\n4. Conduct LAC sessions to interpret and utili', '1. Strengthen teachers’ capacity in conducting test item analysis.\r\n2. Use assessment results to improve teaching strategies and learner performance.\r\n3. Identify least learned competencies for targeted intervention.\r\n4. Enhance data-driven decision-', '1. Completed item analysis reports per grading period.\r\n2. List of least mastered competencies per subject.\r\n3. Instructional intervention plans based on data.\r\n4. Improved learner performance through targeted instruction.', '- Data-driven instruction\r\n- Collaborative analysis sessions\r\n- LAC-based capacity building\r\n- Feedback and instructional adjustment cycles\r\n- Monitoring and evaluation of interventions', 'School Year 2026–2027 (After each quarterly e', 'School Head, Subject Teachers, Master Teacher', '15000', 'This activity strengthens data-informed instruction by ensuring that assessment results are properly analyzed and used as basis for remediation, enrichment, and improved teaching strategies.', 2026, 129114, 60, 12, 25),
(5049, 'Report and present  the SRC during  3rd Assembly meeting .', 'To track and update the Learning Outcomes and Performance indicators of SBM', 'Updated Learning Outcomes and SRC', 'The FGD will update and track the performance indicators  and ILO of school SBM . The updated will be presented  by  school head during the Assembly meeting.', 'March 1st wk- March 3rd week, 2027', 'School principal,  parents,  teachers', '800.00', 'Updated ILO and SRC will be presented during Assembly meeting', 2026, 128882, 60, 12, 32),
