(5056, 'ACTIVITY 1: Conduct Item Analysis Training and Workshop for Teachers\r\n\r\nACTIVITY 2: Implement Classroom-Level Item Analysis After Each Quarterly Examination\r\n\r\nACTIVITY 3: Utilize Item Analysis Results for Data-Driven Instruction and Remediation', 'To capacitate teachers in  acquire knowledge and skills in conducting item analysis; identify poorly performing test items for revision\r\n\r\nTeachers systematically analyze test results to determine which items were too easy, too hard, or non-discrimin', 'Accomplished workshop attendance sheets; completed item analysis worksheets; list of flagged test items per teacher\r\n\r\nAccomplished Item Analysis Form (DepEd format); Item Analysis Summary Report per subject; Remediation Plan for low-scoring items/competencies\r\n\r\nRevised lesson plans with noted instructional adjustments; list of learners for remediation; post-remediation assessment results showing improvement', 'Half-day workshop led by the School Head/Master Teacher; hands-on practice using actual recent exam data; use of item analysis template (p-value, discrimination index)\r\n\r\nEach teacher encodes exam results into the Item Analysis Form within 5 days after exam; Master Teacher/Department Head reviews and validates; results discussed in department meeting\r\n\r\nTeachers identify least mastered competencies from item analysis; design remedial activities (group work, differentiated tasks, re-teaching); conduct remediation sessions; re-assess learners after 2 weeks', 'Week 3, August 2025, After each quarterly exa', 'School Head, Master Teacher, Advisers and Sub', '1500', 'To be Implemented', 2026, 501079, 60, 12, 33),
