(5120, '1. Reorganization and activation of the Child Protection Committee.\r\n2. Conduct orientation on Child Protection Policy and responsibilities of CPC members.\r\n3. Develop clear reporting, referral, and documentation system for child protection cases.\r\n4', '1. Strengthen the functionality of the School Child Protection Committee (CPC).\r\n2. Ensure proper implementation of Child Protection Policy (CPP).\r\n3. Improve reporting, monitoring, and documentation of child protection cases.\r\n4. Promote a safe, inc', '1. Fully functional and active Child Protection Committee.\r\n2. Established reporting and referral system for child protection concerns.\r\n3. Documented CPC meetings and actions taken.\r\n4. Increased awareness of learners, teachers, and parents on child protection policies.', '- Orientation and capacity building\r\n- Policy dissemination and advocacy\r\n- Regular monitoring and reporting\r\n- Stakeholder collaboration (LGU, DSWD, barangay)\r\n- Case management and referral system strengthening', 'School Year 2026–2027 (Initial activation in ', 'School Head, Child Protection Committee Membe', '15000', 'This activity aims to fully activate and strengthen the CPC to ensure a safe learning environment and strict compliance with DepEd Child Protection Policy.', 2026, 129114, 60, 12, 25),
(5121, '1. Conduct assessment of existing school facilities for accessibility gaps.\r\n2. Install or improve ramps, handrails, signage, and accessible pathways.\r\n3. Upgrade comfort rooms to be PWD-friendly.\r\n4. Provide SPED instructional materials and assistiv', '1. Improve accessibility of school facilities for learners with disabilities (PWD/SPED learners).\r\n2. Strengthen inclusive education support systems and learning environment.\r\n3. Ensure compliance with basic accessibility standards in school infrastr', '1. Improved and more accessible school facilities for PWD learners.\r\n2. Available SPED and inclusive learning materials.\r\n3. Teachers trained in inclusive education practices.\r\n4. Enhanced participation and learning experience of SPED learners.', '- Infrastructure upgrading and rehabilitation\r\n- Stakeholder partnership and resource mobilization\r\n- Training and capacity building\r\n- Inclusive education integration in instruction\r\n- Monitoring and evaluation of accessibility improvements', 'School Year 2026–2027 (Phased implementation ', 'School Head, SPED Coordinator, Teachers, PTA ', '20000', 'This activity aims to promote inclusive education by improving accessibility and providing adequate support systems for SPED and PWD learners to ensure equal learning opportunities.', 2026, 129114, 60, 12, 25),
(5122, '1. Conduct needs assessment for ICT equipment and laboratory requirements.\r\n2. Procure and install computer units, peripherals, and networking equipment.\r\n3. Set up computer laboratory space including electrical wiring and internet connectivity.\r\n4. ', '1. Establish a functional computer laboratory/classroom to support ICT-integrated instruction.\r\n2. Enhance learners’ digital literacy and 21st-century skills.\r\n3. Provide teachers and learners access to ICT-based learning resources.\r\n4. Support curri', '1. Fully functional computer laboratory/classroom.\r\n2. Installed and operational ICT equipment and internet connection.\r\n3. Teachers trained in ICT integration.\r\n4. Improved learner engagement in technology-based activities.', '- Infrastructure development and procurement\r\n- Stakeholder engagement and resource mobilization\r\n- ICT training and capacity building\r\n- Pilot implementation and evaluation\r\n- Maintenance and sustainability planning', 'School Year 2026–2027 (Phased implementation:', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Teachers, PTA O', '150000', 'This project aims to establish a functional ICT learning environment to enhance digital literacy and support modern teaching and learning needs aligned with 21st-century education.', 2026, 129114, 60, 12, 25),
