(5464, 'Review and update School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP', 'Enhance school planning and governance', 'Updated SIP and AIP', '1.Conduct collaborative planning workshops involving teachers, parents, learners, and community stakeholders in the preparation and review of the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).\r\n2.Utilize data-driven decision-making by analyzing school performance indicators, assessment results, and stakeholder feedback in identifying school priorities and needs.\r\n3.Organize consultative meetings and focus group discussions to gather recommendations and strengthen participatory governance.\r\n4.Establish clear roles and responsibilities among school personnel and stakeholders in the implementation of school programs and projects.\r\n5.Develop and implement monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to track the progress of school plans, programs, and activities', 'JULY 2026', 'School Planning Team', '0.00', '', 2026, 500443, 106, 12, 132),
(5465, 'Post financial reports and school accomplishments on transparency board', 'Promote transparency and accountability', 'Transparent school operations', '1.Regularly present and post school financial reports, procurement updates, and accomplishment reports on the transparency board and other communication platforms.\r\n2.Conduct periodic stakeholders’ meetings and consultations to discuss school programs, projects, budget utilization, and accomplishments.\r\n3.Establish clear policies and procedures in financial management, procurement, and implementation of school activities in accordance with existing DepEd rules and regulations', 'Monthly', 'School Head, Property Custodian, Bookkeeper', '0.00', '', 2026, 500443, 106, 12, 132),
(5466, 'Conduct Brigada Eskwela and school clean-up activities', 'Improve learning environment', 'Clean and safe school environment', '1.Conduct regular school clean-up drives, Brigada Eskwela, and maintenance activities to ensure a safe, clean, and learner-friendly environment.\r\n2.Mobilize teachers, parents, learners, and community volunteers to participate in school improvement and beautification projects.\r\n3.Repair and maintain school facilities, classrooms, furniture, and equipment to provide a conducive learning atmosphere.', 'May-June 2026', 'Teachers, Parents, Volunteers', '10000.00', '', 2026, 500443, 106, 12, 132),
(5467, 'Conduct classroom observations and coaching sessions', 'Strengthen instructional supervision', 'Monthly', '1.Conduct regular classroom observations using standardized observation tools aligned with DepEd teaching standards and instructional objectives.\r\n2.Prepare an observation schedule to ensure systematic and continuous instructional supervision among teachers.\r\n3.Provide pre-observation conferences to discuss lesson objectives, teaching strategies, and areas of focus prior to classroom observation.\r\n4.Utilize constructive feedback and coaching approaches to help teachers improve instructional practices and classroom management.', 'Improved teaching practices', 'School Head, Master Teachers', '0.00', '', 2026, 500443, 106, 12, 132),
(5468, 'Implement remediation and enrichment programs', 'Enhance learners’ academic performance', 'Improved learner achievement', 'Learner-centered approach\r\nDifferentiated instruction\r\nConstructivist approach\r\nInquiry-based learning', 'Whole School Year', 'Teachers, Learners, Parents', '0.00', '', 2026, 500443, 106, 12, 132),
(5469, 'Conduct Capacity Building for Teachers and Staff', 'To enhance competencies in leadership and instruction', 'Personnel equipped with updated knowledge and skills', 'Trainings, webinars and workshops', 'Whole Year', 'Teachers and Non-Teaching Staff', '7000', 'Based on training needs, In-Service Trainings', 2026, 128613, 106, 12, 132),
(5470, 'Conduct INSET, LAC sessions, and capability-building trainings', 'Develop teachers’ competencies', 'Enhanced teacher skills', '1.Conduct regular capacity-building activities such as INSET (In-Service Training), workshops, and seminars aligned with teachers’ identified needs and DepEd priorities.\r\nI2.mplement Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions to promote collaborative learning, sharing of best practices, and instructional problem-solving among teachers.\r\n3.Provide mentoring and coaching programs where master teachers and school leaders guide teachers in improving instructional competencies.\r\n4.Encourage participation in online and face-to-face professional development courses, including webinars and accredited training programs.', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers', '0.00', '', 2026, 500443, 106, 12, 132),
(5471, 'Conduct regular monitoring of SBM implementation and prepare reports', 'Strengthen monitoring and evaluation', 'Timely submission of reports', '1.Develop and implement a clear Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) plan aligned with the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).\r\n2.Conduct regular school monitoring visits and classroom observations to assess the implementation of programs, projects, and activities.\r\n3.Use standardized tools and checklists in gathering data to ensure consistency and accuracy of monitoring results.\r\n4.Establish a schedule for periodic evaluation of school performance indicators, including learner achievement, attendance, and program implementation.', 'Quarterly', 'SBM Coordinator, School Head', '0.00', '', 2026, 500443, 106, 12, 132),
(5472, 'Establish linkages with NGOs, alumni, and private stakeholders', 'Build partnerships and resource generation', 'Increased school support and resources', '1.Identify and map potential partners such as LGUs, NGOs, alumni, private companies, and local community organizations that can support school programs and projects.\r\n2.Conduct stakeholder meetings and partnership dialogues to present school needs and explore possible areas of collaboration and support.\r\n3.Develop partnership proposals and solicitations outlining specific projects, budget requirements, and expected outcomes.', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, PTA, Community Leaders', '0.00', '', 2026, 500443, 106, 12, 132),
(5473, 'Integrative LAC Sessions', 'To improve teaching quality through collaborative problem-solving.', 'Narrative reports and localized Lesson Plans.', 'Use existing Learning Action Cell (LAC) time to tackle actual classroom issues.', 'end of each term', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Teachers', '3000', '', 2026, 304236, 106, 12, 134),
(5474, 'Basic Transparency Board Update', 'To comply with accountability standards using a simple, visible system.', 'Updated posted budget (MOOE) and school performance charts.', 'Designate a \"Transparency Corner\" in the lobby; update after every liquidation.', 'Monthly', 'School Head, Administrative Officer (AO)', '0', '', 2026, 304236, 106, 12, 134),
(5475, 'Prepare and Post School Report Card (SRC)', 'To ensure transparency and accountability in school operations', 'Posted and disseminated School Report Card', 'Data gathering, report preparation, public posting', 'End of School Year', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator', '2000', 'For printing and reproduction purposes', 2026, 128613, 106, 12, 132),
(5476, 'Conduct Monitoring and Evaluation of SBM Programs', 'To assess implementation progress and identify areas for improvement', 'Monitoring reports and improvement recommendations', 'Classroom observation, surveys, meetings', 'Quarterly', 'Monitoring Team, School Head', '4000', 'Internal monitoring', 2026, 128613, 106, 12, 132),
(5477, 'Recognition of Stakeholders and Partners', 'To acknowledge contributions and sustain partnerships', 'Motivated and active stakeholders', 'Awarding ceremonies and recognition programs', 'March 2027', 'School Head, PTA, Teachers', '6000', 'Year-end evaluation', 2026, 128613, 106, 12, 132),
(5479, 'Conduct literacy and numeracy intervention programs for Grade 3 learners', 'Improve learners’ proficiency in early language, literacy, and numeracy skills', 'Increased percentage of Grade 3 learners reaching proficiency level', '1. Conduct baseline and quarterly assessments.\r\n2. Implement targeted remediation and intervention programs (e.g., Project THRIVE, CRLA, reading camps, numeracy drills).\r\n3. Provide differentiated instruction and learning materials.\r\n4. Conduct parent orientation and home learning support sessions.\r\n5. Monitor learner progress monthly.', 'SY 2026–2027', 'School Head, Master Teacher, SBM Team, Teache', '1500', 'Assessment tools, intervention materials, printing funds', 2026, 128537, 57, 12, 108),
(5480, 'Strengthen NAT preparation for Grades 6, 10, and 12', 'Increase learner achievement in 21st-century skills and core learning areas', 'Improved NAT performance and proficiency levels', '1. Conduct NAT review sessions and mock examinations.\r\n2. Analyze previous NAT results and identify least-mastered competencies.\r\n3. Integrate critical thinking, problem-solving, and communication tasks in lessons.\r\n4. Strengthen intervention classes for low-performing learners.\r\n5. Engage parents in learner support programs.', 'SY 2026–2027', 'School Head, Master Teacher, SBM Team, Subjec', '1500', 'NAT reviewers, test materials, learning modules, inks and bond papers', 2026, 128537, 57, 12, 108),
(5481, 'Institutionalize test item analysis after assessments', 'Strengthen data-driven instruction', 'Teachers regularly submit and use item analysis reports', '1. Conduct training on test item analysis and interpretation.\r\n2. Require teachers to perform item analysis after every major assessment.\r\n3. Use analysis results to adjust lesson plans and remediation strategies.\r\n4. Review assessment tools for alignment with MELCs.\r\n5. Monitor implementation during LAC sessions.', 'SY 2026–2027', 'School Head, Master Teacher, SBM Team, Teache', '1500', 'TOS templates, laptops, printing supplies', 2026, 128537, 57, 12, 108),
(5482, 'Upgrade school facilities to be SPED- and PWD-friendly', 'Improve inclusivity and accessibility of school facilities', 'Accessible and compliant school facilities', '1. Conduct school facility audit for accessibility needs.\r\n2. Install ramps, handrails, accessible comfort rooms, and signage.\r\n3. Designate inclusive learning spaces.\r\n4. Coordinate with LGU and stakeholders for funding and support.\r\n5. Promote awareness on inclusive education practices.', 'SY 2026–2027', 'School Head, Master Teacher, SBM Team, Stakeh', '1500', 'School funds, construction materials, stakeholder support', 2026, 128537, 57, 12, 108),
(5483, 'Decentralized Digital Learning', 'To provide learners access to computing resources (desktop computer and laptop) without constructing a dedicated building or maintaining a high-cost hardware fleet.', 'Functional mobile, shared, or blended computer learning system established. Enhanced readiness of learners for technology-driven education.', '1. Utilizing AI to analyze a learner\'s progress across various decentralized platforms and suggest the next best step\r\n2.  The project will use a developmental and descriptive approach to identify practical and cost-effective ways of providing learners access to computing resources without constructing a dedicated computer laboratory or maintaining expensive hardware systems.\r\n3.  Bring-Your-Own-Device (BYOD) approach', 'SY 2026–2027', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Teachers, Stake', '150000', 'Purchase Desktop Computer and Laptop', 2026, 128537, 57, 12, 108),
(5484, 'Convert part of a classroom, office or hallway into a reading area.', 'Create a comfortable and organized space that encourages reading and learning. Allocate and redesign at least one unused corner or section into a functional reading area.  Achieve daily use of the reading area by at least 20 students within one month', 'A functional reading corner or section is successfully converted into a clean, organized, and comfortable reading space. The area contains proper seating, lighting, decorations, and reading materials that encourage learning and relaxation.\r\nBooks, magazines, or educational materials are arranged and accessible to learniers.', '1. Use a systematic approach to transform an unused classroom, office, or hallway corner into a functional reading area that promotes learning and reading habits among students. The first strategy is space assessment and planning, where the group will identify a suitable location, evaluate available resources, and gather suggestions from students or teachers regarding the preferred design and reading materials.\r\n2. Resource collection and management, where books, magazines, and educational materials will be gathered through donations, school resources, or community support. Materials will then be categorized and organized for easy access.\r\n3. apply a student engagement strategy by encouraging students to use the reading area through reading activities, class orientations, and promotional materials. Rules and schedules may also be introduced to maintain order and cleanliness.', 'SY 2026–2027', 'School Head, Master Teacher, SBM Team, Stakeh', '10000', 'Magazines, Books, Modules, Laminating Film, Bond Paper, Ink, ', 2026, 128537, 57, 12, 108),
(5486, 'Conduct RMA, CRLA and PHIL-IRI Assessment', 'To identify the literacy and numeracy proficiency level of learners', 'Identified learners with low proficiency level in literacy and numeracy', 'Administer RMA , CRLA and PHIL-IRI tools to learners', '1st Quarter', 'School Head, Teachers, Learners', '1000', 'For implementation', 2026, 128598, 106, 12, 133),
(5487, 'Implementation of Reading Remediation Program', 'To improve learners’ reading comprehension and fluency', 'Improved literacy skills among struggling readers', 'Conduct individualized reading sessions, peer tutoring, and guided reading activities', '1st–3rd Quarter', 'Reading Teachers, Learners', '10000', 'Weekly monitoring', 2026, 128598, 106, 12, 133),
(5488, 'Implementation of Numeracy Remediation Program', 'To enhance learners’ basic numeracy skills', 'Improved numeracy performance of learners', 'Conduct drills, manipulatives activities, and differentiated instruction', '1st–3rd Quarter', 'Math Teachers, Learners', '10000', 'Weekly assessment', 2026, 128598, 106, 12, 133),
(5489, 'Progress Monitoring and Assessment', 'To monitor learners’ progress in literacy and numeracy', 'Progress reports and assessment results', 'Conduct regular formative tests and performance monitoring', 'Quarterly', 'Teachers, School Head', '1000', 'For evaluation', 2026, 128598, 106, 12, 133),
(5490, 'Conduct Post-Assessment (RMA ,CRLA and PHIL-IRI)', 'To measure improvement in learners’ proficiency level', 'Increased Mean Percentage Score and proficiency level', 'Administer post-tests using RMA ,CRLA, and PHIL-IRI tools', '4th Quarter', 'Teachers, Learners', '1000', 'End-of-year evaluation', 2026, 128598, 106, 12, 133),
(5492, 'Conduct of NAT Intervention and Remediation Program for Learners with Low PL\r\n', 'To improve the Performance Level (PL) of learners in the National Achievement Test through focused remediation activities, enrichment lessons, and regular assessment practices.\r\n', 'Improved NAT Performance Level of learners\r\n', 'Conduct remediation classes, review sessions, item analysis,  utilization of NAT-based learning materials, and regular monitoring of learner progress. Coordinate with teachers, parents, and school stakeholders for support.\r\n', 'June 2026- April 2027', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Subject Teacher', '10000', 'For implementation and monitoring\r\n', 2026, 128598, 106, 12, 133),
(5495, 'Class Remediation', 'Implement Aral Program to address learning- gaps in reading and comprehension in mathematics and science', '>Test results\r\n> Data ', 'Profiling\r\nSubmission of test results and data', 'June-March', 'Aral Tutors, Teacher , Aral focal & School he', '36000', 'Regularly monitored by the school head and school  Aral focal', 2026, 128549, 57, 12, 108),
(5496, 'Formulate SDRRM plan', 'Develop realistic responsive school Disaster- Risks Reduction Management  Plan', 'Approved SDRRM Plan', '>Planning Workshop\r\n> FGDs', 'July-Aug', 'School head, School DRRM focal, Selected teac', '2000', 'To be conducted', 2026, 128549, 57, 12, 108),
(5497, 'Form SBM and SGC planning team', 'Organize SBM and SGC school - community planning team', '> Approved SBM and SGC  Organization\r\n> List of members &  committee', '>Meetings\r\n>Election/Selection of members', 'July', 'School head, Selected teachers, Parents, Stud', '4000', 'To be conducted', 2026, 128549, 57, 12, 108),
(5498, 'Strengthening partnership', 'Strengthen collaborations and partnership with stakeholders and other schools', '> List of partnership and Donors\r\n> Approved letter of request and invitations\r\n>Approved Budget and liquidation report', '> Fund raising and Partnership building\r\n>Send letter request and Invitations', 'May- April', 'School head, AO ,BE focal', '6000', '', 2026, 128549, 57, 12, 108),
(5499, 'School - Based Action Cell', 'Conduct needs- based learning action cell', '> Accomplishment report\r\n> TA plan', 'FGDs  by grade level/ learning area', 'July- March', 'Master Teachers, School head, Teachers', '10000', '', 2026, 128549, 57, 12, 108),
(5500, 'Functional Computer Laboratory', 'Revive  functional computer laboratory', 'One classroom for computer laboratory', '>Coordinate with Division ICT focal\r\n>Assessment and Inventory\r\n>Repair, Rehabilitation and Upgrade', 'August to March', 'School ICT coor, School head', '160000', '', 2026, 128549, 57, 12, 108),
(5501, 'Strengthen linkages and partnerships with external stakeholders.\r\nConduct seminars and advocacy campaigns on the roles and responsibilities of the SGC', 'To generate resources and support for school programs and projects.\r\n\r\n', 'Established partnerships and increased stakeholder support.', 'Partnership meetings, stakeholder consultations, and networking activities.\r\nResource mobilization and partnership building.\r\nNeeds assistance from NGOs, alumni, private sectors, and LGUs.', 'Whole year round', 'school head, teachers, External partners', '', 'Needs assistance from NGOs, alumni, private sectors and LGUs', 2026, 128559, 57, 12, 109),
(5502, 'Conduct assessment and inventory of teachers’ workloads, teaching loads, and ancillary assignments.\r\n\r\nRequest additional teaching items or substitute teachers from higher offices and external stakeholders.\r\n', 'To address teacher shortage and reduce excessive workloads.', 'Submitted requests and possible augmentation of teaching personnel.', 'Preparation of requests, coordination meetings, and stakeholder consultations.\r\nResource mobilization and partnership building.\r\nAssistance from DepEd Division Office, LGU, and other stakeholders is necessary to address lack of manpower.', 'year round', 'School Head, Teachers', '', 'The school experiences challenges in fairly and equitably distributing teacher workloads due to the lack of teaching personnel. Teachers are often assigned other tasks functions and additional classes, especially when another teacher is on maternity leave, sick leave, or extended absence because there are no available substitute teachers. As a result, existing teachers absorb the workloads of absent personnel, affecting efficiency and teacher well-being. Through this action plan, the school aims to strengthen workload management practices, request additional teaching support, and seek assistance from external stakeholders and higher offices to improve the implementation of School-Based Management (SBM).', 2026, 128559, 57, 12, 109);
INSERT INTO `sgod_action_plan` (`id`, `activity`, `objective`, `ex_output`, `metho_strategy`, `time_frame`, `person_involved`, `bud_req`, `remarks`, `fy`, `school_id`, `division`, `region`, `district`) VALUES
(5503, 'Establish or strengthen a School Mental Wellness Committee\r\nImplement regular psychosocial support activities', 'To create a dedicated group responsible for planning and implementing mental wellness programs\r\nTo provide emotional and psychological support to learners and personnel, staff', 'Functional mental wellness committee with assigned roles and responsibilities\r\nEstablished psychosocial support activities and documented interventions\r\n ', 'Organization meeting and designation of members\r\nCollaborative governance and shared responsibility\r\nCounselling sessions, group discussions and mentoring activities\r\nCapacity Building and wellness promotion', 'Year round', 'Teachers, school head, external support', '', 'Requires support from external mental health advocates and partner agencies\r\nLimited trained guidance personnel; external support from LGU/DOH or partner NGO is needed', 2026, 128559, 57, 12, 109),
(5504, '\"ATTEND\"  (Attendance Tracking and Targeted Engagement for Development)', '1.To reduce the number of irregular and frequently absent learners  \r\n\r\n2.To identify root causes of absenteeism and provide timely interventions\r\n\r\n3.To strengthen parental involvement and community support\r\n', '1. Improved daily attendance rate (target: 90–95%)\r\n\r\n2. Active participation of parents and community stakeholders', 'Home visitation: addressing absenteeism cases directly at home', 'Whole School Year ', 'School Head Class Advisers / Teachers SBM Coo', '', '1. Implementation will depend on school resources and stakeholder support\r\n2. Priority will be given to learners with chronic absenteeism and those from remote areas\r\n3. Continuous monitoring and adjustment of interventions will be conducted\r\n4. Strong collaboration with parents and community is essential for success', 2026, 128557, 57, 12, 108),
(5505, '“STAY” (Strengthening Tracking and Assistance for Young Learners)', '1. To improve learner retention and reduce dropout rate\r\n2. To identify early signs of learners at risk of leaving school\r\n3. To provide timely academic and social interventions', '1. Increased retention rate per grade level\r\n2. Reduced dropout and repetition cases\r\n3. Functional tracking system for at-risk learners', '1. Early identification and profiling of at-risk learners\r\n2. Regular home visitation and follow-up\r\n3. Parent conferences and written agreements for intervention', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head Class Advisers / Teachers SBM Coo', '', '1. Priority intervention will be given to learners with repeated absences and academic difficulties.\r\n2. Strong collaboration with parents and community is essential for successful retention.\r\n3. Continuous monitoring and immediate response to risk cases will be implemented.\r\n4. Flexible strategies will be applied based on learner needs and school context.', 2026, 128557, 57, 12, 108),
(5506, 'Conduct of Project FLARE', 'To increase the number of learners with grade ready/independent reading level ', 'Increased number of learners with grade-ready/independent reading level ', 'Implementation of reading proficiency improvement program ', 'SY 2026-2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents, Learners', '50000', '', 2026, 128514, 57, 12, 118),
(5507, 'Implement Project DATOS', 'To establish online school data bank', 'Established online school data bank', 'Development of an online school data bank', 'SY 2026-2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Non-Teaching Personnel', '1000', '', 2026, 128514, 57, 12, 118),
(5508, 'Reading Remediation Program and Numeracy Enhancement Sessions', 'Improve students’ reading comprehension skills as well as Strengthen basic mathematical and problem-solving skills.', 'Improved reading fluency and comprehension scores, and Increased numeracy test performance', 'Guided reading, peer tutoring, phonics activities, comprehension exercises, Drill exercises, manipulatives, math games and differentiated instruction.', 'SY 2026–2027', 'School Head, Master Teacher, Teacher, Parents', '1500', 'Magazines, Books, Modules, Bond Paper, Ink', 2026, 128551, 57, 12, 108),
(5509, 'Integration of Technology in Classroom Activities', 'Expose students to technology-enhanced learning', 'Increased use of digital tools in academic tasks', 'Use of multimedia presentations, online learning platforms, educational apps', 'SY 2026–2027', 'School Head, Master Teacher, Subject Teache, ', '3000', 'Laptop, computer, notebook, tablet, mobile phone', 2026, 128551, 57, 12, 108),
(5510, 'Classroom Discussions and Values Integration Activities', 'Promote positive behavior, respect, and conflict resolution among students', 'Students exhibit improved behavior and respect for others', 'Role-playing, storytelling, reflective discussions, cooperative learning', 'SY 2026–2027', 'School Head, Master Teacher, Subject Teacher', '1500', 'Tarpulin, Bond Paper, Ink', 2026, 128551, 57, 12, 108),
(5511, 'Development of Standardized Assessment Tools', 'Ensure quality and aligned assessment tools are used in evaluating learners', 'Improved and validated test questionnaires', 'Collaborative test construction and review', 'SY 2026–2027', 'School Head, Master Teacher, SBM Team, Teache', '1500', '', 2026, 128551, 57, 12, 108),
(5512, 'Stakeholder Consultation and Planning Meeting', 'Identify common concerns, priorities, and schedules of stakeholders and partner schools', 'Agreed collaboration plans and activity calendar', 'Coordination meetings, surveys, collaborative planning', 'SY 2026-2027', 'School Head, Master Teacher, SBM Team, Teache', '1500', '', 2026, 128551, 57, 12, 108),
(5513, 'Conduct Needs Assessment for Reading Corners inside the classroom', 'Identify classroom space needs to put up a reading corner, available resources, and priority requirements', 'Assessment report and reading corner development plan', 'Survey, inventory, consultation meetings', 'SY 2026-2027', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers', '1500', '', 2026, 128551, 57, 12, 108),
(5514, 'Implementation of ICT-Based Learning Activities', 'Improve learners’ digital literacy and 21st-century skills', 'Increased student engagement in ICT-related activities', 'Computer-assisted lessons, research activities, digital projects', 'SY 2026-2027', 'Teachers, Learners', '1500', '', 2026, 128551, 57, 12, 108),
(5515, 'Conduct activities with SGC members', 'To activate SGC members through training, regular meetings, recognition and clear involvement in the school plans and initiatives.', 'Mobilized SGC members to support school engagement ', 'Orientation, meetings, collaborative planning, trainings, capacity building and recognition programs ', 'Within school year', 'School head, teachers and SGC members ', '5250', 'To be conducted.', 2026, 128483, 57, 12, 111),
(5516, 'ICT Capacity-Building Training\r\n', 'Strengthen digital literacy among teachers and pupils', 'Trained teachers and non teaching personnel  and functional computer lab', 'Conduct ICT workshops and peer mentoring', 'SEPTEMBER 2026', 'Teacher and Non Teaching Personnel', '20000', '', 2026, 128275, 57, 12, 124),
(5517, 'Student Leadership Development', 'Empower Supreme Pupil Government officers', 'Leadership training modules and student-led projects', 'Organize leadership camps and mentoring sessions', 'SEPTEMBER 2026', 'Principal, Teacher sand Learners', '5000', '', 2026, 128275, 57, 12, 124),
(5518, 'Health and Wellness Campaign', 'Promote student and staff well-being', 'Regular health check-ups and awareness sessions', 'Partner with barangay health workers', 'Quarterly', 'Teaching, Non Teaching  and Students', '10000', '', 2026, 128275, 57, 12, 124),
(5519, 'Health and Wellness Campaign', 'Promote student and staff well-being', 'Regular health check-ups and awareness sessions', 'Partner with barangay health workers', 'Quarterly', 'Teaching, Non Teaching  and Students', '10000', '', 2026, 128275, 57, 12, 124),
