(5521, 'Monitoring and Evaluation Framework', 'Track progress of SBM implementation', 'Consolidated M&E reports', 'Use scorecards and feedback tools', 'Quarterly', 'SBM coordinator and School Principal', '0', '', 2026, 128275, 57, 12, 124),
(5523, '1.1 Establish Peer Support Groups', 'Encourage peer-to-peer emotional support and early intervention', 'Active peer support groups assisting students with concerns', 'Selection and training of peer facilitators and regular meetings', 'August, 2026', 'Guidance Counselor, Teachers, Student Leaders', '2500.00', 'Peer facilitators to submit reports', 2026, 128555, 57, 12, 0),
(5524, '1.2 Mental Health Training and Wellness Activities Program', 'To address lack of trained counselors and increase mental health support and activities for learners', 'Trained school personnel on basic counseling skills; regular mental health activities conducted; improved learner well-being and participation in support programs', 'Conduct training workshops for teachers on basic counseling and psychological first aid; implement monthly mental health activities (stress management, peer support groups, mindfulness sessions); establish referral system for serious cases', 'Whole School Year (Training: 1–2 days per qua', 'School Head, Guidance Counselor, Teachers, Ex', '8000.00', 'Ensure confidentiality of learners; strengthen referral system to external professionals for specialized cases', 2026, 128555, 57, 12, 0),
(5525, '2. Strengthen and improve computer laboratory/classroom facilities.', 'The school aims to improve access to ICT resources and facilities, enhance ICT integration in teaching and learning, and ensure the functionality and sustainability of ICT equipment and infrastructure.', 'Establish a functional and improved computer laboratory or classroom, increase learner access to ICT resources, enhance the ICT skills of teachers and learners, and improve internet connectivity and ICT support systems.', 'Procure additional computers through MOOE, donations, or DepEd programs, repair and upgrade existing ICT equipment, strengthen ICT capacity through teacher training, establish a dedicated computer laboratory or classroom with proper facilities, and coordinate with stakeholders for ICT support and assistance.', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Teachers, LGU, ', '200000.00', 'Priority shall be given to repair, upgrading, and sustainability of ICT facilities.', 2026, 128555, 57, 12, 0),
(5526, '3. Conduct Disaster Preparedness Orientation and Training', 'Enhance knowledge and skills on disaster preparedness and response', 'Increased awareness and readiness among students and staff', 'Seminars, workshops, and hands-on demonstrations', '1st Semester of 2026', 'DRRM Coordinator, Teachers, BFP, MDRRMO Perso', '6000.00', 'Include first aid and basic rescue training', 2026, 128555, 57, 12, 0),
(5527, '4. Conduct regular inspection and preventive maintenance of school facilities', '\"Ensure safety and usability of facilities, strengthen monitoring and documentation system.\r\nand improve coordination among concerned personnel.\"', 'Safe and functional school facilities, updated inspection and monitoring reports and immediate response to repair needs.', 'Strengthen preventive maintenance, promote proper use and care of facilities, improve communication and repair mechanisms and conduct regular inspection and monitoring.', 'Every Semester / Whole School Year', 'School Head, Inspection Team, Property Custod', '25000.00', 'Continuous monitoring shall be implemented.', 2026, 128555, 57, 12, 0),
(5528, 'W.A.S.H. (Water, Access, Sanitation, and Hygiene): Installation of a Sustainable School Water Supply System and rainwater harvesting facility.', '1. To secure a stable, safe, and continuous water supply for school learners and personnel.\r\n2. To improve school sanitation, handwashing compliance, and daily maintenance of restroom facilities.\r\n3. To achieve a 100% functional water access point ac', '1. Fully operational centralized water system (e.g., deep well with electric pump/overhead tank or functional commercial water line connection).\r\n2. Installed rainwater storage tanks as a secondary/back-up resource for sanitation.\r\n3. Zero disruptions in school handwashing activities and restroom maintenance due to water scarcity.', '1. Assessment and Coordination: Conduct a technical assessment of the best water source location and collaborate with local water districts or engineering experts.\r\n2. Stakeholder Engagement: Mobilize the Parents-Teachers Association (PTA) and Barangay Local Government Unit (BLGU) for counterpart labor and security assistance.\r\n3. Resource Resource Generation: Allocate a portion of school funds and initiate a \"Brigada Eskwela\" donation drive for plumbing materials, tanks, and water pumps.\r\n4. Implementation & Monitoring: Execute the installation phase, followed by regular weekly maintenance checks by the school physical facilities coordinator.', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, Administrative Officer, School P', '20000', 'This action plan directly supports SBM Pillar 4 (Management of Resources) and Pillar 2 (Curriculum and Instruction - by ensuring a safe, healthy learning environment that prevents water-borne illnesses and student absenteeism). Regular monitoring reports will be attached to the monthly liquidation and SBM progress folder.', 2026, 128556, 57, 12, 108),
(5529, 'Preparation and utilization of contextualized learning materials', 'To develop learner-centered and contextualized instructional materials suited to the needs, interests, and abilities of learners.', 'Localized and contextualized learning materials for classroom use', 'Conduct school based training for localized and contextualized instructional material', 'Whole School Year 2026–2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Master Teachers, Learn', '10000.00', 'Continuous monitoring and evaluation shall be conducted to ensure effectiveness and responsiveness of learning materials to learners’ needs.', 2026, 315812, 57, 12, 116),
(5530, 'Conduct of remediation and intervention activities in Reading, Comprehension, Science and Technology, and Mathematics under Project E.C.O', 'To improve learners’ academic performance and address identified learning gaps through targeted remediation activities.', 'To improve learners’ academic performance and address identified learning gaps through targeted remediation activities.', 'Conduct diagnostic assessments, provide remediation sessions, utilize differentiated instruction, peer tutoring, and contextualized intervention materials', 'Whole School Year 2026–2027', 'School Head, Subject Teachers, Reading/Math/S', '15000.00', 'Progress monitoring and regular assessment shall be conducted to evaluate learners’ improvement and effectiveness of interventions.', 2026, 315812, 57, 12, 116),
