(5663, 'Conduct orientation, workshops, and continuous monitoring of SBM principles, standards, and processes; establish functional SBM structures and committees; implement self-assessment and improvement planning.', '- To fully orient all school personnel, parents, and community stakeholders on the concepts, principles, and benefits of School-Based Management.\r\n- To organize and operationalize the School Governing Council (SGC) and other required committees as ma', '- Conducted orientation sessions and training workshops with attendance sheets, minutes of meetings, and learning materials.\r\n- Approved composition and terms of reference of the School Governing Council and working committees.\r\n- Completed School Self-Evaluation Tool (SSET) and SBM assessment report.\r\n- Updated and approved School Improvement Plan (SIP), Annual Implementation Plan (AIP), and School Report Card (SRC).\r\n- Documented proceedings of meetings, decision-making processes, and resource utilization reports.\r\n- Increased stakeholder participation and awareness of school governance and operations.', '- Information Dissemination: Conduct assemblies, meetings, and distribution of materials to explain SBM policies, roles, and responsibilities.\r\n- Capability Building: Organize workshops, seminars, and learning sessions focused on leadership, planning, financial management, and monitoring.\r\n- Organization and Structuring: Facilitate the election or selection of members to the SGC and committees; define roles and functions clearly.\r\n- Assessment and Planning: Guide stakeholders in using standard tools to evaluate school performance; analyze results and formulate action plans to address identified needs.\r\n- Participatory Governance: Encourage active involvement of stakeholders in planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation of school programs and projects.\r\n- Monitoring and Feedback: Establish regular review mechanisms; conduct periodic checking of progress; provide feedback and make necessary adjustments to plans and activities.\r\n- Documentation and Reporting: Systematically record all activities, decisions, and outputs; prepare and submit required reports to relevant authorities and share with stakeholders.', '- Year-round / Quarterly: Orientation, meetin', 'School Head, Teachers, SGC, PTA Officers and ', '17000', '- Activities are aligned with DepEd Orders and guidelines on School-Based Management.\r\n- Funds will be utilized in accordance with government accounting and auditing rules and regulations.\r\n- Progress will be reported regularly to the District and Division Offices.\r\n- Success depends on active participation and commitment of all stakeholders.', 2026, 129102, 60, 12, 25),
