(5683, 'aily Reading Remediation\r\n\r\nConduct guided reading sessions focusing on phonics, fluency, vocabulary, and comprehension.', 'To improve Grade 3 learners’ phonics, fluency, vocabulary, and reading comprehension skills through daily guided reading remediation activities.', '1. Improved reading fluency and comprehension skills among Grade 3 learners\r\n2. Increased number of learners achieving grade-level literacy proficiency', 'Use guided reading, phonics instruction, peer-assisted learning, and differentiated remediation activities.', 'June 2026 - April 2027', 'Teachers, Master Teacher, School Head, and Vo', '15000', 'Ongoing implementation subject to monitoring and evaluation of learners’ reading progress and the budget depends on the MOOE availability. ', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5684, 'Intensified NAT Review and 21st-Century Skills Enhancement Program – conduct regular review sessions, competency-based remediation, and skills-focused activities in critical areas.', 'To improve learners’ proficiency in core learning areas and strengthen 21st-century skills in preparation for the National Achievement Test (NAT) in Grade-6.', '1. Improved NAT performance and higher proficiency levels in core learning areas\r\n2. Enhanced 21st-century skills such as critical thinking, communication, collaboration, and problem-solving among learners', 'Conduct intensive review sessions, competency-based remediation, mock NAT assessments, differentiated instruction, and integration of 21st-century skills activities through collaborative, inquiry-based, and technology-enhanced learning approaches.', 'September 16 - March 23, 2027', 'Master Teacher, Subject Teachers,  School Hea', '18000', 'Not yet implemented; to be scheduled after the teachers’ assessment during the first term and based on identified learning gaps.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5685, 'Scheduled Collaborative Test Item Analysis Sessions – conduct short, structured  monthly meetings where teachers review assessment results, identify least-mastered skills, and immediately integrate findings into targeted remediation activities despit', 'To strengthen the consistent conduct and utilization of test item analysis results despite limited time and capacity, in order to improve teaching and learning processes.', '1.  Regularly conducted test item analysis reports used in instructional planning\r\n2. Improved teaching strategies based on identified least-mastered skills and competencies', 'Conduct simplified and time-efficient test item analysis using ready-made templates, integrate results during short LAC sessions, and prioritize least-mastered skills for targeted remediation and instructional adjustments.', 'Monthly', 'Teachers, Master Teacher, School Head and SPT', '5000', 'Implementation may be affected by limited time and workload; therefore, analysis will be simplified and integrated into regular LAC sessions for sustainability.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5686, 'Construction of additional comfort rooms, ramps, septic tank, wash facilities and concreted pathwalks', 'To construct additional comfort rooms, ramps, septic tanks, wash facilities and concreted pathwalks.', 'Constructed dditional comfort rooms, ramps, septic tanks, wash facilities and concreted pathwalks.', 'Conduct needs assessment and site planning, secure approvals and funding support, coordinate with stakeholders for resource mobilization, and implement phased construction of comfort rooms, ramps, septic tank, wash facilities, and concreted pathways with regular monitoring of quality and safety standards.', 'June 2026- May 2027', 'School Planning Team andSchool Project Team', '380000', 'To be implemented in phases subject to fund availability, stakeholder support, and compliance with safety and accessibility standards.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5687, 'School Safety and Preparedness Improvement Initiative – organize procurement, donation drives, and stakeholder partnerships to complete emergency equipment and ensure accessibility during drills and actual emergencies.', 'To enhance collaboration with stakeholders in providing and sustaining adequate emergency preparedness resources for the safety of learners and personnel.', '1. Complete and well-maintained emergency kits available in school clinic and evacuation area\r\n2. Strengthened stakeholder support and partnerships for school emergency preparedness resources', 'Establish a school safety committee responsible for monitoring, maintenance, and regular updating of emergency kits and equipment.', 'By Term', 'School Planning Team and School Project Team', '10000', 'Implementation will be done in phases depending on the availability of resources and stakeholder support.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5688, 'Participatory School Planning System Strengthening – establish structured mechanisms such as focus group discussions and planning committees to ensure inclusive decision-making..', 'To enhance stakeholder involvement in school planning through structured and inclusive consultation mechanisms.', 'Documented consultation results and planning outputs reflecting stakeholder inputs.', 'Use standardized documentation tools (minutes of meeting, attendance sheets, and consultation forms) to systematically capture stakeholder inputs.', 'By Term', 'School Planning Team and School Project Team', '5000', 'o be implemented by term  with proper documentation and consolidation of stakeholder inputs.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5689, 'Stakeholder Coordination and Communication Enhancement Activity – strengthen communication channels through reminders, notices, and follow-ups to improve attendance and participation.', 'To enhance coordination and engagement of stakeholders by ensuring timely dissemination of meeting schedules and updates.', 'Improved and timely communication system through consistent reminders, notices, and follow-ups', 'Assign focal persons per stakeholder group to send reminders and conduct follow-ups before scheduled activities.', 'By Term', 'School Planning Team and School Project Team', '5000', 'To be implemented continuously to ensure effective communication and sustained stakeholder participation in school activities.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5690, 'Stakeholder Coordination and Communication Enhancement Activity – strengthen communication channels through reminders, notices, and follow-ups to improve attendance and participation.', 'To enhance coordination and engagement of stakeholders by ensuring timely dissemination of meeting schedules and updates.', 'Improved and timely communication system through consistent reminders, notices, and follow-ups', 'Assign focal persons per stakeholder group to send reminders and conduct follow-ups before scheduled activities.', 'By Term', 'School Planning Team and School Project Team', '5000', 'To be implemented continuously to ensure effective communication and sustained stakeholder participation in school activities.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5691, 'Contextualized Instructional Material Development Activity – develop ready-to-use lesson exemplars, activity sheets, and modules that naturally integrate peace education and core values across learning areas.', 'To used contextualized instructional material development activity.', 'Increased use of ready-to-use materials by teachers in daily lesson implementation.', 'Establish a shared repository (print and digital) of instructional materials for easy access and utilization by all teachers.', 'By Term', 'Teachers, Master Teacher, and School Head ', '5000', 'Ongoing implementation by term validation and improvement based on classroom feedback and learner outcomes.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5692, 'Strengthening Child Protection Committee (CPC) Capacity Building Program – conduct regular orientation and refresher training sessions for CPC members on updated child protection policies, protocols, and procedures to ensure proper implementation and', 'To enhance the knowledge and capacity of Child Protection Committee members on updated policies and protocols to ensure effective and compliant implementation of child protection mechanisms in the school.', 'Improved implementation and compliance of child protection policies and procedures in the school', 'Provide printed copies of updated policies and quick-reference guides for CPC members.', 'March 2027', 'School Planning Team and School Project Team', '5000', 'To be implemented at the end of March 2027  to ensure continuous updating of CPC members’ knowledge and skills on child protection policies.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5693, 'Teacher Peer Sharing and Material Exchange Program – encourage sharing and adaptation of effective contextualized materials among teachers to reduce workload and improve responsiveness.', 'To strengthen collaboration among teachers in sharing and adapting contextualized instructional materials in order to reduce workload and improve responsiveness to diverse learner needs.', 'Increased use of adapted and improved teaching materials that address diverse learner needs', 'Conduct regular peer-sharing sessions during LAC meetings for presentation, critique, and adaptation of effective teaching materials.', 'By Term', 'Teachers, Master Teacher, and School Head ', '5000', 'Ongoing implementation subject to availability of time for collaboration and access to shared platforms or repositories.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5694, 'Learning Gap Assessment and Targeted Intervention Activity – administer diagnostic tests and analyze results to identify specific least-mastered skills for focused remediation.\r\n', 'To identify learners’ least-mastered competencies through diagnostic assessment and use the results to design and implement focused, targeted remediation activities that address specific learning gaps.', '1. Consolidated diagnostic test results showing learners’ strengths and least-mastered competencies                                            2. List of identified target learners per least-mastered skill', '1. Adjust interventions based on ongoing assessment results and feedback\r\n2. Document progress and maintain learner intervention records for continuous improvement', 'By Term', 'Teachers, Master Teacher, and School Head ', '5000', 'Emphasizes the importance of accurate documentation for tracking learner progress and informing decisions.', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
(5695, 'Reading and Numeracy Intervention Program', 'Increase literacy and numeracy skills among learners', 'Increased reading comprehension and numeracy proficiency', 'Daily reading drills; peer tutoring; reproduction of low-cost instructional materials', '1st Trimester – Launch program, 2nd Trimester', 'Phil-IRI,RMA,CRLA, Reading Coordinator and te', '8000', '', 2026, 501770, 57, 12, 116),
(5696, 'Creation of a shared repository of culture-sensitive learning resources for teacher use', 'To  update and sustain a shared repository of culture-sensitive learning resources that supports teachers in delivering inclusive, relevant, and culturally responsive instruction while fostering collaboration and improving learner outcomes.', 'Feedback and usage reports on the effectiveness of shared resources.', 'Monitor frequency of resource access and utilization from the repository (logbook)', 'By Term', 'Teachers, Master Teacher, and School Head ', '5000', 'Encourages efficient use of available culture-sensitive materials in instruction', 2026, 128552, 57, 12, 108),
