(5760, 'Student Leadership Enhancement Program', 'Develop basic leadership skills of SPG officers\r\nEncourage active participation in school activities and decision-making\r\nPromote responsibility, teamwork, and good behavior among pupils', 'Trained SPG officers\r\nSimple SPG plan of activities\r\nConducted at least 1 pupil-led school activity (teacher\'s day tribute program)', 'Short leadership orientation for pupils\r\nSimple workshops (role-playing, group activities)\r\nGuided planning of SPG activities\r\nTeacher-assisted implementation of a small project', 'July', 'School Head, SPG Adviser, SPG Officers (Grade', '5,000.00', 'On-going', 2026, 128480, 57, 12, 111),
(5762, 'PWD-Friendly School Accessibility Improvement Program', 'To improve accessibility and ensure a more inclusive learning environment for learners with disabilities through simple and doable facility enhancements.', 'Improved or installed basic ramps, clearer pathways, and identified priority areas for PWD accessibility improvement.', 'The school will conduct a simple accessibility check, prioritize urgent needs, and implement small-scale improvements using available school resources and stakeholder support.', 'The activity will be implemented gradually th', 'School head, teachers, DRRM/facilities coordi', '20,000.00', 'On-going and implemented in phases', 2026, 128480, 57, 12, 111),
(5763, 'LIBREAD: Library-Based Reading Empowerment for Academic Development', 'To enhance learners’ reading comprehension, vocabulary, and overall academic performance by promoting active and sustained engagement in library-based reading activities, fostering a culture of reading, and providing accessible, interactive, and tech', 'Improved reading comprehension, fluency, and vocabulary among learners\r\nIncreased student participation in library and reading-related activities\r\nEnhanced interest and motivation in reading and independent learning\r\nDevelopment of a positive reading culture within the school community\r\nImproved academic performance across learning areas\r\nIncreased utilization of library resources and technology-assisted reading tools\r\nStrengthened learners’ critical thinking and communication skills through regular reading engagement', 'The LIBREAD program will be implemented through structured and engaging library-based reading activities tailored to the needs of learners in a multigrade setting. As a school with four teachers handling different grade levels, reading sessions will be carefully scheduled to ensure effective supervision and learner participation. The following strategies will be applied:\r\n\r\nReading Assessment and Grouping\r\nLearners will undergo reading assessments to determine their reading levels and key stages. Based on the results, learners will be grouped according to their reading ability to provide appropriate reading materials and interventions.\r\n30-Minute Scheduled Reading Sessions\r\nEach class will be given a designated 30-minute reading period. Teachers will rotate and supervise learners according to the multigrade class structure to ensure that all learners receive guidance and support during reading activities.\r\nGuided and Independent Reading Activities\r\nLearners will participate in guided reading, silent reading, peer reading, storytelling, and comprehension exercises using age-appropriate and level-based books available in the library.\r\nMotivational Reward System\r\nTo encourage active participation and reading improvement, learners who successfully read according to their assigned key stage or reading level will be rewarded with toys and educational playtime activities. This motivational strategy aims to make reading enjoyable and encourage learners to actively improve their reading skills.\r\nInteractive and Enjoyable Learning Environment\r\nThe library will serve as a learner-friendly and engaging space where reading is combined with fun and interactive activities to build learners’ confidence and interest in reading.\r\nTeacher Collaboration in a Multigrade Setting\r\nThe four teachers will collaborate in planning schedules, monitoring learner progress, preparing reading materials, and conducting interventions suited to the different grade levels and reading abilities.\r\nMonitoring and Evaluation\r\nLearners’ progress will be monitored regularly through reading records, oral reading assessments, and teacher observations to evaluate improvements in reading comprehension, fluency, and participation.', 'June-April', 'School Head', '', '', 2026, 128438, 57, 12, 121),
(5766, 'Advocacy & Enrollment Campaign', 'Encourage enrollment in alternative learning programs', 'Increased enrollment of OSYs and adult learners', 'Conduct surveys, coordinate with barangay officials and community leaders and ALS teacher.', '1- 2 Months', 'Teachers, ALS coordinators, PTA	', '2000', 'ALS program not yet implemented', 2026, 128425, 57, 12, 121),
(5767, 'Teachers prepare contextualized learning materials responsive to the needs of learners', 'To develop and provide contextualized and learner-responsive instructional materials that address the varied learning needs, abilities, and interests of learners in a multigrade classroom setting.', 'Contextualized learning materials aligned with learners’ needs and competencies\r\nImproved learner engagement and participation in classroom activities\r\nEnhanced understanding of lessons through localized and relevant instructional resources\r\nAvailability of teacher-made learning materials suited for multigrade instruction', 'Teachers will collaboratively prepare and develop contextualized learning materials based on learners’ reading levels, interests, and academic needs. The materials will include localized examples, visual aids, activity sheets, and differentiated tasks appropriate for multigrade learners. Teachers will conduct regular planning sessions to identify competencies that require intervention and enhancement. The prepared materials will be utilized during classroom instruction, remediation, and enrichment activities to support effective and inclusive learning.', 'June-April', 'School Head, Class Adviser', '30000', 'The preparation of contextualized learning materials is essential in addressing the diverse learning needs of learners, especially in a multigrade setting. Continuous collaboration among teachers is encouraged to ensure that instructional materials remain relevant, engaging, and responsive to learners’ needs despite limited resources.', 2026, 128438, 57, 12, 121),
(5768, 'Needs Assessment & Learner Profiling', 'Identify OSYs and potential ALS learners', 'Master list of target learners', 'Coordinate with barangay, ALS Teacher,  conduct surveys and interviews', '1- 2 Months', 'School head, teachers, ALS teacher, barangay ', '2000', 'No identified ALS learners in school records', 2026, 128425, 57, 12, 121),
(5770, 'Implementation of Reading and numeracy intervention program', 'To strengthen reading and numeracy intervention programs, provide continuous remediation classes, engage parents in monitoring learner progress, and utilize appropriate instructional materials to improve proficiency levels.', 'Improved reading and numeracy skills', 'Conduct regular remediation classes, use differentiated instructional materials, monitor learner progress, involve parents through meetings and follow-ups, provide continuous assessment and feedback', 'Whole school year', 'School Head, Teachers, Tutor, AO', '3000', 'Subject for monitoring and evaluation', 2026, 128495, 57, 12, 111),
