(5968, 'Conduct NAT Review and Enhancement Program focusing on core learning areas (Math, Science, English, Filipino, Araling Panlipunan); Organize mock NAT examinations and feedback sessions.;  Integrate 21st Century Skills Development Modules (critical thi', '•	Improve Grade 6 learners’ mastery of competencies across all core subjects.; •	Strengthen learners’ application of 21st century skills in problem-solving and collaborative tasks;  •	Enhance teachers’ capacity to deliver instruction aligned with NAT', '•	At least 85% of Grade 6 learners achieve proficiency in NAT core learning areas.;  •	Learners demonstrate improved performance in critical thinking, communication, and collaboration tasks.;  •	Teachers apply innovative strategies in classroom instruction and assessment.', '•	Diagnostic and formative assessments to identify learning gaps early.\r\n•	Peer tutoring and small-group interventions for struggling learners.\r\n•	Regular progress monitoring through mock exams and performance tracking.\r\n•	Parental and community involvement to reinforce study habits and provide support resources.\r\n•	Use of ICT-based learning platforms and interactive activities to strengthen engagement.\r\n•	 Project-based learning to integrate 21st century skills with subject content.\r\n•	LAC Sessions/ School INSET', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Grade 6 teachers, Master Teacher, School Head', '5000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5969, 'Orientation and Capacity Building for SGC Members                                                                                      \r\nRegular SGC Meetings and Stakeholder Consultation', 'To increase awareness of SGC roles, functions, duties, and responsibilities\r\nTo improve the participation and engagement of SGC members', 'SGC members are knowledgeable and actively participate in meetings and school programs\r\nIncreased attendance and active involvement during meetings and school activities', 'Conduct orientation seminars, workshops, and interactive discussions. \r\nSchedule regular meetings, send advance notices, and provide open forum discussions.', 'JUNE  2026 - APRIL  2027', 'School Head, SGC Officers, Teachers, SPTA Off', '1000.00', 'Strengthen commitment and participation.\r\nEnsure transparency and collaboration.', 2026, 128279, 57, 12, 116),
(5970, 'Remedial Reading Program on Numeracy, Science,  and English', 'To improve learners’ reading comprehension and vocabulary skills\r\nTo strengthen learners’ understanding of basic and advanced Mathematics concepts\r\nTo enhance understanding of difficult concepts in Science and English', 'Improved reading comprehension and fluency among learners\r\nIncreased numeracy skills and improved Mathematics performance\r\nImproved academic performance in Science and English subjects', 'Conduct daily reading sessions, guided reading, and peer tutoring\r\nUse differentiated instruction, drills, games, interactive activities, and problem-solving activities', 'JUNE  2026 - APRIL  2027', 'Subject Teachers, Reading/ Mathematics/ Scien', '3000.00', 'Prioritize struggling readers. Monitor learner progress regularly. Focus on the least mastered competencies.', 2026, 128279, 57, 12, 116),
(5971, 'Targeted Remediation Program (subject-specific small-group tutoring), Teacher Capacity Building (differentiation & assessment), Attendance Support, and Monthly Data Review.', 'Strengthen early identification and support for learners below benchmarks; improve teaching strategies; raise attendance; achieve at least 80% proficiency by NAT administration.', 'Individual Learning Plans (ILPs); weekly 45–60 min tutoring (2–3x/week); one teacher workshop + 3 coaching visits per teacher; attendance logs and monthly progress reports; baseline, midline, endline assessments per grade.', 'Screen learners in Weeks 1–4 using quick NAT-aligned checks; group learners by skill gaps (4–6 per group); set 3–6 week ILP targets; run multisensory, competency-focused tutoring; hold teacher workshops with classroom modeling and feedback cycles; assign focal staff for attendance follow-up and parent engagement; convene monthly data meetings to adjust interventions.', 'Weeks 1–4: screening and ILPs. Weeks 5–36: tu', 'School Head, Grade 6/10/12 subject teachers, ', '', 'Start with teacher‑led, low‑cost strategies; partner with SGC/PTA/LGU for resources and volunteer tutors; adapt ILPs for learners with special needs; reduce group size or increase frequency if progress is slow; align schedule with NAT timetables.', 2026, 128325, 57, 12, 116),
(5972, 'Mentor-led workshops, collaborative material-development sessions, peer review/sharing hub, classroom coaching, and repository creation.', 'Build teacher skills in designing contextualized, differentiated materials; produce ready-to-use CLMs; promote peer sharing and continuous improvement.', 'At least 10 contextualized lesson materials per grade/subject, one repository (digital/print), 1 workshop, 3 coaching visits per teacher, peer review logs.', 'One-day workshop on CLM design and differentiation; teachers form small subject teams to draft materials using local contexts; master teacher coaches via model lesson and observe–feedback cycles; peer review meeting to refine materials; upload final CLMs to repository.', 'Week 1: workshop and team formation. Weeks 2–', 'School Head, Master Teacher/Resource Person, ', '', 'Use existing free templates and local resources to minimize cost. Encourage teachers to contribute one CLM per term. Coordinate with SGC/PTA and LGU for contextual content (local stories, data). Want this as a one-page printable template?', 2026, 128325, 57, 12, 116),
(5973, 'Training on item analysis, use of a school-wide item-analysis template, analysis of quarterly/formative tests, and integration of results into LAC sessions and lesson planning.', 'To strengthen early use of item-analysis results to identify learner gaps, adjust teaching strategies, and improve future assessments and lesson design.', 'Standard item-analysis template used by all teachers; item-analysis reports per subject/quarter; at least 2 LAC sessions per quarter focused on item results; revised lesson plans addressing identified weak competencies.', 'School Head and Master Teacher introduce a simple item-analysis template (easy to compute facility index and difficulty index). Teachers analyze their own quarterly/formative tests within 1 week after checking. In LAC, teachers share top strengths and weakest items, then co-plan reteaching and remediation.', 'Before each quarter: brief orientation and te', 'School Head, Master Teacher/Subject Coordinat', '4000.00', 'Use simple, teacher-friendly tools; avoid heavy computation. Store item-analysis reports in a subject file or folder for future reference. Align remediation and next quarter’s tests with the weakest items.', 2026, 128325, 57, 12, 116),
(5974, 'School-Based Management Re-Orientation and Capacity-Building Workshop', 'To strengthen stakeholders’ understanding and participation in SBM by equipping teachers, staff, parents, and community members with knowledge and skills on planning, monitoring, and evaluating school programs.', 'Enhanced stakeholder participation, improved transparency, and stronger alignment of school initiatives with SBM standards, leading to better governance and student outcomes.', 'The school will adopt a participatory and collaborative approach by engaging teachers, parents, learners, and community stakeholders in planning and decision-making. Activities will be implemented through workshops, consultations, and capacity-building sessions to ensure shared responsibility. Monitoring and evaluation mechanisms will be established using regular reporting, feedback systems, and performance reviews to track progress. ', 'Long-Term (7–12 months): Sustain initiatives ', 'School Head, Teachers,Learners,  Parents/Guar', '5000', '', 2026, 128682, 106, 12, 134),
(5975, 'Develop contextualized lesson plans and instructional materials aligned with learners’ cultural, linguistic, and socio-economic backgrounds; Conduct teacher training workshops on contextualization and localization of curriculum; Organize peer-sharing', '•	Equip teachers with the skills to design learning materials that reflect learners’ realities and community contexts.•	Ensure instructional materials are inclusive, culturally relevant, and responsive to diverse learner needs.•	Promote collaboration', '•	At least 90% of teachers produce contextualized lesson plans and instructional materials. •	A repository of school-based contextualized learning resources is established and maintained. •	Improved learner engagement and performance as evidenced by classroom observations and formative assessments.\r\n•	Teachers demonstrate increased confidence and creativity in instructional delivery.\r\n', '•	Needs assessment surveys to identify learners’ backgrounds, interests, and challenges.\r\n•	Use of local stories, examples, and resources in teaching materials.\r\n•	Collaborative workshops and mentoring sessions to guide teachers in contextualization.\r\n•	Integration of indigenous knowledge, local culture, and community practices into lessons.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation of materials through classroom application and learner feedback.\r\n•	Recognition and incentives for teachers who excel in producing contextualized materials.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '5000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5976, ' Implement Remediation Sessions in reading, science, and mathematics for identified learners;\r\nConduct diagnostic and formative assessments to determine specific learning gaps; Establish peer tutoring and mentoring programs within classes.\r\nOrganize ', '•	Address individual learning gaps in reading comprehension, science concepts, and mathematical skills; \r\n•	Improve learners’ mastery of foundational competencies to meet grade-level standards.\r\n•	Strengthen teachers’ capacity to design and implement', '•	At least 80% of learners with identified gaps show improvement in post-assessment results.\r\n•	Teachers consistently integrate remediation strategies into lesson delivery.\r\n•	Learners demonstrate increased confidence and participation in reading, science experiments, and math problem-solving.\r\n•	A repository of remediation materials and strategies is developed and shared among teachers.', '•	Early identification of struggling learners through diagnostic tests and classroom observations.\r\n•	Small-group and one-on-one remediation sessions focusing on specific skills.\r\n•	Use of interactive and contextualized materials (local stories for reading, hands-on experiments for science, real-life math problems).\r\n•	Peer-assisted learning where advanced learners help classmates.\r\n•	Regular progress monitoring through quizzes, oral reading tests, and performance tasks.\r\n•	Collaboration with parents to reinforce remediation activities at home.\r\n•	Recognition programs for learners showing significant improvement.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '5000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5977, 'Develop and integrate lesson plans and modules embedding peace education and DepEd core values (Maka-Diyos, Maka-tao, Makakalikasan, Makabansa);  Conduct teacher training workshops on values integration and peace education strategies; Organize school', '•	Equip teachers with skills to integrate peace education and DepEd core values across subject areas.\r\n•	Foster a school culture of respect, empathy, and collaboration among learners.\r\n•	Strengthen learners’ understanding and practice of values in da', '•	At least 90% of teachers integrate peace and values topics into their lessons.\r\n•	Learners demonstrate improved behavior, respect for diversity, and conflict-resolution skills.\r\n•	A repository of contextualized lesson exemplars promoting peace and values is established.\r\n•	Increased participation in school-wide peace and values-based activities.', '•	Contextualization of lessons using local stories, cultural practices, and real-life scenarios.\r\n•	Project-based learning focusing on peace-building and community service.\r\n•	Collaborative classroom activities (role plays, debates, group projects) to practice values.\r\n•	Integration of peace themes in co-curricular activities (arts, sports, clubs).\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation through classroom observations, learner reflections, and behavior tracking.\r\n•	Recognition programs for teachers and learners who exemplify DepEd core values.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5978, 'Establishment of Digital Help Desk and Information System', 'To provide faster and accessible frontline services to stakeholders', 'Functional digital help desk, online inquiry system, and stakeholder assistance logbook', 'Use of Google Forms, Messenger, QR Codes, and information desk', 'June–July 2026', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Teachers, Non-T', '5000', 'Can be integrated with existing ICT program', 2026, 128443, 57, 12, 121),
(5979, 'Establishment of Reading Corner per Classroom', 'To provide temporary access to reading materials despite absence of functional library', 'Functional classroom reading corners with books and learning materials', 'Collection and distribution of books, improvised shelves, and reading materials', 'June–July 2026', 'Teachers, SPTA, Learners', '5000', 'Immediate intervention for learners', 2026, 128443, 57, 12, 121),
(5980, 'Conduct regular test item analysis of quarterly and summative assessments in all subject areas; Organize teacher workshops on interpreting item analysis results and applying them to instruction;  Establish a school-based assessment committee to revie', '•	Identify strengths and weaknesses in learners’ performance across subject areas.\r\n•	Improve the quality of test items to ensure validity, reliability, and alignment with curriculum standards.\r\n•	Use item analysis results to guide remediation, enric', '•	Comprehensive item analysis reports generated after each major assessment.\r\n•	Teachers adjust lesson plans and strategies based on identified learning gaps.\r\n•	Improved learner performance in subsequent assessments.\r\n•	A repository of validated test items for future use.', '•	Collect and analyze test data using item difficulty, discrimination index, and distractor efficiency.\r\n•	Conduct collaborative discussions among teachers to interpret results and plan interventions.\r\n•	Integrate findings into remediation and enrichment programs for learners.\r\n•	Use technology tools (spreadsheets, assessment software) to streamline analysis.\r\n•	Monitor progress by comparing learner performance before and after instructional adjustments.\r\n•	Recognize teachers who effectively utilize item analysis to improve learner outcomes.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head; Master Teacher', '3500.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5981, 'Conduct of Computer Donation and Resource Mobilization Drive', 'To acquire additional computers and ICT equipment', 'Increased number of functional computers and ICT devices', 'Partnership with LGU, alumni, NGOs, private partners, and stakeholders', 'July–August 2026', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, PTA, Stakeholde', '3000', 'Encourages community support', 2026, 128443, 57, 12, 121),
(5982, 'Conduct school-wide anti-bullying campaigns (seminars, posters, assemblies, classroom discussions);  Establish a Child Protection Committee (CPC) to monitor, report, and address bullying cases;  Organize values formation activities integrated into le', '•	Promote a safe, inclusive, and supportive school environment.\r\n•	Raise awareness among learners, teachers, parents, and stakeholders about the negative impacts of bullying.\r\n•	Strengthen reporting and intervention mechanisms to immediately address ', '•	Zero reported bullying cases within the school year.\r\n•	Learners demonstrate positive behavior and respect for peers.\r\n•	Teachers and staff actively implement child protection policies.\r\n•	Parents and community members participate in anti-bullying initiatives.\r\n•	A functional school-based reporting and monitoring system is in place.', '•	Information dissemination through orientations, classroom discussions, and school assemblies.\r\n•	Integration of anti-bullying themes in lesson plans and values education.\r\n•	Anonymous reporting mechanisms (drop boxes, digital reporting forms) to encourage learners to speak up.\r\n•	Counseling and mediation sessions for learners involved in conflicts.\r\n•	Recognition programs for classes or learners who exemplify respect and kindness.\r\n•	Regular monitoring and evaluation by the CPC to ensure compliance with DepEd Child Protection Policy.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head, parents, GAD Focal', '10000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5983, 'Conduct school-wide orientations on the DepEd Child Protection Policy for teachers, learners, parents, and stakeholders; Establish and strengthen the Child Protection Committee (CPC) to monitor, report, and address child protection concerns; Organize', '•	Ensure a safe and nurturing school environment free from child abuse.\r\n•	Raise awareness among all stakeholders about child protection policies and reporting mechanisms.\r\n•	Strengthen teachers’ and staff’s ability to detect, prevent, and respond to', '•	Zero reported child abuse cases within the school year.\r\n•	Learners demonstrate improved awareness of their rights and responsibilities.\r\n•	Teachers and staff actively implement child protection measures in classrooms and school activities.\r\n•	Parents and community members participate in child protection initiatives.\r\n•	A functional school-based reporting and monitoring system is established and maintained.', '•	Information dissemination through orientations, classroom discussions, and school assemblies.\r\n•	Integration of child protection themes in lesson plans, values education, and co-curricular activities.\r\n•	Anonymous reporting mechanisms (drop boxes, digital reporting forms) to encourage learners to speak up.\r\n•	Counseling and mediation sessions facilitated by the CPC and guidance counselors.\r\n•	Partnerships with LGUs, NGOs, and child protection agencies to strengthen support systems.\r\n•	Regular monitoring and evaluation by the CPC to ensure compliance with DepEd Child Protection Policy.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head, parents', '5000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5984, 'Conduct early identification and profiling of learners at risk of dropping out.\r\nImplement remediation and enrichment programs to address academic difficulties;  \r\nOrganize counseling and mentoring sessions for learners with behavioral, emotional, or', '•	Reduce the number of learners dropping out by addressing academic, behavioral, and socio-economic factors. \r\n•	Provide targeted interventions to learners at risk of leaving school.\r\n•	Strengthen collaboration among teachers, parents, and community ', '•	Reduced drop-out rate compared to the previous school year.\r\n•	Learners at risk of dropping out receive timely interventions and support.\r\n•	Increased parental and community involvement in learner retention programs.\r\n•	Improved learner attendance and academic performance.', '•	Learner profiling and monitoring using attendance records, academic performance, and socio-economic background.\r\n•	Remediation classes and peer tutoring for struggling learners\r\n•	Counseling sessions facilitated by guidance counselors and trained teachers.\r\n•	Home visitation programs to strengthen school-family partnerships.\r\n•	Scholarship and feeding programs in collaboration with LGUs, NGOs, and private stakeholders.\r\n•	Recognition and incentive programs for learners with improved attendance and performance.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '5000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5985, 'Organize school-wide cultural celebrations (e.g., Buwan ng Wika, Indigenous Peoples’ Month, local heritage festivals); Develop lesson plans and instructional materials that integrate local traditions, languages, and practices.); Conduct teacher train', '•	Promote respect, appreciation, and pride in learners’ cultural identity and heritage.\r\n•	Ensure teaching and learning processes are inclusive and responsive to diverse cultural backgrounds.\r\n•	Strengthen collaboration between the school and communi', '•	At least 90% of teachers integrate culture-sensitive content into lessons\r\n•	Learners actively participate in cultural activities and demonstrate appreciation for diversity.\r\n•	A repository of contextualized cultural learning materials is developed and maintained.\r\n•	Increased community involvement in school cultural programs.', '•	Collaborative activities (storytelling, traditional games, arts workshops) involving learners and community members.\r\n•	Contextualization of lessons using local stories, folklore, and indigenous knowledge.\r\n•	Project-based learning focusing on cultural preservation and creative expression.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation through learner reflections, teacher reports, and community feedback.\r\n•	Partnerships with LGUs, NGOs, and cultural organizations to support cultural initiatives.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '5000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5986, 'Establish and strengthen the Child Protection Committee (CPC) with clear roles and responsibilities; Conduct orientation sessions for teachers, learners, parents, and stakeholders on child protection policies; Implement reporting and monitoring mecha', '•	Ensure a safe and nurturing school environment free from abuse, neglect, and bullying.\r\n•	Raise awareness among all stakeholders about child protection policies and reporting procedures.\r\n•	Strengthen CPC’s capacity to respond effectively to child ', '•	A functional CPC actively monitoring and addressing child protection issues.\r\n•	Zero reported child abuse cases within the school year.\r\n•	Learners demonstrate improved awareness of their rights and responsibilities.\r\n•	Teachers and staff consistently apply child protection measures in classrooms and activities.\r\n•	Parents and community members participate in child protection initiatives.', '•	Information dissemination through orientations, assemblies, and classroom discussions.\r\n•	Integration of child protection themes in lesson plans, values education, and co-curricular activities.\r\n•	Anonymous reporting mechanisms to encourage learners to speak up safely.\r\n•	Counseling and mediation sessions facilitated by CPC members and guidance counselors.\r\n•	Partnerships with LGUs, NGOs, and child protection agencies to strengthen support systems.\r\n•	Regular monitoring and evaluation by the CPC to ensure compliance with DepEd Child Protection Policy.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '5000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5987, 'Develop SPED- and PWD-Friendly Facilities', 'Provide inclusive and accessible learning environment', 'Installation of ramps, accessible CRs, assistive devices', 'Facility assessment, coordinate with LGU, seek funding support', 'Whole Year', 'School Head, LGU, PTA and Stakeholders', '50000', '', 2026, 128425, 57, 12, 121),
(5988, 'Develop and implement a School Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Plan aligned with DepEd and LGU guidelines;  Conduct risk assessment and hazard mapping within the school and community;  Organize disaster preparedness drills (earthquake, fire, t', '•	Ensure the safety and preparedness of learners, teachers, and staff during disasters.\r\n•	Strengthen the school’s capacity to respond effectively to emergencies.\r\n•	Promote awareness and active participation of the school community in disaster risk ', '•	A functional DRRM Plan documented and implemented in the school.\r\n•	Learners and staff demonstrate knowledge of safety protocols during drills.\r\n•	Reduced risks and vulnerabilities within the school environment.\r\n•	Active collaboration with community stakeholders in disaster preparedness and response.', '•	Hazard and risk assessment through surveys, mapping, and consultations.\r\n•	Simulation drills to practice evacuation and emergency response.\r\n•	Integration of DRRM topics in classroom lessons and co-curricular activities.\r\n•	Collaboration with LGUs, BFP, PNP, and NGOs for technical assistance and resources.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation of DRRM implementation by the School DRRM Committee.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '3000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5989, 'Establish a School Mental Wellness Committee composed of teachers, guidance counselors, and health partners; Conduct mental health awareness campaigns (seminars, posters, classroom discussions); Organize regular counseling and peer support sessions f', '•	Promote mental wellness among learners, teachers, and staff.\r\n•	Provide accessible support mechanisms for those experiencing stress, anxiety, or emotional challenges.\r\n•	Strengthen teachers’ and staff’s capacity to identify and respond to mental he', '•	A functional school-based mental wellness program recognized by stakeholders.\r\n•	Learners and staff demonstrate improved coping skills and emotional resilience.\r\n•	Increased participation in mental wellness activities.\r\n•	Reduced cases of absenteeism, behavioral issues, and stress-related concerns.', '•	Information dissemination through orientations, posters, and classroom integration of mental wellness topics.\r\n•	Peer mentoring and support groups to encourage openness and empathy.\r\n•	Counseling services provided by trained teachers or guidance counselors, with referrals to professionals when needed.\r\n•	Integration of wellness activities into co-curricular programs (sports, arts, clubs).\r\n•	Community partnerships with health agencies and NGOs for technical assistance and resources.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation of learners’ and staff’s mental wellness through surveys, feedback, and case tracking.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '10000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5990, 'Conduct a school accessibility audit to identify gaps in facilities for learners with disabilities; Construct or improve PWD-friendly infrastructure (ramps, handrails, accessible toilets, signage, pathways); Provide special education classrooms equip', '•	Ensure equitable access to education for learners with disabilities and special needs.\r\n•	Create a safe, inclusive, and supportive learning environment.\r\n•	Strengthen teachers’ capacity to deliver instruction tailored to diverse learner needs. \r\n•	', '•	A functional set of PWD-friendly facilities (ramps, toilets, signage, classrooms).\r\n•	Increased enrollment and participation of learners with disabilities in school programs.\r\n•	Teachers demonstrate improved practices in inclusive education.\r\n•	Stronger collaboration with stakeholders to sustain special education initiatives.', 'Accessibility audit and planning with input from teachers, parents, and learners.\r\n•	Infrastructure development guided by national accessibility standards.\r\n•	Provision of assistive devices (Braille materials, hearing aids, ICT tools) for learners with special needs.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation of facility use and learner outcomes.\r\n•	Capacity-building workshops for teachers on inclusive pedagogy and classroom management.\r\n•	Community partnerships to mobilize resources and technical expertise.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '20000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5991, 'Conduct a School Strategic Planning Workshop involving teachers, parents, learners, and community stakeholders; Perform a situational analysis (SWOT: strengths, weaknesses, opportunities, threats) to identify priorities; Draft and refine the School I', '•	Develop a comprehensive and evidence-based strategic plan that guides school improvement initiatives.\r\n•	Align school goals with DepEd priorities and community needs.\r\n•	Ensure stakeholder participation and ownership in the planning process.\r\n•	Pro', '•	A documented School Improvement Plan with clear vision, mission, goals, and strategies.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder awareness and participation in school improvement.\r\n•	Improved alignment of school programs with learner needs and community priorities.\r\n•	A functional monitoring and evaluation system for tracking progress.', '•	Participatory planning workshops to ensure inclusivity and collaboration.\r\n•	Use of data-driven analysis (test results, attendance, drop-out rates, community surveys) to inform priorities.\r\n•	Goal-setting and action planning with measurable indicators and timelines.\r\n•	Resource mapping to identify available and potential support from LGUs, NGOs, and private partners.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation through quarterly reviews and stakeholder feedback.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head, School Planning Team', '12000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5992, 'Establish/Upgrade Computer Laboratory', 'Provide ICT-based learning environment', 'Functional computer lab/classroom', 'Procure computers, install internet, ICT training', '1 Year', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, LGU and stakeho', '100000', '', 2026, 128425, 57, 12, 121),
(5993, 'Establish and formalize the School-Community Planning Team (SCPT) with ; epresentatives from teachers, parents, learners, LGUs, NGOs, and community stakeholders; Conduct orientation and capacity-building sessions for SCPT members on participatory pla', '•	Ensure participatory and collaborative planning between the school and community stakeholders.\r\n•	Strengthen community ownership of school programs and projects.\r\n•	Align school improvement initiatives with local needs, resources, and cultural cont', '•	A functional SCPT actively engaged in school planning and decision-making.\r\n•	Documented School Improvement Plan (SIP) and other plans developed with SCPT participation.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder involvement in school programs and projects.\r\n•	Improved resource mobilization and sustainability of school initiatives.', '•	Participatory planning workshops using tools such as SWOT analysis, resource mapping, and needs assessment.\r\n•	Inclusive representation ensuring voices of parents, learners, and marginalized groups are heard.\r\n•	Regular meetings and consultations to monitor progress and adjust plans as needed.\r\n•	Transparent communication through assemblies, newsletters, and digital platforms.\r\n•	Partnership-building with LGUs, NGOs, and private stakeholders for technical and financial support.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation of SCPT activities to ensure effectiveness and accountability.\r\n•	Recognition programs for active SCPT members and stakeholders who contribute significantly to school development.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '5000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5994, 'Conduct school-wide elections to establish the SELG with democratic processes; Provide leadership training and orientation for elected SELG officers; Organize student-led activities and projects promoting leadership, responsibility, and school partic', '•	Develop learners’ leadership skills, responsibility, and active citizenship.\r\n•	Ensure student representation in school decision-making and activities.\r\n•	Promote SELG-led initiatives that enhance school culture and learner participation.\r\n•	Streng', '•	A functional SELG organization with elected officers and documented activities.\r\n•	Increased learner participation in school governance and projects.\r\n•	SELG-led initiatives that promote discipline, cooperation, and school pride.\r\n•	Improved communication between learners and school administration.', '•	Democratic election process supervised by teachers to ensure fairness and inclusivity.\r\n•	Capacity-building workshops on leadership, communication, and project management for SELG officers.\r\n•	Integration of SELG activities into the School Improvement Plan (SIP).\r\n•	Mentoring and guidance from teachers and administrators to support SELG projects.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation of SELG performance through reports, reflections, and stakeholder feedback.\r\n•	Recognition programs (e.g., “Outstanding SELG Leaders Award”) to motivate learners.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5995, 'Establish a School Frontline Services Desk (physical and digital) to address stakeholder concerns promptly; Develop innovative communication channels (chat groups, SMS alerts, school website, social media updates); Implement digital record-keeping an', '•	Provide efficient, transparent, and responsive frontline services to learners, parents, and community stakeholders.\r\n•	Innovate service delivery through technology and streamlined processes.\r\n•	Strengthen stakeholder trust and satisfaction with sch', '•	A functional frontline services desk/system accessible to all stakeholders.\r\n•	Reduced processing time for requests, permits, and certificates.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder satisfaction and positive feedback.\r\n•	Documented innovations in service delivery recognized by DepEd and community partners.', '•	Process mapping and streamlining to eliminate delays and redundancies in service delivery.\r\n•	Digital platforms (school website, social media, SMS alerts) to provide timely updates and information.\r\n•	Capacity-building workshops for staff on customer service, communication, and digital tools.\r\n•	Stakeholder engagement through surveys, consultations, and feedback sessions.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation of service performance using key indicators (response time, satisfaction ratings).', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head, AO, AdSup-COS', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109);
INSERT INTO `sgod_action_plan` (`id`, `activity`, `objective`, `ex_output`, `metho_strategy`, `time_frame`, `person_involved`, `bud_req`, `remarks`, `fy`, `school_id`, `division`, `region`, `district`) VALUES
(5996, 'S.A.F.E. Grounds\r\n(Securing and Advancing Functional and Even Grounds for Learners)', '1. To provide a safer, accessible, and learner-friendly school environment through ground leveling activities\r\n2. To seek support and resources from stakeholders and partners', '1. Identified areas needing improvement\r\n2. Stakeholder support and assistance secured\r\n3. Safer and leveled school ground', '1. Conduct ocular inspection and assessment of affected areas\r\n2. Coordinate with LGU, PTA, and stakeholders for assistance and materials\r\n', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, Teachers, DRRM Coordinator, PTA ', '', 'Implementation is subject to availability of funds, materials, and support from stakeholders and partner agencies. Continuous monitoring and maintenance shall be observed to ensure sustainability of the improved school ground.', 2026, 128556, 57, 12, 108),
(5997, 'Formulate an Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) based on the approved Strategic Plan; Conduct planning workshops with teachers, parents, learners, and stakeholders to translate strategic goals into actionable programs; Assign roles and responsibilities', '•	Ensure the school’s strategic plan is translated into concrete, actionable steps.\r\n•	Align implementation activities with DepEd priorities and community needs.\r\n•	Promote accountability and ownership among teachers, learners, and stakeholders.\r\n•	P', '•	An Annual Implementation Plan aligned with the school’s strategic plan.\r\n•	Clear assignment of responsibilities and timelines for each activity.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder participation in school programs and projects.\r\n•	Improved efficiency and effectiveness in achieving school improvement goals.', '•	Participatory planning workshops to ensure inclusivity and collaboration.\r\n•	Data-driven prioritization using school performance indicators, learner needs, and community feedback.\r\n•	Action planning with SMART objectives (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound).\r\n•	Resource mapping to identify available and potential support from LGUs, NGOs, and private partners.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation system with quarterly reviews, reports, and stakeholder consultations.\r\n•	Recognition and celebration of milestones to sustain motivation and commitment.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head, School Planning Team', '3500.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5998, 'Reorganization and strengthening of School Governance Council (SGC); Strengthening and functionality assessment of the School Governance Council (SGC)', '•	Strengthen participatory leadership\r\n•	Ensure shared decision-making\r\n•	Institutionalize shared leadership\r\n•	Improve quality of school decisions', '•	Approved Constitution and By-Laws\r\n•	Functional SGC with clear roles\r\n•	Updated SGC work  and action plan', '•	Stakeholder orientation\r\n•	Democratic election of Officers\r\n•	SGC self-assessment\r\n•	Reorientation on roles and responsibilities\r\n•	Regular governance meetings', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(5999, ' L.E.A.D. (Leadership Enhancement and Development)', '1. To develop leadership skills of SELG officers\r\n2. To ensure active participation in school programs and activities\r\n3. To organize and re-establish SELG officers', '1. Trained and functional SELG officers\r\n2. Active and functional SELG organization\r\n3. Sustained and functional SELG operations', '1. Conduct consultation meeting to identify concerns and issues affecting SELG\r\n2. Conduct election/selection of SELG officers\r\n3. Regular meetings and involvement in school activities\r\n4. Conduct periodic assessment of SELG activities', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, SELG Adviser, Class Advisers, St', '', 'Implementation is subject to the election/selection of SELG officers, availability of funds, and support from school administration and stakeholders.', 2026, 128556, 57, 12, 108),
(6000, 'Establish and formalize the Parent-Teacher Association (PTA) through elections and orientation of officers; Conduct capacity-building sessions for PTA officers on leadership, governance, and resource mobilization; Facilitate regular PTA meetings to d', '•	Strengthen collaboration between parents and teachers in promoting learner welfare and school improvement.\r\n•	Ensure active parental involvement in school governance and decision-making.\r\n•	Mobilize resources and support for school programs and pro', '•	A functional PTA with elected officers, documented meetings, and implemented projects.\r\n•	Increased parental participation in school activities and decision-making.\r\n•	Improved learner welfare through PTA-led initiatives.\r\n•	Enhanced resource mobilization and sustainability of school programs.', '•	Democratic election process for PTA officers to ensure inclusivity and transparency.\r\n•	Capacity-building workshops to equip PTA leaders with skills in governance and project management.\r\n•	Regular meetings and consultations scheduled quarterly or as needed.\r\n•	Transparent communication channels (assemblies, newsletters, digital platforms) to share updates and decisions.\r\n•	Partnership-building with LGUs, NGOs, and private stakeholders for technical and financial support.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation of PTA activities to ensure effectiveness and accountability.\r\n•	Recognition programs for active PTA members and parents who contribute significantly to school development.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6001, 'Improvement of PWD-Friendly Facilities and Pathways', 'To improve accessibility and ensure an inclusive and safe school environment for PWD learners and visitors', '1. Functional and accessible PWD facilities\r\n2. Increased awareness and inclusive culture.', '1. Conduct assessment of existing school facilities for PWD accessibility gaps\r\n2. Coordination with LGU and stakeholders for technical assistance and support\r\n3. Installation/repair of ramps, handrails, and accessible pathways', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, DRRM Coordinator, PTA Officers, ', '', 'Implementation is subject to availability of funds, technical assistance from LGU, and stakeholder support for infrastructure improvements.', 2026, 128557, 57, 12, 108),
(6002, 'Strengthening Stakeholders Participation', 'Organize regular meetings with parents, community leaders, and local government units\r\nFoster collaboration and shared responsibility in school governance', ' Increased stakeholder involvement in school projects and policy-making', 'Quarterly assemblies, focus group discussions, and surveys', 'Quarterly throughout the academic year', 'School head, PTA & SGC officers, barangay off', '1000', 'Document agreements and track implementation progress', 2026, 128479, 57, 12, 119),
(6003, 'Establish a School Partnership Committee to coordinate collaborations with stakeholders and other schools; Organize joint projects and activities (e.g., inter-school competitions, shared training workshops, community service programs); Develop Memora', '•	Strengthen collaboration between the school, stakeholders, and other schools to enhance educational programs.\r\n•	Mobilize resources and expertise from partners to support school improvement initiatives.\r\n•	Promote shared responsibility and communit', '•	A functional partnership system with documented agreements and active collaborations.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder participation in school programs and projects.\r\n•	Joint initiatives with other schools that enhance learner outcomes and teacher capacity.\r\n•	Improved resource mobilization and sustainability of school projects.', '•	Stakeholder mapping and engagement through meetings, surveys, and consultations.\r\n•	Formalization of partnerships via MOAs, contracts, or resolutions.\r\n•	Collaborative planning workshops with partners to align goals and resources.\r\n•	Joint implementation of projects such as training, competitions, environmental campaigns, and outreach programs.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation of partnership activities through reports, feedback, and performance indicators.\r\n•	Recognition programs for stakeholders and partner schools who contribute significantly to school development.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6004, 'Reading numeracy and literacy for grade 3 learners', 'To improve reading fluency, comprehension, and vocabulary development.', 'Learners can recognize letters, sounds, words, and sentences correctly.', 'Provide varied activities based on learners’ abilities and needs.', 'Year round', 'School Head, Teachers, reading tutor', '1500.00', 'Propose 3 minutes reading before classes start.', 2026, 204014, 57, 12, 111),
(6005, 'Conduct annual stakeholder satisfaction surveys (parents, learners, teachers, LGUs, NGOs, alumni); Establish a feedback and grievance mechanism (suggestion boxes, online forms, consultation meetings); Organize school-community assemblies to present a', '•	Measure and sustain stakeholder satisfaction with school services and programs.\r\n•	Strengthen transparency, accountability, and responsiveness in school governance.\r\n•	Foster trust and collaboration between the school and its stakeholders.\r\n•	Use f', '•	Documented satisfaction survey results showing at least a “satisfactory” average rating.\r\n•	Functional feedback mechanisms actively used by stakeholders.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder participation in school programs and decision-making.\r\n•	Continuous improvement initiatives implemented based on feedback.\r\n•	Recognition programs that motivate staff and stakeholders to maintain high-quality service.', '•	Survey administration using standardized tools (Likert scale questionnaires, online forms).\r\n•	Data analysis and reporting of satisfaction ratings to identify strengths and areas for improvement.\r\n•	Consultative meetings with stakeholders to validate findings and co-create solutions.\r\n•	Integration of feedback into the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and annual action plans.\r\n•	Transparent communication of survey results and improvement measures through assemblies, newsletters, and digital platforms.\r\n•	Recognition and incentive programs for teachers, staff, and stakeholders who contribute to high satisfaction ratings.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation to ensure sustained stakeholder trust and satisfaction.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '8000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6006, 'Conduct orientation sessions on IPCR standards, performance indicators, and evaluation tools; Implement professional development programs (training, seminars, mentoring) aligned with identified competency gaps; Establish peer coaching and collaborati', '•	Ensure all school personnel understand IPCR standards and expectations.\r\n•	Strengthen teacher and staff competencies to achieve “Very Satisfactory” ratings.\r\n•	Promote a culture of continuous improvement and accountability in performance.\r\n•	Enhanc', '•	At least 90% of school personnel achieve a “Very Satisfactory” rating in IPCR.\r\n•	Improved teaching and non-teaching performance aligned with DepEd standards.\r\n•	Documented professional development activities and feedback reports.\r\n•	Increased motivation and commitment among personnel to sustain high performance.', '•	Capacity-building workshops on instructional strategies, classroom management, and administrative efficiency.\r\n•	Performance monitoring through classroom observations, portfolio reviews, and self-assessments.\r\n•	Peer mentoring and coaching to share best practices and provide support.\r\n•	Feedback and evaluation sessions conducted quarterly to track progress.\r\n•	Integration of performance targets into the School Improvement Plan (SIP).\r\n•	Recognition programs via School PRAISE to motivate personnel.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation by the School Head and IPCR Committee to ensure accountability.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '45000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6007, 'Conduct orientation sessions for school heads and office personnel on OPCR standards, indicators, and evaluation tools; Develop and implement annual office performance targets aligned with DepEd priorities and the School Improvement Plan (SIP); Provi', '•	Ensure school offices understand OPCR standards and expectations.\r\n•	Strengthen administrative and management competencies to achieve “Very Satisfactory” ratings.\r\n•	Promote accountability, transparency, and continuous improvement in office perform', '•	At least 90% of office performance indicators achieve a “Very Satisfactory” rating in OPCR.\r\n•	Improved efficiency and effectiveness in school governance and administrative functions.\r\n•	Documented office performance reports and feedback mechanisms.\r\n•	Increased motivation and commitment among personnel to sustain high performance.', '•	Capacity-building workshops on office management, leadership, and performance evaluation.\r\n•	Performance monitoring through quarterly reviews, reports, and self-assessments.\r\n•	Collaborative planning sessions to align office targets with SIP and DepEd priorities.\r\n•	Feedback and evaluation sessions conducted quarterly to track progress and address gaps.\r\n•	Integration of performance targets into the school’s strategic and implementation plans.\r\n•	Recognition programs (via School PRAISE) to motivate personnel.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation by the School Head and OPCR Committee to ensure accountability.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6008, 'Establishing a school Resource Management System', 'Ensure efficient allocation and utilization of school resources\r\nPromote accountability and transparency in resource handling\r\nSustain resources for long-term school development', 'Clear inventory of school assets and resources\r\n\r\nImproved budgeting and resource allocation aligned with school priorities\r\n\r\nAnnual resource management report shared with stakeholders', 'Form a Resource Management Committee (school head, teachers, PTA, student leaders)\r\n\r\nConduct resource mapping (financial, material, human resources)\r\n\r\nImplement tracking tools (inventory logs, budget monitoring sheets)\r\n\r\nHold quarterly resource review meetings with stakeholders\r\n\r\n', 'Committee formation: June  Resource mapping: ', 'School head, Resource Management Committee, P', '1000', 'Transparency ensured through public posting of reports and stakeholder consultations', 2026, 128479, 57, 12, 119),
(6009, 'Conduct a needs assessment survey among teachers and staff to identify priority areas for professional development; Establish Learning Action Cells (LACs) focused on specific themes (e.g., reading remediation, contextualized materials, inclusive educ', '•	Strengthen teachers’ and staff’s competencies through collaborative and needs-based professional development.\r\n•	Promote a culture of continuous learning and reflective practice.\r\n•	Ensure LACs and L&D activities directly address learner needs and ', '•	Functional LAC sessions conducted regularly with documented minutes and outputs.\r\n•	At least 90% of teachers and staff participate in LACs and L&D activities.\r\n•	Improved teaching practices and learner outcomes based on identified needs.\r\n•	Compilation of best practices and innovations for replication and sharing.\r\n•	Strengthened collaboration with external partners for professional development.', '•	Needs assessment tools (surveys, interviews, performance data) to identify priority areas.\r\n•	Collaborative learning sessions facilitated by master teachers, subject coordinators, or external experts.\r\n•	Peer mentoring and coaching to support teachers in applying new strategies.\r\n•	Integration of LAC outputs into lesson planning, SIP, and classroom practices.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation of LAC and L&D effectiveness through feedback forms, classroom observations, and learner performance data.\r\n•	Recognition programs for teachers and staff who actively contribute to professional learning communities.', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '10000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6010, 'Exercises on sentence structure, verbs, punctuation, and subject-verb agreement.', 'Improve the academic performance of Grade 6 learners in all learning areas covered in the National Achievement Test (NAT).', 'Improved reading comprehension, numeracy, problem-solving, and critical-thinking skills among learners.', 'Focus instruction on Most Essential Learning Competencies (MELCs) and NAT-aligned skills.', 'Once a year', 'SH,Teachers.Parents/Stakeholders and Learners', '3000.00', 'The program becomes successful  with active participation from teachers, learners, parents, and stakeholders.', 2026, 204014, 57, 12, 111),
(6011, 'Conduct a Training Needs Assessment (TNA) to identify areas for professional growth among teachers and staff; Organize Learning & Development (L&D) programs such as seminars, workshops, benchmarking, and in-service training; Establish mentoring and c', '•	Promote continuous professional growth and career advancement of school personnel.\r\n•	Strengthen competencies in teaching, leadership, and school management.\r\n•	Align professional development activities with learner needs and school improvement pri', '•	Documented professional development plan aligned with school priorities.\r\n•	At least 90% of personnel participate in L&D activities annually.\r\n•	Improved teaching practices, leadership skills, and learner outcomes.\r\n•	Compilation of best practices and innovations for replication and sharing.\r\n•	Increased number of personnel availing scholarships, training, and advanced studies.', '•	Needs assessment tools (surveys, performance reviews, classroom observations) to identify training priorities.\r\n•	Capacity-building workshops and seminars facilitated by experts and partner institutions.\r\n•	Peer mentoring and coaching to support application of new strategies in classrooms and offices.\r\n•	Integration of professional development outputs into lesson planning, SIP, and school governance.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation of L&D effectiveness through feedback, performance ratings, and learner achievement data.\r\n•	Recognition programs for personnel who excel in professional development initiatives.', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6012, ' Establish a continuous monitoring and evaluation framework for SBM implementation', 'Track progress of SBM activities in real time\r\n\r\nIdentify strengths, gaps, and areas for improvement\r\n\r\nEnsure accountability and transparency in school governance', 'Quarterly progress reports on SBM indicators\r\n\r\nActionable recommendations for improvement shared with stakeholders\r\n\r\nEvidence-based decision-making in school planning', 'Form a Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) Committee composed of teachers, PTA, student leaders, and barangay representatives\r\n\r\nUse digital tools (Google Forms, spreadsheets) for data collection and reporting\r\n\r\nConduct classroom observations, stakeholder surveys, and performance scorecards\r\n\r\nHold quarterly reflection workshops to discuss findings and adjust plans', 'Committee formation: June  Monthly monitoring', ' School head, M&E Committee, teachers, PTA of', '1000', 'Findings will be publicly shared through bulletin boards, assemblies, and school website for transparency', 2026, 128479, 57, 12, 119),
(6013, 'Establish a Recognition and Rewards Committee to design and oversee programs; Conduct annual recognition ceremonies (e.g., Teachers’ Day, Service Excellence Awards, Retirement Honors); Provide certificates, plaques, or tokens of appreciation for mile', '•	Motivate personnel by acknowledging their contributions and achievements.\r\n•	Foster a culture of appreciation, excellence, and continuous improvement.\r\n•	Strengthen morale and commitment among teachers and staff.\r\n•	Promote stakeholder awareness of', '•	A functional recognition program implemented annually.\r\n•	Increased motivation and job satisfaction among personnel.\r\n•	Documented recognition activities with photos, certificates, and reports.\r\n•	Stronger stakeholder support and appreciation for school personnel.', '•	Participatory planning with input from teachers, staff, and stakeholders to design recognition programs.\r\n•	Transparent criteria for awards (e.g., years of service, performance ratings, innovations, leadership).\r\n•	Formal ceremonies and informal acknowledgments to celebrate achievements.\r\n•	Public communication of achievements through newsletters, assemblies, and digital platforms.\r\n•	Partnership-building with stakeholders to provide resources and sponsorships.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation of recognition programs to ensure fairness and sustainability.', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '5000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6014, 'Conduct a workload assessment and inventory of teaching assignments, ancillary tasks, and special duties; Develop a Workload Distribution Matrix to ensure equitable assignment of teaching loads, advisory classes, and committee work; Hold consultative', '•	Ensure equitable distribution of teaching and non-teaching responsibilities among teachers.\r\n•	 Prevent teacher burnout and promote work-life balance.\r\n•	Strengthen transparency and accountability in workload assignment.\r\n•	Enhance teacher morale, ', '•	 A documented workload distribution plan approved by the School Head and teachers.\r\n•	At least 90% of teachers reporting satisfaction with workload distribution.\r\n•	Reduced cases of teacher overload and improved efficiency in task completion.\r\n•	Increased teacher morale and commitment to school programs.', '•	Data collection on teaching loads, advisory classes, and ancillary assignments.\r\n•	Consultative planning workshops with teachers to co-create workload distribution guidelines.\r\n•	Rotation and sharing system for ancillary tasks and committee work.\r\n•	Transparent communication of workload assignments through memos and meetings.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation of workload distribution through surveys, feedback sessions, and performance reviews.', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '2000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6015, 'Intensified Implementation of \"Catch-up Fridays\" Reading and Numeracy Intervention Program (Project R.E.A.D. - Reading Enhancement and Academic Development)', 'To increase the reading comprehension and basic numeracy proficiency levels of struggling learners in Key Stages 1 and 2 by at least 75% by the end of the school year, and to cultivate a genuine love for reading among pupils.', 'Improved learner reading profiles based on Pre and Post Phil-IRI results.\r\n\r\nEnhanced numeracy skills reflected in periodic assessments.\r\n\r\nProduction and utilization of contextualized reading and math intervention materials.\r\n\r\nDocumented attendance and progress reports of learners undergoing remediation.', 'Conduct pre-assessments (Phil-IRI and Numeracy tests) to identify baseline data.\r\n\r\nGroup learners according to their specific reading and numeracy levels.\r\n\r\nUtilize contextualized and localized learning activity sheets during dedicated Catch-Up Friday sessions.\r\n\r\nConduct monthly LAC (Learning Action Cell) sessions among teachers to track progress and share best practices.\r\n\r\nAdminister post-assessments to measure program impact.', 'June 2026 to March2027 (Every Friday of the S', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Class Advisers,', '6000.00', 'Requires continuous monitoring and evaluation by the School Head. Strong partnership with the General PTA is highly encouraged to ensure parents monitor and support the regular attendance of learners involved in the intervention program.', 2026, 129120, 60, 12, 0),
(6016, 'Develop learning materials that are relevant to learners’ local culture, experiences, environment, and community.', 'To develop learning materials that are relevant to learners’ local culture, experiences, environment, and community.', 'Developed and utilized contextualized learning materials aligned with the curriculum and MELCs.', 'Identify learners’ needs, interests, cultural background, and learning difficulties through observation, interviews, and assessment results.', 'Year round', 'SH,Teachers. and Learners', '4000.00', 'the use of contextualized materials contributed to improved learner comprehension, retention, and academic performance.', 2026, 204014, 57, 12, 111),
(6018, 'Conduct regular inspections of classrooms, offices, laboratories, playgrounds, water systems, and sanitation facilities; Develop an inspection checklist aligned with DepEd standards and safety regulations; Schedule quarterly maintenance reviews with ', '•	Ensure all school infrastructure and facilities are safe, functional, and conducive to learning.\r\n•	Identify and address maintenance needs promptly to prevent hazards and deterioration.\r\n•	Promote accountability and transparency in facility managem', '•	A documented inspection report with identified issues and recommended actions.\r\n•	Improved safety, cleanliness, and functionality of school facilities.\r\n•	Reduced cases of facility-related hazards or disruptions.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder participation in infrastructure maintenance and improvement.', '•	Inspection checklist and tools to standardize facility reviews.\r\n•	Participatory inspections involving teachers, PTA members, learners, and stakeholders.\r\n•	Documentation and reporting of findings through photos, logs, and written reports.\r\n•	Prioritization of repairs based on urgency, safety, and resource availability.\r\n•	Resource mobilization through partnerships with LGUs, NGOs, alumni, and private donors.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation of maintenance activities to ensure sustainability.\r\n•	Recognition of stakeholders who contribute significantly to facility improvement.', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '1000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6019, 'Conduct needs assessment and facility audit to identify priority areas for improvement (classrooms, laboratories, sanitation, playgrounds, water systems); mplement repair, renovation, and upgrading projects based on identified needs; Mobilize resourc', '•	Ensure school facilities are safe, functional, and conducive to quality learning.\r\n•	Address infrastructure gaps through systematic planning and resource mobilization.\r\n•	Strengthen collaboration with stakeholders in maintaining and upgrading facil', '•	A documented infrastructure improvement plan with clear priorities and timelines.\r\n•	Upgraded and well-maintained classrooms, sanitation facilities, and learning spaces.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder participation in infrastructure projects.\r\n•	Improved learner and teacher satisfaction with school facilities.\r\n•	Recognition of the school as a model for proactive facility improvement.', '•	Facility audit and needs assessment using checklists and stakeholder consultations.\r\n•	Participatory planning workshops to align infrastructure priorities with SIP goals.\r\n•	Resource mapping and mobilization through partnerships with LGUs, NGOs, alumni, and private donors.\r\n•	Community involvement programs (e.g., Brigada Eskwela, volunteer workdays) to foster ownership.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation of infrastructure projects through reports, photos, and stakeholder feedback.\r\n•	Recognition and appreciation for partners and volunteers who contribute to facility improvement.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '100000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6020, 'Conduct a library needs assessment to identify gaps in resources, facilities, and services; Establish or upgrade the school library facility with adequate space, furniture, and ICT support; Acquire books, reference materials, digital resources, and m', '•	Provide learners and teachers with access to quality learning and reference materials.\r\n•	Promote a culture of reading, research, and lifelong learning.\r\n•	Ensure the library is functional, accessible, and aligned with school improvement priorities', '•	A functional school library with updated resources, facilities, and management systems.\r\n•	Increased learner and teacher utilization of library services.\r\n•	Documented library programs and activities supporting literacy and research.\r\n•	Improved learner performance and engagement through access to diverse learning materials.\r\n•	Strengthened partnerships with stakeholders for resource mobilization.', '•	Needs assessment and resource mapping to identify priorities and available support.\r\n•	Resource mobilization through partnerships with LGUs, NGOs, alumni, and private donors for books and ICT tools.\r\n•	Capacity-building workshops for library staff on management and digital literacy.\r\n•	Integration of library use into classroom instruction and school activities.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation of library utilization through logs, surveys, and feedback.\r\n•	Recognition of learners, teachers, and stakeholders who actively support library development.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '40000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6021, 'Hold meetings on the importance of education and regular attendance\r\nStrengthen parent-school partnership.', 'To strengthen collaboration among teachers, parents, and stakeholders in supporting learners’ academic and personal needs.', 'Increased learner retention and completion rates.', 'Identify at-risk learners through attendance monitoring, academic performance tracking, and behavior observation.', 'Year round', 'SH,Teachers.Parents/Stakeholders and Learners', '2000.00', 'Continuous monitoring and collaboration among teachers, parents, and stakeholders are essential to sustain learner retention.', 2026, 204014, 57, 12, 111),
(6022, 'Conduct a facility audit of water supply, electrical systems, and internet connectivity; Establish a maintenance and monitoring committee to oversee utilities; Coordinate with LGUs, utility providers, and private partners for technical support and up', '•	Ensure reliable and safe access to water, electricity, and internet facilities for learners and personnel.\r\n•	Prevent service interruptions that may affect teaching, learning, and school operations.\r\n•	Strengthen collaboration with stakeholders for', '•	A functional water system with safe drinking water and sanitation facilities.\r\n•	Reliable electricity supply with minimal interruptions.\r\n•	Stable internet connectivity supporting digital learning and administrative tasks.\r\n•	Documented inspection and maintenance reports.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder satisfaction with school facilities.', '•	Needs assessment and facility audit using checklists and technical inspections.\r\n•	Preventive maintenance schedules for water, electrical, and ICT systems.\r\n•	Partnership-building with LGUs, utility companies, NGOs, and alumni for technical and financial support.\r\n•	Installation of backup systems (generators, water tanks, internet boosters) to ensure continuity.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation through quarterly reports, feedback surveys, and stakeholder consultations.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '60000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6023, 'Orientation on SBM Implementation', 'To familiarize stakeholders with SBM principles, processes, and roles', 'Increased awareness and understanding of SBM', 'Conduct seminars, meetings, and workshops', 'June 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA, Stakeholders', '2000.00', 'Use DepEd SBM materials', 2026, 128532, 57, 12, 108),
(6024, 'Conduct a needs assessment to determine ICT requirements (computers, peripherals, software, internet connectivity); Establish or upgrade the computer laboratory/classroom with sufficient units, furniture, and ventilation; Acquire and maintain compute', '•	Provide learners and teachers with access to functional ICT facilities for teaching and learning.\r\n•	Promote digital literacy and 21st-century skills among learners.\r\n•	Ensure the computer laboratory supports curriculum integration and innovative t', '•	A functional computer laboratory/classroom with updated equipment and reliable internet access.\r\n•	Increased learner and teacher utilization of ICT facilities.\r\n•	Documented ICT-based learning activities and outputs.\r\n•	Improved learner performance in ICT-related competencies.\r\n•	Strengthened collaboration with stakeholders for ICT support.', '•	Needs assessment and resource mapping to identify ICT priorities.\r\n•	Resource mobilization through partnerships with LGUs, NGOs, alumni, and private donors for equipment and software.\r\n•	Capacity-building workshops for teachers on ICT integration in teaching.\r\n•	Integration of ICT use into lesson planning, classroom instruction, and co-curricular activities.\r\n•	Preventive maintenance schedules for ICT equipment to ensure sustainability.\r\n•	Monitoring and evaluation of ICT utilization through logs, reports, and learner performance data.\r\n•	Recognition of teachers, learners, and stakeholders who actively support ICT initiatives.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head', '30000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
(6025, 'Conduct annual resource mapping and needs assessment to align MOOE utilization with school priorities; Prepare a transparent MOOE budget plan based on the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP); Implement systematic disbur', '•	Ensure effective and efficient use of MOOE funds to support school operations and improvement projects.\r\n•	Achieve a utilization rate of 100% annually with proper documentation.\r\n•	Strengthen transparency and accountability in financial management.', '•	Documented MOOE utilization reports showing 100% expenditure.\r\n•	Improved alignment of expenditures with SIP and AIP priorities.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder confidence in school financial management.\r\n•	Reduced cases of underutilization or misallocation of funds.\r\n•	Recognition of the school as a model of transparent and efficient resource use.', '•	Needs assessment and resource mapping to identify priority expenditures.\r\n•	Participatory budgeting workshops with teachers, PTA, and stakeholders.\r\n•	Systematic monitoring of expenditures through financial logs, vouchers, and receipts.\r\n•	Quarterly consultations and reviews to track utilization and adjust plans.\r\n•	Compliance with DepEd financial guidelines for disbursement and liquidation.\r\n•	Transparent communication of MOOE utilization through assemblies, newsletters, and digital platforms.\r\n•	Continuous monitoring and evaluation by the School Head, finance staff, and stakeholders.', 'June 2026 to March 2027', 'Teachers; School Head, AO, AdSup-COS', '10000.00', '', 2026, 128560, 57, 12, 109),
