(6200, 'Classroom Observation and Coaching', 'To improve instructional delivery and learner outcomes', 'Enhanced teaching strategies and classroom management', 'Coaching, mentoring, classroom observation', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Master Teachers', '3000', 'Continuous instructional improvement', 2026, 300607, 57, 12, 111),
(6201, 'Monitoring and Evaluation of SBM Programs', 'To ensure effective implementation of school programs and projects', 'Monitoring reports and accomplishment reports', 'Data gathering, evaluation meetings, reporting', 'Monthly', 'SBM Coordinator, Monitoring Team', '2000', 'For program improvement', 2026, 300607, 57, 12, 111),
(6202, 'School Facilities Improvement Project', 'To provide safe and conducive learning environment', 'Improved classrooms and school facilities', 'Repair works, Brigada Eskwela, maintenance activities', 'Year-round', 'School Head, DRRM Team, Stakeholders', '5000', 'Depends on available funds', 2026, 300607, 57, 12, 111),
(6203, 'Teacher training on Child Protection and Positive Discipline', 'To strengthen awareness of learners, parents, and staff on child protection policies\r\nTo establish effective reporting, monitoring, and intervention mechanisms', '100% awareness of learners and staff on anti-bullying policies\r\nFunctional School Child Protection Committee\r\nFunctional reporting and referral system for incidents\r\nDecreased or zero reported bullying and abuse cases\r\nConducted regular guidance and values formation sessions\r\nTrained teachers and parents on child protection strategies', 'Information, Education, and Communication (IEC) campaign\r\nCollaborative stakeholder engagement (teachers, parents, LGU, learners)\r\nPreventive education through integration in daily lessons and homeroom sessions\r\nConfidential reporting and immediate response system\r\nCapacity building through seminars and workshops\r\nContinuous monitoring, evaluation, and feedback system', 'Year-round', 'School Head, Guidance Counselor, Designate Ch', '15000', 'Strict implementation of Child Protection Policy is required\r\nImmediate reporting and response to all incidents must be observed', 2026, 304187, 57, 12, 124),
(6204, 'Conduct PTA General Assembly', 'To strengthen school-community partnership', 'Increased PTA participation and support', 'Meetings, presentations, consultations', 'Quarterly/Semestral', 'School Head, PTA Officers, Teachers', '3000', 'Support for school activities', 2026, 300607, 57, 12, 111),
(6205, 'Strengthening Child Protection Committee (CPC)', 'To ensure child-friendly and safe school environment', 'Functional CPC with documented interventions', 'Orientation, monitoring, reporting system', 'Year-round', 'CPC Members, Guidance Teacher', '2000', 'Compliance with Child Protection Policy', 2026, 300607, 57, 12, 111),
(6206, 'Reconstitution/Updating of SGC membership and committees', 'To reactivate and strengthen the functionality of the School Governing Council\r\nTo ensure active participation of stakeholders in school planning and decision-making', 'Fully organized and functional SGC with updated membership\r\nRegularly conducted and well-documented SGC meetings (monthly/minimum quarterly compliance)', 'articipatory governance approach\r\nCollaborative planning and decision-making sessions\r\nCapacity building through training and workshops', 'Year-round', 'School Head, (SGC Chair and Co-chairperson, S', '30000', 'Regular attendance and participation of members must be encouraged and monitored', 2026, 304187, 57, 12, 124),
