(6209, 'SBM Validation and Documentation', 'To prepare for SBM assessment and validation', 'Complete SBM MOVs and documentation', 'Portfolio preparation, validation meetings', 'Quarterly/Semestral', 'SBM Coordinator, Teachers, Stakeholders', '4000', 'Preparation for SBM validation', 2026, 300607, 57, 12, 111),
(6210, 'Conduct inventory of computer laboratory equipment and ICT resources', 'To determine the availability and condition of ICT facilities', 'Updated inventory report of ICT equipment', 'Physical inventory, equipment checking, and documentation', 'May- June 2026', 'ICT Coordinator, Property Custodian, School H', '1500', 'Basis for ICT improvement and maintenance', 2026, 128448, 57, 12, 121),
(6211, 'Provision of potable water and stable internet connection', 'Install potable water supply and acquire stable internet connection', 'Connection to Hydro Water supplier\r\nStable and improved internet connection in key school areas', 'Technical assessment and coordination with service providers (water and ISP)\r\nInfrastructure improvement and upgrading', 'Year-round', 'School Head, Physical Facilities In-charge, W', '20000', '130000', 2026, 304187, 57, 12, 124),
(6212, 'Conduct of quarterly monitoring of SIP/AIP implementation', 'To ensure effective implementation of SIP/AIP targets and school programs\r\nTo identify gaps, issues, and areas for improvement in school performance\r\nTo provide timely feedback and recommendations for decision-making\r\nTo strengthen accountability, tr', 'Functional SMEA Core Team with defined roles\r\nStandardized monitoring and evaluation tools/forms\r\nUpdated SIP/AIP based on evaluation results\r\nImproved school performance indicators (learning outcomes, attendance, etc.)\r\nEvidence-based decision-making system in place', 'Results-based Management (RBM) approach\r\nData-driven monitoring and evaluation system\r\nCollaborative review sessions involving stakeholders', 'as per trimester', 'School Head, SMEA Coordinator, School Plannin', '10000', 'SMEA implementation must be continuous and not treated as a one-time activity\r\nAccurate and timely data collection is essential for meaningful evaluation\r\nStrong collaboration among teachers and administrators is required\r\nResults of SMEA must directly inform school planning and improvement decisions', 2026, 304187, 57, 12, 124),
(6213, 'Item 5: Remediation Activities in Core Learning Areas (Reading, Science, Math)', 'To institutionalize a structured, data-driven remedial program that ensures 100% of struggling readers and low-performing learners achieve mastery.', 'ontextualized remedial materials (e.g., localized reading toolkits).\r\n\r\n100% completion rate for identified frustration-level readers and struggling math learners.', 'Conduct pull-out or after-school modular catch-up sessions using interactive, gamified software or activity sheets.', 'Whole year round/ Progressive implementation', 'School Head, Subject teacher ( English/Filipi', '3000', 'Success monitored via pre- and post-test results (e.g., Phil-IRI for reading; quarterly assessment performance trends).', 2026, 128308, 57, 12, 116),
(6215, 'Item 6: Integration of Peace Education and DepEd Core Values\r\nSBM Indicator: Teachers integrate topics promoting peace and DepEd core values (Maka-Diyos, Maka-Tao, Makalikasan, Makabansa).', 'To visibly embed the DepEd core values across all subject areas and daily classroom cultures.', 'Lesson plans (DLL/WHLE) detailing explicit integration of peace education and values.\r\n\r\nReduced behavioral infractions among learners.', 'Conduct a School LAC Session on contextualizing values integration in daily lesson delivery.\r\n\r\nLaunch campus-wide monthly value campaigns (e.g., \"Makalikasan Clean-Up drives\" or \"Maka-Tao peer appreciation weeks\").', 'Year-Round / Progressive Implementation', 'School Head, EsP Coordinator, Master Teachers', '500', 'Documented through checked lesson plans and observation notes during instructional supervision.', 2026, 128308, 57, 12, 116),
(6216, 'Item 7:Test Item Analysis to Inform Instruction\r\nSBM Indicator: The school conducts test item analysis to inform its teaching and learning process.', 'To utilize systematic item analysis results after every major examination to modify teaching strategies and target unmastered competencies.', 'Completed Item Analysis forms for every subject per quarter.\r\n\r\nDocumented modifications in teacher lesson logs addressing least-mastered skills.', 'Automate the item analysis process using basic spreadsheet templates shared during a faculty workshop.', 'Whole year round/ Progressive implementation', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Subject Area Ch', '500', 'Monitored via submission of Trimester Item Analysis Reports and checking of adjusted instructional plans.', 2026, 128308, 57, 12, 116),
(6217, 'Reorientation and updating of stakeholders on the School-Based Management (SBM)', 'To conduct reorientation on the updates on SBM', '100% of the expected participants oriented on the updates on SBM', 'One-Day Reorientation Program with invited division focal or SEPS in M & E', 'Opening Block (June 11, 2026)', 'School Head, Invited Resource Speaker, SBM fo', '6000', 'For implementation', 2026, 501778, 57, 12, 120),
(6218, 'Item 9: Monitored via submission of Quarterly Item Analysis Reports and checking of adjusted instructional plans.', 'To sustain and reinforce a safe, inclusive environment that proactively deters all forms of physical, verbal, and cyber-bullying.', 'Zero reported or verified bullying cases in the school record.\r\n\r\nHeightened student awareness of anti-bullying protocols.', 'Conduct a symposia or seminar on Child Protection Policies and Anti-Bullying Laws during National Children\'s Month or school opening.\r\n\r\nSet up an anonymous digital or physical \"Feedback/Report Box\" for early detection of peer conflicts.', 'Whole year round/ Progressive implementation', 'School Head, Child Protection Committee (CPC)', '1000', 'Monitored monthly through the Record Book and intake sheets', 2026, 128308, 57, 12, 116),
(6219, 'BOSY SBM Assessment', 'To identify the SBM level of practice of the school in the BOSY', 'BOSY assessment result', 'Self-Assessment through FTAD dashboard', 'May 11, 2026', 'School Head and Teachers', '500', 'Done', 2026, 501778, 57, 12, 120),
(6220, 'Item 10: Maintenance of Zero Child Abuse Incidence                                                                                                                                               SBM Indicator: The school has zero child abuse incidence.', 'To protect every learner from any form of exploitation, discrimination, or harsh disciplinary practices by reinforcing professional teaching ethics and positive discipline.', 'Maintained record of zero child abuse allegations or incidents.\r\n\r\n100% of teachers trained in Positive Discipline in Everyday Teaching.', 'Re-orient school personnel on the DepEd Child Protection Policy (DO 40, s. 2012) and the Code of Ethics for Professional Teachers.\r\n\r\nDistribute digital or physical handouts containing alternative strategies for positive classroom management.', 'ist Trimester (Regular Orientation)', 'School Head, Child Protection Committee (CPC)', '500', 'Documented via certificates of attendance from the policy orientation and signed commitment sheets from school personnel.', 2026, 128308, 57, 12, 116),
(6221, 'EOSY SBM Assessment', 'To identify the SBM level of practice of the school', 'Improved SBM level of practice in the EOSY', 'Focus Group Discussion', 'March 24, 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, and Stakeholders', '5000', 'For implementation', 2026, 501778, 57, 12, 120),
(6222, 'Item 11: Professional Development Programs Linked to IPCRG/PPST\r\nSBM Indicator: The school designs and implements professional development programs for teachers based on their IPCRG (Individual Performance Commitment and Review Group) and PPST (Phili', 'To deliver targeted, data-driven School LAC (Learning Action Cell) sessions that directly answer the core competencies teachers find challenging in their IPCRF.', 'A school-wide Professional Development Plan / LAC Plan.\r\n\r\nApproved LAC training designs and completed certificates of participation.', 'Consolidate the electronic IPCRF-Development Plans at the start of the year to identify common training needs.\r\n\r\nExecute monthly, highly practical peer-led LAC sessions utilizing Master Teachers as resource speakers.', 'Whole year round/ Progressive implementation', 'School Head, Master Teachers, LAC Coordinator', '4000', 'Success evaluated through improved classroom observation scores (COT-RPMS) in subsequent trimester.', 2026, 128308, 57, 12, 116),
(6223, 'Item 12: Implementation of the Comprehensive Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WINS) Program\r\nSBM Indicator: The school effectively implements the WinS Program (DepEd Order No. 10, s. 2016).', 'To maintain a Three-Star WinS rating by ensuring regular access to safe water, functional handwashing facilities, and strict compliance with personal hygiene practices among all learners.', 'Maintained, clean handwashing stations with stable water and soap supply.\r\n\r\n100% participation of learners in daily supervised handwashing and toothbrushing drills (as permitted by health protocols).', 'Partner with the PTA and Barangay Health Workers to schedule routine cleaning, inspection, and minor repairs of school latrines and wash facilities.\r\n\r\nDistribute hygiene advocacy posters and run student-led hygiene campaigns via the SSLG/SPG.', 'Continous/ Daily monitoring', 'School Head, WinS Coordinator, School Nurse/H', '3000', 'Monitored quarterly using the online WinS Monitoring Tool.', 2026, 128308, 57, 12, 116),
(6224, 'Item 13: Functional Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (DRRM) System\r\nSBM Indicator: The school establishes and maintains a functional School Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (SDRRM) System.', 'Objective: To safeguard the school populace and physical assets from natural and man-made hazards through regular capacity building and strict emergency preparedness protocols.', 'Updated School Hazard Map and functional evacuation routes prominently displayed.\r\n\r\nUp-to-date DRRM emergency equipment (first-aid kits, fire extinguishers).', 'Conduct the mandatory quarterly Nationwide Simultaneous Earthquake Drills (NSED) and fire safety simulations.    Organize structural integrity assessments of school buildings before typhoon seasons in partnership with local engineering offices.', 'Quarterly (NSED Schedule) / Before Typhoon Se', 'School Head, SDRRM Coordinator, Faculty, Lear', '1500.00', 'Documented through compliance reports, drill photos, and certificates submitted to the Division DRRM Coordinator.', 2026, 128308, 57, 12, 116),
(6225, 'Item 14: Regular Inventory and Preventive Maintenance of School Facilities                                                                                      SBM Indicator: The school conducts regular inventory and physical maintenance of its build', 'To maximize the lifespan and safety of all school properties through early detection of wear-and-tear and an organized repair system.', 'An updated School Property Inventory Logbook / Database.\r\n\r\nTimely repair of broken armchairs, electrical systems, and roofs before they degrade further.', 'Establish a systematic \"School Facility Inspection Checklist\" accomplished monthly by the property custodian.\r\n\r\nUtilize the annual Brigada Eskwela and quarterly maintenance rounds to immediately address carpentry or electrical needs.', 'Monthly Inspections / Major Repairs during sc', 'School Head, Property Custodian, Supply Offic', '4000', 'Success verified through clean property audit records and operational, hazard-free classrooms.', 2026, 128308, 57, 12, 116),
(6226, 'Building Strong Foundations in Literacy and Numeracy', 'Improve grade 3 learners literacy and numeracy competencies', 'Improved literacy and numeracy results in ELLNA', 'Conduct intervention programs, remediation classes, and regular assessments', 'June 2026-March 2027', 'School head, teachers', '1000.00', '', 2026, 128546, 57, 12, 108),
