(7232, 'Implementation of Project A.C.E. (ALS Completion and Equivalency) Intensive Review and Modular Remediation Sessions', 'To achieve a minimum 90% passing and certification rate for school-based ALS Elementary  candidates in the next regional assessment cycle.', '1. 15 regular ALS attendees tracked via individual monitoring cards.\r\n2. Weekly customized, localized test-readiness mock examinations conducted and recorded.\r\n3. Digital and physical storage banks of simplified review portfolios established.\r\n', '1. Develop localized, contextualized weekend and night mock-A&E review questionnaires.\r\n2. Conduct mandatory diagnostic baseline exams to group learners based on competencies needing improvement.\r\n3. Roll out peer-tutoring circles and localized learning modules targeting low-performing domains.\r\n4. Implement parallel modular home-delivery systems for learners with absolute work conflicts.\r\n', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, ALS Mobile Teacher, Instructiona', '7500', 'Needs direct technical assistance and alignment from the District ALS Coordinator to ensure simulated mock exams conform closely to recent DepEd A&E standards.', 2026, 129372, 61, 12, 14),
