(7237, 'NAT proficiency', 'Raise achievement levels in Grades 6, 10, and 12', 'Higher NAT scores in 21st century skills and core learning areas', 'Review sessions, test item analysis, integration of higher-order thinking skills', 'Annually before NAT', 'Subject Teachers, School Head', '10000', 'Progressing but needs consistency', 2026, 204009, 57, 12, 123),
(7238, 'Project S.C.A.L.E.-ALS: Sustaining Community Advancement and Literacy Empowerment through Digitalized ALS Tracks.', 'Project S.C.A.L.E.-ALS: Sustaining Community Advancement and Literacy Empowerment through Digitalized ALS Tracks.\r\nTo increase the retention and final completion rate of registered school-based ALS learners from the current baseline to 95% within the', '1. An operational Offline Digital ALS Kiosk -pre-loaded tablets/flash drives with DepEd ALS modules.\r\n\r\n2. Completed Community Mapping Report signed by the school and Barangay Council.\r\n\r\n3. 95% of active ALS registrants successfully moving from baseline diagnostics to the formal Accreditation and Equivalency (A&E) readiness phase.', '1.Community Mapping Drive: Partner with the Barangay Health Workers (BHWs) and local officials to update the database of out-of-school youth and adult dropouts in the immediate community.\r\n2. Tracking & Retention Intervention: Establish a bi-weekly \"Kamustahan\" text/online check-in system managed by the ALS mobile teacher or volunteer teachers to catch struggling or busy learners before they drop out.\r\n3. Contextualized Localized Mock Reviews: Implement customized, short quiz evaluations at the end of every major functional block to prepare candidates continuously for final certification.', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, Assigned ALS Mobile Teacher / In', '4000', '', 2026, 129372, 61, 12, 14),
