(7402, 'Strengthening School Personnel Performance and Professional Development Program', '1. To sustain and improve the very satisfactory performance rating of school personnel.\r\n2. To enhance leadership and administrative efficiency among school heads and coordinators.   3. To promote continuous professional development and recognition s', '1. Improved IPCRF and OPCRF ratings (Very Satisfactory or higher) 2. Annual PRAISE (Awards and Recognition) Program implemented', '1. Conduct Monthly LAC Sessions\r\nFocus on teaching strategies, assessment, and professional sharing\r\n2. Leadership and Capacity-Building Workshops\r\nTraining for department heads and coordinators 3. Recognition and Incentive Programs (PRAISE)\r\nReward achievements and milestones', 'Monthly: LAC Sessions and monitoring Quarterl', '1. School Head (Overall Lead) 2. Department H', '15000', '1. Align activities with DepEd standards and SBM indicators 2. Ensure continuous monitoring and evaluation 3. Documentation is essential for validation and reporting', 2026, 315815, 57, 12, 123),
(7403, 'Sustain SBM implementation', 'To sustain effective SBM implementation by strengthening stakeholders engagement, continuous improvement practices and institutionalization of established processes.', 'Sustained SBM Implementation', 'Continuous stakeholders engagement, regular capacity building activities. Institutionalization of best practices, periodic monitoring, feedback mechanism. recognition of good practices, collaboration among stakeholders.', 'Year round', 'School Head, Teachers, Stakeholders', '3000.00', '', 2026, 129263, 61, 12, 8),
(7404, 'Brigada Eskwela Implementation', 'To prepare the school for the opening of classes through community participation', 'Active participation and support from stakeholders', 'Mobilize stakeholders, clean up drive, repair classrooms and encourage partner\'s assistance', 'Before opening of the School year', 'School Head, internal and external stakeholde', '100000', 'This activity shall be done every before the opening  of classes.', 2026, 502911, 106, 12, 132),
(7405, 'School Infrastructure and Resource Enhancement Program (SIREP)', '1. Ensure regular inspection and maintenance of school infrastructure and facilities.\r\n2. Improve and upgrade school facilities such as library, classrooms, and computer laboratory.\r\n3. Maintain functional water, electricity, and internet services.', '1. Completed infrastructure inspection reports.\r\n2. Improved and repaired classrooms and facilities.\r\n3. Fully functional library and computer laboratory.', '1. Conduct quarterly facility inspections using standardized checklists.\r\n2. Organize school-based repair and maintenance initiatives (e.g., Brigada Eskwela).\r\n3. Coordinate with LGU, stakeholders, and partners for resource support.', 'Planning-June, Implementation (Inspection & R', 'School Head (Program Lead), Property Custodia', '20000', '\r\nSustainability depends on continuous stakeholder engagement.\r\nProper documentation is required for audit and compliance.\r\nFlexibility in budget allocation is necessary based on urgent needs.', 2026, 315815, 57, 12, 123),
(7406, ' Creation  of an SBM group chat for files and communication', 'To strengthen communication and collaboration among SBM Technical working Group (SMB-TWG) members through digital platforms', 'Established a functional SBM Group Chat with updated files, and communication records for SBM documentation and monitoring purposes', 'The SBM Chairperson shall manager an official group chat for SBM related files, announcements, reports, and documentation. The SBM -TWG members shall regularly submit pictures, videos and copies of accomplishments and activities for proper monitoring and SBM implementation.', 'Novermber 2025-June 2026', 'School Head, SBM Chairperson, SBM-TWG members', '250.00', 'On-going activity', 2026, 500457, 61, 12, 8),
(7407, 'Maintain satisfactory rating from stakeholders', 'Improve stakeholder satisfaction with school services', 'Stakeholder feedback reports showing satisfactory ratings', 'Feedback forms, online surveys, consultations', 'November 2026', 'Principal, Administrative Officer II, Teacher', '2000', 'Address concerns promptly', 2026, 128404, 57, 12, 123),
(7408, 'Enhanced Instructional Support and Remediation Program (EISRP)', '1. Improve learners’ performance in the National Achievement Test (NAT) 2. Strengthen teachers’ capacity in developing contextualized learning materials.\r\n3. Promote integration of peace education and DepEd core values in lessons.', 'Improved NAT scores and learner proficiency levels\r\nCompleted and implemented contextualized learning materials\r\nRemediation session reports and learner progress tracking\r\nLesson plans integrating peace and core values', '1. Conduct regular diagnostic and formative assessments 2. Develop and use localized/contextualized learning resources 3. Integrate values education and peace concepts across subjects', '1. Diagnostic Test-June (Start of SY) 2. Test', 'School Head (overall supervision), Master Tea', '5000', 'The program supports institutional strengthening and continuous improvement in teaching practices.\r\nEmphasis should be given on data-driven instruction using assessment results.\r\nSustainability will depend on teacher collaboration and stakeholder support.\r\nRegular monitoring is necessary to ensure effectiveness of interventions.', 2026, 315815, 57, 12, 123),
(7409, 'Conduct needs-based Learning Action Cells (LACs) and Learning & Development activities', 'Address professional development needs of teachers and staff', 'Improved teaching strategies, enhanced teacher competencies', 'Needs assessment, LAC sessions, workshops, peer mentoring', 'Quarterly (June, Sept, Dec, March)', 'Principal, AO II, Teachers', '15000', 'Ensure sessions are aligned with actual teacher needs', 2026, 128404, 57, 12, 123),
