(7472, 'Gather self-data assessment documents', 'To collect self-assessment survey responses from stakeholders to evaluate their understanding, engagement, and participation in school-based management processes, thereby supporting continuous improvement and effective school governance,', 'A comprehensive collection of completed self-assessment surveys from relevant stakeholders, along with a compiled report analyzing the responses to identify strengths, areas for improvement, and actionable insights for enhancing school-based management practices', 'Distribute the survey through multiple channels such as online platforms, printed copies, and in-person sessions to maximize accessibility', 'March 2026', 'School Head', '100.00', 'The strategy effectively emphasizes stakeholder engagement and participation, which are crucial for meaningful self-assessment.', 2026, 129203, 61, 12, 4),
(7473, 'Fair workload distribution', 'Ensure equitable workload among teachers', 'Balanced teacher assignments', 'Review teaching loads, adjust schedules', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers', '5000', 'Always manifested', 2026, 204009, 57, 12, 123),
(7474, 'Consultative Conference', 'To conduct consultative meeting with the in-charge of each dimension to discuss the preparation of documents, the documents to be gathered and the tool to be used during the SBM assessment.', 'Organized collection of documents gathered from each teacher or in-charge per dimension', 'Send a memorandum to all in-charge of each dimension', 'March 2026', 'School Head', '500.00', 'To ensure a collaborative and comprehensive approach to data gathering and this will facilitate consensus on the most suitable tools to be used, align expectations, and clarify roles and responsibilities.', 2026, 129203, 61, 12, 4),
(7475, 'Conduct Monitoring and Evaluation Activities\r\n\r\n\r\n', 'Ensure effective implementation of programs and projects', 'Timely reports and improved program implementation', 'Utilize monitoring tools, conduct evaluations, and feedback sessions', 'Monthly / Quarterly', 'School Head, Coordinators', '1500', '', 2026, 128316, 57, 12, 116),
(7476, 'Improve School Infrastructure and Facilities\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n', 'Provide safe and conducive learning environment', 'Improved classrooms and school facilities', 'Conduct repairs, maintenance, and facility upgrading', 'Whole Year', 'School Head, LGU, Stakeholders', '5000', '', 2026, 128316, 57, 12, 116),
(7477, 'Infrastructure inspection', 'Ensure safety and functionality of facilities', 'Regular inspection reports', 'Conduct scheduled inspections, document findings', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers, LGU Engineer', '3000', 'Frequently manifested', 2026, 204009, 57, 12, 123),
(7478, 'Coordination with stakeholders', 'To coordinate with the stakeholders and conduct follow -up meetings to ensure their participation, engagement and support in the gathering of documents/data for SBM validation', 'Awareness of the stakeholders about the school activities and their role in the management of school', 'Send formal invitations or communication outlining the purpose, benefits, and expectations', 'May 2026', 'School Head', '700.00', 'Effective coordination with stakeholders has significantly contributed to enhanced support and resource mobilization for the school.', 2026, 129203, 61, 12, 4),
(7479, 'Infrastructure improvement', 'Upgrade school facilities', 'Improved classrooms and learning spaces', 'Propose projects, coordinate with LGU and stakeholders', 'Annually', 'School Head, Stakeholders', '50000', 'Rarely manifested', 2026, 204009, 57, 12, 123),
(7480, 'Improve Water Connection and Facilities\r\n\r\n', 'Ensure functional utility services for school operations', 'Stable utility and internet services', 'Coordinate with service providers and conduct regular maintenance', 'Whole Year', 'ICT Coordinator, School Head', '2500', '', 2026, 128316, 57, 12, 116),
(7481, 'Functional library', 'Provide access to learning resources', 'Operational library with updated materials', 'Acquire books, digital resources, organize reading programs', 'Ongoing', 'Librarian, Teachers', '30000', 'Rarely manifested', 2026, 204009, 57, 12, 123),
(7482, 'Conduct school-based assessment/validation', 'To systematically conduct school-based validation for each grade level across all relevant dimensions, ensuring accurate assessment and continuous improvement of educational practices and learner performance.', 'Clear documentation of areas where learners and school practices excel or need improvement based on validation results.', 'Create a schedule for validation activities to ensure minimal disruption.', 'July 2026	S', 'School Head, all teachers', '500.00', 'The validation process was systematically conducted, ensuring the accuracy and reliability of assessment data across all grade levels.', 2026, 129203, 61, 12, 4),
(7483, '“READy to Grow: Strengthening Reading through CRLA Guided Support', 'To decrease the number of learners who belong to struggling learners from Grades 1 to 3', 'Reduced percentage of struggling readers from grade 1 to 3 based on post-assessment results; Profiled literacy data and individual progress tracking sheets for all targeted learners; Contextualized reading intervention materials, flashcards, and localized storybooks developed and utilized; Functional and well-utilized reading corners established across all key stage 1 classrooms', 'Administer the CRLA pre-test to identify and profile struggling readers; Group learners according to their specific literacy intervention needs; Conduct localized SLAC session focusing on early literacy teaching strategies; Implement a dedicated daily reading intervention window using localized materials and reading drill cards; Conduct mid-year and post CRLA assessment to track development and fine-tune intervention strategies.', 'year round', 'School Head, School Reading Coordinators, and', '25000.00', 'Progress and literacy metrics will be strictly monitored and presented during the quarterly SMEA conferences; Home-school reading partnership will be reinforced through regular parent updates and localized home-reading guides.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7484, 'Utility facilities', 'Ensure reliable utilities', 'Functional water, electricity, and internet', 'Regular maintenance, coordination with providers', 'Ongoing', 'School Head, Utility Staff', '7000', 'Frequently manifested', 2026, 204009, 57, 12, 123),
(7486, 'Computer laboratory', 'Support ICT-based learning', 'Operational computer lab/classroom', 'Maintain equipment, provide ICT training', 'Ongoing', 'ICT Coordinator, Teachers', '5000', 'Rarely manifested', 2026, 204009, 57, 12, 123),
(7487, 'Strengthen Child Protection and Mental Wellness Programs\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n', 'Promote learner safety and well-being', 'Functional child protection and wellness support systems', 'Conduct orientations, counseling sessions, and wellness activities', 'Whole Year', 'CPC Members, Guidance Coordinator', '1500', '', 2026, 128316, 57, 12, 116),
(7489, 'Review Teacher Workload Distribution\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n', 'Ensure fair and equitable assignment of tasks', 'Balanced teacher workload distribution', 'Conduct workload assessment and consultation meetings', 'Start of School Year', 'School Head', '1000', '', 2026, 128316, 57, 12, 116),
(7490, 'Recognition to teachers of each grade level or dimension and to stakeholders', 'To recognize and commend teachers across all dimensions and supportive stakeholders who have contributed to the successful implementation and validation of the School-Based Management (SBM) system, thereby fostering motivation and appreciation.', 'A formal recognition ceremony or event conducted to honor teachers and stakeholders involved in the SBM validation process.', 'Develop criteria and standards for recognition', 'July 2026	', 'School  Head', '1500.00', 'Recognition to teachers of each grade level or dimension and to stakeholders could motivate them to work even more efficiently and consistently because they are aware that their hardwork and contribution to school  are seen.', 2026, 129203, 61, 12, 4),
(7491, 'MOOE utilization', 'Ensure efficient use of funds', '72–100% utilization rate', 'Align expenditures with school priorities', 'Annually', 'School Head, Finance Staff', '', 'Frequently manifested', 2026, 204009, 57, 12, 123),
(7493, 'MOOE liquidation', 'Ensure accountability in fund use', '100% liquidation reports', 'Prepare financial reports, submit on time', 'Annually', 'School Head, Finance Staff', '', 'Frequently manifested', 2026, 204009, 57, 12, 123),
(7494, 'Strengthen DRRM Preparedness\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n', 'Improve school disaster preparedness and response', 'Functional DRRM plan and regular drills', 'Conduct DRRM trainings, drills, and plan updating', 'Quarterly', 'DRRM Coordinator', '1000', '', 2026, 128316, 57, 12, 116),
(7495, 'Implement Drop-Out Reduction Program\r\n\r\n\r\n', 'Reduce absenteeism and learner drop-out incidence', 'Improved learner attendance and retention', 'Conduct home visitations and learner intervention programs', 'Whole Year', 'Teachers, Guidance Coordinator', '500', '', 2026, 128316, 57, 12, 116),
(7497, '“SCI-QUEST: Empowering Experience to Build Knowledge and Confidence”', 'To increase the proficiency level in Science subject in National Achievement Test by 5%', 'Increased MPS and overall proficiency level in Science for the NAT', 'Administer a diagnostic test or mock NAT to identify specific learning gaps and LCM in Science ; Design and utilize targetted SIM and interactive review modules abased on the assessment results; Conduct regular item analysis of quarterly exams to monitor progress and adjust remediation strategies promptly; Integrate hands-on science experiments and practical applications during instruction to enhance conceptual understanding and memory retentions; Organize scheduled NAT review sessions focusing on higher-order thinking skills (HOTS) and standardized test formats.', 'year round', 'School Head and School Science Coordinator', '25000.00', 'Implementation progress and NAT readiness metrics will be monitored and reported quarterly during SMEA conferences; Collaboration with parents and stakeholders will be maintained to support home-based science review activities and resource allocation.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7498, '“Project KANDILI: Kalinga at Dignidad para sa Lahat ng Bata”', 'Trained teachers and students on Child Protection Policy and other Guidance Programs for learners’ mental and physical well-being', 'Conducted school-wide orientation and capability-building seminar on the CPC and positive discipline to all teachers and personnel; Established an active, well-presented CPC and guidance advocacy group; distributed localized mental health awareness, anti bullying information drives, and child rights campaign materials to learners and parents; Decreased incidence reports related to behavioral misunderstanding and peer conflict through active guidance mediation records', 'Organize a structure orientation workshop for faculty members focusing on positive discipline approaches and child defense mandates; Formulate a localized advocacy plan utilizing guidance hours to educate learners on child rights, safety protocols, and mental health wellness; Set up a confidential, accessible child protection desk or digital drop-box system for early reporting of counseling or interventions needs; Collaborate closely with the guidance coordinator and external healthcare/social workers to establish a swift psychological referral mechanism for at-risk learners; Conduct regular parent-teacher engagement dialogues to strengthen values education and promote safe home-school environments.', 'year round', 'School Head,  School Planning Team, School Gu', '15000.00', 'Project milestones, counseling data profiles, and policy execution indicators will be strictly monitored and presented during quarterly SMEA conferences. All operations will comply seamlessly with the DepEd CPP framework and child defense standard.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7499, '\"Project LEAD: Empowering the School Elementary Learner Government (SELG) for Active Student Leadership\"', 'To enhance leadership skills of student leaders and promote active learner participation in school governance, child protection campaigns, and student-led community projects.', 'Formulate SELG annual constitution, action plan, and calendar of activities; Conduct leadership capability-building training and team-building workshops for officers; Implement student-led campus projects targeting clean-and green- drives and antibullying awareness; Documented minutes of regular monthly coordination meeting and project completion folders.', 'Facilitate democratic election and execute a mandatory orientation program on roles and responsibilities for newly elected SELG Officers; Conduct a structures leadership training seminar focusing on project planning, communication, and values integration; Establish focused student working committee to delegate tasks effectively; Collaborate with the School Head, Guidance Coordinator, and PTA to secure institutional support and resources for student initiatives; Launch student-led advocacy projects.', 'year round', 'Shool Head, SELG Adviser, SELG Officers, & le', '10000.00', 'SELG achievements, resolutions, and project outcomes will be highlighted and reported quarterly during SMEA conferences; All student-led activities will remain strictly aligned with DepEd CPC and school safety protocols.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7500, '\"Project EXCEL: Comprehensive Preparation and Intervention for Grade 6 Learners in the National Achievement Test (NAT)\"', 'To increase the overall Mean Percentage Score (MPS) and ensure Grade 6 Learners achieve the target proficiency level in all 21st-century skills and core learning areas in the National Achievement Test (NAT)', 'Elevated NAT performance metric meeting or exceeding division/regional targets; Formulated database of diagnostic test results, item analysis, and individual tracking profiles; Developed and distributed contextualized review materials and Strategic Intervention Materials (SIM); Conducted scheduled mock NAT drills and specialized critical-thinking test clinics.', 'Administer a standardized pre-test or diagnostic assessment to evaluate student baseline readiness; Conduct precise item analysis to pinpoint specific LCMs across core subjects; Design and utilize context-specific review sheets, flashcards, and interactive instructional drills; Integrate high-order thinking skills (HOTS) questions into everyday classroom tests and quizzes; Implement structured periodic mock testing simulations to build student stamina and testing familiarity.', 'year round', 'School Head, Grade 6 adviser and subject teac', '15000.00', 'Progress tracking profiles and mock assessment data will be strictly monitored and presented during quarterly SMEA conferences. Strong partnerships with parents will be maintained to reinforce home-based review regimens and ensure excellent attendance during review blocks.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7502, '\"Project LIFT: Intensified Remediation and Intervention Program in Reading, Science, and Mathematics\"', 'To address gaps and improve the mastery level of struggling learners in reading comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics through structured remediation activities.', 'Reduced number of learners under \"struggling\" or \"frustration\" level across all core learning areas; documented pre-assessment and post-assessment data (CRLA, PHIL-IRI, RMA); localized and contextualized remedial worksheets, reading booklets, and math drill cards; individual learner progress tracking profiles updated regularly.', 'Administer standardized diagnostic test (CRLA, Phil IRI, RMA) to identify and profile  learners with learning gaps; Group learners according to specific intervention needs and design targeted remedial session guides; Utilize localized flashcards, and hands-on science intervention modules during scheduled remedial hours; conduct continuous formative tracking and give immediate constructive feedbacks to learners during intervention blocks; Administer periodic post-assessment to measure program effectiveness and determine readiness for mainstream instruction.', 'year round', 'School Head, Reading Coordinator, Science Coo', '10000.00', 'Remediation milestones, learner progress metrics, and program adjustments will be presented  during quarterly SMEA conferences. Active home-school partnership will be sustained through regular parent-teacher updates to ensure continuous learning reinforcement at home.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7503, '\"Project PRIME: Strengthening the Institutional School Monitoring, Evaluation, and Adjustment (SMEA) Mechanism\"', 'To systematically monitor and evaluate all school programs, projects and activities (PPAs) every quarter to ensure data-driven adjustments and continuous school improvement. ', 'Functional School Monitoring and Evaluation committee with clear task delegations; Standardized, automated digital SMEA dashboards and tracking tools; Documented quarterly  SMEA reports, minutes of validation conferences, and approved policy adjustments proposals; Increased utilization rate of evaluation data for physical and instructional adjustments', 'Organize and capacitate the internal  School Quality Assurance(QA)/M&E team on standard data validation protocols; Establish a fixed annual dashboard timeline for program coordinators to upload monthly accomplishment verifications; Conduct structures SMEA conferences to analyze implementation gaps, financial execution and target shortfalls; Formulate operational adjustment recommendations based on verified findings, to address bottlenecks promptly; Present evaluated data outcomes to school planning teams, the SGC, and external stakeholders for transparency.', 'year round', 'School Head, M&E Coordinator, Planning Team M', '10000.00', 'Quarterly SMEA synthesis reports and policy adjustments will be submitted to the SDO via the functional district validation network. Data transparency will be sustained by updating the physical school bulletin board following each quarterly evaluation cycle.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7504, '\"Project SMART-Frontline: Streamlining and Innovating School Frontline Service Delivery for Enhanced Stakeholder Satisfaction\"', 'To introduce innovative digital and physical mechanism in the provision of school frontline services, ensuring fast, transparent, and highly accessible transactions for all stakeholders.', 'Established automated, Excel-based, or QR-coded document request and tracking system; Reduced processing and waiting times for standard frontline requests; Functional, visually organized, and comfortable physical frontline desk or kiosk; High rating results collected regularly via Client Satisfactory Survey (CSS).', 'Review and map existing frontline transaction workflows to eliminate redundant procedural steps; Develop or adopt a localized digital request system to allow advance requests; Set up a clean, dedicated, frontline transaction desk equipped with clear citizen\'s charter signage; Conduct regular technical orientations for non-teaching staff and administrative assistants on customer  service excellence; Standardized the distributions and digital collection of CSS to gather immediate stakeholder feedback.', 'year round', 'School Head, AO, School clerk, Registrar-desi', '10000.00', 'Frontline satisfaction metrics, average document processing timelines, and CSS analysis results will be evaluated and reported quarterly during SMEA conferences. Feedback trends will be utilized to continuously upgrade service delivery protocols.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7505, 'Orientation and Advocacy on SBM to Stakeholders', 'To orient teachers, parents, barangay officials, and community members on the principles and importance of SBM', '100% of teachers and staff oriented\r\nand at least 70% of parents and community leaders attended', 'Conduct general assembly and/ or focus group discussions ', 'June 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers, Barangay', '', '', 2026, 129175, 61, 12, 2),
(7506, 'Orientation on SBM FTAD & Planning Conference of teachers and Stakeholders on the implementation of School Based Management', 'To orient/capacitate teachers & stakeholders and plan the implementation of School-Based Management', 'Oriented and capacitated teachers and stakeholders on the implementation of SBM and planned School PPA\'s', 'Orientation & Teachers\' Conference, FGD with the stakeholders', 'March 27, 2026', 'PTA, Teachers & stakeholders', '2000', '', 2026, 129164, 61, 12, 2),
(7507, 'NAT Review and Enhancement Program', 'To improve learner performance in NAT competencies and 21st century skills', 'Increased NAT readiness and improved test scores', 'Conduct regular review classes, remedial sessions, and mock tests', 'Quarterly/Whole School Year', 'School Heads, Teachers, Learners', '5000.00', 'For printing of review materials, bond paper, and snacks', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7508, 'Conduct the FTAD Self-Assessment (Pre)', 'To conduct the Self-Assessment to identify the CIGPB\'s in the school context', 'Conducted Self-Assessment to identified the CIGPB\'s in the school context', 'Check the Self-assessment', 'April 20, 2026', 'Teachers & School Head', '', '', 2026, 129164, 61, 12, 2),
(7509, '\"Project DATA DRIVEN: Standardizing Automated Test Item Analysis for Targeted Instructional Remediation\"', 'To institutionalize the regular conduct of test item analysis for quarterly assessment to identify learning gaps and utilize the results to inform, adjust, and improve the teaching and learning process.', 'Automated, Excel-based test item analysis templates deployed across all grade levels and learning areas; Detailed item analysis reports identifying the MPS and LMCs; Formulate data-driven remedial lesson plans, instructional materials, and localized intervention strategies; Documented collaborative evaluation notes from grade-level SLAC analysis sessions.', 'Distribute standardized, automated electronic item analysis templates to all teaching staff prior to assessment periods; Require teachers to encode quarterly exam scores immediately to extract the difficulty index, discrimination index, and LMCs; Conduct specialized SLAC sessions after each major examination period to collectively interpret item analysis data trends; modify instructional pacing guides and design focused remedial materials targeting the identified least mastered skills; Conduct regular supervisory classroom observations to verify the implementation of data-informed instructional adjustments', 'year round', 'School Head, Master Teacher, School Testing C', '10000.00', 'Item analysis summaries, school-wide MPS tracking, and lists of LMC will be systematically reported quarterly during SMEA conferences. Instructional adjustments based on this data will serve as a primary indicator during regular school-level; quality circles.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7510, 'Conduct Diagnostic and Pre-Test Assessment', 'To identify least-mastered competencies and learning gaps', 'Consolidated assessment results and intervention plan', 'Administer pre-tests and conduct item analysis', 'Beginning of School Year ', 'Teachers, Coordinators ', '2000.00', 'For test papers and reproduction expenses', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7511, 'Identify CIGPB\'s and SBM FTAD Encoding', 'To Identify and encode CIGPB\'s for an immediate intervention', 'Identified CIGPB\'s/upload in the system and finding solutions and interventions for improvement', 'FGD, Encoding, Identifying, Resource Mobilization', 'May 21, 2026', 'PTA, Teachers & stakeholders', '', '', 2026, 129164, 61, 12, 2),
(7512, 'Remediation and Intervention Classes', 'To address learning gaps of struggling learners', 'Improved learner mastery level', 'Small-group tutoring, peer mentoring, and differentiated instruction', 'Weekly', 'Subject Teachers, Learners', '3000.00', 'For instructional materials and activity sheets', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7513, 'Learning Action Cell (LAC) on NAT Strategies', 'To enhance teachers\' instructional and assessment practices', 'Teachers equipped with effective NAT preparation strategies', 'Conduct LAC sessions and sharing of best practices', 'Quarterly', 'School Heads, Teachers', '2500.00', 'For training materials and documentation', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7514, 'Improvement, enhancement & Adjustment of SBM implementation with MOV\'s (SBM Implementation)', 'To improve, enhance and adjust SBM Implementation with corresponding MOV\'s ', 'Improved, enhanced and adjusted the Implementation of SBM with MOV\'s', 'Implementation of PPA\'s', 'June-February, 2027', 'PTA, Teachers & stakeholders', '3000', '', 2026, 129164, 61, 12, 2),
(7515, 'Integration of 21st Century Skills in Teaching', 'To strengthen critical thinking, collaboration, communication, and problem-solving skills', 'Improved learner engagement and performance', 'Project-based learning and ICT Integration', 'Whole School Year ', 'Teachers, Learners', '4000.00', 'For ICT materials and classroom resources', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7516, 'Review on the Conduct of Self Assessment (Post)', 'To review on the Conduct of Self Assessment (Post)', 'Reviewed he conduct of self-assessment and adjusted according to what degree of manifestation to each indicators', 'Self-Assessment (POST)', 'February 2027', 'PTA, Teachers & stakeholders', '', '', 2026, 129164, 61, 12, 2),
(7517, '“ MACOPA STAR”\r\nMeritorious Achievement of Committed, Optimistic and Progress Goal Advocators: Stakeholders and Teachers Awards and Recognition', 'To sustain the conduct of PRAISE to recognize teachers performance and  stakeholder’s engagement and support', 'Established clear and objective evaluation guidelines or matrices for school level Rewards and Recognition (R&R) matching PRAISE committee standards; Conducted annual or milestone award ceremonies honoring outstanding teacher performance and continuous stakeholder contributions; Complied portfolio or certificates, plaque tokens, plaques of appreciation, and documentation reports for all awardees; Increased teacher motivation levels and sustained high stakeholder engagement rates in supporting school improvement projects.', 'Organize and convene the school PRAISE committee to finalize selection parameters; Disseminate information regarding award categories, qualifications timeliness, and documentary requirements to all teachers and school stakeholders; Gather, validate, and evaluate submitted nomination portfolios objectively against approved criteria guidelines; Procure standard certificates, plaques, or alternative incentives utilizing designated MOOE or partnership rewards funds; Stage organized recognition program or gala to publicly celebrate milestone accomplishments and foster a culture of institutional appreciation.', 'year round', 'School Head and School PRAISE Coordinator', '15000.00', 'Project outcomes, award rosters, and partner contributions will be documented and presented quarterly   during SMEA conferences; All R&R processes will remain perfectly aligned with civil service rules, division guidelines, and local DepEd PRAISE council mandates.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7518, 'Parent and Stakeholder Engagement Program', 'To strengthen parental and stakeholder support', 'Increased learner participation and support system', 'Conduct orientation meetings and progress monitoring', 'Every Year', 'Parents, Teachers, PTA Officers', '1500.00', 'For meeting materials and communication expenses', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7519, 'PSDS Technical Assistance and Plan for improvement', 'Request PSDS for Technical Assistance or invite  Division FTAD In-charge ', 'The school is given technical assistance for improvement', 'Technical assistance, FGD', 'March 2027', 'Division FTAD In-charge, PSDS, School Head, P', '3000', '', 2026, 129164, 61, 12, 2),
(7520, 'Monitoring and Evaluation of NAT Performance', 'To monitor effectiveness of interventions and learner progress', 'Quarterly progress reports and adjusted interventions', 'Conduct monitoring, feedbacking, and evaluation sessions', 'Monthly/Quarterly', 'School Heads, Coordinators, Teachers', '2000.00', 'For documentation and printing expenses', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7521, '“Project SIGLA”', 'To ensure payment for school utilities and mandatory operational expenses', 'Sustained and uninterrupted water, electricity, and internet connectivity for the school campus; Zero delays or penalties in the monthly settlement of critical utility accounts; Up-to-date financial record keeping and systematic collection of official utility billing statements; Maximized efficiently in the consumption of school resources among personnel and learners.', 'Conduct a routine monthly collection, checking, and validation of all incoming utility billing notices; Allocate a fixed and regular portion of the monthly school MOOE cash advance specifically for utilities; Establish standard tracking sheets to log monthly consumption data and flag sudden billing spikes; Coordinate closely with the AO and school clerk to facilitate early voucher preparation; Launch a campus-wide resource conservation campaign to promote energy and water-saving habits.', 'year round', 'School Head, AO, School Clerk, Teachers', '10000.00', 'Financial statements, monthly liquidation receipts, and utility efficiency records will be audited during quarterly SMEA; Procurement processes will strictly comply with COA rules and regular division budgeting timelines.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7522, 'Conduct School Accessibility Assessment', 'To identify barriers and facility needs for learners with disabilities and special needs', 'Assessment report and list of priority facility needs', 'Ocular inspection, consultation with teachers, parents, and stakeholders', 'June 2006', 'School Heads, SBM Coordinator, DRRM Coordinat', '2000.00', 'To be conducted before the implementation of improvement projects', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7523, 'Install Basic PWD-Friendly Signages and Handrails', 'To improve accessibility and safety within the school premises', 'Installed signages and handrails in priority areas', 'School-based repair and maintenance activities with stakeholder support', 'July-August 2026', 'School Heads, Property Custodian, PTA, LGU/Ba', '15000.00', 'Priority areas include entrances, stairs, and corridors', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7524, 'Establish Accessible Comfort Room Corner', 'To provide learner-friendly and inclusive sanitation facilities', 'One accessible comfort room or modified toilet area', 'Minor renovation and procurement of basic fixtures', 'August-September 2026', 'School Heads, School Engineer/Skilled Workers', '25000.00', 'Subject to availability of funds and materials', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7525, 'Project Kapit-Bisig: Kaagapay sa Pag-unlad ng Bata at Eskwela', 'To strengthen and increase the active participation of key stakeholders during Brigada Eskwela and other school activities', 'Increased volunteer turnout and active participation from parents, local government officials, alumni, and private partners; Signed partnerships, MOA, or commitments of support from community stakeholders; Formulate database mapping stakeholder profiles, donation records; and volunteer hours; Successfully organized Brigada Eskwela, advocacy campaigns, and school-community general assemblies.', 'Conduct a community mapping activity to identify potential external stakeholders, local business, and socio-civic organizations; Launch multi-channel advocacy campaigns using social media, physical leaflets, and community visitations to promote school projects; Organize structured stakeholder convergence meetings to discuss school development needs and draft collaborative project plans, Institutionalize a transparent feedback and reporting mechanism to keep partners updated on the utilization of their contributions; Conduct regular stakeholders recognition programs and appreciation ceremonies to honor active volunteer commitments.', 'year round', 'School Head, School Planning Team, Brigada Es', '15000.00', 'Stakeholders engagement metrics, partnerships established, and donation summaries will be reported quarterly during SMEA conferences; Resource mobilization and partnership processes will adhere strictly to standard DepEd guidelines on stakeholder collaboration and accountability.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7526, 'Create Learner Support/Inclusive Learning Corner', 'To provide a safe and supportive learning space for learners with special needs', 'Functional inclusive learning corner with basic materials', 'Reuse available resources and solicit donations from stakeholders', 'September 2026', 'Teachers, SPG/SSG, PTA, Stakeholders', '8000.00', 'Utilize recyclable and donated materials whenever possible', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7527, 'Conduct Orientation on Inclusive Education and PWD Awareness', 'To increase awareness and support for inclusive education practices', 'Teachers, learners, and stakeholders oriented on inclusivity and accessibility', 'Seminar-workshop and advocacy campaign', 'October 2026', 'School Heads, Guidance Coordinator, Teachers,', '5000.00', 'Can be integrated during INSET, PTA meetings, or school programs', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7528, 'Strengthen Partnerships for Resource Mobilization', 'To generate support for future SPED-and PWD-related projects', 'Partnership agreements and donated materials/resources', 'Coordination with LGU, NGOs, alumni, and private partners', 'Whole Year', 'School Heads, SBM Coordinator, PTA,  Stakehol', '3000.00', 'Continuous monitoring and follow-up with stakeholders needed', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7529, '\"Project BALANSE: Enhancing Teacher Welfare Through Fair and Equitable Workload Distribution\"', 'To implement a transparent, fair, and equitable distribution of teaching loads and ancillary tasks among faculty members in accordance with DepEd guidelines to maximize instructional efficiency and support teacher well-being.', 'Formulated master class program and loading matrix aligned with standard DepEd guidelines; Balanced distribution of institutional ancillary assignments and special committee duties; High levels of teacher job satisfaction and reduced administrative burnout; Clear instructional and supervisory monitoring plans across all grade levels.', 'Review existing DepEd advisories and policies regarding ,maximum teaching loads and ancillary functions; Convene a collaborative school programming committee meeting prior to the opening of the school year to assess personal specializations and preferences; Design a transparent workload matrix balancing daily actual teaching hours, preparation time, and extra-curricular assignments; Implement a rotating system or peer-pairing structure for complex committee responsibilities to divide workloads evenly; Conduct regular feedback surveys or open dialogue sessions with personnel to identify overloading concerns and adjust task delegations promptly.', 'year round', 'School Head, Master Teacher, Subject Coordina', '1000.00', 'Workload distribution schedules, loading adjustments, and teacher feedback summaries will be systematically presented quarterly during SMEA conferences. Strict  adherence to employee welfare mandates will be monitored continuously to sustain a highly productive and positive school climate.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7530, 'Coordinate with the District ALS Coordinator and nearby schools offering ALS programs.', 'To establish coordination with nearby ALS providers.', 'Partnership or linkage established with nearby ALS implementing schools or centers, increased access of out-of-school youth and adults to ALS services and \r\nreferred learners successfully enrolled in ALS programs.', 'Orientation and advocacy campaigns will be organized to inform the community about ALS opportunities and the Accreditation and Equivalency (A&E) program. Identified learners will be referred to nearby ALS providers, while the school will assist in monitoring, follow-up, and providing available support facilities when necessary.', '2nd quarter(April-June 2026)', 'School Head, Teachers, ALS Coordinator', '', '', 2026, 128550, 57, 12, 109),
(7531, 'Conduct Mapping and Identification of Disadvantaged Learners, OSYs, and Adult Learners', 'To identify potential learners in the community who are not attending school or need alternative learning opportunities', 'Master list/profile of identified learners', 'House-to-house survey, barangay coordination, use of enrollment and community data', 'June–July 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Barangay Officials, PT', '3000.00', 'For printing, transportation, and materials\r\nInitial activity for planning interventions', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7532, '“Project CHEER-UP: Creating Hope and Engagement to Enhance Reading – Unlocking Potential”', 'To decrease the number of learners in frustration level of Grades 4 to 6', 'Decreased the number of learners in frustration level of Grades 4 to 6', 'Administer the Phil IRI pre-test to identify and profile frustration-level readers in Grades 4 to 6; Design and implement a structured daily remedial reading window utilizing specialized reading modules and contextualized instructional materials; Conduct focused \"Reading Clinics\" and peer-assisted learning approaches; Organize regular SLAC sessions for KS2 teachers to share best [practices in vocabulary and comprehension development; Conduct mid-year and post Phi-IRI assessments to track reader progression and evaluate intervention outcomes.', 'year round', 'School Head, School Reading Coordinators, and', '20000.00', 'Learner progress metrics and reading profile updates will be monitored regularly and reported quarterly during SMEA conferences; Home-school partnership will be strengthened by providing parents with localized home-reading guides to reinforce reading practice at home.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7533, 'Community Awareness Campaign on Inclusive Education and ALS Programs', 'To inform the community about available educational opportunities for OSYs and adult learners', 'Increased community awareness and inquiries/enrollees', 'Distribution of flyers, community meetings, social media posting, school orientation', 'July 2026', 'Teachers, ALS Coordinator, Barangay Officials', '2500.00', 'For tarpaulins, flyers, snacks\r\nCan be integrated with Brigada Eskwela activities', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7534, 'Conduct simple school-based activities related to gardening, cooking, handicrafts, or entrepreneurship.', 'To integrate basic livelihood skills in elementary activities.', 'Learners developed basic practical and life skills appropriate to their grade level, and enhanced support from parents and community volunteers in school activities.', 'Career orientations, demonstrations, and simple livelihood-related activities will be conducted to expose elementary learners to practical skills appropriate to their level, also, the school will also strengthen collaboration with parents and community stakeholders to support learners in pursuing TLE-TVL pathways upon entering secondary education.', 'Whole School Year/June- March', 'Teachers, PTA, Community Volunteers', '', 'nn', 2026, 128550, 57, 12, 109),
(7535, 'Establish Learning Support Sessions/ALS Corner', 'To provide accessible learning space and support materials for disadvantaged learners', 'Functional learning corner with materials and schedules', 'Setting up reading corner, modular learning area, and referral system', 'August 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Librarian, Volunteers', '5000.00', 'For tables, chairs, printed materials\r\nUse existing classrooms or library space', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7536, '“Project MIND-UP: Mastery in Numeracy Development – Unlocking Potential”', 'To increase the Proficiency level in Mathematics Subject', 'Increased the Proficiency level in Math by 1 % every year', 'Administer RMA pre-test across all KS2 learners to identify specific gaps and least mastered competencies; Implement a structured 15-minute mental math drill and window using contextualized flashcards and automated math exercises; Develop and distribute SIM and localized math problem solving worksheets tailored to struggling learners;  Conduct SLAC sessions for teacher innovative and interactive methods for teaching math concepts; Conduct regular quarterly assessments and item analysis to monitor growth metrics and fine-tune remedial sessions accordingly.', 'year round', 'School Head and School Math Coordinator', '20000.00', 'School proficiency trends and program implementation milestones will be tracked strictly and reported quarterly during SMEA conferences; Parental support will be mobilized  through regular progress briefings and the provision of simplified home-based numeracy guide activities.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7537, 'Conduct Weekly Remedial and Literacy Sessions', 'To improve literacy and numeracy skills of identified learners', 'Improved learner participation and basic skills', 'Small-group teaching, peer tutoring, volunteer-assisted learning', 'August 2026 – March 2027', 'Teachers, Volunteer Tutors, PTA', '4000.00', 'For instructional materials and snacks\r\n', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7538, 'Partner with Barangay and Stakeholders for Support Programs', 'To strengthen support system for disadvantaged and adult learners', 'Signed partnership agreements and stakeholder assistance', 'Coordination meetings and stakeholder engagement', 'September 2026', 'School Head, Barangay Council, NGOs, PTA', '2000.00', 'Seek donations and learning materials', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7539, 'Refer identified learners to nearby ALS providers or centers.', 'Support ALS implementation through referrals.', 'List of identified out-of-school youth and adult learners, and there will be an increase number of ALS enrollees from the school/community catchment area.', 'Conduct mapping and profiling of out-of-school youth and adult learners in the community and  conduct orientation with identified learners and parents about ALS enrollment and requirements.', 'Whole School Year/June- March', 'School Head, Teachers, ALS Coordinator', '', '', 2026, 128550, 57, 12, 109),
(7540, 'Conduct Career Guidance and Life Skills Training', 'To equip learners with practical life and employability skills', 'Conducted training sessions and certificates', 'Workshops, invited speakers, demonstrations', 'October–November 2026', 'Guidance Coordinator, Teachers, LGU Represent', '6000.00', 'For materials and honorarium\r\nCan be tied with livelihood programs', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7541, '“Project INKLUSYON: Empowering Teachers in Nurturing Learning Opportunities for Learners with Special Needs”', 'To train teachers with skill and knowledge in manifesting and dealing learners with disability', 'At least 1 teacher will be trained on SNED management', 'Identify and nominate target teaching teaching personnel to attend division, regional, or national specialized training and seminars on SNED and inclusive education management;  Conduct localized SLAC echoing sessions led by the trained personnel to cascade knowledge on handling learners with disabilities to all faculty members; Coordinate with the SDO and health stakeholders to acquire standard screening tools and instructional guides for identifying diverse learning disabilities; Collaborate with local government units  supplementary funds and socio-civic partners to gather supplementary funds and assistive resource materials for inclusive classrooms; Monitor the adaptation of individualized instruction plans and classroom adjustments through regular school head supervisory visits.', 'year round', 'SNED Teachers, School Head, Stakeholders, BLG', '10000.00', 'Training compliance profiles, echoed SLAC completion reports, and inclusive teaching indicators will be systematically compiled and presented quarterly during SMEA conferences; All professional development activities align strictly with standard DepEd Inclusive education policies and professional training parameters.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
(7542, 'Formation/Reorganization of School Governing Council (SGC)', 'To establish a functional SGC that will actively participate in school decision-making', 'Functional SGC with elected officers and clear roles & responsibilities', 'Election of representatives (parents, teachers, barangay, alumni, students)', 'July 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents, Barangay Repr', '', '', 2026, 129175, 61, 12, 2),
(7543, 'Monitor and Evaluate Participation and Progress', 'To assess effectiveness of interventions and learner progress', 'Monitoring reports and updated learner records', 'Quarterly monitoring, interviews, attendance tracking', 'Quarterly', 'School Heads, Teachers, SBM Coordinator', '1500.00', 'Basis for continuous improvement', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7544, 'Organize a simple classroom-based or centralized reading corner.', 'To set up a basic school reading corner or mini-library.', 'Functional reading corner established.', 'School head, teachers, learners, and stakeholders (PTA, parents, and barangay officials) will collaborate in identifying a suitable space either inside each classroom or in a centralized school area.', 'Whole School Year/June- March', 'Teachers, PTA, School Head', '', '', 2026, 128550, 57, 12, 109),
