(7563, 'Peer Support / Barkada Kontra Drop-Out', 'To  promote peer encouragement among learners', 'Improved learner engagement', 'Organize peer mentoring and support groups', 'Monthly', 'SSLG Officers, Teachers, Learners', '1000.00', 'Encourage positive peer influence', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7564, 'Conduct SBM orientation and planning workshop for stakeholders\r\n\r\nRegular School Governing Council (SGC) meetings\r\n\r\nConduct LAC sessions, INSET, and peer coaching\r\n\r\nImplement remediation and enrichment programs\r\n\r\nPresent school accomplishments and', 'Strengthen participatory school leadership and decision-making\r\n\r\nImprove collaboration among stakeholders\r\n\r\nEnhance quality of teaching and learning\r\n\r\nIncrease learner achievement\r\n\r\nEnsure transparency and accountability\r\n\r\nImprove school perform', 'Improved school governance and stakeholder participation\r\n\r\nEnhanced learner performance and school effectiveness\r\n\r\nStrengthened transparency and accountability\r\n\r\nIncreased community support and partnerships\r\n\r\nSafe, inclusive, and learner-centered school environment\r\n\r\nMinutes of meetings and implemented resolutions\r\n\r\nImproved classroom observation ratings\r\n\r\nIncreased academic performance and completion rate\r\n\r\nStakeholders informed and reports submitted\r\n\r\nImproved school performance indicators\r\n\r\nUpdated inventory records\r\n\r\nIncreased donations/support received\r\n\r\nIncreased volunteer participation\r\n\r\nImproved parent participation rate\r\n\r\nSafe and learner-friendly school environment\r\n\r\nImproved learner attendance and participation', 'The implementation of School-Based Management (SBM) shall utilize a participatory, collaborative, and learner-centered approach to ensure effective governance and continuous school improvement. The school shall engage internal and external stakeholders in planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation of programs and projects aligned with the schoo\'s vision, mission, and goals.\r\n\r\nThe methodology shall include the following approaches:\r\n1. Participatory Planning Approach\r\n     Teachers, parents, learners, community leaders, and stakeholders shall needs, setting \r\n      priorities, and preparing action plans.\r\n2. Collaborative Decision-Making\r\n      The School Governing Council (SGC), PTA, teachers, and community partners shall work \r\n       together in making decisions to improve school performance and learner outcomes.\r\n3. Data-Driven Management\r\n      School programs and interventions shall be based on school data such as learner \r\n      performance, attendance, SBM assessment results, and other school indicators.\r\n4. Continuous Improvement Process (CIP)\r\n      Regular monitoring, evaluation, reflection, and feedback mechanisms shall be \r\n      conducted to improve implementation and address gaps.\r\n5. Inclusive and Child-Friendly Practices\r\n     The school shall ensure that all learners, including those with disabilities and learners at \r\n      risk, are given equal opportunities and support. ', 'School Year 2026 - 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Master Teacher, PTA, S', '62000', 'Quarterly monitoring of implementation\r\n\r\nSubmission of accomplishment reports\r\n\r\nEvaluation through SBM assessment tools\r\n\r\nStakeholder feedback and consultation', 2026, 128697, 106, 12, 134),
(7565, 'Installation of Suggestion Box and Online Feedback Form', 'To gather stakeholder feedback for service improvement', 'Functional feedback system established', 'Place suggestion box and create Google Form', '1st Quarter', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Teachers', '1500.00', 'Monitor feedback regularly', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7566, 'Frontline Service Orientation', 'To improve staff awareness on quality customer service', 'Personnel oriented on proper frontline services', 'Conduct short seminar/workshop', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers, Staff', '3000.00', 'Include customer handling tips', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7567, 'Creation of School Help Desk', 'To provide easy assistance to stakeholders', 'Organized help desk for inquiries and concerns', 'Assign personnel and designate service area', 'Whole School Year', 'School Heads, Office Staff, Teachers', '2500.00', 'Use visible signage', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7568, 'Digital Communication Platform', 'To improve communication with parents and stakeholders', 'Active school FB page/Messenger group', 'Post announcements and respond to inquiries online', 'Whole School Year', 'ICT Coordinator, Teachers', '1000.00', 'Ensure timely updates', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7569, 'Client Satisfaction Survey', 'To assess effectiveness of school services', 'Collected stakeholder feedback reports', 'Conduct simple surveys after transactions', 'Every Semester', 'School Heads, Teachers, Stakeholders', '1500.00', 'Use results for improvement planning', 2026, 304208, 57, 12, 109),
(7570, '“Project Konek\"', 'To strengthen the implementation of the Alternative Delivery Mode during face-to-face class suspension', 'Increase the percentage of learners who successfully complete ADM learning task and requirements during face to face class suspension', 'Establish a systematic mapping and distribution protocol for self-learning modules and activity sheets immediately upon notice of face-to-face class suspension; Utilize localized text messaging platforms, social media group chats, or online links to maintain active communication lines for academic guidelines between teachers, students, and parents; Set up contactless drop boxes for printed outputs; Collect quick feedback from parents on learning difficulties; Provide targeted support for students who missed deadlines.', 'year round', 'School Head, Teachers, Students, Parents', '15000.00', 'Use blended teaching to make the ADM teaching accessible to all, printed self-learning modules or digital channels may applied based on the availability for the learners.', 2026, 128436, 57, 12, 0),
