(7968, 'Strengthening School-Based Management through active participation of the School Governing Council (SGC)', '•	To institutionalize participatory decision-making in school governance.\r\n•	To enhance transparency and accountability in school operations.\r\n•	To improve learner outcomes by aligning school programs with community priorities.\r\n•	To foster collabora', '•	Functional SGC actively engaged in planning, monitoring, and evaluation.\r\n•	School Improvement Plan (SIP) reviewed and endorsed by SGC.\r\n•	Increased stakeholder participation in school programs and projects.\r\n•	Documented reports of decisions, resolutions, and implemented activities.', '•	Conduct orientation and capacity-building sessions for SGC members.\r\n•	Regular quarterly meetings to discuss school performance, needs, and projects.\r\n•	Establish feedback mechanisms (surveys, consultations, assemblies).\r\n•	Integrate SGC recommendations into the SIP and Annual Implementation Plan (AIP).\r\n•	Transparent posting of school financial reports and project updates.', '•	Strengthening School-Based Management throu', 'Strengthening School-Based Management through', 'Strengthening School-Based Management through active participation of the School Governing Council (SGC)	•	To institutionalize participatory decision-making in school governance.	•	Functional SGC actively engaged in planning, monitoring, and evaluati', '•	The success of SBM depends on sustained collaboration and trust among stakeholders. •	The SGC must ensure inclusivity, giving voice to parents and learners in decision-making.• LGU support and community involvement are critical for resource mobilization. • Continuous documentation and transparency will strengthen accountability and credibility.', 2026, 323411, 106, 12, 133),
