(8046, 'Implement regular NAT review sessions, provide competency-based learning materials, and conduct mock tests.', '1. Improve learners\' performance and readiness for the National Achievement Test (NAT).\r\n2.Improve learners\' performance and readiness for the National Achievement Test (NAT).\r\n3.Assess learner preparedness through periodic mock tests and diagnostic ', '1. Increased NAT readiness and improved learner performance in core subjects.\r\n2. Developed and distributed review modules, worksheets, and practice exercises.\r\n3. Mock test results and performance analysis reports.', '1. Conduct weekly NAT review sessions focusing on identified least-mastered competencies.\r\n2. Prepare, reproduce, and utilize competency-based learning materials during review sessions and home-based learning activities.\r\n3. Conduct quarterly mock tests, item analysis, and remediation activities based on results.', 'June 2026 – February 2027', 'Teachers, Master Teachers, School Head', '10000.00', '1. Priority given to Grade 6 learners.\r\n2.Materials shall be aligned with MELCs and NAT competencies.\r\n3.Results will guide intervention programs.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8047, '6. Operate SBM Systems', '•Regularize meetings, decision-making & transparency \r\n•Follow agreed processes', '•Monthly meeting minutes\r\n•Posted financial & progress reports', '•Hold scheduled meetings \r\n•Post reports in public areas\r\n•Document all decisions', 'Nov 2026- Ongoing', 'SGC, School Head, Bookkeeper', ' ₱400     (supplies, folders)', 'Continuous activity', 2026, 129194, 61, 12, 4),
(8048, 'Strengthen community advocacy, provide flexible learning schedules, and encourage learner participation through follow-ups.', '1. Strengthen community awareness and advocacy on the importance of education and regular school attendance.\r\n2. Provide flexible learning schedules and support mechanisms for learners at risk of absenteeism or dropping out.\r\n3. Encourage active lear', '1. Increased community support and awareness of school programs and learner retention initiatives.\r\n2. Increased learner participation and reduced absenteeism.\r\n3. Improved learner engagement and attendance records.', '1. Conduct advocacy campaigns, community assemblies, house-to-house visits, and information dissemination through posters, flyers, and social media platforms.\r\n2. Implement flexible learning schedules, remedial classes, take-home learning packets, and individualized learning plans.\r\n3. Conduct home visits, phone calls, text messaging, counseling sessions, and learner mentoring activities.', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Barangay Officials, PT', '8000.00', 'Collaboration with local stakeholders is encouraged.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8049, '7. Implement SIP/AIP Projects', '•Execute programs for instruction, facilities, health & resources\r\n•Improve school services  ', '•Completed activities/projects \r\n•Accomplishment reports with photos  ', '•Assign working committees \r\n• Involve parents & community\r\n•Regular check-ups \r\n ', 'Jan 2026- Dec 2026     Jan 2027- May 2027', 'All stakeholders, Teachers, LGU', '₱153,500 (MOOE + donations) ', 'Prioritize small, high impact project', 2026, 129194, 61, 12, 4),
(8050, 'Pivot focus toward local agricultural and community-based partnership to support elementary-appropriate programs like the Gulayan sa Paaralan or basic livelihood workshops.', '1. Strengthen partnerships with community stakeholders to support school-based programs and learner development.\r\n2. Enhance the implementation of the Gulayan sa Paaralan Program (GPP) to support nutrition and environmental awareness.\r\n3. Develop lea', '1. Established partnerships and signed agreements with community stakeholders.\r\n2. Functional and productive school garden with active learner participation.\r\n3. Learners acquire basic skills in gardening, recycling, food processing, and simple handicrafts.', '1. Conduct stakeholder consultations, partnership meetings, and Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) signing with local government units, NGOs, parents, and community organizations.\r\n2. Organize gardening activities, provide seeds and tools, establish garden plots, and conduct gardening demonstrations.\r\n3. Conduct workshops, demonstrations, and hands-on activities facilitated by community resource persons and skilled parents.', 'June – July 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, Barangay Officials, PT', '12000.00', '1. Encourage active stakeholder participation in school programs.\r\n2.Harvests may supplement school feeding and nutrition programs.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8051, 'Strengthen anti-bullying policies, conduct regular awareness seminars, improve supervision, and encourage confidential reporting mechanism.', '1. Strengthen the implementation of the school\'s anti-bullying policy to ensure a safe and child-friendly learning environment.\r\n2. Increase awareness among learners, parents, and school personnel about bullying prevention and positive behavior.\r\n3. ', '1. Updated and disseminated anti-bullying policy guidelines.\r\n2. Conducted awareness seminars and advocacy activities.\r\n3. Increased visibility of teachers and reduced bullying incidents.', '1. Review and reinforce school anti-bullying policies; orient learners, teachers, and parents on policy provisions and reporting procedures.\r\n2. Organize anti-bullying seminars, classroom discussions, symposiums, poster-making contests, and advocacy campaigns.\r\n3. Implement duty schedules, regular patrols, monitoring during recess and dismissal, and supervision in common areas.', 'June – July 2026', 'School Head, Child Protection Committee, Teac', '8', '1. Aligned with DepEd Child Protection Policy.\r\n2. Promote respect, empathy, and inclusivity.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
