(8053, 'Conduct regular child protection orientations, strengthen partnerships with stakeholders, and ensure immediate reporting and intervention procedures.', '1. Strengthen partnerships with stakeholders to support learner welfare, safety, and school programs.\r\n2. Establish an efficient and responsive reporting system for learner concerns and protection issues.\r\n3. Ensure immediate intervention and respons', '1. Established and active partnerships with stakeholders and community organizations.\r\n2. Functional reporting mechanism and documented reports.\r\n3. Timely intervention records and case management reports.', '1. Conduct stakeholder consultations, partnership meetings, and signing of commitments/MOAs to support learner protection and intervention programs.\r\n2. Develop and disseminate reporting protocols; designate focal persons; provide reporting forms, drop boxes, and communication channels.\r\n3. Implement standard intervention procedures, referral systems, counseling sessions, home visits, and coordination with concerned agencies when necessary.', 'June – July 2026', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers, Barangay', '4000.00', '1. Strengthen community ownership and support for school initiatives.\r\n2. Follow DepEd Child Protection and referral guidelines.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8054, '9. Institutionalize & Apply for  Certification ', '•Make SBM part of regular work \r\n•Reach higher SBM Level', '•Official SBM Level Certification \r\n•SBM systems embedded in school operations ', '•Update school policies \r\n•Document best practices \r\n•Apply for validation', 'June-Aug 2027 onwards ', 'School Head, SGC, Division Office', ' ₱500 (Documentation) ', 'Goal: Level 1 → Level 2 → Level 3 ', 2026, 129194, 61, 12, 4),
(8055, 'Intensify home visitation, provide interventions for at risk learners, strengthen parent engagement, and continue support programs.', '1. Intensify home visitation efforts to address absenteeism, poor academic performance, and potential dropout risks.\r\n2. Provide appropriate academic, behavioral, and psychosocial interventions for at-risk learners.\r\n3. Strengthen parent engagement i', '1. Completed home visitation reports and action plans for identified learners.\r\n2. Individualized intervention plans and improved learner participation and performance.\r\n3. Increased parental involvement and participation in school activities.', '1. Conduct regular home visits, learner profiling, parent consultations, and case conferences for at-risk learners.\r\n2. Implement remediation classes, peer tutoring, counseling, mentoring, and referral services when necessary.\r\n3. Conduct Parent-Teacher Conferences, parenting seminars, family engagement activities, and regular communication with parents.', 'Monthly / As Needed', 'chool Head, Teachers, Class Advisers, Parents', '8000.00', '1. Priority given to learners with chronic absenteeism and learning difficulties.\r\n2. Interventions shall be based on learner needs assessment.\r\n3. Parents recognized as key partners in learner success.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8056, '10. Recognized & Share Best Practices', '•Honor contributors \r\n•Share success with others ', '•Awarded partners\r\n•Shared best practices in district/division ', '•Recognition program\r\n•Prepare program \r\n•Prepare simple report/presentation', 'June 2027 onwards', 'School, District Office', ' ₱700 (Certificates + tokens)  ', 'Encourages sustainability', 2026, 129194, 61, 12, 4),
(8057, 'Strengthen community partnerships, provide additional learning resources, and conduct continuous monitoring of learners.', '1.Strengthen partnerships with community stakeholders to support educational programs and learner development.\r\n2. Provide additional learning resources to enhance teaching and learning outcomes.\r\n', '1.  Active partnerships and stakeholder commitments established.\r\n2. Increased availability of learning materials and educational resources.', '1. Conduct stakeholder meetings, partnership-building activities, resource mobilization campaigns, and signing of partnership agreements.\r\n2. Procure, develop, and distribute supplementary learning materials, reading resources, and instructional aids through stakeholder support and school funds.', 'June – July 2026 and Ongoing', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers, Barangay', '12000.00', '1. Strengthen collaboration to support school improvement initiatives.\r\n2. Focus on literacy, numeracy, and foundational skills.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8058, 'Coordinators with DepEd ALS coordinators, conduct advocacy campaigns, and allocate resources for ALS implementations', '1. Strengthen coordination and collaboration with DepEd ALS Coordinators to support out-of-school youth and adult learners in the community. \r\n2. Increase community awareness of ALS opportunities and the importance of lifelong learning.\r\n', '1. Functional partnership and coordinated ALS implementation plan.\r\n2. Conducted advocacy campaigns and increased community awareness.', '1. Conduct coordination meetings, planning sessions, and regular consultations with ALS Coordinators and education stakeholders.\r\n2. Organize information drives, community assemblies, house-to-house advocacy, distribution of flyers, and social media campaigns.', 'June – July 2026 and Ongoing', 'School Head, ALS Coordinator, Teachers, Distr', '10000.00', '1. Ensures alignment with DepEd ALS programs and policies.\r\n2. Focus on out-of-school youth and adult learners.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8059, 'Conduct regular DRRM trainings and drills, improve emergency preparedness, and procure necessary supplies and equipment. ', '1. Enhance the knowledge and skills of learners and school personnel on Disaster Risk Reduction and Management (DRRM).\r\n2. Conduct regular disaster preparedness drills to improve response during emergencies.\r\n3. Improve school emergency preparedness ', '1. Learners and personnel trained on disaster preparedness and response procedures.\r\n2. Successful implementation of earthquake, fire, and evacuation drills.\r\n3. Updated School DRRM Plan and emergency response protocols.', '1. Conduct DRRM orientations, seminars, workshops, and capacity-building activities in coordination with local DRRM offices and partner agencies.\r\n2. Schedule and conduct quarterly drills, simulations, and post-drill evaluations to identify strengths and areas for improvement.\r\n3. Review and update contingency plans, evacuation maps, communication systems, and emergency procedures.', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, DRRM Coordinator, Teachers, Lear', '8000.00', '1. Align activities with DepEd DRRM policies and programs\r\n2.Ensure participation of all learners and personnel.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8060, 'Conduct mental health awareness activities, strengthen guidance services, and establish referral systems with health agencies.', '1. Promote mental health awareness and psychosocial well-being among learners, teachers, and parents.\r\n2. Strengthen school guidance and counseling services to support learners\' emotional and behavioral needs.\r\n3. Establish and operationalize referra', '1. Increased awareness and understanding of mental health and well-being.\r\n2. Functional guidance and counseling support system.\r\n3. Referral protocols and partnerships with health service providers established.', '1. Conduct mental health awareness campaigns, symposiums, classroom sessions, and wellness activities for learners, teachers, and parents.\r\n2. Conduct individual and group counseling, mentoring programs, classroom guidance sessions, and psychosocial support activities.\r\n3. Coordinate with local health units, hospitals, social workers, and mental health professionals; develop referral procedures and communication protocols.', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Guidance Coordinator/Designate, ', '8000.00', '1. Activities should be age-appropriate and learner-centered.\r\n2. Maintain confidentiality and child protection standards.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8061, 'Improve facilities, provide SPED training for teachers, and seek additional funding/support for inclusive education resources.', '1. Improve school facilities to create a more accessible and inclusive learning environment for learners with special educational needs.\r\n2. Provide appropriate learning resources and assistive materials for learners with special needs.', '1. Improved and learner-friendly facilities with accessibility features.\r\n2. Availability of inclusive learning materials and assistive devices.', '1. Conduct facility assessment; install or improve ramps, handrails, accessible pathways, and learning spaces suitable for learners with disabilities.\r\n2. Procure and develop instructional materials, visual aids, manipulative resources, and assistive learning tools.', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, Property Custodian, Teachers, PT', '15000.00', '1. Priority shall be given to accessibility and safety improvements.\r\n2. Resources shall address diverse learner needs.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8062, 'Seek additional funding and encourage participation in free online trainings and webinars', '1. Generate additional resources to support school programs, projects, and professional development activities.\r\n2. Encourage teachers and school personnel to participate in free online trainings, webinars, and professional development programs.\r\n3. ', '1. Increased funding and resource support from stakeholders and partners.\r\n2. Increased participation in online learning and professional development activities.\r\n3. Teachers equipped with updated instructional and leadership skills.', '1. Conduct resource mobilization activities, prepare funding proposals, and establish partnerships with LGUs, NGOs, private organizations, and community stakeholders.\r\n2. Disseminate training opportunities, create a training calendar, and encourage registration in free DepEd, government, and partner-sponsored webinars.\r\n3. Conduct Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions, post-training sharing sessions, and application of acquired learning in classroom practices.', 'Throughout the School Year', 'School Head, Property Custodian, Teachers, PT', '17000.00', '1. Priority shall be given to accessibility and safety improvements.\r\n2. Capacity-building activities shall focus on differentiated instruction and learner support.\r\n3.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8063, 'Conduct regular recognition and awarding activities', '1.Recognize and reward learners for outstanding academic performance, good behavior, leadership, attendance, and participation.\r\n2. Promote positive behavior, excellence, and active participation among learners.\r\n3. Strengthen parental and stakeholde', '1. Increased learner motivation and recognition of achievements.\r\n2. Improved learner engagement, attendance, and performance.\r\n3. Increased parent and stakeholder participation in recognition activities.', '1. Conduct quarterly and year-end recognition ceremonies; award certificates, medals, and tokens to deserving learners.\r\n2. implement incentive and recognition programs for academic excellence, leadership, sports, attendance, and co-curricular activities.\r\n3. Invite parents, PTA officers, and community stakeholders to attend and support recognition programs.', 'Quarterly and Year-End', 'School Head, Teachers, Learners, Parents', '8000.00', 'Recognition shall be based on established school criteria.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8064, 'Ensure timely submission and monitoring of payroll documents', '1. Ensure the timely preparation and submission of payroll-related documents.\r\n2. Strengthen monitoring and tracking of payroll documents to minimize delays and errors.\r\n3. Improve the accuracy and completeness of payroll-related documents.', '1. Payroll documents submitted accurately and on schedule.\r\n2. Updated payroll monitoring records and tracking system.\r\n3. Reduced payroll discrepancies and document deficiencies.', '1. Establish a payroll preparation calendar, checklist system, and submission timeline for all required documents.\r\n2. Maintain payroll monitoring logs, document trackers, and submission records for reference and verification.\r\n3. Conduct document verification, review, and validation before submission.', 'Monthly', 'School Head, Administrative Officer/Designate', '5000.00', '1. Adhere to Division Office deadlines and requirements.\r\n2. Ensure proper documentation and record management.\r\n3. Ensure compliance with accounting and auditing standards.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8065, 'Conduct regular inspection and immediate repair of damaged facilities', '1. Ensure school facilities are safe, functional, and conducive to learning.\r\n2. Address damaged facilities promptly to prevent accidents and disruptions in learning.', '1. Safe and well-maintained classrooms, buildings, and school facilities.\r\n2. Damaged facilities repaired and restored in a timely manner.', '1. Conduct regular facility inspections using standard inspection checklists and identify areas requiring repair or maintenance.\r\n2. Implement immediate repair and maintenance activities for identified defects and damaged structures.', 'Monthly', 'School Head, Property Custodian, School Facil', '15000.00', 'Priority shall be given to safety-related concerns.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25);
INSERT INTO `sgod_action_plan` (`id`, `activity`, `objective`, `ex_output`, `metho_strategy`, `time_frame`, `person_involved`, `bud_req`, `remarks`, `fy`, `school_id`, `division`, `region`, `district`) VALUES
(8066, 'Prioritize and implement school improvement projects gradually', '1. Identify and prioritize school improvement projects based on urgency, impact, and available resources.', '1. Prioritized School Improvement Project (SIP) implementation plan.', '1. Conduct needs assessment, facility inspection, stakeholder consultation, and project prioritization workshops.', 'une – July 2026', 'School Head, SBM Team, Teachers, PTA Officers', '50000.00', '1. Prioritization shall be based on learner needs, safety, and school development goals.\r\n2. Projects may include classroom improvement, sanitation facilities, learning spaces, and safety enhancements.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8067, 'Request additional books and improve library facilities', ' Increase the availability of books and learning resources to support literacy and academic achievement.', 'Additional books and reference materials acquired.', 'Submit requests to DepEd, LGUs, NGOs, private donors, and stakeholders; conduct book donation drives and resource mobilization activities.', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, Librarian/Teacher-Librarian, Tea', '20000.00', 'Prioritize age-appropriate and curriculum-aligned materials.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8068, 'Improve internet connectivity and maintain utility facilities regularly', 'Improve internet connectivity to support teaching, learning, and school operations.', 'Stable and reliable internet connection available for school use.', 'Coordinate with internet service providers, upgrade internet plans and equipment, and install signal boosters or additional access points when needed.', 'June 2026 – March 2027', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Property Custod', '40000.00', 'Priority support for digital learning and school reporting requirements.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8069, 'Acquire additional computers and conduct regular maintenance', 'Increase the availability of computers to support teaching, learning, and administrative operations.', 'Additional functional computers acquired and installed.', 'Procure computers through school funds, stakeholder donations, LGU assistance, and DepEd support programs.', 'June – October 2026', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, Property Custod', '120000.00', 'Acquisition of at least 4–6 desktop computers or equivalent units, subject to available funds.', 2026, 129127, 60, 12, 25),
(8070, 'Conduct SBM Orientation for the PTA, SGC, teachers, students and other stakeholders.\r\n\r\n\r\nConduct quarterly PTA and SGC Meetings\r\n', 'To strengthen the implementation of School-Based Management (SBM) by enhancing participatory governance, improving teaching-learning processes, ensuring transparency  and accountability, and maximizing resource utilization.\r\n\r\nTo strengthen the imple', 'Conducted SBM Orientation for the PTA, SGC, teachers, students and other stakeholders.\r\n\r\nConducted PTA and SGC Meetings, Notice of Meetings, Accomplished Attendance \r\nSheets, Minutes, Pictoria', 'Face-to-Face Orientation', 'June 2026', 'School Head/SBM Coordinator, SGC, SSLG, PTA, ', '7500.00', '1. This will be taken  up as one of the agenda during the PTA General Assembly.\r\n\r\n2. This will be done quarterly with the PTA and the SGC', 2026, 302004, 105, 12, 23),
(8071, 'Facilitate the yearly School Improvement Planning (SIP) Workshop', 'Enhance collaborative leadership and governance practices', 'Approved SIP updated and implemented', 'Participatory Planning Approach, Collaborative Decision-making, Stakeholder Consultation and Engagement, Data-Driven Planning, Workshop and Focus Group Discussions (FGD)', 'June 2026', 'School head, SBM Coordinator, Teachers, Stake', '11000', '5,000', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8072, 'Convene periodic School Governing Council (SGC) meetings', 'Promote greater stakeholder participation in decision-making processes', 'At least 4 meetings conducted annually', 'Stakeholder Engagement, Participatory Governance, Consultative Meetings, Consensus-Building Discussions', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, SGC Officers', '5000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8073, 'Hold PTA meetings and community engagement sessions', 'Foster effective communication among stakeholders', 'Increased attendance and participation', 'Conduct regular consultative meetings, community dialogues, information dissemination activities, and collaborative discussions to strengthen stakeholder engagement and promote shared responsibility in school programs and initiatives.', 'Quarterly', 'Teachers, PTA Officers', '5000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8074, 'Provide leadership and management capability-building activities', 'Develop leadership competencies of teachers and coordinators.', 'Teachers demonstrate improved leadership skills', 'Conduct capacity/building trainings, leadership workshops, mentoring and coaching sessions, peer learning activities, and professional development programs to enhance leadership, decision-making, and management skills.', 'Twice a year', 'School head, Master Teacher', '20000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8075, 'Create working committees for school programs and initiatives', 'Encourage collective responsibility and accountability', 'Functional committees with clear responsibilities', 'Establish collaborative committee structures through participatory planning, delegation of resposibilities, role clarification sessions, and regular monitoring meetings to promote shared accountability and effective implementation of school programs.', 'June-July 2026', 'School head, Teachers, Stakeholders', '5000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8076, 'Learning Action Cell (LAC) Session on Values-Based Teaching Strategies', 'To enhance teachers’ competence in embedding values-based instruction through regular LAC sessions and instructional coaching.', 'Conducted LAC sessions and trainings focusing on strategies for integrating peace education and Core Values in teaching.', 'Capacity Building through LAC Sessions and Trainings\r\nConduct regular Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions focusing on strategies for integrating peace education and DepEd Core Values in daily lesson planning and classroom instruction.', 'whole school year', 'Teachers, School head', '2000', '', 2026, 128368, 57, 12, 113),
(8077, 'Enhance academic achievement in key learning areas', 'Implement intervention and enrichment  activities', 'Improved learner achievement scores', 'Conduct diagnostic assessments, targeted remediation, differentiated insteuction, tutorial sessions, enrichment programs, and regilar progress monitoring to address learning gaps and improve learner performance', 'Whole School Year', 'Teachers, Reading Coordinator', '10000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8078, 'Carry out literacy and numeracy enhancement programs', 'Improve literacy and numeracy competencies', 'Increased reading and numeracy proficiency', 'Implement structured literacy and numeracy interventions through guided reading sessions, remediation classes, peer tutoring, differentiated instruction, learning camps, use of manipulatives, and continuous assessment and progress monitoring to strengthen foundational skills.', 'Weekly', 'Teachers, Volunteers', '10000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8079, 'Facilitate Learning Action Cell (LAC) sessions', 'Improve instructional practices and teaching effectiveness', 'Improved classroom observation ratings', 'Conduct collaborative learning sessions, peer coaching, lesson study, classroom-based action research sharing, demonstration teaching, and reflective discussions to enhance pedagogical knowledge, instructional strategies, and professional practice.', 'Monthly', 'School Head, Teachers', '5000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8080, 'Conduct ICT capacity-building and digital learning initiatives', 'Promote ICT integration in teaching and learning', 'Increased use of ICT in lessons', 'Provide hands-on ICT training, digital literacy workshops, coaching and mentoring sessions, technology-enhanced lesson planning, and sharing of best practices to strengthen teachers’ competence in integrating ICT into instruction and learning activities.', 'Quarterly', 'ICT Coordinator, Teachers', '3000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8081, 'Apply differentiated and inclusive teaching approaches', 'Foster inclusive and learner-focused educational practices', 'Improved learner participation and attendance', 'Implement differentiated instruction, inclusive education strategies, learner-centered teaching methods, individualized support interventions, flexible learning activities, and continuous assessment to address diverse learning needs and promote active participation among all learners.', 'Whole school year', 'Teachers', '3000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8082, 'Apply differentiated and inclusive teaching approaches', 'Foster inclusive and learner-focused educational practices', 'Improved learner participation and attendance', 'Implement differentiated instruction, inclusive education strategies, learner-centered teaching methods, individualized support interventions, flexible learning activities, and continuous assessment to address diverse learning needs and promote active participation among all learners.', 'Whole school year', 'Teachers', '3000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8083, 'Carry out systematic classroom observations and program reviews', 'Enhance school monitoring and evaluation mechanisms', 'Monitoring reports completed on time', 'Implement regular classroom observations, program monitoring, data collection and analysis, performance reviews, feedback conferences, and continuous improvement planning to ensure effective implementation of educational programs and instructional practices.', 'Monthly', 'School Head, Master Teachers', '3000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8084, 'Review assessment outcomes and school performance data', 'Strengthen evidence-based decision-making processes', 'Data used in planning and interventions', 'Conduct data-driven analysis, assessment reviews, performance monitoring, collaborative data discussions, and action planning sessions to identify learning gaps, inform interventions, and guide school improvement initiatives.', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers', '8000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8085, 'Disseminate financial reports and accomplishment updates', 'Promote transparency and accountability in school operations', 'Stakeholders informed of school accomplishments', 'Conduct regular financial reporting, accomplishment reviews, information dissemination activities, stakeholder consultations, and public posting of reports to ensure transparency, accountability, and informed stakeholder participation in school governance.', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Finance Committee', '3000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8086, 'Undertake annual SBM evaluation and assessment', 'Sustain continuous school development efforts', 'Improved SBM level rating', 'Conduct systematic self-assessment, stakeholder validation, document review, data analysis, and action planning sessions to identify strengths, address gaps, and guide continuous school improvement based on SBM principles and standards.', 'March 2027', 'SBM Coordinator, Stakeholders', '5000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8087, 'Administer stakeholder satisfaction assessments', 'Foster stakeholder feedback and collaborative engagement', 'Positive stakeholder feedback results', 'Conduct stakeholder satisfaction surveys, feedback-gathering sessions, focus group discussions, data analysis, and consultation meetings to identify areas for improvement and strengthen stakeholder participation in school programs and decision-making processes.', 'Twice a year', 'Teachers, PTA Officers', '3000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8088, 'Carry out inventory and monitoring of school assets and learning resources', 'Ensure efficient management and utilization of school resources', 'Updated inventory records', 'Conduct regular inventory audits, resource tracking, asset verification, utilization monitoring, and record management to ensure proper accountability, maintenance, and efficient use of school properties and learning resources.', 'Semi-annually', 'Property Custodian, Teachers', '2000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8089, 'Expand collaboration with LGUs, NGOs, and private-sector partners', 'Strengthen community engagement and strategic partnerships', 'Increased donations and partnerships', 'Conduct partnership-building initiatives through stakeholder consultations, networking activities, advocacy campaigns, proposal development, resource mobilization, and regular coordination meetings to foster sustainable support for school programs and projects.', 'Whole school year', 'School Head, Stakeholders', '10000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8090, 'Implement Brigada Eskwela and campus clean-up activities', 'Enhance school facilities and the learning environment', 'Cleaner and safer school environment', 'Mobilize stakeholders through volunteerism, community participation, resource-sharing, clean-up drives, minor repair and maintenance activities, and environmental stewardship programs to improve the safety, cleanliness, and functionality of school facilities.', 'Before school opening and quarterly', 'Teachers, Parents, Community Volunteers', '20000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8091, 'Facilitate fire drills and DRRM awareness programs', 'Strengthen disaster preparedness and safety awareness', 'Increased preparedness and safety awareness', 'Conduct regular emergency drills, disaster risk reduction and management (DRRM) orientations, safety awareness campaigns, simulation exercises, first-aid training, and coordination with local emergency response agencies to enhance preparedness and promote a culture of safety.', 'Quarterly', 'DRRM Coordinator, Barangay Officials', '5000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8092, 'Implement school gardening and solid waste management programs', 'Objective	Activities/Programs	Methodology/Strategy	Persons Responsible	Timeline	Resources Needed	Budgetary Requirements	Success Indicators\r\nPromote sustainable school-based initiatives', 'Functional school garden and waste segregation system', 'Conduct environmental education activities, school gardening projects, waste segregation campaigns, composting initiatives, stakeholder participation activities, and regular monitoring to promote environmental stewardship and sustainable practices among learners and the school community.', 'Whole school year', 'YES-O Coordinator, Teachers', '15000', '', 2026, 128729, 106, 12, 133),
(8093, 'School-Based Profiling of Learners & Resources ', 'To tract and update  learners profile and assess the availability and condition of existing school resources for inventory and intervention. ', '100% profiled learners and updated resource inventory', 'Online and Offline Encoding, Inventory of Class Profile, CRLA, Phil-IRI, RMA, Inventory Form', 'Opening Block  June 8-11, 2026 ', 'School Head, Teachers, ICT Coordinator, learn', '1000', 'for implementation', 2026, 128739, 106, 12, 133),
(8094, 'Provide adequate and contextualized instructional materials', 'To develop and enhance localized instructional materials', '80% of developed and enhanced IMs utilized', 'Actual usability of developed Instructional Materials', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'Teachers, School Head', '10000', 'for implementation', 2026, 128739, 106, 12, 133),
(8095, 'Classroom Management', 'To strengthen classroom management', 'Improved Classroom Structuring, \r\nZero conflict incident\r\n', 'Face to face peer tutoring, Class routines, and learner groupings, setting of standards in providing Seat Plan, Classroom Readiness Checklist, Rules and Regulations', 'Terms 1 to 3  of Instructional Blocks', 'School Head, Teachers and Learners', '2000', 'for implementation', 2026, 128739, 106, 12, 133),
(8096, 'Revitalization of Instructional Supervision & Technical Assistance ', 'Strengthen teacher competence by conducting regular classroom observations, coaching sessions, and targeted technical assistance. ', '100% of teachers observed and given feedback\r\n\r\nImproved COT ratings,\r\n', 'Face to face Classroom Observations and Feedback  in facilitating COT-RPMS/PMES \r\nTool; TA Log Sheets ', 'Terms 1 to 3 of Instructional Blocks', 'School Head, Teachers ', '2000', 'for implementation', 2026, 128739, 106, 12, 133),
(8097, 'Leaners\' Achievement', 'Improve academic performance of learners', 'Increase at least 2% in learners\' quarterly assessment results', 'Actual teaching-learning process in facilitating Test Analysis, Progress Monitoring Tool', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, learners', '5000', 'for implementation', 2026, 128739, 106, 12, 133),
(8098, 'Reading & Numeracy Intervention  ', 'Enhance the literacy and numeracy performance of struggling learners through targeted interventions and remediation. ', '85–90% of learners progress from frustration to instructional reading levels ', 'Face to face remedial classes; Peer tutoring; Marungko; Numeracy Drills; ARAL Program  in facilitating CRLA; Phil-IRI, Numeracy Assessment ', 'June 2026- March 2027', 'School Head, Teachers, Learners', '5000', 'for implementation', 2026, 128739, 106, 12, 133),
(8099, 'Learning Action Cell Sessions', 'Conduct LAC sessions on the alignment to the new Learning System Reform Policies in lesson planning (ILAW), Grading system, Awards and recognition, Flexible Learning Program and Education in Emergencies', 'At least 90% of teachers participated the sessions', 'Blended Workshop, Meeting, Conferences in providing Attendance records, activity outputs, Reflection journals\r\n', 'End-Of -Term Blocks  Sept. 2-15, 2026 and Dec', 'Teachers, School Head, Resource Speakers', '5000', 'for implementation', 2026, 128739, 106, 12, 133),
(8100, 'Stakeholder Advocacy & Partnership for School Support ', 'Mobilize community stakeholders—PTA, barangay officials, NGOs, and partners—to support the learning needs of the learners by providing materials and resources. ', 'At least three (3) new support materials provided through donations ', 'Face to face meetings; PTA Conferences in facilitating Attendance and Pledge of Commitment ', 'June 2026 (Brigada  Eskwela) ', 'School Head, Teachers, Parents, Barangay Offi', '10000', 'for implementation', 2026, 128739, 106, 12, 133),
(8101, 'Reorientation and Restructuring of the School Governing Council (SGC)', 'To strengthen school leadership and stakeholder participation in SBM processes.', 'Updated SGC composition with signed Terms of Reference (TOR) and an active SBM committee.', 'Conduct a general assembly with PTA, local government units (LGU), and faculty; establish clear roles.', '1st Quarter', 'School Head, Teachers, PTA Officers, LGU/Bara', '1500', 'For immediate implementation', 2026, 304250, 106, 12, 0),
(8102, 'Self-Assessment of SBM Level of Practice', 'To identify the current SBM level (Developing, Maturing, Advanced) and pinpoint areas for improvement.', 'Accomplished SBM Assessment Tool with complete baseline data and supporting evidence.', 'Conduct focused group discussions (FGDs) and internal auditing of school documents per dimension.', '1st Quarter', 'SBM Coordinator, School Head, Committee Chair', '1000', 'For evaluation and planning reference', 2026, 304250, 106, 12, 0),
(8103, 'Updating the School Improvement Plan (SIP) and AIP', 'To align the Annual Implementation Plan (AIP) with the newly identified SBM priorities and targets.', 'Approved, stakeholder-validated SIP/AIP reflecting SBM-aligned technical targets.', 'Facilitate a strategic planning workshop with the School Planning Team (SPT) and community stakeholders.', '2nd Quarter', 'School Head, Master Teachers, SGC, PTA Presid', '3000', 'Subject to Division review', 2026, 304250, 106, 12, 0),
(8104, 'Enhancing Learning Action Cells (LAC) for SBM Integration', 'To improve curriculum delivery and classroom management using data-driven SBM approaches.', 'Documented LAC sessions, updated instructional materials, and improved teacher competencies.', 'Conduct regular, structured peer-mentoring sessions, teaching demonstrations, and collaborative lesson planning.', 'Monthly / Quarterly', 'School Head, Master Teachers, Department Head', '2000', 'Weekly/Monthly monitoring', 2026, 304250, 106, 12, 0),
(8105, 'Stakeholder Accountability and Progress Reporting', 'To sustain transparency and public accountability regarding school performance and fund utilization.', 'State of the School Address (SOSA) presented; School Report Card (SRC) distributed.', 'Organize a mid-year and year-end school assembly; publish transparency boards and digital infographics.', '2nd & 4th Quarter', 'School Head, SGC, ICT Coordinator, Parents', '1500', 'For institutional transparency', 2026, 304250, 106, 12, 0),
(8106, 'Establishing a Continuous Improvement (CI) Project', 'To resolve critical localized issues affecting student performance (e.g., drop-out rates or reading gaps).', 'At least one functional CI project successfully implemented and institutionalized.', 'Form a dedicated CI team; diagnose a specific problem using root-cause analysis, and deploy localized interventions.', '2nd–4th Quarter', 'CI Team, Subject Coordinators, Guidance Couns', '5000', 'Subject to quarterly assessment', 2026, 304250, 106, 12, 0),
(8107, 'Final SBM Validation and Exhibit Preparation', 'To successfully pass the Division-level SBM validation and achieve the next higher Level of Practice.', 'Organized, digitized, and physically arranged SBM artifacts (MOVs) across all dimensions.', 'Conduct mock evaluations, validate Means of Verification (MOVs), and set up a systematic school SBM room/digital repository.', '4th Quarter', 'All Faculty, School Head, SBM Committee, Stak', '4000', 'For end-of-year Division validation', 2026, 304250, 106, 12, 0),
(8108, 'Revisit SBM for school year 2026-2027', 'To update SBM', 'Updated SBM for school year 2026-2027', 'Conduct FGD and SLAC', 'Sept 2026', 'School Head , AO , Teachers', '1000', 'Task will be completed', 2026, 128875, 59, 12, 140),
(8109, 'PRE-IMPLEMENTATION\r\n1. Conduct SBN self-assessment using the 42 indicators\r\n2. Analyze indicators with \"Rarely Manifested\" and \"Not Yet Manifested\"\r\n3. Prioritize interventions per SBM dimension\r\n4. Conduct strategic planning workshop\r\n5. Organize Sc', 'PRE-IMPLEMENTATION\r\n1. Establish baseline status across 6 SBM dimensions\r\n2. Identify priority improvement areas\r\n3. Focus planning on weak areas\r\n4. Develop SBM-based improvement plan\r\n5. Strengthen governance structure\r\n6. Strengthen community part', 'PRE-IMPLEMENTATION\r\n1. Comprehensive SBM Baseline Profile Report\r\n(with ratings across 6 dimensions and validated MOVs)\r\n2. Gap Analysis Report\r\n(list of “Rarely” and “Not Yet Manifested” indicators per dimension)\r\n3. Prioritized Intervention Matrix / Action List\r\n(ranked based on urgency, impact, and feasibility)\r\n4. Draft SBM Action Plan aligned with SIP/AIP\r\n(with timelines, persons involved, and resources)\r\n5. Organized and Functional School Governance Council (SGC)\r\n(with defined roles and meeting structure)\r\n6. Reorganized and Active PTA Structure\r\n(with elected officers and engagement plan)\r\n7. Revised SIP aligned with SBM Findings\r\n(evidence-based and responsive to gaps)\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 1\r\n1. Improved learner achievement in Math, Science, and Reading based on quarterly assessments and NAT results.\r\n2. 100% of teachers produce and utilize contextualized instructional materials aligned with MELCs.\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 2\r\n1. Zero reported cases of bullying and child abuse within the school year.\r\n2. Fully functional DRRM system with quarterly conducted drills and updated preparedness plans.\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 3\r\n1. Updated and SBM-aligned SIP based on data and stakeholder consultation.\r\n2. Active and functional school-community planning team with documented meetings and outputs.\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 4\r\n1. Ensured SIP implementation through AIP\r\n(100% implementation of approved PPAs based on AIP.)\r\n2. Improved governance participation\r\n(Functional SGC and PTA with regular meetings and active involvement in school programs.)\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 5\r\n1. Improved teaching quality through LAC\r\n(Monthly LAC outputs with documented instructional improvements.)\r\n2. Enhanced teacher competencies\r\n100% participation of teachers in professional development activities.\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 6\r\n1. Improved facility safety and condition\r\n(Complete quarterly facility inspection reports with compliance to safety standards.)\r\n2. Improved school infrastructure\r\n(Functional upgraded facilities (library, laboratories, classrooms, and learning spaces).\r\n3. Strengthened ICT systems\r\nFully functional ICT infrastructure supporting teaching and learning processes.\r\n4. Ensure financial accountability\r\n(100% MOOE liquidation compliance with complete and clean financial records.)\r\n\r\nPOST-IPLEMENTATION\r\n1. Measured SBM improvement\r\n(Completed SBM end-line evaluation showing improved ratings across all six dimensions.)\r\n2. Document SBM implementation\r\n(Completed SBM accomplishment report with consolidated MOVs and evidence.)\r\n3. Improved school planning system\r\n(Revised SIP aligned with SBM results and priority improvement areas.)\r\n', 'PRE-IMPLEMENTATION\r\n1. Use SBM assessment tool and validation workshop\r\n3. Conduct data analysis workshop per dimension\r\n3. Rank and cluster indicators\r\n4. Facilitate participatory planning with stakeholders\r\n5. Select and orient  members\r\n6. Conduct election and orientation meetings\r\n7. Review SBM results and integrate into SIP\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 1\r\n1. Conduct intervention classes\r\n2. Implement LAC-based development\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 2\r\n1. Conduct campaigns and monitoring\r\n2. DRRM drills\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 3\r\n1. Implement data-based planning\r\n2. Conduct regular meetings\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 4\r\n1. Execute programs\r\n2. Conduct Regular meetings\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 5\r\n1. Conduct Needs-based LAC\r\n2. Conduct Trainings\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 6\r\n1. Conduct Quarterly inspection\r\n2. Conduct Facility development\r\n3. Upgrade systems\r\n4. Monitor system\r\n\r\nPOST-IMPLEMENTATION\r\n1. Re-assess SBM Practice\r\n2. Consolidation of MOVs\r\n3. Data-based revision\r\n', 'APRIL 2026 TO MARCH 2027', 'SCHOOL HEAD, COORDINATORS, TEACHERS, SPT, STA', '30,000.00', 'PRE-IMPLEMENTATION\r\n1. Ensures accurate baseline data through participatory validation and complete MOV documentation\r\n2. Provides clear evidence-based identification of priority improvement areas\r\n3. Supports focused and strategic planning based on identified gaps\r\n4. Remarks:\r\nEnsures participatory planning and alignment of school improvement priorities\r\n5. Strengthens shared governance and accountability in school management\r\n6. Enhances community involvement and sustained stakeholder participation\r\n7. Ensures data-driven and needs-responsive school improvement planning\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 1\r\n1. Targets learner learning gaps through structured intervention programs and continuous monitoring of quarterly assessment and NAT performance\r\n2. Ensures instructional responsiveness by producing localized and learner-centered materials aligned with MELCs\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 2\r\n1. Ensures a safe and protective school environment through continuous awareness campaigns, monitoring, and strict implementation of child protection policies\r\n1. Ensures a safe and protective school environment through continuous awareness campaigns, monitoring, and strict implementation of child protection policies\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 3\r\n1. Ensures data-driven and stakeholder-informed school planning aligned with SBM findings and improvement priorities\r\n2. Strengthens participatory governance through regular collaboration, shared decision-making, and documented planning outputs\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 4\r\n1. Ensures full implementation of school improvement initiatives through efficient execution of approved programs, projects, and activities aligned with the AIP\r\n2. Enhances shared governance by ensuring active participation, regular meetings, and sustained engagement of school stakeholders\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 5\r\nStrengthens instructional competence through continuous, collaborative learning sessions focused on improving teaching practices and learner outcomes\r\n1. Enhances teacher competencies and instructional effectiveness through sustained participation in structured professional development programs\r\n\r\nDIMENSION 6\r\n1.  Ensures safety and functionality of school facilities through regular inspection and compliance with established safety standards\r\n2. Enhances the learning environment by upgrading and improving school facilities to support effective teaching and learning processes\r\n3. Supports digital learning by improving ICT infrastructure and ensuring reliable connectivity for instructional use\r\n4. Promotes financial transparency and accountability through timely monitoring and complete liquidation of MOOE funds\r\n\r\nPOST-IMPLEMENTATION\r\n1. Assesses the overall effectiveness of SBM implementation by comparing baseline and end-line results across all six dimensions\r\n2. Ensures proper documentation and consolidation of accomplishments, including complete MOVs to support SBM validation and reporting\r\n3. Promotes continuous improvement by updating the SIP using evaluation results and identified priority areas for development\r\n', 2026, 323407, 106, 12, 134),
(8110, 'Establishment of Reading Corner per Classroom', 'To provide temporary access to reading materials despite absence of functional library.', 'Functional classroom reading corners with books and learning materials', 'Collection and distribution of books, improvised shelves, and reading materials', 'June–July 2026', 'Teachers, SPTA, Learners', '5000', 'Immediate intervention for learners', 2026, 128447, 57, 12, 121),
(8111, 'Conduct of Computer Donation and Resource Mobilization Drive', 'To acquire additional computers and ICT equipment.', 'Increased number of functional computers and ICT devices', 'Partnership with LGU, alumni, NGOs, private partners, and stakeholders', 'July–August 2026', 'School Head, ICT Coordinator, PTA, Stakeholde', '3000', 'Encourages community support', 2026, 128447, 57, 12, 121),
(8112, 'RMES- READING REMEDIATION PROGRAM', 'Helps learners at Full Refresher and Moderate Refresher become Grade-level Ready', 'Leaners at Full Refresher and Moderate Refresher will become Grade level Ready', 'Intensify the reading remediation program in collaboration with PTA, BLGU, LGU, PLGU, and other professional groups.', 'JUNE 2026- FEBRUARY 2027', 'SH, MT, TEACHERS, PARENTS, STAKEHOLDERS', '30,000.00', 'The RMES- Reading Remediation Program is a collaboration of internal and external stakeholders with a concerted effort to help learners become grade-ready.', 2026, 128449, 57, 12, 121),
(8113, '1. Orientation on SBM Principles and Processes', 'To familiarize stakeholders with SBM policies, principles, and roles.', 'Stakeholders oriented and committed to SBM implementation.', 'Orientation/Meeting\r\n', 'June–July 2026', 'All SGC Members', '500', 'Conducted before full SBM implementation.', 2026, 128867, 59, 12, 140),
(8114, '2. Reconstitution and Strengthening of SGC', 'To ensure active participation of stakeholders in school governance.', 'Stakeholders oriented and committed to SBM implementation.', 'Meeting and Election, Collaborative decision-making', '\'June-July 2026', 'All SGC Members', '500', 'Functional SGC established to support SBM implementation.', 2026, 128867, 59, 12, 140),
(8115, 'Conduct SBM Assessment and Planning Workshop', 'To identify priority areas for school improvement and strengthen SBM implementation.', 'Updated SBM Action Plan based on identified needs and gaps.', 'Conduct assessment, consultation, and collaborative planning with stakeholders.', 'June–July 2026', 'School Head, SBM Coordinator, Teachers, PTA, ', '3000', 'For continuous SBM improvement and monitoring.', 2026, 129015, 59, 12, 146),
(8116, 'Strengthen Literacy and Numeracy Intervention Programs', 'To improve learners’ proficiency in reading, comprehension, and numeracy skills.', 'Implemented remediation and enrichment activities for learners.', 'Conduct intervention activities, progress monitoring, and assessment.', 'Whole School Year', 'Teachers, Reading Coordinator, Parents', '5000', 'Prioritize learners with identified learning gaps.', 2026, 129015, 59, 12, 146),
(8117, 'Enhance Stakeholder Engagement and Partnerships', 'To strengthen collaboration with stakeholders in supporting school programs.', 'Active participation and increased stakeholder involvement.', 'Conduct meetings, partnership activities, and resource mobilization initiatives.', 'One per Term', 'School Head, PTA, SGC, Community Partners', '2000', 'Sustain school-community partnership.', 2026, 129015, 59, 12, 146),
(8118, 'Conduct School-Based Learning Action Cell', 'To improve teachers’ competencies in instruction and assessment practices.', 'Improved teaching strategies and professional skills.', 'Implement LAC sessions, workshops, and peer sharing activities.', 'Monthly', 'School Head, Teachers, Master Teacher', '5000', 'Based on identified professional needs.', 2026, 129015, 59, 12, 146),
(8119, 'Improve School Facilities and Learning Resources', 'To provide a safe and conducive learning environment.', 'Enhanced facilities and additional learning resources.', 'Conduct facility assessment, maintenance, and resource enhancement activities.', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, Property Custodian, Teachers, St', '10000', 'Subject to available resources and support.', 2026, 129015, 59, 12, 146),
(8120, 'Strengthen Child Protection and Learner Support Programs', 'To maintain a safe, inclusive, and learner-friendly school environment.', 'Functional child protection and learner support mechanisms.', 'Conduct awareness campaigns, monitoring, and psychosocial activities.', 'Whole School Year', 'CPC, Guidance Coordinator, Teachers, Parents', '3000', 'Ensure learner safety and well-being.', 2026, 129015, 59, 12, 146),
(8121, 'Monitor and Evaluate SBM Programs and Projects', 'To ensure effective implementation and continuous improvement of SBM initiatives.', 'Monitoring reports and recommendations for improvement.', 'Conduct regular monitoring, evaluation, and feedback sessions.', 'Whole School Year', 'School Head, SBM Team, Stakeholders', '2000', 'Basis for future planning and decision-making.', 2026, 129015, 59, 12, 146),
(8122, 'Conduct School Governing Council (SGC) Meetings and Stakeholders\' Consultation', 'Strengthen shared governance and encourage active participation of stakeholders in school decision-making.', 'Conducted three terms SGC meetings\r\nApproved resolutions and action plans\r\nIncreased stakeholder participation', 'Conduct consultations, planning sessions, and collaborative decision-making activities.', 'By Term (July 2025–April 2026)', 'School Head, SGC Members, Teachers, PTA Offic', '5000', 'Continuous implementation', 2026, 316004, 59, 12, 139),
(8123, 'Conduct quarterly reading intervention for struggling readers', 'To improve the reading proficiency level of identified struggling readers from Grade 1-6 through systematic, quarterly reading intervention sessions focused on phonics, fluency, and comprehension.', 'Pre-test data, Intervention plan, Post-test data, Learners attendance', 'Conduct a quarterly intervention weekly .', 'July - September', 'Reading Coordinator, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 128345, 57, 12, 114),
(8124, 'Quarterly School Governing Council meeting', 'Strengthen participative decision-making among stakeholders', 'Created organizational structure of the roles and responsibility of stakeholders', 'Quarterly meeting, Orientation, and transparency board updates', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, SGC Chair', '500', 'Minutes of meeting, Attendance sheet', 2026, 128345, 57, 12, 114),
(8125, 'Conduct Quarterly School Report Card', 'To ensure transparent use of school funds & resources.', 'Transparency report posted on bulletin board', 'Quarterly School report card conducted', 'Quarterly', 'School Head, Teachers, SPTA Officers', '1000', 'Posted reports on transparency board', 2026, 128345, 57, 12, 114),
(8126, 'Updated MOOE liquidation reports ', 'To monitor MOOE Funds and School Projects Implementation', 'Approved MOOE liquidation', 'Updated MOOE liquidation reports and completed school projects implementation', 'January-December', 'School Head, Teachers, AO ', '1000', 'Liquidation Report submitted', 2026, 128345, 57, 12, 114),
(8127, 'Conduct learner support and remediation sessions to assist struggling learners in improving attendance, addressing learning gaps, and enhancing academic performance through targeted interventions, regular monitoring, and parent engagement.', 'To improve the attendance, address learning gaps, and enhance the academic performance of struggling learners through targeted remediation, regular monitoring, and active parent engagement.', '', '', 'June to April 2025', 'Reading Coordinator, Master Teachers ', '200.00', 'Conduct monitoring and evaluation based on the results of the progress of the Reading intervention', 2026, 129254, 61, 12, 8),
(8128, 'Support Grade 3 learners in achieving proficiency in early language, literacy, and numeracy skills through structured, cluster-based enhancement sessions focused on identified learning competencies.', 'To enable Grade 3 learners to achieve proficiency in each cluster of early language, literacy, and numeracy skills through structured, targeted enhancement sessions.', 'Improved proficiency of Grade 3 learners in early language, literacy, and numeracy skills per competency cluster', 'Implement a cluster-based, learner-centered remediation approach where Grade 3 learners are grouped according to specific skill gaps in early language, literacy, and numeracy. Teachers will conduct structured enhancement sessions using differentiated instruction, guided practice, and formative assessments. Continuous monitoring, feedback, and periodic reassessment will be done to track progress, while parents will be engaged to support learning at home.', 'July to March 2025', 'Reading Coordinator, Master Teachers, & Class', '200', 'Implementation shall be closely coordinated with class advisers and subject teachers to ensure proper grouping and scheduling of learners. Continuous monitoring and documentation are required to track progress per cluster. Parent engagement and follow-up activities are essential for reinforcing learning at home. Adjustments in grouping and strategies may be made based on ongoing assessment results.', 2026, 129254, 61, 12, 8),
(8129, 'Conduct a targeted review and enhancement program focused on strengthening learners’ competencies in 21st century skills and core learning areas in preparation for the National Achievement Test (NAT), through structured review sessions, diagnostic as', 'To ensure that Grade 6, 10, and 12 learners achieve proficiency in 21st century skills and core learning areas as measured by improved performance in the National Achievement Test (NAT).', 'Improved NAT readiness and proficiency levels of Grade 6, 10, and 12 learners\r\n\r\nIncreased mean percentage scores in core learning areas and 21st century skills\r\n\r\nCompleted diagnostic tests, review materials, and enhancement session records\r\n\r\nRegularly updated learner progress monitoring reports\r\nReduced number of learners at low mastery levels', 'Implement a data-driven review and enhancement strategy anchored on diagnostic assessment results. Learners will undergo targeted review sessions per learning area, focusing on least mastered competencies and 21st century skills. Teachers shall employ differentiated instruction, formative assessments, and periodic mock tests to monitor progress. Continuous feedback, remediation, and parental support shall be integrated to strengthen learner preparation for the National Achievement Test (NAT).', 'July to March 2025', 'Reading Coordinator and Class Advisers, SH', '500.00', 'Implementation shall be coordinated with subject teachers and grade level coordinators to ensure alignment of review materials with least mastered competencies. Regular monitoring through mock tests and progress tracking is required. Coordination with parents is encouraged to support home-based review. Adjustments in instruction and grouping shall be made based on assessment results and learner performance trends.', 2026, 129254, 61, 12, 8),
(8130, 'Conduct structured remediation activities to address identified learning gaps in reading, comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics through targeted instructional support and differentiated learning tasks.', 'To improve learners’ academic performance by implementing structured remediation activities that address identified learning gaps in reading, comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics through targeted instructional support and differenti', 'Improved learner performance in reading, comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics.\r\n\r\nIncreased percentage of learners achieving proficiency levels in targeted competencies.\r\n\r\nIndividual learner progress reports documenting improvement areas and mastery levels.', 'Assessment and Identification of Learning Gaps – Conduct diagnostic and formative assessments in reading, comprehension, science and technology, and mathematics to determine specific competencies that learners have not mastered.\r\nGrouping of Learners – Organize learners based on identified needs (e.g., below basic, basic, and approaching proficiency) to ensure targeted intervention.\r\nDevelopment of Differentiated Learning Materials – Prepare leveled worksheets, activity sheets, reading passages, manipulatives, and enrichment tasks aligned with least mastered skills.\r\nTargeted Instruction and Intervention Sessions – Provide small-group instruction, one-on-one tutoring, peer-assisted learning, and guided practice sessions focusing on specific skill gaps.', 'July to March 2026', 'Reading Coordinator, Math Coor. and grade lev', '500', 'Implementation shall be based on identified learning gaps using assessment results. Teachers are expected to provide differentiated and targeted interventions, monitor learner progress regularly, and adjust strategies as needed. Coordination with parents and submission of progress reports are required to ensure effective implementation and sustained learner improvement.', 2026, 129254, 61, 12, 8),
(8131, 'Accomplish school based SBM technical assistance provision report', 'To accomplish school based SBM technical assistance provision report', 'Accomplished school based SBM technical assistance provision report', 'Documentation', 'September 4-5, 2026', 'Teachers, Stakeholders, School Head', '500', 'Accomplish school based SBM technical assistance provision report', 2026, 129285, 61, 12, 9),
(8132, 'Conduct consultative meeting with chairman of respective SBM dimension', 'To conduct consultative meeting with chairman of respective SBM dimension to discuss about data/ documents gathered, tools to be used and schedule and school based SBM assessment', 'Attendance sheets, Minutes of the Meetings, Documentation', 'Documentation', 'August 22, 2026', 'Teachers, Stakeholders, School Head', '500', 'Conduct consultative meeting with chairman of respective SBM dimension', 2026, 129285, 61, 12, 9),
(8133, 'Conduct Self- Assessment with internal stakeholders', 'To conduct Self- Assessment with internal stakeholders', 'Conducted Self- Assessment with internal stakeholders', 'Documentation', 'August 28-29, 2026', 'Teachers, Stakeholders, School Head', '500', 'Conduct Self- Assessment with internal stakeholders', 2026, 129285, 61, 12, 9),
(8134, 'Gather self-assessment data and documentation.', 'To gather self assessment data and documentation.', 'Accomplished assessment data', 'Documentation', 'August 28-29, 2026', 'Teachers, Stakeholders, School Head', '500', 'Gather self assessment data and documentation', 2026, 129285, 61, 12, 9),
(8135, 'Orientation of the school personnel of D.O. 007 s. 2024', 'To oriental of the school personnel of D.O. 007 s. 2024', 'Number of teachers oriented.', 'Documentation, Lecture', 'August 22, 2026', 'Teachers, Stakeholders, School Head', '1000', 'Orientation of the teachers of D.O. 007 s. 2024', 2026, 129285, 61, 12, 9),
(8136, 'Orientation of the teachers SBM dimensions.', 'To orient the teachers of SBM dimensions.', 'Number of teachers oriented.', 'Documentation', 'August 22, 2026', 'Teachers, Stakeholders, School Head', '500', 'Orient of the teachers of SBM dimensions', 2026, 129285, 61, 12, 9),
(8137, 'Conduct School Based Orientation to various stakeholders ', 'To increase stakeholders’ awareness and understanding of School-Based Management (SBM) principles and the school’s programs, strengthen their active participation and collaboration in school governance, clarify their roles and responsibilities in sup', 'A completed Stakeholders’ Participation and Commitment Checklist indicating attendance, assigned roles/responsibilities, agreed support contributions, and signed commitments aligned with the implementation of School-Based Management (SBM) initiatives.', '1. Stakeholder Mapping and Invitation – Identify key stakeholders (parents, barangay officials, PTA officers, partners) and ensure proper invitations are sent in advance to guarantee full participation.\r\n2. Orientation and Presentation of SBM Framework – Conduct a clear presentation on School-Based Management (SBM), including its principles, roles of stakeholders, and school priorities to build understanding and commitment.\r\n3. Interactive Open Forum and Consultation – Provide opportunities for stakeholders to ask questions, raise concerns, and give suggestions to strengthen engagement and ownership.\r\n4. Role Assignment and Commitment Signing – Facilitate the identification of specific roles and responsibilities of stakeholders and secure their signed commitments through a participation checklist.\r\n5. Documentation and Consolidation of Outputs – Record attendance, commitments, and agreements, then consolidate them into a Stakeholders’ Participation and Commitment Checklist for monitoring and follow-up', 'July 2026', 'School Head, Teaching and Non-Teaching Staff', '2000', 'Attend Barangay Development Committee Meeting to invite stakeholders and strengthen coordination with local officials in mobilizing support and participation for School-Based Management (SBM) initiatives, school programs, and other related school activities.', 2026, 129201, 61, 12, 4),
(8138, 'Establish small-group reading remediation and phonics workshops for Grade 1-3 students identified as low emerging and frustrated readers', 'To transition at least 30% of participating low emerging learners to transitioning and frustration readers to the instructional or independent reading level by the of the academic year, significantly reducing the school\'s overall literacy deficit.', 'Formative and summative reading assessment result (baseline), weekly learners\' attendance logs and progress tracking sheet', 'Assessment Phase administer the BOSY assessment\r\nExecution Phase Conduct ARAL session 3 times a week', 'July-March 2026', 'School Head, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 129284, 61, 12, 9),
(8139, 'SLAC session on DO 007, s. 2024', 'To conduct SLAC session on DO 007, s. 2024', 'Attendance sheet, narrative report', 'discussion, Lectures, open forums', 'August-December 2026', 'School Head, Teachers', '', '', 2026, 129284, 61, 12, 9);
